translate chinese strings:

    old "Uh? Who's there?"
    new "Uh? Who's there?\n嗯？谁在那儿？"

    old "Dago, Shadow, Spell."
    new "Dago, Shadow, Spell.\nDago、Shadow、Spell。"

    old "The three dwarves turns towards Kusho."
    new "The three dwarves turns towards Kusho.\n三个矮人转向 Kusho。"

    old "Uh? Don't tell me that those are their names?"
    new "Uh? Don't tell me that those are their names?\n嗯？别告诉我那就是他们的名字？"

    old "Well, not everyone can be as creative as me and come up with a cool fake name like 'Kusho'."
    new "Well, not everyone can be as creative as me and come up with a cool fake name like 'Kusho'.\n这个嘛，不是每个人都能像我一样有创意，想出“Kusho”这么酷的假名。"

    old "What is this? What do you want from us, Kusho?"
    new "What is this? What do you want from us, Kusho?\n这是什么？你想从我们这儿得到什么，Kusho？"

    old "I know about the job you took."
    new "I know about the job you took.\n我知道你们接的那份活儿。"

    old "That's unfortunate. We wanted to surprise you."
    new "That's unfortunate. We wanted to surprise you.\n真不巧。我们本来想给你个惊喜。"

    old "Sorry about that. No hard feelings, but... I have no intention of dying today."
    new "Sorry about that. No hard feelings, but... I have no intention of dying today.\n抱歉。没有恶意，不过……我今天可没打算死。"

    old "And yet, you still will."
    new "And yet, you still will.\n可你还是会死。"

    old "The dwarf caster uses a magic scroll and my limbs suddenly feel heavy."
    new "The dwarf caster uses a magic scroll and my limbs suddenly feel heavy.\n那个矮人施法者用了一张魔法卷轴，我的四肢突然变得沉重。"

    old "What is this?"
    new "What is this?\n这是什么？"

    old "Damn! I didn't think he'd get his hands on such a powerful scroll! Be careful, [protag]. He used that scroll to slow our movements."
    new "Damn! I didn't think he'd get his hands on such a powerful scroll! Be careful, [protag]. He used that scroll to slow our movements.\n可恶！我没想到他能弄到这么强的卷轴！小心点，[protag]。他用那张卷轴减缓了我们的动作。"

    old "This is not good."
    new "This is not good.\n这下不妙了。"

    old "It's done. You can go, I'll take care of hiding the bodies myself."
    new "It's done. You can go, I'll take care of hiding the bodies myself.\n搞定了。你们可以走了，藏尸的事我自己处理。"

    old "Good. We have wasted enough of our time on this already."
    new "Good. We have wasted enough of our time on this already.\n很好。我们已经在这件事上浪费够多时间了。"

    old "May they rest peacefully in the desert's embrace."
    new "May they rest peacefully in the desert's embrace.\n愿他们在沙漠的怀抱中安息。"

    old "Nuala, they were assassins."
    new "Nuala, they were assassins.\nNuala，他们是刺客。"

    old "So are you. Everyone needs forgiveness when they meet their death."
    new "So are you. Everyone needs forgiveness when they meet their death.\n你也是。每个人在临终之时都需要被宽恕。"

    old "Finally! This heat was killing me."
    new "Finally! This heat was killing me.\n终于凉快了！这热天可把我折腾坏了。"

    old "But it's night now. It's not so bad..."
    new "But it's night now. It's not so bad...\n但现在已经是晚上了。没那么糟……"

    old "It's still too dry for my tastes. I miss the salty sea air already."
    new "It's still too dry for my tastes. I miss the salty sea air already.\n对我来说还是太干了。我已经开始想念咸咸的海风了。"

    old "What a waste. No fancy rings or jewels on them..."
    new "What a waste. No fancy rings or jewels on them...\n真浪费。他们身上连个像样的戒指或珠宝都没有……"

    old "The mage had a fancy spellbook though."
    new "The mage had a fancy spellbook though.\n不过那个法师倒是有本精致的法术书。"

    old "Spellbooks are useless to me. I wanted something new to adorn my hand."
    new "Spellbooks are useless to me. I wanted something new to adorn my hand.\n法术书对我没用。我想要点新东西来装点我的手。"

    old "That was fun! Who's next? Any more assassins to assassinate?"
    new "That was fun! Who's next? Any more assassins to assassinate?\n真有趣！下一个是谁？还有刺客等着我去收拾吗？"

    old "Ugh, Sylrissa please..."
    new "Ugh, Sylrissa please...\n呃，Sylrissa，拜托……"

    old "I'll let you know if someone else wants me dead. But, I think after tonight, it will be awhile before anyone dares to try again."
    new "I'll let you know if someone else wants me dead. But, I think after tonight, it will be awhile before anyone dares to try again.\n要是还有人想要我的命，我会告诉你的。不过我想，过了今晚，一时半会儿没人敢再来试了。"

    old "Dasyra? Are you OK?"
    new "Dasyra? Are you OK?\nDasyra？你没事吧？"

    old "Yes, yes. It's just..."
    new "Yes, yes. It's just...\n没事，没事。只是……"

    old "I don't know. Killing someone in battle is one thing, but actually planning their death like this..."
    new "I don't know. Killing someone in battle is one thing, but actually planning their death like this...\n我不知道。在战场上杀人是一回事，可像这样精心策划他们的死法……"

    old "We plan the attacks on N'Mar as well."
    new "We plan the attacks on N'Mar as well.\n我们对 N'Mar 的进攻也是策划过的。"

    old "Yes, but those are undead! These were... dwarves..."
    new "Yes, but those are undead! These were... dwarves...\n对，可那些是亡灵！这些可是……矮人……"

    old "I'm sorry, Dasyra. I understand how you feel but, really, you shouldn't feel pity for them. They may have seemed innocent enough, but they weren't. Trust me."
    new "I'm sorry, Dasyra. I understand how you feel but, really, you shouldn't feel pity for them. They may have seemed innocent enough, but they weren't. Trust me.\n抱歉，Dasyra。我理解你的感受，但说真的，你不必同情他们。他们看起来也许够无辜，其实不然。相信我。"

    old "I hope so, Kusho. I hope so."
    new "I hope so, Kusho. I hope so.\n希望如此，Kusho。希望如此。"

    old "The others leave and I move to join them. However, Kusho takes ahold of my arm to stop me. It looks like he wants to tell me something."
    new "The others leave and I move to join them. However, Kusho takes ahold of my arm to stop me. It looks like he wants to tell me something.\n其他人离开了，我也动身跟上。然而 Kusho 抓住我的手臂拦住了我。看来他有话想对我说。"

    old "[protag]..."
    new "[protag]...\n[protag]……"

    old "I won't forget what you did today."
    new "I won't forget what you did today.\n我不会忘记你今天所做的一切。"

    old "You're not used to thanking people, are you?"
    new "You're not used to thanking people, are you?\n你还不习惯感谢别人，对吧？"

    old "I think your companions are waiting for you. You should go."
    new "I think your companions are waiting for you. You should go.\n我想你的同伴在等你了。你该走了。"

    old "You're welcome, Kusho. I'll see you back in Grandtree."
    new "You're welcome, Kusho. I'll see you back in Grandtree.\n不用谢，Kusho。回 Grandtree 见。"

    old "Kusho! Thank the gods you're alive!"
    new "Kusho! Thank the gods you're alive!\nKusho！感谢诸神，你还活着！"

    old "No thanks to you."
    new "No thanks to you.\n这可不是托你的福。"

    old "I'm sorry, but I couldn't make the time."
    new "I'm sorry, but I couldn't make the time.\n抱歉，但我实在抽不出时间。"

    old "I understand. I can't say I was happy that you didn't help me, but I'm sure the Envoy of Grimoire had more important matters to attend to."
    new "I understand. I can't say I was happy that you didn't help me, but I'm sure the Envoy of Grimoire had more important matters to attend to.\n我理解。我没法说你没来帮忙我有多高兴，但我相信 Grimoire 的特使有更要紧的事要处理。"

    old "Believe me, if I could have..."
    new "Believe me, if I could have...\n相信我，如果我能来……"

    old "You know what's the worst part?"
    new "You know what's the worst part?\n你知道最糟的是什么吗？"

    old "I couldn't find anyone who was willing to help me. Except... one."
    new "I couldn't find anyone who was willing to help me. Except... one.\n我找不到一个愿意帮我的人。除了……一个。"

    old "Rei. It was humiliating. He only did it to show me that he could kill more targets than me."
    new "Rei. It was humiliating. He only did it to show me that he could kill more targets than me.\nRei。太丢人了。他帮我，只是为了让我看看，他能杀的目标比我多。"

    old "Did he?"
    new "Did he?\n他做到了？"

    old "He did."
    new "He did.\n做到了。"

    old "It was just luck. He just happened to spot two of the three assassins faster than me. Still..."
    new "It was just luck. He just happened to spot two of the three assassins faster than me. Still...\n只是运气好。他只是碰巧比我更早发现三个刺客里的两个。不过……"

    old "Kusho drifts off into an uncomfortable silence so I awkwardly try to steer the conversation in a more positive direction."
    new "Kusho drifts off into an uncomfortable silence so I awkwardly try to steer the conversation in a more positive direction.\nKusho 陷入一阵令人不自在的沉默，于是我尴尬地试着把话题往更积极的方向引。"

    old "Well, at least it sounds like the 'operation' went smoothly."
    new "Well, at least it sounds like the 'operation' went smoothly.\n嗯，至少听起来这次“行动”进展得很顺利。"

    old "The killing was no problem. Perhaps I overestimated those assassins..."
    new "The killing was no problem. Perhaps I overestimated those assassins...\n杀人倒不是问题。也许是我高估了那些刺客……"

    old "Or perhaps you underestimated Rei's skills?"
    new "Or perhaps you underestimated Rei's skills?\n又或者是你低估了 Rei 的身手？"

    old "Hmph. I doubt it. Anyway, what happened made me think. I really don't have many friends. True friends, who will come to your help in moments of need."
    new "Hmph. I doubt it. Anyway, what happened made me think. I really don't have many friends. True friends, who will come to your help in moments of need.\n哼。我可不觉得。总之，这件事让我想了很多。我确实没几个朋友。真正的朋友，会在你需要的时刻来帮你。"

    old "Kusho..."
    new "Kusho...\nKusho……"

    old "It's fine, [protag]. I suppose this is a consequence of the life I choose to live. At least it made me realize where I stand."
    new "It's fine, [protag]. I suppose this is a consequence of the life I choose to live. At least it made me realize where I stand.\n没事，[protag]。我想这是我选择的生活所带来的代价。至少它让我认清了自己身处的位置。"

    old "And don't worry, I'm still dedicated to our mission. The undead must be stopped. Whenever you need me, you know where to find me."
    new "And don't worry, I'm still dedicated to our mission. The undead must be stopped. Whenever you need me, you know where to find me.\n别担心，我依然忠于我们的使命。必须阻止那些亡灵。任何时候你需要我，你知道去哪儿找我。"

    old "Kusho says nothing else and disappears in the forest, leaving me wondering if I really couldn't have spared the time to help him."
    new "Kusho says nothing else and disappears in the forest, leaving me wondering if I really couldn't have spared the time to help him.\nKusho 没再说什么，消失在了森林里，只留下我暗自思量，我是否真的抽不出时间去帮他。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. What can I do for you?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. What can I do for you?\n啊，[protag]。有什么能为你效劳的吗？"

    old "Nothing in particular, Larik. I just came to see how you were doing."
    new "Nothing in particular, Larik. I just came to see how you were doing.\n没什么特别的事，Larik。我只是来看看你过得怎么样。"

    old "Ah, you're looking for a report on my well-being? Well, you can rest assured that I am in good health."
    new "Ah, you're looking for a report on my well-being? Well, you can rest assured that I am in good health.\n啊，你是想听一份我的健康报告？那你可以放心，我身体很好。"

    old "Thanks for the status report, Larik. But that's not why I came by today. I just wanted to talk to you."
    new "Thanks for the status report, Larik. But that's not why I came by today. I just wanted to talk to you.\n谢谢你的这份状态报告，Larik。不过我今天来可不是为了这个。我只是想和你聊聊。"

    old "You wanted to talk? To what end?"
    new "You wanted to talk? To what end?\n你想聊聊？是为了什么？"

    old "To get to know you better."
    new "To get to know you better.\n为了更了解你。"

    old "Ah. You need to truly understand the people that you work with. I understand."
    new "Ah. You need to truly understand the people that you work with. I understand.\n啊。你需要真正了解与你共事的人。我明白了。"

    old "That seems like a good leadership skill to have. The ability to know and understand the people that you lead. To grasp their fears and anxieties. To see what their strengths and weaknesses are."
    new "That seems like a good leadership skill to have. The ability to know and understand the people that you lead. To grasp their fears and anxieties. To see what their strengths and weaknesses are.\n这似乎是种不错的领导才能。能够了解和理解你所领导的人，把握他们的恐惧与焦虑，看清他们的长处和短处。"

    old "Yeah, I think that's true."
    new "Yeah, I think that's true.\n是啊，我也这么认为。"

    old "Is that why you take the time to meet with your followers, [protag]? To figure out their talents, and figure out the best way to use them on the battlefield?"
    new "Is that why you take the time to meet with your followers, [protag]? To figure out their talents, and figure out the best way to use them on the battlefield?\n这就是你肯花时间会见追随者的原因吗，[protag]？为了弄清他们的才能，找出在战场上发挥他们作用的最佳方式？"

    old "Well, it is enjoyable to chat with people, but yes, the real reason that I take the time to meet with people that I'm working with—people like you—is that I want to get a better understanding of what their capabilities are."
    new "Well, it is enjoyable to chat with people, but yes, the real reason that I take the time to meet with people that I'm working with—people like you—is that I want to get a better understanding of what their capabilities are.\n嗯，和人聊天确实很愉快，不过没错，我之所以肯花时间会见与我共事的人——像你这样的人——真正的原因，是我想更好地了解他们的能力。"

    old "Larik, you're an interesting person, and it's fascinating to have an opportunity to learn from you. But Grimore, and in fact all of Aravorn, is filled with interesting people, each with interesting lessons to teach."
    new "Larik, you're an interesting person, and it's fascinating to have an opportunity to learn from you. But Grimore, and in fact all of Aravorn, is filled with interesting people, each with interesting lessons to teach.\nLarik，你是个有趣的人，能有机会向你学习，这很让人着迷。不过 Grimore，乃至整个 Aravorn，到处都是有趣的人，每个人都能教给你有趣的道理。"

    old "I've chosen to meet with you specifically because I think that we have things to learn from each other, but the truth is our relationship never would have come to fruition were it not for our shared goals."
    new "I've chosen to meet with you specifically because I think that we have things to learn from each other, but the truth is our relationship never would have come to fruition were it not for our shared goals.\n我特意选择与你见面，是因为我觉得我们彼此有值得学习的地方，但说实话，若不是因为我们有共同的目标，我们之间的这份情谊根本不会有结果。"

    old "That's a good attitude to have, [protag]. I myself had problems in my early days of leadership with keeping my priorities straight. I tried to involve myself in the everyday affairs of everyone in the tribe, but there simply isn't enough time in the day. You have to focus specifically on the people who are critical to your mission."
    new "That's a good attitude to have, [protag]. I myself had problems in my early days of leadership with keeping my priorities straight. I tried to involve myself in the everyday affairs of everyone in the tribe, but there simply isn't enough time in the day. You have to focus specifically on the people who are critical to your mission.\n这个态度很好，[protag]。我在刚当领袖时，自己也曾在分清轻重缓急上犯过难。我试图插手部落里每个人的日常事务，但一天的时间根本不够用。你必须把精力专门放在对你使命至关重要的人身上。"

    old "And in a way, it's flattering to know that you consider me to be important enough to your mission that you'd take time to talk to me. You could have spent your afternoon with anyone, but you decided to check in on me instead."
    new "And in a way, it's flattering to know that you consider me to be important enough to your mission that you'd take time to talk to me. You could have spent your afternoon with anyone, but you decided to check in on me instead.\n而且从某种意义上说，知道你把我视为对使命足够重要的人、愿意抽出时间和我谈话，这让我很受用。你本可以和任何人共度这个下午，却选择了来看我。"

    old "I'm not just concerned with how useful people are, Larik. I consider them as individuals."
    new "I'm not just concerned with how useful people are, Larik. I consider them as individuals.\n我并不只关心别人有没有用，Larik。我把他们当作独立的个体来看待。"

    old "So what is it that brings you here today?"
    new "So what is it that brings you here today?\n那么，今天是什么风把你吹来的？"

    old "It's true, I do want to get to know you. And my understanding you better may allow me to make better judgments about how to utilize your strengths. But more than that, I enjoy the process. It's interesting to learn about people and hear their personal stories."
    new "It's true, I do want to get to know you. And my understanding you better may allow me to make better judgments about how to utilize your strengths. But more than that, I enjoy the process. It's interesting to learn about people and hear their personal stories.\n没错，我确实想了解你。而且更了解你之后，我也许能更准确地判断该如何发挥你的长处。但更重要的是，我享受这个过程。了解别人、听他们讲自己的故事，是件很有意思的事。"

    old "So, you came to hear stories from me, eh? Well, I'll have to come up with some good ones, then. I hope you won't be disappointed."
    new "So, you came to hear stories from me, eh? Well, I'll have to come up with some good ones, then. I hope you won't be disappointed.\n那么，你是来听我讲故事的，嗯？那我可得准备几个精彩的了。希望不会让你失望。"

    old "I understand that your tribe has a history that you'd like to share with people like me, but don't forget your own personal struggles as well. It's easy to look at heroes in terms of the battles they won, or the beasts they slew, but sometimes the most interesting part of a hero's story can be the personal struggles he has."
    new "I understand that your tribe has a history that you'd like to share with people like me, but don't forget your own personal struggles as well. It's easy to look at heroes in terms of the battles they won, or the beasts they slew, but sometimes the most interesting part of a hero's story can be the personal struggles he has.\n我明白，你的部落有一段历史，你愿意讲给我这样的人听，但也别忘了你自己的亲身挣扎。人们很容易从英雄赢过的战斗、斩杀过的野兽去看待他们，但有时英雄故事里最有趣的部分，恰恰是他个人的挣扎。"

    old "Don't forget about your own feelings in all of this."
    new "Don't forget about your own feelings in all of this.\n在这些事里，也别忘了你自己的感受。"

    old "Well, if you want to know how I've been feeling recently..."
    new "Well, if you want to know how I've been feeling recently...\n好吧，如果你想知道我最近感觉如何……"

    old "It's an interesting experience, being the one who is led, rather than the leader."
    new "It's an interesting experience, being the one who is led, rather than the leader.\n被人领导而不是领导别人，这是一种有趣的体验。"

    old "You weren't born a leader, were you?"
    new "You weren't born a leader, were you?\n你不是生来就是领袖的吧？"

    old "No, but I always strived to be a leader. Even when I was a young boy, I would look at the people of my tribe, and I thought to myself, 'I want to lead these people.' Perhaps it was the ego in me, or perhaps it was my better instincts as a protector. I wanted to be their guardian."
    new "No, but I always strived to be a leader. Even when I was a young boy, I would look at the people of my tribe, and I thought to myself, 'I want to lead these people.' Perhaps it was the ego in me, or perhaps it was my better instincts as a protector. I wanted to be their guardian.\n不是，但我一直努力想当领袖。甚至在我还是个小男孩时，我就会看着部落里的人，心里想：‘我想领导这些人。’也许那是我心中的自负，又或许是作为保护者更良善的本能。我想成为他们的守护者。"

    old "But when it comes to working with you, I'm more than happy to allow you to be the leader. When I was a lad, I coveted leadership. Under you, I don't. Maybe it's because I understand that the goals you pursue are so much larger than I am. Actually, I don't envy your position at all."
    new "But when it comes to working with you, I'm more than happy to allow you to be the leader. When I was a lad, I coveted leadership. Under you, I don't. Maybe it's because I understand that the goals you pursue are so much larger than I am. Actually, I don't envy your position at all.\n但在与你共事时，我非常乐意让你来当领袖。我年轻时曾渴望领导之位。可在你手下，我不再渴望了。也许是因为我明白，你所追求的目标远比我本人宏大。实际上，我一点也不羡慕你的位置。"

    old "I feel a bit odd talking to you like this, as though we're peers. One leader talking to another. But the truth is, the stakes of your conflict are so much greater. I hold the fate of a tribe in my hands. You may very well hold the fate of an entire city, and even the surrounding lands."
    new "I feel a bit odd talking to you like this, as though we're peers. One leader talking to another. But the truth is, the stakes of your conflict are so much greater. I hold the fate of a tribe in my hands. You may very well hold the fate of an entire city, and even the surrounding lands.\n像这样和你说话，我觉得有点不自在，仿佛我们是平辈。一个领袖与另一个领袖交谈。但事实是，你这场斗争的利害关系要大得多。我手中握着的是一个部落的命运。而你握着的，很可能是整座城市，乃至周边大地的命运。"

    old "That's why I feel my time is better spent with you than tending directly to my own people. Even if I die in combat serving you, I know the Dunemarcher clan elders can appoint someone to replace me. But if the blight from N'Mar continues to ooze across the lands, what hope do we have for the future?"
    new "That's why I feel my time is better spent with you than tending directly to my own people. Even if I die in combat serving you, I know the Dunemarcher clan elders can appoint someone to replace me. But if the blight from N'Mar continues to ooze across the lands, what hope do we have for the future?\n正因如此，我觉得把时间花在你身上，比直接照顾自己的族人更有价值。即使我在为你作战时战死，我知道 Dunemarcher 氏族的长老们也能任命别人来接替我。可若是来自 N'Mar 的瘟疫继续在大地上蔓延，我们的未来还有什么希望？"

    old "I've always thought that we were all in this together, Larik. I find it comforting to know that you think of it the same way."
    new "I've always thought that we were all in this together, Larik. I find it comforting to know that you think of it the same way.\n我一直觉得我们是一条船上的人，Larik。知道你也这么想，让我很安心。"

    old "Larik flashes a big grin."
    new "Larik flashes a big grin.\nLarik 咧开嘴，露出一个大大的笑容。"

    old "I hope that my talk of the importance of your mission hasn't come across as too somber. I know there are some people who might join you out of fear of what might happen if they don't. And if I am to tell the truth, I do feel a bit of fear."
    new "I hope that my talk of the importance of your mission hasn't come across as too somber. I know there are some people who might join you out of fear of what might happen if they don't. And if I am to tell the truth, I do feel a bit of fear.\n我希望我谈到你使命的重要性时，没有显得太过沉重。我知道有些人加入你，是出于若不加入会怎样的恐惧。而要说实话，我确实感到一丝恐惧。"

    old "But more than the fear, I feel excitement. It seems like a grand opportunity to be part of something so big. In a way, I feel that the greatest service I could perform for my people is to come back a hero—or even, if fate demands it, to die a hero."
    new "But more than the fear, I feel excitement. It seems like a grand opportunity to be part of something so big. In a way, I feel that the greatest service I could perform for my people is to come back a hero—or even, if fate demands it, to die a hero.\n但比起恐惧，我更感到兴奋。能参与如此宏大的事业，似乎是千载难逢的机会。从某种意义上说，我觉得我能为族人做出的最大贡献，就是作为英雄归来——或者，若命运如此要求，作为英雄死去。"

    old "The Dunemarchers are a people who have spent most of their days on the world's fringes—we march across regions of the desert that most people consider uninhabitable, and we call those sands our home. In many ways, we have removed ourselves from most of the people of Aravorn, even the other desert tribes."
    new "The Dunemarchers are a people who have spent most of their days on the world's fringes—we march across regions of the desert that most people consider uninhabitable, and we call those sands our home. In many ways, we have removed ourselves from most of the people of Aravorn, even the other desert tribes.\nDunemarchers 是一个常年游走于世界边缘的民族——我们穿行在多数人视为不毛之地的沙漠地带，把那些沙丘称作家园。在许多方面，我们都与 Aravorn 的多数人保持着距离，甚至包括其他沙漠部落。"

    old "By serving under you, in an indirect way, I'm allowing my tribe to become part of something larger. Perhaps one day we'll be mentioned in the pages of Grimoire's history books, even if it is only as a footnote."
    new "By serving under you, in an indirect way, I'm allowing my tribe to become part of something larger. Perhaps one day we'll be mentioned in the pages of Grimoire's history books, even if it is only as a footnote.\n通过在你麾下效力，我间接地让我的部落成为了更宏大事业的一部分。也许有一天，我们会被写进 Grimoire 的史书里，哪怕只是作为一个脚注。"

    old "Let's make history together, Larik."
    new "Let's make history together, Larik.\n让我们一起创造历史吧，Larik。"

    old "Larik waves at me."
    new "Larik waves at me.\nLarik 朝我挥手。"

    old "Hello there, leader. Are you coming in with fresh orders for me?"
    new "Hello there, leader. Are you coming in with fresh orders for me?\n你好啊，头儿。你是给我带新命令来了吗？"

    old "Relax, Larik. I just came to talk. A conversation between two friends."
    new "Relax, Larik. I just came to talk. A conversation between two friends.\n放松点，Larik。我只是来聊聊。朋友之间的闲谈。"

    old "A conversation between two leaders."
    new "A conversation between two leaders.\n领袖之间的交谈。"

    old "Larik grins."
    new "Larik grins.\nLarik 咧嘴一笑。"

    old "Has the subject of leadership been on your mind lately?"
    new "Has the subject of leadership been on your mind lately?\n最近你一直在想领导这件事吗？"

    old "Yes, it has. After we talked last, I was thinking about how you say you take the time to meet with your followers. I'm amazed that you find the time to do it, what with all of the responsibilities of leadership."
    new "Yes, it has. After we talked last, I was thinking about how you say you take the time to meet with your followers. I'm amazed that you find the time to do it, what with all of the responsibilities of leadership.\n是啊。上次我们谈过之后，我一直在想，你说你会抽出时间去会见你的追随者。在肩负领导重任的情况下还能挤出时间，这让我很惊讶。"

    old "It's something that I endeavor to do every day myself as I lead the Dunemarchers. However, it can sometimes be difficult for me to do as a leader. If I spend too much time with any given family or member of the tribe, I risk being seen as playing favorites."
    new "It's something that I endeavor to do every day myself as I lead the Dunemarchers. However, it can sometimes be difficult for me to do as a leader. If I spend too much time with any given family or member of the tribe, I risk being seen as playing favorites.\n在领导 Dunemarchers 时，我自己也每天都在努力这么做。不过，作为领袖，这有时并不容易。我若在某个家庭或某个族人身上花太多时间，就有被人看成偏心的风险。"

    old "I wonder, do you have the same issue? Or perhaps more directly, do you have favorites?"
    new "I wonder, do you have the same issue? Or perhaps more directly, do you have favorites?\n我想知道，你也有同样的困扰吗？或者更直白点说，你有没有偏爱的人？"

    old "I must admit, there are certain people that I prefer. When you are undergoing a mission and there is a limit on the number of people you can take with you, you have to be honest with yourself about which of your allies will prove to be the most effective party members."
    new "I must admit, there are certain people that I prefer. When you are undergoing a mission and there is a limit on the number of people you can take with you, you have to be honest with yourself about which of your allies will prove to be the most effective party members.\n我必须承认，我确实偏爱某些人。当你执行任务、能带走的人数又有限时，你就得诚实地面对自己，看哪些盟友会成为最得力的队员。"

    old "I have to agree, [protag]. Things are especially more dire in your situation. In my case, my job as the leader of the Dunemarchers is not only to ensure that we have effective individuals to accomplish the tasks of today, but also to ensure that the younger members of the tribe can have the opportunity to get experience and training."
    new "I have to agree, [protag]. Things are especially more dire in your situation. In my case, my job as the leader of the Dunemarchers is not only to ensure that we have effective individuals to accomplish the tasks of today, but also to ensure that the younger members of the tribe can have the opportunity to get experience and training.\n我不得不赞同，[protag]。你的处境尤其严峻。就我而言，作为 Dunemarchers 的领袖，我的职责不仅是确保我们有得力的人手来完成当下的任务，还要确保部落里的年轻成员有机会积累经验和接受训练。"

    old "Sometimes, I intentionally pick someone to do a task that they are unsuited to, simply based on the value of what they will learn from the experience. But you don't have the same luxury."
    new "Sometimes, I intentionally pick someone to do a task that they are unsuited to, simply based on the value of what they will learn from the experience. But you don't have the same luxury.\n有时，我会故意挑一个人去做他不擅长的任务，仅仅是因为看重他能从这次经历中学到的东西。可你没有这种奢侈。"

    old "In my case, I can take a long-term view. I have to consider the question of what will be best for my tribe a year from now, or even a decade in the future. But your deadlines are urgent. The next full moon draws near. You need people who are strong now."
    new "In my case, I can take a long-term view. I have to consider the question of what will be best for my tribe a year from now, or even a decade in the future. But your deadlines are urgent. The next full moon draws near. You need people who are strong now.\n就我而言，我可以从长远考虑。我必须思考，一年之后，乃至未来十年，什么对我的部落最有利。但你的期限迫在眉睫。下一个满月越来越近。你需要的是现在就足够强大的人。"

    old "I can see why you would want to spend time with your followers."
    new "I can see why you would want to spend time with your followers.\n我明白你为什么想和追随者共度时光了。"

    old "And I must say, I hope that you judge me to be worthy to follow you into the most important battles. I know that there are many others who could could take up that mantle."
    new "And I must say, I hope that you judge me to be worthy to follow you into the most important battles. I know that there are many others who could could take up that mantle.\n而且我必须说，我希望你能判定我配得上随你奔赴最关键的战场。我知道还有很多人可以担起这份职责。"

    old "All I ask is that you do your best, Larik."
    new "All I ask is that you do your best, Larik.\n我只要求你尽力而为，Larik。"

    old "I try to see everyone equally."
    new "I try to see everyone equally.\n我尽量平等地看待每一个人。"

    old "Now, that's interesting to hear you say. How can everyone be equal in your eyes? Clearly, there are people who are more effective than others."
    new "Now, that's interesting to hear you say. How can everyone be equal in your eyes? Clearly, there are people who are more effective than others.\n哦，听你这么说倒有意思。在你眼里，每个人怎么可能都一样？显然，有些人就是比另一些人更得力。"

    old "Different people have different strengths and weaknesses. How 'effective' someone is in combat can be a difficult thing to quantify. Does a healer contribute more to a team's victory than a warrior? Does a fast fighter with low stamina have more value than a slower-moving warrior with more stamina?"
    new "Different people have different strengths and weaknesses. How 'effective' someone is in combat can be a difficult thing to quantify. Does a healer contribute more to a team's victory than a warrior? Does a fast fighter with low stamina have more value than a slower-moving warrior with more stamina?\n不同的人有不同的长处和短处。一个人在战斗中究竟有多‘得力’，是很难量化的。治疗者对团队胜利的贡献就一定比战士大吗？一个体力差但动作快的战士，就一定比行动慢、体力更充沛的战士更有价值吗？"

    old "I often ask myself the question of whether it's better for a sword fighter to wear light armor to give them freedom of movement, or heavy armor to give them better protection. And oftentimes, there is no clear answer."
    new "I often ask myself the question of whether it's better for a sword fighter to wear light armor to give them freedom of movement, or heavy armor to give them better protection. And oftentimes, there is no clear answer.\n我常常问自己，剑士是穿轻甲以换取行动自由更好，还是穿重甲以获得更好的防护更好。而很多时候，并没有明确的答案。"

    old "Depending on the situation, different people will be more effective than others. But that doesn't mean they are 'better.'"
    new "Depending on the situation, different people will be more effective than others. But that doesn't mean they are 'better.'\n视情况而定，总会有某些人比其他人更得力。但这并不意味着他们就‘更优秀’。"

    old "It depends on the situation. That's why I try to involve everyone. Different tasks call for different people."
    new "It depends on the situation. That's why I try to involve everyone. Different tasks call for different people.\n这要视情况而定。所以我尽量让每个人都参与进来。不同的任务需要不同的人。"

    old "Well said, [protag]. Spending time with someone seems like a good way to discover their weaknesses and strengths."
    new "Well said, [protag]. Spending time with someone seems like a good way to discover their weaknesses and strengths.\n说得好，[protag]。和一个人共处，似乎是了解其弱点和长处的好办法。"

    old "I must admit, though I do admire your capabilities as a leader, I do have to wonder how many of them I should adopt myself. You and I are different, in many ways."
    new "I must admit, though I do admire your capabilities as a leader, I do have to wonder how many of them I should adopt myself. You and I are different, in many ways.\n我必须承认，虽然我很钦佩你的领导才能，但我也确实会想，其中有多少是我自己也该学习的。你和我，在许多方面都不同。"

    old "You and I both lead tribes, in a sense. But in my tribe, people are born into it. From the moment that they leave the womb, a Dunemarcher is a Dunemarcher."
    new "You and I both lead tribes, in a sense. But in my tribe, people are born into it. From the moment that they leave the womb, a Dunemarcher is a Dunemarcher.\n从某种意义上说，你我都领导着各自的部落。但在我的部落里，人们生来便是其中一员。从离开娘胎的那一刻起，一个 Dunemarcher 就是 Dunemarcher。"

    old "Even before they have the ability to actually march. Or walk."
    new "Even before they have the ability to actually march. Or walk.\n甚至在他们还不会行军、连走路都不会的时候。"

    old "Yes, even an infant who can't stand can call himself a Dunemarcher. Well, maybe the infant even lacks the ability to speak and call itself a Dunemarcher, but you understand my meaning, yes? Many of the people who follow me did not choose me as their leader. I was anointed by our tribe's elders."
    new "Yes, even an infant who can't stand can call himself a Dunemarcher. Well, maybe the infant even lacks the ability to speak and call itself a Dunemarcher, but you understand my meaning, yes? Many of the people who follow me did not choose me as their leader. I was anointed by our tribe's elders.\n是的，甚至一个还站不起来的婴儿都能称自己是 Dunemarcher。好吧，也许婴儿连说话、自称 Dunemarcher 的能力都没有，但你明白我的意思，对吧？许多追随我的人并不是选我当领袖的。我是由我们部落的长老们任命的。"

    old "You, on the other hand, need to win the loyalty of your followers. You go out into the world, find capable people to serve your cause, and tell them, 'Come with me.' When I think about how you approached me, the idea of doing the same thing myself seems very odd. In a way, I am envious of your talents."
    new "You, on the other hand, need to win the loyalty of your followers. You go out into the world, find capable people to serve your cause, and tell them, 'Come with me.' When I think about how you approached me, the idea of doing the same thing myself seems very odd. In a way, I am envious of your talents.\n而你则不同，你需要赢得追随者的忠诚。你走向世界，找到有能力的人来为你的事业效力，然后告诉他们：‘跟我走。’每当我想到你是如何来接近我的，就会觉得让我自己做同样的事会非常别扭。从某种意义上说，我很羡慕你的才能。"

    old "Larik."
    new "Larik.\nLarik。"

    old "[protag]. It's good to see you. I've actually been thinking a bit about you, recently. Or at least, our mission."
    new "[protag]. It's good to see you. I've actually been thinking a bit about you, recently. Or at least, our mission.\n[protag]。很高兴见到你。其实我最近一直在想你，至少是在想我们的使命。"

    old "What have you been thinking about in particular?"
    new "What have you been thinking about in particular?\n你具体在想些什么？"

    old "Well, it has occurred to me that if defeating whatever lurks in N'Mar's castle is really the most important thing I can be doing, I should act more like it. But the truth is, I spend more time doing many other things that aren't related directly to the mission."
    new "Well, it has occurred to me that if defeating whatever lurks in N'Mar's castle is really the most important thing I can be doing, I should act more like it. But the truth is, I spend more time doing many other things that aren't related directly to the mission.\n嗯，我忽然想到，如果击败潜伏在 N'Mar 城堡里的那东西，真的是我能做的最重要的事，那我就该表现得更加上心。可事实是，我把更多时间花在了许多与任务没有直接关系的事情上。"

    old "You've been doing other things, such as..."
    new "You've been doing other things, such as...\n你一直在做别的事，比如……"

    old "For example, yesterday I led several Dunemarchers to a jackal nest near our settlement. The jackals had been menacing our sentries, you see, so I decided the best thing to do was act pre-emptively, and break up the pack before they grew in numbers and strength."
    new "For example, yesterday I led several Dunemarchers to a jackal nest near our settlement. The jackals had been menacing our sentries, you see, so I decided the best thing to do was act pre-emptively, and break up the pack before they grew in numbers and strength.\n比如，昨天我带着几个 Dunemarcher 去了我们定居点附近的一个豺狼窝。那些豺狼一直在骚扰我们的哨兵，所以我决定最好的办法就是先发制人，趁它们数量和力量壮大之前把那个狼群拆散。"

    old "Was that really necessary? You said it was a small group."
    new "Was that really necessary? You said it was a small group.\n那真的有必要吗？你说过那只是个小群体。"

    old "Yes, in fact, it was more important than ever to strike when me did. You must realize, jackals themselves are communal animals. They travel in packs. So when you find a small group of jackals, it's likely that they splintered off from a larger group."
    new "Yes, in fact, it was more important than ever to strike when me did. You must realize, jackals themselves are communal animals. They travel in packs. So when you find a small group of jackals, it's likely that they splintered off from a larger group.\n是的，事实上，趁我们当时动手比以往任何时候都更重要。你必须明白，豺狼本身是群居动物。它们成群行动。所以当你发现一小群豺狼时，它们很可能是从更大的群体里分裂出来的。"

    old "The larger groups send smaller groups off to do their dirty work?"
    new "The larger groups send smaller groups off to do their dirty work?\n大群体会派小群体去替它们干那些脏活？"

    old "No, quite the opposite. When a smaller group of jackals fractures from the main pack, it is often because they have ostracized by the larger group. And like people, jackals understand the need for community. So the jackals that are ostracized often tend to be the ones that are the most aggressive and the most likely to kill indiscriminately."
    new "No, quite the opposite. When a smaller group of jackals fractures from the main pack, it is often because they have ostracized by the larger group. And like people, jackals understand the need for community. So the jackals that are ostracized often tend to be the ones that are the most aggressive and the most likely to kill indiscriminately.\n不，恰恰相反。当一小群豺狼从主群中分裂出来时，往往是因为它们遭到了大群体的排挤。而和人类一样，豺狼也懂得群体的必要。所以被排挤出来的豺狼，往往是最凶悍、最可能滥杀的那一批。"

    old "Think about it. If a jackal is part of a large pack, it doesn't make sense for them to target a group of people. There's too much risk of retaliation, and we have the means to defend ourselves. They're much better off hunting smaller prey. Jackals can even eat venomous snakes."
    new "Think about it. If a jackal is part of a large pack, it doesn't make sense for them to target a group of people. There's too much risk of retaliation, and we have the means to defend ourselves. They're much better off hunting smaller prey. Jackals can even eat venomous snakes.\n你想想。如果一只豺狼属于一个大群体，它们去袭击一群人就说不过去。遭到报复的风险太大，而我们又有自卫的手段。它们更该去猎杀更小的猎物。豺狼甚至能吃毒蛇。"

    old "Trying to make a meal out of a venemous snake seems dangerous."
    new "Trying to make a meal out of a venemous snake seems dangerous.\n想把毒蛇做成一顿饭，听起来很危险。"

    old "The snake's venom is all in their fangs, so it's not the eating itself that is a danger."
    new "The snake's venom is all in their fangs, so it's not the eating itself that is a danger.\n蛇的毒液全在毒牙里，所以危险并不在于吃蛇本身。"

    old "Yes, I'm aware of that, but the risk of being bitten seems...well, it's certainly something I would consider."
    new "Yes, I'm aware of that, but the risk of being bitten seems...well, it's certainly something I would consider.\n对，这我知道，但被咬的风险似乎……嗯，反正我肯定会把这点考虑进去。"

    old "A venomous snake's bite is intended to incapacitate smaller prey. It won't be enough to kill a jackal. The jackal might get sick, but it won't die."
    new "A venomous snake's bite is intended to incapacitate smaller prey. It won't be enough to kill a jackal. The jackal might get sick, but it won't die.\n毒蛇的咬伤是为了让更小的猎物失去行动能力。那点毒还不足以杀死一只豺狼。豺狼也许会不舒服，但它不会死。"

    old "A person with a spear, however, is very likely to pose a mortal threat to a jackal."
    new "A person with a spear, however, is very likely to pose a mortal threat to a jackal.\n然而，一个手持长矛的人，却很可能对豺狼构成致命威胁。"

    old "That is why, when jackals begin menacing our settlement, that we feel the need to be so aggressive about defending ourselves."
    new "That is why, when jackals begin menacing our settlement, that we feel the need to be so aggressive about defending ourselves.\n正因如此，当豺狼开始威胁我们的定居点时，我们才觉得必须如此积极地自卫。"

    old "That's all very interesting, Larik."
    new "That's all very interesting, Larik.\n这些都很有意思，Larik。"

    old "Yes, it's taken up most of my attention lately. But the more I think about it, the more I wonder if I really should have gone myself."
    new "Yes, it's taken up most of my attention lately. But the more I think about it, the more I wonder if I really should have gone myself.\n是啊，最近我大部分注意力都花在这上面了。但我越想越怀疑，我是不是真该亲自去。"

    old "Why would you feel guilty about that?"
    new "Why would you feel guilty about that?\n你为什么会为此感到内疚？"

    old "This is something my people have done before. I could have let other members of the tribe handle the task. But I felt the need to go out myself, to deliver punishment to the jackals with my own axe. Why? I could have left the jackals to my followers while I focused on much bigger problems. Problems like N'Mar."
    new "This is something my people have done before. I could have let other members of the tribe handle the task. But I felt the need to go out myself, to deliver punishment to the jackals with my own axe. Why? I could have left the jackals to my followers while I focused on much bigger problems. Problems like N'Mar.\n这件事我的族人以前也做过。我本可以让部落里的其他人去处理。但我就是觉得自己得亲自出马，用我自己的斧头去教训那些豺狼。为什么？我本可以把豺狼交给我的追随者，自己专心应付更大的难题。像 N'Mar 那样的难题。"

    old "Larik, you going out to kill those jackals {i}was{/i} doing your duty for N'Mar."
    new "Larik, you going out to kill those jackals {i}was{/i} doing your duty for N'Mar.\nLarik，你出去杀掉那些豺狼，{i}就是{/i}在为 N'Mar 尽你的职责。"

    old "I don't understand."
    new "I don't understand.\n我不明白。"

    old "If you want to be an effective tool of destruction against the undead, you need to keep your warrior's instinct sharp. I can't think of a better way to do that than by slaying jackals."
    new "If you want to be an effective tool of destruction against the undead, you need to keep your warrior's instinct sharp. I can't think of a better way to do that than by slaying jackals.\n如果你想成为对付亡灵的一件得力毁灭工具，就得保持战士的敏锐本能。我想不出比猎杀豺狼更好的办法了。"

    old "But I could have been off in N'Mar, fighting shambling undead."
    new "But I could have been off in N'Mar, fighting shambling undead.\n可我本可以去 N'Mar，和蹒跚的亡灵战斗。"

    old "I don't think so, Larik. I think that N'Mar is your proving ground. I think it's where your mettle will be tested."
    new "I don't think so, Larik. I think that N'Mar is your proving ground. I think it's where your mettle will be tested.\n我不这么认为，Larik。我觉得 N'Mar 是你的试炼场。那里才是检验你成色的地方。"

    old "But I think this desert has much to teach you about being a warrior, and I think that it will continue to be a place where you can learn new lessons. You may pick up new skills in N'Mar, but also treat the desert as a place where you can improve yourself for the battle that lies ahead."
    new "But I think this desert has much to teach you about being a warrior, and I think that it will continue to be a place where you can learn new lessons. You may pick up new skills in N'Mar, but also treat the desert as a place where you can improve yourself for the battle that lies ahead.\n但我认为，这片沙漠能教你许多关于如何做一名战士的道理，它还会继续成为你学到新东西的地方。你在 N'Mar 也许能学到新本领，但也请把沙漠当作一个让你为将来的战斗提升自己的地方。"

    old "Actually, this is why I travel alone, most of the time. The people that I fight alongside have their own lives to attend to. And oftentimes, simply allowing them to live their own lives, with a bit of suggestion and interaction from me, is a way that they can come up with new skills to bring to the battlefield."
    new "Actually, this is why I travel alone, most of the time. The people that I fight alongside have their own lives to attend to. And oftentimes, simply allowing them to live their own lives, with a bit of suggestion and interaction from me, is a way that they can come up with new skills to bring to the battlefield.\n其实，这就是我大多数时候独自旅行的原因。与我并肩作战的人，都有各自的生活要顾。而很多时候，只要让他们过自己的生活，再配上我一点点的建议和互动，他们就能琢磨出可以带上战场的新本领。"

    old "I see. You say that you give them instruction? Do you lay out a training regimen for them?"
    new "I see. You say that you give them instruction? Do you lay out a training regimen for them?\n我明白了。你说你会指导他们？你会为他们安排一套训练方案吗？"

    old "No, nothing quite so rigid as that. I let them decide what to do, albeit with a small amount of suggestion and guidance from time to time. Followers, even simple footsoldiers, can be creative people."
    new "No, nothing quite so rigid as that. I let them decide what to do, albeit with a small amount of suggestion and guidance from time to time. Followers, even simple footsoldiers, can be creative people.\n不，没有这么刻板。我让他们自己决定做什么，只是时不时给一点建议和引导。追随者，哪怕是普通步兵，也可以是有创造力的人。"

    old "There are times when I've had followers who have come up to me, completely unprompted, to tell me that they'd studied or developed some kind of new technique that they thought would help in battle."
    new "There are times when I've had followers who have come up to me, completely unprompted, to tell me that they'd studied or developed some kind of new technique that they thought would help in battle.\n有些时候，会有追随者主动找上我，完全没人要求，就告诉我他们研究出或开发出了某种新战法，觉得能在战斗里派上用场。"

    old "Interesting. How did you get people to come up with these creative ideas?"
    new "Interesting. How did you get people to come up with these creative ideas?\n有意思。你是怎么让人们想出这些创意点子的？"

    old "I didn't 'get them to come up with creative ideas.' It's something they did on their own. But I think that, in some cases, just being there for them as a companion helped give theme the confidence to take initiative and come to me with new ideas."
    new "I didn't 'get them to come up with creative ideas.' It's something they did on their own. But I think that, in some cases, just being there for them as a companion helped give theme the confidence to take initiative and come to me with new ideas.\n我没有‘让他们想出创意点子’。那是他们自己做的。不过我认为，在某些情况下，仅仅作为同伴陪在他们身边，就能给他们信心去主动尝试，并带着新想法来找我。"

    old "If they have questions, I answer them, but I don't come to them to tell them the best way to prepare for battle all of the time."
    new "If they have questions, I answer them, but I don't come to them to tell them the best way to prepare for battle all of the time.\n他们有问题，我就回答，但我不会老是凑过去告诉他们备战的最佳方式。"

    old "Well, then. I have a question for you, [protag]."
    new "Well, then. I have a question for you, [protag].\n那么，我有个问题想问你，[protag]。"

    old "I'm happy to answer it."
    new "I'm happy to answer it.\n我很乐意回答。"

    old "It's about my own role in the battlefield. You see, when I take my Dunemarcher warriors into battle, I fill the role of leader. I enable my tribesmen to fight to the best of their ability."
    new "It's about my own role in the battlefield. You see, when I take my Dunemarcher warriors into battle, I fill the role of leader. I enable my tribesmen to fight to the best of their ability.\n是关于我自己在战场上的角色。你看，当我带着 Dunemarcher 战士上战场时，我扮演的是领袖的角色。我让族人们能尽最大努力战斗。"

    old "Sometimes, that means leading by example. If they see me rushing into battle yelling with my axe drawn overhead, it inspires them to follow me into battle with the same fervor. When it's time to charge, I don't want my tribesmen to make any risk that I myself wouldn't be willing to make."
    new "Sometimes, that means leading by example. If they see me rushing into battle yelling with my axe drawn overhead, it inspires them to follow me into battle with the same fervor. When it's time to charge, I don't want my tribesmen to make any risk that I myself wouldn't be willing to make.\n有时，那意味着以身作则。如果他们看到我高举斧头、呐喊着冲进战场，就会激励他们以同样的激情跟着我冲杀。到了该冲锋的时候，我不希望族人们去冒我自己都不愿冒的险。"

    old "However, there are times when the best thing that I can do to unlock my companions' potential is to play a supportive role. Sometimes, swinging my own axe is less important than making sure that everyone around me is swinging theirs."
    new "However, there are times when the best thing that I can do to unlock my companions' potential is to play a supportive role. Sometimes, swinging my own axe is less important than making sure that everyone around me is swinging theirs.\n然而，有时要激发同伴的潜力，我能做的最好的事就是扮演辅助角色。有时，挥动我自己的斧头，反而不如确保周围每个人都在挥动他们自己的斧头重要。"

    old "It occurs to me that when I go into battle with you, I won't be the leader of the group. So I'm curious to hear what you think I ought to do with myself."
    new "It occurs to me that when I go into battle with you, I won't be the leader of the group. So I'm curious to hear what you think I ought to do with myself.\n我突然想到，当我随你上战场时，我就不是队伍的领袖了。所以我很想听听，你觉得我该把自己摆在什么位置。"

    old "What role would you rather have me in, [protag]?"
    new "What role would you rather have me in, [protag]?\n你更想让我担当什么角色，[protag]？"

    old "With that deadly-looking axe of yours, I think you're better as a tool of destruction. That doesn't mean that you can't occasionally help a friend in need, but I think that I'd rather have you prioritize on brutalizing our foes."
    new "With that deadly-looking axe of yours, I think you're better as a tool of destruction. That doesn't mean that you can't occasionally help a friend in need, but I think that I'd rather have you prioritize on brutalizing our foes.\n凭你那把杀气腾腾的斧头，我觉得你更适合当一件毁灭工具。这倒不是说你就不能偶尔去帮帮有需要的朋友，但我更希望你优先去痛击我们的敌人。"

    old "Team synergy is important. Sometimes, you have to sacrifice your own performance for the sake of your friend's safety."
    new "Team synergy is important. Sometimes, you have to sacrifice your own performance for the sake of your friend's safety.\n团队协作很重要。有时，为了朋友的安全，你不得不牺牲自己的发挥。"

    old "Obviously, we need to be prepared to slay monsters. But what's most important is that we keep ourselves safe. That means avoiding injuries and being there to help each other in critical moments."
    new "Obviously, we need to be prepared to slay monsters. But what's most important is that we keep ourselves safe. That means avoiding injuries and being there to help each other in critical moments.\n显然，我们得准备好斩杀怪物。但最重要的是保护好我们自己。这意味着要避免受伤，并在关键时刻彼此照应。"

    old "Larik looks at his axe and turns it over in his hands a few times."
    new "Larik looks at his axe and turns it over in his hands a few times.\nLarik 看着自己的斧头，在手里翻来覆去了几下。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. I'll take this under advisement, and see what I can implement in my own training."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. I'll take this under advisement, and see what I can implement in my own training.\n谢谢你，[protag]。我会把你的建议放在心上，看看能如何运用到我的训练里。"

    old "Truth be told, it's actually been awhile since I've sparred with any of the younger warriors in my clan. But I think it's good to try out new things, and make sure I don't lose my edge. I'll let you know if I come up with any creative ways to use my talents in combat."
    new "Truth be told, it's actually been awhile since I've sparred with any of the younger warriors in my clan. But I think it's good to try out new things, and make sure I don't lose my edge. I'll let you know if I come up with any creative ways to use my talents in combat.\n说实话，我确实有好一阵子没和族里的年轻战士对练了。不过我觉得尝试新事物是好事，也能确保我不生疏。如果我想出什么把才能用在战斗里的新点子，会告诉你的。"

    old "I venture into the desert, and I see Larik standing at the edge of the sand dunes. He must have seen me before I saw him, because by the time my eyes focus on him, he's already waving at me."
    new "I venture into the desert, and I see Larik standing at the edge of the sand dunes. He must have seen me before I saw him, because by the time my eyes focus on him, he's already waving at me.\n我走进沙漠，看见 Larik 站在沙丘的边缘。他一定比我先看到我，因为等我的目光聚焦到他身上时，他已经朝我挥手了。"

    old "I walk across the sands to meet Larik."
    new "I walk across the sands to meet Larik.\n我穿过沙地走向 Larik。"

    old "Hello, Larik. You're awfully far away from the Dunemarchers settlement. Do you usually stray this far away?"
    new "Hello, Larik. You're awfully far away from the Dunemarchers settlement. Do you usually stray this far away?\n你好，Larik。你离 Dunemarchers 的定居点可真远。你平时也走这么远吗？"

    old "No. Now, I am but a sentry. Today, a new leader watches over the Dunemarchers."
    new "No. Now, I am but a sentry. Today, a new leader watches over the Dunemarchers.\n不。现在，我不过是个哨兵。今天，有位新领袖在照看 Dunemarchers。"

    old "Larik. You haven't been deposed as leader, have you?"
    new "Larik. You haven't been deposed as leader, have you?\nLarik。你该不会是被罢免了领袖之位吧？"

    old "Me? Deposed? Ha!"
    new "Me? Deposed? Ha!\n我？被罢免？哈！"

    old "Larik laughs a deep and gutteral laugh."
    new "Larik laughs a deep and gutteral laugh.\nLarik 发出一阵低沉沙哑的笑声。"

    old "No, nothing of the sort. Actually, I fought hard to have this happen."
    new "No, nothing of the sort. Actually, I fought hard to have this happen.\n不，完全不是那么回事。其实，是我费了好大劲才促成这件事的。"

    old "You're going to need to explain to me what happened."
    new "You're going to need to explain to me what happened.\n你得跟我解释解释到底发生了什么。"

    old "[protag], the process by which our tribe's leader is chosen has always been one that has been somewhat...fraught. I'm not sure if you know this, but there is no second in command. Not formally, at least."
    new "[protag], the process by which our tribe's leader is chosen has always been one that has been somewhat...fraught. I'm not sure if you know this, but there is no second in command. Not formally, at least.\n[protag]，我们部落选举领袖的过程，一直都……颇多波折。我不确定你是否知道，我们其实没有副手。至少没有正式的副手。"

    old "So who would replace you if you were to die?"
    new "So who would replace you if you were to die?\n那么万一你死了，谁来接替你？"

    old "That is a good question, and it's a question that doesn't have a clear answer. That is what I am setting out to change."
    new "That is a good question, and it's a question that doesn't have a clear answer. That is what I am setting out to change.\n这是个好问题，也是个没有明确答案的问题。而我要改变的正是这一点。"

    old "You see, the way that our tribe works, any warrior who lives to see the seventh decade of his life is granted elder status within the tribe. And collectively, the elders decide who is the tribe's leader. However, the decision is not made until the previous leader is killed."
    new "You see, the way that our tribe works, any warrior who lives to see the seventh decade of his life is granted elder status within the tribe. And collectively, the elders decide who is the tribe's leader. However, the decision is not made until the previous leader is killed.\n你看，我们部落的规矩是，任何活到自己人生第七个十年的战士，都会在部落内获得长老的地位。然后由长老们共同决定谁是部落的领袖。然而，这个决定要等到上一任领袖被杀死后才会作出。"

    old "So how did you become leader?"
    new "So how did you become leader?\n那你又是怎么当上领袖的？"

    old "I was anointed by the elders. I was tremendously lucky. I had, in my childish egotism, presumed that it would be me who would lead the tribe one day. So I spent my entire life preparing for that day, and it eventually came."
    new "I was anointed by the elders. I was tremendously lucky. I had, in my childish egotism, presumed that it would be me who would lead the tribe one day. So I spent my entire life preparing for that day, and it eventually came.\n我是被长老们任命的。我运气极好。早年间我怀着幼稚的自负，就认定总有一天会是我来领导部落。于是我用了一生为那一天做准备，而那一天最终也来了。"

    old "However, the decision came as a surprise to me. The elders never bothered to ask whether I was ready for the task. I didn't find out myself until the moment that they announced their decision to the entire tribe. It was jarring, to say the least."
    new "However, the decision came as a surprise to me. The elders never bothered to ask whether I was ready for the task. I didn't find out myself until the moment that they announced their decision to the entire tribe. It was jarring, to say the least.\n然而，这个决定来得出乎我的意料。长老们从没问过我是否做好了准备。直到他们向整个部落宣布决定的那一刻，我才知道自己被选中。那滋味，说轻了也是让人措手不及。"

    old "I began thinking: what if they had chosen someone else, someone who wasn't ready to take on the mantle?"
    new "I began thinking: what if they had chosen someone else, someone who wasn't ready to take on the mantle?\n我开始想：如果他们选了别人，选了个还没准备好担起这份重任的人，会怎样？"

    old "Perhaps they chose you specifically because they judged you worthy."
    new "Perhaps they chose you specifically because they judged you worthy.\n也许他们特意选了你，是因为他们认定你配得上。"

    old "Yes, that is the system as it has been for generations, and it has worked reasonably well. However, the more time I spend as leader of the Dunemarchers, the more I come to realize just how fragile the thing is. One bad leader could lead the tribe to ruination. Leaders can only be deposed by death, you see."
    new "Yes, that is the system as it has been for generations, and it has worked reasonably well. However, the more time I spend as leader of the Dunemarchers, the more I come to realize just how fragile the thing is. One bad leader could lead the tribe to ruination. Leaders can only be deposed by death, you see.\n是的，这套制度已经延续了数代，运作得也还算不错。然而，我当 Dunemarchers 领袖的时间越久，就越意识到这套东西有多脆弱。一个糟糕的领袖就可能把部落带向毁灭。你看，领袖只有死了才会被替换。"

    old "A leader needs many skills. To lead the Dunemarchers, one must be a warrior. But one must also have an understanding of a person's soul. One must have the ability to look into someone's eyes and see their worth, to be able to speak to them in a way that confirms their trust."
    new "A leader needs many skills. To lead the Dunemarchers, one must be a warrior. But one must also have an understanding of a person's soul. One must have the ability to look into someone's eyes and see their worth, to be able to speak to them in a way that confirms their trust.\n领袖需要很多本领。要领导 Dunemarchers，首先得是一名战士。但同时也得懂得一个人的灵魂。他得能直视对方的眼睛、看出对方的价值，还得能用一种赢得信任的方式与他们交谈。"

    old "I'm sorry, I must sound as though I'm talking nonsense."
    new "I'm sorry, I must sound as though I'm talking nonsense.\n抱歉，我听起来大概像是在胡言乱语。"

    old "It may sound grandiose, but I understand your meaning."
    new "It may sound grandiose, but I understand your meaning.\n听起来也许有些夸大，但我懂你的意思。"

    old "The point is that it's difficult to know someone will do the job until they've had a chance to do it. That's why I'm appointing different people, promising indivuals who show potential, and giving them temporary authority over the tribe."
    new "The point is that it's difficult to know someone will do the job until they've had a chance to do it. That's why I'm appointing different people, promising indivuals who show potential, and giving them temporary authority over the tribe.\n关键在于，在一个人真正得到机会之前，很难知道他能不能胜任。所以我正在任命不同的人——那些有潜力的可造之材——让他们临时掌管部落。"

    old "What do the elders think of all this?"
    new "What do the elders think of all this?\n长老们对此怎么看？"

    old "They were surprisingly supportive. You know, I think they're growing increasingly aware of the fact that I might die sooner rather than later. Maybe it will be at the fangs of vampires, or maybe it will in the face of jackals, but they need to be aware."
    new "They were surprisingly supportive. You know, I think they're growing increasingly aware of the fact that I might die sooner rather than later. Maybe it will be at the fangs of vampires, or maybe it will in the face of jackals, but they need to be aware.\n他们意外地很支持。你知道，我觉得他们越来越意识到，我可能说死就死了。也许是死在吸血鬼的獠牙下，也许是死在豺狼面前，但总归得让他们心里有数。"

    old "Delegating responsibility has actually been somewhat refreshing for me. Letting someone else take care of day-to-day affairs has freed me up."
    new "Delegating responsibility has actually been somewhat refreshing for me. Letting someone else take care of day-to-day affairs has freed me up.\n把责任分派出去，对我来说反倒有些焕然一新。让别人去打理日常事务，我一下子轻松了不少。"

    old "What are you doing with all your newfound spare time?"
    new "What are you doing with all your newfound spare time?\n那你多出来的这些空闲时间都在做什么？"

    old "I've been spending a lot of time alone with my thoughts. I've been thinking especially about how it is that our tribe has, in the past, always managed to have a good leader. Why do you think that is?"
    new "I've been spending a lot of time alone with my thoughts. I've been thinking especially about how it is that our tribe has, in the past, always managed to have a good leader. Why do you think that is?\n我花了很多时间独自思考。我尤其在想，我们部落在过去为何总能拥有一位好领袖。你觉得是为什么呢？"

    old "What is it that makes someone a great leader? Is it something they're born with, meaning it's simply a matter of the elders sensing who among the most worthy? Or is there something about leadership itself that makes people great? Does simply being burdened with responsibility force them to become the strongest versions of themselves?"
    new "What is it that makes someone a great leader? Is it something they're born with, meaning it's simply a matter of the elders sensing who among the most worthy? Or is there something about leadership itself that makes people great? Does simply being burdened with responsibility force them to become the strongest versions of themselves?\n究竟是什么让一个人成为伟大的领袖？是天生如此吗，也就是说，只是长老们能察觉到谁最配得上？还是说领导这件事本身就能让人变得伟大？仅仅是被责任压身，就会迫使他们成为最强大的自己吗？"

    old "Leadership is something that you're born with."
    new "Leadership is something that you're born with.\n领导才能是天生的。"

    old "You came out of the womb a leader?"
    new "You came out of the womb a leader?\n你一出生就是领袖？"

    old "It sounds absurd when you frame it that way, but yes, I think that all of the attributes that made me who I am, including my capabilities as a leader, are things that I was born with."
    new "It sounds absurd when you frame it that way, but yes, I think that all of the attributes that made me who I am, including my capabilities as a leader, are things that I was born with.\n这么一说确实挺荒谬，不过没错，我认为造就今天这个我的所有特质，包括我的领导才能，都是与生俱来的。"

    old "Over time, certain talents get honed, and some innate talents may never be discovered. But you can't take someone who wasn't born to lead and force them into that position."
    new "Over time, certain talents get honed, and some innate talents may never be discovered. But you can't take someone who wasn't born to lead and force them into that position.\n随着时间推移，有些才能会得到磨砺，也有些天生的才能可能永远不被发现。但你没法把一个天生不是领袖的人硬塞到那个位置上。"

    old "An interesting position to take, [protag]. And a slightly disturbing one, since it would make it seem as though the consequences of choosing the wrong leader would be quite dire."
    new "An interesting position to take, [protag]. And a slightly disturbing one, since it would make it seem as though the consequences of choosing the wrong leader would be quite dire.\n有意思的立场，[protag]。而且多少有点令人不安，因为照这么说，选错领袖的后果会相当可怕。"

    old "I don't think leadership is an innate talent. I think it's a skill. It's something that you can learn. And I don't think there's any better method of learning than by doing."
    new "I don't think leadership is an innate talent. I think it's a skill. It's something that you can learn. And I don't think there's any better method of learning than by doing.\n我不认为领导才能是天生的。我觉得它是一门技艺，是能学会的东西。而且我认为，没有比亲身实践更好的学习方法了。"

    old "So, you're saying that experience has made you the [manwoman] you are today?"
    new "So, you're saying that experience has made you the [manwoman] you are today?\n所以，你的意思是，是经历把你变成了今天这样的[manwoman]？"

    old "Yes. I like to think that I'm doing a good job now, but when I was first tasked with gathering people from across the land to unite together and defeat magical menace at the heart of a dark castle, the proposition seemed beyond my reach."
    new "Yes. I like to think that I'm doing a good job now, but when I was first tasked with gathering people from across the land to unite together and defeat magical menace at the heart of a dark castle, the proposition seemed beyond my reach.\n是的。我愿意相信我现在做得还不错，但当初刚被委以重任、要把天南海北的人聚集起来、齐心协力击败一座黑暗城堡深处的魔法威胁时，这件事看起来远超出我的能力。"

    old "Then why did you accept the responsibility?"
    new "Then why did you accept the responsibility?\n那你为什么还是接下了这个担子？"

    old "Maybe because I assumed that I would be able to do what was asked of me when the time came."
    new "Maybe because I assumed that I would be able to do what was asked of me when the time came.\n也许是因为，我认定到了紧要关头，自己总能做到别人要求的事。"

    old "Well, it seems to have worked for you so far."
    new "Well, it seems to have worked for you so far.\n嗯，至少到目前为止，这招对你挺管用。"

    old "There is no guaranteed 'happy end' here. If we want success, we need to work for it. Sometimes, that means making the right decisions and choosing to place our trust in the right people. Other times, it means honing your skills to become the best version of yourself."
    new "There is no guaranteed 'happy end' here. If we want success, we need to work for it. Sometimes, that means making the right decisions and choosing to place our trust in the right people. Other times, it means honing your skills to become the best version of yourself.\n这件事没有保证的‘美满结局’。想要成功，就得靠自己去争取。有时，那意味着做出正确的决定，选择信任正确的人。有时，则意味着磨练自己的本领，成为最好的自己。"

    old "On the subject of 'honing your skills,' I thought I'd bring up something that I've been working on in training."
    new "On the subject of 'honing your skills,' I thought I'd bring up something that I've been working on in training.\n说到‘磨练本领’，我倒想提一件我最近在训练里琢磨的事。"

    old "Oh, you've been practicing with the axe, have you?"
    new "Oh, you've been practicing with the axe, have you?\n哦，你一直在练斧头，是吧？"

    old "In a manner of speaking, yes. But I've been experimenting with attacking not just with my axe, but with my lungs."
    new "In a manner of speaking, yes. But I've been experimenting with attacking not just with my axe, but with my lungs.\n某种程度上，是的。不过我一直在尝试的，不只是用斧头攻击，还有用我的肺。"

    old "Attacking with your lungs?"
    new "Attacking with your lungs?\n用肺攻击？"

    old "Larik takes a deep breath, then lets out a ear-splitting yell."
    new "Larik takes a deep breath, then lets out a ear-splitting yell.\nLarik 深吸一口气，然后发出一声震耳欲聋的怒吼。"

    old "What do you think?"
    new "What do you think?\n你觉得怎么样？"

    old "I think that sounds terrifying."
    new "I think that sounds terrifying.\n我觉得那声音挺吓人的。"

    old "Yes, a good battle cry has that effect. It inspires fear in the hearts of enemies, and it can also inspire courage in the hearts of allies, who know that someone else is leading the charge."
    new "Yes, a good battle cry has that effect. It inspires fear in the hearts of enemies, and it can also inspire courage in the hearts of allies, who know that someone else is leading the charge.\n是啊，一声好的战吼就有这种效果。它能让敌人心生恐惧，也能让盟友鼓起勇气，因为盟友知道，有人正带头冲锋。"

    old "Well, Larik. If it works for you, far be it from me to criticize an effective battle technique. If bellowing will increase our odds of victory, then bellow away."
    new "Well, Larik. If it works for you, far be it from me to criticize an effective battle technique. If bellowing will increase our odds of victory, then bellow away.\n嗯，Larik。既然对你有用，我哪能去挑剔一门有效的战斗技巧。如果大声怒吼能提高我们的胜算，那你就尽情吼吧。"

    old "I was hoping you might say that."
    new "I was hoping you might say that.\n我就盼着你会这么说。"

    old "Larik thumps his chest again and lets out another fearsome war cry. I hear several voices in the distance, whooping back in reply."
    new "Larik thumps his chest again and lets out another fearsome war cry. I hear several voices in the distance, whooping back in reply.\nLarik 又捶了捶胸膛，发出又一声骇人的战吼。我听见远处传来几声呼喊，正回应着他。"

    old "It sounds like your fellow Dunemarchers have come to recognize that call of yours."
    new "It sounds like your fellow Dunemarchers have come to recognize that call of yours.\n听起来，你的 Dunemarcher 同胞们已经认得出你那声呼喊了。"

    old "Call and response. It's such a basic way to communicate, isn't it? And I think that communication makes a team fight better, even if that communication happens on a primal level."
    new "Call and response. It's such a basic way to communicate, isn't it? And I think that communication makes a team fight better, even if that communication happens on a primal level.\n一呼一应。这是种再基本不过的交流方式，不是吗？而且我认为，交流能让队伍打得更出色，哪怕这种交流只停留在本能层面。"

    old "Yes, I have. I've always seen the axe as a tool for aggression. But more recently, I've been considering its possible use as a tool for protection. It's a menacing tool. A tool that can be used to threaten, intimidate, or as I've recently discovered, retaliate."
    new "Yes, I have. I've always seen the axe as a tool for aggression. But more recently, I've been considering its possible use as a tool for protection. It's a menacing tool. A tool that can be used to threaten, intimidate, or as I've recently discovered, retaliate.\n是的，有过。我一直把斧头当作进攻的工具。但最近，我一直在琢磨它作为防护工具的可能。它是一件有威慑力的武器，可以用来威胁、恐吓，或者如我最近发现的那样，用来反击。"

    old "You see, whenever an enemy attacks, be it a jackal, a giant scorpion, or even a ghoul, they tend to leave themselves open, if only for the briefest of moments."
    new "You see, whenever an enemy attacks, be it a jackal, a giant scorpion, or even a ghoul, they tend to leave themselves open, if only for the briefest of moments.\n你看，每当敌人发起攻击，不管是豺狼、巨蝎，还是食尸鬼，他们都会露出破绽，哪怕只有短短一瞬。"

    old "Most of the time, it is difficult to take advantage of that window of opportunity. If you dodge their attack, it's difficult to both dodge and strike back. But retaliation becomes much easier when you are not the target of the beast's attack."
    new "Most of the time, it is difficult to take advantage of that window of opportunity. If you dodge their attack, it's difficult to both dodge and strike back. But retaliation becomes much easier when you are not the target of the beast's attack.\n大多数时候，很难抓住那一瞬的机会。你要是躲开敌人的攻击，就很难既躲闪又反击。可当你不是野兽攻击的目标时，还手就变得容易多了。"

    old "So I've taken to studying my enemies more closely, watching out for the moment when they decide to strike an ally. And when that happens, I can jump in and punish them for it."
    new "So I've taken to studying my enemies more closely, watching out for the moment when they decide to strike an ally. And when that happens, I can jump in and punish them for it.\n所以我开始更仔细地观察敌人，留意他们打算攻击哪个盟友的瞬间。等那一刻来临，我就能扑上去狠狠惩罚他们。"

    old "It's a style of fighting very different from what I've used to. It requires patience and planning. But I've found it to be quite effective."
    new "It's a style of fighting very different from what I've used to. It requires patience and planning. But I've found it to be quite effective.\n这种打法和我的老习惯很不一样。它需要耐心和谋划。但我发现它相当有效。"

    old "A calmer style of combat seems a bit unexpected from a man who wieleds a weapon as large as yours, Larik. But perhaps that will make it just the surprise we need to overtake our enemies. I look forward to seeing your weapon protecting me in combat."
    new "A calmer style of combat seems a bit unexpected from a man who wieleds a weapon as large as yours, Larik. But perhaps that will make it just the surprise we need to overtake our enemies. I look forward to seeing your weapon protecting me in combat.\nLarik，对一个挥着你这般巨大武器的人来说，如此沉稳的打法倒有点出人意料。不过，也许这份出人意料，正是我们击败敌人所需要的。我期待在战斗中看到你的武器护我周全。"

    old "Have you decided when to meet with the team?"
    new "Have you decided when to meet with the team?\n你决定好什么时候跟队伍碰头了吗？"

    old "Not yet."
    new "Not yet.\n还没。"

    old "We should not wait any longer. Queen Karen grows impatient."
    new "We should not wait any longer. Queen Karen grows impatient.\n我们不能再等下去了。Karen 女王越来越不耐烦了。"

    old "I'll do it as soon as I'm ready."
    new "I'll do it as soon as I'm ready.\n我一准备好就去做。"

    old "Hello, Leena. I hope I didn't catch you at a busy moment."
    new "Hello, Leena. I hope I didn't catch you at a busy moment.\n你好，Leena。希望我没挑在你不方便的时候打扰你。"

    old "I'm always occupied, but I endeavor to never be busy."
    new "I'm always occupied, but I endeavor to never be busy.\n我始终有事在身，但我努力做到从不忙碌。"

    old "It means that I'm constantly present, but always ready to drop what I'm doing at a moment's notice. That's a warrior's instinct. You never know when crisis will strike."
    new "It means that I'm constantly present, but always ready to drop what I'm doing at a moment's notice. That's a warrior's instinct. You never know when crisis will strike.\n意思是说，我时刻都在场，却随时准备在一瞬间放下手头的事。这是战士的本能。你永远不知道危机何时会降临。"

    old "What if crisis strikes when you're asleep?"
    new "What if crisis strikes when you're asleep?\n要是你睡着的时候危机降临了呢？"

    old "I sleep with a dagger bound to my wrist. If I'm ever woken, I can have a weapon in my palm within a moment."
    new "I sleep with a dagger bound to my wrist. If I'm ever woken, I can have a weapon in my palm within a moment.\n我睡觉时会在手腕上绑一把匕首。一旦被叫醒，我随时能让武器出现在掌心。"

    old "Isn't that kind of dangerous, sleeping with a dagger? What if it slips and you stab yourself?"
    new "Isn't that kind of dangerous, sleeping with a dagger? What if it slips and you stab yourself?\n带着匕首睡觉，难道不危险吗？万一它滑脱了，你不就把自己扎伤了？"

    old "I crafted myself a leather bracer that allows me to keep the knife within reach while keeping the blade separate from my body. I have no worry of hurting myself. Besides, I don't roll in my sleep."
    new "I crafted myself a leather bracer that allows me to keep the knife within reach while keeping the blade separate from my body. I have no worry of hurting myself. Besides, I don't roll in my sleep.\n我给自己做了个皮革护腕，既能让刀保持在手边，又能让刀刃不贴着身体。我完全不担心伤到自己。再说了，我睡觉也不翻身。"

    old "How could you know that? After all, you're not really in a position to observe yourself while sleeping."
    new "How could you know that? After all, you're not really in a position to observe yourself while sleeping.\n你怎么知道？毕竟你睡着的时候，也没法观察自己。"

    old "My mother trained me."
    new "My mother trained me.\n是我母亲训练出来的。"

    old "Is that an ordinary Amazon practice? Mothers training their daughters to sleep without moving?"
    new "Is that an ordinary Amazon practice? Mothers training their daughters to sleep without moving?\n这是 Amazon 的普遍做法吗？母亲训练女儿们睡觉时保持不动？"

    old "No, I was a special case. I expressed to my mother from a very early age that I wanted to be the greatest Amazon warrior. She told me that if I wanted to be the greatest, I had to be the most committed. She said that if I had what it took, I could start by proving it to her. So I began training from an early age."
    new "No, I was a special case. I expressed to my mother from a very early age that I wanted to be the greatest Amazon warrior. She told me that if I wanted to be the greatest, I had to be the most committed. She said that if I had what it took, I could start by proving it to her. So I began training from an early age.\n不，我是特例。我很小的时候就对母亲说，我想成为最伟大的 Amazon 战士。她告诉我，想成为最伟大的，就得是最投入的。她说，如果我真有那本事，可以先向她证明。于是我很小就开始了训练。"

    old "How do you train someone to sleep in a certain way? I mean, it's kind of hard to learn when you're not conscious."
    new "How do you train someone to sleep in a certain way? I mean, it's kind of hard to learn when you're not conscious.\n你是怎么训练一个人按特定方式睡觉的？我是说，人不清醒的时候，学东西可不容易。"

    old "The body has ways of learning, even when the mind can't. My mother had me sleep on the floor, and placed hot embers on the floor surrounding me. If I tossed or turned in my sleep, my body would flinch away from the searing heat."
    new "The body has ways of learning, even when the mind can't. My mother had me sleep on the floor, and placed hot embers on the floor surrounding me. If I tossed or turned in my sleep, my body would flinch away from the searing heat.\n就算头脑学不会，身体也有自己的学习方式。我母亲让我睡在地上，然后在我四周的地上摆满烧红的炭。我睡觉时只要翻个身，身体就会因灼热而猛地缩回。"

    old "I have to say, that's an impressive approach. Finding a way to train someone to react in their sleep. Was that your mother's idea?"
    new "I have to say, that's an impressive approach. Finding a way to train someone to react in their sleep. Was that your mother's idea?\n我得说，这法子真了不起。能想出办法训练人在睡梦中也做出反应。这是你母亲的主意吗？"

    old "Yes. My mother was not the most adept with a blade, but she was a resourceful woman who prided herself on making the best use of the tools available to her."
    new "Yes. My mother was not the most adept with a blade, but she was a resourceful woman who prided herself on making the best use of the tools available to her.\n是的。我母亲算不上用剑的好手，但她是个足智多谋的女人，最引以为傲的，就是能把手中可用的工具发挥到极致。"

    old "That sounds cruel. Who would surround their own child with burning coals?"
    new "That sounds cruel. Who would surround their own child with burning coals?\n听起来很残忍。谁会拿烧红的炭围住自己的孩子？"

    old "It was done with my consent. If I'd wanted to, I could have stopped at any time. But I wanted to become the greatest warrior. So I accepted the challenge."
    new "It was done with my consent. If I'd wanted to, I could have stopped at any time. But I wanted to become the greatest warrior. So I accepted the challenge.\n那是在我同意下做的。只要我想，随时都能停下。但我想成为最伟大的战士。所以我接受了这个挑战。"

    old "How old were you at the time?"
    new "How old were you at the time?\n你当时多大？"

    old "I was in my seventh year when I learned to sleep without turning or tossing."
    new "I was in my seventh year when I learned to sleep without turning or tossing.\n我七岁时学会了睡觉不翻身、不折腾。"

    old "And to what end was this? What advantage do you gain by sleeping perfectly rested?"
    new "And to what end was this? What advantage do you gain by sleeping perfectly rested?\n这么做是为了什么呢？睡得一动不动，能给你带来什么好处？"

    old "Well, for one thing, your posture affects your reactive time. I sleep with a blade, remember. That blade isn't much use to me if I'm caught lying on my side, with all of my weight on that arm."
    new "Well, for one thing, your posture affects your reactive time. I sleep with a blade, remember. That blade isn't much use to me if I'm caught lying on my side, with all of my weight on that arm.\n首先，睡姿会影响你的反应时间。我睡觉时带着刀，别忘了。如果我侧躺着、全身重量压在那只胳膊上，那把刀对我可没多大用处。"

    old "For another, there are some precarious sleeping places that could prove dangerous for someone whose sleep is not disciplined. Do you remember when we first met?"
    new "For another, there are some precarious sleeping places that could prove dangerous for someone whose sleep is not disciplined. Do you remember when we first met?\n再者，有些险要的睡处，对睡眠不守规矩的人来说相当危险。你还记得我们初次见面吗？"

    old "When I was walking to the citadel. You caught me unawares from one of the towering spires."
    new "When I was walking to the citadel. You caught me unawares from one of the towering spires.\n那时我正走向城堡。你从一座高耸的尖塔上冷不丁地抓住了我。"

    old "Those spires would be a dangerous place to sleep for someone who tossed and turned in their slumber. Roll one time too many, and you'd fall to the ground, and have very little chance of landing on your feet."
    new "Those spires would be a dangerous place to sleep for someone who tossed and turned in their slumber. Roll one time too many, and you'd fall to the ground, and have very little chance of landing on your feet.\n对那些睡觉翻来覆去的人来说，那些尖塔可是危险的睡处。多翻一次身，你就会摔到地上，而且几乎不可能稳稳落地。"

    old "Are you saying that you sleep on those spires?"
    new "Are you saying that you sleep on those spires?\n你是说，你睡在那些尖塔上？"

    old "I did once, just to assure myself that I could. Truth be told, my ability to sleep anywhere isn't a talent that I use very often, especially since becoming captain of the royal guard. I've become much more of a permanent fixture here in the citadel. But it never hurts to have survival skills."
    new "I did once, just to assure myself that I could. Truth be told, my ability to sleep anywhere isn't a talent that I use very often, especially since becoming captain of the royal guard. I've become much more of a permanent fixture here in the citadel. But it never hurts to have survival skills.\n我睡过一次，只为确认自己能做到。说实话，随处能睡的本事我并不常用，尤其是当上皇家卫队队长以后。我如今更像是这座城堡里常驻的一部分了。但多掌握些生存本领总没坏处。"

    old "I like to think of each survival skill as one tool that may one day save my life. You can never have too many of those. But you may one day find that you have one too few."
    new "I like to think of each survival skill as one tool that may one day save my life. You can never have too many of those. But you may one day find that you have one too few.\n我喜欢把每项生存本领都看成一件也许哪天能救我命的工具。这样的工具永远不嫌多。可也许有一天，你会发现偏偏就少了那么一件。"

    old "That makes sense. You know, I've developed a survival toolkit of my own over the years."
    new "That makes sense. You know, I've developed a survival toolkit of my own over the years.\n有道理。你知道，这些年来我也琢磨出了自己的一套生存工具箱。"

    old "Are we still talking about survival techniques, or are you saying that you have a literal survival toolkit?"
    new "Are we still talking about survival techniques, or are you saying that you have a literal survival toolkit?\n我们还在谈生存技巧，还是说，你真的有个实打实的生存工具包？"

    old "Well, both, actually. There is a small pouch of essentials that I take with me everywhere I go."
    new "Well, both, actually. There is a small pouch of essentials that I take with me everywhere I go.\n嗯，其实两者都有。我随身带着一个小袋子，装着些必需品，走到哪儿都带着。"

    old "What's in the pouch?"
    new "What's in the pouch?\n袋子里装了什么？"

    old "Oh, not much of note. A bit of string, for mending clothes in a pinch. Some flint, for starting fires. Some bandages, in case I need to dress a wound. A small knife, too small to be used as a weapon, but sharp enough to cut through rope and vines if I ever find myself in a bind."
    new "Oh, not much of note. A bit of string, for mending clothes in a pinch. Some flint, for starting fires. Some bandages, in case I need to dress a wound. A small knife, too small to be used as a weapon, but sharp enough to cut through rope and vines if I ever find myself in a bind.\n哦，没什么特别的。一小段绳子，应急时补衣服用。一点火石，用来生火。一些绷带，万一需要包扎伤口。还有一把小刀，小得没法当武器，但足够锋利，万一我被捆住，能割断绳子和藤蔓。"

    old "'Find yourself in a bind,' eh? Is that something that happens often?"
    new "'Find yourself in a bind,' eh? Is that something that happens often?\n‘被捆住’，嗯？这种事常发生吗？"

    old "It happened to me once, and that was one time too many. I was caught unprepared, and I swore to myself I wouldn't make the same mistake again."
    new "It happened to me once, and that was one time too many. I was caught unprepared, and I swore to myself I wouldn't make the same mistake again.\n我遇到过一次，一次就够了。那次我毫无防备地中了招，于是我发誓绝不再犯同样的错误。"

    old "I'm quite good at making mistakes, actually. If my only talent is that I never make the same mistake twice, then the way I see it, the best way for me to lessen my vulnerabilities and improve as a person is to make as many mistakes as I can."
    new "I'm quite good at making mistakes, actually. If my only talent is that I never make the same mistake twice, then the way I see it, the best way for me to lessen my vulnerabilities and improve as a person is to make as many mistakes as I can.\n其实，我很擅长犯错。如果我唯一的长处是同样的错误绝不犯第二次，那么在我看来，减少自身弱点、让自己成长的最好办法，就是尽可能多犯错。"

    old "But there are certain mistakes which you can only make once. For example, failing to raise your weapon to shunt a blade that is being swung at your head."
    new "But there are certain mistakes which you can only make once. For example, failing to raise your weapon to shunt a blade that is being swung at your head.\n但有些错误，你只能犯一次。比如，没来得及举起武器挡开劈向你脑袋的刀。"

    old "That's what practice is for. It's true, a steel blade swung at my head could fatally punish me for failing to respond. But if I have the same experience with a dull wooden blade in training, the worst I'll get is a bruise on my forehead."
    new "That's what practice is for. It's true, a steel blade swung at my head could fatally punish me for failing to respond. But if I have the same experience with a dull wooden blade in training, the worst I'll get is a bruise on my forehead.\n这正是练习的意义所在。没错，一把砍向我脑袋的钢刀，会因为我反应不及而要了我的命。但如果在训练里，同样的经历换成一把钝木刀，那最糟也不过是额头上留块淤青。"

    old "I suppose that's true. You know, I never thought of it as such, but most of the purpose of combat training is actually failing. Failing to block blows that would be lethal, if they came from a real weapon."
    new "I suppose that's true. You know, I never thought of it as such, but most of the purpose of combat training is actually failing. Failing to block blows that would be lethal, if they came from a real weapon.\n我想是这样。你知道，我从没这么想过，但其实战斗训练的大部分意义就在于失败。挡不住那些若是真刀真枪就会要命的攻击。"

    old "Failing to win in combat against sparring partners who could end your life, if they were real foes. Each mistake you make is a lesson on how not to repeat the same mistake."
    new "Failing to win in combat against sparring partners who could end your life, if they were real foes. Each mistake you make is a lesson on how not to repeat the same mistake.\n输给那些若是真敌人便能取你性命的对练伙伴。你犯的每个错误，都是一堂课，教你如何不再重蹈覆辙。"

    old "You have an interesting way of looking at things, [protag]. If you spend enough time in this citadel, I may just learn a thing or two from you."
    new "You have an interesting way of looking at things, [protag]. If you spend enough time in this citadel, I may just learn a thing or two from you.\n你看事情的角度很有意思，[protag]。你若在这座城堡里待得够久，我也许真能从你身上学到一两手。"

    old "I came here thinking that things might be the other way around. You are captain of the queen's royal guard, after all. That's not something you can achieve without possessing a very high level of aptitude."
    new "I came here thinking that things might be the other way around. You are captain of the queen's royal guard, after all. That's not something you can achieve without possessing a very high level of aptitude.\n我来时还想着，情况也许正相反。毕竟你是女王的皇家卫队队长。没有极高的才能，可坐不到这个位置。"

    old "I am good at what I do, it's true. And I do pride myself on possessing a large array of unique skills. But you seem like a much more well-traveled, much more worldly person than I."
    new "I am good at what I do, it's true. And I do pride myself on possessing a large array of unique skills. But you seem like a much more well-traveled, much more worldly person than I.\n我确实擅长自己的工作。也的确为身怀一身独特的本事而自豪。但你看起来，比我见多识广、老于世故得多。"

    old "What I'm saying is that you've piqued my curiosity, [protag]. I wonder if you're as interesting as you seem."
    new "What I'm saying is that you've piqued my curiosity, [protag]. I wonder if you're as interesting as you seem.\n我想说的是，你勾起了我的好奇心，[protag]。我想知道，你是否真像看上去那么有意思。"

    old "Well, I hope I don't disappoint."
    new "Well, I hope I don't disappoint.\n嗯，希望我不会让你失望。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Here on business?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Here on business?\n啊，[protag]。是来办正事的吗？"

    old "Not really, although simply being here in the Amazon citadel makes me feel like maybe I should be here on business. Just the structure alone is quite intimidating. I suppose it only stands to reason that a strong military nation would also have a physically intimidating capital."
    new "Not really, although simply being here in the Amazon citadel makes me feel like maybe I should be here on business. Just the structure alone is quite intimidating. I suppose it only stands to reason that a strong military nation would also have a physically intimidating capital.\n也不算，只是单单站在 Amazon 城堡里，就让我觉得也许自己该来办点正事。光这建筑本身就够让人望而生畏的。我想，一个军事强国的都城如此气势逼人，也自有其道理。"

    old "[protag], do you know what makes the Amazons the greatest military race on the whole Aravorn?"
    new "[protag], do you know what makes the Amazons the greatest military race on the whole Aravorn?\n[protag]，你知道是什么让 Amazons 成为整个 Aravorn 最强大的军事民族吗？"

    old "You're great fighters. It's just good logical sense that the best fighters would decide the outcome of any battle."
    new "You're great fighters. It's just good logical sense that the best fighters would decide the outcome of any battle.\n你们是了不起的战士。最优秀的战士能决定任何一场战斗的胜负，这是再简单不过的道理。"

    old "We are great fighters [protag], but I'm sure you recall how it is that you and I came to be on speaking terms. Am I wrong?"
    new "We are great fighters [protag], but I'm sure you recall how it is that you and I came to be on speaking terms. Am I wrong?\n我们是了不起的战士，[protag]，但我相信你还记得，你我是怎么搭上话的。我没说错吧？"

    old "Well, we share a goal. We both want to see N'mar rid of the stuff of nightmares."
    new "Well, we share a goal. We both want to see N'mar rid of the stuff of nightmares.\n嗯，我们目标一致。我们都想让 N'mar 摆脱那些噩梦般的祸害。"

    old "If having the best fighters were all that mattered in a military conflict, do you think that my people would need to work together with your people to assault the Castle of N'mar?"
    new "If having the best fighters were all that mattered in a military conflict, do you think that my people would need to work together with your people to assault the Castle of N'mar?\n如果在一场军事冲突里，只要拥有最优秀的战士就够了，那你觉得，我的人民还需要和你的人民联手，去攻打 N'mar 城堡吗？"

    old "No, probably not. But you need Grimoire's help. And Grimoire needs yours."
    new "No, probably not. But you need Grimoire's help. And Grimoire needs yours.\n不，大概不需要。但你需要 Grimoire 的帮助。而 Grimoire 也需要你的帮助。"

    old "There's more to winning a war than just having the best soldiers. You don't just need the best soldiers, you need a lot of them. And those soldiers need to be supplied. And making sure that your armies are supplied even when they enter enemy territory requires logistical planning."
    new "There's more to winning a war than just having the best soldiers. You don't just need the best soldiers, you need a lot of them. And those soldiers need to be supplied. And making sure that your armies are supplied even when they enter enemy territory requires logistical planning.\n打赢一场战争，光有最优秀的士兵远远不够。你不仅需要最优秀的士兵，还需要很多士兵。而这些士兵需要补给。要确保军队即使深入敌境也能得到补给，就需要周密的后勤规划。"

    old "Having the best sword fighters or archers on the planet doesn't mean a thing if you can't find a way to feed them."
    new "Having the best sword fighters or archers on the planet doesn't mean a thing if you can't find a way to feed them.\n就算拥有世上最顶尖的剑士或弓箭手，若找不到办法喂饱他们，也毫无意义。"

    old "So, if it's not Amazon fighters that make you great as a people, then what is it that makes you the most greatest military?"
    new "So, if it's not Amazon fighters that make you great as a people, then what is it that makes you the most greatest military?\n那么，既然不是 Amazon 的战士让你们成为一个伟大的民族，又是什么让你们成为最强大的军队呢？"

    old "Good soldiers win battles, but they don't win wars. It takes a brilliant military strategist to maintain an army, deploy soldiers effectively, and decide which strategic battles need to be fought to win the war."
    new "Good soldiers win battles, but they don't win wars. It takes a brilliant military strategist to maintain an army, deploy soldiers effectively, and decide which strategic battles need to be fought to win the war.\n好士兵能打赢战斗，却赢不了战争。要维持一支军队、有效部署兵力，并决定需要打哪些关键战役才能赢得整场战争，非得有出色的军事战略家不可。"

    old "Exactly. And do you know what the key to good decision-making is?"
    new "Exactly. And do you know what the key to good decision-making is?\n正是如此。那你知道，做出正确决策的关键是什么吗？"

    old "Information, of course. It's very rare that military strategists will exhibit genuinely bad judgment. Most of the time, when someone makes a bad decision, it's because they were operating with incomplete information."
    new "Information, of course. It's very rare that military strategists will exhibit genuinely bad judgment. Most of the time, when someone makes a bad decision, it's because they were operating with incomplete information.\n当然是情报。军事战略家极少会做出真正错误的判断。大多数时候，有人做出糟糕决策，是因为他们是在信息不完整的情况下行事。"

    old "I'd contend that the Amazon's aren't actually the greatest known military force."
    new "I'd contend that the Amazon's aren't actually the greatest known military force.\n我倒要争辩一句：Amazon 其实并不是公认最强大的军事力量。"

    old "Really. Now that's a claim I'd like to hear you try to defend."
    new "Really. Now that's a claim I'd like to hear you try to defend.\n是吗。这个说法，我倒很想听你辩护辩护。"

    old "The Amazons are an insular society. You never have to face an enemy who engages in total war. Your military does an excellent job of maintaining your borders, but the Amazons will never be a people that pride themselves on conquest. The Amazons have military strength, but they don't have military domination."
    new "The Amazons are an insular society. You never have to face an enemy who engages in total war. Your military does an excellent job of maintaining your borders, but the Amazons will never be a people that pride themselves on conquest. The Amazons have military strength, but they don't have military domination.\nAmazons 是个与世隔绝的社会。你们从不必面对发动全面战争的敌人。你们的军队在守卫边疆上做得极为出色，但 Amazons 永远不会以征服为荣。Amazons 拥有军事力量，却没有军事霸权。"

    old "The Amazons are an army. The Amazons are soldiers. But an army is only as strong as the nation that backs it. And the Amazons are weak in that regard."
    new "The Amazons are an army. The Amazons are soldiers. But an army is only as strong as the nation that backs it. And the Amazons are weak in that regard.\nAmazons 是一支军队。Amazons 是士兵。但军队的强大，取决于背后支撑它的国家。而 Amazons 在这方面很薄弱。"

    old "The dwarven lands hold greater wealth, and the elves have a larger pool of possible labor if they choose to harness it, with a bountiful supply of natural resources. The human empire boasts both a large labor force and the wealth to back it. The Amazons can't hold a candle to that."
    new "The dwarven lands hold greater wealth, and the elves have a larger pool of possible labor if they choose to harness it, with a bountiful supply of natural resources. The human empire boasts both a large labor force and the wealth to back it. The Amazons can't hold a candle to that.\nDwarves 的领地拥有更雄厚的财富；Elves 若愿意加以利用，也坐拥更庞大的劳动力储备和丰饶的自然资源。人类帝国既有庞大的劳动力，又有支撑它的财富。Amazons 与之相比，望尘莫及。"

    old "The Amazons have a strong military, and in times of peace, their standing military is the most potent of forces. But if it ever comes time for total war, when every person within every empire in the land is endeavoring to see that their existence is preserved, the Amazons will find themselves quickly outclassed."
    new "The Amazons have a strong military, and in times of peace, their standing military is the most potent of forces. But if it ever comes time for total war, when every person within every empire in the land is endeavoring to see that their existence is preserved, the Amazons will find themselves quickly outclassed.\nAmazons 拥有强大的军队，在和平时期，他们的常备军是最精锐的力量。可一旦到了全面开战的时候，当这片土地上每个帝国的每一个人都竭力保全自己的生存时，Amazons 很快就会发现自己落了下风。"

    old "Riddle me this. If the Amazons truly boast the greatest military, then why is it that they require allies to take the castle of N'mar?"
    new "Riddle me this. If the Amazons truly boast the greatest military, then why is it that they require allies to take the castle of N'mar?\n那你来解解这个谜。如果 Amazons 真拥有最强大的军队，那他们攻打 N'mar 城堡时，为何还需要盟友？"

    old "Well reasoned. But you're committing a grave error in assuming that the humans and other races are strong simply because they are numerous."
    new "Well reasoned. But you're committing a grave error in assuming that the humans and other races are strong simply because they are numerous.\n推理得不错。但你犯了个严重错误，那就是假定人类和其他种族强大，仅仅是因为他们数量众多。"

    old "You assume that the humans, dwarves, and elves are all ready to band together when the bell tolls and total war calls every man, woman, and child to sacrifice for their country. But that's not something that you can take for granted."
    new "You assume that the humans, dwarves, and elves are all ready to band together when the bell tolls and total war calls every man, woman, and child to sacrifice for their country. But that's not something that you can take for granted.\n你假定，当钟声敲响、全面战争召唤每个男女老少为国家牺牲时，人类、Dwarves 和 Elves 都会立刻团结起来。但这件事，你可不能想当然。"

    old "A citizen's willingness to devote their life to the interests of their country is a rare and precious thing. When war comes, nationalism is a resource, and it's just as important as iron or food."
    new "A citizen's willingness to devote their life to the interests of their country is a rare and precious thing. When war comes, nationalism is a resource, and it's just as important as iron or food.\n一个公民愿意把生命奉献给国家利益，这是稀有而珍贵的事。战争来临时，民族主义就是一种资源，和铁、粮食一样重要。"

    old "It takes a very special kind of nationalism to persuade an entire nation of people—including those far, far away from the borders where conflict is being waged—to fight for a cause greater than themselves."
    new "It takes a very special kind of nationalism to persuade an entire nation of people—including those far, far away from the borders where conflict is being waged—to fight for a cause greater than themselves.\n需要一种非常特殊的民族主义，才能说服整个国家的民众——包括那些远离战火边境的人——去为比自己更伟大的事业而战。"

    old "The Amazons possess nationalism in spades. We cultivate it and stockpile it for times of need, just like you would cultivate and store up grain. We know that when the call comes, our warriors will fight for whatever they're called to."
    new "The Amazons possess nationalism in spades. We cultivate it and stockpile it for times of need, just like you would cultivate and store up grain. We know that when the call comes, our warriors will fight for whatever they're called to.\nAmazons 最不缺的就是民族主义。我们培育它、囤积它，以备不时之需，就像你们种植并储备粮食一样。我们知道，一旦召唤到来，我们的战士会为一切使命而战。"

    old "Can you say the same of the human empire? I know for a fact that the elves could never achieve that. Even within their own borders, they lack unity."
    new "Can you say the same of the human empire? I know for a fact that the elves could never achieve that. Even within their own borders, they lack unity.\n人类帝国能做到吗？我敢肯定 Elves 永远做不到。即便在他们自己的疆界内，他们也缺乏团结。"

    old "Perhaps you are right. Perhaps we'll know the answer some day, if that day ever comes when all the world goes to war."
    new "Perhaps you are right. Perhaps we'll know the answer some day, if that day ever comes when all the world goes to war.\n也许你是对的。也许有一天我们会知道答案，如果真有那么一天，全世界都陷入战争。"

    old "Let us hope it doesn't."
    new "Let us hope it doesn't.\n但愿没有那一天。"

    old "The thing that makes the Amazons great as a military isn't our weapons, or our fighters. It's our griffons."
    new "The thing that makes the Amazons great as a military isn't our weapons, or our fighters. It's our griffons.\n让 Amazons 成为军事强者的，不是我们的武器，也不是我们的战士。是我们的狮鹫。"

    old "Griffons are that powerful?"
    new "Griffons are that powerful?\n狮鹫有那么强大？"

    old "Griffons are powerful. But not in the way that most people think."
    new "Griffons are powerful. But not in the way that most people think.\n狮鹫确实强大。但强的方式，和大多数人想的不一样。"

    old "Have you ever taken a ride on the back of a griffon?"
    new "Have you ever taken a ride on the back of a griffon?\n你骑过狮鹫吗？"

    old "I haven't. I imagine most people haven't."
    new "I haven't. I imagine most people haven't.\n没有。我想大多数人也没骑过。"

    old "Well, since you've never had the experience of flight, I'd like to ask, what do you suppose it's like to ride on the back of a griffon?"
    new "Well, since you've never had the experience of flight, I'd like to ask, what do you suppose it's like to ride on the back of a griffon?\n嗯，既然你从没体验过飞行，我倒想问问，你觉得骑在狮鹫背上会是什么感觉？"

    old "It must be terrifying."
    new "It must be terrifying.\n一定很吓人。"

    old "What about it seems scary?"
    new "What about it seems scary?\n哪里让你觉得可怕？"

    old "Well, looking down on the world from that height. I've never been someone who's weak of will, but standing at the edge of a cliff can be enough to give me chills. I can't imagine what it's like to look down from the back of a bird."
    new "Well, looking down on the world from that height. I've never been someone who's weak of will, but standing at the edge of a cliff can be enough to give me chills. I can't imagine what it's like to look down from the back of a bird.\n嗯，从那样的高度俯瞰世界。我从来不是意志薄弱的人，但站在悬崖边上都能让我脊背发凉。我无法想象从鸟背上往下看是什么感觉。"

    old "Do you suppose that birds are scared of flying?"
    new "Do you suppose that birds are scared of flying?\n你觉得鸟儿会害怕飞行吗？"

    old "No, they do seem to be cut out for that sort of thing."
    new "No, they do seem to be cut out for that sort of thing.\n不会，它们似乎天生就是干这行的。"

    old "Well, when you ride on the back of a griffon, it doesn't fear falling. All it knows is flight. And as long as you remain fixed upon its back, you can be just as confident as the griffon is that you will land safely."
    new "Well, when you ride on the back of a griffon, it doesn't fear falling. All it knows is flight. And as long as you remain fixed upon its back, you can be just as confident as the griffon is that you will land safely.\n嗯，当你骑在狮鹫背上时，它并不害怕坠落。它只知道飞翔。而只要你稳稳待在它背上，你就能和狮鹫一样确信，自己会安全落地。"

    old "I can't imagine how exhilarating it must be to fly through the air on the back of a griffon."
    new "I can't imagine how exhilarating it must be to fly through the air on the back of a griffon.\n我无法想象骑在狮鹫背上翱翔天际，会是多么畅快淋漓。"

    old "To feel the wind rushing past you, to explore the sky like almost no one ever has before...it must be breathtaking."
    new "To feel the wind rushing past you, to explore the sky like almost no one ever has before...it must be breathtaking.\n感受狂风从身边呼啸而过，像几乎无人做到过的那样探索天空……那一定美得令人窒息。"

    old "You're right. Sitting on the back of griffon as it tears through the skies is a thrill ride."
    new "You're right. Sitting on the back of griffon as it tears through the skies is a thrill ride.\n你说得对。坐在狮鹫背上、随它划破长空，就是一趟惊险刺激的旅程。"

    old "I bet it's fascinating."
    new "I bet it's fascinating.\n我敢打赌，那一定很迷人。"

    old "What about it seems so fascinating to you?"
    new "What about it seems so fascinating to you?\n哪里让你觉得那么迷人？"

    old "Being able to see the world from up above must be an incredible privilege. I've been all around these lands on foot, and I never cease to be amazed by what I see. But to be able to travel at such speed across the land, observing everything from above...it must be the most interesting thing in the world."
    new "Being able to see the world from up above must be an incredible privilege. I've been all around these lands on foot, and I never cease to be amazed by what I see. But to be able to travel at such speed across the land, observing everything from above...it must be the most interesting thing in the world.\n能从高空俯瞰世界，一定是一种不可思议的特权。我徒步走遍了这片土地，所见之景总让我惊叹不已。但若能以那样的速度掠过大地、从上方观察一切……那一定是世上最有趣的事。"

    old "It sounds like you understand exactly what it means to ride a griffon."
    new "It sounds like you understand exactly what it means to ride a griffon.\n听起来，你完全明白骑狮鹫意味着什么。"

    old "I bet it's boring."
    new "I bet it's boring.\n我打赌那很无聊。"

    old "Why would you think that?"
    new "Why would you think that?\n你怎么会这么想？"

    old "Well, it's the bird that's doing the work. And in most cases, you're just flying in a straight like from point A to point B. You've probably spent countless hours on the backs of griffons. I imagine that must grow tiresome to fly over the same lands."
    new "Well, it's the bird that's doing the work. And in most cases, you're just flying in a straight like from point A to point B. You've probably spent countless hours on the backs of griffons. I imagine that must grow tiresome to fly over the same lands.\n嗯，出力的毕竟是鸟。而且大多数时候，你只是从 A 点笔直飞到 B 点。你大概在狮鹫背上度过过数不清的时光。我想，总飞过同样的土地，也会渐渐觉得厌倦吧。"

    old "I can see how you might conclude that. And your answer is actually more informed thae I would have expected. Yes, I've spent hours upon hours being carried by griffons across the land. But it never grows boring."
    new "I can see how you might conclude that. And your answer is actually more informed thae I would have expected. Yes, I've spent hours upon hours being carried by griffons across the land. But it never grows boring.\n我明白你为什么会这么推断。而且你的答案，其实比我想象的更有见地。没错，我曾被狮鹫载着飞越这片土地，一飞就是好几个钟头。可它从来不会变得无聊。"

    old "Do you know how many times I have ridden on the back of a griffon?"
    new "Do you know how many times I have ridden on the back of a griffon?\n你知道我骑过多少次狮鹫吗？"

    old "How many?"
    new "How many?\n多少次？"

    old "Two hundred twenty eight times. I still keep count."
    new "Two hundred twenty eight times. I still keep count.\n二百二十八次。我至今都数着。"

    old "When I was a young girl, dreaming of one day seeing combat for myself, I heard of griffon riders who could tell you the exact number of rides they'd made, numbering in the hundreds. I thought that they kept track of that number simply to boast."
    new "When I was a young girl, dreaming of one day seeing combat for myself, I heard of griffon riders who could tell you the exact number of rides they'd made, numbering in the hundreds. I thought that they kept track of that number simply to boast.\n我还是个小姑娘时，梦想着有朝一日亲眼见识战斗，那时就听说有些狮鹫骑手能报出自己骑行的确切次数，多达数百次。我以为他们记这个数字，纯粹是为了炫耀。"

    old "I thought that once I had ridden dozens of times, I would eventually lose count of how many times I'd flown."
    new "I thought that once I had ridden dozens of times, I would eventually lose count of how many times I'd flown.\n我以为，等我骑过几十次之后，终究会数不清自己飞过多少次。"

    old "But once I began riding myself, I began to realize how it was that each rider had such an acute awareness of their ride count. It's because each ride is such an incredibly unique and amazing experience."
    new "But once I began riding myself, I began to realize how it was that each rider had such an acute awareness of their ride count. It's because each ride is such an incredibly unique and amazing experience.\n但等我开始亲自骑行后，我才渐渐明白，为什么每个骑手都对自己的骑行次数记得一清二楚。因为每一次骑行，都是那样独一无二、令人惊叹的体验。"

    old "What's it like?"
    new "What's it like?\n那是什么感觉？"

    old "The first time you ride, you cling to the familiar. You look for landmarks that you recognize. Hills you've tread on foot. Spires and mountains that you've seen from the ground. Anything that you can look at with some sense of, 'I know this,' because that recognition is all that keeps you from screaming in terror and awe at the wonder that is flight."
    new "The first time you ride, you cling to the familiar. You look for landmarks that you recognize. Hills you've tread on foot. Spires and mountains that you've seen from the ground. Anything that you can look at with some sense of, 'I know this,' because that recognition is all that keeps you from screaming in terror and awe at the wonder that is flight.\n第一次骑行时，你会拼命抓住熟悉的东西。你寻找认得出的地标。那些你徒步走过的山丘，那些你从地面仰望过的尖塔和山峦。任何能让你产生‘这我知道’的感觉的东西，因为正是这份熟悉感，才让你没有在飞行奇迹带来的惊恐与敬畏中尖叫出声。"

    old "Your first few times flying, that's all that you have the capacity to take in. It takes time to internalize what you're seeing."
    new "Your first few times flying, that's all that you have the capacity to take in. It takes time to internalize what you're seeing.\n头几次飞行，你的承受能力也就仅限于此。把所见的一切消化吸收，需要时间。"

    old "You can see your home from hundreds of feet up in the sky, and then walk on that same ground hours later, but it takes days for your mind to fully realize that the world that you see from up on high is the same world that people tread on foot."
    new "You can see your home from hundreds of feet up in the sky, and then walk on that same ground hours later, but it takes days for your mind to fully realize that the world that you see from up on high is the same world that people tread on foot.\n你能从数百英尺的高空看见自己的家，几个小时后又能走在那片土地上，但你的头脑要花上好几天，才能彻底明白：你从高处望见的世界，和人们徒步行走的，是同一个世界。"

    old "Once you've rooted yourself in the familiar, and you've learned to trust in your griffon and in your own ability to control it, you begin to notice the elements of the landscape that are truly beautiful."
    new "Once you've rooted yourself in the familiar, and you've learned to trust in your griffon and in your own ability to control it, you begin to notice the elements of the landscape that are truly beautiful.\n一旦你把自己扎根于熟悉之中，学会信任你的狮鹫、也信任自己驾驭它的能力，你就会开始留意到这片地貌中真正美丽的元素。"

    old "You recognize the splendor of the Great Forest. The intricate architecture of Hammerhands' tallest towers. The bizarre and grotesque features of the Chzulu Ruins."
    new "You recognize the splendor of the Great Forest. The intricate architecture of Hammerhands' tallest towers. The bizarre and grotesque features of the Chzulu Ruins.\n你会认出 Great Forest 的壮丽，Hammerhands 最高塔楼的精巧建筑，还有 Chzulu Ruins 那怪异而狰狞的地貌。"

    old "You could fly over these lands a hundred times and not run out of new sights to discover. But eventually, even the oddest of things begin to look familiar. And that's when you truly begin to see the world for the first time."
    new "You could fly over these lands a hundred times and not run out of new sights to discover. But eventually, even the oddest of things begin to look familiar. And that's when you truly begin to see the world for the first time.\n你可以在这片土地上飞上一百次，也不愁没有新的景致可发现。但终有一天，连最稀奇古怪的东西都开始显得熟悉。而那一刻，你才真正第一次开始看清这个世界。"

    old "Not just observing the features and facets of the world, but seeing the world as it is: you truly comprehend the enormity of these lands, and how every city you see is only a tiny slice of a massive landscape."
    new "Not just observing the features and facets of the world, but seeing the world as it is: you truly comprehend the enormity of these lands, and how every city you see is only a tiny slice of a massive landscape.\n不只是观察世界的面貌与细节，而是看清它的本来面目：你真正领会到这片土地的广袤，也明白你看到的每座城市，都不过是辽阔地貌上的小小一隅。"

    old "You begin to notice patterns. On a fall day, you might fly over the fields outside Grimoire, and see that the wheat yield looks quite meager. Then minutes later, your griffon's flight takes you over the trade district of Lothark and see that the streets are thicker with activity than they were last year, even before the harvest has come in."
    new "You begin to notice patterns. On a fall day, you might fly over the fields outside Grimoire, and see that the wheat yield looks quite meager. Then minutes later, your griffon's flight takes you over the trade district of Lothark and see that the streets are thicker with activity than they were last year, even before the harvest has come in.\n你开始注意到规律。某个秋日，你飞过 Grimoire 城外的田野，看见麦子的收成颇为稀薄。几分钟后，狮鹫又载着你掠过 Lothark 的贸易区，你发现那里的街道比去年更加熙攘，甚至赶在收成入仓之前。"

    old "After the flight, you reflect on what you've observed, and realize that the two are connected: the merchants are fearful of inflation from a weak harvest, so they are racing to transfer their wealth to whatever commodity they view as the best hedge against it."
    new "After the flight, you reflect on what you've observed, and realize that the two are connected: the merchants are fearful of inflation from a weak harvest, so they are racing to transfer their wealth to whatever commodity they view as the best hedge against it.\n飞行结束，你回想所见，意识到这两件事其实是相连的：商人们担心歉收引发物价飞涨，于是争相把财富换成他们眼中最能对冲风险的货物。"

    old "Eventually, your mind begins to recognize patterns where you wouldn't even think to look for them. You realize that when the northern region of the Great Forest begins to thin, that's a sign that a new great house is being built in Hammerhand, because only noble dwarves would go to the length of poaching that wood."
    new "Eventually, your mind begins to recognize patterns where you wouldn't even think to look for them. You realize that when the northern region of the Great Forest begins to thin, that's a sign that a new great house is being built in Hammerhand, because only noble dwarves would go to the length of poaching that wood.\n渐渐地，你的头脑开始在你根本想不到的地方发现规律。你会明白，当 Great Forest 的北部开始变得稀疏，就意味着 Hammerhand 正在兴建一座新的豪门宅邸，因为只有贵族 Dwarves 才会大费周章去偷伐那些木材。"

    old "You learn how the world is not just a collection of empires, but a single entity with many interwoven and interlocking parts."
    new "You learn how the world is not just a collection of empires, but a single entity with many interwoven and interlocking parts.\n你会懂得，这个世界不只是一堆帝国的集合，而是一个由众多相互交织、彼此咬合的部分组成的整体。"

    old "Flight is more than the ability to travel. Flight is the ability to observe. To learn. To understand. You begin to understand which wars are worth fighting and which you're best to avoid."
    new "Flight is more than the ability to travel. Flight is the ability to observe. To learn. To understand. You begin to understand which wars are worth fighting and which you're best to avoid.\n飞行不只是旅行的能力。飞行是观察、学习、理解的能力。你开始明白，哪些战争值得去打，哪些最好避开。"

    old "You learn which sides will be in a position to reward you if you provide them with aid. You recognize threats to your homeland, and develop an understanding of how to squelch them before they even begin."
    new "You learn which sides will be in a position to reward you if you provide them with aid. You recognize threats to your homeland, and develop an understanding of how to squelch them before they even begin.\n你会明白，你若施以援手，哪一方有能力回报你。你能察觉来自家乡的威胁，并琢磨出如何在威胁成形之前就将其掐灭。"

    old "That is why the Amazons are the greatest military power in the world. It's not because of our strength. It's because of the keen insight that can only be developed when you've devoted years of your life to traversing the land on the back of a griffon."
    new "That is why the Amazons are the greatest military power in the world. It's not because of our strength. It's because of the keen insight that can only be developed when you've devoted years of your life to traversing the land on the back of a griffon.\n这就是为什么 Amazons 是世界上最强大的军事力量。不是因为我们的武力，而是因为那份敏锐的洞察力——只有当你把多年岁月都献给狮鹫背上的旅途，才能培养出来。"

    old "In times of war, there are fewer resources more valuable than intelligence. In a way, I think that you intuitively should already understand this. After all, it's a significant part of how you entered this arrangement as well."
    new "In times of war, there are fewer resources more valuable than intelligence. In a way, I think that you intuitively should already understand this. After all, it's a significant part of how you entered this arrangement as well.\n战争时期，几乎没有什么资源比情报更宝贵。从某种意义上说，我想你凭直觉早就明白这一点。毕竟，你能加入这场行动，很大程度上也靠的是它。"

    old "I'm not sure I understand your meaning. How does the art of gathering intelligence relate to my occupation?"
    new "I'm not sure I understand your meaning. How does the art of gathering intelligence relate to my occupation?\n我不太明白你的意思。搜集情报这门本事，和我的营生有什么关系？"

    old "You're a debt collector, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a significant portion of that job involves finding information."
    new "You're a debt collector, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a significant portion of that job involves finding information.\n你是个收债人，对吧？至少，在卷进 N'Mar 这档子事之前是。我想那份活儿有很大一部分就是打探消息。"

    old "After all, collecting debts isn't just as simple as confronting someone and demanding payment."
    new "After all, collecting debts isn't just as simple as confronting someone and demanding payment.\n毕竟，收债可不只是当面堵住对方、要求还钱那么简单。"

    old "I see what you mean. You're right. Shaking people down is actually a very small part of what I do. In most cases, the critical thing is finding them, investing them, and trying to discern what places they might flee to."
    new "I see what you mean. You're right. Shaking people down is actually a very small part of what I do. In most cases, the critical thing is finding them, investing them, and trying to discern what places they might flee to.\n我明白你的意思。你说得对。实际上，逼人掏钱只占我工作的很小一部分。大多数时候，关键在找到他们、调查他们，再琢磨出他们可能逃往何处。"

    old "And just as you notice patterns when flying over the lands time after time, I began to notice patterns when I went to collect people's debts."
    new "And just as you notice patterns when flying over the lands time after time, I began to notice patterns when I went to collect people's debts.\n而正如你一次次飞越大地时能发现规律，我在上门收债时，也开始注意到一些规律。"

    old "What kind of patterns?"
    new "What kind of patterns?\n什么样的规律？"

    old "Well, some are quite obvious. Whenever someone goes into hiding, they often go straight to their relatives seeking refuge. Nine times out of ten, when someone is apparently missing, I can find them living in the basement of a sibling or a cousin."
    new "Well, some are quite obvious. Whenever someone goes into hiding, they often go straight to their relatives seeking refuge. Nine times out of ten, when someone is apparently missing, I can find them living in the basement of a sibling or a cousin.\n嗯，有些相当明显。每当有人躲起来，他们常常会直奔亲戚家寻求庇护。十有八九，当一个表面失踪的人，我都能发现他住在兄弟姐妹或堂表亲的地下室里。"

    old "Other patterns are less obvious. For example, the kinds of people who are hurting for money so much that they'd fail to pay a debt usually have friends or family members who are in the same situation. And those who are hurting for money can often be easily plied for money."
    new "Other patterns are less obvious. For example, the kinds of people who are hurting for money so much that they'd fail to pay a debt usually have friends or family members who are in the same situation. And those who are hurting for money can often be easily plied for money.\n其他规律则不那么明显。比如，那些缺钱缺到还不起债的人，通常也有同样处境的朋友或家人。而那些缺钱的人，往往又很容易被金钱打动。"

    old "You spend money to get information about your targets? I thought you were the one getting paid to find them in the first place."
    new "You spend money to get information about your targets? I thought you were the one getting paid to find them in the first place.\n你还花钱打听目标的消息？我还以为，你是收了钱去追债的那一方呢。"

    old "Every job has business expenses. The longer I pursue a target, the more I spend on traveling. And my time is valuable, too. Finding a target even one day sooner with the help of bought information is often worth the investment."
    new "Every job has business expenses. The longer I pursue a target, the more I spend on traveling. And my time is valuable, too. Finding a target even one day sooner with the help of bought information is often worth the investment.\n哪一行都有业务开支。我追一个目标越久，路上的开销就越大。而且我的时间也很宝贵。靠花钱买来的情报，哪怕只早一天找到目标，这笔投入往往也值了。"

    old "Do you have companions that assist you in the collection of debts?"
    new "Do you have companions that assist you in the collection of debts?\n你有同伴帮你讨债吗？"

    old "No. I work alone."
    new "No. I work alone.\n没有。我单干。"

    old "That sounds somewhat dangerous. Chasing someone means they can usually expect to know where you are, and you have only one set of eyes. I'd worry for your safety."
    new "That sounds somewhat dangerous. Chasing someone means they can usually expect to know where you are, and you have only one set of eyes. I'd worry for your safety.\n那听起来有点危险。追人意味着对方往往能猜到你在哪儿，而你只有一双眼睛。我会替你担心。"

    old "Most jobs are actually not life-threatening at all. The people who flee their debts run away because they wanted to avoid confrontation. Plus, think about the sort of people who borrow money from a bank."
    new "Most jobs are actually not life-threatening at all. The people who flee their debts run away because they wanted to avoid confrontation. Plus, think about the sort of people who borrow money from a bank.\n其实大多数活儿根本不危及性命。逃债的人逃跑，是因为他们想躲开正面冲突。再说，你想想向银行借钱的都是些什么人。"

    old "They tend to be people who fancy themselves as regular honest folk, and they are driven to break the law only by fear. The really dangerous ones, the ones that would fight you in an alleyway to escape their debts, they're not the type to borrow money in the first place, not when they could just as easily get their money through thievery."
    new "They tend to be people who fancy themselves as regular honest folk, and they are driven to break the law only by fear. The really dangerous ones, the ones that would fight you in an alleyway to escape their debts, they're not the type to borrow money in the first place, not when they could just as easily get their money through thievery.\n他们多半自认为是本分的良民，只是被恐惧逼着才去犯法。真正危险的那种人——为了赖账会在小巷里跟你动手的——压根就不是会去借钱的人，他们大可直接靠偷抢弄到钱。"

    old "So what you're saying is that it's actually a safe job."
    new "So what you're saying is that it's actually a safe job.\n所以你的意思是，这其实是份安全的差事。"

    old "Not precisely, no. What I mean is that I rarely come across the type who are trained in the art of hurting other people. You won't find an assassin or a violent ruffian who owes money to the bank. But otherwise normal people, when pressed into desperate situations, can discover an inner darkness that makes them quite volatile."
    new "Not precisely, no. What I mean is that I rarely come across the type who are trained in the art of hurting other people. You won't find an assassin or a violent ruffian who owes money to the bank. But otherwise normal people, when pressed into desperate situations, can discover an inner darkness that makes them quite volatile.\n也不完全是。我的意思是，我很少遇到受过伤人训练的那种人。你不会看到一个刺客或暴徒欠银行的钱。但反过来，普通人在被逼到绝境时，会发现自己内心的阴暗面，变得相当难以捉摸。"

    old "In a certain way, this can actually make the job more dangerous. A trained fighter has a certain predictability to him. But a man-or woman-driven mad by fear, that's something else altogether."
    new "In a certain way, this can actually make the job more dangerous. A trained fighter has a certain predictability to him. But a man-or woman-driven mad by fear, that's something else altogether.\n从某种角度说，这反而让这份工作更危险。受过训练的战士，行为有迹可循。但一个被恐惧逼疯的男人——或女人——就完全是另一回事了。"

    old "You can't predict how they'll behave. And unlike a stone-cold killer who is driven by premeditated calculation, they can't be reasoned with. The most fearsome opponent I ever encountered, well..."
    new "You can't predict how they'll behave. And unlike a stone-cold killer who is driven by premeditated calculation, they can't be reasoned with. The most fearsome opponent I ever encountered, well...\n你无法预测他们会怎么做。而且不同于那种冷血、步步算计的杀手，你没法跟他们讲道理。我遇到过的最可怕的对手，嗯……"

    old "I'm sorry, I don't mean to bore you. You're an Amazon warrior. I doubt very much that my tales of combat are of any interest to you."
    new "I'm sorry, I don't mean to bore you. You're an Amazon warrior. I doubt very much that my tales of combat are of any interest to you.\n抱歉，我不是想让你觉得无聊。你是 Amazon 战士。我很怀疑我这些打斗故事，你会感兴趣。"

    old "Quite the contrary, [protag]. You've got me interested, and I'll be quite disappointed if you don't finish this story of yours."
    new "Quite the contrary, [protag]. You've got me interested, and I'll be quite disappointed if you don't finish this story of yours.\n恰恰相反，[protag]。你已经勾起我的兴趣了，你要是不把这故事讲完，我可会很失望。"

    old "Well. I was hunting down a man, a stone mason. He specialized in finer stone masonry, and was mainly in the employ of nobles. Some years, his services would be in demand, and he did very well, enough to save away money for future seasons."
    new "Well. I was hunting down a man, a stone mason. He specialized in finer stone masonry, and was mainly in the employ of nobles. Some years, his services would be in demand, and he did very well, enough to save away money for future seasons.\n好吧。我当时在追一个男人，一个石匠。他专做精细的石工，主要受雇于贵族。有些年份，他的手艺很抢手，收入颇丰，攒下的钱足够应付往后的淡季。"

    old "Others, there would not be enough building projects for him to pay his expenses, and he would dip into his savings. Such is the nature of contract work."
    new "Others, there would not be enough building projects for him to pay his expenses, and he would dip into his savings. Such is the nature of contract work.\n另一些年份，又没有足够的工程可接，不够他开销，他就得动用积蓄。接散活的营生就是如此。"

    old "He apparently had a run of particularly bad luck, and needed a loan to cover his expenses while he waited for more work. Since he was a well-known mason with a long career and reputation within the local community, he had no difficulty getting the loan."
    new "He apparently had a run of particularly bad luck, and needed a loan to cover his expenses while he waited for more work. Since he was a well-known mason with a long career and reputation within the local community, he had no difficulty getting the loan.\n他显然赶上了一段特别倒霉的日子，需要一笔贷款来维持开销，等更多的活儿上门。因为他是当地有名的石匠，从业多年、口碑良好，所以拿到贷款毫不费力。"

    old "Another season passed, and he did quite well for himself. And another season came and went, and again, his business seemed to be flourishing. But when confronted by the bank's representatives, he reported that he was light on cash. He would always say something about his money being tied up in the business."
    new "Another season passed, and he did quite well for himself. And another season came and went, and again, his business seemed to be flourishing. But when confronted by the bank's representatives, he reported that he was light on cash. He would always say something about his money being tied up in the business.\n又一个季度过去，他干得相当不错。再一个季度来了又走，他的生意看起来依然红火。可当银行的代表找上门时，他却说自己手头紧。他总是说什么钱都压在生意里了。"

    old "It was at this point that I was hired to settle the matter. I went to his house, and to my surprise, he greeted me at the door. He told me something like, 'I know why you're here.'"
    new "It was at this point that I was hired to settle the matter. I went to his house, and to my surprise, he greeted me at the door. He told me something like, 'I know why you're here.'\n就是在这时候，我受雇去解决这件事。我来到他家，出乎意料的是，他竟在门口迎我。他对我说了句类似‘我知道你为什么来’的话。"

    old "And that's when things got ugly?"
    new "And that's when things got ugly?\n然后事情就变得难看了？"

    old "You might think that. But right out of the door, he was rather amicable. He told me that he was ready to walk out of that house with me, but he needed to grab his coat from his room. He was very...unassuming. I couldn't help but believe that he meant exactly what he said."
    new "You might think that. But right out of the door, he was rather amicable. He told me that he was ready to walk out of that house with me, but he needed to grab his coat from his room. He was very...unassuming. I couldn't help but believe that he meant exactly what he said.\n你可能这么想。但一见面，他倒是相当和气。他说他愿意跟我走出那栋房子，只是得回房间拿件外套。他非常……不起眼。我不由得相信，他说的就是心里话。"

    old "So I told him that he could go get his coat, and he invited me to step into his house to wait."
    new "So I told him that he could go get his coat, and he invited me to step into his house to wait.\n于是我就让他去拿外套，他则请我进屋等着。"

    old "Near the door, there was a kitchen area, where there was a woman, I presume his wife, preparing what looked like a pot of soup. She looked like a very frail, very slight woman. Very pale, with skin that looked soft, like it hadn't been out of the house in a very long time."
    new "Near the door, there was a kitchen area, where there was a woman, I presume his wife, preparing what looked like a pot of soup. She looked like a very frail, very slight woman. Very pale, with skin that looked soft, like it hadn't been out of the house in a very long time.\n门边是厨房，那里有个女人，我猜是他妻子，正在准备一锅汤。她看起来十分虚弱、十分瘦小。脸色苍白，皮肤柔软，仿佛很久没出过门了。"

    old "I noticed that she had a very large scar across her cheek. It was a small scar, like the kind that might have come from a puncture, or a punch. I found myself wondering, how did a tiny woman like this get a scar like that?"
    new "I noticed that she had a very large scar across her cheek. It was a small scar, like the kind that might have come from a puncture, or a punch. I found myself wondering, how did a tiny woman like this get a scar like that?\n我注意到她脸颊上有一道很大的疤。其实是道小疤，像是被扎过或打过留下的。我不禁纳闷，这样一个瘦小的女人，怎么会有那样的疤？"

    old "I offered her a hello, and she averted her gaze downward. Her lips were pursed. It was as if she was frightened at the prospect of speaking to a stranger. I asked myself: what kind of man has this woman been living with?"
    new "I offered her a hello, and she averted her gaze downward. Her lips were pursed. It was as if she was frightened at the prospect of speaking to a stranger. I asked myself: what kind of man has this woman been living with?\n我向她问好，她却把目光垂了下去。嘴唇紧抿着。仿佛一想到要和陌生人说话，她就满心恐惧。我不禁自问：这个女人一直跟什么样的男人生活在一起？"

    old "At that moment, the man emerged from his room, and I reflexively stepped forward to position myself between the man and the woman. Not an aggressive movement, mind you, just trying to place myself in his path."
    new "At that moment, the man emerged from his room, and I reflexively stepped forward to position myself between the man and the woman. Not an aggressive movement, mind you, just trying to place myself in his path.\n就在这时，那个男人从房间里出来了。我下意识地上前一步，站到他和那个女人之间。你别误会，不是挑衅的动作，只是想挡在他的去路上。"

    old "I slipped a hand to the scabbard at my side and took hold of the blade I was carrying with me. It was a gesture of intimidation. Inwardly, I was praying that I wouldn't have to draw that blade."
    new "I slipped a hand to the scabbard at my side and took hold of the blade I was carrying with me. It was a gesture of intimidation. Inwardly, I was praying that I wouldn't have to draw that blade.\n我一只手摸向身侧的剑鞘，握住了随身带的刀。那是种威慑的姿态。而我心里，却暗暗祈祷着不必真的拔刀。"

    old "He nodded to me. He said, 'well, can't hide from the law forever. Jail awaits. Let's go.' And then the woman behind me spoke up."
    new "He nodded to me. He said, 'well, can't hide from the law forever. Jail awaits. Let's go.' And then the woman behind me spoke up.\n他朝我点点头，说：‘也罢，总躲不过律法。牢房在等着呢。走吧。’这时，我身后的女人开口了。"

    old "She said, 'Going to jail?' And I said, 'yes, ma'am.' I heard what sounded like a sigh behind me. And then I felt it."
    new "She said, 'Going to jail?' And I said, 'yes, ma'am.' I heard what sounded like a sigh behind me. And then I felt it.\n她说：‘要坐牢吗？’我说：‘是的，夫人。’我听见身后传来一声像是叹息的动静。紧接着，我感受到了。"

    old "Scalding heat on my back, hitting the bare skin on my arms and legs. The pot of soup that she'd been cooking, she'd thrown it on me. You know, it's the oddest thing, you never expect to be burned by water of all things. But there are fewer things that burn worse than the steam that comes off boiling hot water."
    new "Scalding heat on my back, hitting the bare skin on my arms and legs. The pot of soup that she'd been cooking, she'd thrown it on me. You know, it's the oddest thing, you never expect to be burned by water of all things. But there are fewer things that burn worse than the steam that comes off boiling hot water.\n滚烫的热气扑上我的后背，溅在我裸露的胳膊和腿上。那锅她一直在煮的汤，被她整个泼到了我身上。你知道吗，最怪的是，你从不会想到自己竟会被水烫伤。可几乎没有什么，比沸水腾起的水蒸气烫得更狠。"

    old "I spun around, barely registering the pain in my flesh, and raised my blade just in time to intercept the kitchen knife she was swinging at my head. Our blades hit each other with such force that we both lost our grip, and both my blade and her knife were sent to the floor."
    new "I spun around, barely registering the pain in my flesh, and raised my blade just in time to intercept the kitchen knife she was swinging at my head. Our blades hit each other with such force that we both lost our grip, and both my blade and her knife were sent to the floor.\n我猛地转身，几乎顾不上皮肉的剧痛，及时举起刀，挡住了她朝我脑袋挥来的厨刀。两把刀相撞的力道之大，让我们俩都脱了手，我的刀和她的刀一起掉在了地上。"

    old "I kicked her knife away and tried to grab and restrain her, but she had already grabbed a cleaver from the counter. I wrapped my arms around her, and she swung the cleaver back, catching me in the leg. I swore in pain and loosened my grip on her."
    new "I kicked her knife away and tried to grab and restrain her, but she had already grabbed a cleaver from the counter. I wrapped my arms around her, and she swung the cleaver back, catching me in the leg. I swore in pain and loosened my grip on her.\n我把她的刀踢开，想抓住她、把她制住，可她已经从台面上抄起了一把剁骨刀。我双手环抱住她，她却反手一挥剁骨刀，砍中了我的腿。我疼得骂出声，手上的劲也松了。"

    old "I reached down to grab my sword, but she charged at me with the pot-the searing pot that had been holding the boiling water that had scalded me only moments before. I kicked her in the shin, and she dropped the pot. I shudder to think what might have happened if she'd been able to hit me in the face with it and hold it against my skin."
    new "I reached down to grab my sword, but she charged at me with the pot-the searing pot that had been holding the boiling water that had scalded me only moments before. I kicked her in the shin, and she dropped the pot. I shudder to think what might have happened if she'd been able to hit me in the face with it and hold it against my skin.\n我俯身去捡剑，她却端着那口锅冲了过来——就是那口刚才还盛着滚水、烫伤了我的滚烫的锅。我一脚踢在她小腿上，她松了手，锅掉在地上。我后怕得直打颤，心想她要是拿那锅砸在我脸上、再死死按住不放，真不知会怎样。"

    old "Leena, when you find yourself fighting someone inside of a kitchen, you become suddenly aware of how many things in a kitchen are capable of killing you."
    new "Leena, when you find yourself fighting someone inside of a kitchen, you become suddenly aware of how many things in a kitchen are capable of killing you.\nLeena，当你在厨房里跟人打起来时，你会突然意识到，厨房里有多少东西能要你的命。"

    old "I have been ambushed by robbers on wayward paths, and I have been woken in the middle of the night by the feeling of a blade pressing against my throat. I have climbed mountains, and I have fought ghouls, I have wrestled with snakes, and I have been caught on a small boat at sea in the middle of the storm."
    new "I have been ambushed by robbers on wayward paths, and I have been woken in the middle of the night by the feeling of a blade pressing against my throat. I have climbed mountains, and I have fought ghouls, I have wrestled with snakes, and I have been caught on a small boat at sea in the middle of the storm.\n我在荒僻小路上遭遇过强盗埋伏，也曾在深夜被刀刃抵住喉咙的感觉惊醒。我爬过高山，战过食尸鬼，与蛇搏斗过，还曾在风暴中困于海上的一艘小船。"

    old "But none of the dangers I have encountered in this world could hold a candle to the perils of that kitchen."
    new "But none of the dangers I have encountered in this world could hold a candle to the perils of that kitchen.\n可我在这个世界上遇到的所有危险，都远不及那间厨房里的凶险。"

    old "So, how did that encounter end? You survived, all limbs intact, I presume. How did she fare?"
    new "So, how did that encounter end? You survived, all limbs intact, I presume. How did she fare?\n那么，那场遭遇最后怎样了？我想你活了下来，四肢俱全。那她呢？"

    old "In my desperate flailing, I somehow managed to push her back into the stove, and her apron caught fire. She burned to death right in front of me."
    new "In my desperate flailing, I somehow managed to push her back into the stove, and her apron caught fire. She burned to death right in front of me.\n在我绝望的胡乱推搡中，我竟把她推得撞上了炉子，她的围裙着起了火。她就在我眼前被活活烧死了。"

    old "What a grisly end."
    new "What a grisly end.\n多么凄惨的结局。"

    old "What a grisly woman. Her husband, while this was going on, had retreated into his room. I went back to arrest him afterward, and he insisted that I rush him straight to jail. Once he had been properly locked up in a solitary cell, he thanked me."
    new "What a grisly woman. Her husband, while this was going on, had retreated into his room. I went back to arrest him afterward, and he insisted that I rush him straight to jail. Once he had been properly locked up in a solitary cell, he thanked me.\n多么可怕的女人。这期间，她丈夫一直躲在房间里。事后我回去逮捕他，他坚持要我立刻把他送进大牢。等他被好好关进单人牢房后，他向我道了谢。"

    old "He thanked you?"
    new "He thanked you?\n他向你道谢？"

    old "Apparently, his wife was a criminal of some infamy, though she kept her identity well-hidden from the public eye. She had made off with most of his earnings to fund her own counterfeiting operation, and had been taking money from her own husband to serve as investment capital for her illegitimate business."
    new "Apparently, his wife was a criminal of some infamy, though she kept her identity well-hidden from the public eye. She had made off with most of his earnings to fund her own counterfeiting operation, and had been taking money from her own husband to serve as investment capital for her illegitimate business.\n原来，他的妻子是个颇有些名气的罪犯，只是把身份藏得很好，从不暴露在公众眼前。她卷走了他大部分的收入，用来资助自己的伪造生意，还一直从丈夫那里拿钱，当作她那非法勾当的本钱。"

    old "She kept her husband quiet through intimidation, as she had a considerable criminal network at her disposal. At the time that we arrested him, she had been running no fewer than four major counterfeiting rings throughout the region. She had mistakenly assumed that I was coming to arrest her, and that was when she attacked me."
    new "She kept her husband quiet through intimidation, as she had a considerable criminal network at her disposal. At the time that we arrested him, she had been running no fewer than four major counterfeiting rings throughout the region. She had mistakenly assumed that I was coming to arrest her, and that was when she attacked me.\n她靠着恐吓让丈夫不敢声张，因为她手下有一张相当庞大的犯罪网。我们逮捕她丈夫时，她在整个地区经营的伪造团伙不下四个。她误以为我是来抓她的，于是才对我动手。"

    old "That's a blasted situation. What became of the man?"
    new "That's a blasted situation. What became of the man?\n真是糟透了。那男人后来怎样了？"

    old "Well, he eventually found it in himself to provide testimony that led to those counterfeiting rings being dismantled. That led to a significant amount forgiveness in his sentencing, and he was eventually able to work off his debts."
    new "Well, he eventually found it in himself to provide testimony that led to those counterfeiting rings being dismantled. That led to a significant amount forgiveness in his sentencing, and he was eventually able to work off his debts.\n嗯，他最终鼓足勇气作证，让那些伪造团伙被一网打尽。这为他争取到了量刑上的大幅宽恕，最终他也得以还清了债务。"

    old "All told, he only spent a week in jail. To this day, he's a free man, still practicing stone masonry, with a great deal more success than when his burdensome wife was sapping money away from him to fund her criminal enterprises."
    new "All told, he only spent a week in jail. To this day, he's a free man, still practicing stone masonry, with a great deal more success than when his burdensome wife was sapping money away from him to fund her criminal enterprises.\n加起来，他只坐了一个星期的牢。直到今天，他仍是自由身，继续干着石匠的营生，而且比当初那个累赘的妻子从他身上榨钱、资助她的犯罪勾当时，成功得多。"

    old "That's certainly not the story I expected to hear. [protag], you are full of surprises."
    new "That's certainly not the story I expected to hear. [protag], you are full of surprises.\n这故事确实出乎我的意料。[protag]，你真是处处给人惊喜。"

    old "You're a bard, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a significant portion of that job involves exploring and discovering new things about the world."
    new "You're a bard, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a significant portion of that job involves exploring and discovering new things about the world.\n你是吟游诗人，对吧？至少，在卷进 N'Mar 这档子事之前是。我想那份活儿有很大一部分，就是去探索、去发现这个世界的新鲜事物。"

    old "After all, being a bard isn't all song and dance. You use music to tell stories. And that means having stories to tell."
    new "After all, being a bard isn't all song and dance. You use music to tell stories. And that means having stories to tell.\n毕竟，当吟游诗人可不只是唱歌跳舞。你用音乐来讲故事。而这意味着，你得有故事可讲。"

    old "You're right. As a bard, I spun many tales, and in the process, began to recognize patterns. However, for a bard, the key is figuring out where the patterns become broken. If you write ten ballads about ten different knights, and yet they all sound the same, you've done each of those knights a great disservice."
    new "You're right. As a bard, I spun many tales, and in the process, began to recognize patterns. However, for a bard, the key is figuring out where the patterns become broken. If you write ten ballads about ten different knights, and yet they all sound the same, you've done each of those knights a great disservice.\n你说得对。作为吟游诗人，我编织过许多故事，也在这过程中开始辨认出种种套路。但对吟游诗人来说，关键在于找出套路在哪儿被打破。如果你为十个不同的骑士写十首歌谣，听起来却全都一个样，那你就是对这十位骑士都大大不敬。"

    old "Whenever I am hired to write a song, I look for the things that are unique."
    new "Whenever I am hired to write a song, I look for the things that are unique.\n每当有人雇我写歌，我都会去寻找那些独一无二的东西。"

    old "The great irony is that everyone who has ever hired a bard has preconceived notions about the kinds of heroic feats that a bard ought to chronicle. So they almost deliberately construct their 'adventure' as a cliche."
    new "The great irony is that everyone who has ever hired a bard has preconceived notions about the kinds of heroic feats that a bard ought to chronicle. So they almost deliberately construct their 'adventure' as a cliche.\n最大的讽刺在于，每个雇过吟游诗人的人，都预先认定吟游诗人该歌颂哪些英雄壮举。于是他们几乎是有意把自己的‘冒险’编排成老套的桥段。"

    old "My job as a bard is to pick the gems of truly special behavior. Sometimes, that results in my ballads being very different than the commissioner expects."
    new "My job as a bard is to pick the gems of truly special behavior. Sometimes, that results in my ballads being very different than the commissioner expects.\n我作为吟游诗人的职责，就是挑出那些真正与众不同的闪光之处。有时，这会让我的歌谣和雇主预期的相去甚远。"

    old "I'd feel a bit odd if I were in that position. Someone pays you to do a job, and then you give theme something that doesn't match what they expect? Sounds like a recipe for dissatisfied customers."
    new "I'd feel a bit odd if I were in that position. Someone pays you to do a job, and then you give theme something that doesn't match what they expect? Sounds like a recipe for dissatisfied customers.\n换作是我，会觉得有点别扭。人家花钱雇你办事，你却给出他们意料之外的东西？听起来简直是专招不满的顾客。"

    old "Indeed. And yet I gained a bit of renown for the tales I wove, and judging by the number of referrals I received, my customers were on the whole quite satisfied. But that's not always immediately the case. One of my greatest success stories chronicled the exploits of a man who was quite angry when he heard my song about him."
    new "Indeed. And yet I gained a bit of renown for the tales I wove, and judging by the number of referrals I received, my customers were on the whole quite satisfied. But that's not always immediately the case. One of my greatest success stories chronicled the exploits of a man who was quite angry when he heard my song about him.\n确实。然而我编的故事还是为我赢得了些许名声，从接到的转介绍数量看，我的主顾们总体上相当满意。但事情并不总是一开始就如此。我最成功的作品之一，记述的是一位男子的功绩，而他听到我写他的那首歌时，却气得不轻。"

    old "I think I'd like to hear that song."
    new "I think I'd like to hear that song.\n我倒想听听那首歌。"

    old "I don't suppose you happen to have a mandolin or a harp I might play?"
    new "I don't suppose you happen to have a mandolin or a harp I might play?\n我想你这里碰巧不会有曼陀林或竖琴让我弹一弹吧？"

    old "Unfortunately not."
    new "Unfortunately not.\n很可惜，没有。"

    old "Well, in that case, I suppose my voice will have to do. Ahem."
    new "Well, in that case, I suppose my voice will have to do. Ahem.\n嗯，那样的话，恐怕就只能将就我的歌喉了。咳咳。"

    old "Sir Robin was a knight, quite true\n And though he was devoted\n He was quite a weakling, too\n And hence became demoted"
    new "Sir Robin was a knight, quite true\n And though he was devoted\n He was quite a weakling, too\n And hence became demoted\nRobin 爵士是位骑士，千真万确\n尽管他忠心耿耿\n可他也是个软弱的家伙\n于是就这样被降了职"

    old "I am beginning to see how someone might object to having such a song written about him. Sorry, continue."
    new "I am beginning to see how someone might object to having such a song written about him. Sorry, continue.\n我开始明白，为什么会有人反对别人为自己写这样一首歌了。抱歉，请继续。"

    old "Sir Robin fought to prove his worth\n And be known throughout the lands,\n But since the day of his humble birth\n He was cursed with shaky hands."
    new "Sir Robin fought to prove his worth\n And be known throughout the lands,\n But since the day of his humble birth\n He was cursed with shaky hands.\nRobin 爵士为证明自己的价值而战\n盼着名扬四海\n可自打他卑微降生的那天起\n他就受了诅咒，双手抖个不停"

    old "Now at this time a terror came,\n A drake that fought with fire\n Could Robin then erase his shame,\n And be rewarded by his sire?"
    new "Now at this time a terror came,\n A drake that fought with fire\n Could Robin then erase his shame,\n And be rewarded by his sire?\n那时节一场灾祸降临\n一条喷火的恶龙肆虐\nRobin 能否就此洗刷耻辱\n得到君主的奖赏？"

    old "\"What better way to prove mettle,\"\n he said with trepidation,\n \"than fight that dragon and not settle.\"\n Could this knight save the nation?"
    new "\"What better way to prove mettle,\"\n he said with trepidation,\n \"than fight that dragon and not settle.\"\n Could this knight save the nation?\n‘还有什么比这更能证明胆色，’\n他战战兢兢地说，\n‘胜过与那恶龙一战、绝不退缩。’\n这位骑士能拯救国家吗？"

    old "Sir Robin ran to face the drake,\n and charged with all his might,\n but his hand again began to shake,\n and with that, he scarce could fight."
    new "Sir Robin ran to face the drake,\n and charged with all his might,\n but his hand again began to shake,\n and with that, he scarce could fight.\nRobin 爵士奔向那恶龙\n用尽全身力气冲锋\n可他的手又开始颤抖\n如此一来，他几乎无法战斗"

    old "He yelled in anger, bemoaning his curse,\n his sword clattered to the ground.\n \"This situation could not be worse,\"\n he said, but then he heard a sound."
    new "He yelled in anger, bemoaning his curse,\n his sword clattered to the ground.\n \"This situation could not be worse,\"\n he said, but then he heard a sound.\n他愤怒地嘶吼，哀叹自己的诅咒\n长剑哐当落地\n‘没有比这更糟的局面了，’\n他说道，可随即听见一阵响动"

    old "Behind him, other knights had took up lances\n And they charged toward the beast.\n They yelled, \"If even Robin can take his chances,\n we owe him this, at least.\""
    new "Behind him, other knights had took up lances\n And they charged toward the beast.\n They yelled, \"If even Robin can take his chances,\n we owe him this, at least.\"\n在他身后，其他骑士举起了长矛\n朝着那野兽冲锋\n他们高喊：‘既然 Robin 都敢放手一搏，\n至少我们也欠他这份情。’"

    old "Sir Robin's fellows struck as they called,\n the fire drake was felled.\n And a chant arose amoung them all,\n \"Sir Robin! Sir Robin!\" they yelled."
    new "Sir Robin's fellows struck as they called,\n the fire drake was felled.\n And a chant arose amoung them all,\n \"Sir Robin! Sir Robin!\" they yelled.\nRobin 爵士的同伴们应声出击\n喷火的恶龙被击倒在地\n他们当中响起一片呼喊\n‘Robin 爵士！Robin 爵士！’他们齐声高呼"

    old "Sir Robin never got to swing his blade,\n But still, he can be admired\n For his courage, others came to aid\n because they were inspired."
    new "Sir Robin never got to swing his blade,\n But still, he can be admired\n For his courage, others came to aid\n because they were inspired.\nRobin 爵士始终没能挥出那一剑\n但他依然值得敬佩\n因为他的勇气，众人前来相助\n因为他们受到了鼓舞"

    old "Sir Robin was the first person that I played that song for. I was so impressed by his act of courage, I thought that his actions deserved to be reported."
    new "Sir Robin was the first person that I played that song for. I was so impressed by his act of courage, I thought that his actions deserved to be reported.\nRobin 爵士是我第一个为之弹唱这首歌的人。他的勇气之举深深打动了我，我觉得他的事迹值得被传颂。"

    old "He saw things differently, however. He was upset by the fact that the tale highlighted his complete inability to properly handle himself in battle. He pleaded with me not to share it publicly. And, for the first time in my life, I violated the wishes of one of my subjects and began performing it."
    new "He saw things differently, however. He was upset by the fact that the tale highlighted his complete inability to properly handle himself in battle. He pleaded with me not to share it publicly. And, for the first time in my life, I violated the wishes of one of my subjects and began performing it.\n然而，他却不这么看。这个故事凸显了他在战斗中完全无法掌控自己的窘态，这让他很是不快。他恳求我不要公开传唱。而我生平头一次，违背了自己笔下人物的意愿，开始公开表演这首歌。"

    old "He must have been furious."
    new "He must have been furious.\n他一定气坏了。"

    old "He was, at first. But then he began attracted many fans and admirers, who loved the clumsy-yet-brave Sir Robin. They didn't love him in spite of his clumsiness, but because of it. It humanized him."
    new "He was, at first. But then he began attracted many fans and admirers, who loved the clumsy-yet-brave Sir Robin. They didn't love him in spite of his clumsiness, but because of it. It humanized him.\n起初是。但后来，他竟吸引了众多追随者和仰慕者，他们都喜爱这位笨拙却勇敢的 Robin 爵士。他们爱他，不是不在乎他的笨拙，而恰恰是因为他的笨拙。这让他变得有血有肉。"

    old "As a professional storyteller, there is a constant contradiction that I have frequently observed. People love a hero who does the impossible, someone who inspires them to be better than they really are."
    new "As a professional storyteller, there is a constant contradiction that I have frequently observed. People love a hero who does the impossible, someone who inspires them to be better than they really are.\n作为一名职业说书人，我常常观察到一种矛盾。人们喜爱能做到不可能之事的英雄，一个能激励他们变得比真实的自己更出色的人。"

    old "But people also love someone who is relatable, someone who they can look at and see some of themselves in. It is a paradox: they want someone who is like them, but simultaneously better than them."
    new "But people also love someone who is relatable, someone who they can look at and see some of themselves in. It is a paradox: they want someone who is like them, but simultaneously better than them.\n但人们也喜爱能引起共鸣的人，一个能让他们从中看到自己影子的人。这实在是个悖论：他们想要一个和自己相似、却又比自己更出色的人。"

    old "Sir Robin was the perfect hero. He was the everyman: he had no amazing talents, no impressive abilities. But he did have one exceptional attribute: his unrelenting courage in the face of danger. He inspired people to be better versions of himself. He was both the everyman and the superman."
    new "Sir Robin was the perfect hero. He was the everyman: he had no amazing talents, no impressive abilities. But he did have one exceptional attribute: his unrelenting courage in the face of danger. He inspired people to be better versions of himself. He was both the everyman and the superman.\nRobin 爵士正是完美的英雄。他是个普通人：没有惊人的天赋，也没有出众的本领。但他确有一项非凡的品质：面对危险时毫不退缩的勇气。他激励人们成为更好的自己。他既是普通人，又是超人。"

    old "Many people, Sir Robin himself included, told me that my tale uplifted them in times of woe. That experience, more than any other, has taught me the power of heroism, and the power of a good story."
    new "Many people, Sir Robin himself included, told me that my tale uplifted them in times of woe. That experience, more than any other, has taught me the power of heroism, and the power of a good story.\n许多人，包括 Robin 爵士本人，都告诉我，我的故事在他们困顿之时给了他们鼓舞。那段经历比什么都更让我明白英雄主义的力量，也明白了好的故事的力量。"

    old "An interesting story. I think that much of its significance may be partly lost on me. As an Amazon, Sir Robin hardly seems like an inspiring figure, based on his physical weakness."
    new "An interesting story. I think that much of its significance may be partly lost on me. As an Amazon, Sir Robin hardly seems like an inspiring figure, based on his physical weakness.\n有意思的故事。我想这其中的意义，或许有一部分我是体会不到的。身为 Amazon，凭 Robin 爵士的羸弱体格，他实在很难算得上一个鼓舞人心的人物。"

    old "But I am familiar enough with other cultures to know what a premium they place on immutable qualities like courage and selflessness. I presume, just based on your story, that Sir Robin was a human."
    new "But I am familiar enough with other cultures to know what a premium they place on immutable qualities like courage and selflessness. I presume, just based on your story, that Sir Robin was a human.\n但我也足够了解其他文化，知道他们多么看重勇气、无私这类恒久不变的品质。仅凭你的故事，我猜 Robin 爵士是个人类。"

    old "You presume correctly. And Leena, I don't think that you should discount the importance of courage. As you said, it is an immutable quality. Strength is something that can grow and wane."
    new "You presume correctly. And Leena, I don't think that you should discount the importance of courage. As you said, it is an immutable quality. Strength is something that can grow and wane.\n你猜得没错。而且 Leena，我觉得你不该小看勇气的重要性。正如你所说，它是种恒久不变的品质。而力量则会时强时弱。"

    old "A weak man can be trained in the ways of the sword to become a competent fighter, and by the same token, a strong man can be reduced when stricken down in combat."
    new "A weak man can be trained in the ways of the sword to become a competent fighter, and by the same token, a strong man can be reduced when stricken down in combat.\n一个弱小的人可以经剑术训练成为合格的战士，同样的道理，一个强壮的人也会在战斗中受创倒下。"

    old "That is an interesting view to take. I've always assumed bards to be romantics at heart, and it seems you do have a certain affinity for emotional stories. But you also have a pragmatic side to you as well."
    new "That is an interesting view to take. I've always assumed bards to be romantics at heart, and it seems you do have a certain affinity for emotional stories. But you also have a pragmatic side to you as well.\n这个看法很有意思。我一直以为吟游诗人骨子里都是浪漫主义者，你似乎也确对情感故事情有独钟。但你身上也有务实的一面。"

    old "[protag], what other surprises does your personality hold? I find myself wondering this more every day."
    new "[protag], what other surprises does your personality hold? I find myself wondering this more every day.\n[protag]，你的个性里还藏着多少惊喜？我发现自己一天比一天更好奇了。"

    old "You're a scholar, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a scholar's prestige is based on [hisher] knowledge. That's not so different from the concept of military intelligence."
    new "You're a scholar, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I imagine that a scholar's prestige is based on [hisher] knowledge. That's not so different from the concept of military intelligence.\n你是学者，对吧？至少，在卷进 N'Mar 这档子事之前是。我想，学者的声望靠的是[hisher]学识。这和军事情报的概念倒有几分相似。"

    old "Indeed. It is a scholar's duty to collect, learn, and catalog information. And oftentimes, the most piercing insights come not from gaining new information, but studying known information to recognize new patterns."
    new "Indeed. It is a scholar's duty to collect, learn, and catalog information. And oftentimes, the most piercing insights come not from gaining new information, but studying known information to recognize new patterns.\n确实。收集、学习和编目信息，正是学者的职责。而很多时候，最深刻的洞见并非来自新获取的信息，而是来自研究已知的信息、从中辨认出新的规律。"

    old "It's actually quite similar to what you observed from the back of a griffon. Some find the process of reading texts repetitiously to be a tedious tasks. But there are many texts that I find myself returning to, over and over again, constantly divining new information and insight."
    new "It's actually quite similar to what you observed from the back of a griffon. Some find the process of reading texts repetitiously to be a tedious tasks. But there are many texts that I find myself returning to, over and over again, constantly divining new information and insight.\n这其实和你从狮鹫背上观察到的东西十分相似。有些人觉得反复阅读文献是件枯燥的苦差。但有很多典籍，我会一遍又一遍地回头去读，不断从中参悟出新的信息和洞见。"

    old "I have to admit, I would probably be one of the people to find that idea rather boring."
    new "I have to admit, I would probably be one of the people to find that idea rather boring.\n我得承认，我大概就是会觉得那很无聊的人之一。"

    old "I have to be honest, I have some of that in me as well. As a scholar, I've spent lots of time reading. But I still prefer to observe the world through my own eyes, rather than the eyes of others."
    new "I have to be honest, I have some of that in me as well. As a scholar, I've spent lots of time reading. But I still prefer to observe the world through my own eyes, rather than the eyes of others.\n说实话，我身上也有那么一点。作为学者，我花了大量时间读书。但我依然更愿意用自己的眼睛去观察世界，而不是透过别人的眼睛。"

    old "Many older texts, and even some of the newer ones, are quite lacking. There's a limit to how far you can get in this world just through studying the research of others."
    new "Many older texts, and even some of the newer ones, are quite lacking. There's a limit to how far you can get in this world just through studying the research of others.\n许多古老的文献，甚至一些较新的著述，都相当欠缺。只靠研读他人的研究，你在这个世界上能走多远，是有上限的。"

    old "So why did you continue down the path of being a scholar?"
    new "So why did you continue down the path of being a scholar?\n那你为什么还是继续走了学者这条路？"

    old "I just told you. I found many current texts to be wanting. Some have inaccuracies that are the result of the passage of time, and others are just plain wrong. Clearly, someone has to do something to improve them. Why shouldn't it be me?"
    new "I just told you. I found many current texts to be wanting. Some have inaccuracies that are the result of the passage of time, and others are just plain wrong. Clearly, someone has to do something to improve them. Why shouldn't it be me?\n我刚刚说过了。我发现许多当下的文献有所欠缺。有些因岁月流逝而出现讹误，还有些压根就是错的。显然，总得有人做点什么去改进它们。为什么不能是我呢？"

    old "That's...certainly an interesting perspective. Most people choose scholarly professions because they prefer to work indoors, avoiding the outside world. Or at least, that's what I'd always assumed."
    new "That's...certainly an interesting perspective. Most people choose scholarly professions because they prefer to work indoors, avoiding the outside world. Or at least, that's what I'd always assumed.\n这……倒确实是个有趣的看法。大多数人选择学术行当，是因为更愿意待在室内工作，避开外面的世界。至少，我一直是这么以为的。"

    old "Your assumption is a fair one. One of my early mentors told me explicitly that he became a scholar because he hates to sweat, and wanted to avoid any profession that involved working hard enough to sweat, or even being outside in the summer months long enough to sweat."
    new "Your assumption is a fair one. One of my early mentors told me explicitly that he became a scholar because he hates to sweat, and wanted to avoid any profession that involved working hard enough to sweat, or even being outside in the summer months long enough to sweat.\n你的假设也不无道理。我早先的一位导师就明明白白告诉过我，他当学者，是因为他讨厌出汗，想避开任何会累到出汗的行当，甚至不想在夏天出门在外待久到出汗。"

    old "And that's not to discredit him as a person. He was a brilliant, humble man. He's just not the type of man who I would try to emulate."
    new "And that's not to discredit him as a person. He was a brilliant, humble man. He's just not the type of man who I would try to emulate.\n我这么说并不是要贬低他这个人。他是个才华横溢又谦逊的人。只是，他不是我想效仿的那种人。"

    old "There's certain kinds of knowledge that are impossible to impart through words. I can read about combat all that I want. I can read about how soldiers are trained, I can read about how weapons are crafted, and I can read about the techniques that are used in a sword fight."
    new "There's certain kinds of knowledge that are impossible to impart through words. I can read about combat all that I want. I can read about how soldiers are trained, I can read about how weapons are crafted, and I can read about the techniques that are used in a sword fight.\n有些知识，是无法靠文字传授的。我想读多少关于战斗的书都行。我可以读到士兵如何受训、武器如何锻造、剑术交锋中用到哪些技法。"

    old "But until I hold that sword for myself and actually stare danger in the face, I really won't know what it means to be a soldier."
    new "But until I hold that sword for myself and actually stare danger in the face, I really won't know what it means to be a soldier.\n但除非我亲手握住那把剑、真正直面危险，否则我永远不会真正明白当一名士兵意味着什么。"

    old "There are so many scholars who observe and write about poverty, about the ravages of war, and about foreign cultures without ever having directly immersed themselves in it. There are many economists who have concluded that by all measures, it should be impossible for a properly-motivated person to starve to death."
    new "There are so many scholars who observe and write about poverty, about the ravages of war, and about foreign cultures without ever having directly immersed themselves in it. There are many economists who have concluded that by all measures, it should be impossible for a properly-motivated person to starve to death.\n有太多学者观察并书写贫困、战争的摧残和异国文化，自己却从未真正置身其中。也有许多经济学家得出结论说，按任何标准衡量，一个足够上进的正常人都绝不可能饿死。"

    old "But until you actually live among those people, until you feel hunger for yourself, you won't understand their experience."
    new "But until you actually live among those people, until you feel hunger for yourself, you won't understand their experience.\n但除非你真的生活在那些人中间，亲身体会到饥饿的滋味，否则你永远无法理解他们的处境。"

    old "And even then, even when I immerse myself in the subjects that I study, even when I stare death in the face, or learn from experience what it means to live a modest existence in a rural town, I still won't know exactly what it means to be like those people."
    new "And even then, even when I immerse myself in the subjects that I study, even when I stare death in the face, or learn from experience what it means to live a modest existence in a rural town, I still won't know exactly what it means to be like those people.\n即便如此，即便我沉浸于自己所研究的对象之中，即便我直面死亡，或亲身经历在乡间小镇过清贫日子的滋味，我依然无法确切知道，成为那样的人究竟是什么感觉。"

    old "In the end, I am still an observer. I am like a tourist. But at the very least, I hope that I can taste their struggle, to see it personally for myself."
    new "In the end, I am still an observer. I am like a tourist. But at the very least, I hope that I can taste their struggle, to see it personally for myself.\n说到底，我终究只是个观察者。我像个游客。但至少，我希望自己能够尝到他们的挣扎，亲眼去看一看。"

    old "Perhaps you should give yourself more credit. It's true that you've never experienced true poverty, or at least I presume that. Even if you live like a poor man, you always have the ability stop it all and leave that poor existence behind."
    new "Perhaps you should give yourself more credit. It's true that you've never experienced true poverty, or at least I presume that. Even if you live like a poor man, you always have the ability stop it all and leave that poor existence behind.\n也许你该更看得起自己一些。你确实从没经历过真正的贫困——至少我猜是这样。即便你过着穷人的生活，你也随时有能力停下一切，把那种贫苦的日子抛在身后。"

    old "But danger, threats on your life, those are real. And you've seen more than your fair share of real danger."
    new "But danger, threats on your life, those are real. And you've seen more than your fair share of real danger.\n但危险、生命威胁，那些可是真的。而你见识过的真正危险，已经远超一般人了。"

    old "I find that odd, coming from an Amazon warrior. Surely you've seen more danger than I."
    new "I find that odd, coming from an Amazon warrior. Surely you've seen more danger than I.\n这话出自一位 Amazon 战士之口，我倒觉得奇怪。你见过的危险肯定比我多。"

    old "Yes, but that doesn't make the danger that you've faced any less real. Just look at our current mission. When we go to N'Mar, we will literally be fighting side-by-side. I think that you've seen enough of combat to know what a warrior truly feels when they face an enemy."
    new "Yes, but that doesn't make the danger that you've faced any less real. Just look at our current mission. When we go to N'Mar, we will literally be fighting side-by-side. I think that you've seen enough of combat to know what a warrior truly feels when they face an enemy.\n没错，但这并不代表你面对过的危险就不真实。看看我们眼下的任务吧。等我们前往 N'Mar，可就要真真正正地并肩作战了。我想，你已经见识过足够多的战斗，懂得战士面对敌人时真正的感受。"

    old "You know, you may be right. There are times when I think I'm immersing myself too much in life-threatening existence of a fighter. This certainly isn't what I was preparing for when I was a young student. But..."
    new "You know, you may be right. There are times when I think I'm immersing myself too much in life-threatening existence of a fighter. This certainly isn't what I was preparing for when I was a young student. But...\n你知道，你也许说得对。有时我会觉得，自己太过沉浸于战士那种随时可能丧命的生活了。这当然不是我年轻时当学生所准备面对的东西。不过……"

    old "There's something empowering about learning to defend yourself, or even defend others. It's empowering to not have to rely on others for protection. Of knowing that, even when you're alone and you have your back against a wall, you still may have what it takes to bring yourself out alive."
    new "There's something empowering about learning to defend yourself, or even defend others. It's empowering to not have to rely on others for protection. Of knowing that, even when you're alone and you have your back against a wall, you still may have what it takes to bring yourself out alive.\n学会保护自己，甚至保护他人，是种能给人力量的事。不必依赖别人的保护，这本身就给人力量。知道自己即便孤身一人、背抵墙根，也依然有本事活着脱身。"

    old "They say that the pen is mightier than the sword, but a sword has saved my life more times than a pen has."
    new "They say that the pen is mightier than the sword, but a sword has saved my life more times than a pen has.\n人们说笔杆子比剑更有力，但剑救过我命的次数，比笔多得多。"

    old "I never expected to hear those words from a scholar. You are full of surprises, [protag]."
    new "I never expected to hear those words from a scholar. You are full of surprises, [protag].\n我从没想过会从一位学者口中听到这种话。你真是处处给人惊喜，[protag]。"

    old "Maybe that means I'm a bad scholar."
    new "Maybe that means I'm a bad scholar.\n也许这说明我是个不称职的学者。"

    old "Don't ever stop being what you are, even if that means spending more time with weapons than books, or even abandoning books entirely. The world has plenty of learned book-wise readers already, but there is only one [protag]."
    new "Don't ever stop being what you are, even if that means spending more time with weapons than books, or even abandoning books entirely. The world has plenty of learned book-wise readers already, but there is only one [protag].\n永远不要停止做你自己，即便那意味着与武器相处的时间多过书本，甚至彻底放下书本。这世上博学的书虫已经够多了，可 [protag] 只有一个。"

    old "You're a merchant, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I would imagine that the art of studying the way people behave and recognizing patterns isn't that foreign to you."
    new "You're a merchant, aren't you? Or at least, you were one, before you got wrapped up in this business with N'Mar. I would imagine that the art of studying the way people behave and recognizing patterns isn't that foreign to you.\n你是商人，对吧？至少，在卷进 N'Mar 这档子事之前是。我想，研究人们的行为方式、辨认规律这门本事，对你来说应该不陌生。"

    old "Were I a typical merchant, you would be right. A successful merchant is a merchant who keeps [hisher] ear to the ground. Conventional wisdom is that the merchant with the best information and who has the keenness to act on that information will be the one who reaps the greatest profits."
    new "Were I a typical merchant, you would be right. A successful merchant is a merchant who keeps [hisher] ear to the ground. Conventional wisdom is that the merchant with the best information and who has the keenness to act on that information will be the one who reaps the greatest profits.\n若我是个寻常商人，那你说的没错。成功的商人，是那种时刻把[hisher]耳朵贴在地上的人。世俗的智慧认为，谁掌握最灵通的消息、又足够敏锐地据此行动，谁就能赚到最大的利润。"

    old "For years, I chased the ghost of the 'best information.' But those days are behind me."
    new "For years, I chased the ghost of the 'best information.' But those days are behind me.\n多年来，我一直在追逐那‘最佳信息’的幻影。但那些日子已经过去了。"

    old "I don't understand. You're a merchant, and yet you don't seek the best information?"
    new "I don't understand. You're a merchant, and yet you don't seek the best information?\n我不明白。你是商人，却不追寻最灵通的消息？"

    old "If I compete with other merchants, then how difficult would it be for me to have the best information? By definition, only one person could be the most well-informed. And though I do consider myself a very competent observer and planner..."
    new "If I compete with other merchants, then how difficult would it be for me to have the best information? By definition, only one person could be the most well-informed. And though I do consider myself a very competent observer and planner...\n如果我与其他商人竞争，那么我拿到最灵通消息的难度该有多大？按定义，消息最灵通的人只能有一个。而尽管我自认是个相当称职的观察者和谋划者……"

    old "This land holds hundreds—no, thousands—of merchants. Do I really have the hubris to presume that I can outperform all of them?"
    new "This land holds hundreds—no, thousands—of merchants. Do I really have the hubris to presume that I can outperform all of them?\n这片土地上有成百——不，成千——个商人。我难道真有那份狂妄，以为自己能胜过他们所有人？"

    old "Even if I optimistically assume that I am in the top tenth of merchants, that still means that there are dozens, if not hundreds, of equally-competent merchants. Only a minority of them can be winners. Competition is for losers, statistically speaking."
    new "Even if I optimistically assume that I am in the top tenth of merchants, that still means that there are dozens, if not hundreds, of equally-competent merchants. Only a minority of them can be winners. Competition is for losers, statistically speaking.\n即便我乐观地假设自己跻身商人中的前十分之一，那也仍意味着有几十乃至上百个与我同样出色的商人。他们当中只有少数能成为赢家。从统计上说，竞争是留给输家的。"

    old "You're saying that most merchants are losers? That can't be right, surely. If they were losing money every season, they'd be fools to continue down the path of being a merchant."
    new "You're saying that most merchants are losers? That can't be right, surely. If they were losing money every season, they'd be fools to continue down the path of being a merchant.\n你是说大多数商人都是输家？这肯定不对吧。要是他们每个季度都在亏钱，还继续当商人，那岂不都是傻瓜。"

    old "My definition of 'loser' is perhaps a bit more broad than most. There are many merchants who get by on their modest earnings, following conventional wisdom to modest gains. But if you want a steady, stable income, mercantilism is the wrong profession."
    new "My definition of 'loser' is perhaps a bit more broad than most. There are many merchants who get by on their modest earnings, following conventional wisdom to modest gains. But if you want a steady, stable income, mercantilism is the wrong profession.\n我对‘输家’的定义，或许比多数人要宽泛些。有很多商人靠着微薄的利润勉强度日，循规蹈矩地赚些小钱。但如果你想要一份安稳、稳定的收入，行商就是错误的行当。"

    old "Being a merchant demands that you constantly invest in yourself and your future earnings. A single bad season has the potential to leave you destitute. Who in their right mind would take on that risk and stress just to eke out a modest living?"
    new "Being a merchant demands that you constantly invest in yourself and your future earnings. A single bad season has the potential to leave you destitute. Who in their right mind would take on that risk and stress just to eke out a modest living?\n当商人要求你不断投资自己和未来的收益。一个糟糕的季节，就可能让你倾家荡产。头脑正常的人，谁会为了勉强糊口，去承担那样的风险和压力？"

    old "If you're a merchant with half a mind for what makes sense, you're chasing big wins. Many compete, few succeed. So I decided not to compete."
    new "If you're a merchant with half a mind for what makes sense, you're chasing big wins. Many compete, few succeed. So I decided not to compete.\n如果你是个稍微明白事理的商人，就该去追逐大的胜利。竞争的人多，成功的人少。所以我决定不参与竞争。"

    old "I don't understand. How can you be a merchant without competing?"
    new "I don't understand. How can you be a merchant without competing?\n我不明白。不竞争，怎么还能当商人？"

    old "Suppose I did want to compete. A rival merchant sells imported wheat at ten coin for a bushel. If I wanted to compete with that, I would have to offer my wheat for nine coin a bushel. A fine strategy, until my neighbor decides to offer his for eight coin a bushel."
    new "Suppose I did want to compete. A rival merchant sells imported wheat at ten coin for a bushel. If I wanted to compete with that, I would have to offer my wheat for nine coin a bushel. A fine strategy, until my neighbor decides to offer his for eight coin a bushel.\n假设我真想竞争。有个对手商人以每蒲式耳十枚金币的价格出售进口小麦。我若想和他竞争，就得把自家小麦定价九枚金币一蒲式耳。这策略本来不错，直到我隔壁那家决定卖八枚金币一蒲式耳。"

    old "And I, in turn, am forced to lower my own prices, driving him to lower his prices in response, until eventually my profits are driven nearly to the point of zero. That's what competition looks like. It's brilliant for the buyers, since they get the lowest price. But for a profit-seeking merchant? Competition is their bane."
    new "And I, in turn, am forced to lower my own prices, driving him to lower his prices in response, until eventually my profits are driven nearly to the point of zero. That's what competition looks like. It's brilliant for the buyers, since they get the lowest price. But for a profit-seeking merchant? Competition is their bane.\n而我反过来又被迫降价，逼得他也跟着降，直到最后我的利润几乎被压到零。竞争就是这么回事。对买家来说妙极了，因为他们能拿到最低价。可对追求利润的商人来说，竞争就是他们的灾星。"

    old "So, how do you avoid the loser's game of competition? When you see other merchants transacting a certain sort of business, you run far, far away. You have to do what no other merchant is doing."
    new "So, how do you avoid the loser's game of competition? When you see other merchants transacting a certain sort of business, you run far, far away. You have to do what no other merchant is doing.\n那么，要怎样才能避开这场属于输家的竞争游戏？当你看到别的商人在做某类生意时，你就远远地躲开。你得去做没有任何其他商人在做的事。"

    old "Usually, if no merchant is doing something, I'd take that as a sign that there's no money to be made doing it. Otherwise, other merchants would already be doing it."
    new "Usually, if no merchant is doing something, I'd take that as a sign that there's no money to be made doing it. Otherwise, other merchants would already be doing it.\n通常，如果没一个商人在做某件事，我会把它当作这事赚不到钱的信号。否则，其他商人早就去做了。"

    old "You might think that. As a young merchant, I thought the same thing. But you would be wrong, just as wrong as I was in my youth."
    new "You might think that. As a young merchant, I thought the same thing. But you would be wrong, just as wrong as I was in my youth.\n你可能会这么想。我年轻时也这么想过。但你会错的，就像我年轻时一样错。"

    old "You expect merchants to always chase profits. But implicit in the character of a merchant is a certain hatred of traditional work. And with that natural bias comes a certain blindness for opportunities that are menial and demanding."
    new "You expect merchants to always chase profits. But implicit in the character of a merchant is a certain hatred of traditional work. And with that natural bias comes a certain blindness for opportunities that are menial and demanding.\n你以为商人总是追逐利润。但商人的骨子里，隐含着对传统劳作的某种厌恶。而这种天生的偏见，又让他们对费时费力的机会视而不见。"

    old "Making a living can be a very simple thing. You find someone, perhaps a farmer, who is in need of a laborer, and you perform the labor demanded of that occupation. Work hard in the fields, and you'll see that effort reflected in the harvest, and part of it will be yours to share in."
    new "Making a living can be a very simple thing. You find someone, perhaps a farmer, who is in need of a laborer, and you perform the labor demanded of that occupation. Work hard in the fields, and you'll see that effort reflected in the harvest, and part of it will be yours to share in.\n谋生其实可以很简单。你找一个需要帮工的人，比如一个农夫，然后干那份营生所要求的活计。在田里卖力劳作，你的付出就会反映在收成上，其中也有一部分归你。"

    old "Being a laborer is an incredibly simple way to get through life. Not easy, mind you, but simple."
    new "Being a laborer is an incredibly simple way to get through life. Not easy, mind you, but simple.\n当一名雇工，是过完这一生极其简单的办法。注意，不是轻松，而是简单。"

    old "Merchants are merchants because they wanted to avoid that simple-but-hard life. Every merchant, in their soul, is chasing the complicated-but-easy route to success. They want the mythical plan that, while intellectually novel and difficult to comprehend, requires minimal effort to execute."
    new "Merchants are merchants because they wanted to avoid that simple-but-hard life. Every merchant, in their soul, is chasing the complicated-but-easy route to success. They want the mythical plan that, while intellectually novel and difficult to comprehend, requires minimal effort to execute.\n商人之所以当商人，就是想避开那种简单却辛苦的生活。每个商人内心深处，都在追寻那条复杂却轻松的成功之路。他们想要一个传说中的妙计——虽然思想上新奇、难以参透，执行起来却几乎不费力气。"

    old "Every trader is looking for that elusive one hot tip that will allow the to amass great wealth in a short period of time."
    new "Every trader is looking for that elusive one hot tip that will allow the to amass great wealth in a short period of time.\n每个商贩都在寻找那条可遇不可求的捷径，能让自己在短时间内积累起巨额财富。"

    old "There's a word that dwarves use. 'Schlep.' Is it a word you're familiar with?"
    new "There's a word that dwarves use. 'Schlep.' Is it a word you're familiar with?\nDwarves 有个词叫‘schlep’。你熟悉这个词吗？"

    old "I don't spend much time in the company of dwarves, so no, I'm not familiar with the term 'schlep.'"
    new "I don't spend much time in the company of dwarves, so no, I'm not familiar with the term 'schlep.'\n我不常和 Dwarves 打交道，所以不，我不熟悉‘schlep’这个词。"

    old "It means, literally, to carry or lug something, but it generally just refers to any tedious, awkward, slow task."
    new "It means, literally, to carry or lug something, but it generally just refers to any tedious, awkward, slow task.\n字面意思是搬或拖什么东西，但通常泛指任何乏味、别扭、费时的苦差事。"

    old "That does sound like a very dwarven word."
    new "That does sound like a very dwarven word.\n这词听起来确实很像 Dwarves 会用的词。"

    old "Doesn't it? Dwarves seem to have a natural talent, or at least a natural tolerance, for boring and unpleasant tasks. It's something that has to be built into a race for them to achieve such feats of architecture. Beautiful buildings are built with an eye for design, but mostly hard labor."
    new "Doesn't it? Dwarves seem to have a natural talent, or at least a natural tolerance, for boring and unpleasant tasks. It's something that has to be built into a race for them to achieve such feats of architecture. Beautiful buildings are built with an eye for design, but mostly hard labor.\n可不是吗？Dwarves 似乎天生就有做无聊、不愉快工作的才能，至少天生就能忍受。一个种族得天生具备这种本事，才能成就那样的建筑伟业。美丽的建筑固然有设计的眼光，但靠的大多是苦工。"

    old "Merchants hate schleps. Of course, no one likes schleps, but merchants hate them more than anyone. They can't help it. It's in their nature."
    new "Merchants hate schleps. Of course, no one likes schleps, but merchants hate them more than anyone. They can't help it. It's in their nature.\n商人们最恨 schlep。当然，没人喜欢苦差事，但商人对它们的厌恶胜过任何人。他们身不由己。那是天性使然。"

    old "Every merchant wants to get rich quick, even the wiser ones who realize that getting rich fast isn't a realistic goal, and they rationalize their belief in the existence of these shortcuts to success by concluding that they must exist, only their peers have failed to discover them for lack of cleverness."
    new "Every merchant wants to get rich quick, even the wiser ones who realize that getting rich fast isn't a realistic goal, and they rationalize their belief in the existence of these shortcuts to success by concluding that they must exist, only their peers have failed to discover them for lack of cleverness.\n每个商人都想快速致富，就连那些明白快速致富不现实的聪明人也不例外。他们为自己相信成功捷径的存在找理由，得出结论说：捷径肯定存在，只是同行们不够聪明，没能发现罢了。"

    old "Always looking for shortcuts goes beyond just hating the boring or inconvenient. It actually affects the way that you perceive the world."
    new "Always looking for shortcuts goes beyond just hating the boring or inconvenient. It actually affects the way that you perceive the world.\n总是寻找捷径，可不仅仅意味着讨厌无聊或不方便。它其实会影响你看待世界的方式。"

    old "For example, take the town of Icesilia. You're familiar with it, yes?"
    new "For example, take the town of Icesilia. You're familiar with it, yes?\n比如说 Icesilia 这个镇子。你熟悉吧？"

    old "Not intimately, but I am aware of it. You speak of the town near the eastern coast of the continent, yes?"
    new "Not intimately, but I am aware of it. You speak of the town near the eastern coast of the continent, yes?\n不算太熟，但我知道。你说的是大陆东海岸附近的那座镇子，对吧？"

    old "Yes, Icesilia is near the eastern coast. Every merchant who has ever looked at a map has spotted Icesilia, and noted that it is close to the sea, just as you have. And immediately, the merchant begins formulating ideas of how trade routes might be established by way of ship between Icesilia and the bustling metropolis of Horus."
    new "Yes, Icesilia is near the eastern coast. Every merchant who has ever looked at a map has spotted Icesilia, and noted that it is close to the sea, just as you have. And immediately, the merchant begins formulating ideas of how trade routes might be established by way of ship between Icesilia and the bustling metropolis of Horus.\n对，Icesilia 靠近东海岸。每个看过地图的商人都会注意到 Icesilia，并且和你一样发现它临近大海。紧接着，商人马上就开始盘算，如何通过海路，在 Icesilia 和繁华大都会 Horus 之间开辟贸易航线。"

    old "The eastern and western coasts of the continent vary wildly in geography, and with that distance comes variances in the natural resources that can be grown or mined there, and the crops that the land can support."
    new "The eastern and western coasts of the continent vary wildly in geography, and with that distance comes variances in the natural resources that can be grown or mined there, and the crops that the land can support.\n大陆的东海岸和西海岸在地理上差异极大，而随着距离而来的，是两地在可种植、可开采的自然资源以及土地所能供养的作物上的种种不同。"

    old "It seems like a ripe opportunity for trading. The only question is, how to get that ship? Once you've secured passage by sea, trading between the two regions becomes easy."
    new "It seems like a ripe opportunity for trading. The only question is, how to get that ship? Once you've secured passage by sea, trading between the two regions becomes easy.\n这看起来是个绝佳的贸易机会。唯一的问题是，怎么弄到船？一旦打通了海路，两地之间的贸易就变得容易了。"

    old "So quickly do merchants begin contemplating how to tame the sea that they never consider the more direct option: travel across the land instead."
    new "So quickly do merchants begin contemplating how to tame the sea that they never consider the more direct option: travel across the land instead.\n商人们如此迅速地开始盘算如何征服大海，以至于从没考虑过那个更直接的选择：改走陆路。"

    old "The idea of traveling across the continent, rather than around it, must seem insane to most merchants. It requires significantly more effort, planning, and travel time. And the volume of goods that you can transport by ship is so much greater."
    new "The idea of traveling across the continent, rather than around it, must seem insane to most merchants. It requires significantly more effort, planning, and travel time. And the volume of goods that you can transport by ship is so much greater.\n横穿大陆而不是绕海而行的想法，在大多数商人看来肯定荒唐透顶。那需要付出多得多的精力、谋划和旅途时间。而且船运能载的货量也要大得多。"

    old "The land route is not without its perils, as well. The long route from Icesilia to Horus takes you through the Forest of Howlgrove, which is home to all manner of magical dangers."
    new "The land route is not without its perils, as well. The long route from Icesilia to Horus takes you through the Forest of Howlgrove, which is home to all manner of magical dangers.\n而且陆路也并非没有凶险。从 Icesilia 到 Horus 的漫漫长路，会带你穿过 Howlgrove 森林，那里栖息着各种各样的魔法危险。"

    old "Here's something rather encounter-intuitive that I came to realize: the things that make the route through the Forest of Howlgrove so hazardous also make it a treasure trove for any merchant."
    new "Here's something rather encounter-intuitive that I came to realize: the things that make the route through the Forest of Howlgrove so hazardous also make it a treasure trove for any merchant.\n而我还领悟到一件颇为反直觉的事：让穿越 Howlgrove 森林的路线如此凶险的种种因素，恰恰也让它成为商人的宝库。"

    old "You see, the Forest of Howlgrove is home to many witches. Witches generally don't take kindly to unwanted visitors, and consequently many endeavor to avoid that forest. But witches are like anyone else: they desire nice things, be they sweet confections from the city, or simple varied sustenance."
    new "You see, the Forest of Howlgrove is home to many witches. Witches generally don't take kindly to unwanted visitors, and consequently many endeavor to avoid that forest. But witches are like anyone else: they desire nice things, be they sweet confections from the city, or simple varied sustenance.\n你看，Howlgrove 森林是许多女巫的家园。女巫通常对不请自来的访客没什么好脸色，因此许多人都极力避开那片森林。但女巫和普通人一样：她们也渴望好东西，无论是城里的甜美糕点，还是简单多样的食物。"

    old "And witches tend to produce and hold many curios as well. That's in part due to their occupation, and in part due to the many magical creatures that live in the woods and serve as their...ingredients. I won't lecture you on the particulars, but suffice to say there are many goods that you can find only in the Forest of Howlgrove."
    new "And witches tend to produce and hold many curios as well. That's in part due to their occupation, and in part due to the many magical creatures that live in the woods and serve as their...ingredients. I won't lecture you on the particulars, but suffice to say there are many goods that you can find only in the Forest of Howlgrove.\n而且女巫们往往还会制作和持有许多稀奇物件。这一半是因为她们的营生，一半是因为林子里生活着许多魔法生物，充当她们的……原料。细节我就不多说了，总之，有很多货物，你只能在 Howlgrove 森林里找到。"

    old "Some people look at a forest full of witches and see danger. Others look at a forest full of witches and see potential clients. As far as I can tell, I'm alone in the latter category."
    new "Some people look at a forest full of witches and see danger. Others look at a forest full of witches and see potential clients. As far as I can tell, I'm alone in the latter category.\n有些人看见一片住满女巫的森林，看到的是危险。另一些人看见同样的森林，看到的却是潜在的客户。据我所知，我独自属于后一类。"

    old "If I wanted to compete with other merchants, I would be planning ways to determine the most efficient way to stock trade goods on a ship bound from Icesilia to Horus. Instead, I chose a different route. I chose not to compete. And that has brought me quite a healthy level of success as a merchant."
    new "If I wanted to compete with other merchants, I would be planning ways to determine the most efficient way to stock trade goods on a ship bound from Icesilia to Horus. Instead, I chose a different route. I chose not to compete. And that has brought me quite a healthy level of success as a merchant.\n如果我想和其他商人竞争，我就会琢磨，怎样最高效地给一艘从 Icesilia 开往 Horus 的船配货。但我选择了另一条路。我选择不竞争。而这也让我作为商人，取得了相当可观的成就。"

    old "And I'm sure that success is deserved. I must confess, when I was told I would be meeting with former experience as a merchant, I certainly didn't expect someone...someone like you. You are full of surprises, [protag]."
    new "And I'm sure that success is deserved. I must confess, when I was told I would be meeting with former experience as a merchant, I certainly didn't expect someone...someone like you. You are full of surprises, [protag].\n而我相信这成功是你应得的。我得承认，当初听说要会见一位有过从商经历的人时，我可真没想到会是……会是你这样的人。你真是处处给人惊喜，[protag]。"

    old "I feel like I could spend days with you, swapping stories back and forth, and never get bored. I don't know when we'll meet next, but I look forward to it."
    new "I feel like I could spend days with you, swapping stories back and forth, and never get bored. I don't know when we'll meet next, but I look forward to it.\n我觉得哪怕和你聊上几天几夜，彼此交换故事，也不会觉得腻。我不知道下次何时再见，但我很期待。"

    old "So do I, Leena. So do I."
    new "So do I, Leena. So do I.\n我也是，Leena。我也是。"

    old "I find Leena just outside the Citadel walls, nearby a camp fire. The sun is starting to set."
    new "I find Leena just outside the Citadel walls, nearby a camp fire. The sun is starting to set.\n我在城堡城墙外找到了 Leena，她就在一堆篝火旁。太阳正开始西沉。"

    old "Hello, Leena."
    new "Hello, Leena.\n你好，Leena。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. Here to chat, or is this a business visit?"
    new "Ah, [protag]. Here to chat, or is this a business visit?\n啊，[protag]。是来聊天的，还是来办公事的？"

    old "I'm just here to chat. What's that you have in your hand?"
    new "I'm just here to chat. What's that you have in your hand?\n我只是来聊聊。你手里拿的是什么？"

    old "This? Oh, it's one of my boots. I'm repairing it."
    new "This? Oh, it's one of my boots. I'm repairing it.\n这个？哦，是我的一只靴子。我在修它。"

    old "You're captain of the royal guard, aren't you? Isn't that task kind of beneath you?"
    new "You're captain of the royal guard, aren't you? Isn't that task kind of beneath you?\n你可是皇家卫队队长，不是吗？这种活儿对你来说，是不是有点屈才了？"

    old "I'd have to be mighty arrogant to presume that any kind of work is below me."
    new "I'd have to be mighty arrogant to presume that any kind of work is below me.\n要是以为有什么活儿配不上我，那我也未免太狂妄了。"

    old "Well, I mean, don't you have people who take care of those kinds of trivial things for me?"
    new "Well, I mean, don't you have people who take care of those kinds of trivial things for me?\n嗯，我是说，难道没有人替你打理这些琐事吗？"

    old "If I deemed this task trivial, I could assign it to one of my underlings. But it's no trivial task."
    new "If I deemed this task trivial, I could assign it to one of my underlings. But it's no trivial task.\n如果我觉得这活儿琐碎，大可以派给某个手下。可它并不琐碎。"

    old "You're stitching a boot. I have a hard time believing that it's an important task."
    new "You're stitching a boot. I have a hard time believing that it's an important task.\n你只是在缝靴子。我很难相信这是件要紧事。"

    old "I'm not one to march into battle barefoot."
    new "I'm not one to march into battle barefoot.\n我可不是那种赤着脚上战场的人。"

    old "Well, okay. Having working shoes is important to a warrior. But why do you have to waste your time with a task like this instead of delegating it?"
    new "Well, okay. Having working shoes is important to a warrior. But why do you have to waste your time with a task like this instead of delegating it?\n好吧。有双合脚的鞋，对战士来说确实重要。可你为什么要浪费时间亲自做这种活儿，而不交给别人呢？"

    old "I'm practiced in the art of stitching my own boots. It requires finesse to stitch it in such a manner that the fibers of the laces do not rub against the exterior of the shoe when I move or flex my feet. I wouldn't trust anyone else with this task."
    new "I'm practiced in the art of stitching my own boots. It requires finesse to stitch it in such a manner that the fibers of the laces do not rub against the exterior of the shoe when I move or flex my feet. I wouldn't trust anyone else with this task.\n我练就了一手缝自己靴子的本事。要缝得恰到好处，让我活动或屈伸双脚时，鞋带纤维不会磨到鞋面，这是门精细活儿。这种活儿，我信不过别人。"

    old "So you're saying that in the Amazon citadel, the most skilled shoe-maker is also the captain of the queen's royal guard? No one is better than you at making shoes?"
    new "So you're saying that in the Amazon citadel, the most skilled shoe-maker is also the captain of the queen's royal guard? No one is better than you at making shoes?\n所以你的意思是，在 Amazon 城堡里，手艺最好的鞋匠，同时也是女王的皇家卫队队长？没人比你更会做鞋？"

    old "I'm no cobbler. I don't make shoes. The craftsmanship that went into making this sole isn't something I could hope to match. But I am very skilled when it comes to stitching. And perhaps more importantly, I am the Amazons' foremost expert when it comes to a very specific topic: my feet."
    new "I'm no cobbler. I don't make shoes. The craftsmanship that went into making this sole isn't something I could hope to match. But I am very skilled when it comes to stitching. And perhaps more importantly, I am the Amazons' foremost expert when it comes to a very specific topic: my feet.\n我可不是鞋匠。我不做鞋。做出这只鞋底的手艺，我是望尘莫及的。但在缝合这方面，我确实十分在行。而更重要的也许是，在某个极其专门的领域，我是 Amazons 首屈一指的专家：我自己的脚。"

    old "No one else understands how the muscle of my foot contracts when I leap or tightens when I land from a fall. No one else understands my stride quite like I do. I know all of the places where my foot is going to exert the most force, and where friction will cause the most damage to the boot."
    new "No one else understands how the muscle of my foot contracts when I leap or tightens when I land from a fall. No one else understands my stride quite like I do. I know all of the places where my foot is going to exert the most force, and where friction will cause the most damage to the boot.\n没有别人懂得，我起跳时脚上的肌肉如何收缩，落地时又如何绷紧。没有别人像我一样了解我的步伐。我知道脚上哪些部位会使出最大的力，也知道哪里摩擦对靴子的损耗最严重。"

    old "So, in a manner of speaking, I am uniquely qualified for the task of putting the final touches on my combat boots. And when they break, no one else has the same intimate knowledge of how it is that they came apart. I know exactly what caused this break, and I know exactly how to prevent it from happening again."
    new "So, in a manner of speaking, I am uniquely qualified for the task of putting the final touches on my combat boots. And when they break, no one else has the same intimate knowledge of how it is that they came apart. I know exactly what caused this break, and I know exactly how to prevent it from happening again.\n所以，可以说，唯独我最有资格给我的战靴做最后的收尾。而且它们坏掉时，也没有别人像我一样，如此熟悉它们是如何开裂的。我确切地知道是什么导致了这次开裂，也确切地知道该如何防止它再次发生。"

    old "This boot broke through no fault of the original crafter. She did the very best that she could, and there's no way she could have anticipated the extend to which I would test its durability and strength. So, I'm now taking it upon myself to succeed where she fell short."
    new "This boot broke through no fault of the original crafter. She did the very best that she could, and there's no way she could have anticipated the extend to which I would test its durability and strength. So, I'm now taking it upon myself to succeed where she fell short.\n这只靴子坏掉，并不是原匠人的过错。她已经尽力做到了最好，也不可能预见到我会把它的耐用和结实程度考验到何种地步。所以，现在由我亲自动手，去补上她没能做到的地方。"

    old "That does seem important. Having a loose boot in the heat of battle could be deadly under the wrong circumstances. Imagine something as simple as losing your footing when facing down an opponent. Sometimes, even the smallest disadvantages can have the most dire of consequences."
    new "That does seem important. Having a loose boot in the heat of battle could be deadly under the wrong circumstances. Imagine something as simple as losing your footing when facing down an opponent. Sometimes, even the smallest disadvantages can have the most dire of consequences.\n这么说来确实要紧。激战正酣时靴子松了，在某些情况下可能是致命的。想想看，面对对手时，仅仅是脚下打滑这么简单的事。有时候，最微小的劣势，也能带来最惨重的后果。"

    old "Indeed. When your life is on the line, margins for error are tiny to non-existent."
    new "Indeed. When your life is on the line, margins for error are tiny to non-existent.\n确实。当你命悬一线时，容错的空间小之又小，甚至为零。"

    old "Does that really make a big difference?"
    new "Does that really make a big difference?\n那真的会有很大差别吗？"

    old "When you dig your foot into the ground and rely on your combat stance to allow you to effectively block a blow to the head, then yes, the sureness of your footing can make a big difference. Having your equipment fail when your life is on the line is not a glorious way to go."
    new "When you dig your foot into the ground and rely on your combat stance to allow you to effectively block a blow to the head, then yes, the sureness of your footing can make a big difference. Having your equipment fail when your life is on the line is not a glorious way to go.\n当你把脚牢牢扎进地里，靠战斗站姿有效挡开劈向头部的一击时，那么没错，脚下是否稳当，差别就很大了。命悬一线之际装备失灵，可不是什么光荣的死法。"

    old "It seems like a pretty insignificant thing. But I guess the smallest advantage is still an advantage. And if you're a warrior, putting your life on the line, you can't afford to give up tiny margins that might mean the difference between life and death."
    new "It seems like a pretty insignificant thing. But I guess the smallest advantage is still an advantage. And if you're a warrior, putting your life on the line, you can't afford to give up tiny margins that might mean the difference between life and death.\n看起来确实是件微不足道的小事。但我想，再小的优势也是优势。而如果你是个把性命押上的战士，就绝不能放弃那些可能关乎生死的小小余地。"

    old "Indeed. Most freak accidents that occur on the battlefield could be prevented if people were more fastidious in their preparation."
    new "Indeed. Most freak accidents that occur on the battlefield could be prevented if people were more fastidious in their preparation.\n确实。战场上发生的大多数离奇事故，其实只要人们在准备上更一丝不苟，就本可避免。"

    old "I once saw a man killed in battle when his axe's head lodged in an enemy and became detached from the handle. If he'd checked his weapon before the battle, he might have lived to fight another day."
    new "I once saw a man killed in battle when his axe's head lodged in an enemy and became detached from the handle. If he'd checked his weapon before the battle, he might have lived to fight another day.\n我曾见过一个人死在战场上，只因他的斧头砍进敌人身体时，斧刃从斧柄上脱落了。他若在战前检查过武器，也许就能活下来，改日再战。"

    old "How did your boot break in the first place?"
    new "How did your boot break in the first place?\n你的靴子最初是怎么坏的？"

    old "Well, I've just finished the last stitch, so why don't I give you a little demonstration of what I was doing when it happened?"
    new "Well, I've just finished the last stitch, so why don't I give you a little demonstration of what I was doing when it happened?\n嗯，我正好缝完了最后一针，不如我来给你小演示一下，它坏掉时我在做什么吧。"

    old "Sure, let's see it."
    new "Sure, let's see it.\n好啊，让我瞧瞧。"

    old "Follow me inside the Citadel."
    new "Follow me inside the Citadel.\n跟我进城堡里面。"

    old "I follow her inside the Citadel, and we enter a room which looks strangely empty."
    new "I follow her inside the Citadel, and we enter a room which looks strangely empty.\n我跟着她进了城堡，我们走进一个看起来出奇空旷的房间。"

    old "In case you're wondering, this is my training room. It's empty on purpose. Wait and you'll understand."
    new "In case you're wondering, this is my training room. It's empty on purpose. Wait and you'll understand.\n你大概在纳闷吧，这是我的训练室。空着是故意的。等着看，你就明白了。"

    old "You might want to back up and get out of the way."
    new "You might want to back up and get out of the way.\n你最好往后退退，让开点。"

    old "Um, Leena, why are you holding that sword?"
    new "Um, Leena, why are you holding that sword?\n呃，Leena，你拿着那把剑干什么？"

    old "You'll see."
    new "You'll see.\n你马上就会明白。"

    old "Leena checks to see that both her boots are secured to her feet, and dashes toward the wall. She pushes off her left foot, launching herself toward the ceiling."
    new "Leena checks to see that both her boots are secured to her feet, and dashes toward the wall. She pushes off her left foot, launching herself toward the ceiling.\nLeena 确认了两只靴子都牢牢系在脚上，然后朝墙壁冲去。她用左脚一蹬，朝着天花板腾空而起。"

    old "She pushes off the wall with both feet, sending her body toward me in a horizontal trajectory, and cartwheels in the air."
    new "She pushes off the wall with both feet, sending her body toward me in a horizontal trajectory, and cartwheels in the air.\n她双脚蹬墙，身体沿水平方向朝我飞来，还在空中翻了个跟头。"

    old "Leena turns her blade toward the floor, and lands in front of me, planting her blade in the tile at my feet."
    new "Leena turns her blade toward the floor, and lands in front of me, planting her blade in the tile at my feet.\nLeena 把剑尖转向地面，落在我面前，将剑插进我脚边的地砖里。"

    old "Yikes. That was a little close for comfort."
    new "Yikes. That was a little close for comfort.\n嚯。这也太近了点，让人心里发毛。"

    old "Hopefully close enough to get the point across. If you'd been standing two steps ahead of where you were, that blade would have entered your chest and been driven straight down through your ribcage, hitting every vital along the way."
    new "Hopefully close enough to get the point across. If you'd been standing two steps ahead of where you were, that blade would have entered your chest and been driven straight down through your ribcage, hitting every vital along the way.\n希望近得足够让你明白。你要是再往前站两步，那把剑就会刺进你的胸膛，一路直直劈穿你的胸腔，途中命中每一处要害。"

    old "So, what do you think of my new combat trick?"
    new "So, what do you think of my new combat trick?\n那么，你觉得我这新格斗招式怎么样？"

    old "It seems pretty deadly. I mean, even moreso than a thrust of the sword would normally be."
    new "It seems pretty deadly. I mean, even moreso than a thrust of the sword would normally be.\n看起来相当致命。我是说，比普通的一剑刺击还要致命。"

    old "'Exceptionally deadly' is exactly what I intended. I began working on this technique by thinking about the kinds of foes we'll be facing in the future."
    new "'Exceptionally deadly' is exactly what I intended. I began working on this technique by thinking about the kinds of foes we'll be facing in the future.\n我要的正是‘极其致命’。我琢磨这个招式，是从思考我们将来会面对什么样的敌人开始的。"

    old "You mean vampires?"
    new "You mean vampires?\n你是说吸血鬼？"

    old "Vampires, zombies, ghouls, the whole lot of them. They tend to be a good deal more tenacious than the sort of foes I'm used to fighting. So I devised a maneuver that would allow me to deliver a decisive blow with more force."
    new "Vampires, zombies, ghouls, the whole lot of them. They tend to be a good deal more tenacious than the sort of foes I'm used to fighting. So I devised a maneuver that would allow me to deliver a decisive blow with more force.\n吸血鬼、僵尸、食尸鬼，那一大帮子。它们往往比我打惯了的敌人顽强得多。于是我设计了这个招式，让我能以更大的力道给出决定性的一击。"

    old "Of course, that added force comes at a cost. This move requires a good deal more finesse to pull off. If I fail to hand the blow, I could find myself in quite a vulnerable situation. And even if I succeed, driving a blade deep into a foe's flesh leaves you with the task of removing your blade from where it's embedded in their chest."
    new "Of course, that added force comes at a cost. This move requires a good deal more finesse to pull off. If I fail to hand the blow, I could find myself in quite a vulnerable situation. And even if I succeed, driving a blade deep into a foe's flesh leaves you with the task of removing your blade from where it's embedded in their chest.\n当然，这多出的力道是有代价的。这个招式需要细腻得多的手法才能完成。我若没能使出这一击，就会陷入相当被动的境地。而即便成功了，把剑深深刺进敌人身体后，你还得想办法把剑从他们胸膛里拔出来。"

    old "Still, it seems like a potentially useful technique under the right circumstances."
    new "Still, it seems like a potentially useful technique under the right circumstances.\n不过，在合适的场合下，这似乎是个可能派上用场的招式。"

    old "And I do believe that we'll see those circumstances arise when we invade the castle of N'Mar. Indoor fighting is not my forte, but I think that this technique should give me a leg up."
    new "And I do believe that we'll see those circumstances arise when we invade the castle of N'Mar. Indoor fighting is not my forte, but I think that this technique should give me a leg up.\n而且我确信，等我们攻打 N'Mar 城堡时，这样的场合就会出现。室内战斗不是我的强项，但我想这招式能给我添几分胜算。"

    old "It seems horribly impractical."
    new "It seems horribly impractical.\n它看起来实在不切实际。"

    old "Well, for one thing, it only works when you have a horizontal surface to launch from. It works well enough indoors where you can find walls or supports to push off, but in an open battlefield, it would be impossible to pull off."
    new "Well, for one thing, it only works when you have a horizontal surface to launch from. It works well enough indoors where you can find walls or supports to push off, but in an open battlefield, it would be impossible to pull off.\n嗯，首先，它只有在有横向表面可借力时才使得出来。在室内效果不错，因为能找到墙壁或支柱来蹬踏；但在开阔的战场上，就不可能施展了。"

    old "You're dismissing it because it's not useful in all scenarios? That seems akin to criticizing fire arrows for being impractical when it's raining."
    new "You're dismissing it because it's not useful in all scenarios? That seems akin to criticizing fire arrows for being impractical when it's raining.\n你就因为它不是在所有场合都有用，就把它否定了？这跟抱怨火箭在下雨天不实用，有什么两样。"

    old "I get it, just because it's not useful everywhere doesn't mean it can't come in handy sometimes. But it's not just the circumstantial nature of the technique that's at issue."
    new "I get it, just because it's not useful everywhere doesn't mean it can't come in handy sometimes. But it's not just the circumstantial nature of the technique that's at issue.\n我懂，不是处处有用，不代表它偶尔派不上用场。但有问题的，不只是这招式的场合局限性。"

    old "You described it as a technique for driving a blade deep into someone's ribcage. Well, I might be more fragile than most, but driving a blade just partway into my ribcage would probably be enough to do me in. Delivering the blow with that kind of force seems like overkill."
    new "You described it as a technique for driving a blade deep into someone's ribcage. Well, I might be more fragile than most, but driving a blade just partway into my ribcage would probably be enough to do me in. Delivering the blow with that kind of force seems like overkill.\n你把它描述成一种把剑深深刺入别人胸腔的招式。嗯，我或许比多数人更脆弱，但即便只是刺进我胸腔一半，大概也足够要我的命了。用那么大的力道出招，似乎有点小题大做。"

    old "There's also the matter of what to do when your blade is lodged in someone's chest, and his friend comes to punish you for it. And what if you miss? Either way, you're left in a rather vulnerable position."
    new "There's also the matter of what to do when your blade is lodged in someone's chest, and his friend comes to punish you for it. And what if you miss? Either way, you're left in a rather vulnerable position.\n还有个问题：当你的剑卡在别人胸口里，他的同伴冲过来找你算账时，你该怎么办？而且要是你刺空了呢？无论哪种情况，你都会陷入相当被动的境地。"

    old "You're right on several counts. It's true that this technique leaves me vulnerable to attacks, regardless of whether it connects or not. And it's true that against most foes, it would be a bit excessive to deal such a forceful blow."
    new "You're right on several counts. It's true that this technique leaves me vulnerable to attacks, regardless of whether it connects or not. And it's true that against most foes, it would be a bit excessive to deal such a forceful blow.\n你在好几点上都说对了。没错，无论这一击是否命中，这招式都会让我暴露在攻击之下。也没错，对大多数敌人来说，使出这么大力的一击确实有点过了。"

    old "And if you wish to argue that the vast majority of regular combat occurs outside where there are no walls, you might be right. But this is not a technique conceived with ordinary combat in mind."
    new "And if you wish to argue that the vast majority of regular combat occurs outside where there are no walls, you might be right. But this is not a technique conceived with ordinary combat in mind.\n而如果你想论证，绝大多数常规战斗都发生在没有墙壁的户外，那你也许是对的。但这招式，本就不是为普通战斗而构思的。"

    old "In the future, we're going to be fighting the undead. My knowledge of ghouls and there ilk doesn't extend far, but what I do know is that the undead are a very tenacious sort, the sort to easily withstand blows that might be enough to kill an ordinary man."
    new "In the future, we're going to be fighting the undead. My knowledge of ghouls and there ilk doesn't extend far, but what I do know is that the undead are a very tenacious sort, the sort to easily withstand blows that might be enough to kill an ordinary man.\n将来，我们要对付的是亡灵。我对食尸鬼之流的了解并不深，但我知道，亡灵是种极其顽强的存在，足以轻易扛下那些本可杀死普通人的攻击。"

    old "Furthermore, within the castle of N'Mar, we're going to be doing a good deal of fighting indoors. Like any castle, I'm sure that it is full of walls and pillars that would make a good horizontal surface to launch from."
    new "Furthermore, within the castle of N'Mar, we're going to be doing a good deal of fighting indoors. Like any castle, I'm sure that it is full of walls and pillars that would make a good horizontal surface to launch from.\n此外，在 N'Mar 城堡内部，我们会有大量战斗要在室内进行。和任何城堡一样，我相信那里满是墙壁和立柱，正适合作为借力起跳的横向表面。"

    old "I probably won't have much use for this technique in the far future. But I think it may be a useful tool for the time that I serve as your companion."
    new "I probably won't have much use for this technique in the far future. But I think it may be a useful tool for the time that I serve as your companion.\n在遥远的将来，这招式大概就没多大用处了。但我想，在我做你同伴的这段时间里，它或许是个有用的工具。"

    old "I hadn't even thought of that."
    new "I hadn't even thought of that.\n这我倒完全没想到。"

    old "I'm not sure how effective that technique would be in actual combat, but you sure looked cool doing it."
    new "I'm not sure how effective that technique would be in actual combat, but you sure looked cool doing it.\n我不确定这招式在实战中能有多管用，但你使出来的时候，看着确实很帅。"

    old "Really? That's not the response I expected to hear."
    new "Really? That's not the response I expected to hear.\n是吗？这可不是我预料中的回答。"

    old "You asked for my first reaction, and I gave it. Watching an Amazon warrior gracefully flying through the air, it's not something I see every day, though I wouldn't mind if I did."
    new "You asked for my first reaction, and I gave it. Watching an Amazon warrior gracefully flying through the air, it's not something I see every day, though I wouldn't mind if I did.\n你问我的第一反应，我就如实说了。看着一位 Amazon 战士在空中优雅地翻飞，这可不是我天天能见到的，不过我倒也不介意多见几回。"

    old "I just mean that it's always a treat to see a skilled fighter in action. I can appreciate good technique when I see it."
    new "I just mean that it's always a treat to see a skilled fighter in action. I can appreciate good technique when I see it.\n我只是想说，看到高手出招，总是件赏心悦目的事。好身手，我一眼就能看出好来。"

    old "I just mean that you're really quite a lovely woman. I can appreciate beauty when I see it."
    new "I just mean that you're really quite a lovely woman. I can appreciate beauty when I see it.\n我只是想说，你实在是个很迷人的女子。美，我一眼就能看出美来。"

    old "Oh, so you being impressed has nothing to do with my skill and technique?"
    new "Oh, so you being impressed has nothing to do with my skill and technique?\n哦，所以你被我打动，跟我的身手和技巧一点关系都没有？"

    old "Not at all. Your grace and poise is part of your natural beauty. It's not just about how you look, but the way you move."
    new "Not at all. Your grace and poise is part of your natural beauty. It's not just about how you look, but the way you move.\n完全不是。你的优雅和仪态，本就是你天生之美的一部分。不只是你的模样，还有你的一举一动。"

    old "It must have taken you a lot of practice to pull off a move like that."
    new "It must have taken you a lot of practice to pull off a move like that.\n能做出那样的动作，你一定练了很久。"

    old "Indeed it did. It's actually a relatively new technique I'm working on. I started training specifically for the task ahead. I thought to myself, how will fighting undead foes in the castle of N'Mar differ from the combat I'm accustomed to?"
    new "Indeed it did. It's actually a relatively new technique I'm working on. I started training specifically for the task ahead. I thought to myself, how will fighting undead foes in the castle of N'Mar differ from the combat I'm accustomed to?\n确实练了很久。其实这是我在琢磨的一个比较新的招式。我是专门为眼前的任务开始训练的。我心想，在 N'Mar 城堡里与亡灵敌人作战，和我习惯的战斗会有什么不同？"

    old "The first thing I thought of is the fact that we would be indoors. How can I use that to my advantage? So I thought of using the walls as one of my tools."
    new "The first thing I thought of is the fact that we would be indoors. How can I use that to my advantage? So I thought of using the walls as one of my tools.\n我首先想到的，就是我们会身处室内。我该怎么利用这一点呢？于是我想到了把墙壁当作我的工具之一。"

    old "Furthermore, the undead tend to be a good deal more resilient than your typical warrior. Simply stabbing a vampire in the chest probably isn't enough to dispatch it. So I tried to come up with a way to deliver that blow with more force."
    new "Furthermore, the undead tend to be a good deal more resilient than your typical warrior. Simply stabbing a vampire in the chest probably isn't enough to dispatch it. So I tried to come up with a way to deliver that blow with more force.\n此外，亡灵往往比普通战士坚韧得多。仅仅一剑刺进吸血鬼的胸口，恐怕不足以结果它。于是我想方设法，让这一击带上更大的力道。"

    old "The downside is that it leaves me a bit more vulnerable than delivering a blow from a standing position. It's hard to feint or move evasively after embedding your blade in someone's chest, or worse whiffing the blow entirely and finding yourself with your blade planted in the ground. But I think that's a risk worth taking."
    new "The downside is that it leaves me a bit more vulnerable than delivering a blow from a standing position. It's hard to feint or move evasively after embedding your blade in someone's chest, or worse whiffing the blow entirely and finding yourself with your blade planted in the ground. But I think that's a risk worth taking.\n缺点在于，比起站着出招，它会让我更容易暴露。剑刺进对方胸口之后，你就很难再虚晃或灵活闪避了；更糟的是完全挥空，结果剑插进了地里。但我觉得，这个险值得冒。"

    old "Well, color me impressed."
    new "Well, color me impressed.\n嗯，我算是被你折服了。"

    old "I'd like to see how this combat trick holds up in practice."
    new "I'd like to see how this combat trick holds up in practice.\n我倒想看看，这格斗招式在实战里表现如何。"

    old "It probably won't be my first choice when we fight the undead. But it's something that may come in handy."
    new "It probably won't be my first choice when we fight the undead. But it's something that may come in handy.\n等我们和亡灵交战时，它大概不会是我的首选。但它总归是件可能派得上用场的东西。"

    old "I arrive at the Amazon citadel, and ask one of the sentries where to find Leena."
    new "I arrive at the Amazon citadel, and ask one of the sentries where to find Leena.\n我来到 Amazon 城堡，向一名哨兵打听去哪儿能找到 Leena。"

    old "Oh, Leena? She's on the west cobble with the princess."
    new "Oh, Leena? She's on the west cobble with the princess.\n哦，Leena？她和公主在西边石坪上。"

    old "The west cobble?"
    new "The west cobble?\n西边石坪？"

    old "It's like an indoor courtyard. Anyway, Leena is busy at the moment."
    new "It's like an indoor courtyard. Anyway, Leena is busy at the moment.\n就像个室内庭院。总之，Leena 现在正忙着。"

    old "That's fine, I'm willing to wait."
    new "That's fine, I'm willing to wait.\n没关系，我愿意等。"

    old "She might have another commitment after she's done with the princess, I'm not sure. You could be waiting quite awhile."
    new "She might have another commitment after she's done with the princess, I'm not sure. You could be waiting quite awhile.\n她和公主练完，可能还有别的安排，我不太确定。你兴许得等上好一阵子。"

    old "Well, I'm prepared to wait. You said she was on the west cobble?"
    new "Well, I'm prepared to wait. You said she was on the west cobble?\n嗯，我做好等的准备了。你说她在西边石坪？"

    old "Yes, I'll take you there."
    new "Yes, I'll take you there.\n是的，我带你过去。"

    old "Hiya!"
    new "Hiya!\n哈！"

    old "The princess's sword comes down at a harsh angle toward Leena's head, but Leena steps back and leans back, removing her head from its path. The blade hits Leena's breastplate with a resounding 'clang.'"
    new "The princess's sword comes down at a harsh angle toward Leena's head, but Leena steps back and leans back, removing her head from its path. The blade hits Leena's breastplate with a resounding 'clang.'\n公主的剑以一个刁钻的角度劈向 Leena 的头顶，但 Leena 后退一步、仰身一避，把头让开了剑路。剑刃击中 Leena 的胸甲，发出一声清脆的‘当’。"

    old "Leena pivots her body, swinging her leg toward the arms that are still gripping the sword. The princess drops the blade, sending it clattering to the floor."
    new "Leena pivots her body, swinging her leg toward the arms that are still gripping the sword. The princess drops the blade, sending it clattering to the floor.\nLeena 扭身转体，一腿扫向公主仍紧握着剑的双手。公主脱了手，剑哐当一声落在地上。"

    old "Leena continues spinning, swinging her leg in a complete arc, this time at ground level. With a quick sweep, the princess is knocked off her feet, and she falls to the ground, landing on her back."
    new "Leena continues spinning, swinging her leg in a complete arc, this time at ground level. With a quick sweep, the princess is knocked off her feet, and she falls to the ground, landing on her back.\nLeena 继续旋转，这次她的腿划出一道完整的弧线，贴着地面扫去。一个利落的扫堂腿，公主双脚离地，仰面摔倒在地。"

    old "Leena picks up the dropped sword and plants a foot on the princess's chest, positioning the point of the blade at her throat."
    new "Leena picks up the dropped sword and plants a foot on the princess's chest, positioning the point of the blade at her throat.\nLeena 捡起掉落的剑，一只脚踏在公主胸口，将剑尖抵在她的咽喉处。"

    old "Stab. You're dead."
    new "Stab. You're dead.\n一刺。你已经死了。"

    old "Leena tosses the sword aside and extends an open hand to the princess."
    new "Leena tosses the sword aside and extends an open hand to the princess.\nLeena 把剑丢到一旁，向公主伸出一只摊开的手。"

    old "Stand up."
    new "Stand up.\n站起来。"

    old "Leena helps the princess to her feet. The princess, still shaky from her fall, teeters a bit before regaining her footing."
    new "Leena helps the princess to her feet. The princess, still shaky from her fall, teeters a bit before regaining her footing.\nLeena 扶公主站起身来。公主仍因摔倒而双腿发软，摇晃了几下，才重新站稳。"

    old "Now, Loren. What did we learn today?"
    new "Now, Loren. What did we learn today?\n那么，Loren。今天学到了什么？"

    old "Colossal strikes leave you open to colossal punishment."
    new "Colossal strikes leave you open to colossal punishment.\n雷霆万钧的重击，会让自己暴露在雷霆万钧的惩罚之下。"

    old "What else?"
    new "What else?\n还有呢？"

    old "Landing on your back can be fatal against an alert opponent. And even when it isn't fatal, it hurts a lot."
    new "Landing on your back can be fatal against an alert opponent. And even when it isn't fatal, it hurts a lot.\n面对警觉的对手，仰面倒地可能是致命的。即便不致命，也疼得厉害。"

    old "Blades and lances are not your only weapons in battle. A well-placed kick or sweep can bring someone to their knees."
    new "Blades and lances are not your only weapons in battle. A well-placed kick or sweep can bring someone to their knees.\n刀剑和长枪，并不是你战斗中仅有的武器。一记恰到好处的踢击或扫腿，就能把人撂倒。"

    old "Um..."
    new "Um...\n呃……"

    old "Come on, Loren. What did you learn from this? Think about how we began the exercise."
    new "Come on, Loren. What did you learn from this? Think about how we began the exercise.\n想想看，Loren。你从中学到了什么？回想一下我们是怎么开始这场练习的。"

    old "A superior warrior can win even with inferior weapons?"
    new "A superior warrior can win even with inferior weapons?\n强大的战士，即便用劣等的武器也能取胜？"

    old "Try again."
    new "Try again.\n再想想。"

    old "Keep your wits about you?"
    new "Keep your wits about you?\n要保持头脑清醒？"

    old "Now you're not even trying."
    new "Now you're not even trying.\n这下你连猜都不认真猜了。"

    old "Amazon warriors with years of training and experience tend to be more adept at combat than teenage girls."
    new "Amazon warriors with years of training and experience tend to be more adept at combat than teenage girls.\n经过多年训练和实战的 Amazon 战士，通常比十几岁的少女更擅长战斗。"

    old "Well, if you're going to be sarcastic with me, then I guess there's nothing more to be gained from forcing you to guess. Count yourself lucky, Loren, that it's my role only to discipline you in matters of combat readiness, and not attitude."
    new "Well, if you're going to be sarcastic with me, then I guess there's nothing more to be gained from forcing you to guess. Count yourself lucky, Loren, that it's my role only to discipline you in matters of combat readiness, and not attitude.\n好吧，既然你要跟我耍嘴皮子，那我想逼你继续猜也没意义了。算你走运，Loren，我的职责只是管教你的战备，而不是你的态度。"

    old "A large swing is a high variance maneuver. It is a move that has high risk and high reward. Under what circumstances should you resort to tactics and maneuvers with high variance?"
    new "A large swing is a high variance maneuver. It is a move that has high risk and high reward. Under what circumstances should you resort to tactics and maneuvers with high variance?\n大幅挥砍，是一种高波动的招式。它风险高、回报也高。在什么情况下，你才该采用这种高波动的战术和招式？"

    old "When you are at a disadvantage and you need to shift the balance of a fight."
    new "When you are at a disadvantage and you need to shift the balance of a fight.\n当你处于劣势、需要扭转战局的时候。"

    old "Now, tell me. When one fighter is armed, and her opponent is not, who holds the advantage?"
    new "Now, tell me. When one fighter is armed, and her opponent is not, who holds the advantage?\n现在告诉我。当一方战士持有武器，而她的对手没有时，谁占优势？"

    old "The one holding the sword."
    new "The one holding the sword.\n持剑的那一方。"

    old "And who benefits from the introduction of higher variance?"
    new "And who benefits from the introduction of higher variance?\n那么，一旦引入更高的波动，谁又会受益？"

    old "The one who is unarmed."
    new "The one who is unarmed.\n手无寸铁的那一方。"

    old "So, tell me how you should have handled this scenario."
    new "So, tell me how you should have handled this scenario.\n那么，告诉我你本该如何应对这个局面。"

    old "I should have done my best to maintain the power advantage I had. I should have been more conservative, and focused on delivering short, quick stabs without compromising my combat posture. I should have taken control of the fight's tempo, and used my superior power to win a superior position to secure and assure my victory."
    new "I should have done my best to maintain the power advantage I had. I should have been more conservative, and focused on delivering short, quick stabs without compromising my combat posture. I should have taken control of the fight's tempo, and used my superior power to win a superior position to secure and assure my victory.\n我本该尽力保住自己已有的力量优势。我本该更稳健些，专注于使出短促迅捷的刺击，而不破坏自己的战斗姿态。我本该掌控战斗的节奏，用我更胜一筹的力量去抢占更有利的位置，从而确保、巩固我的胜利。"

    old "Well reasoned, Loren."
    new "Well reasoned, Loren.\n说得很在理，Loren。"

    old "Leena turns to me and gives a nod of recognition."
    new "Leena turns to me and gives a nod of recognition.\nLeena 转向我，点头致意。"

    old "Loren, we have a guest. This is [protag], a friend to both me and the queen."
    new "Loren, we have a guest. This is [protag], a friend to both me and the queen.\nLoren，我们有客人了。这位是 [protag]，是我和女王共同的朋友。"

    old "Hello, princess. I hope you'll pardon my interruption."
    new "Hello, princess. I hope you'll pardon my interruption.\n你好，公主。请原谅我的打扰。"

    old "You're not interrupting anything. We've actually just finished for the day. Loren, your last responsibility for today is to sharpen that blade of yours. That blow to my breastplate likely dulled it."
    new "You're not interrupting anything. We've actually just finished for the day. Loren, your last responsibility for today is to sharpen that blade of yours. That blow to my breastplate likely dulled it.\n你并没有打扰什么。我们其实正好结束今天的练习。Loren，你今天最后的任务，是把你的剑磨一磨。刚才那一下砍在我的胸甲上，剑刃八成卷了。"

    old "Hello, Loren. You're Karen's daughter, aren't you?"
    new "Hello, Loren. You're Karen's daughter, aren't you?\n你好，Loren。你是 Karen 的女儿，对吧？"

    old "She nods."
    new "She nods.\n她点了点头。"

    old "Being the princess is something that comes with a lot of responsibility. Hopefully, with the help of Leena here, you'll be ready to fill your mother's shoes when the time comes."
    new "Being the princess is something that comes with a lot of responsibility. Hopefully, with the help of Leena here, you'll be ready to fill your mother's shoes when the time comes.\n当公主，意味着要肩负许多责任。希望在 Leena 的帮助下，等时候到了，你能做好接替你母亲位置的准备。"

    old "Loren, we're done for today. Go sharpen that blade of yours. That blow to my breastplate likely dulled it."
    new "Loren, we're done for today. Go sharpen that blade of yours. That blow to my breastplate likely dulled it.\nLoren，今天就到此为止。去磨磨你的剑吧。刚才那一下砍在我的胸甲上，剑刃八成卷了。"

    old "Loren picks up the sword and leaves."
    new "Loren picks up the sword and leaves.\nLoren 捡起剑，离开了。"

    old "Hello, Leena. I hope I wasn't intruding."
    new "Hello, Leena. I hope I wasn't intruding.\n你好，Leena。希望我没有打扰到你。"

    old "Not at all. I think it does the princess some good to have an occasional spectator during her training. She can't live her whole life toiling away in private."
    new "Not at all. I think it does the princess some good to have an occasional spectator during her training. She can't live her whole life toiling away in private.\n一点也不。我觉得公主训练时偶尔有个人旁观，对她有好处。她不能一辈子都关起门来埋头苦练。"

    old "Was that a real sword she was using?"
    new "Was that a real sword she was using?\n她刚才用的，是一把真剑吗？"

    old "Why do you use real weapons for training? Wouldn't a wooden training sword be safer?"
    new "Why do you use real weapons for training? Wouldn't a wooden training sword be safer?\n你们为什么用真兵器训练？用木制的练习剑不是更安全吗？"

    old "A wooden sword lacks the same weight, feel, and heft of a real steel blade. And a dull practice blade doesn't cut through the air like a true, sharpened blade does. In order for the princess to prepare to use real weapons, she must practice with real weapons."
    new "A wooden sword lacks the same weight, feel, and heft of a real steel blade. And a dull practice blade doesn't cut through the air like a true, sharpened blade does. In order for the princess to prepare to use real weapons, she must practice with real weapons.\n木剑没有真钢剑那样的重量、手感和分量。而且钝的练习剑，划破空气的感觉也不如真正的利剑。为了让公主准备好使用真兵器，她就必须用真兵器来练习。"

    old "But what if you hadn't dodged her blow the way you did? What if that blade had gone straight into your skull like she intended?"
    new "But what if you hadn't dodged her blow the way you did? What if that blade had gone straight into your skull like she intended?\n可如果你没能像刚才那样躲开她的一击呢？如果那把剑如她所愿，径直刺进你的头颅呢？"

    old "Then the princess would have proved her merit in combat. My services as teacher would no longer be needed. If she misses, then I live to see another day. If she strikes me down, then the Amazon can rejoice in the fact that they have a princess who has proven her skill and overcome her teacher. Either way, it's a win-win."
    new "Then the princess would have proved her merit in combat. My services as teacher would no longer be needed. If she misses, then I live to see another day. If she strikes me down, then the Amazon can rejoice in the fact that they have a princess who has proven her skill and overcome her teacher. Either way, it's a win-win.\n那公主就在战斗中证明了自己的本事。我这老师便不再被需要了。她若失手，我就能活到明天。她若将我击倒，Amazon 们就该庆幸，他们有一位已证明自己的实力、并战胜了自己老师的公主。无论哪种结果，都是双赢。"

    old "I'm not sure I'd call it a win-win when one of the outcomes involves you dying."
    new "I'm not sure I'd call it a win-win when one of the outcomes involves you dying.\n当其中一种结果是你死掉时，我不确定这还能叫双赢。"

    old "Then you clearly don't understand the responsibilities that an Amazon of my station carries. I am the captain of the royal guard. I serve the interests of the royal bloodline. What's good for the bloodline is good for all the Amazons. And I am an Amazon. So really, by sacrificing my life for the queen, I am serving myself."
    new "Then you clearly don't understand the responsibilities that an Amazon of my station carries. I am the captain of the royal guard. I serve the interests of the royal bloodline. What's good for the bloodline is good for all the Amazons. And I am an Amazon. So really, by sacrificing my life for the queen, I am serving myself.\n那你显然还不明白，我这个身份的 Amazon 所肩负的责任。我是皇家卫队队长，效命于王室血脉的利益。对血脉有利的，就是对全体 Amazons 有利。而我也是 Amazon。所以，为女王献出生命，说到底也是在为我自己效命。"

    old "I suppose I can understand the idea of someone devoting herself to a higher calling. I can't say that I can relate to the idea of dying for duty, but at least I understand it."
    new "I suppose I can understand the idea of someone devoting herself to a higher calling. I can't say that I can relate to the idea of dying for duty, but at least I understand it.\n我想，我能理解一个人把自己奉献给更高使命的想法。虽然为职责而死，我还谈不上感同身受，但至少我能理解。"

    old "Perhaps one day you will find that calling which you are willing to die for."
    new "Perhaps one day you will find that calling which you are willing to die for.\n也许有一天，你会找到那个你甘愿为之赴死的使命。"

    old "I'll let you know if I ever do."
    new "I'll let you know if I ever do.\n若真有那么一天，我会告诉你的。"

    old "That's absurd. How can sacrificing your own life be self-serving?"
    new "That's absurd. How can sacrificing your own life be self-serving?\n太荒唐了。牺牲自己的性命，怎么还能说是为自己好？"

    old "Although I am a teacher, this is a lesson that I cannot forcibly impart to you or any other student. Perhaps one day, you will discover a higher calling of your own, and understand what it means to be willing to die for a cause. Until then, I hope that you can at least respect my own conviction to do so."
    new "Although I am a teacher, this is a lesson that I cannot forcibly impart to you or any other student. Perhaps one day, you will discover a higher calling of your own, and understand what it means to be willing to die for a cause. Until then, I hope that you can at least respect my own conviction to do so.\n虽然我是老师，但这一课，我却没法强行灌输给你或任何其他学生。也许有一天，你会找到属于自己的更高使命，明白甘愿为事业赴死意味着什么。在那之前，我希望你至少能尊重我这样做的信念。"

    old "You know that you have my respect, Leena."
    new "You know that you have my respect, Leena.\n你知道的，你一直拥有我的尊敬，Leena。"

    old "When did you make the decision to commit your life to the welfare of the Amazon royal bloodline? Was it part of your initiation into the royal guard?"
    new "When did you make the decision to commit your life to the welfare of the Amazon royal bloodline? Was it part of your initiation into the royal guard?\n你是从什么时候起，决定把自己的生命献给 Amazon 王室血脉的福祉的？那是你加入皇家卫队仪式的一部分吗？"

    old "I was committed to the royal bloodline long before I joined the guard. Commitment to a higher cause is not something that happens in any singular moment. It is something that you realize only in retrospect."
    new "I was committed to the royal bloodline long before I joined the guard. Commitment to a higher cause is not something that happens in any singular moment. It is something that you realize only in retrospect.\n早在我加入卫队之前，就已投身于王室血脉了。投身于更高的使命，并不是发生在某一个瞬间的事。它往往要等你回首往事时，才会意识到。"

    old "So, there's a moment of discovery and epiphany, but no moment of decision and choice?"
    new "So, there's a moment of discovery and epiphany, but no moment of decision and choice?\n那么，有的是发现与顿悟的时刻，却没有决定与选择的时刻？"

    old "Exactly. Commitment and loyalty is not a choice you make. It is something you discover within yourself."
    new "Exactly. Commitment and loyalty is not a choice you make. It is something you discover within yourself.\n正是如此。承诺与忠诚，不是你所做的选择，而是你在内心深处发现的东西。"

    old "Of course, there are vows that we take, and there is an initiation ceremony. But these rituals are mere formality. An Amazon protector is no less loyal the day before her commencement than the day after it."
    new "Of course, there are vows that we take, and there is an initiation ceremony. But these rituals are mere formality. An Amazon protector is no less loyal the day before her commencement than the day after it.\n当然，我们也会立誓，也有入门仪式。但这些仪式不过是形式罢了。一名 Amazon 护卫，在受任前一天，和受任后一天，忠诚丝毫不减。"

    old "I guess all relationships are like that. You don't ever decide to start liking someone. There usually isn't a point at which you decide to become someone's friend or companion. You only realize in retrospect that you've become close."
    new "I guess all relationships are like that. You don't ever decide to start liking someone. There usually isn't a point at which you decide to become someone's friend or companion. You only realize in retrospect that you've become close.\n我想所有关系都是如此。你从不会刻意决定去喜欢一个人。通常也没有哪个时刻，你会决定去成为某人的朋友或同伴。你只是回首时才发觉，彼此已经变得亲近。"

    old "So, [protag]. Would you say we're friends?"
    new "So, [protag]. Would you say we're friends?\n那么，[protag]。你觉得我们是朋友吗？"

    old "'Friend' isn't a label that I apply loosely. Friendship is a very intimate thing. My closest friends are trusted confidants."
    new "'Friend' isn't a label that I apply loosely. Friendship is a very intimate thing. My closest friends are trusted confidants.\n‘朋友’这个标签，我不会随便乱用。友谊是种非常亲密的关系。我最亲近的朋友，都是我信赖的知己。"

    old "Leena, you and I are allies. We share a mission. We have the same goals. And I trust your talent in combat and your faithfulness to our shared objective. I'd even trust you with my life. But to say that we're friends..."
    new "Leena, you and I are allies. We share a mission. We have the same goals. And I trust your talent in combat and your faithfulness to our shared objective. I'd even trust you with my life. But to say that we're friends...\nLeena，你我是盟友。我们共担使命，目标一致。我相信你的战斗才能，也相信你对我们共同目标的忠诚。我甚至敢把性命托付给你。但要说我们是朋友……"

    old "Maybe we will be friends some day. Until then, I'm still happy to have you watching my back."
    new "Maybe we will be friends some day. Until then, I'm still happy to have you watching my back.\n也许有一天，我们会成为朋友。在那之前，有你在我身后照应，我依然很高兴。"

    old "I appreciate your candidness. It's a rare thing to find, especially outside the walls of this citadel."
    new "I appreciate your candidness. It's a rare thing to find, especially outside the walls of this citadel.\n我很感激你的坦诚。这份坦诚实属难得，尤其在这座城堡的城墙之外。"

    old "Let's give those vampires what's coming to them. The Castle of N'Mar is an imposing structure, but with you in command, that goal doesn't feel so far-fetched."
    new "Let's give those vampires what's coming to them. The Castle of N'Mar is an imposing structure, but with you in command, that goal doesn't feel so far-fetched.\n让我们去给那些吸血鬼一点应有的教训。N'Mar 城堡固然气势逼人，但有你在指挥，那个目标也就不显得那么遥不可及了。"

    old "Are we friends? I'd like to think so."
    new "Are we friends? I'd like to think so.\n我们是朋友吗？我挺愿意这么想。"

    old "I'd like to think so too, [protag]. I'm glad you feel the same way."
    new "I'd like to think so too, [protag]. I'm glad you feel the same way.\n我也愿意这么想，[protag]。很高兴你也这么觉得。"

    old "Do you think think that maybe we're..."
    new "Do you think think that maybe we're...\n你觉得，也许我们……"

    old "Maybe we're what?"
    new "Maybe we're what?\n也许我们什么？"

    old "I don't know. I'm not sure what we are, what you call this thing between me and you. Would it be horrible for me to just say that right now I'm enjoying it for what it is, whatever that may happen to be?"
    new "I don't know. I'm not sure what we are, what you call this thing between me and you. Would it be horrible for me to just say that right now I'm enjoying it for what it is, whatever that may happen to be?\n我不知道。我不确定我们算什么，也不知道该怎么称呼你我之间的这种关系。如果我就直说，眼下我很享受它本来的样子，不管它到底是什么，会不会显得很糟？"

    old "I was thinking exactly the same thing."
    new "I was thinking exactly the same thing.\n我也正是这么想的。"

    old "[protag], you're a very...you're a special woman. You're someone that, for better or for worse, I've grown quite fond of."
    new "[protag], you're a very...you're a special woman. You're someone that, for better or for worse, I've grown quite fond of.\n[protag]，你是一个非常……你是个特别的女人。你是我不管怎样，都已经越来越喜欢的人。"

    old "I've never felt like this before. Where will it lead? I don't know. But I want to keep feeling this excited every time I see you."
    new "I've never felt like this before. Where will it lead? I don't know. But I want to keep feeling this excited every time I see you.\n我以前从没有过这样的感觉。它会走向何方？我不知道。但我希望每次见到你，都能一直这样怦然心动。"

    old "I feel exactly the same way."
    new "I feel exactly the same way.\n我也完全一样。"

    old "[protag]. What a pleasure to see you."
    new "[protag]. What a pleasure to see you.\n[protag]。见到你真是荣幸。"

    old "Is it really a pleasure to see me?"
    new "Is it really a pleasure to see me?\n见到我，真的是荣幸吗？"

    old "Ha, that's a fair question. I have to admit, most of the time when people impose on me to chat, I tend to offer a formal greeting, sometimes saying even saying 'it's a pleasure' when it really isn't. But with you, I really mean it. I enjoy talking to you."
    new "Ha, that's a fair question. I have to admit, most of the time when people impose on me to chat, I tend to offer a formal greeting, sometimes saying even saying 'it's a pleasure' when it really isn't. But with you, I really mean it. I enjoy talking to you.\n哈，这问题问得在理。我得承认，大多数时候别人硬凑过来找我闲聊，我往往会客套地打个招呼，有时甚至会说‘荣幸之至’，其实并不然。但对你，我是真心实意的。我喜欢和你聊天。"

    old "I've enjoyed talking to you as well, Leena."
    new "I've enjoyed talking to you as well, Leena.\n我也很喜欢和你聊天，Leena。"

    old "It's strange. Normally I find conversation so ordinary and routine. I'd much rather spend my time doing things than talking about them. That's not to say that I find conversation boring, per se, but when I compare it to the rush I get from swinging a blade, there's on comparison."
    new "It's strange. Normally I find conversation so ordinary and routine. I'd much rather spend my time doing things than talking about them. That's not to say that I find conversation boring, per se, but when I compare it to the rush I get from swinging a blade, there's on comparison.\n很奇怪。我通常觉得交谈平淡而乏味。我更愿意把时间花在做事情上，而不是谈论事情。这倒不是说我觉得交谈本身无聊，只是和挥剑带来的快感相比，实在没法比。"

    old "But talking with you is different. A conversation with you is like a small adventure. I can never predict what you'll say next. It's energizing."
    new "But talking with you is different. A conversation with you is like a small adventure. I can never predict what you'll say next. It's energizing.\n但和你聊天不一样。和你聊天就像一场小小的冒险。我永远猜不到你下一句会说什么。这让人精神振奋。"

    old "Yet, in spite of all your surprises, you're a capable and solid leader. I can follow you into battle without fearing for my life. Somehow, whenever I'm fighting with you, I feel assured that no matter how the battle goes, everything will turn out alright. And yet, on the battlefield, you are still that wildcard who is full of surprises."
    new "Yet, in spite of all your surprises, you're a capable and solid leader. I can follow you into battle without fearing for my life. Somehow, whenever I'm fighting with you, I feel assured that no matter how the battle goes, everything will turn out alright. And yet, on the battlefield, you are still that wildcard who is full of surprises.\n然而，尽管你处处出人意料，你却是个能干又可靠的领袖。我可以跟着你上战场，而不必担心性命。不知怎的，每当和你并肩作战，我就感到安心：无论战局如何，一切都会没事的。可在战场上，你依然还是那个充满惊喜的变数。"

    old "I never know what awaits us when we go to battle. But I never have to feel afraid or unsure."
    new "I never know what awaits us when we go to battle. But I never have to feel afraid or unsure.\n我从来不知道上战场后等待我们的是什么。但我从不必感到害怕或忐忑。"

    old "How does that make sense? You are reliable, yet unpredictable. It seems like a paradox, and yet, that's who you've proven yourself to be, time and time again."
    new "How does that make sense? You are reliable, yet unpredictable. It seems like a paradox, and yet, that's who you've proven yourself to be, time and time again.\n这怎么讲得通？你可靠，却又难以捉摸。这看似是个悖论，可你一次又一次证明了自己就是这样的人。"

    old "Leena, I think what you're describing is known as 'trust.' It's what happens when you put your faith in someone. It's the same relationship that you have with any leader. I would hope that your underlings put the same kind of faith in you."
    new "Leena, I think what you're describing is known as 'trust.' It's what happens when you put your faith in someone. It's the same relationship that you have with any leader. I would hope that your underlings put the same kind of faith in you.\nLeena，我想你描述的，正是所谓的‘信任’。当你把信念寄托在某人身上时，就会如此。这跟你与任何领袖的关系都一样。我也希望你的部下能对你抱有同样的信任。"

    old "It's the kind of loyalty that inspires you to pledge to follow someone orders, even when you don't know what those orders are going to be, because you trust that person to make the right decisions."
    new "It's the kind of loyalty that inspires you to pledge to follow someone orders, even when you don't know what those orders are going to be, because you trust that person to make the right decisions.\n正是这种忠诚，激励你宣誓服从某人的命令，哪怕你并不知道那命令会是什么，因为你相信那个人会做出正确的决定。"

    old "I'm glad to have earned your loyalty, Leena. I get the feeling that it's not something that you dispense lightly."
    new "I'm glad to have earned your loyalty, Leena. I get the feeling that it's not something that you dispense lightly.\n能赢得你的忠诚，我很高兴，Leena。我感觉，你的忠诚绝不是轻易给予的。"

    old "You assume correctly. [protag], there's something I haven't told you about. I've been working on a little side project. I wasn't sure if it would lead anywhere, so I kept quiet about it, but now I finally have something to show for my efforts."
    new "You assume correctly. [protag], there's something I haven't told you about. I've been working on a little side project. I wasn't sure if it would lead anywhere, so I kept quiet about it, but now I finally have something to show for my efforts.\n你猜得没错。[protag]，有件事我一直没告诉你。我一直在捣鼓一个小项目。我不确定它会不会有结果，所以一直没声张。但现在，我的努力终于有了点拿得出手的成果。"

    old "Though, really they're not my own efforts so much as the efforts of a certain smithy in Grimoire, and the guidance of a certain archwizard. You've met Apolimesho yourself, I'm sure."
    new "Though, really they're not my own efforts so much as the efforts of a certain smithy in Grimoire, and the guidance of a certain archwizard. You've met Apolimesho yourself, I'm sure.\n不过说真的，这与其说是我自己的努力，不如说是 Grimoire 某位铁匠的心血，外加某位大法师的指点。你本人肯定见过 Apolimesho 了。"

    old "Yes, I've met him. But I'm curious what kind of assistance an Amazon like you would need from a wizard. I thought Amazons didn't have much affinity for magic."
    new "Yes, I've met him. But I'm curious what kind of assistance an Amazon like you would need from a wizard. I thought Amazons didn't have much affinity for magic.\n是的，我见过他。不过我很好奇，像你这样的 Amazon，会需要一位法师提供什么帮助。我还以为 Amazons 对魔法没多少亲和力。"

    old "I could tell you, but showing you would be much more exciting. Come on, follow me."
    new "I could tell you, but showing you would be much more exciting. Come on, follow me.\n我可以讲给你听，不过亲眼看看要刺激得多。来吧，跟我走。"

    old "Leena draws a sword from its sheath and holds it aloft."
    new "Leena draws a sword from its sheath and holds it aloft.\nLeena 从剑鞘中抽出一把剑，高高举起。"

    old "What's special about this one?"
    new "What's special about this one?\n这把有什么特别之处？"

    old "Watch."
    new "Watch.\n看好了。"

    old "Leena swings the sword in a horizontal arc, and as it cuts through the air, I see flames erupt from its edge."
    new "Leena swings the sword in a horizontal arc, and as it cuts through the air, I see flames erupt from its edge.\nLeena 横着挥出一个圆弧，剑刃破空之际，我看见火焰从剑锋上喷涌而出。"

    old "Is that...fire?"
    new "Is that...fire?\n那是……火？"

    old "Indeed it is."
    new "Indeed it is.\n正是。"

    old "You forged a flame-bladed sword?"
    new "You forged a flame-bladed sword?\n你打造了一把带火焰的剑？"

    old "It's not the blade that's special, actually. It's the hilt. That's what's so interesting about this one: theoretically, I should be able to match this hilt with any blade. Forging it was no small task."
    new "It's not the blade that's special, actually. It's the hilt. That's what's so interesting about this one: theoretically, I should be able to match this hilt with any blade. Forging it was no small task.\n其实特别的不在剑刃，而在剑柄。这才是它有趣的地方：理论上，我应该能把这只剑柄配到任何剑刃上。打造它可费了不少功夫。"

    old "So that's what you needed Apolimesho's help for. How did you get the council to approve something like this? Given the relationship that the Amazons have with the human empire, it seems odd for them to share something like this."
    new "So that's what you needed Apolimesho's help for. How did you get the council to approve something like this? Given the relationship that the Amazons have with the human empire, it seems odd for them to share something like this.\n所以你需要 Apolimesho 帮忙，就是为了这个。你是怎么说动议会批准这种东西的？考虑到 Amazons 与人类帝国的关系，他们会分享这样的东西，实在有些奇怪。"

    old "The relationship between the Amazons and humans has changed, thanks to this business with N'Mar. I also get some unique treatment, due to the nature of our relationship. So really, I have you to thank for this blade here."
    new "The relationship between the Amazons and humans has changed, thanks to this business with N'Mar. I also get some unique treatment, due to the nature of our relationship. So really, I have you to thank for this blade here.\n多亏了 N'Mar 这档子事，Amazons 与人类的关系已经变了。加上你我之间的关系，我也得到了一些特殊对待。所以，这把剑，我其实该谢你。"

    old "How does it work, if you have no magical affinity yourself?"
    new "How does it work, if you have no magical affinity yourself?\n你本人没有魔法亲和力，它又是怎么起作用的？"

    old "Honestly? I wish I knew. Apolimesho himself doesn't entirely understand it. Ordinary magic is something that originates from within a person, but making the flame dance from this blade is something else entirely. It's all about technique. And that technique has taken me hundreds of hours of practice to hone."
    new "Honestly? I wish I knew. Apolimesho himself doesn't entirely understand it. Ordinary magic is something that originates from within a person, but making the flame dance from this blade is something else entirely. It's all about technique. And that technique has taken me hundreds of hours of practice to hone.\n说实话，我也希望自己知道。连 Apolimesho 本人都不完全明白。普通魔法源自人的体内，但让火焰从这剑上腾跃而起，却是完全另一回事。关键全在技巧。而这技巧，我花了数百小时的练习才磨炼出来。"

    old "It would probably not be practical to outfit an entire army with these. But for as long as I'm fighting with you, you can have at least one flame-kissed blade at your side."
    new "It would probably not be practical to outfit an entire army with these. But for as long as I'm fighting with you, you can have at least one flame-kissed blade at your side.\n给整支军队都配上这种剑，大概不现实。但在我与你并肩作战的日子里，你身边至少能有一把吻过火焰的利剑。"

    old "That's incredible, Leena. I look forward to seeing it in action."
    new "That's incredible, Leena. I look forward to seeing it in action.\n这太了不起了，Leena。我期待看到它实战发挥。"

    old "I find Leena standing in one of the Citadel's halls, conversing with another Amazon. She finishes her conversation, and the other woman leaves. Leena spots me and smiles, waving a hand to beckon me over."
    new "I find Leena standing in one of the Citadel's halls, conversing with another Amazon. She finishes her conversation, and the other woman leaves. Leena spots me and smiles, waving a hand to beckon me over.\n我找到 Leena 时，她正站在城堡的一间厅堂里，与另一位 Amazon 交谈。她结束了谈话，那女人便离开了。Leena 看到了我，笑着挥手示意我过去。"

    old "What was that about? Something I should be aware of?"
    new "What was that about? Something I should be aware of?\n刚才那是什么事？有什么我该知道的吗？"

    old "Ah, funny you should ask. I've been trying to come up with tools that might be effective against the undead. I've always considered fire to be a particularly potent weapon."
    new "Ah, funny you should ask. I've been trying to come up with tools that might be effective against the undead. I've always considered fire to be a particularly potent weapon.\n啊，你问得正巧。我一直在琢磨能有效对付亡灵的工具。我一直认为火是种格外有力的武器。"

    old "Fighting with fire, eh? I didn't realize that Amazons had an affinity for magic."
    new "Fighting with fire, eh? I didn't realize that Amazons had an affinity for magic.\n用火作战，嗯？我倒不知道 Amazons 对魔法还有亲和力。"

    old "We don't, actually. I had this one special ordered from a smithy in Grimoire who specializes in this sort of thing, and got a little help from a certain archwizard on the council."
    new "We don't, actually. I had this one special ordered from a smithy in Grimoire who specializes in this sort of thing, and got a little help from a certain archwizard on the council.\n其实并没有。这是我特意从 Grimoire 一家专做此道的铁匠铺订制的，还得了议会里某位大法师的一点帮助。"

    old "Seems strange for the Grimoire council to approve that kind of request, coming from an Amazon."
    new "Seems strange for the Grimoire council to approve that kind of request, coming from an Amazon.\nGrimoire 议会居然批准一位 Amazon 提出这种请求，这似乎有点奇怪。"

    old "We live in unusual times, [protag]. Humans and Amazons normally don't get along this well, but when a common enemy appears, alliances pop up in the oddest of places."
    new "We live in unusual times, [protag]. Humans and Amazons normally don't get along this well, but when a common enemy appears, alliances pop up in the oddest of places.\n我们身处不寻常的年代，[protag]。人类和 Amazons 平时不会这么和睦，可一旦出现共同的敌人，联盟就会在最意想不到的地方冒出来。"

    old "Much like the alliance between Grimoire and the Amazons, our relationship seems anything but ordinary."
    new "Much like the alliance between Grimoire and the Amazons, our relationship seems anything but ordinary.\n就像 Grimoire 与 Amazons 之间的联盟一样，我们之间的关系也绝不普通。"

    old "Is that a good thing?"
    new "Is that a good thing?\n这是件好事吗？"

    old "Well, there is one thing in particular about our relationship that I find odd. I almost hesitate to bring it up."
    new "Well, there is one thing in particular about our relationship that I find odd. I almost hesitate to bring it up.\n嗯，我们的关系里，有一件事特别让我觉得奇怪。我几乎犹豫着要不要提。"

    old "Knowing you, 'odd' probably means exciting. Hit me with it."
    new "Knowing you, 'odd' probably means exciting. Hit me with it.\n以我对你的了解，‘奇怪’大概意味着刺激。说来听听吧。"

    old "I feel strange sharing this with you, considering that I don't really understand it myself, but the time that I spent with you is...special."
    new "I feel strange sharing this with you, considering that I don't really understand it myself, but the time that I spent with you is...special.\n跟你说这个，我觉得有些难为情，因为我自己也说不清，但和你共度的时光……很特别。"

    old "Special in what way?"
    new "Special in what way?\n怎么个特别法？"

    old "Well, I have a way of categorizing activities. As part of my training I've learned to actively monitor my heartbeat, and I keep track of the effect that certain activities have on my the rate at which it beats."
    new "Well, I have a way of categorizing activities. As part of my training I've learned to actively monitor my heartbeat, and I keep track of the effect that certain activities have on my the rate at which it beats.\n嗯，我有种给活动分类的方法。作为训练的一部分，我学会了主动监测自己的心跳，并记录某些活动对我心跳快慢的影响。"

    old "That's certainly...unique."
    new "That's certainly...unique.\n这确实……很独特。"

    old "There are activities that elevate my heart rate, like running or practicing physical combat. And there are activities which seem to lower my heart rate-menial and relaxing tasks."
    new "There are activities that elevate my heart rate, like running or practicing physical combat. And there are activities which seem to lower my heart rate-menial and relaxing tasks.\n有些活动会让我心跳加速，比如跑步或练习格斗。还有些活动似乎会让我的心跳放缓——那些琐碎而放松的活计。"

    old "Depending on who I'm talking to, my heart's activity tends to be very consistent. When speaking to the queen, for example, I am in a state of heightened alertness, and my heart rate goes up. But when I talk to a casual acquaintance, I tend to relax, and my heart rate goes down."
    new "Depending on who I'm talking to, my heart's activity tends to be very consistent. When speaking to the queen, for example, I am in a state of heightened alertness, and my heart rate goes up. But when I talk to a casual acquaintance, I tend to relax, and my heart rate goes down.\n根据我谈话对象的不同，我心脏的活动往往非常一致。比如和女王说话时，我处于高度警觉的状态，心率会上升。但和泛泛之交聊天时，我往往会放松下来，心率也随之下降。"

    old "So, which one am I?"
    new "So, which one am I?\n那么，我属于哪一种？"

    old "That's the strangest thing. With you, it's never just one or the other. There are a lot of times when talking to you makes makes my heart beat slower. Like I'm relaxing, and letting my guard down. But there are other times when the opposite happens."
    new "That's the strangest thing. With you, it's never just one or the other. There are a lot of times when talking to you makes makes my heart beat slower. Like I'm relaxing, and letting my guard down. But there are other times when the opposite happens.\n最奇怪的地方就在这。跟你在一起，从来不是非此即彼。很多时候，和你说话会让我的心跳变慢，就像我放松下来、卸下了防备。但另一些时候，又恰恰相反。"

    old "I don't know why my heart speeds up, but there are some moments when it just happens."
    new "I don't know why my heart speeds up, but there are some moments when it just happens.\n我不知道我的心为什么会加速，但有那么一些时刻，它就是会这样。"

    old "Leena takes a step toward me and looks into my eyes. Her voice lowers to a whisper."
    new "Leena takes a step toward me and looks into my eyes. Her voice lowers to a whisper.\nLeena 朝我走近一步，凝视着我的眼睛。她的声音低成了耳语。"

    old "This is one of those moments."
    new "This is one of those moments.\n现在就是那样的时刻。"

    old "Leena grabs my hand, and guides it upward, placing it on her chest. I can feel the rapid thumping of her heartbeat."
    new "Leena grabs my hand, and guides it upward, placing it on her chest. I can feel the rapid thumping of her heartbeat.\nLeena 抓住我的手，引着它向上，按在她的胸口上。我能感觉到她的心跳，正急促地怦怦直跳。"

    old "I lean in and whisper."
    new "I lean in and whisper.\n我俯身凑近，低声说道。"

    old "Your heart is beating so fast right now."
    new "Your heart is beating so fast right now.\n你的心跳现在好快。"

    old "I grab her hand and pace it against my chest."
    new "I grab her hand and pace it against my chest.\n我抓住她的手，把它按在我的胸口上。"

    old "Mine too."
    new "Mine too.\n我也是。"

    old "I hold eye contact, gazing into her eyes. Have I ever seen eyes as blue and as beautiful as hers?"
    new "I hold eye contact, gazing into her eyes. Have I ever seen eyes as blue and as beautiful as hers?\n我凝视着她的双眼，目光不曾移开。我何曾见过这样湛蓝、这样美丽的眼睛？"

    old "Leena wraps an arm around me, pulling me in, and I close my eyes as our lips meet."
    new "Leena wraps an arm around me, pulling me in, and I close my eyes as our lips meet.\nLeena 用一只手臂环住我，把我拉向她，就在我们的唇相触的那一刻，我闭上了眼睛。"

    old "Our kiss lasts for...minutes? Hours? Whatever it is, it's not nearly enough."
    new "Our kiss lasts for...minutes? Hours? Whatever it is, it's not nearly enough.\n这个吻持续了……几分钟？几小时？不管多久，都远远不够。"

    old "As our lips part, a gasp escapes my lips."
    new "As our lips part, a gasp escapes my lips.\n当我们的唇分开时，一声轻喘逸出了我的嘴角。"

    old "Leena-what is happening?"
    new "Leena-what is happening?\nLeena——这是怎么回事？"

    old "Shh."
    new "Shh.\n嘘。"

    old "Leena places a hand on the small of my back, and pulls me in tighter this time as she guides my mouth to hers."
    new "Leena places a hand on the small of my back, and pulls me in tighter this time as she guides my mouth to hers.\nLeena 一只手放在我的后腰上，这次把我拉得更紧，同时引着我的嘴迎向她的唇。"

    old "I can feel her chest-her heartbeat-against my chest. As her mouth explores mine and her hands caress my back, I place my arms around her waist, her pulling her hips in to meet mine."
    new "I can feel her chest-her heartbeat-against my chest. As her mouth explores mine and her hands caress my back, I place my arms around her waist, her pulling her hips in to meet mine.\n我能感觉到她的胸口——她的心跳——紧贴着我的胸膛。她的唇探索着我的唇，她的手抚过我的背，我也用双臂环住她的腰，把她拉向我，让她的髋部贴上来。"

    old "I hear the sound of a door opening, and we both freeze in place. Footsteps grow closer, and Leena pushes me against a pillar connected to the wall."
    new "I hear the sound of a door opening, and we both freeze in place. Footsteps grow closer, and Leena pushes me against a pillar connected to the wall.\n我听见开门的声音，我们俩都僵在了原地。脚步声越来越近，Leena 把我推到墙边的一根柱子上。"

    old "The footsteps start to recede, and we both begin breathing heavily. Every time Leena's hot breath tickles my ear, I feel my heart skip."
    new "The footsteps start to recede, and we both begin breathing heavily. Every time Leena's hot breath tickles my ear, I feel my heart skip.\n脚步声开始远去，我们俩都大口喘着气。Leena 灼热的呼吸每次搔过我的耳畔，我的心都会漏跳一拍。"

    old "We can't be doing this out here. Meet me up in my room."
    new "We can't be doing this out here. Meet me up in my room.\n我们不能在这儿这样。到我房间来找我。"

    old "Leena leads me up to her room, and asks me to wait at the door for a minute before she beckons me in."
    new "Leena leads me up to her room, and asks me to wait at the door for a minute before she beckons me in.\nLeena 带我上了楼，来到她房间前，让我在门口等一会儿，然后才招手唤我进去。"

    old "I gasp and find myself breathless at the sight of the beauty before me."
    new "I gasp and find myself breathless at the sight of the beauty before me.\n望着眼前的美人，我深吸一口气，竟看得屏住了呼吸。"

    old "I think this is the first time I've ever seen you out of armor, Leena."
    new "I think this is the first time I've ever seen you out of armor, Leena.\n我想，这还是我第一次看到你脱下盔甲的样子，Leena。"

    old "I've spent so much time wearing armor that I've become more comfortable when wearing it. Without it, I feel vulnerable. It can be unsettling to face the world without covering your weaknesses."
    new "I've spent so much time wearing armor that I've become more comfortable when wearing it. Without it, I feel vulnerable. It can be unsettling to face the world without covering your weaknesses.\n我穿了太久盔甲，反而穿着它才更自在。没了它，我觉得自己很脆弱。不遮住自己的弱点就去面对世界，会让人心里发慌。"

    old "But when I'm with you, I feel like I want to become vulnerable. I want you to touch me and feel me where I'm most tender and sensitive."
    new "But when I'm with you, I feel like I want to become vulnerable. I want you to touch me and feel me where I'm most tender and sensitive.\n但和你在一起时，我却想变得脆弱。我想让你触碰我，感受我最柔软、最敏感的地方。"

    old "Do you really mean that?"
    new "Do you really mean that?\n你这话是当真的吗？"

    old "Would I have said it if I didn't?"
    new "Would I have said it if I didn't?\n若不是当真，我又何必说出口？"

    old "I smirk back."
    new "I smirk back.\n我也回以一个坏笑。"

    old "You should be careful what you wish for."
    new "You should be careful what you wish for.\n那你可得小心，别乱许愿。"

    old "I spend one last moment admiring Leena's body before tearing off my own equipment. I leap onto the bed, landing on top of her, and place my hands on her shoulders, pinning her to the bed."
    new "I spend one last moment admiring Leena's body before tearing off my own equipment. I leap onto the bed, landing on top of her, and place my hands on her shoulders, pinning her to the bed.\n我最后欣赏了片刻 Leena 的身体，便扯下自己的装备。我跳上床，落在她身上，双手按住她的肩膀，把她压在了床上。"

    old "Leena yelps as I push my face into her neck and begin caressing it with my mouth, planting kisses in a line from her ear to the base of her throat."
    new "Leena yelps as I push my face into her neck and begin caressing it with my mouth, planting kisses in a line from her ear to the base of her throat.\n我把脸埋进她的颈间，用嘴轻轻摩挲，从她的耳畔一路吻到她的颈窝。Leena 轻叫出声。"

    old "[protag]—"
    new "[protag]—\n[protag]——"

    old "Leena gasps as I tickle her earlobe with my tongue."
    new "Leena gasps as I tickle her earlobe with my tongue.\n我用舌尖逗弄她的耳垂，Leena 喘了一声。"

    old "I wasn't expecting you to be so—ah—aggressive."
    new "I wasn't expecting you to be so—ah—aggressive.\n我没想到你会这么——啊——狂野。"

    old "I've always wanted to see what was under that armor of yours. Now I finally get to enjoy it."
    new "I've always wanted to see what was under that armor of yours. Now I finally get to enjoy it.\n我一直想看看，你那身盔甲底下是什么样。现在总算能好好欣赏了。"

    old "I resume kissing Leena's neck, slowly working my way down to her chest. As I tear the last strips of cloth from her body, I lock eyes with her. She smiles at me with large, loving eyes."
    new "I resume kissing Leena's neck, slowly working my way down to her chest. As I tear the last strips of cloth from her body, I lock eyes with her. She smiles at me with large, loving eyes.\n我继续亲吻 Leena 的脖颈，缓缓向下移到她的胸口。当我扯下她身上最后几缕衣物时，我迎上了她的目光。她对我微笑，那双大眼睛里满是爱意。"

    old "That day when I first met you, I never expected it would lead to this."
    new "That day when I first met you, I never expected it would lead to this.\n初次见你的那天，我从没想过会走到这一步。"

    old "What about this?"
    new "What about this?\n那这样呢？"

    old "I place a hand on her inner thigh, and give it a light squeeze. I place my ear against her chest, allowing myself to hear her heartbeat. As I work my fingers up her leg, her heartbeat grows faster and faster."
    new "I place a hand on her inner thigh, and give it a light squeeze. I place my ear against her chest, allowing myself to hear her heartbeat. As I work my fingers up her leg, her heartbeat grows faster and faster.\n我一只手抚上她的大腿内侧，轻轻一捏。我把耳朵贴在她胸口，让自己听见她的心跳。随着我的手指沿她的腿缓缓上移，她的心跳也越来越快。"

    old "[protag], you are full of surpris—ah!"
    new "[protag], you are full of surpris—ah!\n[protag]，你真是处处给人惊——啊！"

    old "I notice Leena seems about to speak but she stops. Could it be that something is on her mind that she's afraid to tell me?"
    new "I notice Leena seems about to speak but she stops. Could it be that something is on her mind that she's afraid to tell me?\n我注意到 Leena 似乎想说什么，却又停住了。莫非她心里有什么事，不敢告诉我？"

    old "What is it, Leena? Tell me."
    new "What is it, Leena? Tell me.\n怎么了，Leena？告诉我。"

    old "The naga you recruited."
    new "The naga you recruited.\n你招募的那个 Naga。"

    old "Well, I admit she's rather... unique, but she's an excellent fighter. And very good if you need to lighten the mood."
    new "Well, I admit she's rather... unique, but she's an excellent fighter. And very good if you need to lighten the mood.\n嗯，我承认她是挺……独特的，但她是名出色的战士。而且要想活跃气氛，她也很拿手。"

    old "Enok? He is a valuable member of our team. An excellent mage who comes with combat prowess and a lot of knowledge."
    new "Enok? He is a valuable member of our team. An excellent mage who comes with combat prowess and a lot of knowledge.\nEnok？他是我们队里宝贵的一员。一位出色的法师，既有一身战斗本领，又学识渊博。"

    old "Are you familiar with nagas? They're... brutal. They have no remorse when it comes to killing other living beings."
    new "Are you familiar with nagas? They're... brutal. They have no remorse when it comes to killing other living beings.\n你熟悉 Nagas 吗？他们……很凶残。杀害其他生灵时，他们毫无悔意。"

    old "Don't get me wrong. I think they are very talented, and I'm glad they're on our side."
    new "Don't get me wrong. I think they are very talented, and I'm glad they're on our side.\n别误会。我觉得他们很有本事，也很高兴他们站在我们这边。"

    old "However, there's something disturbing in the way nagas fight. They really enjoy it."
    new "However, there's something disturbing in the way nagas fight. They really enjoy it.\n不过，Nagas 的战斗方式里有种令人不安的东西。他们是真的乐在其中。"

    old "I kill enemies too, but for necessity. Not for fun."
    new "I kill enemies too, but for necessity. Not for fun.\n我也杀敌，但那是出于必要，而不是为了取乐。"

    old "I understand what you're saying. But given the task ahead of us, I'm going to take all the help I can get."
    new "I understand what you're saying. But given the task ahead of us, I'm going to take all the help I can get.\n我明白你的意思。但考虑到眼前的艰巨任务，能有的帮手，我都想用上。"

    old "If this means having a...bloodthirsty naga in our team, then so be it."
    new "If this means having a...bloodthirsty naga in our team, then so be it.\n哪怕这意味着队里要有个……嗜血的 Naga，那也无妨。"

    old "You don't understand. They can't be trusted. They could be a danger for our own team."
    new "You don't understand. They can't be trusted. They could be a danger for our own team.\n你不明白。他们不可信。他们可能会危及我们自己的队伍。"

    old "In which way?"
    new "In which way?\n怎么个危及法？"

    old "They're reckless. They could charge an enemy, in a situation where it was better to pause and think."
    new "They're reckless. They could charge an enemy, in a situation where it was better to pause and think.\n他们很莽撞。在那种本该停下来三思的情况下，他们却可能径直冲向敌人。"

    old "A good fighter realizes that survival and killing are both important. But a bloodlust causes you to lose sight of the importance of your own survival–and the survival of your allies."
    new "A good fighter realizes that survival and killing are both important. But a bloodlust causes you to lose sight of the importance of your own survival–and the survival of your allies.\n优秀的战士明白，生存与杀敌同样重要。但嗜血的冲动，会让你忘记自身生存的重要——以及盟友生存的重要。"

    old "I didn't think about it that way. However..."
    new "I didn't think about it that way. However...\n我倒没从这个角度想过。不过……"

    old "Leena, let me reassure you about one thing."
    new "Leena, let me reassure you about one thing.\nLeena，有件事我要让你放心。"

    old "When I met Sylrissa and Enok, Enok told me their story. They reject the nagas mentality completely. They're exiles, and there's a reason for that. They're more like us than you seem to think."
    new "When I met Sylrissa and Enok, Enok told me their story. They reject the nagas mentality completely. They're exiles, and there's a reason for that. They're more like us than you seem to think.\n我遇到 Sylrissa 和 Enok 时，Enok 给我讲了他们的故事。他们彻底摒弃了 Nagas 的那套心态。他们是流亡者，而流亡自有其原因。他们比你想的要更像我们。"

    old "Maybe, but it still shows in the fights. The brutality..."
    new "Maybe, but it still shows in the fights. The brutality...\n也许吧，但在战斗中还是会显露出来。那股凶残劲……"

    old "As long as they're brutal with undead, I have no problems with it. But anyway, what would you want me to do?"
    new "As long as they're brutal with undead, I have no problems with it. But anyway, what would you want me to do?\n只要他们对亡灵凶残，我就没意见。不过话说回来，你想让我做什么？"

    old "Keep an eye on her."
    new "Keep an eye on her.\n盯着她点。"

    old "Keep an eye on him."
    new "Keep an eye on him.\n盯着他点。"

    old "That I can do."
    new "That I can do.\n这我做得到。"

    old "Thank you for listening to my concerns, [protag]."
    new "Thank you for listening to my concerns, [protag].\n谢谢你听我倾诉这些顾虑，[protag]。"

    old "You're welcome, Leena."
    new "You're welcome, Leena.\n不用谢，Leena。"

    old "Ah, Leena. Hello."
    new "Ah, Leena. Hello.\n啊，Leena。你好。"

    old "Leena doesn't actually ask what I'm doing but, sensing a slight hint of curiousity in her steady gaze, I go ahead and explain."
    new "Leena doesn't actually ask what I'm doing but, sensing a slight hint of curiousity in her steady gaze, I go ahead and explain.\nLeena 其实并没有开口问我在做什么，但我从她那沉稳的目光中察觉出一丝好奇，于是便主动解释起来。"

    old "I was just observing the people inside the citadel."
    new "I was just observing the people inside the citadel.\n我只是在观察城堡里的人。"

    old "And?"
    new "And?\n然后呢？"

    old "And I have to admit that I find amazon society pretty interesting."
    new "And I have to admit that I find amazon society pretty interesting.\n而且我得承认，我觉得 Amazon 社会挺有意思的。"

    old "Everyone here works towards a common goal. I don't think I've come across a single idle person in the whole citadel."
    new "Everyone here works towards a common goal. I don't think I've come across a single idle person in the whole citadel.\n这里的每个人都朝着共同的目标努力。我想，在这整座城堡里，我还没遇见过一个闲人。"

    old "That sounds like a compliment."
    new "That sounds like a compliment.\n这听起来像是在夸奖。"

    old "That's probably because it's supposed to be. What you Amazons have accomplished here is impressive to say the least."
    new "That's probably because it's supposed to be. What you Amazons have accomplished here is impressive to say the least.\n大概因为它本来就是夸奖。你们 Amazons 在这里取得的成就，说句谦虚的，也实在令人赞叹。"

    old "Thanks, [protag]."
    new "Thanks, [protag].\n谢谢，[protag]。"

    old "It's quite different than the chaos of Grimoire, isn't it?"
    new "It's quite different than the chaos of Grimoire, isn't it?\n这跟 Grimoire 的混乱很不一样，对吧？"

    old "I can agree with that much. Though..."
    new "I can agree with that much. Though...\n这点我同意。不过……"

    old "It's just... Well, I feel like people in Grimoire have more freedom."
    new "It's just... Well, I feel like people in Grimoire have more freedom.\n只是……嗯，我觉得 Grimoire 的人拥有更多的自由。"

    old "More freedom? What do you mean by that?"
    new "More freedom? What do you mean by that?\n更多的自由？你这话是什么意思？"

    old "Choose your words carefully, [protag]."
    new "Choose your words carefully, [protag].\n说话可得当心点，[protag]。"

    old "Hey, I lov- I like Karen too. I'm only saying that I don't think that a monarchy is necessarily the best way to lead a nation."
    new "Hey, I lov- I like Karen too. I'm only saying that I don't think that a monarchy is necessarily the best way to lead a nation.\n嘿，我也喜——我也喜欢 Karen。我只是说，我不觉得君主制就一定是治理国家的最佳方式。"

    old "Nonsense. The Amazons have always had a queen. It's been that way for centuries and that's because it works."
    new "Nonsense. The Amazons have always had a queen. It's been that way for centuries and that's because it works.\n胡说。Amazons 一直都有女王。几百年来都是如此，而那是因为它行之有效。"

    old "I don't see that changing. I don't WANT it to change."
    new "I don't see that changing. I don't WANT it to change.\n我看不出它会改变。我也不希望它改变。"

    old "There's never been any problems? Like, I don't know, a mad or violent queen, an incompetent-"
    new "There's never been any problems? Like, I don't know, a mad or violent queen, an incompetent-\n难道从来没出过问题？比如，我也说不准，一个疯癫或残暴的女王，一个不称职的——"

    old "There have been a few problematic queens in the past but our society has a way of dealing with them."
    new "There have been a few problematic queens in the past but our society has a way of dealing with them.\n过去也曾有过几位有问题的女王，但我们的社会自有对付她们的办法。"

    old "How?"
    new "How?\n什么办法？"

    old "If another amazon believes that the current queen is not fit to rule, she can challenge the queeen to a duel. If the challenger wins, she becomes the new queen."
    new "If another amazon believes that the current queen is not fit to rule, she can challenge the queeen to a duel. If the challenger wins, she becomes the new queen.\n如果另一位 Amazon 认为现任女王不配统治，她就可以向女王发起决斗挑战。若挑战者获胜，她就成为新的女王。"

    old "Really? And you don't see any issues with this method?"
    new "Really? And you don't see any issues with this method?\n真的？你难道看不出这办法有什么问题？"

    old "I wasn't finished. It's a little more complicated than it sounds."
    new "I wasn't finished. It's a little more complicated than it sounds.\n我还没说完。事情比听起来要复杂一些。"

    old "Before the challenger can demand a duel, she needs to get approval from the amazon elders."
    new "Before the challenger can demand a duel, she needs to get approval from the amazon elders.\n挑战者在提出决斗之前，必须先得到 Amazon 长老们的批准。"

    old "Amazon elders? This is the first time I've heard of them. Who are they?"
    new "Amazon elders? This is the first time I've heard of them. Who are they?\nAmazon 长老？这还是我第一次听说。他们是谁？"

    old "Old amazons, sometimes ex-queens that are too old to rule. Basically, the most valiant and erudite figures our society has to offer."
    new "Old amazons, sometimes ex-queens that are too old to rule. Basically, the most valiant and erudite figures our society has to offer.\n年迈的 Amazon，有时是年事已高、无法再执政的前任女王。基本上，是我们社会中最英勇、最博学的人物。"

    old "They're the ones who decide who can challenge a current queen."
    new "They're the ones who decide who can challenge a current queen.\n就是他们来决定，谁有资格挑战现任女王。"

    old "How they do it?"
    new "How they do it?\n他们是怎么决定的？"

    old "I'm not sure. I think that it's through a series of trials. It's been centuries since anyone actually attempted such a thing."
    new "I'm not sure. I think that it's through a series of trials. It's been centuries since anyone actually attempted such a thing.\n我不太清楚。我想是通过一连串的考验。毕竟已经有好几个世纪，没人真正尝试过这种事了。"

    old "I see. Well, thanks for the amazon history lesson, Leena. It was enlightening."
    new "I see. Well, thanks for the amazon history lesson, Leena. It was enlightening.\n明白了。嗯，谢谢你这堂 Amazon 历史课，Leena。很涨见识。"

    old "You're quite welcome."
    new "You're quite welcome.\n不必客气。"

    old "Ah, in that sense."
    new "Ah, in that sense.\n啊，是这个意思。"

    old "Don't get me wrong. I often wondered if men are really all that useful myself. I mean, you don't exactly need them for anything besides procreation and... recreation. For those who are interested, of course."
    new "Don't get me wrong. I often wondered if men are really all that useful myself. I mean, you don't exactly need them for anything besides procreation and... recreation. For those who are interested, of course.\n别误会。我自己也常常琢磨，男人到底有多大用处。我的意思是，除了繁衍后代和……消遣，你其实并不怎么需要他们。当然，那是指有兴趣的人而言。"

    old "I always found... odd that the amazons are a matriarchal society."
    new "I always found... odd that the amazons are a matriarchal society.\n我一直觉得……Amazon 是个母系社会，这点挺奇怪的。"

    old "Does it bother you?"
    new "Does it bother you?\n这让你不舒服吗？"

    old "A bit, I suppose. It doesn't seem entirely fair. I mean, imagine if it was the opposite and only men could rule. You would feel the same, right?"
    new "A bit, I suppose. It doesn't seem entirely fair. I mean, imagine if it was the opposite and only men could rule. You would feel the same, right?\n有一点吧，我想。这似乎不太公平。我是说，想象一下反过来的情形，只有男人才能统治。你也会觉得不舒服，对吧？"

    old "I think there are some nomad tribes ruled by men who only use women to procreate. That's sort of the opposite of what we do."
    new "I think there are some nomad tribes ruled by men who only use women to procreate. That's sort of the opposite of what we do.\n我想，确实有一些由男人统治的游牧部落，他们只用女人来繁衍后代。那大概就是与我们截然相反的做法。"

    old "Yes, but the fact that I've never heard of them means they're not a big tribe. Everyone knows about the Amazons."
    new "Yes, but the fact that I've never heard of them means they're not a big tribe. Everyone knows about the Amazons.\n是的，但我从没听说过他们，正说明他们不是什么大部族。而 Amazons，可是无人不知。"

    old "True. But what else do you expect me to say, [protag]? I like amazon society how it is. I wouldn't change anything."
    new "True. But what else do you expect me to say, [protag]? I like amazon society how it is. I wouldn't change anything.\n没错。可你还指望我说什么呢，[protag]？我喜欢 Amazon 社会现在的样子。我什么都不想改变。"

    old "Even you admitted that you were impressed by it. Why change something that works so well?"
    new "Even you admitted that you were impressed by it. Why change something that works so well?\n就连你自己都承认对它印象深刻。运行得这么好的东西，为什么要改？"

    old "You're right. Sometimes I wish other races and nations would put more power in the hands of women. I even think we'd be more fit to rule than men because we're less impulsive."
    new "You're right. Sometimes I wish other races and nations would put more power in the hands of women. I even think we'd be more fit to rule than men because we're less impulsive.\n你说得对。有时我真希望其他种族和国家能把更多权力交到女人手中。我甚至觉得，我们比男人更适合统治，因为我们没那么冲动。"

    old "Well, at least in general. I probably can't say the same of you."
    new "Well, at least in general. I probably can't say the same of you.\n嗯，至少总体上是如此。对你，我大概就不能这么说了。"

    old "Ever wondered what the other races and nations might think of you? They probably see you as a sexist society."
    new "Ever wondered what the other races and nations might think of you? They probably see you as a sexist society.\n你有没有想过，其他种族和国家会怎么看你们？他们大概会觉得你们是个性别歧视的社会。"

    old "The other nations usually fear us. They also tend to respect our traditions. We never tell the other races how to behave and, in return, we expect them to show us the same courtesy."
    new "The other nations usually fear us. They also tend to respect our traditions. We never tell the other races how to behave and, in return, we expect them to show us the same courtesy.\n其他国家通常都畏惧我们。他们也往往尊重我们的传统。我们从不指手画脚地告诉其他种族该如何行事，作为回报，也期望他们给予我们同样的尊重。"

    old "I guess there's no point in arguing. It's not your fault that you were born in this society. It's all you've known since you were a kid."
    new "I guess there's no point in arguing. It's not your fault that you were born in this society. It's all you've known since you were a kid.\n我想争辩也没意义。你出生在这样的社会里，不是你的错。这是你从小就知道的一切。"

    old "You'll have to excuse me, [protag]. I have recruits to train."
    new "You'll have to excuse me, [protag]. I have recruits to train.\n请原谅，[protag]。我有新兵要训练。"

    old "Her abrupt exit makes me wonder if I said something wrong..."
    new "Her abrupt exit makes me wonder if I said something wrong...\n她突然告辞，让我不禁怀疑自己是不是说错了什么……"

    old "Oh, really?"
    new "Oh, really?\n哦，是吗？"

    old "Yes. Didn't you know?"
    new "Yes. Didn't you know?\n是的。你难道不知道？"

    old "Of course I know. I was being sarcastic."
    new "Of course I know. I was being sarcastic.\n我当然知道。我是在说反话。"

    old "Let me explain. You say there are no slaves in Grimoire? Yes, there are no explicit laws that allow slavery, but in practice there are slaves in Grimoire too."
    new "Let me explain. You say there are no slaves in Grimoire? Yes, there are no explicit laws that allow slavery, but in practice there are slaves in Grimoire too.\n让我来解释。你说 Grimoire 没有奴隶？没错，那里没有明确允许奴隶制的法律，但实际上，Grimoire 同样有奴隶。"

    old "Massive amounts of poor people in the streets, people who owe money to banks, people who owe their freedom to the Empire's army. For the believers, they are tied to their respective god's traditions."
    new "Massive amounts of poor people in the streets, people who owe money to banks, people who owe their freedom to the Empire's army. For the believers, they are tied to their respective god's traditions.\n街头大批的穷人，欠着银行钱的人，还有把自由抵押给帝国军队的人。至于信徒，他们则被各自神明的传统所束缚。"

    old "I don't see all that freedom that you were talking about, [protag]. One can be a slave without being labeled one."
    new "I don't see all that freedom that you were talking about, [protag]. One can be a slave without being labeled one.\n我可看不出你所说的那些自由，[protag]。一个人可以当奴隶，却不被贴上奴隶的标签。"

    old "Well, while I don't entirely agree, that is an interesting perspective."
    new "Well, while I don't entirely agree, that is an interesting perspective.\n虽然我并不完全同意，但这倒是个有趣的观点。"

    old "I'm glad that you find my reasoning interesting, at least."
    new "I'm glad that you find my reasoning interesting, at least.\n我很高兴你至少觉得我的推理有趣。"

    old "Oh? [protag], it's you."
    new "Oh? [protag], it's you.\n哦？[protag]，是你啊。"

    old "Leena seems a bit absent today. I try talking to her a bit, but all I get are short replies. Something is definitely up."
    new "Leena seems a bit absent today. I try talking to her a bit, but all I get are short replies. Something is definitely up.\nLeena 今天似乎有点心不在焉。我试着和她聊了几句，可得到的只是简短的回应。肯定有什么事不对劲。"

    old "Uh? What do you mean?"
    new "Uh? What do you mean?\n嗯？你是什么意思？"

    old "There's something you're not telling me. You've been distant today. And, also... sad?"
    new "There's something you're not telling me. You've been distant today. And, also... sad?\n你有事瞒着我。今天你一直很疏远。而且……还有点难过？"

    old "It's nothing. You don't need to worry about me."
    new "It's nothing. You don't need to worry about me.\n没什么。你不用为我担心。"

    old "I instinctively move closer to her. Wait. Is she...crying?"
    new "I instinctively move closer to her. Wait. Is she...crying?\n我本能地朝她走近了些。等等。她……是在哭吗？"

    old "Go away! Leave me alone!"
    new "Go away! Leave me alone!\n走开！别来烦我！"

    old "Not until you tell me what is going on!"
    new "Not until you tell me what is going on!\n除非你告诉我发生了什么事，否则我不走！"

    old "It's something private."
    new "It's something private.\n是件私事。"

    old "I take another step towards her, but this time Leena pushes me away. I stumble backwards and end up tripping over my own feet, falling flat on my back with a loud thud."
    new "I take another step towards her, but this time Leena pushes me away. I stumble backwards and end up tripping over my own feet, falling flat on my back with a loud thud.\n我又朝她迈出一步，可这一次 Leena 把我推开了。我踉跄着后退，结果被自己的脚绊倒，砰地一声，仰面摔倒在地。"

    old "Ah! [protag]! I-I'm so sorry! I didn't mean to... I--"
    new "Ah! [protag]! I-I'm so sorry! I didn't mean to... I--\n啊！[protag]！我、我太抱歉了！我不是故意的……我——"

    old "Seeing Leena so flustered, I can't help but laugh as I get to my feet."
    new "Seeing Leena so flustered, I can't help but laugh as I get to my feet.\n看到 Leena 如此慌张，我一边爬起身，一边忍不住笑了出来。"

    old "It's okay, Leena. My butt is going to hurt for a bit, but most of the damage is to my pride."
    new "It's okay, Leena. My butt is going to hurt for a bit, but most of the damage is to my pride.\n没事的，Leena。我的屁股得疼上一阵子了，不过受创最重的，是我的自尊心。"

    old "I understand. If you need me though, I'll be here for a bit longer. I need to check with some of the amazons vendors."
    new "I understand. If you need me though, I'll be here for a bit longer. I need to check with some of the amazons vendors.\n我明白。不过如果你需要我，我会在这里再多待一会儿。我得去跟几个 Amazon 商贩核对点事情。"

    old "I linger a second longer than necessary, hoping that she'll change her mind. She doesn't. At least, not until I start to leave. That's when I hear Leena's voice."
    new "I linger a second longer than necessary, hoping that she'll change her mind. She doesn't. At least, not until I start to leave. That's when I hear Leena's voice.\n我多停留了片刻，希望她能改变主意。她没有。至少，直到我转身要走时都没有。也就在那一刻，我听到了 Leena 的声音。"

    old "I turn around and head back over to her."
    new "I turn around and head back over to her.\n我转过身，走回到她身边。"

    old "I think the vendors can wait for now. What's going on, Leena?"
    new "I think the vendors can wait for now. What's going on, Leena?\n我想那些商贩可以先等等。出什么事了，Leena？"

    old "Once more, I move closer to Leena. This time she extends a hand and I take it into mine."
    new "Once more, I move closer to Leena. This time she extends a hand and I take it into mine.\n我再次走近 Leena。这一次，她伸出了一只手，我把它握进自己手里。"

    old "Have you ever had a pet, [protag]?"
    new "Have you ever had a pet, [protag]?\n你养过宠物吗，[protag]？"

    old "No. Between my job and all of the travelling I do, I've never had time to take care of one. But I think I would have liked to have a pet."
    new "No. Between my job and all of the travelling I do, I've never had time to take care of one. But I think I would have liked to have a pet.\n没有。在我的工作和我四处奔波的间隙，我从没有时间照顾宠物。但我想，我是会愿意养一只的。"

    old "Lena nods, accepting my answer."
    new "Lena nods, accepting my answer.\nLeena 点点头，接受了我的回答。"

    old "I told you about our griffons before, but I forgot to mention that we raise them here at the Citadel. I've known many of them since they were little birds."
    new "I told you about our griffons before, but I forgot to mention that we raise them here at the Citadel. I've known many of them since they were little birds.\n我之前跟你说过我们的狮鹫，但我忘了提，我们就在城堡这里饲养它们。其中很多只，我从它们还是小鸟时就认识了。"

    old "Little? I think the smallest griffon I've seen was at least as big as a dog."
    new "Little? I think the smallest griffon I've seen was at least as big as a dog.\n小鸟？我见过最小的狮鹫，也至少有狗那么大。"

    old "Well of course, little compared to how big they are when they're adults."
    new "Well of course, little compared to how big they are when they're adults.\n那当然，我是说跟它们成年后的体型相比，还算小。"

    old " Anyway, there was this one, Jin."
    new " Anyway, there was this one, Jin.\n总之，有这么一只，名叫 Jin。"

    old "Why wouldn't I?"
    new "Why wouldn't I?\n我为什么不呢？"

    old "It just seems weird to me."
    new "It just seems weird to me.\n只是对我来说有点怪。"

    old "How are you supposed to distinguish one griffon from another? How do you assign each amazon scout to her own griffon? It's a lot easier if they all have individual names."
    new "How are you supposed to distinguish one griffon from another? How do you assign each amazon scout to her own griffon? It's a lot easier if they all have individual names.\n你该怎么区分这只狮鹫和那只呢？又怎么给每位 Amazon 侦察兵分配她自己的狮鹫？要是它们都有各自的名字，就省事多了。"

    old "Right. That makes sense."
    new "Right. That makes sense.\n对，有道理。"

    old "Thanks. I picked the name myself when I was 8."
    new "Thanks. I picked the name myself when I was 8.\n谢谢。这名字是我八岁时自己取的。"

    old "You don't just name a griffon because it's cute though, right?"
    new "You don't just name a griffon because it's cute though, right?\n不过你给狮鹫取名，不只是因为它可爱吧？"

    old "Of course not. We need to distinguish each one in order to assign them to a specific amazon scout."
    new "Of course not. We need to distinguish each one in order to assign them to a specific amazon scout.\n当然不是。我们需要把每一只都区分开，好把它们分配给特定的 Amazon 侦察兵。"

    old "You haven't been around griffons enough to know, but the bond between an amazon scout and her griffon is similar to the ones humans share with their horses. They quickly become more than just a means of transportation to their partners."
    new "You haven't been around griffons enough to know, but the bond between an amazon scout and her griffon is similar to the ones humans share with their horses. They quickly become more than just a means of transportation to their partners.\n你和狮鹫相处得还不够多，所以不了解：一位 Amazon 侦察兵和她的狮鹫之间的羁绊，就像人类与自己的马一样。它们很快就会超越单纯的交通工具，成为伙伴。"

    old "And that's what happened between me and Jin. I'd ridden her since I was a child."
    new "And that's what happened between me and Jin. I'd ridden her since I was a child.\n我和 Jin 之间就是如此。我从小就骑着她。"

    old "But you aren't a scout."
    new "But you aren't a scout.\n可你不是侦察兵。"

    old "I wasn't born captain of royal guard, you know. I had to train, rise through the ranks. I was a scout for about ten years of my life."
    new "I wasn't born captain of royal guard, you know. I had to train, rise through the ranks. I was a scout for about ten years of my life.\n你知道，我又不是一生下来就是皇家卫队队长。我得训练，一级一级往上升。我人生中有大约十年，都当着侦察兵。"

    old "I spent ten years of my life riding with Jin through the skies. When we weren't out scouting, she'd often fly near my house to call me out."
    new "I spent ten years of my life riding with Jin through the skies. When we weren't out scouting, she'd often fly near my house to call me out.\n我人生中那十年，是和 Jin 一起驰骋在天空中度过的。我们不出门侦察时，她常常飞到我家附近，叫我出去。"

    old "Call you out?"
    new "Call you out?\n叫你出去？"

    old "To the wine yards outside the city gates. She was a grape addict. I got reported once because I was feeding her too many of them."
    new "To the wine yards outside the city gates. She was a grape addict. I got reported once because I was feeding her too many of them.\n去城门外的那片葡萄园。她是个吃葡萄上瘾的家伙。有次我还被人举报了，就因为我喂她葡萄喂得太多。"

    old "A faint smile forms on her face, but it's shortly replaced by a melancholy expression."
    new "A faint smile forms on her face, but it's shortly replaced by a melancholy expression.\n她脸上泛起一丝淡淡的微笑，但很快又被忧郁的神情取代。"

    old "And now she's gone. She died this morning. She suffered for three days and three nights. I couldn't even be at her side."
    new "And now she's gone. She died this morning. She suffered for three days and three nights. I couldn't even be at her side.\n而现在她走了。今天早上她死了。她苦苦撑了三天三夜。我甚至没能陪在她身边。"

    old "Because of my position, I had things to do, meetings to attend. I've really hated being a guard captain these last three days."
    new "Because of my position, I had things to do, meetings to attend. I've really hated being a guard captain these last three days.\n因为我的职位，我有事情要做，有会议要参加。这三天，我真是恨透了当这个卫队队长。"

    old "Leena... I'm so sorry."
    new "Leena... I'm so sorry.\nLeena……我很遗憾。"

    old "Thank you [protag]. That's why I didn't want to talk. It wasn't about you. I just... I miss her. I miss Jin and I can't seem to stop crying."
    new "Thank you [protag]. That's why I didn't want to talk. It wasn't about you. I just... I miss her. I miss Jin and I can't seem to stop crying.\n谢谢你，[protag]。所以我才不想说话。不是因为你。我只是……我想她。我想 Jin，眼泪怎么也止不住。"

    old "I know it hurts, but you should try to focus on the positive, happy moments you had with her."
    new "I know it hurts, but you should try to focus on the positive, happy moments you had with her.\n我知道这很痛苦，但你应该试着去回想那些和她在一起时积极、快乐的时光。"

    old "Like the wineyard story you just told me. I saw you smiling when you recalled that moment."
    new "Like the wineyard story you just told me. I saw you smiling when you recalled that moment.\n就像你刚才讲的那个葡萄园的故事。你回想起那一刻时，我看见你笑了。"

    old "Jin loved you so that I think that that's what she would have wanted you to focus on."
    new "Jin loved you so that I think that that's what she would have wanted you to focus on.\nJin 那么爱你，所以我想，那也正是她希望你记住的东西。"

    old "Leena's tears stream down her face. She's not holding back any more. She bawls openly as she wraps her arms around me and buries her face in my shoulder."
    new "Leena's tears stream down her face. She's not holding back any more. She bawls openly as she wraps her arms around me and buries her face in my shoulder.\nLeena 的泪水顺着脸颊流下。她不再克制了。她放声痛哭，用双臂环住我，把脸埋进我的肩膀。"

    old "Is this trembling woman really the same one I've come to know? I'm so used to her being the strong one."
    new "Is this trembling woman really the same one I've come to know? I'm so used to her being the strong one.\n眼前这个颤抖的女人，真的和我认识的那个人是同一个吗？我早已习惯了她的坚强。"

    old "Perhaps this isn't the right time to think this, but it's nice to see that, beyond that hard shell, there's a vulnerable person capable of loving something this much."
    new "Perhaps this isn't the right time to think this, but it's nice to see that, beyond that hard shell, there's a vulnerable person capable of loving something this much.\n也许此刻不该想这些，但能看到在那层坚硬外壳之下，有一个如此脆弱、能爱得这么深的人，真好。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. What you say is true. Thank you."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. What you say is true. Thank you.\n谢谢你，[protag]。你说得对。谢谢你。"

    old "Now, I must go. I don't want anyone else to see me like this."
    new "Now, I must go. I don't want anyone else to see me like this.\n现在，我得走了。我不想让别人看到我这样。"

    old "I understand. Take care, Leena."
    new "I understand. Take care, Leena.\n我理解。保重，Leena。"

    old "Leena, I know it still hurts, but you need to move on."
    new "Leena, I know it still hurts, but you need to move on.\nLeena，我知道这还是很痛，但你需要向前看。"

    old "You're the guard captain. What if others saw you crying over the death of a simple griffon?"
    new "You're the guard captain. What if others saw you crying over the death of a simple griffon?\n你是卫队队长。要是别人看到你为一只普普通通的狮鹫的死而哭泣，会怎么想？"

    old "A simple griffon? Yes, that's probably what it'd seem like to someone like you. For me, Jin was more than a simple griffon. She was my best friend."
    new "A simple griffon? Yes, that's probably what it'd seem like to someone like you. For me, Jin was more than a simple griffon. She was my best friend.\n普普通通的狮鹫？是啊，在你这种人看来，大概就是那样吧。但对我而言，Jin 远不止是一只普通的狮鹫。她是我最好的朋友。"

    old "I... Sorry, I didn't mean it like that. Only, think about what the other amazons might think of you if they saw you showing so much weakness."
    new "I... Sorry, I didn't mean it like that. Only, think about what the other amazons might think of you if they saw you showing so much weakness.\n我……抱歉，我不是那个意思。只是想想，如果其他 Amazon 看到你流露出这么多软弱，会怎么看你。"

    old "Yes. I understand what you're trying to say now. I'm a guard captain. I can't afford to appear weak."
    new "Yes. I understand what you're trying to say now. I'm a guard captain. I can't afford to appear weak.\n是的。我现在明白你想说什么了。我是卫队队长。我承受不起显露出软弱。"

    old "Leena wipes away her tears with her arm. Once they're gone, her sad expression is replaced with a determined one. She's decided that she's done grieving."
    new "Leena wipes away her tears with her arm. Once they're gone, her sad expression is replaced with a determined one. She's decided that she's done grieving.\nLeena 用手臂擦去眼泪。泪痕一去，她悲伤的神情便被坚定所取代。她已经决定，不再哀伤了。"

    old "She gives me one last nod before walking off into the distance. I watch as she gives orders to some other amazons in her usual, decisive tone."
    new "She gives me one last nod before walking off into the distance. I watch as she gives orders to some other amazons in her usual, decisive tone.\n她最后朝我点了一下头，便向远处走去。我望着她用惯常的果决口吻，向其他几位 Amazon 下达命令。"

    old "That's it, Leena."
    new "That's it, Leena.\n这样就对了，Leena。"

    old "I understand. It just happened so you'll need some time. I think the best thing I can do for you is give you your space for now."
    new "I understand. It just happened so you'll need some time. I think the best thing I can do for you is give you your space for now.\n我理解。事情刚发生，你需要些时间。我想，眼下我能为你做的最好的事，就是给你留出空间。"

    old "[protag], I already apologized for my behavior-"
    new "[protag], I already apologized for my behavior-\n[protag]，我已经为我的失态道过歉了——"

    old "No, this has nothing to do with that. Don't worry."
    new "No, this has nothing to do with that. Don't worry.\n不，这跟那无关。别担心。"

    old "I simply think that it's the best thing for you right now. You need time to mourn your loss. I don't know how else I can help you."
    new "I simply think that it's the best thing for you right now. You need time to mourn your loss. I don't know how else I can help you.\n我只是觉得，眼下这对你最好。你需要时间来哀悼你的失去。除此之外，我也不知道还能怎么帮你。"

    old "I see. Thanks [protag]. You're right. I just need some time."
    new "I see. Thanks [protag]. You're right. I just need some time.\n我明白了。谢谢，[protag]。你说得对。我只是需要点时间。"

    old "But if you need me for any mission, I'm here and ready to help you. Always."
    new "But if you need me for any mission, I'm here and ready to help you. Always.\n但如果你需要我执行任何任务，我随时都在，随时准备帮你。永远。"

    old "You're welcome, Leena. Take care."
    new "You're welcome, Leena. Take care.\n不用谢，Leena。保重。"

    old "I make my way to the citadel's main square, where some fighters are training. Leena is there which isn't much of a surprise. The fact that Sylrissa is there too, on the other hand, is."
    new "I make my way to the citadel's main square, where some fighters are training. Leena is there which isn't much of a surprise. The fact that Sylrissa is there too, on the other hand, is.\n我来到城堡的主广场，一些战士正在那里训练。Leena 在那儿，这并不让人意外。而 Sylrissa 居然也在，就有点意外了。"

    old "Oh, it's you, Princess Loren."
    new "Oh, it's you, Princess Loren.\n哦，是你啊，Loren 公主。"

    old "Hi, [protag]."
    new "Hi, [protag].\n嗨，[protag]。"

    old "Hello, Leena. Sylrissa, didn't expect to see you here."
    new "Hello, Leena. Sylrissa, didn't expect to see you here.\n你好，Leena。Sylrissa，没想到会在这里见到你。"

    old "Princess Loren kindly invited me."
    new "Princess Loren kindly invited me.\n是 Loren 公主好意邀请我来的。"

    old "Loren invited her? I briefly glance towards Leena and, judging from the look on her face, it's transparently clear that she is not happy about this particular development."
    new "Loren invited her? I briefly glance towards Leena and, judging from the look on her face, it's transparently clear that she is not happy about this particular development.\nLoren 邀请了她？我飞快地瞥了 Leena 一眼，从她脸上的神情看，显而易见，她对眼下的这个进展很不高兴。"

    old "That's correct."
    new "That's correct.\n没错。"

    old "I see. Might I ask why, your majesty?"
    new "I see. Might I ask why, your majesty?\n我明白了。请问这是为什么，殿下？"

    old "I was intrigued by her abilities. Dual wielding is clearly superior to other fighting styles."
    new "I was intrigued by her abilities. Dual wielding is clearly superior to other fighting styles.\n我对她的本事很感兴趣。双持武器，显然比其他格斗流派更胜一筹。"

    old "You mean, compared to the style I'm teaching you."
    new "You mean, compared to the style I'm teaching you.\n你是说，跟我正在教你的流派相比。"

    old "My, my. Is someone jealous that I have the princess' attention?"
    new "My, my. Is someone jealous that I have the princess' attention?\n哎呀呀。是不是有人嫉妒我得了公主的青睐啊？"

    old "Why don't you try challenging me to a duel? I could beat you with my bare hands!"
    new "Why don't you try challenging me to a duel? I could beat you with my bare hands!\n你何不试试跟我决斗？我空手都能把你打趴下！"

    old "Woah. The situation is quickly spiraling out of control. I feel like I should say something..."
    new "Woah. The situation is quickly spiraling out of control. I feel like I should say something...\n哇。局面迅速失控了。我觉得自己该说点什么……"

    old "Leena, I can understand why you're angry about this, but--"
    new "Leena, I can understand why you're angry about this, but--\nLeena，我理解你为什么为此生气，但是——"

    old "But what?"
    new "But what?\n但是什么？"

    old "Take a look at Loren and how she wields those two little swords. Nagas are naturally born ambidextrous, but that's not usually the case for humans."
    new "Take a look at Loren and how she wields those two little swords. Nagas are naturally born ambidextrous, but that's not usually the case for humans.\n看看 Loren，看她挥动那两把小剑的样子。Nagas 天生双手灵巧，可人类通常不是这样。"

    old "What's your point?"
    new "What's your point?\n你想说什么？"

    old "Think about it. Loren seems to be handling those two weapons together rather well. Maybe she's right. Maybe it is the perfect style for her. Have you ever considered that?"
    new "Think about it. Loren seems to be handling those two weapons together rather well. Maybe she's right. Maybe it is the perfect style for her. Have you ever considered that?\n想想看。Loren 似乎把这两件武器配合得相当好。也许她是对的。也许这正适合她。你有没有考虑过这一点？"

    old "Well said."
    new "Well said.\n说得好。"

    old "It doesn't matter. Queen Karen would never approve of a naga teaching the princess anyway."
    new "It doesn't matter. Queen Karen would never approve of a naga teaching the princess anyway.\n无所谓。反正 Karen 女王绝不会同意让一个 Naga 来教公主。"

    old "Well, it looks like we'll can ask her in person right now."
    new "Well, it looks like we'll can ask her in person right now.\n嗯，看来我们现在就能当面问她了。"

    old "Princess Loren, I mean no disrespect, but does your moth- ahem, Queen Karen know about this?"
    new "Princess Loren, I mean no disrespect, but does your moth- ahem, Queen Karen know about this?\nLoren 公主，我无意冒犯，但你的母——咳咳，Karen 女王知道这件事吗？"

    old "That's what I thought. Leena is an amazon and she was specifically chosen by the Queen to train you. I don't think that she would be happy to know what you're doing."
    new "That's what I thought. Leena is an amazon and she was specifically chosen by the Queen to train you. I don't think that she would be happy to know what you're doing.\n我就知道。Leena 是 Amazon，而且是由女王亲自挑选来训练你的。我想，她要是知道你在做什么，恐怕不会高兴。"

    old "But-"
    new "But-\n但是——"

    old "Thanks, [protag]. You hear that, Sylrissa? You can go. I'll take care of her."
    new "Thanks, [protag]. You hear that, Sylrissa? You can go. I'll take care of her.\n谢了，[protag]。听到了吗，Sylrissa？你可以走了。她交给我来管。"

    old "Pity. I liked playing with the princess."
    new "Pity. I liked playing with the princess.\n真可惜。我还挺喜欢跟公主一起玩的。"

    old "Wait! It's not up to you to decide! I say she stays!"
    new "Wait! It's not up to you to decide! I say she stays!\n等等！轮不到你来决定！我说她留下！"

    old "I see Karen approaching us. She probably wants to see what all the fuss is about."
    new "I see Karen approaching us. She probably wants to see what all the fuss is about.\n我看见 Karen 正朝我们走来。她大概是想看看这边在闹什么。"

    old "On second thought, I'm really not sure what I should say. I can see both sides of the argument and, honestly, I already know that no matter which side I pick, it's going to get me in trouble."
    new "On second thought, I'm really not sure what I should say. I can see both sides of the argument and, honestly, I already know that no matter which side I pick, it's going to get me in trouble.\n转念一想，我还真不知道该说什么。争论的双方我都能理解，而且说实话，我已经知道，无论我站在哪一边，都会给自己惹上麻烦。"

    old "Queen Karen is coming this way. She should be able to sort this out."
    new "Queen Karen is coming this way. She should be able to sort this out.\nKaren 女王正朝这边走来。她应该能解决这件事。"

    old "What is going on here?"
    new "What is going on here?\n这里是怎么回事？"

    old "Mom, I want to learn to fight with two weapons!"
    new "Mom, I want to learn to fight with two weapons!\n妈妈，我想学用两把武器战斗！"

    old "Hmm. Is that why Sylrissa is here?"
    new "Hmm. Is that why Sylrissa is here?\n嗯。这就是 Sylrissa 在这里的原因？"

    old "I'm sorry, but it's against the rules. Only an amazon can train another amazon."
    new "I'm sorry, but it's against the rules. Only an amazon can train another amazon.\n抱歉，但这不合规矩。只有 Amazon 才能训练 Amazon。"

    old "Even if the non-amazon is clearly the better fighter?"
    new "Even if the non-amazon is clearly the better fighter?\n即便那个非 Amazon 明显是更强的战士？"

    old "YOU-"
    new "YOU-\n你——"

    old "Enough, Leena. Sylrissa, it doesn't matter if you are a better fighter or not. Are you a better teacher?"
    new "Enough, Leena. Sylrissa, it doesn't matter if you are a better fighter or not. Are you a better teacher?\n够了，Leena。Sylrissa，你是不是更强的战士并不重要。你是更好的老师吗？"

    old "Yes, I think the princess and I are getting along well."
    new "Yes, I think the princess and I are getting along well.\n是的，我想公主和我相处得很好。"

    old "Please, mom..."
    new "Please, mom...\n求你了，妈妈……"

    old "*Sighs* Very well, I'll allow Sylrissa to come here - but no more than once a week - to teach you some dual wielding moves."
    new "*Sighs* Very well, I'll allow Sylrissa to come here - but no more than once a week - to teach you some dual wielding moves.\n（叹气）好吧，我允许 Sylrissa 到这里来——但每周至多一次——教你一些双持的招式。"

    old "Yay!"
    new "Yay!\n耶！"

    old "My Queen! I-"
    new "My Queen! I-\n我的女王！我——"

    old "The decision is made. Now, I need to attend to more important matters."
    new "The decision is made. Now, I need to attend to more important matters.\n决定已经作出。现在，我还要去处理更重要的事务。"

    old "I need to go too. Try to calm down, you two: the last thing we need is to start fighting amongst ourselves."
    new "I need to go too. Try to calm down, you two: the last thing we need is to start fighting amongst ourselves.\n我也得走了。你们两个都冷静点：我们最不需要的，就是自家人先打起来。"

    old "It's not my fault that Leena has no sense of humor."
    new "It's not my fault that Leena has no sense of humor.\nLeena 没有幽默感，这又不是我的错。"

    old "Humor? What does humor have to do with this?!"
    new "Humor? What does humor have to do with this?!\n幽默？这跟幽默有什么关系？！"

    old "You take things too much sersiously. If I'm being honest, I've never seen someone who isn't a naga fight as well as you."
    new "You take things too much sersiously. If I'm being honest, I've never seen someone who isn't a naga fight as well as you.\n你把事情看得太认真了。说实话，我从没见过哪个不是 Naga 的人，能打得像你一样好。"

    old "Is Leena blushing? I imagine Sylrissa's compliment caught her off guard."
    new "Is Leena blushing? I imagine Sylrissa's compliment caught her off guard.\nLeena 是脸红了吗？我想，Sylrissa 的这句夸奖，让她有些措手不及。"

    old "On the other hand, your swiftest fighters still pale in comparison to the speed of our average naga. So yes, I still think that I'm the better fighter."
    new "On the other hand, your swiftest fighters still pale in comparison to the speed of our average naga. So yes, I still think that I'm the better fighter.\n另一方面，你们最迅捷的战士，比起我们普通 Naga 的速度，也仍然相形见绌。所以没错，我依然认为我是更强的那个战士。"

    old "How dare you! You wouldn't stand a chance against me!"
    new "How dare you! You wouldn't stand a chance against me!\n你竟敢！你根本不是我的对手！"

    old "Sigh. This is pointless. I give up. Try not to kill each other."
    new "Sigh. This is pointless. I give up. Try not to kill each other.\n唉。真是没意义。我不管了。别把彼此给打死了。"

    old "I make good on my words and leave, hoping that it's only a healthy competitive spirit that drives those two. They wouldn't actually fight for real, would they? I'm going to try to remain optimistic."
    new "I make good on my words and leave, hoping that it's only a healthy competitive spirit that drives those two. They wouldn't actually fight for real, would they? I'm going to try to remain optimistic.\n我说话算话，转身离开，只希望驱使那两人的只是健康的竞争心。她们不会真打起来吧？我试着保持乐观。"

    old "I approach Sylrissa, who is smiling."
    new "I approach Sylrissa, who is smiling.\n我走向 Sylrissa，她正微笑着。"

    old "You seem happy."
    new "You seem happy.\n你看起来很开心。"

    old "I... I feel accepted. Welcome even. You have no idea how much this means to me."
    new "I... I feel accepted. Welcome even. You have no idea how much this means to me.\n我……我觉得自己被接纳了。甚至是被欢迎了。你不知道这对我有多重要。"

    old "So it wasn't just about training?"
    new "So it wasn't just about training?\n所以，这不仅仅是为了训练？"

    old "Teaching Loren is a real pleasure. But... while I like the swamp, once in a while is nice to stay with other people. And a town full of fierce female fighters? Is there anything better?"
    new "Teaching Loren is a real pleasure. But... while I like the swamp, once in a while is nice to stay with other people. And a town full of fierce female fighters? Is there anything better?\n教 Loren 是种真正的乐趣。不过……虽然我喜欢沼泽，但偶尔和别的人待在一起也不错。而一座满是勇猛女战士的城镇？还有比这更好的吗？"

    old "Haha, glad things turned out well for you. For Leena, on the other hand..."
    new "Haha, glad things turned out well for you. For Leena, on the other hand...\n哈哈，很高兴事情对你来说有了好结果。至于 Leena，就另当别论了……"

    old "I'll try to talk to her."
    new "I'll try to talk to her.\n我会试着去跟她谈谈。"

    old "Please do. There are enough things already trying to kill us without adding each other to that list."
    new "Please do. There are enough things already trying to kill us without adding each other to that list.\n请务必。想杀我们的东西已经够多了，可别再把彼此也加进那份名单。"

    old "I know. It's just that she is so easy to upset that it's funny."
    new "I know. It's just that she is so easy to upset that it's funny.\n我知道。只是她太容易被惹毛了，这反而有点好笑。"

    old "Alright, alright. I'll go and apologize to her now."
    new "Alright, alright. I'll go and apologize to her now.\n好吧，好吧。我这就去向她道歉。"

    old "I approach Leena who is walking away from the square with lowered head."
    new "I approach Leena who is walking away from the square with lowered head.\n我走向 Leena，她正低着头离开广场。"

    old "Leena."
    new "Leena.\nLeena。"

    old "She keeps walking, so I pick up my pace to catch up to her and grab her wrist. She stops but doesn't even try to hide the defeated look her face."
    new "She keeps walking, so I pick up my pace to catch up to her and grab her wrist. She stops but doesn't even try to hide the defeated look her face.\n她继续往前走，于是我加快脚步追上她，抓住了她的手腕。她停了下来，却连掩饰都不掩饰脸上的挫败。"

    old "Leena, you're making this a bigger issue than it actually is."
    new "Leena, you're making this a bigger issue than it actually is.\nLeena，你把这件事想得比它实际严重多了。"

    old "I feel like I failed."
    new "I feel like I failed.\n我觉得自己失败了。"

    old "What? You didn't fail!"
    new "What? You didn't fail!\n什么？你没有失败！"

    old "Then how come even Queen Karen took Sylrissa's side?"
    new "Then how come even Queen Karen took Sylrissa's side?\n那为什么连 Karen 女王都站在了 Sylrissa 那边？"

    old "She only said that Sylrissa can come once a week to teach Loren some moves. You're still in charge of teaching Loren every other day."
    new "She only said that Sylrissa can come once a week to teach Loren some moves. You're still in charge of teaching Loren every other day.\n她只是说 Sylrissa 每周可以来一次，教 Loren 几招。其余日子教导 Loren 的，依然是你。"

    old "...Yes, this is true. But you heard Loren. She's never showed that much enthusiasm for anything I've taught her."
    new "...Yes, this is true. But you heard Loren. She's never showed that much enthusiasm for anything I've taught her.\n……是啊，这倒是真的。可你也听见 Loren 了。她对我教她的任何东西，从没表现出那么高的热情。"

    old "I think that's normal."
    new "I think that's normal.\n我觉得这很正常。"

    old "Normal? How is it normal?"
    new "Normal? How is it normal?\n正常？这怎么正常了？"

    old "A mysterious naga creature never seen before that uses two weapons? Sylrissa is a novelty."
    new "A mysterious naga creature never seen before that uses two weapons? Sylrissa is a novelty.\n一个前所未见、使用两把武器的神秘 Naga？Sylrissa 本身就是件新奇事。"

    old "I see a faint smile forming on Leena's face."
    new "I see a faint smile forming on Leena's face.\n我看见 Leena 脸上浮起一丝淡淡的微笑。"

    old "Remember that Loren is still young. You can't blame her for being charmed by Sylrissa. The princess has never seen anything like her before."
    new "Remember that Loren is still young. You can't blame her for being charmed by Sylrissa. The princess has never seen anything like her before.\n别忘了 Loren 还年轻。她为 Sylrissa 着迷，你也不能怪她。公主以前从没见过像她这样的人。"

    old "Who knows? Maybe Loren will get tired of Sylrissa in a few months. And maybe her interest in dual wielding is a temporary thing."
    new "Who knows? Maybe Loren will get tired of Sylrissa in a few months. And maybe her interest in dual wielding is a temporary thing.\n谁知道呢？也许再过几个月，Loren 就会对 Sylrissa 腻了。也许她对双持的兴趣只是一时兴起。"

    old "Could be."
    new "Could be.\n也许吧。"

    old "Thanks [protag]. I see now that I was taking this the wrong way."
    new "Thanks [protag]. I see now that I was taking this the wrong way.\n谢谢，[protag]。我现在明白了，是我把这件事想岔了。"

    old "You're welcome. And Leena? One last thing."
    new "You're welcome. And Leena? One last thing.\n不用谢。还有，Leena？最后一件事。"

    old "Try to not fight with Sylrissa. Or Enok. Or anyone else for that matter. I need our team to stay focused on our goal."
    new "Try to not fight with Sylrissa. Or Enok. Or anyone else for that matter. I need our team to stay focused on our goal.\n尽量别和 Sylrissa 起冲突。也别和 Enok。还有其他人也一样。我需要我们队伍把注意力集中在目标上。"

    old "Right. Of course. I'll... try to get better at ignoring their provocations."
    new "Right. Of course. I'll... try to get better at ignoring their provocations.\n对。当然。我会……努力学着更好地无视他们的挑衅。"

    old "Thanks, Leena."
    new "Thanks, Leena.\n谢谢，Leena。"

    old "I arrive at the Citadel and start looking for Leena."
    new "I arrive at the Citadel and start looking for Leena.\n我来到城堡，开始寻找 Leena。"

    old "Ah, there she is. I wave my hand to get her attention, but she seems to ignore me."
    new "Ah, there she is. I wave my hand to get her attention, but she seems to ignore me.\n啊，她在那儿。我挥手想引起她的注意，她却似乎对我视而不见。"

    old "I close the gap between us but, even when I'm at her side, Leena stays focused her tasks as if she can't see me."
    new "I close the gap between us but, even when I'm at her side, Leena stays focused her tasks as if she can't see me.\n我走近她，可即便我已站在她身旁，Leena 仍专注于手头的事，仿佛看不见我。"

    old "Hey?"
    new "Hey?\n嘿？"

    old "What's wrong with you?"
    new "What's wrong with you?\n你这是怎么了？"

    old "Nothing. I'm just busy. I don't have time for you right now."
    new "Nothing. I'm just busy. I don't have time for you right now.\n没什么。我只是很忙。现在没空理你。"

    old "She starts walking away and it's then that I catch a slight hint of irritation in her expression. Ah. I think I know what this might be about."
    new "She starts walking away and it's then that I catch a slight hint of irritation in her expression. Ah. I think I know what this might be about.\n她转身要走，就在这时，我从她脸上捕捉到一丝烦躁。啊，我想我知道这是怎么回事了。"

    old "I run and catch up to her again. She seems to be quickly losing her patience."
    new "I run and catch up to her again. She seems to be quickly losing her patience.\n我跑过去再次追上她。她似乎正迅速失去耐心。"

    old "You're angry because you spoke with someone else on our team and found out I slept with them, aren't you?"
    new "You're angry because you spoke with someone else on our team and found out I slept with them, aren't you?\n你生气，是因为你跟队里其他人聊过，发现我和他们上过床了，对吧？"

    old "It's fine. You have no obligations towards me. It was fun while it lasted. But now, I must concentrate on my duties. I cannot be distracted by this anymore."
    new "It's fine. You have no obligations towards me. It was fun while it lasted. But now, I must concentrate on my duties. I cannot be distracted by this anymore.\n没关系。你对我没有义务。那段日子虽然短暂，但很开心。不过现在，我必须专注于自己的职责，不能再为此分心了。"

    old "If that's what you want, Leena."
    new "If that's what you want, Leena.\n如果这是你想要的，Leena。"

    old "She stops and pauses for a moment, as if she's trying to figure out what to say."
    new "She stops and pauses for a moment, as if she's trying to figure out what to say.\n她停下脚步，顿了一会儿，仿佛在斟酌该说些什么。"

    old "Yes. I think this way I'll stay focused on our goal and I'll be even more effective in battle. No more distractions."
    new "Yes. I think this way I'll stay focused on our goal and I'll be even more effective in battle. No more distractions.\n是的。我想这样一来，我就能专注于我们的目标，在战斗中也会更加出色。不再分心。"

    old "That said, she picks up the pace and continues walking away. It's like she's running away from me."
    new "That said, she picks up the pace and continues walking away. It's like she's running away from me.\n说完，她加快脚步，继续走开，就好像在躲着我。"

    old "I am pretty sure that wasn't what she wanted. On the other hand, if I really wanted to stay with her, I should have shown my love for her in a stronger way."
    new "I am pretty sure that wasn't what she wanted. On the other hand, if I really wanted to stay with her, I should have shown my love for her in a stronger way.\n我很确定那不是她想要的。另一方面，如果我真的想和她在一起，我就该用更强烈的方式表达我对她的爱。"

    old "I can be sure about one thing though: she'll keep fighting alongside me in top form. She is too proud to let this... accident have an impact on her battlefield performance."
    new "I can be sure about one thing though: she'll keep fighting alongside me in top form. She is too proud to let this... accident have an impact on her battlefield performance.\n但有一件事我可以确定：她会继续以最佳状态和我并肩作战。她太骄傲了，绝不会让这场……意外影响到她在战场上的表现。"

    old "Leena gently but quickly pushes me away and looks around, embarrassed."
    new "Leena gently but quickly pushes me away and looks around, embarrassed.\nLeena 轻轻但迅速地把我推开，然后尴尬地四下张望。"

    old "Apologizing."
    new "Apologizing.\n道歉。"

    old "For what? We're not engaged. We were just having fun-"
    new "For what? We're not engaged. We were just having fun-\n道什么歉？我们又没订婚。我们只是玩玩——"

    old "I place a finger on her lips to silence her."
    new "I place a finger on her lips to silence her.\n我把一根手指按在她嘴唇上，让她安静下来。"

    old "You don't want to attract the attention of the whole Citadel, do you?"
    new "You don't want to attract the attention of the whole Citadel, do you?\n你不想引来整个 Citadel 的注意吧？"

    old "...No, you're right."
    new "...No, you're right.\n……不，你说得对。"

    old "I know how it is. We had fun. We didn't make any promises to each other. There was no formal relationship between us. And I admit, I couldn't resist the idea of trying some things with-"
    new "I know how it is. We had fun. We didn't make any promises to each other. There was no formal relationship between us. And I admit, I couldn't resist the idea of trying some things with-\n我明白是怎么回事。我们玩得开心，谁也没向对方许下承诺。我们之间没有正式关系。而且我承认，我实在忍不住想试试和——"

    old "Stop it. I don't want to know the details."
    new "Stop it. I don't want to know the details.\n别说了。我不想知道细节。"

    old "Okay. I'm fine with that. But Leena, I need you to know that it clarified something for me. You're the one I want, Leena. The only one I want."
    new "Okay. I'm fine with that. But Leena, I need you to know that it clarified something for me. You're the one I want, Leena. The only one I want.\n好。我无所谓。但是 Leena，我要让你知道，这件事让我看清了一些东西。我想要的只有你，Leena。你是我唯一想要的人。"

    old "Oh really? And I'm just supposed to believe that? Sorry, but I don't want to be anyone's second choice!"
    new "Oh really? And I'm just supposed to believe that? Sorry, but I don't want to be anyone's second choice!\n哦，真的吗？我就该这么信你？抱歉，我可不想当任何人的第二选择！"

    old "That's not how it is, Leena. And if we're being completley fair, you didn't tell me about Ilia either."
    new "That's not how it is, Leena. And if we're being completley fair, you didn't tell me about Ilia either.\n事情不是这样的，Leena。而且要是完全讲公平，你也没把 Ilia 的事告诉我。"

    old "Leena averts her gaze guiltily as she blushes a bright red. Did she really think that I wouldn't find out?"
    new "Leena averts her gaze guiltily as she blushes a bright red. Did she really think that I wouldn't find out?\nLeena 愧疚地移开目光，脸红得厉害。她真以为我不会发现吗？"

    old "I came here looking for you awhile back and one of the guards said that you were in your chambers. I was going to leave but, as I was passing the stables, I saw you and a cute young amazon kissing between two griffons."
    new "I came here looking for you awhile back and one of the guards said that you were in your chambers. I was going to leave but, as I was passing the stables, I saw you and a cute young amazon kissing between two griffons.\n之前我来这里找你，一个守卫说你在自己房间里。我本来要离开，但经过马厩时，我看到你和一个可爱的年轻 Amazon 在两头狮鹫之间接吻。"

    old "I must say, despite the initial shock, it was kind of a nice scene. I asked around a bit afterwards and found out that the name of that cute little girl was Ilia. A beautiful name for a beautiful girl."
    new "I must say, despite the initial shock, it was kind of a nice scene. I asked around a bit afterwards and found out that the name of that cute little girl was Ilia. A beautiful name for a beautiful girl.\n我得说，尽管一开始很震惊，但那场面还挺美的。之后我四处打听了一下，得知那个可爱的小姑娘叫 Ilia。美丽的名字配美丽的女孩。"

    old "Y-you... must hate me now."
    new "Y-you... must hate me now.\n你……你现在一定恨我吧。"

    old "No. I love you. As I said, we had no obligation to each other. Still... in that moment I realized that I didn't want to see you kiss anyone else no matter how cute they were. I don't want to share you with anyone. I want you for me alone."
    new "No. I love you. As I said, we had no obligation to each other. Still... in that moment I realized that I didn't want to see you kiss anyone else no matter how cute they were. I don't want to share you with anyone. I want you for me alone.\n不，我爱你。正如我说的，我们对彼此没有义务。只是……那一刻我意识到，我不想看到你亲吻别人，不管对方多可爱。我不想和任何人分享你。我想独自拥有你。"

    old "Leena smiles and I can see tears forming in her eyes."
    new "Leena smiles and I can see tears forming in her eyes.\nLeena 笑了，我看到她眼中泛起了泪水。"

    old "Come. I want to show you something in my chambers."
    new "Come. I want to show you something in my chambers.\n来。我想给你看看我房间里的东西。"

    old "Oh? I hope it's the same thing you showed Ilia. She seemed to really like it."
    new "Oh? I hope it's the same thing you showed Ilia. She seemed to really like it.\n哦？希望就是当初给 Ilia 看的那样东西。她看起来很喜欢。"

    old "Stop joking and follow me!"
    new "Stop joking and follow me!\n别开玩笑了，跟我来！"

    old "I follow Leena and have the best make-up sex of my life. Maybe I should actually thank Ilia for this..."
    new "I follow Leena and have the best make-up sex of my life. Maybe I should actually thank Ilia for this...\n我跟着 Leena，度过了此生最酣畅的一场和好缠绵。也许我真该为此谢谢 Ilia……"

    old "I notice Leena is speaking with another amazon who doesn't look like a fighter. I approach the two curiously and Leena waves at me."
    new "I notice Leena is speaking with another amazon who doesn't look like a fighter. I approach the two curiously and Leena waves at me.\n我注意到 Leena 正在和另一个看起来不像战士的 Amazon 说话。我好奇地走近她们，Leena 朝我挥了挥手。"

    old "Hello, Leena. What are you doing?"
    new "Hello, Leena. What are you doing?\n你好，Leena。你在做什么？"

    old "Queen Karen wanted to commemorate my efforts against the undead."
    new "Queen Karen wanted to commemorate my efforts against the undead.\nKaren 女王想表彰我对抗亡灵所做的努力。"

    old "I see. Are you getting a medal or something like that?"
    new "I see. Are you getting a medal or something like that?\n我明白了。你是要获得勋章之类的吗？"

    old "No. A painting."
    new "No. A painting.\n不。是一幅画。"

    old "Uh? A painting? That's a surprise."
    new "Uh? A painting? That's a surprise.\n呃？一幅画？真让人意外。"

    old "One day I'll show you the Hall Of Memories."
    new "One day I'll show you the Hall Of Memories.\n总有一天我会带你去看 Hall Of Memories。"

    old "Where's that?"
    new "Where's that?\n那是什么地方？"

    old "Here in the Citadel. It's a very private location, accessible only to the amazon elite. It's a big, long hall, and its walls are adorned with beautiful paintings of all the famous amazons of the past."
    new "Here in the Citadel. It's a very private location, accessible only to the amazon elite. It's a big, long hall, and its walls are adorned with beautiful paintings of all the famous amazons of the past.\n就在 Citadel 这里。那是一处非常私密的地方，只有 Amazon 精英才能进入。它是一座又大又长的大厅，四壁挂满了过去所有著名 Amazon 的精美画像。"

    old "That sounds nice. It's a good way to remember them."
    new "That sounds nice. It's a good way to remember them.\n听起来不错。这是缅怀她们的好方式。"

    old "Exactly. And, since Karen wants my adventures to be remembered, I get to choose how I want myself painted. This amazon here is Polla, our most skilled painter. She's created many marvelous pieces of art in the past."
    new "Exactly. And, since Karen wants my adventures to be remembered, I get to choose how I want myself painted. This amazon here is Polla, our most skilled painter. She's created many marvelous pieces of art in the past.\n正是。而且，既然 Karen 希望我的冒险经历被后人铭记，我可以选择自己想以怎样的姿态入画。这位 Amazon 是 Polla，我们最出色的画师。她过去创作过许多绝妙的艺术品。"

    old "You're too kind, Captain Leena."
    new "You're too kind, Captain Leena.\n您过奖了，Leena 队长。"

    old "Leena seems pretty excited about this portrait. It's kind of contagious."
    new "Leena seems pretty excited about this portrait. It's kind of contagious.\nLeena 对这幅肖像显得相当兴奋，这种情绪还挺有感染力的。"

    old "I suppose the painting involves undead. A battle scene perhaps?"
    new "I suppose the painting involves undead. A battle scene perhaps?\n我想这幅画里有亡灵。也许是战斗场景？"

    old "That's exactly it! Polla is putting the finishing touches on it now."
    new "That's exactly it! Polla is putting the finishing touches on it now.\n正是如此！Polla 正在做最后的润色。"

    old "Leena smiles at me and touches my hand. Then, as if suddenly remembering we're not alone, she quickly retracts it."
    new "Leena smiles at me and touches my hand. Then, as if suddenly remembering we're not alone, she quickly retracts it.\nLeena 对我微笑，碰了碰我的手。然后，仿佛突然想起我们并非单独相处，她迅速把手收了回去。"

    old "The other amazon, Polla, didn't seem to notice, but I swear she is half-smiling."
    new "The other amazon, Polla, didn't seem to notice, but I swear she is half-smiling.\n另一个 Amazon——Polla——似乎没注意到，但我发誓她在偷笑。"

    old "Really? You have to let me see it!"
    new "Really? You have to let me see it!\n真的吗？你得让我看看！"

    old "It should be ready now. Right, Polla?"
    new "It should be ready now. Right, Polla?\n现在应该已经好了。对吧，Polla？"

    old "Wait you haven't seen it yet?"
    new "Wait you haven't seen it yet?\n等等，你还没看过吗？"

    old "No, I saw the sketch of course, but not the finished image."
    new "No, I saw the sketch of course, but not the finished image.\n不，我当然看过草图，但没看过完成的画。"

    old "Here it is. I only hope that I have done your beauty and skill justice, Captain Leena."
    new "Here it is. I only hope that I have done your beauty and skill justice, Captain Leena.\n就是这幅。我只希望没有辜负您的美貌与武艺，Leena 队长。"

    old "I can't help but feel a twinge of jealousy upon hearing the worshipping gaze Polla uses when she looks at Leena. On the other hand, I can understand how she feels. Leena has become a sort of local hero to the amazons."
    new "I can't help but feel a twinge of jealousy upon hearing the worshipping gaze Polla uses when she looks at Leena. On the other hand, I can understand how she feels. Leena has become a sort of local hero to the amazons.\n听到 Polla 望着 Leena 时那满是崇拜的语气，我不禁有些嫉妒。另一方面，我也能理解她的感受。Leena 已经成了 Amazon 们心目中的本地英雄。"

    old "I finally take a look at the painting. The Leena on the canvas boldly stands against a horde of undead, cutting through them with an aura of beauty and grace that I'm frankly surprised Polla was able to capture."
    new "I finally take a look at the painting. The Leena on the canvas boldly stands against a horde of undead, cutting through them with an aura of beauty and grace that I'm frankly surprised Polla was able to capture.\n我终于看向那幅画。画布上的 Leena 英勇地迎着一群亡灵，身姿优美而优雅地从中杀出重围，老实说，我很惊讶 Polla 竟能捕捉到这种神韵。"

    old "It's beautiful! Really, I have no words!"
    new "It's beautiful! Really, I have no words!\n太美了！真的，我无话可说！"

    old "I kind of want to steal it and keep it for myself. They wouldn't notice, right?"
    new "I kind of want to steal it and keep it for myself. They wouldn't notice, right?\n我有点想把它偷走自己留着。她们不会发现的，对吧？"

    old "You did a great job, Polla. There is no better painter in all of Aravorn."
    new "You did a great job, Polla. There is no better painter in all of Aravorn.\n你画得太棒了，Polla。整个 Aravorn 都找不出比你更出色的画师。"

    old "Thank you, your greatness. I hoped you would like it, but your enthusiasm fills me with even more joy."
    new "Thank you, your greatness. I hoped you would like it, but your enthusiasm fills me with even more joy.\n谢谢您，大人。我希望您会喜欢，而您的热情更让我满心欢喜。"

    old "I keep looking at the painting, which is very big. It will take two or three amazons to carry it to the hall. I suppose stealing it is even more out of the question than it was before. As I let out a defeated sigh, I hear Leena talking behind me."
    new "I keep looking at the painting, which is very big. It will take two or three amazons to carry it to the hall. I suppose stealing it is even more out of the question than it was before. As I let out a defeated sigh, I hear Leena talking behind me.\n我继续打量着这幅画，它非常大，要把它搬到大厅得两三个 Amazon 才行。看来偷走它比之前更不可能了。我泄气地叹了口气，这时听到 Leena 在身后说话。"

    old "What about that other thing? Is it ready too?"
    new "What about that other thing? Is it ready too?\n那另外一样东西呢？也准备好了吗？"

    old "Yes, I had it delivered to your room as you requested."
    new "Yes, I had it delivered to your room as you requested.\n是的，我照您的吩咐把它送到您房间了。"

    old "[protag], can you follow me please?"
    new "[protag], can you follow me please?\n[protag]，能跟我来一下吗？"

    old "Hm? Yes, of course."
    new "Hm? Yes, of course.\n嗯？好的，当然。"

    old "I follow Leena to her personal chambers wondering what she has in mind."
    new "I follow Leena to her personal chambers wondering what she has in mind.\n我跟着 Leena 来到她的私人房间，心里琢磨着她想干什么。"

    old "[protag], that painting... It's not the only one I asked Polla to do."
    new "[protag], that painting... It's not the only one I asked Polla to do.\n[protag]，那幅画……我不是只让 Polla 画了这一幅。"

    old "You asked her to do two paintings?"
    new "You asked her to do two paintings?\n你让她画了两幅？"

    old "Yes, as personal favor. Karen doesn't know about this second one. It's a gift. For you."
    new "Yes, as personal favor. Karen doesn't know about this second one. It's a gift. For you.\n是的，算是私人请托。Karen 不知道还有这第二幅。这是份礼物。送给你的。"

    old "You're not going to get in trouble, are you?"
    new "You're not going to get in trouble, are you?\n你不会因此惹上麻烦吧？"

    old "No, don't worry. Polla practically idolizes me-"
    new "No, don't worry. Polla practically idolizes me-\n不，别担心。Polla 几乎把我当偶像了——"

    old "I've noticed."
    new "I've noticed.\n我早就看出来了。"

    old "You're jealous? That's cute."
    new "You're jealous? That's cute.\n你吃醋了？真可爱。"

    old "Anyway, Polla won't talk and the only other people who know about it are you and me."
    new "Anyway, Polla won't talk and the only other people who know about it are you and me.\n总之，Polla 不会说出去的，知道这件事的也只有你和我。"

    old "Here, take a look. Of course, it's not the same size for obvious reasons. You need to be able to carry it with you on your way out the Citadel."
    new "Here, take a look. Of course, it's not the same size for obvious reasons. You need to be able to carry it with you on your way out the Citadel.\n来，看看吧。当然，出于显而易见的原因，这幅的尺寸不一样。你得能带着它离开 Citadel 才行。"

    old "She's thought of everything."
    new "She's thought of everything.\n她什么都想到了。"

    old "Leena picks up the other painting and shows it to me."
    new "Leena picks up the other painting and shows it to me.\nLeena 拿起另一幅画展示给我看。"

    old "Ah a smaller version of- wait! You-you-you're naked in this one!"
    new "Ah a smaller version of- wait! You-you-you're naked in this one!\n啊，是小一点的——等等！你、你、你在这幅画里是裸着的！"

    old "Leena blushes slightly."
    new "Leena blushes slightly.\nLeena 微微脸红了。"

    old "You like what you see?"
    new "You like what you see?\n你喜欢眼前看到的吗？"

    old "Of course! Yes, I like it, but-"
    new "Of course! Yes, I like it, but-\n当然！是的，我喜欢，但是——"

    old "Don't worry. Polla used her imagination. I didn't really pose naked for her. As you can see, she gave me a bit more hair than I have in reality..."
    new "Don't worry. Polla used her imagination. I didn't really pose naked for her. As you can see, she gave me a bit more hair than I have in reality...\n别担心。Polla 全凭想象画的，我可没真的脱光给她当模特。你也看到了，她给我画上的毛发比实际要多了些……"

    old "I've seen already Leena naked and we are in an intimate relationship so this sort of thing shouldn't embarrass me, but still, somehow, I am blushing like never before."
    new "I've seen already Leena naked and we are in an intimate relationship so this sort of thing shouldn't embarrass me, but still, somehow, I am blushing like never before.\n我早就见过 Leena 的裸体，我们的关系也很亲密，所以这种事本不该让我难为情，可不知怎么的，我还是脸红得前所未有。"

    old "Thank you, Leena."
    new "Thank you, Leena.\n谢谢你，Leena。"

    old "This way you'll always remember me, even when we can't be together."
    new "This way you'll always remember me, even when we can't be together.\n这样你就能一直记得我，哪怕我们无法在一起。"

    old "I don't need a picture for that. Of course, I'm still taking it."
    new "I don't need a picture for that. Of course, I'm still taking it.\n要记得你，我不需要一幅画。当然，这幅画我还是收下了。"

    old "Leena chuckles and then leans in for a kiss."
    new "Leena chuckles and then leans in for a kiss.\nLeena 轻笑一声，然后凑过来吻我。"

    old "Things escalate quickly from there and let's just say that the painting isn't the only I get from Leena."
    new "Things escalate quickly from there and let's just say that the painting isn't the only I get from Leena.\n事情就此迅速升温，这么说吧，我从 Leena 那里得到的可不只是这幅画。"

    old "For me? Thank you! It's a smaller version of the bigger painting?"
    new "For me? Thank you! It's a smaller version of the bigger painting?\n送给我的？谢谢你！这是那幅大画的缩小版吗？"

    old "Yes. I thought that this way you could always remember me. Even when you're in your chambers planning our next moves."
    new "Yes. I thought that this way you could always remember me. Even when you're in your chambers planning our next moves.\n是的。我想这样你就能一直记得我，哪怕你在自己房间里筹划我们下一步行动的时候。"

    old "With such a beautiful painting hanging in my chambers, I'm not sure I'll be able to focus enough to plan our next attack. I'll be far too distracted."
    new "With such a beautiful painting hanging in my chambers, I'm not sure I'll be able to focus enough to plan our next attack. I'll be far too distracted.\n有这么美的画挂在我房间里，我怕是没法专心筹划下一次进攻了，肯定会走神。"

    old "Leena smiles and puts the painting down. Then moves in close and starts to undress me. This is what I wanted too, before leaving the Citadel with her precious gift."
    new "Leena smiles and puts the painting down. Then moves in close and starts to undress me. This is what I wanted too, before leaving the Citadel with her precious gift.\nLeena 微笑着把画放下，然后凑近我，开始脱我的衣服。在带着她这份珍贵的礼物离开 Citadel 之前，这也正是我想要的。"

    old "The pressure I've been facing these last few days is enormous."
    new "The pressure I've been facing these last few days is enormous.\n这几天我承受的压力太大了。"

    old "The Council is never happy. Yes, they praise my successes, but then they immediately expect me to be able to repeat those successes or demand that I do even better."
    new "The Council is never happy. Yes, they praise my successes, but then they immediately expect me to be able to repeat those successes or demand that I do even better.\n议会从来都不会满足。没错，他们会称赞我的胜利，但紧接着就指望我能复制那些胜利，甚至要求我做得更好。"

    old "I do have confidence in my team and myself. Still... It's not that easy. They don't understand how hard earned each victory is."
    new "I do have confidence in my team and myself. Still... It's not that easy. They don't understand how hard earned each victory is.\n我确实信任我的团队，也信任自己。只是……事情没那么容易。他们不明白每一场胜利都是多么来之不易。"

    old "I'm so tired, but I can't exactly stop now. Sleeping just leads to nightmares lately anyway. Even if I am tired, I have to..."
    new "I'm so tired, but I can't exactly stop now. Sleeping just leads to nightmares lately anyway. Even if I am tired, I have to...\n我太累了，可现在又没法停下。何况最近一睡着就做噩梦。就算再累，我也必须……"

    old "[protag], my love. Stay strong!"
    new "[protag], my love. Stay strong!\n[protag]，我的爱人。要坚强！"

    old "Leena!"
    new "Leena!\nLeena！"

    old "Together, we can get through this. Nothing can stop us. You don't need to be afraid of anything."
    new "Together, we can get through this. Nothing can stop us. You don't need to be afraid of anything.\n我们一起一定能熬过去。没有什么能阻挡我们。你什么都不用害怕。"

    old "Maybe you're right. It's just... I can't sleep at night anymore. I get so caught up on what might happen on the battlefield the next day that I can't stop myself."
    new "Maybe you're right. It's just... I can't sleep at night anymore. I get so caught up on what might happen on the battlefield the next day that I can't stop myself.\n也许你说得对。只是……我夜里再也睡不着了。我会忍不住一直想第二天战场上可能发生的事，怎么也停不下来。"

    old "One mistake, one thing I didn't think of. I can't afford to miss anything."
    new "One mistake, one thing I didn't think of. I can't afford to miss anything.\n一个失误、一个我没想到的地方，都可能致命。我经不起任何疏忽。"

    old "Oh? but you're dreaming now. You're dreaming about me."
    new "Oh? but you're dreaming now. You're dreaming about me.\n哦？可你现在就在做梦呀。你在梦到我。"

    old "Uh? Am I?"
    new "Uh? Am I?\n呃？是吗？"

    old "Yes. Let me ask you a question, [protag]."
    new "Yes. Let me ask you a question, [protag].\n是的。让我问你一个问题，[protag]。"

    old "What do you like about me most?"
    new "What do you like about me most?\n你最喜欢我哪一点？"

    old "It's hard to say. Your skills, your courage-"
    new "It's hard to say. Your skills, your courage-\n这很难说。你的武艺，你的勇气——"

    old "She shakes her head and then clarifies what she meant."
    new "She shakes her head and then clarifies what she meant.\n她摇了摇头，然后解释了自己的意思。"

    old "What do you like best about my body."
    new "What do you like best about my body.\n你最喜欢我身体的哪个部位？"

    old "Your... your body?"
    new "Your... your body?\n你的……你的身体？"

    old "Yes. My body. I know you love me as a person, but you also love my body, am I right?"
    new "Yes. My body. I know you love me as a person, but you also love my body, am I right?\n是的。我的身体。我知道你爱我这个人，但你也爱我的身体，对吗？"

    old "Ahem, yes, of course. You are beautiful. You have..."
    new "Ahem, yes, of course. You are beautiful. You have...\n咳咳，是的，当然。你很美。你有……"

    old "I have?"
    new "I have?\n我有什么？"

    old "Beautiful legs and-"
    new "Beautiful legs and-\n修长的美腿，还有——"

    old "Suddenly, I stop talking. It's as if I realize that this is indeed a dream but, unlike the times before, it's not a nightmare, it's a pleasant dream."
    new "Suddenly, I stop talking. It's as if I realize that this is indeed a dream but, unlike the times before, it's not a nightmare, it's a pleasant dream.\n我突然停住不说了。仿佛我意识到这的确是一场梦，但和之前不同，这不是噩梦，而是一场美梦。"

    old "I remember that day, when Leena showed me her new jumping sword trick. That was probably the moment I fell in love with her."
    new "I remember that day, when Leena showed me her new jumping sword trick. That was probably the moment I fell in love with her.\n我想起那一天，Leena 向我展示她新练的腾空剑招。也许就是那一刻，我爱上了她。"

    old "I remember the fireplace, the smell of burning wood, the crackling sound of the fire, and the sunset. But most clearly of all, I remember her. I remember Leena."
    new "I remember the fireplace, the smell of burning wood, the crackling sound of the fire, and the sunset. But most clearly of all, I remember her. I remember Leena.\n我记得那座壁炉，柴火燃烧的气味，火焰噼啪作响的声音，还有那天的落日。但记忆最清晰的，是她。我记住了 Leena。"

    old "And in my dream, I imagine her completely naked in that pose."
    new "And in my dream, I imagine her completely naked in that pose.\n而在梦里，我幻想着她以那个姿势完全赤裸的样子。"

    old "I dream about her, when she was too busy working on fixing her boot to look at me. But even then I was happy, because I could admire her body better. Her long legs, her perfect butt..."
    new "I dream about her, when she was too busy working on fixing her boot to look at me. But even then I was happy, because I could admire her body better. Her long legs, her perfect butt...\n我梦见她，那时她正忙着修靴子，顾不上看我。但即便如此我也很开心，因为我可以更尽情地欣赏她的身体。她修长的双腿，她完美的臀部……"

    old "I love you, Leena. I love your body, your skills, your soul. I love everything about you."
    new "I love you, Leena. I love your body, your skills, your soul. I love everything about you.\n我爱你，Leena。我爱你的身体，你的武艺，你的灵魂。我爱你的一切。"

    old "I breathe in, drinking in the damp cool night breeze that rushes over me."
    new "I breathe in, drinking in the damp cool night breeze that rushes over me.\n我深吸一口气，尽情感受拂过身畔那潮湿而凉爽的夜风。"

    old "The air is crisp, the stars are dim, the moon is full, and the dead are out to play. It's exactly the kind of pleasant evening that is best spent in hiding, despite the ever-present allure of the fields outside. The deadliest nights are always the loveliest."
    new "The air is crisp, the stars are dim, the moon is full, and the dead are out to play. It's exactly the kind of pleasant evening that is best spent in hiding, despite the ever-present allure of the fields outside. The deadliest nights are always the loveliest.\n空气清爽，星光黯淡，月亮圆圆的，死灵们纷纷出来游荡。这恰恰是那种最好躲起来度过的怡人夜晚，尽管外面的田野总是充满诱惑。最致命的夜晚，往往也最美丽。"

    old "My tent is situated on a grassy knoll comfortably outside the crawling mists of N'Mar, but close enough for me to see the moonlight dancing across the fields, bent and scattered by the foggy haze."
    new "My tent is situated on a grassy knoll comfortably outside the crawling mists of N'Mar, but close enough for me to see the moonlight dancing across the fields, bent and scattered by the foggy haze.\n我的帐篷搭在一座长满青草的小丘上，舒服地处在 N'Mar 蔓延的雾气之外，却又近得足以让我看到月光在田野上舞动，被朦胧的雾霭折射、散开。"

    old "Oy!"
    new "Oy!\n喂！"

    old "Do my ears deceive me? Could someone be out in the fields on this night of nights?"
    new "Do my ears deceive me? Could someone be out in the fields on this night of nights?\n是我的耳朵听错了吗？在这最不寻常的夜晚，竟会有人跑到野地里？"

    old "I hear the cry louder this time. The voice sounds distinctly human, with an air of distress."
    new "I hear the cry louder this time. The voice sounds distinctly human, with an air of distress.\n这一次，我听到喊声更响了。那声音分明是人发出的，还带着惊慌。"

    old "I step out of my tent and bound down the knoll."
    new "I step out of my tent and bound down the knoll.\n我走出帐篷，快步冲下小丘。"

    old "Hello! Is anyone there?"
    new "Hello! Is anyone there?\n喂！有人吗？"

    old "A figure comes running forward, out of the mist, and drops to the ground in front of me, breathless."
    new "A figure comes running forward, out of the mist, and drops to the ground in front of me, breathless.\n一个人影从雾中跑出来，气喘吁吁地瘫倒在我面前的地上。"

    old "I poke my head out of my tent, and scan the edge of the field."
    new "I poke my head out of my tent, and scan the edge of the field.\n我把头探出帐篷，扫视着田野的边缘。"

    old "At the base of the knoll, I spot a figure running forward, out of the mist-covered fields."
    new "At the base of the knoll, I spot a figure running forward, out of the mist-covered fields.\n在小丘脚下，我看见一个人影从雾霭笼罩的田野里跑了出来。"

    old "The figure begins stumbling up the hill. Evidently he's seen my tent."
    new "The figure begins stumbling up the hill. Evidently he's seen my tent.\n那人影开始踉踉跄跄地往山上爬。显然他看见了我的帐篷。"

    old "The figure trips over himself, and lays sprawled out on the side of the hill. I run up to where he's fallen."
    new "The figure trips over himself, and lays sprawled out on the side of the hill. I run up to where he's fallen.\n那人绊了一下，整个人瘫倒在山坡上。我跑到他摔倒的地方。"

    old "He's wearing armor displaying the emblem of the human empire. But what would a soldier be doing out here, at this hour?"
    new "He's wearing armor displaying the emblem of the human empire. But what would a soldier be doing out here, at this hour?\n他穿着印有人类帝国徽记的铠甲。可一个士兵在这种时候跑到这里来做什么？"

    old "I reach down and help him up."
    new "I reach down and help him up.\n我俯下身，扶他起来。"

    old "Thank you, mister-"
    new "Thank you, mister-\n谢谢您，先生——"

    old "Thank you, miss-"
    new "Thank you, miss-\n谢谢您，小姐——"

    old "My name is [protag]."
    new "My name is [protag].\n我叫 [protag]。"

    old "And I am Reginald. Private Reginald, Grimoire's third division."
    new "And I am Reginald. Private Reginald, Grimoire's third division.\n我是 Reginald。列兵 Reginald，隶属 Grimoire 第三师。"

    old "I don't belive so. But I can't say the same for my comrades."
    new "I don't belive so. But I can't say the same for my comrades.\n我想没有。但我没法替我的战友们这样说。"

    old "Your fellows, are they-"
    new "Your fellows, are they-\n你的同伴们，他们是不是——"

    old "We were given the order to retreat, but I was separated from my squad in the mist."
    new "We were given the order to retreat, but I was separated from my squad in the mist.\n我们接到了撤退的命令，可我在雾中和自己的小队走散了。"

    old "Well, we should try to reunite you with your squad."
    new "Well, we should try to reunite you with your squad.\n那么，我们应该设法让你和小队会合。"

    old "Do you know this area?"
    new "Do you know this area?\n你熟悉这片区域吗？"

    old "It's not my home, but I know it well enough not to run into trouble. I can't guarantee that we'll find your squad mates, but we won't get lost."
    new "It's not my home, but I know it well enough not to run into trouble. I can't guarantee that we'll find your squad mates, but we won't get lost.\n这不是我的家乡，但我对这里足够熟悉，不至于惹上麻烦。我不能保证能找到你的队友，但不会迷路。"

    old "Unfortunately, I dropped my torch as we fled. Do you have a torch?"
    new "Unfortunately, I dropped my torch as we fled. Do you have a torch?\n可惜我们逃跑时我把火把弄丢了。你有火把吗？"

    old "Torch? No. Why, do you expect your fellows to be carrying torches?"
    new "Torch? No. Why, do you expect your fellows to be carrying torches?\n火把？没有。怎么，你指望你的同伴们带着火把吗？"

    old "The moon is out. If your eyes have adjusted to the darkness, and I hope that they have by now, you'll see farther by the light of the moon than by the light of a torch. Besides, torches are unwieldy things - more likely to blind you than to shine a clear path on a night like tonight."
    new "The moon is out. If your eyes have adjusted to the darkness, and I hope that they have by now, you'll see farther by the light of the moon than by the light of a torch. Besides, torches are unwieldy things - more likely to blind you than to shine a clear path on a night like tonight.\n月亮出来了。如果你的眼睛已经适应了黑暗——我希望现在你已经适应了——借着月光能比借着火把看得更远。况且，火把这玩意儿很碍事，在今晚这样的夜里，它更可能晃得你眼花，而不是为你照清前路。"

    old "Our squad always has at least two active torch bearers."
    new "Our squad always has at least two active torch bearers.\n我们小队总是至少有两名举着火把的人。"

    old "Well then, I don't suspect we'll have much difficulty finding them."
    new "Well then, I don't suspect we'll have much difficulty finding them.\n那我想，找到他们不会太难。"

    old "I forage into the fog, and Reginald follows several short steps behind me. The fog grows thicker as we wander further into N'Mar, but I have little difficulty picking out familiar shapes on the landscape."
    new "I forage into the fog, and Reginald follows several short steps behind me. The fog grows thicker as we wander further into N'Mar, but I have little difficulty picking out familiar shapes on the landscape.\n我迈步走进雾中，Reginald 隔着一小段距离跟在后面。随着我们深入 N'Mar，雾气越来越浓，但辨认地貌上熟悉的轮廓对我来说并不难。"

    old "It takes less than a minute for me to spot the dim glow of torches in the distance."
    new "It takes less than a minute for me to spot the dim glow of torches in the distance.\n不到一分钟，我就发现了远处火把的微光。"

    old "Do you see that glimmer of light?"
    new "Do you see that glimmer of light?\n你看到那点微光了吗？"

    old "Looks like we found your friends."
    new "Looks like we found your friends.\n看来我们找到你的朋友们了。"

    old "Let's hope so."
    new "Let's hope so.\n但愿如此。"

    old "I quicken my pace and follow the light."
    new "I quicken my pace and follow the light.\n我加快脚步，朝那光亮走去。"

    old "Call out to your friends. They might not take kindly to the sight of a stranger right now."
    new "Call out to your friends. They might not take kindly to the sight of a stranger right now.\n喊一喊你的朋友们吧。他们这会儿见到陌生人恐怕不会有好脸色。"

    old "Ho!"
    new "Ho!\n喂！"

    old "Who goes there?"
    new "Who goes there?\n谁在那里？"

    old "Sergeant Thomas, it's me."
    new "Sergeant Thomas, it's me.\nThomas 中士，是我。"

    old "Reginald?"
    new "Reginald?\nReginald？"

    old "Yes, sir."
    new "Yes, sir.\n是的，长官。"

    old "Reginald runs up to meet his squad."
    new "Reginald runs up to meet his squad.\nReginald 跑上前去和他的小队会合。"

    old "Thank the gods you're still alive. What happened?"
    new "Thank the gods you're still alive. What happened?\n感谢众神，你还活着。出什么事了？"

    old "My torch went out and I became lost in the mists. Fortunately, I chanced upon this traveler who was able to guide me to you."
    new "My torch went out and I became lost in the mists. Fortunately, I chanced upon this traveler who was able to guide me to you.\n我的火把熄了，在雾里迷了路。幸好我碰巧遇到这位旅人，是他把我带到了你们这里。"

    old "Sergeant Thomas turns to me."
    new "Sergeant Thomas turns to me.\nThomas 中士转向我。"

    old "Thank you for returning my man. To who do I owe the pleasure?"
    new "Thank you for returning my man. To who do I owe the pleasure?\n谢谢你把我的人带回来。请问我该如何称呼您？"

    old "My name is [protag]. I was just passing through these parts. And I suggest that you move as well. This is not the night to loiter about."
    new "My name is [protag]. I was just passing through these parts. And I suggest that you move as well. This is not the night to loiter about.\n我叫 [protag]。我只是路过这一带。我建议你们也动身离开。今晚可不是游荡的时候。"

    old "Aye, we've abandoned our mission and are on the retreat. Can you lead us out of these mists?"
    new "Aye, we've abandoned our mission and are on the retreat. Can you lead us out of these mists?\n是啊，我们放弃了任务，正在撤退。你能带我们走出这片雾吗？"

    old "Indeed I can."
    new "Indeed I can.\n当然可以。"

    old "I begin walking, and the entire squad of Grimoire soldiers falls into step behind me."
    new "I begin walking, and the entire squad of Grimoire soldiers falls into step behind me.\n我迈步出发，整支 Grimoire 小队都跟在了我身后。"

    old "Are you familiar with this region?"
    new "Are you familiar with this region?\n你熟悉这片地区吗？"

    old "I know it well enough. This isn't my first time here."
    new "I know it well enough. This isn't my first time here.\n还算熟悉。我不是第一次来这里。"

    old "What could have brought you here more than once?"
    new "What could have brought you here more than once?\n是什么让你不止一次来到这里？"

    old "I've spent my life working as a merchant, and in my many years of trafficking goods, I've found that there is one consistency among all successful merchants: be willing go travel where other merchants aren't."
    new "I've spent my life working as a merchant, and in my many years of trafficking goods, I've found that there is one consistency among all successful merchants: be willing go travel where other merchants aren't.\n我这辈子都在经商，多年贩运货物的经历让我发现，所有成功的商人都有一个共同点：愿意去别的商人不去的地方闯荡。"

    old "Competition is for dullards and simpletons."
    new "Competition is for dullards and simpletons.\n竞争是留给蠢货和傻瓜的。"

    old "I am a scholar, and my first and greatest loyalty is to knowledge. I endeavor to know and understand the history of all lands across Aravorn. Knowledge of the lands of N'Mar has long evaded my peers. It is my hope that my field research around these parts can benefit my academic fellows."
    new "I am a scholar, and my first and greatest loyalty is to knowledge. I endeavor to know and understand the history of all lands across Aravorn. Knowledge of the lands of N'Mar has long evaded my peers. It is my hope that my field research around these parts can benefit my academic fellows.\n我是一名学者，我首要且最大的忠诚属于知识。我致力于了解并理解 Aravorn 全境所有土地的历史。关于 N'Mar 这片土地的知识，长久以来一直让我的同行们望而却步。我希望自己在这一带的实地考察能惠及学界同仁。"

    old "And, of course, the chance to become a famous figure in scholarly circles has a certain allure to it."
    new "And, of course, the chance to become a famous figure in scholarly circles has a certain allure to it.\n当然，能在学术界扬名立万的机会也自有其吸引力。"

    old "I am a bard by trade. I have, on several occasions, been commissioned by knights and adventurers to accompany on their journey so that I might tell tales of their conquest."
    new "I am a bard by trade. I have, on several occasions, been commissioned by knights and adventurers to accompany on their journey so that I might tell tales of their conquest.\n我以吟游诗人为业。曾多次受骑士和冒险者之托，随他们同行，好把他们征服的故事传唱开来。"

    old "Consequently, I find myself quite well-traveled, even more well-traveled than the so-called adventurers that I often accompany."
    new "Consequently, I find myself quite well-traveled, even more well-traveled than the so-called adventurers that I often accompany.\n因此，我可以说见多识广，甚至比我常陪同的那些所谓冒险者走过更多地方。"

    old "Nowadays, adventures commission me for my experience and wordliness as much as my talents in storycrafting. I've turned myself something of a good luck charm."
    new "Nowadays, adventures commission me for my experience and wordliness as much as my talents in storycrafting. I've turned myself something of a good luck charm.\n如今，冒险者们雇佣我，看重的不只是我编故事的本事，还有我的阅历和见识。我简直把自己变成了某种吉祥物。"

    old "The truth is, I am a debt collector by trade. And some people will travel far and wide to evade their debts. It behooves me to be familiar with all the lands of Aravorn, and the plains of N'Mar seem to be a favored hiding spot for those hoping to escape their financial obligations."
    new "The truth is, I am a debt collector by trade. And some people will travel far and wide to evade their debts. It behooves me to be familiar with all the lands of Aravorn, and the plains of N'Mar seem to be a favored hiding spot for those hoping to escape their financial obligations.\n其实，我的职业是收债人。有些人为了赖账会远走他乡。所以我必须熟悉 Aravorn 的所有土地，而 N'Mar 的平原似乎是那些想逃避债务的人最爱躲藏的地方。"

    old "Well, we certainly appreciate your assistance."
    new "Well, we certainly appreciate your assistance.\n那么，我们非常感谢您的帮助。"

    old "We reach the edge of the mists, and I lead the squad up the knoll where I've pitched my tent."
    new "We reach the edge of the mists, and I lead the squad up the knoll where I've pitched my tent.\n我们来到雾的边缘，我领着这支小队登上我搭帐篷的那座小丘。"

    old "Well, here we are. Do you require any further assistance?"
    new "Well, here we are. Do you require any further assistance?\n好了，我们到了。你们还需要别的帮助吗？"

    old "Thank you for getting my men out safe. I appreciate your help. But I wonder if I might impose upon you once more."
    new "Thank you for getting my men out safe. I appreciate your help. But I wonder if I might impose upon you once more.\n谢谢你让我的弟兄们平安脱身。我很感激你的帮助。不过，我能否再冒昧地麻烦你一次？"

    old "What is it that you want?"
    new "What is it that you want?\n你想要什么？"

    old "I lead a squad, but we are part of a much larger force. An entire company, in fact."
    new "I lead a squad, but we are part of a much larger force. An entire company, in fact.\n我带领的是一支小队，但我们隶属于一支大得多的部队。事实上，是一整个连。"

    old "A company. That's...one hundred men?"
    new "A company. That's...one hundred men?\n一个连。那是……一百人？"

    old "One hundred and twenty."
    new "One hundred and twenty.\n一百二十人。"

    old "I let out a low whistle."
    new "I let out a low whistle.\n我轻轻地吹了声口哨。"

    old "What are one hundred and twenty men doing out here on a night like this?"
    new "What are one hundred and twenty men doing out here on a night like this?\n一百二十个人在这种夜晚跑到这里来做什么？"

    old "This foggy mist that covers N'Mar is unnatural. The council of Grimoire believes that there is sinister magic is behind it. We were sent to investigate, with the castle being the focus of our attention."
    new "This foggy mist that covers N'Mar is unnatural. The council of Grimoire believes that there is sinister magic is behind it. We were sent to investigate, with the castle being the focus of our attention.\n笼罩 N'Mar 的这片浓雾并不自然。Grimoire 议会认为，其背后有邪恶的魔法作祟。我们被派来调查，而那座城堡正是我们关注的重点。"

    old "My squad became so ensnared in the fog that it seemed futile to press on, and so we made the order to retreat and regroup. We made it out unscathed, with your help. But I am forced to wonder if perhaps other platoons weren't so fortunate."
    new "My squad became so ensnared in the fog that it seemed futile to press on, and so we made the order to retreat and regroup. We made it out unscathed, with your help. But I am forced to wonder if perhaps other platoons weren't so fortunate.\n我的小队在雾里陷得太深，继续前进似乎毫无意义，于是我们下令撤退、重新集结。多亏了你，我们毫发无损地走了出来。但我不得不担心，其他排或许就没这么幸运了。"

    old "I'm sorry if this sounds like an unreasonable request, and you are entirely within your rights to refuse. But I'd like to go back in and try to find any other men lost in the fog, with you as our guide."
    new "I'm sorry if this sounds like an unreasonable request, and you are entirely within your rights to refuse. But I'd like to go back in and try to find any other men lost in the fog, with you as our guide.\n如果这个请求听起来有些过分，我很抱歉，你完全有权拒绝。但我还是想再回去，在雾里找找其他走失的人，请你做我们的向导。"

    old "I assisted your private in finding your squad, and I can assist your squad in finding your company."
    new "I assisted your private in finding your squad, and I can assist your squad in finding your company.\n我帮你的列兵找到了小队，也可以帮你这个小队找到你们的大部队。"

    old "Thank you. Your kindness will not be forgotten. I'll do everything I can to ensure that you're rewarded for your efforts."
    new "Thank you. Your kindness will not be forgotten. I'll do everything I can to ensure that you're rewarded for your efforts.\n谢谢你。你的恩情我们不会忘记。我会尽我所能，确保你的付出得到回报。"

    old "I apologize if this sounds cold of me, but you're asking me to assist with a mission that I have no personal stake in. I've already helped your squad to escape the fog. Neither you or I know what fate awaits us if we choose to dive back into the fog. Why should I take that risk?"
    new "I apologize if this sounds cold of me, but you're asking me to assist with a mission that I have no personal stake in. I've already helped your squad to escape the fog. Neither you or I know what fate awaits us if we choose to dive back into the fog. Why should I take that risk?\n如果这话听起来很无情，我道歉，但你是要我去协助一个与我个人毫无利害关系的任务。我已经帮你的小队逃出了雾区。你我都不知道，若选择再一头扎回雾里，等待我们的会是什么命运。我凭什么冒这个险？"

    old "We're here on orders of the council of Grimoire."
    new "We're here on orders of the council of Grimoire.\n我们是奉 Grimoire 议会的命令来这里的。"

    old "Good friends to have."
    new "Good friends to have.\n能和他们交上朋友是件好事。"

    old "I cannot speak for the council, and I can make no guarantees on their behalf. But I can guarantee that I'll do everything in my power to ensure that they're made aware of the role you played in assisting us with our mission."
    new "I cannot speak for the council, and I can make no guarantees on their behalf. But I can guarantee that I'll do everything in my power to ensure that they're made aware of the role you played in assisting us with our mission.\n我不能代表议会说话，也无法替他们作任何保证。但我可以保证，我会尽我所能，让他们知晓你在协助我们完成使命中发挥的作用。"

    old "Well then, I'll do everything I can to see that your mission is a success. But I need you to trust my judgment. Can you agree to that?"
    new "Well then, I'll do everything I can to see that your mission is a success. But I need you to trust my judgment. Can you agree to that?\n那么，我会尽我所能，让你们的使命取得成功。但我需要你信任我的判断。你能答应吗？"

    old "Your judgment in these fields is likely much more sound than my own."
    new "Your judgment in these fields is likely much more sound than my own.\n在这些田野间，你的判断大概比我的可靠得多。"

    old "First of all, I need for your men to extinguish their torches."
    new "First of all, I need for your men to extinguish their torches.\n首先，我需要你的人熄灭他们的火把。"

    old "That's preposterous!"
    new "That's preposterous!\n这太荒唐了！"

    old "Why do you need us to put out our torches?"
    new "Why do you need us to put out our torches?\n你为什么非要我们熄灭火把？"

    old "Those torches of yours won't light the ground more than a few feet in front of you. If you want to see far in the dark of night, do it by the light you've already been given."
    new "Those torches of yours won't light the ground more than a few feet in front of you. If you want to see far in the dark of night, do it by the light you've already been given.\n你们的火把照不到身前几尺远的地方。想在黑夜里看得远，就该借助早已赐予你们的那道亮光。"

    old "I point upward, to the bright full moon."
    new "I point upward, to the bright full moon.\n我向上指了指那轮明亮的满月。"

    old "If you'll do as I say and put out those torches, you'll find that your eyes will gradually adjust to the dark, allowing you to make the best use of that moonlight. Those torches are more of a hindrance than a help."
    new "If you'll do as I say and put out those torches, you'll find that your eyes will gradually adjust to the dark, allowing you to make the best use of that moonlight. Those torches are more of a hindrance than a help.\n只要照我说的把火把灭掉，你们就会发现眼睛会逐渐适应黑暗，从而能更好地利用月光。那些火把非但帮不上忙，反而是累赘。"

    old "Do as he says. Extinguish the torches."
    new "Do as he says. Extinguish the torches.\n照他说的做。把火把熄灭。"

    old "Do as she says. Extinguish the torches."
    new "Do as she says. Extinguish the torches.\n照她说的做。把火把熄灭。"

    old "The torch bearers begrudgingly put out their torches."
    new "The torch bearers begrudgingly put out their torches.\n举火把的人不情不愿地熄灭了火把。"

    old "Secondly, the way that you march is problematic. You march in single file. That's good if you want to conceal your numbers. But if we encounter anything troublesome out there, it's best that you look numerous and intimidating, and ready to fight. If you march in rank formation, all side by side, we'll be better prepared to respond to any threats that come our way."
    new "Secondly, the way that you march is problematic. You march in single file. That's good if you want to conceal your numbers. But if we encounter anything troublesome out there, it's best that you look numerous and intimidating, and ready to fight. If you march in rank formation, all side by side, we'll be better prepared to respond to any threats that come our way.\n其次，你们行军的阵型也有问题。你们排成一列纵队，如果想隐藏人数倒是不错。但万一在外面遇到什么麻烦，你们最好显得人多势众、不好惹，而且随时能开战。如果排成横列、并肩而行，我们就能更好地应对迎面而来的任何威胁。"

    old "Lastly, there are many beasts throughout this land. Sometimes, being quick to attack is not the best way to respond. If we do run into some kind of resistance, will you allow me to decide how your squad responds?"
    new "Lastly, there are many beasts throughout this land. Sometimes, being quick to attack is not the best way to respond. If we do run into some kind of resistance, will you allow me to decide how your squad responds?\n最后，这片土地上野兽众多。有时候，急于出手并不是最好的应对方式。如果我们真的遇到某种抵抗，你能让我来决定你的小队该如何应对吗？"

    old "As I said, I'll have to trust your judgment."
    new "As I said, I'll have to trust your judgment.\n正如我所说，我只能相信你的判断。"

    old "You said your fellows were headed in the direction of the castle, correct?"
    new "You said your fellows were headed in the direction of the castle, correct?\n你说过你的同伴们正朝城堡的方向去，对吗？"

    old "Well, then. Let's get to it."
    new "Well, then. Let's get to it.\n那么，我们动身吧。"

    old "I begin marching into the mist, and Sergeant Thomas and his men fall into step behind me. As I glance to my left and right, I find myself pleased that the men have fallen into a proper rank formation."
    new "I begin marching into the mist, and Sergeant Thomas and his men fall into step behind me. As I glance to my left and right, I find myself pleased that the men have fallen into a proper rank formation.\n我迈步走进雾中，Thomas 中士和他的部下紧随其后。我朝左右扫了一眼，欣慰地发现他们已经排成了整齐的横列阵型。"

    old "I hear a gravely moan in the distance."
    new "I hear a gravely moan in the distance.\n我听到远处传来沙哑的呻吟声。"

    old "Do you hear that?"
    new "Do you hear that?\n你听到了吗？"

    old "Sergeant Thomas nods."
    new "Sergeant Thomas nods.\nThomas 中士点了点头。"

    old "It sounds like zombies. Perhaps a half dozen of them. Have you encountered them before?"
    new "It sounds like zombies. Perhaps a half dozen of them. Have you encountered them before?\n听起来像是僵尸。大概有半打。你们以前遇到过吗？"

    old "No, we haven't. We were warned that we might encounter the formerly dead in this field, but we never came face-to-face with any of them."
    new "No, we haven't. We were warned that we might encounter the formerly dead in this field, but we never came face-to-face with any of them.\n不，没有。有人警告过我们，在这片野地里可能会遇到早已死去的人，但我们还从没和他们正面打过照面。"

    old "Well, you're about to. Zombies are mindless beasts, and we'd do well to dispatch them now. Better than trying to avoid them and risk having them follow us."
    new "Well, you're about to. Zombies are mindless beasts, and we'd do well to dispatch them now. Better than trying to avoid them and risk having them follow us.\n那么，你们马上就要遇到了。僵尸是没脑子的怪物，我们最好现在就把它们解决掉，总比设法避开它们、却要冒着被它们尾随的风险强。"

    old "Are you and your men ready for battle?"
    new "Are you and your men ready for battle?\n你和你的部下准备好战斗了吗？"

    old "Careful! More of them!"
    new "Careful! More of them!\n小心！又来了更多！"

    old "Well, that was a great deal easier than I expected."
    new "Well, that was a great deal easier than I expected.\n嗯，这比我预想的要轻松得多。"

    old "Zombies are dangerous in numbers, but individually they pose little threat. That's why I suggested dispatching them now, before their ranks grow more abundant."
    new "Zombies are dangerous in numbers, but individually they pose little threat. That's why I suggested dispatching them now, before their ranks grow more abundant.\n僵尸成群时很危险，但单个对付起来威胁不大。所以我建议趁现在就把它们解决掉，免得它们越聚越多。"

    old "We're deep enough in the fog that the knoll we came from is now barely visible in the distance. You can see it, can't you?"
    new "We're deep enough in the fog that the knoll we came from is now barely visible in the distance. You can see it, can't you?\n我们在雾里已经走得够深了，出发时那座小丘现在在远处几乎看不到了。你能看到它吧？"

    old "I point to an oak tree, not a stone's throw from where we stand."
    new "I point to an oak tree, not a stone's throw from where we stand.\n我指向一棵橡树，离我们站的地方不过一箭之遥。"

    old "That tree is the largest landmark we'll encounter for awhile on these plains."
    new "That tree is the largest landmark we'll encounter for awhile on these plains.\n这棵树是接下来好一阵子我们在平原上会遇到的最大的地标。"

    old "I turn to the men of Sergeant Thomas's squad."
    new "I turn to the men of Sergeant Thomas's squad.\n我转向 Thomas 中士小队的士兵们。"

    old "If any of you become lost or separated as we move forward, you can make your way to this tree, and then return to the knoll at the edge of the fog. Do you understand?"
    new "If any of you become lost or separated as we move forward, you can make your way to this tree, and then return to the knoll at the edge of the fog. Do you understand?\n继续前进时，如果你们中有人迷路或走散，就朝这棵树走，然后再回到雾边缘的那座小丘。明白了吗？"

    old "The men nod in agreement, and I resume pressing forward."
    new "The men nod in agreement, and I resume pressing forward.\n士兵们点头表示明白，我于是继续向前推进。"

    old "I see the dance of moving torches in the distance."
    new "I see the dance of moving torches in the distance.\n我看见远处有火把在移动，光影摇曳。"

    old "That looks like the rest of your company."
    new "That looks like the rest of your company.\n那看起来像是你们连队的其他人。"

    old "That doesn't look like enough men to be the entire company. And look, they're moving away from the castle. They must be on the retreat."
    new "That doesn't look like enough men to be the entire company. And look, they're moving away from the castle. They must be on the retreat.\n那人手看起来不像是整个连队。而且你看，他们正朝远离城堡的方向移动，一定是在撤退。"

    old "Let's find out what they're running from."
    new "Let's find out what they're running from.\n我们去看看他们到底在逃离什么。"

    old "We run up to meet the retreating soldiers."
    new "We run up to meet the retreating soldiers.\n我们跑上前去迎上那些撤退的士兵。"

    old "Ho there!"
    new "Ho there!\n喂，那边的人！"

    old "Sergeant Thomas!"
    new "Sergeant Thomas!\nThomas 中士！"

    old "The retreating soldiers come to a halt. Sergeant Thomas scans the crowd. There are approximately twenty soldiers—enough to constitute a single platoon."
    new "The retreating soldiers come to a halt. Sergeant Thomas scans the crowd. There are approximately twenty soldiers—enough to constitute a single platoon.\n撤退的士兵们停下脚步。Thomas 中士扫视着这群人。大约有二十名士兵，正好够一个排。"

    old "Where is your commanding officer?"
    new "Where is your commanding officer?\n你们的指挥官呢？"

    old "I was serving under Sergeant Coburn. He was killed in action."
    new "I was serving under Sergeant Coburn. He was killed in action.\n我原本在 Coburn 中士手下服役。他阵亡了。"

    old "I'm part of the fourth platoon. Our sergeant was also killed."
    new "I'm part of the fourth platoon. Our sergeant was also killed.\n我是第四排的。我们的中士也牺牲了。"

    old "Where's the captain?"
    new "Where's the captain?\n上尉呢？"

    old "The young soldier looks down."
    new "The young soldier looks down.\n那名年轻士兵低下了头。"

    old "Also dead."
    new "Also dead.\n也死了。"

    old "What the hell happened out there?"
    new "What the hell happened out there?\n那边到底发生了什么？"

    old "We encountered...something. Men started dying. I heard someone yell the order to retreat, and we made our way out with all due haste."
    new "We encountered...something. Men started dying. I heard someone yell the order to retreat, and we made our way out with all due haste.\n我们遇到了……某种东西。弟兄们开始一个接一个倒下。我听到有人大喊撤退的命令，就拼了命地往外逃。"

    old "Sergeant Thomas looks over the crowd."
    new "Sergeant Thomas looks over the crowd.\nThomas 中士扫视着这群人。"

    old "You twenty men are all that escaped?"
    new "You twenty men are all that escaped?\n逃出来的就只有你们二十个人？"

    old "To my knowledge, sir."
    new "To my knowledge, sir.\n据我所知，是的，长官。"

    old "Well, let's get the hell out of here. [protag], can you lead the way back?"
    new "Well, let's get the hell out of here. [protag], can you lead the way back?\n好了，我们赶紧离开这鬼地方。[protag]，你能带路回去吗？"

    old "I'd say the sooner we get moving, the better."
    new "I'd say the sooner we get moving, the better.\n依我看，我们越早动身越好。"

    old "I turn in the direction of the oak tree, and as I turn, I feel pinpricks on my skin."
    new "I turn in the direction of the oak tree, and as I turn, I feel pinpricks on my skin.\n我转向橡树的方向，就在转身时，我感觉到皮肤上一阵刺痛。"

    old "Do you feel that?"
    new "Do you feel that?\n你感觉到了吗？"

    old "So it's not just me?"
    new "So it's not just me?\n这么说，不只是我？"

    old "There's something malevolent coming."
    new "There's something malevolent coming.\n有某种邪恶的东西正朝我们逼近。"

    old "A figure appears in the mist. It advances on us quickly, but it doesn't have the appearance of running man—it seems to be floating toward us."
    new "A figure appears in the mist. It advances on us quickly, but it doesn't have the appearance of running man—it seems to be floating toward us.\n雾中出现一个人影。它迅速向我们逼近，却不像是人在奔跑，倒像是朝我们飘来。"

    old "Steel yourselves. If you still have your weapons, brandish them. Get ready to stand your ground."
    new "Steel yourselves. If you still have your weapons, brandish them. Get ready to stand your ground.\n稳住。手里还有武器的，都亮出来。准备好坚守阵地。"

    old "Do as he says!"
    new "Do as he says!\n照他说的做！"

    old "Do as she says!"
    new "Do as she says!\n照她说的做！"

    old "I hear the sound of blades being drawn, and look toward the figure in the mist. I furrow my brow in hardened resolve."
    new "I hear the sound of blades being drawn, and look toward the figure in the mist. I furrow my brow in hardened resolve.\n我听到刀剑出鞘的声音，望向雾中的人影。我紧皱眉头，神情坚毅。"

    old "Hello there, interlopers."
    new "Hello there, interlopers.\n你们好啊，不速之客们。"

    old "The figure emerges from the mist. His fangs are bared."
    new "The figure emerges from the mist. His fangs are bared.\n人影从雾中现身。他龇出獠牙。"

    old "A vampire. Not a common sight, but not unheard of for the lands around the castle of N'Mar."
    new "A vampire. Not a common sight, but not unheard of for the lands around the castle of N'Mar.\n是个吸血鬼。虽然不常见，但在 N'Mar 城堡周边的土地上，也并非闻所未闻。"

    old "The vampire turns his head from left to right, scanning the group of soldiers, before settling his eyes on me."
    new "The vampire turns his head from left to right, scanning the group of soldiers, before settling his eyes on me.\n吸血鬼左右转头，扫视着这群士兵，最后把目光落在了我身上。"

    old "He looks me in the eye and snarls, flashing his fangs."
    new "He looks me in the eye and snarls, flashing his fangs.\n他盯着我的眼睛，龇着獠牙低声咆哮。"

    old "His fangs appear bloodless. It's been awhile since this vampire has fed."
    new "His fangs appear bloodless. It's been awhile since this vampire has fed.\n他的獠牙上没有血迹。看来这个吸血鬼已经有段时间没进食了。"

    old "This vampire has the look of an inexperienced juvenile."
    new "This vampire has the look of an inexperienced juvenile.\n这个吸血鬼看起来像个缺乏经验的毛头小子。"

    old "I meet his gaze. His eyes lack the confidence that his violent gesture implies."
    new "I meet his gaze. His eyes lack the confidence that his violent gesture implies.\n我迎上他的目光。他的眼睛里并没有他那副凶相所流露出的底气。"

    old "Vampires are known for having bites that are worse than their bark, but could his growling just be a show of bravado?"
    new "Vampires are known for having bites that are worse than their bark, but could his growling just be a show of bravado?\n吸血鬼向来以“咬人比吠叫更狠”著称，但他的咆哮会不会只是虚张声势？"

    old "I return his snarl with a growl of my own. I flare my nostrils, and I see the vampire's eyes widen for a moment before he regains his composure."
    new "I return his snarl with a growl of my own. I flare my nostrils, and I see the vampire's eyes widen for a moment before he regains his composure.\n我也低吼一声，回敬他的咆哮。我鼻孔一张，看见那吸血鬼眼睛瞬间瞪大，随即又恢复了镇定。"

    old "Unlike you, I promise I won't bite. Well, maybe. I might be lying."
    new "Unlike you, I promise I won't bite. Well, maybe. I might be lying.\n跟你可不一样，我保证不咬人。嗯，也许吧。我可能是在说谎。"

    old "I gesture to the group of men behind me."
    new "I gesture to the group of men behind me.\n我朝身后那群士兵比了个手势。"

    old "Perhaps I need to point out the obvious. I have thirty men at my side, and there is only one of you. If you want a fight, we'll give you a fight. But for your sake, I think you'd best be on your way."
    new "Perhaps I need to point out the obvious. I have thirty men at my side, and there is only one of you. If you want a fight, we'll give you a fight. But for your sake, I think you'd best be on your way.\n也许我该点明一件明摆着的事。我身边有三十个人，而你只有一个。想打架，我们奉陪。但为你自己着想，我劝你最好赶紧走人。"

    old "Thirty? I think I can manage that."
    new "Thirty? I think I can manage that.\n三十个？我想我还应付得来。"

    old "The vampire kneels down and places a palm on the ground. A glow radiates from his hand, and the ground around him begins to shake."
    new "The vampire kneels down and places a palm on the ground. A glow radiates from his hand, and the ground around him begins to shake.\n吸血鬼单膝跪下，把一只手掌按在地上。他的手上泛出光芒，周围的地面开始震动。"

    old "The ground around him breaks, and I see a ghastly hand poke its way through the soil. Then another hand beside it. And another. And another."
    new "The ground around him breaks, and I see a ghastly hand poke its way through the soil. Then another hand beside it. And another. And another.\n他周围的地面裂开，我看见一只苍白可怖的手破土而出。接着旁边又伸出一只手。又一只。又一只。"

    old "The men behind me gasp, as ghouls emerge from the ground."
    new "The men behind me gasp, as ghouls emerge from the ground.\n我身后的士兵倒吸一口凉气，食尸鬼从地里爬了出来。"

    old "Now, if I recall correctly, you were just offering me a fight. I'd like to take you up on that."
    new "Now, if I recall correctly, you were just offering me a fight. I'd like to take you up on that.\n那么，如果我没记错，你刚才可是要跟我打一场。我乐意奉陪。"

    old "I killed all of your friends back at the castle. Scores of them, slain in seconds. Now I'm going to kill you. With my army of ghouls, thirty men is nothing to me."
    new "I killed all of your friends back at the castle. Scores of them, slain in seconds. Now I'm going to kill you. With my army of ghouls, thirty men is nothing to me.\n你们在城堡里的那些朋友，全都被我杀了。几十个人，几秒钟就没了。现在轮到你们。有我这支食尸鬼大军，三十个人对我来说算不了什么。"

    old "I doubt that very much. You don't have the look of a vampire who's just killed scores of men."
    new "I doubt that very much. You don't have the look of a vampire who's just killed scores of men.\n我对此深表怀疑。你可没有刚杀了几十个人的吸血鬼该有的样子。"

    old "If you were really so busy killing, how is it that your garb is so clean? I'd expect someone like you to walk away stained with the blood of his enemies. But you've got nothing to show for your killing. In fact, I question whether you've ever killed a man in your life."
    new "If you were really so busy killing, how is it that your garb is so clean? I'd expect someone like you to walk away stained with the blood of his enemies. But you've got nothing to show for your killing. In fact, I question whether you've ever killed a man in your life.\n你要是真杀了那么多人，衣裳怎么还这么干净？我本以为像你这样的人会满身是敌人的血。可你身上毫无杀戮的痕迹。事实上，我倒怀疑你这辈子有没有杀过人。"

    old "Your flesh still has the scent of a freshly-turned corpse. You're no elder vampire, that's for certain. You're a greenhorn. You're barely even a vampire. You, kill dozens of men? I doubt it."
    new "Your flesh still has the scent of a freshly-turned corpse. You're no elder vampire, that's for certain. You're a greenhorn. You're barely even a vampire. You, kill dozens of men? I doubt it.\n你身上还带着刚转化尸体的气味。你肯定不是什么老资历的吸血鬼。你就是个新手，甚至还算不上真正的吸血鬼。就你，杀几十个人？我不信。"

    old "If that's true, then why do I see fear in your eyes? A predator that fears his prey, now that's a riot. Could it be that you're not a predator at all?"
    new "If that's true, then why do I see fear in your eyes? A predator that fears his prey, now that's a riot. Could it be that you're not a predator at all?\n如果真是这样，那我怎么会在你眼里看到恐惧？一个害怕自己猎物的猎手，这可真是笑话。该不会你根本就不是猎手吧？"

    old "If killing thirty men is really nothing to you, why haven't you done it yet?"
    new "If killing thirty men is really nothing to you, why haven't you done it yet?\n如果杀三十个人对你来说真不算什么，那你为什么还不动手？"

    old "Come on, vampire. If you're really such a deadly savage, then let's see some death."
    new "Come on, vampire. If you're really such a deadly savage, then let's see some death.\n来啊，吸血鬼。你要是真那么凶残，就让我们见识见识。"

    old "I take a step toward the vampire, and he takes a step back."
    new "I take a step toward the vampire, and he takes a step back.\n我朝吸血鬼迈出一步，他却往后退了一步。"

    old "Come on, vampire. I'm beginning to think that you're all bark and no bite."
    new "Come on, vampire. I'm beginning to think that you're all bark and no bite.\n来啊，吸血鬼。我开始觉得你只会叫不会咬。"

    old "Listen, vampire. It's clear that you have no desire to fight me. And truth be told, taking the time to dispatch you and your ghoul allies would be a complete waste of my time. I value my time, and you value your life. Now why don't you get lost, and save us both the trouble?"
    new "Listen, vampire. It's clear that you have no desire to fight me. And truth be told, taking the time to dispatch you and your ghoul allies would be a complete waste of my time. I value my time, and you value your life. Now why don't you get lost, and save us both the trouble?\n听着，吸血鬼。你显然没有跟我交手的欲望。说实话，花时间收拾你和你的食尸鬼同伙，纯属浪费我的时间。我珍惜我的时间，你珍惜你的小命。何不赶紧滚开，省得我们俩都麻烦？"

    old "I'll let you live tonight. But you'll soon rue the day that you set foot on these plains."
    new "I'll let you live tonight. But you'll soon rue the day that you set foot on these plains.\n今晚我饶你一命。但你很快就会后悔踏上这片平原的那一天。"

    old "The vampire turns and gallops into the night, quickly vanishing into the mists."
    new "The vampire turns and gallops into the night, quickly vanishing into the mists.\n吸血鬼转身疾驰而去，迅速消失在雾中。"

    old "The ghouls that stood at his command collapse to the ground, now completely inanimate."
    new "The ghouls that stood at his command collapse to the ground, now completely inanimate.\n听命于他的那些食尸鬼瘫倒在地，如今彻底没了生气。"

    old "I step forward and poke at one of the ghouls. Its body crumbles at my touch."
    new "I step forward and poke at one of the ghouls. Its body crumbles at my touch.\n我走上前，戳了戳其中一只食尸鬼。它的身体在我的触碰下碎裂开来。"

    old "What are they?"
    new "What are they?\n它们是什么？"

    old "Lifeless husks. Mere puppets that can do nothing without their master magically controlling them."
    new "Lifeless husks. Mere puppets that can do nothing without their master magically controlling them.\n没有生命的躯壳。不过是些傀儡，没有主人用魔法操控，它们就什么都做不了。"

    old "This vampire wields powerful magic, but his behavior struck me as foolhardy. Summoning this many ghouls is an impressive trick, but there's no way that he could hope to individually control this many ghouls at once."
    new "This vampire wields powerful magic, but his behavior struck me as foolhardy. Summoning this many ghouls is an impressive trick, but there's no way that he could hope to individually control this many ghouls at once.\n这个吸血鬼掌握着强大的魔法，但他的行为在我眼里实在鲁莽。召唤这么多食尸鬼固然是很了得的把戏，可他根本不可能同时逐一操控这么多。"

    old "You called his bluff."
    new "You called his bluff.\n你戳穿了他的虚张声势。"

    old "And thankfully he didn't decide to stay and press his luck. I don't know what we might have done if more vampires had arrived while we were fighting."
    new "And thankfully he didn't decide to stay and press his luck. I don't know what we might have done if more vampires had arrived while we were fighting.\n幸好他没有留下来碰运气。要是在我们交战时又有更多吸血鬼赶到，我可真不知道该怎么办了。"

    old "We shouldn't waste any more time. Let's get out of these mists."
    new "We shouldn't waste any more time. Let's get out of these mists.\n我们不能再浪费时间了。赶紧离开这片雾吧。"

    old "You think you have what it takes to fight me? Prove it. Come at me."
    new "You think you have what it takes to fight me? Prove it. Come at me.\n你以为你有本事跟我打？那就来试试。放马过来。"

    old "I turn my palms upward and present them to the vampire."
    new "I turn my palms upward and present them to the vampire.\n我把手掌朝上摊开，亮给那吸血鬼看。"

    old "Look, I'm empty-handed. Shouldn't I be an easy kill? If you think so, come and take it."
    new "Look, I'm empty-handed. Shouldn't I be an easy kill? If you think so, come and take it.\n看，我两手空空。我不该是很好杀的猎物吗？如果你这么想，就来试试吧。"

    old "The vampire shrieks and lunges toward me. And in an instant, the ghouls around him collapse to the ground."
    new "The vampire shrieks and lunges toward me. And in an instant, the ghouls around him collapse to the ground.\n吸血鬼尖啸一声，朝我猛扑过来。就在这一瞬间，他周围的食尸鬼纷纷瘫倒在地。"

    old "I step backward, ducking behind the men standing behind me in rank formation."
    new "I step backward, ducking behind the men standing behind me in rank formation.\n我往后退去，躲到身后排成横列的士兵们中间。"

    old "The vampire looks behind him, at the inanimate cadavers that were once his army, and I see a look of terror appear on his face."
    new "The vampire looks behind him, at the inanimate cadavers that were once his army, and I see a look of terror appear on his face.\n吸血鬼回头看了看那些曾是他人马、如今却毫无生气的尸骸，脸上露出了惊恐的神情。"

    old "Get him!"
    new "Get him!\n抓住他！"

    old "The men begin charging forward, but the vampire turns his back on us and gallops into the night, faster than any man could hope to pursue."
    new "The men begin charging forward, but the vampire turns his back on us and gallops into the night, faster than any man could hope to pursue.\n士兵们开始向前冲锋，可那吸血鬼转过身，疾驰进夜色中，速度快得谁也别想追上。"

    old "I look down at the ground, where thirty ghouls now sit, completely inanimate."
    new "I look down at the ground, where thirty ghouls now sit, completely inanimate.\n我低头看着地面，三十只食尸鬼瘫在那里，彻底没了生气。"

    old "I kick one of the ghouls, and its body disintegrates as I touch it."
    new "I kick one of the ghouls, and its body disintegrates as I touch it.\n我踢了其中一只食尸鬼一脚，它的身体在我碰到时便化成了碎屑。"

    old "Lifeless husks. They were only given motion by the power of his magic."
    new "Lifeless husks. They were only given motion by the power of his magic.\n没有生命的躯壳。它们只是靠他的魔法力量才动得起来。"

    old "I provoked him, and in a moment of anger, he lost control of his minions. They're mere puppets, and without their master controlling the strings, they're powerless."
    new "I provoked him, and in a moment of anger, he lost control of his minions. They're mere puppets, and without their master controlling the strings, they're powerless.\n我激怒了他，他一时怒火攻心，就失去了对爪牙的控制。它们不过是些傀儡，没有主人牵线操控，便毫无威力。"

    old "You had me worried for a moment there."
    new "You had me worried for a moment there.\n你刚才可让我捏了把汗。"

    old "I was quaking in my boots too. I took a gamble, and thankfully it paid off."
    new "I was quaking in my boots too. I took a gamble, and thankfully it paid off.\n我自己也吓得腿软。我赌了一把，幸好赌赢了。"

    old "Let's get out of here. We don't know what else might be lurking about."
    new "Let's get out of here. We don't know what else might be lurking about.\n我们离开这里吧。谁知道附近还藏着什么别的东西。"

    old "Your friends have thinned our ranks, I will admit that. But you've merely culled the weakest among us. You see not just thirty men, but thirty of our best men, those men who saw combat with your kin and lived to tell the tale."
    new "Your friends have thinned our ranks, I will admit that. But you've merely culled the weakest among us. You see not just thirty men, but thirty of our best men, those men who saw combat with your kin and lived to tell the tale.\n你的同族确实削减了我们的人数，这点我承认。但你只是淘汰了我们中最弱的那批。你眼前这三十人，个个都是精锐，他们都和你的同类交过手，并且活着讲述了那段经历。"

    old "Some men have died out here tonight. They were ambushed, by vampires, many of them. Here you are, a solitary vampire, entirely lacking in the element of surprise. What chance do you suppose you have against us?"
    new "Some men have died out here tonight. They were ambushed, by vampires, many of them. Here you are, a solitary vampire, entirely lacking in the element of surprise. What chance do you suppose you have against us?\n今晚这里确实死了些人。他们是被吸血鬼伏击的，而且对方人多势众。可你呢，孤零零一个吸血鬼，毫无突袭之利。你觉得对上我们能有多少胜算？"

    old "I've no love for destructive revelry. Do yourself a favor. Go back and regroup with your allies. Don't throw your life away."
    new "I've no love for destructive revelry. Do yourself a favor. Go back and regroup with your allies. Don't throw your life away.\n我可不喜欢没必要的流血。就当帮你自己一个忙，回去和你的同伙会合吧。别白白送命。"

    old "The vampire laughs."
    new "The vampire laughs.\n吸血鬼笑了。"

    old "Unlike you, I have no life to throw away. You may have evened the numbers, but do you think that your men can really hold a candle to my ghouls? Your friends will bleed when cut. Mine don't."
    new "Unlike you, I have no life to throw away. You may have evened the numbers, but do you think that your men can really hold a candle to my ghouls? Your friends will bleed when cut. Mine don't.\n我可不像你，我没什么命可以丢。你或许拉平了人数，但你真觉得你手下能比得过我的食尸鬼吗？你的同伴挨上一刀就会流血，我的可不会。"

    old "That's an impressive army you have there. But I wonder. Can you really command them effectively?"
    new "That's an impressive army you have there. But I wonder. Can you really command them effectively?\n你带的这支军队倒是挺唬人。不过我很好奇，你真能有效地指挥它们吗？"

    old "You have thirty minions, and many of them appear quite fearsome. Maybe even bloodthirsty. And yet they mainly stand in place, doing nothing. I wonder why that might be?"
    new "You have thirty minions, and many of them appear quite fearsome. Maybe even bloodthirsty. And yet they mainly stand in place, doing nothing. I wonder why that might be?\n你有三十个爪牙，其中不少看起来相当可怕，甚至嗜血成性。可它们大多只是站在原地，一动不动。我纳闷这是为什么呢？"

    old "I wonder, what might happen if we sat back and waited for your minions to come at us?"
    new "I wonder, what might happen if we sat back and waited for your minions to come at us?\n我很好奇，要是我们就这么按兵不动，等着你的爪牙冲过来，会怎么样？"

    old "The vampire scowls at me."
    new "The vampire scowls at me.\n吸血鬼恶狠狠地瞪着我。"

    old "You want to leave this field? Save your lives now and hope to regroup later? Fine. But the passage of time may not be so kind to you and your ilk."
    new "You want to leave this field? Save your lives now and hope to regroup later? Fine. But the passage of time may not be so kind to you and your ilk.\n你想离开这片野地？现在就逃命，指望日后再集结？行。但时间流逝，对你和你的同类可未必仁慈。"

    old "The vampire turns his back on me and gallops into the night, headed for the direction of the castle."
    new "The vampire turns his back on me and gallops into the night, headed for the direction of the castle.\n吸血鬼转过身，疾驰进夜色中，朝城堡的方向去了。"

    old "I'm beginning to get the feeling you really don't understand what you're dealing with here."
    new "I'm beginning to get the feeling you really don't understand what you're dealing with here.\n我越来越觉得，你根本不明白自己面对的是什么。"

    old "These men behind me came out as part of a company known within their battalion as the tip of the spear."
    new "These men behind me came out as part of a company known within their battalion as the tip of the spear.\n我身后这些人所属的连队，在他们营里被称作“矛尖”。"

    old "The vampire cocks his head and gives me an inquisitive squint."
    new "The vampire cocks his head and gives me an inquisitive squint.\n吸血鬼歪了歪头，狐疑地眯起眼睛打量我。"

    old "Gods, do I need to spell it out for you? These men here are just part of a single company. There's an entire brigade at the edge of the mists, hundreds of men, who will be storming across these plains when the appointed time comes."
    new "Gods, do I need to spell it out for you? These men here are just part of a single company. There's an entire brigade at the edge of the mists, hundreds of men, who will be storming across these plains when the appointed time comes.\n天哪，我非得把话挑明吗？这里的人只不过是一个连队的一部分。雾区边缘还驻扎着一整个旅，几百号人，等预定时间一到，他们就会横扫这片平原。"

    old "Now, I'm not so good at telling time by the moonlight. Those men could be moments away or minutes away. Either way, I've still got thirty men behind me until then. We may not have what it takes to crush you now, but we can hold our ground long enough."
    new "Now, I'm not so good at telling time by the moonlight. Those men could be moments away or minutes away. Either way, I've still got thirty men behind me until then. We may not have what it takes to crush you now, but we can hold our ground long enough.\n不过，我不太会借着月光判断时间。那些人也许片刻即到，也许要几分钟。无论如何，在那之前我身后都还有三十个人。我们眼下或许没法碾碎你，但足够撑到他们赶到。"

    old "Tell me, vampire. Do you want to be stuck out here fighting us when that moment arrives?"
    new "Tell me, vampire. Do you want to be stuck out here fighting us when that moment arrives?\n告诉我，吸血鬼。那一刻到来时，你想被困在这里跟我们死战吗？"

    old "The vampire turns his back on me and scowls."
    new "The vampire turns his back on me and scowls.\n吸血鬼背过身去，面色阴沉。"

    old "You haven't seen the last of me, I assure you that."
    new "You haven't seen the last of me, I assure you that.\n你还没见识到我的厉害，我向你保证。"

    old "The vampire turns his back and dashes into the night, faster than any man could hope to pursue."
    new "The vampire turns his back and dashes into the night, faster than any man could hope to pursue.\n吸血鬼转过身，疾驰进夜色中，速度快得谁也别想追上。"

    old "The ghouls that stood at his command collapse to the ground."
    new "The ghouls that stood at his command collapse to the ground.\n听命于他的那些食尸鬼瘫倒在地。"

    old "I step forward and kick at one of the ghouls. Its body disintegrates as I touch it."
    new "I step forward and kick at one of the ghouls. Its body disintegrates as I touch it.\n我走上前，朝其中一只食尸鬼踢去。它的身体在我碰到时便化成了碎屑。"

    old "There ghouls were mere puppets. Now that there's no puppetmaster here to magically control them, they pose no threat to us."
    new "There ghouls were mere puppets. Now that there's no puppetmaster here to magically control them, they pose no threat to us.\n那些食尸鬼不过是傀儡。既然没有傀儡师在此用魔法操控它们，它们对我们便构不成威胁。"

    old "That was one hell of a bluff."
    new "That was one hell of a bluff.\n那可真是一场大胆的豪赌。"

    old "Well, it paid off. Let's not squander the opportunity to get out of here."
    new "Well, it paid off. Let's not squander the opportunity to get out of here.\n好在赌赢了。我们可别浪费这个离开的机会。"

    old "I lead Sergeant Thomas and his men through the mists, back to where my encampment sits at the edge of the field."
    new "I lead Sergeant Thomas and his men through the mists, back to where my encampment sits at the edge of the field.\n我领着 Thomas 中士和他的部下穿过雾霭，回到我扎在野地边缘的营地。"

    old "There's someone standing at the top of the knoll where my tent rests."
    new "There's someone standing at the top of the knoll where my tent rests.\n有人站在我帐篷所在的小丘顶上。"

    old "A woman steps out."
    new "A woman steps out.\n一个女人走了出来。"

    old "My name is Karen. I'm an Amazon from the west."
    new "My name is Karen. I'm an Amazon from the west.\n我叫 Karen。我是来自西方的 Amazon。"

    old "What brings you here?"
    new "What brings you here?\n是什么风把你吹到这里来的？"

    old "I saw a group of human men fleeing near the gates of the Castle of N'Mar. It looked like they encountered something dire out there. I came to look for survivors."
    new "I saw a group of human men fleeing near the gates of the Castle of N'Mar. It looked like they encountered something dire out there. I came to look for survivors.\n我看到一群人类男子在 N'Mar 城堡大门附近奔逃。他们似乎在那里遇到了可怕的东西。我是来找幸存者的。"

    old "Karen looks behind me, appraising the group of soldiers."
    new "Karen looks behind me, appraising the group of soldiers.\nKaren 看了看我身后，打量着那群士兵。"

    old "I take it that these are all that remain of the group I saw."
    new "I take it that these are all that remain of the group I saw.\n我想，这些就是我看见的那批人里剩下的全部了吧。"

    old "How is it that you managed to see everything that happened in N'Mar?"
    new "How is it that you managed to see everything that happened in N'Mar?\n你是怎么看到 N'Mar 里发生的一切的？"

    old "Well, I didn't see everything. The fog was thick—too thick for me to fly in and land. So I came out here."
    new "Well, I didn't see everything. The fog was thick—too thick for me to fly in and land. So I came out here.\n哦，我并没有看到全部。雾太浓了，浓得我无法飞进去降落。所以我就到了这里。"

    old "Fly? Land?"
    new "Fly? Land?\n飞？降落？"

    old "I came here by griffon."
    new "I came here by griffon.\n我是骑狮鹫来的。"

    old "But griffons are forbidden to fly in the lands over the human empire!"
    new "But griffons are forbidden to fly in the lands over the human empire!\n但狮鹫被禁止飞越人类帝国的领空！"

    old "Relax, soldier. Our treaty with the human empire allows the council of Grimoire to approve the use of griffons for non-military ventures. I was on my way to Grimoire on a diplomatic mission when I saw your men under attack."
    new "Relax, soldier. Our treaty with the human empire allows the council of Grimoire to approve the use of griffons for non-military ventures. I was on my way to Grimoire on a diplomatic mission when I saw your men under attack.\n别紧张，士兵。我们与人类帝国的条约允许 Grimoire 议会批准将狮鹫用于非军事行动。我正要去 Grimoire 执行外交使命，途中看到你的人遭到袭击。"

    old "You'll have to answer to the council for this."
    new "You'll have to answer to the council for this.\n这件事你得向议会做出解释。"

    old "I intend to do exactly that. I was headed in precisely their direction. And the events I observed will no doubt be of interest to them as well."
    new "I intend to do exactly that. I was headed in precisely their direction. And the events I observed will no doubt be of interest to them as well.\n我正有此意。我本来就是要朝他们那儿去的。而且我所目睹的事件，他们肯定也会感兴趣。"

    old "You and your men will be headed back to Grimoire as well, I trust?"
    new "You and your men will be headed back to Grimoire as well, I trust?\n我想，你和你的人也要回 Grimoire 吧？"

    old "Yes. Our mission is over. We've nothing left to do but report back to the council."
    new "Yes. Our mission is over. We've nothing left to do but report back to the council.\n是的。我们的任务结束了。除了向议会报告，我们也没什么可做的了。"

    old "Dwarf, you should head back to Grimoire with these men. I believe the council will want to hear your report of the events as well."
    new "Dwarf, you should head back to Grimoire with these men. I believe the council will want to hear your report of the events as well.\nDwarf，你应该和这些人一起回 Grimoire。我想议会也想听听你对这些事件的报告。"

    old "You, with the pointy ears. You should head back to Grimoire with these men. I believe they'll wish to hear your report of the events that transpired here tonight."
    new "You, with the pointy ears. You should head back to Grimoire with these men. I believe they'll wish to hear your report of the events that transpired here tonight.\n你，尖耳朵的那个。你应该和这些人一起回 Grimoire。我想他们会想听听你对今晚这些事件的报告。"

    old "You, elf. You should head back to Grimoire with these men. The council will no doubt be interested in hearing your account of what happened here tonight."
    new "You, elf. You should head back to Grimoire with these men. The council will no doubt be interested in hearing your account of what happened here tonight.\n你，Elf。你应该和这些人一起回 Grimoire。议会肯定会有兴趣听听你对今晚这里所发生之事的讲述。"

    old "Karen turns to me."
    new "Karen turns to me.\nKaren 转向我。"

    old "You're not with these men, are you?"
    new "You're not with these men, are you?\n你不是和这些人一伙的吧？"

    old "I'm not a soldier, no."
    new "I'm not a soldier, no.\n我不是士兵，不是。"

    old "Well, you should head back to Grimoire with them all the same. You've seen what happened here tonight, and the council will no doubt be interested to hear your account of what transpired here tonight."
    new "Well, you should head back to Grimoire with them all the same. You've seen what happened here tonight, and the council will no doubt be interested to hear your account of what transpired here tonight.\n那么，你仍然应该和他们一起回 Grimoire。你亲眼看到了今晚发生的一切，议会肯定会有兴趣听听你的讲述。"

    old "I'll fly ahead to report to the council. You should make your own way there with all due haste."
    new "I'll fly ahead to report to the council. You should make your own way there with all due haste.\n我先飞回去向议会报告。你们应当尽快自行赶过去。"

    old "Hold up. What authority do you have to report directly to the council?"
    new "Hold up. What authority do you have to report directly to the council?\n等等。你有什么权力直接向议会报告？"

    old "I already told you. I'm Karen. The queen of the Amazons."
    new "I already told you. I'm Karen. The queen of the Amazons.\n我已经说过了。我是 Karen。Amazon 女王。"

    old "Karen turns her back on us, and walks back. I follow her with my eyes, and now spy her griffon, sitting on the other side of the knoll behind my tent."
    new "Karen turns her back on us, and walks back. I follow her with my eyes, and now spy her griffon, sitting on the other side of the knoll behind my tent.\nKaren 背过身去，走了回去。我的目光追随着她，这才发现她的狮鹫，就蹲在我帐篷后的小丘另一侧。"

    old "Once I get to Grimoire, I'll let them know to anticipate your arrival."
    new "Once I get to Grimoire, I'll let them know to anticipate your arrival.\n等我到了 Grimoire，我会让他们知道你们即将到达。"

    old "Karen hops onto her griffon, and the beast leaps into the air, quickly vanishing into the night."
    new "Karen hops onto her griffon, and the beast leaps into the air, quickly vanishing into the night.\nKaren 跃上她的狮鹫，那头巨兽腾空而起，很快消失在了夜色中。"

    old "She's right, you know. You should come back to Grimoire with us."
    new "She's right, you know. You should come back to Grimoire with us.\n她说得对，你知道的。你应该和我们一起回 Grimoire。"

    old "You've done me and my men a great service. I'll do everything I can to see that you're recognized for your charity."
    new "You've done me and my men a great service. I'll do everything I can to see that you're recognized for your charity.\n你帮了我和我部下一个大忙。我会尽我所能，让你的善举得到认可。"

    old "After we arrive in Grimoire, Sergeant Thomas leads me to the council chambers. I'm left to wait outside, and several minutes later, a man emerges from the chamber."
    new "After we arrive in Grimoire, Sergeant Thomas leads me to the council chambers. I'm left to wait outside, and several minutes later, a man emerges from the chamber.\n到达 Grimoire 后，Thomas 中士领我来到议会大厅。我被留在外面等候，几分钟后，一个男人从大厅里走了出来。"

    old "You're [protag], is that right?"
    new "You're [protag], is that right?\n你就是 [protag]，对吗？"

    old "Yes indeed, I certainly am."
    new "Yes indeed, I certainly am.\n正是，我就是。"

    old "Sergeant Thomas has told us what you did. We'd like to inquire on a few points."
    new "Sergeant Thomas has told us what you did. We'd like to inquire on a few points.\nThomas 中士已经告诉我们你所做的事。我们想就几个问题询问一下。"

    old "I follow the man into the council chamber."
    new "I follow the man into the council chamber.\n我跟着那人走进议会大厅。"

    old "The chamber is a circular room. There are seats all around its perimeter, filled with people who I can only presume are elder council members. The room is too dimly-lit for me to make out any faces."
    new "The chamber is a circular room. There are seats all around its perimeter, filled with people who I can only presume are elder council members. The room is too dimly-lit for me to make out any faces.\n大厅是一间圆形房间，四周一圈都是座位，坐满了我只能猜测是议会元老的人。房间里光线太暗，我分辨不出任何人的面孔。"

    old "The council has a few questions for you, not the least of which is this: how is it that you happened to be camping in the fields around N'Mar last night?"
    new "The council has a few questions for you, not the least of which is this: how is it that you happened to be camping in the fields around N'Mar last night?\n议会有几个问题要问你，其中最关键的是：你昨晚怎么碰巧在 N'Mar 周边的野地里露营？"

    old "I am a merchant by trade. It's in my nature to spend time in locations that others find to be unpleasant. The more unpleasant a place is, the less likely I'm to find other merchants, which means less competition."
    new "I am a merchant by trade. It's in my nature to spend time in locations that others find to be unpleasant. The more unpleasant a place is, the less likely I'm to find other merchants, which means less competition.\n我以经商为业。待在别人觉得不舒服的地方，是我的天性。一个地方越让人难受，我就越不可能遇到其他商人，也就是说竞争越少。"

    old "And paths which few merchants trade tend to be the safest. Less chance of being ambushed by ruffians and brigands in a low-traffic area."
    new "And paths which few merchants trade tend to be the safest. Less chance of being ambushed by ruffians and brigands in a low-traffic area.\n而很少有商人往来的道路往往也最安全。在人迹罕至的地方，被地痞和强盗伏击的几率更低。"

    old "That is an interesting business philosophy, but it doesn't explain your presence on the fields around N'Mar."
    new "That is an interesting business philosophy, but it doesn't explain your presence on the fields around N'Mar.\n这是个有趣的经商哲学，但它解释不了你为什么会出现在 N'Mar 周边的野地里。"

    old "There are certain dwarven houses in the land of Hammerhands that have a vested interest in monitoring activity around N'Mar. There are a scant few outposts that exist around the periphery of those fields, and they're lightly staffed."
    new "There are certain dwarven houses in the land of Hammerhands that have a vested interest in monitoring activity around N'Mar. There are a scant few outposts that exist around the periphery of those fields, and they're lightly staffed.\nHammerhands 之地有一些 Dwarf 家族，对监视 N'Mar 周边的动静有切身利益。那些野地外围零星分布着几座前哨站，人手都很少。"

    old "Those outposts are stocked with the bare minimum of amenities. Those men have bread and water to keep them alive, and they're compensated generously for their time, but they have little in the way of more savory vittles."
    new "Those outposts are stocked with the bare minimum of amenities. Those men have bread and water to keep them alive, and they're compensated generously for their time, but they have little in the way of more savory vittles.\n那些前哨站只有最基本的生活物资。那些人靠面包和水维持生计，虽然报酬丰厚，却没什么像样的可口食物。"

    old "Those men crave for finer things, and I'm willing to accept their generous payment in exchange."
    new "Those men crave for finer things, and I'm willing to accept their generous payment in exchange.\n那些人渴望更讲究的吃食，而我也乐意收下他们慷慨的酬劳。"

    old "I am a scholar. I have dedicated myself to many causes during my lifetime, but my calling is the pursuit of knowledge. As a scholar, I have discovered much literature describing the numerous cultures and lands across Aravorn."
    new "I am a scholar. I have dedicated myself to many causes during my lifetime, but my calling is the pursuit of knowledge. As a scholar, I have discovered much literature describing the numerous cultures and lands across Aravorn.\n我是一名学者。我一生致力于许多事业，但我的使命是追求知识。身为学者，我发现了大量描述 Aravorn 各地文化与土地的文献。"

    old "But one area which remains an unknown in my research is the area around N'Mar. I've taken it upon myself to conduct my own research."
    new "But one area which remains an unknown in my research is the area around N'Mar. I've taken it upon myself to conduct my own research.\n但在我研究中仍属空白的一个区域，就是 N'Mar 周边地区。于是我决定亲自去开展研究。"

    old "I don't mean to pretend that I'm entirely selfless in my pursuits. As a scholar, I crave not wealth, but recognition."
    new "I don't mean to pretend that I'm entirely selfless in my pursuits. As a scholar, I crave not wealth, but recognition.\n我不想假装自己的追求完全无私。身为学者，我渴望的不是财富，而是认可。"

    old "Being on the leading edge of field research around N'Mar has granted me numerous opportunities to advance my career. My early field reports are now considered seminal works. I owe that largely to my appetite for unpleasant work."
    new "Being on the leading edge of field research around N'Mar has granted me numerous opportunities to advance my career. My early field reports are now considered seminal works. I owe that largely to my appetite for unpleasant work.\n走在 N'Mar 周边实地研究的前沿，给了我许多推动事业发展的机会。我早期的田野报告如今被视为开创性著作。这在很大程度上要归功于我对苦差事的胃口。"

    old "I make coin as a bard, but truthfully my actual occupation can be described as somewhat similar to a tour guide."
    new "I make coin as a bard, but truthfully my actual occupation can be described as somewhat similar to a tour guide.\n我靠当吟游诗人挣钱，但老实说，我的实际职业倒更像是个向导。"

    old "Knights and would-be heroes who crave recognition will frequently commission me to accompany them on their journeys so that I can spin and recite tales of their conquest."
    new "Knights and would-be heroes who crave recognition will frequently commission me to accompany them on their journeys so that I can spin and recite tales of their conquest.\n渴望扬名的骑士和准英雄们，常常会雇佣我随他们同行，好让我编撰并传唱他们建功立业的故事。"

    old "This has turned me into something of a serial adventurer, and consequently, one of the greatest services I provide is not my talent for music and verse, but my experience and the acumen that comes with it."
    new "This has turned me into something of a serial adventurer, and consequently, one of the greatest services I provide is not my talent for music and verse, but my experience and the acumen that comes with it.\n这让我简直成了个连环冒险家，因此，我能提供的最有价值的服务，并不是我作乐赋诗的本事，而是我的阅历以及随之而来的见识。"

    old "The demands of my unique profession drive me to familiarize myself with the more exciting elements of Aravorn's landscape, particularly those which are close to human settlements."
    new "The demands of my unique profession drive me to familiarize myself with the more exciting elements of Aravorn's landscape, particularly those which are close to human settlements.\n我这独特职业的要求，促使我去熟悉 Aravorn 地貌中那些更惊险的去处，尤其是靠近人类聚居地的地方。"

    old "The Castle of N'Mar, and the lands that surround it, fit that criteria exactly."
    new "The Castle of N'Mar, and the lands that surround it, fit that criteria exactly.\nN'Mar 城堡及其周边的土地，恰好符合这个标准。"

    old "I'm a debt collector. A certain dwarf thought he could escape his financial obligations by fleeing into the fields of N'Mar. I presume he was under the impression that no one would pursue him there. It's not the first time I've pursued a debtor into those lands."
    new "I'm a debt collector. A certain dwarf thought he could escape his financial obligations by fleeing into the fields of N'Mar. I presume he was under the impression that no one would pursue him there. It's not the first time I've pursued a debtor into those lands.\n我是收债人。某个 Dwarf 以为逃进 N'Mar 的野地就能躲掉债务。我想他大概是觉得没人会追到那里去。这也不是我第一次追债追到那些地方了。"

    old "And what of the dwarf? Did you find him?"
    new "And what of the dwarf? Did you find him?\n那那个 Dwarf 呢？你找到他了吗？"

    old "No, and I don't believe I will. There's a good chance that his foolhardiness drove him into the waiting jaws of some zombie or other foul beast. It wouldn't be the first time I've seen a debtor run into death's waiting maw to escape his fiscal commitment."
    new "No, and I don't believe I will. There's a good chance that his foolhardiness drove him into the waiting jaws of some zombie or other foul beast. It wouldn't be the first time I've seen a debtor run into death's waiting maw to escape his fiscal commitment.\n没有，而且我想我也找不到了。他的鲁莽很可能把他送进了僵尸或其他恶兽张开的血盆大口。我也不是第一次看见债务人为了躲债，一头撞进死神的怀抱。"

    old "What exactly made you choose debt collection as a profession?"
    new "What exactly made you choose debt collection as a profession?\n究竟是什么让你选择收债这个职业的？"

    old "I shrug."
    new "I shrug.\n我耸了耸肩。"

    old "It fits my skills and it makes me money. I have a certain talent for finding and apprehending people. Banks and lenders value that kind of talent, and banks and lenders tend to be the type who have money to pay generously for the things they value."
    new "It fits my skills and it makes me money. I have a certain talent for finding and apprehending people. Banks and lenders value that kind of talent, and banks and lenders tend to be the type who have money to pay generously for the things they value.\n这行适合我的本事，又能让我赚钱。我在找人、抓人方面颇有一套。银行和放贷人很看重这种本事，而他们往往正是那种有钱、肯为自己看重的东西慷慨付钱的主儿。"

    old "So, you're familiar with the terrain and territory around N'Mar."
    new "So, you're familiar with the terrain and territory around N'Mar.\n这么说，你很熟悉 N'Mar 周边的地形和地域。"

    old "That I am."
    new "That I am.\n确实如此。"

    old "Our understanding is that you were also successful in repelling an assault by a vampire."
    new "Our understanding is that you were also successful in repelling an assault by a vampire.\n据我们所知，你还成功击退了一个吸血鬼的袭击。"

    old "In a manner of speaking, yes. But I didn't do it by force."
    new "In a manner of speaking, yes. But I didn't do it by force.\n可以这么说吧。不过我不是靠武力做到的。"

    old "The vampire we encountered looked young and inexperienced. He had a certain timidity about him that manifested itself as false bravado."
    new "The vampire we encountered looked young and inexperienced. He had a certain timidity about him that manifested itself as false bravado.\n我们遇到的吸血鬼看上去年轻又缺乏经验。他骨子里有某种怯懦，却表现成虚张声势的蛮横。"

    old "He summoned a large number of ghouls. A very impressive show. But it was just that: a show. A conjured ghoul such as the ones he summoned must be controlled individually."
    new "He summoned a large number of ghouls. A very impressive show. But it was just that: a show. A conjured ghoul such as the ones he summoned must be controlled individually.\n他召唤了大批食尸鬼。场面十分唬人。但那终究只是场面。像他召唤的这种食尸鬼，必须逐个加以操控。"

    old "You might call them puppets: they are under his complete control, but they're powerless unless he is pulling the strings. And pulling the strings of thirty different ghouls would prove an impossible task for an inexperienced vampire."
    new "You might call them puppets: they are under his complete control, but they're powerless unless he is pulling the strings. And pulling the strings of thirty different ghouls would prove an impossible task for an inexperienced vampire.\n你可以称它们为傀儡：它们完全受他掌控，但除非他牵动提线，否则便毫无威力。而同时牵动三十只食尸鬼的提线，对缺乏经验的吸血鬼来说，是根本不可能完成的任务。"

    old "A truly skilled vampire wouldn't need to summon thirty minions. He'd be able to get the job done with far fewer. A dozen ghouls would have been more than a match for your men. No offense intended."
    new "A truly skilled vampire wouldn't need to summon thirty minions. He'd be able to get the job done with far fewer. A dozen ghouls would have been more than a match for your men. No offense intended.\n真正老练的吸血鬼根本用不着召唤三十个爪牙。用少得多的数量就能成事。十几只食尸鬼就足以胜过你的人马。无意冒犯。"

    old "It seems you have a certain talent for outsmarting vampires."
    new "It seems you have a certain talent for outsmarting vampires.\n看来你很擅长智胜吸血鬼。"

    old "You could say that. If I were forced to fight a vampire on fair terms, he would likely overpower me. My combat strength is no match for a vampire. But with my wits, I was able to best him. Or, at the very least, force him to flee."
    new "You could say that. If I were forced to fight a vampire on fair terms, he would likely overpower me. My combat strength is no match for a vampire. But with my wits, I was able to best him. Or, at the very least, force him to flee.\n可以这么说。要是我被迫跟吸血鬼公平交手，他多半能压我一头。论战斗力，我不是吸血鬼的对手。但凭着头脑，我胜过了他。至少逼得他逃走了。"

    old "You could say that I outsmarted the vampire, but the truth is that in this case, I got lucky. I had the good fortune to encounter a vampire who was the right mix of anxious and overconfident. His inexperience led him to overextend, and reveal his hand in doing so. All I did was keep him honest."
    new "You could say that I outsmarted the vampire, but the truth is that in this case, I got lucky. I had the good fortune to encounter a vampire who was the right mix of anxious and overconfident. His inexperience led him to overextend, and reveal his hand in doing so. All I did was keep him honest.\n你可以说我智胜了吸血鬼，但说实话，这次我只是运气好。我碰巧遇上了一个既紧张又自大的吸血鬼。缺乏经验让他把招式用过了头，反而露了底牌。我所做的，不过是让他没法耍花招罢了。"

    old "I couldn't have done it without the help of your men. Had I encountered that vampire alone, I would have had no chips to bet with. It's easy to negotiate a confrontation when you have thirty soldiers standing behind you."
    new "I couldn't have done it without the help of your men. Had I encountered that vampire alone, I would have had no chips to bet with. It's easy to negotiate a confrontation when you have thirty soldiers standing behind you.\n没有你们士兵的帮助，我是做不到的。要是我独自遇上那个吸血鬼，我手里连可押的筹码都没有。身后站着三十个士兵，对峙起来自然好谈得多。"

    old "A man sitting near the edge of the room stands in his chair."
    new "A man sitting near the edge of the room stands in his chair.\n坐在房间边缘的一个男人从椅子上站了起来。"

    old "Apolimesho, you wish to speak?"
    new "Apolimesho, you wish to speak?\nApolimesho，你想发言？"

    old "I would like to request the council's permission to speak with [protag] privately. There are certain questions I'd like to ask [himher] that I believe would be poorly suited to a wider forum."
    new "I would like to request the council's permission to speak with [protag] privately. There are certain questions I'd like to ask [himher] that I believe would be poorly suited to a wider forum.\n我想请求议会允许我与 [protag] 私下谈谈。有几个问题我想问 [himher]，觉得不太适合在更大的场合讨论。"

    old "You have permission to speak to the subject privately, but you do not have the authority to make promises on the council's behalf. [protag], you must realize that in questioning you, Apolimesho does not represent the interests of the council. Understood?"
    new "You have permission to speak to the subject privately, but you do not have the authority to make promises on the council's behalf. [protag], you must realize that in questioning you, Apolimesho does not represent the interests of the council. Understood?\n你获准与这位当事人私下交谈，但你无权代表议会做出承诺。[protag]，你必须明白，Apolimesho 向你提问并不代表议会的立场。明白吗？"

    old "Yes, I understand."
    new "Yes, I understand.\n是的，我明白。"

    old "Apolimesho escorts me from the council chamber to a smaller room within the complex."
    new "Apolimesho escorts me from the council chamber to a smaller room within the complex.\nApolimesho 领着我离开议会大厅，来到建筑群里一个较小的房间。"

    old "I'd like to ask you some questions. These are questions with no right or wrong answer. I will think no less or more of you based on your responses. I simply wish to discover what kind of person you are. All I ask is that you be completely honest."
    new "I'd like to ask you some questions. These are questions with no right or wrong answer. I will think no less or more of you based on your responses. I simply wish to discover what kind of person you are. All I ask is that you be completely honest.\n我想问你几个问题。这些问题没有对错之分。无论你怎么回答，我都不会对你另眼相看。我只是想了解你是个什么样的人。我只要求你完全诚实。"

    old "What do you believe makes someone a great leader?"
    new "What do you believe makes someone a great leader?\n你认为是什么让一个人成为伟大的领袖？"

    old "Which is more important?"
    new "Which is more important?\n哪个更重要？"

    old "If working cooperatively with others to accomplish a shared goal, which is more important?"
    new "If working cooperatively with others to accomplish a shared goal, which is more important?\n在与他人合作实现共同目标时，哪个更重要？"

    old "You are in a familiar place, and you see a stranger looking lost and confused. What is your first response?"
    new "You are in a familiar place, and you see a stranger looking lost and confused. What is your first response?\n你身处一个熟悉的地方，看到一个陌生人神情迷茫困惑。你的第一反应是什么？"

    old "Suppose you are tending to someone who is sick. Which is more important to their recovery?"
    new "Suppose you are tending to someone who is sick. Which is more important to their recovery?\n假设你在照料一个病人。对他的康复来说，哪个更重要？"

    old "Good. I have no more questions."
    new "Good. I have no more questions.\n很好。我没有别的问题了。"

    old "One last question. Which of these elements of nature do you feel the most connected with?"
    new "One last question. Which of these elements of nature do you feel the most connected with?\n最后一个问题。这些自然元素中，你觉得与哪一个最有共鸣？"

    old "Interesting. You strike me as the kind of person who is able to get what [heshe] wants. Others may sometimes see you as demanding, but at your core you are both practical and passionate."
    new "Interesting. You strike me as the kind of person who is able to get what [heshe] wants. Others may sometimes see you as demanding, but at your core you are both practical and passionate.\n有意思。你给我的印象是，你属于那种能得到 [heshe] 想要之物的人。别人有时可能觉得你要求很高，但你的本质既务实又热情。"

    old "Interesting. You seem like a very thoughtful individual, one who weighs all decisions before [himher] before making a decision. You don't strike me as the social type, but I suspect that your wit and reasoned approach often prove useful in social situations."
    new "Interesting. You seem like a very thoughtful individual, one who weighs all decisions before [himher] before making a decision. You don't strike me as the social type, but I suspect that your wit and reasoned approach often prove useful in social situations.\n有意思。你看起来是个思虑很周全的人，做决定之前会先权衡一切。你给我的印象不像是善于交际的类型，但我猜想，你的机智和理性方式在社交场合往往很管用。"

    old "You strike me as a confident and energetic individual. You seem like the type of person that others find enthralling. I think that a cheerful and compassionate disposition suits you well, but I caution you against investing in others more than you invest in yourself."
    new "You strike me as a confident and energetic individual. You seem like the type of person that others find enthralling. I think that a cheerful and compassionate disposition suits you well, but I caution you against investing in others more than you invest in yourself.\n你给我的印象是自信而充满活力。你似乎是那种令人着迷的人。我觉得开朗而富有同情心的性情很适合你，但我要提醒你，别在他人身上投入得比在自己身上还多。"

    old "If I had to guess, I'd say that patience and dependability are your greatest attributes. You seem like the type who is at [hisher] best when supporting other individuals. A docile nature may strike others as a sign of weakness, but your subtle and elegant manner may ultimately rule the day, even if others don't see it at first."
    new "If I had to guess, I'd say that patience and dependability are your greatest attributes. You seem like the type who is at [hisher] best when supporting other individuals. A docile nature may strike others as a sign of weakness, but your subtle and elegant manner may ultimately rule the day, even if others don't see it at first.\n如果要我猜，我会说耐心和可靠是你最大的优点。你似乎是在支持他人时最能发挥 [hisher] 本色的那种人。温顺的性情在别人眼里可能像是软弱，但你细腻而优雅的作风最终可能会主导局面，即便别人起初看不出来。"

    old "Let us rejoin the council."
    new "Let us rejoin the council.\n我们回到议会那边去吧。"

    old "Apolimesho leads me back to the council chambers. When we enter, I see Karen at the center of the chamber, addressing the group. I stand with Apolimesho by the entrance and observe."
    new "Apolimesho leads me back to the council chambers. When we enter, I see Karen at the center of the chamber, addressing the group. I stand with Apolimesho by the entrance and observe.\nApolimesho 带我回到议会大厅。我们进去时，我看见 Karen 站在大厅中央，正在向众人讲话。我和 Apolimesho 站在入口处旁观。"

    old "What happened at N'Mar was tragic."
    new "What happened at N'Mar was tragic.\nN'Mar 发生的事是一场悲剧。"

    old "More than half an entire company died at the hands of those devilish beasts. It was a massacre."
    new "More than half an entire company died at the hands of those devilish beasts. It was a massacre.\n超过半个连的人死在了那些恶魔般野兽的手里。那是一场屠杀。"

    old "And that's all the more reason to redouble your efforts."
    new "And that's all the more reason to redouble your efforts.\n而这正是你更该加倍努力的理由。"

    old "That's insanity. Scores of men are lying dead, and your response is to send more men out? We can't throw more lives away. We didn't send a company of men out there to fight a war. They were there to gather information."
    new "That's insanity. Scores of men are lying dead, and your response is to send more men out? We can't throw more lives away. We didn't send a company of men out there to fight a war. They were there to gather information.\n这简直是疯了。几十个人尸横遍野，你的回应居然是再派更多人出去？我们不能再白白葬送人命了。我们派那连人出去，不是去打仗的，他们是去搜集情报的。"

    old "The mists surrounding N'Mar expand with each passing day. If something is not done about this, the mists will envelop Grimoire by the end of the year. Other lands, including the domain of my own people, will be soon to follow."
    new "The mists surrounding N'Mar expand with each passing day. If something is not done about this, the mists will envelop Grimoire by the end of the year. Other lands, including the domain of my own people, will be soon to follow.\n环绕 N'Mar 的迷雾一天比一天扩大。若再不想办法，到年底，迷雾就会吞没 Grimoire。其他土地，包括我族人的领地，很快也会步其后尘。"

    old "We have neither the military nor the political capital for total war, and that's what another battle at the gates of the castle will lead to."
    new "We have neither the military nor the political capital for total war, and that's what another battle at the gates of the castle will lead to.\n我们既没有打全面战争的军力，也没有那个政治资本，而再在城堡门前打一仗，恰恰会招致全面战争。"

    old "The men who died were not there to start a war. They were sent to gather intelligence."
    new "The men who died were not there to start a war. They were sent to gather intelligence.\n那些死去的人，并不是去开战的。他们是被派去搜集情报的。"

    old "And what good is that intelligence if you're not prepared to do anything with it?"
    new "And what good is that intelligence if you're not prepared to do anything with it?\n可若你根本不打算拿这情报做点什么，那情报又有何用？"

    old "The mission was a failure. We are no closer to discovering what is behind those creeping mists."
    new "The mission was a failure. We are no closer to discovering what is behind those creeping mists.\n任务失败了。我们丝毫没有更接近真相，弄不清那些蔓延迷雾背后究竟是什么。"

    old "What happened last night was an anomaly. Your mission could not have been more poorly timed. You picked the night of a full moon."
    new "What happened last night was an anomaly. Your mission could not have been more poorly timed. You picked the night of a full moon.\n昨晚发生的事是个例外。你们任务的时机糟得不能再糟。你们偏偏选了满月之夜。"

    old "The night of a full moon is when visibility is at its best."
    new "The night of a full moon is when visibility is at its best.\n满月之夜，能见度才是最好的。"

    old "The night of a full moon is when the vampires are at their strongest and most numerous. The night of a full moon is when the gates of the castle open, and the vampires leave to feed."
    new "The night of a full moon is when the vampires are at their strongest and most numerous. The night of a full moon is when the gates of the castle open, and the vampires leave to feed.\n满月之夜，是吸血鬼最强、数量最多的时刻。满月之夜，城堡的大门会打开，吸血鬼会出来觅食。"

    old "How is it that you came to know this?"
    new "How is it that you came to know this?\n你是怎么知道这些的？"

    old "As I said before, the growing mists around N'Mar are a growing concern for the Amazons as well. We have been flying surveillance missions over those fields for many moons. All, of course, to further the shared interests of both the human empire and the Amazons' domain."
    new "As I said before, the growing mists around N'Mar are a growing concern for the Amazons as well. We have been flying surveillance missions over those fields for many moons. All, of course, to further the shared interests of both the human empire and the Amazons' domain.\n正如我之前所说，N'Mar 周边不断扩大的迷雾，也日益令 Amazon 感到忧虑。许多个月以来，我们一直飞越那些田野执行侦察任务。当然，这一切都是为了促进人类帝国与 Amazon 领地双方的共同利益。"

    old "Why did you not relay this information to the council?"
    new "Why did you not relay this information to the council?\n你为什么没有把这个情报转告议会？"

    old "My people have reported everything we know to the council through proper diplomatic channels. If that information failed to reach you, you have only your own bureaucratic inefficiency and political idiocy to blame."
    new "My people have reported everything we know to the council through proper diplomatic channels. If that information failed to reach you, you have only your own bureaucratic inefficiency and political idiocy to blame.\n我的人民已经通过正当的外交渠道，把我们所知道的一切都报告给了议会。如果这些情报没能送到你们手上，那只能怪你们自己官僚机构的低效和政治上的愚蠢。"

    old "People around the council chamber begin to murmur."
    new "People around the council chamber begin to murmur.\n议会大厅四周的人开始窃窃私语。"

    old "Stay your tongue, woman. You may be a queen in the Amazons' citadel, but you stand before the governing body of the human empire."
    new "Stay your tongue, woman. You may be a queen in the Amazons' citadel, but you stand before the governing body of the human empire.\n管好你的嘴，女人。你在 Amazon 的城堡里或许是个女王，但此刻你面对的是人类帝国的统治机构。"

    old "I speak only the truth. Ignore it at your own peril."
    new "I speak only the truth. Ignore it at your own peril.\n我说的全是实话。无视它，后果自负。"

    old "You've said your piece. We require time for internal deliberation. All non-council members, please exit to the waiting chamber. We'll report back once we've reached a decision."
    new "You've said your piece. We require time for internal deliberation. All non-council members, please exit to the waiting chamber. We'll report back once we've reached a decision.\n你已经说完了。我们需要时间进行内部审议。所有非议会成员，请到等候厅去。我们做出决定后会通知大家。"

    old "Karen and I leave the council chamber."
    new "Karen and I leave the council chamber.\nKaren 和我离开了议会大厅。"

    old "So, dwarf. I don't believe I ever caught your name."
    new "So, dwarf. I don't believe I ever caught your name.\n那么，Dwarf。我想我还不知道你的名字。"

    old "How did you get mixed up in all this mess? I presume you have no ties to the human empire."
    new "How did you get mixed up in all this mess? I presume you have no ties to the human empire.\n你是怎么卷进这团乱麻里的？我猜你和人类帝国没什么瓜葛吧。"

    old "So, pointy-ears. I presume you have a name, but I don't think I've had occasion to learn it."
    new "So, pointy-ears. I presume you have a name, but I don't think I've had occasion to learn it.\n那么，尖耳朵。我想你该有个名字，只是我一直没机会知道。"

    old "How did you get mixed up in all this? You certainly don't have the look of someone who would be wrapped up in human empire affairs."
    new "How did you get mixed up in all this? You certainly don't have the look of someone who would be wrapped up in human empire affairs.\n你是怎么卷进这摊事里的？你看起来可不像会掺和人类帝国事务的人。"

    old "So, human. I don't believe I ever got your name."
    new "So, human. I don't believe I ever got your name.\n那么，人类。我想我还没请教过你的名字。"

    old "A human, yet neither a member of the human army nor the human council. What are you, exactly?"
    new "A human, yet neither a member of the human army nor the human council. What are you, exactly?\n你是个人类，却既不属于人类军队，也不是议会成员。你到底算什么人？"

    old "So, elf. I don't believe I ever got your name."
    new "So, elf. I don't believe I ever got your name.\n那么，Elf。我想我还没请教过你的名字。"

    old "An elf, in the council chambers of the human empire. You're awfully far from home."
    new "An elf, in the council chambers of the human empire. You're awfully far from home.\n一个 Elf，竟出现在人类帝国的议会大厅里。你离家可真够远的。"

    old "GrandTree isn't my home, if that's what you're implying."
    new "GrandTree isn't my home, if that's what you're implying.\n如果你是在暗示那个的话，GrandTree 不是我的家。"

    old "No? Then where you do call home?"
    new "No? Then where you do call home?\n不是吗？那你把哪里称作家？"

    old "Nowhere and everywhere."
    new "Nowhere and everywhere.\n无处不是，处处皆是。"

    old "A wanderer, eh? So how is it that you got mixed up in all this business?"
    new "A wanderer, eh? So how is it that you got mixed up in all this business?\n是个浪迹天涯的人，嗯？那你是怎么卷进这档子事里的？"

    old "I happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. Or the right place and the right time, depending on how you look at it."
    new "I happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. Or the right place and the right time, depending on how you look at it.\n我碰巧在错误的时间出现在错误的地点。或者也可以说，是正确的时间、正确的地点，全看你怎么看。"

    old "What part of this would you consider good fortune?"
    new "What part of this would you consider good fortune?\n这有什么好算作运气的？"

    old "Well, I was able to help the few men that escaped the incident at N'Mar."
    new "Well, I was able to help the few men that escaped the incident at N'Mar.\n哦，我好歹帮上了那几个从 N'Mar 事件中逃出来的人。"

    old "Ah, that's right. You were escorting them out. How's that worked out for you since?"
    new "Ah, that's right. You were escorting them out. How's that worked out for you since?\n啊，对了。是你护送他们出来的。那之后，你过得怎么样？"

    old "Well, the council of Grimoire considers me a person of interest. I'm not sure that's a good thing, but I don't see how it could be a bad thing."
    new "Well, the council of Grimoire considers me a person of interest. I'm not sure that's a good thing, but I don't see how it could be a bad thing.\n嗯，Grimoire 议会把我当成了重点关注对象。我不确定这是好事，但也看不出能坏到哪里去。"

    old "Those council elders, they know nothing. Actually, I take that back. They do have some awareness of what's going on. And that makes their stupidity all the more infuriating."
    new "Those council elders, they know nothing. Actually, I take that back. They do have some awareness of what's going on. And that makes their stupidity all the more infuriating.\n那些议会元老，他们什么都不懂。其实，我收回这话。他们确实对事态有所了解。正因为如此，他们的愚蠢才更让人火大。"

    old "There's foul magic afoot at the Castle of N'Mar. It's shrouded in mist, and horrors befall anything or anyone caught in it. The mists that cover those plains grow with each passing day."
    new "There's foul magic afoot at the Castle of N'Mar. It's shrouded in mist, and horrors befall anything or anyone caught in it. The mists that cover those plains grow with each passing day.\nN'Mar 城堡里有邪恶的魔法在作祟。它笼罩在迷雾之中，任何卷入其中的事物或人都会遭遇恐怖。覆盖那些平原的迷雾一天比一天扩大。"

    old "It spreads the defilement of death across lands that were once home to the living, but it also seems to imbue the dead with an uncanny sort of undeath, unlike any we've seen before."
    new "It spreads the defilement of death across lands that were once home to the living, but it also seems to imbue the dead with an uncanny sort of undeath, unlike any we've seen before.\n它把死亡的污秽散播到曾是生灵家园的土地上，似乎还赋予了死者一种前所未见、诡异莫测的不死之态。"

    old "Walking corpses and shambling skeletons already seem plenty uncanny to me."
    new "Walking corpses and shambling skeletons already seem plenty uncanny to me.\n行走的尸体和蹒跚的骷髅，在我看来已经够诡异的了。"

    old "We've long thought that these sorts of reanimated undead beasts were nothing but flesh and bone possessed by the instinct to kill. Early scouts described them as seeming to act of their individual volition. They seemed...hesitant."
    new "We've long thought that these sorts of reanimated undead beasts were nothing but flesh and bone possessed by the instinct to kill. Early scouts described them as seeming to act of their individual volition. They seemed...hesitant.\n我们一直以为，这类复活的亡灵野兽不过是被杀戮本能支配的血肉骨头。可早期的侦察兵却描述它们似乎各有各的意志在行动。它们显得……犹豫。"

    old "Hesitant?"
    new "Hesitant?\n犹豫？"

    old "There are some spirits that seem to still possess something of a soul, but lesser undead like zombies are merely animated flesh. They don't flinch. They don't feel fear, or any other emotion. And yet we've heard rumors that seem to contradict this."
    new "There are some spirits that seem to still possess something of a soul, but lesser undead like zombies are merely animated flesh. They don't flinch. They don't feel fear, or any other emotion. And yet we've heard rumors that seem to contradict this.\n有些鬼魂似乎仍残留着一丝灵魂，但像僵尸这样的低等亡灵，不过是会动的血肉。它们不会退缩，感受不到恐惧，也没有任何情绪。然而，我们却听到一些与之相悖的传闻。"

    old "Only rumors? Have they been confirmed?"
    new "Only rumors? Have they been confirmed?\n只是传闻？得到证实了吗？"

    old "Unfortunately, it's hard to confirm rumors of this sort. Most these reports came from people who were understandably traumatized by the experience. That kind of reaction is understandable, but it can also lead to false reporting."
    new "Unfortunately, it's hard to confirm rumors of this sort. Most these reports came from people who were understandably traumatized by the experience. That kind of reaction is understandable, but it can also lead to false reporting.\n可惜，这类传闻很难证实。这些报告大多来自那些经历了创伤的人，这情有可原。这种反应可以理解，但也可能导致误报。"

    old "But even if the reports of undead acting of their own will are false, we are still left with an undead menace and N'Mar's creeping corrosion. Something has to be done."
    new "But even if the reports of undead acting of their own will are false, we are still left with an undead menace and N'Mar's creeping corrosion. Something has to be done.\n但即便那些关于亡灵自主行动的报道是假的，我们仍然要面对亡灵的威胁，以及 N'Mar 那不断蔓延的侵蚀。总得采取行动。"

    old "The council knew this, and so they did do something. They sent a company of soldiers to investigate, and most of those men met with a grisly demise. That's terrible, but it should be evidence that now more than ever, it's time to act. It's time to strike decisively. And yet still they tarry, talking of political feasibility."
    new "The council knew this, and so they did do something. They sent a company of soldiers to investigate, and most of those men met with a grisly demise. That's terrible, but it should be evidence that now more than ever, it's time to act. It's time to strike decisively. And yet still they tarry, talking of political feasibility.\n议会明白这一点，所以他们确实做了点什么。他们派了一个连的士兵去调查，结果大多数人落得惨死的下场。这固然可怕，但恰恰证明，现在比任何时候都更需要行动，需要果断出击。可他们却仍在拖延，大谈什么政治可行性。"

    old "I'm prepared to lend them the support of my own fighters, but only the human empire has the resources needed to fight this battle."
    new "I'm prepared to lend them the support of my own fighters, but only the human empire has the resources needed to fight this battle.\n我准备把自己的战士交给他们支援，但只有人类帝国才拥有打赢这一仗所需的资源。"

    old "Apolimesho emerges from the council chamber."
    new "Apolimesho emerges from the council chamber.\nApolimesho 从议会大厅里走了出来。"

    old "The council has reached a collective decision about what their action will be on this matter."
    new "The council has reached a collective decision about what their action will be on this matter.\n议会已就此事采取何种行动达成了集体决定。"

    old "What is that?"
    new "What is that?\n是什么决定？"

    old "The council took special interest in your remarks regarding what you've observed of the castle gates during the full moon. If we're to mount an invasion, the council believes it would be best to do it at this time."
    new "The council took special interest in your remarks regarding what you've observed of the castle gates during the full moon. If we're to mount an invasion, the council believes it would be best to do it at this time.\n议会对你所描述的在满月之夜观察到的城堡大门情况特别感兴趣。若要发动一次突入，议会认为最好就选在这个时机。"

    old "That's absurd. Fight the vampires at their strongest?"
    new "That's absurd. Fight the vampires at their strongest?\n这太荒唐了。在吸血鬼最强的时刻去跟他们打？"

    old "This isn't a full-on assault. The council believes it would be best for a few individuals to sneak in and gather what information they can. The belief is that we can't effectively wage war when we have no clear idea what it is that we're fighting."
    new "This isn't a full-on assault. The council believes it would be best for a few individuals to sneak in and gather what information they can. The belief is that we can't effectively wage war when we have no clear idea what it is that we're fighting.\n这不是全面进攻。议会认为最好派少数人潜入，尽可能搜集情报。他们的想法是，当我们连自己在跟什么作战都说不清时，是无法有效开战的。"

    old "So, they're assembling a task force?"
    new "So, they're assembling a task force?\n那么，他们是在组建一支特遣队？"

    old "No. They're authorizing you to assemble one."
    new "No. They're authorizing you to assemble one.\n不。他们是在授权你去组建一支。"

    old "The council is foisting this task upon me? Assembling a task force in the span of a single lunar cycle is no small task, and while I have a vested interest in this matter, I also have my own domain to run. I am a queen, if the council hasn't forgotten, and internal affairs consume the bulk of my time."
    new "The council is foisting this task upon me? Assembling a task force in the span of a single lunar cycle is no small task, and while I have a vested interest in this matter, I also have my own domain to run. I am a queen, if the council hasn't forgotten, and internal affairs consume the bulk of my time.\n议会是要把这差事硬塞给我吗？在一个月相周期内组建一支特遣队，可不是件小事，何况我虽然对这事有切身利害，却也得打理自己的领地。我可是一位女王，如果议会还没忘记的话，内政占去了我大部分的时间。"

    old "[protag], the council has taken special interest in you. Specifically, they are impressed with your knowledge of the lands surrounding N'Mar, and your heroic efforts to rescue the survivors of the catastrophe by the castle."
    new "[protag], the council has taken special interest in you. Specifically, they are impressed with your knowledge of the lands surrounding N'Mar, and your heroic efforts to rescue the survivors of the catastrophe by the castle.\n[protag]，议会对你有特别的兴趣。具体来说，他们很欣赏你对 N'Mar 周边土地的了解，以及你英勇营救城堡灾难幸存者的努力。"

    old "It's our understanding that you are someone who works in the pursuit of knowledge. You are a scholar who endeavors to discover the unknown."
    new "It's our understanding that you are someone who works in the pursuit of knowledge. You are a scholar who endeavors to discover the unknown.\n据我们了解，你是以追求知识为业的人。你是一名致力于探索未知的学者。"

    old "[protag], as a man who knows well the ways of the tome and scroll, I can think of no better way to better understand N'Mar and the undead that inhabit it than with direct personal experience."
    new "[protag], as a man who knows well the ways of the tome and scroll, I can think of no better way to better understand N'Mar and the undead that inhabit it than with direct personal experience.\n[protag]，作为一个深谙典籍卷轴之道的人，我想不出比亲身经历更好的方式来了解 N'Mar 及其中的亡灵。"

    old "The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon. Should you accept, and should your mission be a success, your reports will fill the history books of our nation. If you seek recognition, I can think of no better way to pursue that goal."
    new "The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon. Should you accept, and should your mission be a success, your reports will fill the history books of our nation. If you seek recognition, I can think of no better way to pursue that goal.\n议会想聘用你，负责组建一支在下个满月之夜潜入城堡的队伍。倘若你接受，且使命成功，你的报告将被载入我们国家的史册。如果你追求的是名望，我想不出比这更好的途径了。"

    old "It's our understanding that you are one who accompanies adventurers. Someone who sells [hisher] services as a traveling guide of sorts."
    new "It's our understanding that you are one who accompanies adventurers. Someone who sells [hisher] services as a traveling guide of sorts.\n据我们了解，你是那种陪伴冒险者的人，靠出售 [hisher] 服务为生，算是个旅行向导。"

    old "The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon. With your experience as adventurer, I believe you would be well-suited to the task."
    new "The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon. With your experience as adventurer, I believe you would be well-suited to the task.\n议会想聘用你，负责组建一支在下个满月之夜潜入城堡的队伍。以你作为冒险者的经验，我相信你很适合这项任务。"

    old "It's our understanding that you are a mercenary of sorts."
    new "It's our understanding that you are a mercenary of sorts.\n据我们了解，你算是个雇佣兵。"

    old "That is true, in a manner of speaking, although I'm not strictly a fighter."
    new "That is true, in a manner of speaking, although I'm not strictly a fighter.\n可以这么说，不过我并非严格意义上的战士。"

    old "It's our understanding that you are one who pursues wealth in the trade of goods."
    new "It's our understanding that you are one who pursues wealth in the trade of goods.\n据我们了解，你是靠贩运货物追求财富的人。"

    old "I wonder if you might be persuaded to offer your services to us instead. The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon."
    new "I wonder if you might be persuaded to offer your services to us instead. The council would like to hire you to oversee the creation of a group that will infiltrate the castle during the next full moon.\n我在想，能否说服你转而为我们效力。议会想聘用你，负责组建一支在下个满月之夜潜入城堡的队伍。"

    old "So, I'd be undertaking a stealth mission?"
    new "So, I'd be undertaking a stealth mission?\n那么，我要执行的是一次潜入任务？"

    old "We don't know what kind of resistance you'll face. You're better equipped than any of us to answer that question."
    new "We don't know what kind of resistance you'll face. You're better equipped than any of us to answer that question.\n我们不知道你会遇到什么样的抵抗。你比我们任何人都更有能力回答这个问题。"

    old "I'll need a small team of dedicated fighters."
    new "I'll need a small team of dedicated fighters.\n我需要一支由精锐战士组成的小队。"

    old "The council doesn't believe it's politically feasible to risk the lives of more human soldiers when so many have already been slain. Recruiting the individuals who will join you is part of the task that's being presented to you."
    new "The council doesn't believe it's politically feasible to risk the lives of more human soldiers when so many have already been slain. Recruiting the individuals who will join you is part of the task that's being presented to you.\n议会认为，在已经死了这么多人的情况下，再拿更多人类士兵的性命去冒险，在政治上不可行。招募加入你的人选，正是交给你的任务的一部分。"

    old "This isn't what is needed to deal with the crisis at N'Mar. Not even close."
    new "This isn't what is needed to deal with the crisis at N'Mar. Not even close.\n这根本不是应对 N'Mar 危机所需要的做法。差得远了。"

    old "Karen, I'm aware of your disdain for the council. And if I am completely honest, I have little fondness for their ways. Being a member of the council myself, I am fully aware of the extent to which politics has mired their ability to function as a ruling body."
    new "Karen, I'm aware of your disdain for the council. And if I am completely honest, I have little fondness for their ways. Being a member of the council myself, I am fully aware of the extent to which politics has mired their ability to function as a ruling body.\nKaren，我知道你对议会不屑。说实话，我对他们的作风也没什么好感。身为议会的一员，我完全清楚政治在多大程度上拖累了他们作为统治机构运作的能力。"

    old "However, it's for precisely this reason that I encourage you to look favorably on this chosen course of action. [protag], if you choose to accept this mission, you will have almost complete autonomy."
    new "However, it's for precisely this reason that I encourage you to look favorably on this chosen course of action. [protag], if you choose to accept this mission, you will have almost complete autonomy.\n然而，也正因如此，我才鼓励你以积极的眼光看待这一选定的行动方案。[protag]，如果你选择接受这项任务，你将拥有几乎完全的自主权。"

    old "The council will not need to approve your actions. You can fill your team with absolutely the best soldiers, rather than being bogged down with officers who are seeking only to further their own political career."
    new "The council will not need to approve your actions. You can fill your team with absolutely the best soldiers, rather than being bogged down with officers who are seeking only to further their own political career.\n议会无需批准你的行动。你可以给自己的团队配上最优秀的战士，而不必被那些一心只想往上爬的军官拖累。"

    old "Imagine if personal or institutional schisms played no role in the formation of your team. Elf, dwarf, Amazon, imagine if you could have a team of them, all working in a tightly-knit unit to achieve a common goal."
    new "Imagine if personal or institutional schisms played no role in the formation of your team. Elf, dwarf, Amazon, imagine if you could have a team of them, all working in a tightly-knit unit to achieve a common goal.\n想象一下，如果组建团队时，个人的或派系的嫌隙都不再作数。Elf、Dwarf、Amazon，想象一下，你能拥有一支由他们组成的队伍，大家紧密协作，共同实现一个目标。"

    old "The council is deliberately avoiding involvement. Karen, I realize it's easy to look at this as a bad thing. But I see it as more of a blessing than a curse."
    new "The council is deliberately avoiding involvement. Karen, I realize it's easy to look at this as a bad thing. But I see it as more of a blessing than a curse.\n议会是在刻意回避介入。Karen，我知道这很容易被看成坏事。但我觉得，与其说是诅咒，不如说是一种恩赐。"

    old "[protag], I do not mean to make your decision for you. Ultimately, the choice is yours. But I believe that you are the best chance that we have of overcoming the challenge that is the sinister magic that lives within the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "[protag], I do not mean to make your decision for you. Ultimately, the choice is yours. But I believe that you are the best chance that we have of overcoming the challenge that is the sinister magic that lives within the Castle of N'Mar.\n[protag]，我不是要替你拿主意。归根结底，选择权在你。但我相信，你是我们战胜 N'Mar 城堡里那股邪恶魔法挑战的最大希望。"

    old "You're asking me to assemble a team of fighters, starting from nothing."
    new "You're asking me to assemble a team of fighters, starting from nothing.\n你是要我白手起家，组建一支战士团队。"

    old "Yes. You put it bluntly, but I can't think of any other way to say it. I suspect Karen would be willing to advise you in your recruitment efforts."
    new "Yes. You put it bluntly, but I can't think of any other way to say it. I suspect Karen would be willing to advise you in your recruitment efforts.\n是的。你说得很直白，但我也想不出别的说法。我想 Karen 会愿意在你的招募工作中给你建议。"

    old "You can offer no other resources?"
    new "You can offer no other resources?\n你提供不了其他资源吗？"

    old "Alas, with all the past years wars, the council can offer little financial help. Still, the council is prepared to offer a modest budget of 50 gold coins each day until the next full moon, by which point you should have assembled your task force."
    new "Alas, with all the past years wars, the council can offer little financial help. Still, the council is prepared to offer a modest budget of 50 gold coins each day until the next full moon, by which point you should have assembled your task force.\n唉，由于连年战乱，议会在资金上帮不上什么忙。不过，议会仍准备每天提供 50 枚金币的微薄预算，直到下个满月为止，届时你应该已经组建好了特遣队。"

    old "50 gold coins is not much."
    new "50 gold coins is not much.\n50 枚金币可不算多。"

    old "I'm afraid it will have to do, for the time being. Perhaps, if you impress the council, they may be willing to offer more generous support in the future. In the meantime, that gold will have to suffice to cover your expenses."
    new "I'm afraid it will have to do, for the time being. Perhaps, if you impress the council, they may be willing to offer more generous support in the future. In the meantime, that gold will have to suffice to cover your expenses.\n恐怕眼下只能如此了。也许，如果你能让议会刮目相看，他们将来或许愿意提供更慷慨的支持。在此期间，那点金子得先够你应付开销。"

    old "Of course, any treasures or riches which you happen to discover in the course of your recruitment or exploration missions would be yours to keep. It is a common adage that fate has a way of rewarding intrepid explorers."
    new "Of course, any treasures or riches which you happen to discover in the course of your recruitment or exploration missions would be yours to keep. It is a common adage that fate has a way of rewarding intrepid explorers.\n当然，你在招募或探索途中碰巧发现的任何宝藏或财物，都归你所有。常言道，命运自有办法奖赏无畏的探索者。"

    old "Or to be more accurate, the places that most people consider too dangerous to explore tend to have more valuables yet undiscovered."
    new "Or to be more accurate, the places that most people consider too dangerous to explore tend to have more valuables yet undiscovered.\n或者更准确地说，那些大多数人认为太过危险、不敢涉足的地方，往往藏着更多尚未被发现的财宝。"

    old "Success would also give you quite the reputation. I'm sure someone as shrewd as you could figure out a way to parlay that reputation into some sort of wealth. Or perhaps you see fame as its own reward."
    new "Success would also give you quite the reputation. I'm sure someone as shrewd as you could figure out a way to parlay that reputation into some sort of wealth. Or perhaps you see fame as its own reward.\n成功还能让你声名鹊起。我相信，像你这么精明的人，一定有办法把名声转化为某种财富。又或许，你视名望本身为一种回报。"

    old "What do you think, [protag]?"
    new "What do you think, [protag]?\n你怎么看，[protag]？"

    old "I'm in the practice of offering my services to those who are willing to pay. If the paying party happens to be the council of Grimoire, and the service happens to be mounting an assault on the Castle of N'Mar, then so be it. I accept your proposal."
    new "I'm in the practice of offering my services to those who are willing to pay. If the paying party happens to be the council of Grimoire, and the service happens to be mounting an assault on the Castle of N'Mar, then so be it. I accept your proposal.\n我向来习惯为肯付钱的人效力。如果付钱的一方碰巧是 Grimoire 议会，而要做的差事碰巧是攻打 N'Mar 城堡，那就这么定了。我接受你的提议。"

    old "I'm sorry, but I'm not in a position to accept this mission. I've no desire to take on this heavy of a responsibility, nor do I have any desire to dash into the waiting jaws of death at the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "I'm sorry, but I'm not in a position to accept this mission. I've no desire to take on this heavy of a responsibility, nor do I have any desire to dash into the waiting jaws of death at the Castle of N'Mar.\n抱歉，我无法接受这项任务。我不想扛起这么重的责任，也没有任何冲进 N'Mar 城堡那死神张开的血盆大口里的欲望。"

    old "I'm sure that there are dozens of individuals within the human empire who are equally capable of handling this task. Let it fall to one of them instead."
    new "I'm sure that there are dozens of individuals within the human empire who are equally capable of handling this task. Let it fall to one of them instead.\n我相信人类帝国内有几十个同样能胜任这项任务的人。不如就交给他们中的某一个吧。"

    old "Very well. We'll find someone else."
    new "Very well. We'll find someone else.\n那好吧。我们会另寻他人。"

    old "Are you sure that will be alright?"
    new "Are you sure that will be alright?\n你确定那样行得通吗？"

    old "I cannot be sure of anything. But realize this, [protag]: you are not so special. You said it yourself: there are many individuals who are just as capable as you are, if not more qualified. Will we be able to find them? Only time will tell. But this is not your burden to bear."
    new "I cannot be sure of anything. But realize this, [protag]: you are not so special. You said it yourself: there are many individuals who are just as capable as you are, if not more qualified. Will we be able to find them? Only time will tell. But this is not your burden to bear.\n我什么都不敢打包票。但你得明白，[protag]：你并没有那么特别。你自己也说了：有许多人和你一样有能力，甚至比你更有资格。我们能不能找到他们？只有时间能给出答案。但这副担子，不用你来扛。"

    old "I wish you the best of luck, then."
    new "I wish you the best of luck, then.\n那我就祝你好运了。"

    old "Your answer pleases me. [protag], as I said, you have a large degree of autonomy in how to approach this mission. The particulars of how you will assemble your team are left for you to decide."
    new "Your answer pleases me. [protag], as I said, you have a large degree of autonomy in how to approach this mission. The particulars of how you will assemble your team are left for you to decide.\n你的回答令我欣慰。[protag]，正如我所说，在执行这项任务的方式上，你有很大的自主权。具体如何组建你的团队，由你自己决定。"

    old "However, if you ever find yourself stuck or in need of advice, return here to Grimorie and I'll do my best to advise you on the best possible course of action. Or, at the very least, I can provide hints and suggestions on how to proceed."
    new "However, if you ever find yourself stuck or in need of advice, return here to Grimorie and I'll do my best to advise you on the best possible course of action. Or, at the very least, I can provide hints and suggestions on how to proceed.\n不过，如果你发现自己卡住了或需要建议，就回到 Grimoire 这里来，我会尽力给你指点最佳的行动方向。或者，至少我能就如何推进提供些提示和建议。"

    old "[protag], since our goals are coincident, and you're assembling a team of fighters, I'd be remiss if I neglected to offer you assistance."
    new "[protag], since our goals are coincident, and you're assembling a team of fighters, I'd be remiss if I neglected to offer you assistance.\n[protag]，既然我们的目标一致，而你又在组建一支战士团队，我若是不主动提供帮助，就说不过去了。"

    old "I have obligation in the domain of the Amazons that prevent me from accompanying you on your journey. But I can pick out one of my warriors to assist you in your mission."
    new "I have obligation in the domain of the Amazons that prevent me from accompanying you on your journey. But I can pick out one of my warriors to assist you in your mission.\n我在 Amazon 领地负有职责，无法随你同行。但我可以挑出我的一名战士来协助你的任务。"

    old "Please, come to the Citadel when you have the opportunity, and we can discuss this matter at greater length."
    new "Please, come to the Citadel when you have the opportunity, and we can discuss this matter at greater length.\n请你有空时到 Citadel 来，我们可以更详细地讨论此事。"

    old "Everyone is there. I must admit it's a peculiar sight. The faces I see run the gamut of races to be found across the lands of Aravorn: elf, naga, nomad, dwarf...all that seems to be missing is an amazon face. Or two, if I'm counting Karen."
    new "Everyone is there. I must admit it's a peculiar sight. The faces I see run the gamut of races to be found across the lands of Aravorn: elf, naga, nomad, dwarf...all that seems to be missing is an amazon face. Or two, if I'm counting Karen.\n大家都在。我得承认，这景象颇为奇特。我看到的这些面孔，涵盖了 Aravorn 各地的各个种族：Elf、Naga、Nomad、Dwarf……似乎唯独少了 Amazon 的面孔。若把 Karen 也算上，那还缺两个。"

    old "Thank you for all gathering here. I take it the amazons have yet to arrive?"
    new "Thank you for all gathering here. I take it the amazons have yet to arrive?\n谢谢大家齐聚于此。我想 Amazon 们还没到吧？"

    old "Tall, blonde hair, strong armor, wielding a sword?"
    new "Tall, blonde hair, strong armor, wielding a sword?\n高个子、金发、身披重甲、手持长剑？"

    old "Ooh, I like how you describe her. Is she coming? I want to meet her."
    new "Ooh, I like how you describe her. Is she coming? I want to meet her.\n哦，我喜欢你这样形容她。她会来吗？我想见见她。"

    old "Wait, an amazon is with us? That's so cool! I always wanted to meet one in person!"
    new "Wait, an amazon is with us? That's so cool! I always wanted to meet one in person!\n等等，有 Amazon 和我们一起？太酷了！我一直想亲眼见见呢！"

    old "An amazon? Good, I was worried that I'd be the only one doing the heavy fights."
    new "An amazon? Good, I was worried that I'd be the only one doing the heavy fights.\n有 Amazon？太好了，我本来还担心硬仗都得我一个人打。"

    old "Yes, that's her description. Nuala, I suppose you've seen her?"
    new "Yes, that's her description. Nuala, I suppose you've seen her?\n是的，那就是她的样貌。Nuala，我想你已经见过她了吧？"

    old "Yes, I meet her a few hours ago in the field south of Grimoire. She told me that she was waiting to rendezvous with someone before coming here."
    new "Yes, I meet her a few hours ago in the field south of Grimoire. She told me that she was waiting to rendezvous with someone before coming here.\n是的，几个小时前我在 Grimoire 南边的野地里见过她。她告诉我，她在来之前要等一个人会合。"

    old "Ah, good. That means that Queen Karen should be joining us shortly."
    new "Ah, good. That means that Queen Karen should be joining us shortly.\n啊，很好。那说明 Karen 女王应该很快就会加入我们。"

    old "The amazon queen herself is coming here?"
    new "The amazon queen herself is coming here?\nAmazon 女王本人也要来？"

    old "Ooh, I don't think I've ever met a queen before. This will be a treat."
    new "Ooh, I don't think I've ever met a queen before. This will be a treat.\n哦，我好像还从没见过女王呢。这下可有意思了。"

    old "Ah, Queen Karen. Her beauty is legendary. Matched only by her strong will."
    new "Ah, Queen Karen. Her beauty is legendary. Matched only by her strong will.\n啊，Karen 女王。她的美貌是传奇，唯有她那坚强的意志能与之媲美。"

    old "Karen. Someone once offered me a fortune to get her killed. I refused. Not because I couldn't do it. Would have been tricky, but I could have managed. But simply I don't kill such honorable people."
    new "Karen. Someone once offered me a fortune to get her killed. I refused. Not because I couldn't do it. Would have been tricky, but I could have managed. But simply I don't kill such honorable people.\nKaren。曾有人出重金要我取她性命。我拒绝了。倒不是我做不到。那会有点棘手，但我办得到。只是我不杀这样高尚的人。"

    old "Suddenly, Nuala takes a defensive stance and points to a bush nearby."
    new "Suddenly, Nuala takes a defensive stance and points to a bush nearby.\n突然，Nuala 摆出防御姿态，指向附近的一丛灌木。"

    old "Relax, nomad. It's me."
    new "Relax, nomad. It's me.\n放松，Nomad。是我。"

    old "Oh, Leena, you're back already? Is Queen Karen the person you were meeting with?"
    new "Oh, Leena, you're back already? Is Queen Karen the person you were meeting with?\n哦，Leena，你已经回来了？你要会合的人就是 Karen 女王吗？"

    old "Yes. Queen Karen sends her regrets; unfortunately she won't be able to join us today. She couldn't attend for undisclosed reasons."
    new "Yes. Queen Karen sends her regrets; unfortunately she won't be able to join us today. She couldn't attend for undisclosed reasons.\n是的。Karen 女王深表遗憾，可惜今天不能加入我们。她因不便透露的原因未能出席。"

    old "She didn't tell you?"
    new "She didn't tell you?\n她没告诉你原因？"

    old "She disclosed the reasons to me, but it is an internal matter, so I will not disclose the reasons to you."
    new "She disclosed the reasons to me, but it is an internal matter, so I will not disclose the reasons to you.\n她向我说明了原因，但那是内部事务，所以我不便向你透露。"

    old "Ah, well. Fair enough."
    new "Ah, well. Fair enough.\n啊，好吧。可以理解。"

    old "Still, Karen believes it is important that this meeting take place, for your sake, and the sake of everyone else here. She said it was important for something called 'team-building.'"
    new "Still, Karen believes it is important that this meeting take place, for your sake, and the sake of everyone else here. She said it was important for something called 'team-building.'\n尽管如此，Karen 仍认为这场聚会很重要，既是为了你，也是为了在座的各位。她说，这关乎所谓的“团队建设”。"

    old "I guess the upside is that without the presence of a queen, there's no one here to challenge my authority. So, everyone! Gather 'round!"
    new "I guess the upside is that without the presence of a queen, there's no one here to challenge my authority. So, everyone! Gather 'round!\n我想，好处是既然没有女王在场，这里就没人来挑战我的权威了。所以，大家！都围过来！"

    old "I step into the midst of the group, and they form a circle around me."
    new "I step into the midst of the group, and they form a circle around me.\n我走到人群中央，他们在我四周围成一圈。"

    old "I see quite a diverse array of faces. I answer to the authority of the Grimoire council, but as you might notice, we aren't in Grimoire. It seems fitting that we're meeting in neutral territory, especially given the history that some of you share with the Human Empire."
    new "I see quite a diverse array of faces. I answer to the authority of the Grimoire council, but as you might notice, we aren't in Grimoire. It seems fitting that we're meeting in neutral territory, especially given the history that some of you share with the Human Empire.\n我看到的面孔相当多样。我受 Grimoire 议会辖制，但你们或许也注意到了，我们并不在 Grimoire。尤其考虑到你们中有些人与人类帝国的过往，我们在中立地带会面，倒也合宜。"

    old "My naga friend gives me a knowing nod."
    new "My naga friend gives me a knowing nod.\n我那位 Naga 朋友会意地朝我点了点头。"

    old "All of you joined me for different reasons, but I think all of us have one thing in common: we want to put a stop to whatever is causing the spread of corruption from N'Mar. It's manifested itself in many ways: the perpetual mists, the corroding ground, and perhaps most noticeably, the zombies, skeletons, and ghouls that are shambling all over the plains."
    new "All of you joined me for different reasons, but I think all of us have one thing in common: we want to put a stop to whatever is causing the spread of corruption from N'Mar. It's manifested itself in many ways: the perpetual mists, the corroding ground, and perhaps most noticeably, the zombies, skeletons, and ghouls that are shambling all over the plains.\n你们加入我的原因各不相同，但我想我们大家有一个共同点：我们都想阻止那股从 N'Mar 蔓延开来的腐化。它以种种方式显现：终年不散的迷雾、被侵蚀的大地，或许最显眼的，便是遍布平原、蹒跚而行的僵尸、骷髅和食尸鬼。"

    old "Several members of the crowd chuckle."
    new "Several members of the crowd chuckle.\n人群里有几个人轻笑出声。"

    old "We need to investigate. Actually, perhaps the word 'investigate' is not aggressive enough to describe our next course of action. We are going to infiltrate."
    new "We need to investigate. Actually, perhaps the word 'investigate' is not aggressive enough to describe our next course of action. We are going to infiltrate.\n我们需要调查。其实，“调查”这个词或许不足以形容我们接下来的行动。我们要做的是潜入。"

    old "Infiltrate what, exactly?"
    new "Infiltrate what, exactly?\n具体是潜入哪里？"

    old "We'll be entering the castle itself. The mist-covered plains are only a symptom of the corruption. We need to discover what lies at its source. And the best moment to infiltrate the castle is during the next full moon."
    new "We'll be entering the castle itself. The mist-covered plains are only a symptom of the corruption. We need to discover what lies at its source. And the best moment to infiltrate the castle is during the next full moon.\n我们要进入城堡本身。被迷雾覆盖的平原只是腐化的表象。我们要找出其根源所在。而潜入城堡的最佳时机，就是下一个满月之夜。"

    old "A full moon? The time when vampires come out to feed?"
    new "A full moon? The time when vampires come out to feed?\n满月？那不就是吸血鬼出来觅食的时候吗？"

    old "Yes, precisely. The full moon will be a dangerous time. But while the undead come out to play, we will be going inside to snoop around the castle that they leave behind. Of course, this isn't the kind of 'snooping' that can happen without a combat-ready task force."
    new "Yes, precisely. The full moon will be a dangerous time. But while the undead come out to play, we will be going inside to snoop around the castle that they leave behind. Of course, this isn't the kind of 'snooping' that can happen without a combat-ready task force.\n是的，正是如此。满月之夜会很危险。但当亡灵们出来游荡时，我们正好潜入他们离开后留下的城堡里打探。当然，若是没有一支随时能战斗的特遣队，这种“打探”根本无从谈起。"

    old "Galan raises his hammer and grunts. In response, several other members of the group raise their weapons in a show of solidarity."
    new "Galan raises his hammer and grunts. In response, several other members of the group raise their weapons in a show of solidarity.\nGalan 举起战锤，闷哼一声。作为回应，队伍里又有几个人举起武器，以示团结。"

    old "I didn't sign up for this mission because I expected it to be safe."
    new "I didn't sign up for this mission because I expected it to be safe.\n我加入这项任务，本就不是冲着安全来的。"

    old "You can count on us, [protag]."
    new "You can count on us, [protag].\n你可以信赖我们，[protag]。"

    old "I scan the faces in the group, searching for any look of hesitation or questioning. But all I see are expressions of hardened resolve."
    new "I scan the faces in the group, searching for any look of hesitation or questioning. But all I see are expressions of hardened resolve.\n我扫视着队伍里的每一张脸，想找出一丝犹豫或质疑的神色。可映入眼帘的，只有坚毅决绝的表情。"

    old "That means, tomorrow. There's not much time left, so better be sure we're all equipped and well trained."
    new "That means, tomorrow. There's not much time left, so better be sure we're all equipped and well trained.\n也就是说，就在明天了。时间不多了，所以我们最好确保装备齐全、训练有素。"

    old "That means we have [days_left] days left before this happens. We will keep training in the arena and use the funds the Council generously gives you to be the best equipped we can."
    new "That means we have [days_left] days left before this happens. We will keep training in the arena and use the funds the Council generously gives you to be the best equipped we can.\n也就是说，我们还有 [days_left] 天时间。我们会继续在竞技场训练，并利用议会慷慨拨给你的资金，把装备准备到最好。"

    old "Let's all train hard, and do our best, then!"
    new "Let's all train hard, and do our best, then!\n那么，我们大家就刻苦训练，全力以赴吧！"

    old "Yes, and when battle comes, we'll be ready!"
    new "Yes, and when battle comes, we'll be ready!\n对，等到战斗来临，我们一定准备就绪！"

    old "Cheers erupt all around me, and I find myself turning around the circle, seeing smile after smile from the people around me. These certainly don't look like the faces of people about to march into the face of danger. But somehow, I get the feeling that they're up to the task."
    new "Cheers erupt all around me, and I find myself turning around the circle, seeing smile after smile from the people around me. These certainly don't look like the faces of people about to march into the face of danger. But somehow, I get the feeling that they're up to the task.\n欢呼声在我四周爆发，我环视一圈，看到周围的人们一个接一个地露出笑容。这些面孔，怎么看都不像是即将奔赴险境的人。但不知为何，我总觉得他们足以胜任。"

    old "At the very least, I feel reassured of my own leadership capabilities."
    new "At the very least, I feel reassured of my own leadership capabilities.\n至少，我对自己领导能力多了一份信心。"

    old "All right, let's get back to work."
    new "All right, let's get back to work.\n好了，我们回去继续工作吧。"

    old "The crowd disperses, though several members linger around, chattering with each other excitedly."
    new "The crowd disperses, though several members linger around, chattering with each other excitedly.\n人群散开了，不过有几个人还流连在附近，兴奋地互相交谈。"

    old "[protag]. Karen had some things to tell you, but since she was not able to attend this gathering, she would like for you to come to the citadel to meet with her in person."
    new "[protag]. Karen had some things to tell you, but since she was not able to attend this gathering, she would like for you to come to the citadel to meet with her in person.\n[protag]。Karen 有些话要跟你说，但既然她没能出席这次聚会，她希望你能到 Citadel 亲自与她会面。"

    old "Of course, Leena. Thank you for joining us, even if Karen couldn't make it."
    new "Of course, Leena. Thank you for joining us, even if Karen couldn't make it.\n当然，Leena。虽然 Karen 没能来，也谢谢你能加入我们。"

    old "[protag]? I remembered another thing."
    new "[protag]? I remembered another thing.\n[protag]？我又想起一件事。"

    old "I met with an old man, a wizard. Apolimesho was his name, I think. I explained who I am, and he seemed enthusiastic to meet a fellow magic user. He said that he had something to discuss with you as well, whenever you have the chance. But he didn't specifically tell me how to meet with him."
    new "I met with an old man, a wizard. Apolimesho was his name, I think. I explained who I am, and he seemed enthusiastic to meet a fellow magic user. He said that he had something to discuss with you as well, whenever you have the chance. But he didn't specifically tell me how to meet with him.\n我见到了一位老人，一位巫师。我想他叫 Apolimesho。我说明了我的身份，他见我是同道中人，用魔法的人，显得很热切。他说他也有事要和你谈，等你有空的时候。不过他没有具体告诉我该怎么和他见面。"

    old "I think I know where to find him. Thanks, Nuala."
    new "I think I know where to find him. Thanks, Nuala.\n我想我知道去哪儿找他。谢了，Nuala。"

    old "Apolimesho. You summoned me? Has something important come up?"
    new "Apolimesho. You summoned me? Has something important come up?\nApolimesho。你找我有事？出什么要紧事了吗？"

    old "Something important is coming up. I don't think you need me to remind you."
    new "Something important is coming up. I don't think you need me to remind you.\n有要紧事即将到来。我想不用我提醒你吧。"

    old "Yes, the full moon. In three days."
    new "Yes, the full moon. In three days.\n是的，满月。三天之后。"

    old "I think it may be more helpful to think of it as three days. You'll likely want to spend the daylight hours of the third day resting before you assault the castle."
    new "I think it may be more helpful to think of it as three days. You'll likely want to spend the daylight hours of the third day resting before you assault the castle.\n我想，把它想成三天会更实际些。你多半会想利用第三天白天的时光休息，好为攻打城堡养精蓄锐。"

    old "That's right. It's likely to be an incredibly demanding task, and it will be hard enough with a full day of rest going in."
    new "That's right. It's likely to be an incredibly demanding task, and it will be hard enough with a full day of rest going in.\n没错。那很可能是场极度艰巨的任务，就算休整了一整天再上，也够呛。"

    old "Take care not to fatigue yourself too much, [protag]. If you can, I would suggest that you spend the next two days focused on preparations, whatever form they might take. Now may not be the best time to embark on a new quest."
    new "Take care not to fatigue yourself too much, [protag]. If you can, I would suggest that you spend the next two days focused on preparations, whatever form they might take. Now may not be the best time to embark on a new quest.\n注意别把自己弄得太疲惫，[protag]。如果可以，我建议你接下来两天专注于准备工作，无论以何种形式。眼下或许不是开启新任务的最佳时机。"

    old "Are you telling me to stay in the city?"
    new "Are you telling me to stay in the city?\n你是要我待在城里？"

    old "Not at all. Perhaps for you, the best way to prepare is traveling across the lands to attend to some last-minute business. For some, the anxiety of task left undone can distract them from the current course of action. If that would be the case for you, then by all means, take the time to wrap up that business. But..."
    new "Not at all. Perhaps for you, the best way to prepare is traveling across the lands to attend to some last-minute business. For some, the anxiety of task left undone can distract them from the current course of action. If that would be the case for you, then by all means, take the time to wrap up that business. But...\n完全不是。也许对你来说，最好的准备方式就是走遍各地，去处理一些临行前的琐事。对有些人而言，未了之事的焦虑会让他们无法专注于眼下的行动。如果你正是如此，那就尽管花时间去了结那些事。不过……"

    old "Just be ready. Two more days of preparation, after that, you should stay in Grimoire and rest for the invasion of Castle N'Mar."
    new "Just be ready. Two more days of preparation, after that, you should stay in Grimoire and rest for the invasion of Castle N'Mar.\n一定要做好准备。再准备两天，之后你就该待在 Grimoire 休整，为进攻 N'Mar 城堡养精蓄锐。"

    old "Thank you for the advice, Apolimesho. With so many tasks and people competing for my attention, it's good to have you here to keep me centered on what is truly important."
    new "Thank you for the advice, Apolimesho. With so many tasks and people competing for my attention, it's good to have you here to keep me centered on what is truly important.\n谢谢你的建议，Apolimesho。有这么多任务和人在争夺我的注意力，有你在身边提醒我聚焦真正重要的事，真是太好了。"

    old "Apolimesho takes a bow."
    new "Apolimesho takes a bow.\nApolimesho 鞠了一躬。"

    old "Oh. One more thing you might find helpful. I've convinced the council to offer you a small collection of supplies."
    new "Oh. One more thing you might find helpful. I've convinced the council to offer you a small collection of supplies.\n哦。还有件事或许对你有用。我已经说服议会，给你提供一小批补给。"

    old "Supplies?"
    new "Supplies?\n补给？"

    old "Some potions, medicines, other items that might prove useful on the night of your invasion. You may wish to supplement it with some additional supplies of your own, which I suggest you procure over the next two days. Also, a personal gift from me."
    new "Some potions, medicines, other items that might prove useful on the night of your invasion. You may wish to supplement it with some additional supplies of your own, which I suggest you procure over the next two days. Also, a personal gift from me.\n一些药剂、药品，以及其他在你进攻当晚可能派上用场的物品。你或许还想自己再添置些补给，我建议你在接下来两天内去置办。另外，还有我个人的一份礼物。"

    old "Apolimesho hands me a small leather-bound book."
    new "Apolimesho hands me a small leather-bound book.\nApolimesho 递给我一本用皮革装订的小书。"

    old "A tome of knowledge. I've...tried to collect some of my experience in this book. It's imbued with a small amount of my power. Give it to an ally who you think might benefit from the experience."
    new "A tome of knowledge. I've...tried to collect some of my experience in this book. It's imbued with a small amount of my power. Give it to an ally who you think might benefit from the experience.\n一本知识之书。我……试着把自己的一些经验汇集在了这本书里。它蕴含着我少量的力量。把它交给你认为能从中获益的同伴吧。"

    old "I'll have to pass it around to everyone to read, then."
    new "I'll have to pass it around to everyone to read, then.\n那我得把它传给大家轮流读一读了。"

    old "It's...not that kind of book. It's a magical tome, the kind that is consumed upon use. A one-use item, granting the user a small but permanent boost to their abilities."
    new "It's...not that kind of book. It's a magical tome, the kind that is consumed upon use. A one-use item, granting the user a small but permanent boost to their abilities.\n这……不是那种书。这是一本魔法典籍，使用后即会消耗的那种。属于一次性物品，能为使用者带来小幅但永久的能力提升。"

    old "Who do you suggest I use it on, then?"
    new "Who do you suggest I use it on, then?\n那你建议我用在谁身上？"

    old "You might give it to one of your strongest followers, to further augment their strength. Or perhaps you could take the opposite tack, and give it to one of your weaker followers, to allow them to catch up to their more advanced peers."
    new "You might give it to one of your strongest followers, to further augment their strength. Or perhaps you could take the opposite tack, and give it to one of your weaker followers, to allow them to catch up to their more advanced peers.\n你可以把它交给你最强的追随者之一，进一步增强他们的实力。或者，你也可以反其道而行之，把它交给较弱的追随者，让他们追赶上更强的同伴。"

    old "Just don't get paralyzed by indecision. An item like this is no good if it simply sits in your bag, unused."
    new "Just don't get paralyzed by indecision. An item like this is no good if it simply sits in your bag, unused.\n只是别因犹豫不决而裹足不前。这样的东西若只是闲置在你的背包里，就毫无用处了。"

    old "Good idea, Apolimesho. This is a valuable item indeed, and I'll be sure to make good use of it before heading off to N'Mar."
    new "Good idea, Apolimesho. This is a valuable item indeed, and I'll be sure to make good use of it before heading off to N'Mar.\n好主意，Apolimesho。这确实是件宝贵的物品，我会在动身去 N'Mar 之前好好利用它的。"

    old "I'll meet you at the outskirts of Grimoire on the night of the full moon."
    new "I'll meet you at the outskirts of Grimoire on the night of the full moon.\n满月之夜，我们就在 Grimoire 的郊外碰头。"

    old "Apolimesho. I suppose you want to talk about the other tasks the council has for me?"
    new "Apolimesho. I suppose you want to talk about the other tasks the council has for me?\nApolimesho。我想，你是要和我谈议会交给我的其他任务吧？"

    old "Indeed. As you know, the undead forces are planning an attack on Grimoire. They seem to be marching straight towards our city, ignoring the other towns nearby."
    new "Indeed. As you know, the undead forces are planning an attack on Grimoire. They seem to be marching straight towards our city, ignoring the other towns nearby.\n正是。如你所知，亡灵大军正计划进攻 Grimoire。他们似乎直奔我们的城市而来，全然无视附近的其他城镇。"

    old "I had wondered why the attack seemed to be targeting Grimoire exclusively. Cities like Lothark and Horus could make for closer targets, if they're launching an attack from the castle."
    new "I had wondered why the attack seemed to be targeting Grimoire exclusively. Cities like Lothark and Horus could make for closer targets, if they're launching an attack from the castle.\n我先前还在纳闷，为什么这次进攻似乎专挑 Grimoire。如果是从城堡发起进攻，像 Lothark 和 Horus 这样的城市其实更近。"

    old "This is an attack that seems to have a great deal of planning and forethought behind it. It would be a mistake that just because our enemies are undead there can't be smart leaders behind them. Grimoire is the Empire's capital city, where decisions are made, so it comes as no surprise that they would launch an attack here."
    new "This is an attack that seems to have a great deal of planning and forethought behind it. It would be a mistake that just because our enemies are undead there can't be smart leaders behind them. Grimoire is the Empire's capital city, where decisions are made, so it comes as no surprise that they would launch an attack here.\n这次进攻背后似乎经过了周密的筹划和深思。若因为敌人是亡灵，就以为他们背后没有聪明的首领，那就大错特错了。Grimoire 是帝国的都城，是做出决策的地方，所以他们选择在这里发动进攻，一点也不意外。"

    old "Ah, so it's a decapitation campaign, then? They wish to strike the Empire right at the heart of its leadership?"
    new "Ah, so it's a decapitation campaign, then? They wish to strike the Empire right at the heart of its leadership?\n啊，这么说来，这是一场斩首行动？他们想直捣帝国领导层的核心？"

    old "There is that. As the capital, a successful attack on Grimoire would also be tremendously demoralizing for the rest of the Empire. Even if we did manage to evacuate the council, seeing the city of Grimoire fall before our enemies would be a great loss."
    new "There is that. As the capital, a successful attack on Grimoire would also be tremendously demoralizing for the rest of the Empire. Even if we did manage to evacuate the council, seeing the city of Grimoire fall before our enemies would be a great loss.\n有这层意思。作为都城，若对 Grimoire 的进攻得手，也会极大地挫伤帝国其余部分的士气。即便我们能设法疏散议会，眼睁睁看着 Grimoire 城在敌人面前陷落，仍会是一大损失。"

    old "Losing any city this size would be a great loss, but I see your point."
    new "Losing any city this size would be a great loss, but I see your point.\n失去任何一座这种规模的城市都是巨大损失，不过我明白你的意思。"

    old "Indeed. An attack this well-planned will surely have a lot of resources behind it."
    new "Indeed. An attack this well-planned will surely have a lot of resources behind it.\n确实。谋划得如此周密的进攻，背后必定动用了大量资源。"

    old "Just how massive do you expect this attack to be?"
    new "Just how massive do you expect this attack to be?\n你预计这次进攻规模会有多大？"

    old "Big enough that the Empire wants to have all of the help that it can get."
    new "Big enough that the Empire wants to have all of the help that it can get.\n大到帝国希望能集齐所有能争取到的援助。"

    old "I'm already fully committed to assisting with this defense."
    new "I'm already fully committed to assisting with this defense.\n我已经全身心投入协助这次防御了。"

    old "That's encouraging to hear, and you and your cohorts will no doubt play a vital role in defending the city gates. However, I wasn't talking about you, specifically. I was actually speaking about help from our neighbors."
    new "That's encouraging to hear, and you and your cohorts will no doubt play a vital role in defending the city gates. However, I wasn't talking about you, specifically. I was actually speaking about help from our neighbors.\n听到这个很令人鼓舞，你和你的伙伴们无疑将在守卫城门中发挥重要作用。不过，我指的并不是你们，具体来说，我说的是来自我们邻邦的援助。"

    old "Our neighbors?"
    new "Our neighbors?\n我们的邻邦？"

    old "Specifically, the dwarves and elves."
    new "Specifically, the dwarves and elves.\n具体来说，是 Dwarf 和 Elf。"

    old "They're not involved in this conflict, are they?"
    new "They're not involved in this conflict, are they?\n他们并没有卷入这场冲突吧？"

    old "No, but we're looking to change that. The Empire is on good terms with the dwarves, but they still haven't committed themselves fully to this battle. We could certainly use their help, not in defending Grimoire, but in cutting back the enemy line."
    new "No, but we're looking to change that. The Empire is on good terms with the dwarves, but they still haven't committed themselves fully to this battle. We could certainly use their help, not in defending Grimoire, but in cutting back the enemy line.\n没有，但我们正想改变这一点。帝国与 Dwarf 关系良好，但他们仍未全身心投入这场战斗。我们当然用得上他们的帮助——不是守卫 Grimoire，而是切断敌人的退路。"

    old "When the undead arrive on next fullmoon, if all goes well, we'll manage to repeal their assault. But they can always retreat and go back. Now, imagine if there was a dwarven army behind them, which would eliminate all retreating enemies."
    new "When the undead arrive on next fullmoon, if all goes well, we'll manage to repeal their assault. But they can always retreat and go back. Now, imagine if there was a dwarven army behind them, which would eliminate all retreating enemies.\n当亡灵在下个满月来袭时，如果一切顺利，我们能击退他们的攻势。但他们随时可以撤退回去。现在，想象一下，如果他们身后有一支 Dwarf 大军，就能把撤退的敌人全部歼灭。"

    old "It would be a massacre."
    new "It would be a massacre.\n那会是一场屠杀。"

    old "It would. And it wouldn't even be as difficult as fighting enemies at full strength."
    new "It would. And it wouldn't even be as difficult as fighting enemies at full strength.\n确实如此。而且那甚至比跟全盛状态的敌人交手要容易得多。"

    old "A prime moment for a decisive strike. Surely the dwarves could be persuaded to participate? I'm sure that Galan would jump at the opportunity to be part of such an attack."
    new "A prime moment for a decisive strike. Surely the dwarves could be persuaded to participate? I'm sure that Galan would jump at the opportunity to be part of such an attack.\n那正是发起决定性打击的绝佳时机。想必能说服 Dwarf 参战吧？我敢肯定，Galan 会抓住机会加入这样一场进攻。"

    old "The dwarves have expressed that they would like to assist in our efforts against the undead, and we have no reason to doubt their sincerity. Unfortunately, their resources are spread a bit thin at the moment."
    new "The dwarves have expressed that they would like to assist in our efforts against the undead, and we have no reason to doubt their sincerity. Unfortunately, their resources are spread a bit thin at the moment.\nDwarf 们已经表示愿意协助我们对抗亡灵，我们也没有理由怀疑他们的诚意。可惜，他们目前资源有些吃紧。"

    old "Ah, they have problems of their own to deal with?"
    new "Ah, they have problems of their own to deal with?\n啊，他们也有自己的麻烦要处理？"

    old "Yes. Goblins have taken over an important ore mine near Hammerhands. That has hampered their production of weapon and armor, which has in turn affected their combat readiness. They're in the process of dealing with the goblin situation, but if you could give them a hand..."
    new "Yes. Goblins have taken over an important ore mine near Hammerhands. That has hampered their production of weapon and armor, which has in turn affected their combat readiness. They're in the process of dealing with the goblin situation, but if you could give them a hand...\n是的。Goblin 占据了 Hammerhands 附近一座重要的铁矿。这妨碍了他们生产武器和盔甲，进而影响了他们的战备。他们正在处理 Goblin 的事，但如果你能帮上一把……"

    old "I understand. It would be also a sign of goodwill from the Council."
    new "I understand. It would be also a sign of goodwill from the Council.\n我明白了。这也算是议会释放善意的一种表示。"

    old "Exactly. They'd appreciate the help and would surely do their best to support us in the coming battle."
    new "Exactly. They'd appreciate the help and would surely do their best to support us in the coming battle.\n正是。他们会感激这份帮助，也一定会在即将到来的战斗中尽力支持我们。"

    old "I will travel to Hammerhands immediately then."
    new "I will travel to Hammerhands immediately then.\n那我立刻动身去 Hammerhands。"

    old "Wait, not so fast. There are also the elves. As you know, the relationship between humans and elves is not really good. After the Five Hundred Years War, we're now at peace, but it's a very fragile peace."
    new "Wait, not so fast. There are also the elves. As you know, the relationship between humans and elves is not really good. After the Five Hundred Years War, we're now at peace, but it's a very fragile peace.\n等等，先别急。还有 Elf。如你所知，人类与 Elf 的关系并不好。五百年战争之后，我们现在虽然处于和平，但那和平极其脆弱。"

    old "When a war lasts for so many generations, it can take time for wounds to heal."
    new "When a war lasts for so many generations, it can take time for wounds to heal.\n一场延续了这么多代人的战争，其创伤需要时间才能愈合。"

    old "In this case, we cannot hope for any direct help from them, even if I know many elven warriors would like to support us."
    new "In this case, we cannot hope for any direct help from them, even if I know many elven warriors would like to support us.\n在此事上，我们不能指望他们提供任何直接援助，尽管我知道许多 Elf 战士愿意支持我们。"

    old "That's unfortunate."
    new "That's unfortunate.\n那真遗憾。"

    old "Even more unfortunate is the fact that some elves might take advantage of us in our weakened state as we fight the undead."
    new "Even more unfortunate is the fact that some elves might take advantage of us in our weakened state as we fight the undead.\n更遗憾的是，有些 Elf 可能会趁我们与亡灵作战、实力削弱之际，对我们趁虚而入。"

    old "I'm sorry, I'm not sure I understand. Are you saying that the elves might break the peace treaty and stab us in the back?"
    new "I'm sorry, I'm not sure I understand. Are you saying that the elves might break the peace treaty and stab us in the back?\n抱歉，我不太确定我是否理解。你是说，Elf 可能会撕毁和平条约，从背后捅我们一刀？"

    old "It's a fear that has circulated throughout the council ever since our first encounter with the vampires."
    new "It's a fear that has circulated throughout the council ever since our first encounter with the vampires.\n自从我们第一次遭遇吸血鬼以来，这种忧虑就在议会里流传开了。"

    old "So it's all rumors at this point?"
    new "So it's all rumors at this point?\n那么，目前这都还只是传闻？"

    old "Those suspicions are not without credibility, I'm afraid. While I'm sure that many elves have no desire to go to war with us, there are many in the ranks of their leadership that bear resentment over the old conflict. There is always the risk of them seizing the opportunity to attack us."
    new "Those suspicions are not without credibility, I'm afraid. While I'm sure that many elves have no desire to go to war with us, there are many in the ranks of their leadership that bear resentment over the old conflict. There is always the risk of them seizing the opportunity to attack us.\n恐怕这些猜疑并非没有依据。虽然我确信许多 Elf 并无与我们开战的意愿，但他们的领导层中有不少人对昔日的冲突怀恨在心。始终存在着他们抓住机会攻打我们的风险。"

    old "You really think this could happen?"
    new "You really think this could happen?\n你真觉得这会发生吗？"

    old "From a political standpoint? There's no way to be certain. From a logistical standpoint? It's more than possible. They could move their armies near the border, wait until the battle with the undead is over, and then attack our exhausted armies."
    new "From a political standpoint? There's no way to be certain. From a logistical standpoint? It's more than possible. They could move their armies near the border, wait until the battle with the undead is over, and then attack our exhausted armies.\n从政治角度看？无法确定。从军事后勤角度看？完全有可能。他们可以把军队调到边境附近，等与亡灵的战斗结束，再进攻我们筋疲力尽的军队。"

    old "Sounds really terrible and treacherous. I can't believe elves would do that."
    new "Sounds really terrible and treacherous. I can't believe elves would do that.\n听起来又可怕又背信弃义。我真不敢相信 Elf 会做出这种事。"

    old "Then you need to study history of the Five Hundred Years war more closely. You said it yourself: the wounds of a conflict that lasted for generations do not heal so quickly. The elder druids are the older elves and they still remember the atrocities of that war. The younger generation of elves are more neutral or even friendly towards us. Sadly, the elders are in charge."
    new "Then you need to study history of the Five Hundred Years war more closely. You said it yourself: the wounds of a conflict that lasted for generations do not heal so quickly. The elder druids are the older elves and they still remember the atrocities of that war. The younger generation of elves are more neutral or even friendly towards us. Sadly, the elders are in charge.\n那你需要更仔细地研究五百年战争的历史。你自己也说过：延续了几代人的冲突，其创伤不会那么快愈合。那些年长的德鲁伊都是上了年纪的 Elf，他们仍记得那场战争中的暴行。年轻一代的 Elf 对我们更中立，甚至友好。可惜，掌权的是老一辈。"

    old "I'm sorry, I can't believe that the elves would attack us."
    new "I'm sorry, I can't believe that the elves would attack us.\n抱歉，我还是不敢相信 Elf 会攻击我们。"

    old "Apolimesho lowers his voice and speaks with a serious expression."
    new "Apolimesho lowers his voice and speaks with a serious expression.\nApolimesho 压低声音，神情严肃地说。"

    old "[protag], the council has ways of knowing things far beyond what you could understand. That is all I can say for now."
    new "[protag], the council has ways of knowing things far beyond what you could understand. That is all I can say for now.\n[protag]，议会有办法知晓远超你所能理解的事。目前我只能说这么多。"

    old "Ah, so your suspicions aren't all based on intuition and rumors."
    new "Ah, so your suspicions aren't all based on intuition and rumors.\n啊，所以你们的怀疑并不全凭直觉和传闻。"

    old "You put me in an awkward position when you speak about things directly like this."
    new "You put me in an awkward position when you speak about things directly like this.\n你这样直言不讳，让我处境很尴尬。"

    old "Yes, I understand that the Grimoire council can neither confirm nor deny that they have spies who are sending reports about the elves senior leadership. But you have made your point. The council certainly knows more than I do about how much of a threat they are."
    new "Yes, I understand that the Grimoire council can neither confirm nor deny that they have spies who are sending reports about the elves senior leadership. But you have made your point. The council certainly knows more than I do about how much of a threat they are.\n是的，我明白 Grimoire 议会既不能确认也不能否认，他们是否派有间谍在汇报 Elf 高层领导的情况。不过你已经把意思说清楚了。议会对于他们的威胁程度，肯定比我了解得更多。"

    old "It sounds like you and the council are privy to information that I am not."
    new "It sounds like you and the council are privy to information that I am not.\n听起来，你和议会掌握着我不了解的情报。"

    old "It is the council's job to know such things, [protag]."
    new "It is the council's job to know such things, [protag].\n了解这些事，正是议会的职责所在，[protag]。"

    old "Even if it means having spies?"
    new "Even if it means having spies?\n即便这意味着安插间谍？"

    old "Having spies to report on the elves leadership is the sort of thing that a large nation might engage in. I won't say anything further than that."
    new "Having spies to report on the elves leadership is the sort of thing that a large nation might engage in. I won't say anything further than that.\n派间谍监视 Elf 领导层，是一个大国可能去做的事。除此之外，我不会再多说。"

    old "Well, the point is that you clearly know more than I do. I'll trust the council's judgment, then."
    new "Well, the point is that you clearly know more than I do. I'll trust the council's judgment, then.\n好吧，重点是，你显然知道得比我多。那我就相信议会的判断。"

    old "I've said all that I'm going to say. However, I can't stop you from speculating."
    new "I've said all that I'm going to say. However, I can't stop you from speculating.\n我要说的已经说完了。不过，我也拦不住你去揣测。"

    old "Still...if the council is truly spying on the elves..."
    new "Still...if the council is truly spying on the elves...\n可是……如果议会真的在监视 Elf……"

    old "I suppose it's a necessary step to ensure the protection of the Empire. The fact that you've apparently uncovered murmurs about some potential conspiracy against Grimoire are evidence of that enough."
    new "I suppose it's a necessary step to ensure the protection of the Empire. The fact that you've apparently uncovered murmurs about some potential conspiracy against Grimoire are evidence of that enough.\n我想，这是确保帝国安全所必需的一步。你显然已经听闻了些许关于针对 Grimoire 潜在阴谋的风声，这本身就足以说明问题。"

    old "The council is responsible for ensuring the safety of the Empire's inhabitants. In a way, I suppose they have a moral responsibility to ensure that they have eyes and ears open wherever they can, listening for the rumblings of any possible threat."
    new "The council is responsible for ensuring the safety of the Empire's inhabitants. In a way, I suppose they have a moral responsibility to ensure that they have eyes and ears open wherever they can, listening for the rumblings of any possible threat.\n议会负责保障帝国居民的安全。从某种意义上说，我想他们在道义上有责任尽可能睁大眼睛、竖起耳朵，倾听任何可能威胁的动静。"

    old "This sort of distrust between the Empire and the elves is a big part of the reason the Five Hundred Years War lasted so long, isn't it? When you sign a peace treaty and then spy on them, it calls the nature of the peace treaty into question."
    new "This sort of distrust between the Empire and the elves is a big part of the reason the Five Hundred Years War lasted so long, isn't it? When you sign a peace treaty and then spy on them, it calls the nature of the peace treaty into question.\n帝国与 Elf 之间的这种猜忌，正是五百年战争延续那么久的一大原因，不是吗？签了和平条约，却又去监视对方，这难免让人对条约的性质产生疑问。"

    old "It makes me wonder if perhaps the elves are spying on the council in the same way. Surely the thought has occurred to you, Apolimesho."
    new "It makes me wonder if perhaps the elves are spying on the council in the same way. Surely the thought has occurred to you, Apolimesho.\n这让我不禁想，或许 Elf 也在以同样的方式监视议会。这个念头你一定也想过吧，Apolimesho。"

    old "As I said, I'm not going to comment further."
    new "As I said, I'm not going to comment further.\n如我所说，我不打算再作评论。"

    old "Are you done speculating about how the council obtains privileged information?"
    new "Are you done speculating about how the council obtains privileged information?\n关于议会如何获取机密情报的猜测，你说完了吗？"

    old "I am."
    new "I am.\n说完了。"

    old "I apologize if I come across as curt. To be honest, most of the questions you might have regarding the council's inner workings are mysteries to me as well. There are things known only to the council's most senior members."
    new "I apologize if I come across as curt. To be honest, most of the questions you might have regarding the council's inner workings are mysteries to me as well. There are things known only to the council's most senior members.\n如果我显得无礼，还请见谅。老实说，你关于议会内部运作的大多数疑问，对我来说同样是个谜。有些事情只有议会最高层的成员才知道。"

    old "If you think that I am personally withholding information from you, you can take some solace in knowing that I'm just as ignorant as you are when it comes to how business is conducted. We could spend all day speculating, but I'd rather focus on the information that has been made available to us."
    new "If you think that I am personally withholding information from you, you can take some solace in knowing that I'm just as ignorant as you are when it comes to how business is conducted. We could spend all day speculating, but I'd rather focus on the information that has been made available to us.\n如果你以为是我个人对你隐瞒信息，那你可以宽心些——论及这些事务是如何进行的，我和你一样无知。我们可以整天猜来猜去，但我更愿意专注于已经摆到我们面前的信息。"

    old "Such as...?"
    new "Such as...?\n比如……？"

    old "Several tribes of dark elves have become increasingly bold in raiding against the elven settlements near the desert. Though several efforts have been made to stamp them down, the dark elves seem to be growing in number."
    new "Several tribes of dark elves have become increasingly bold in raiding against the elven settlements near the desert. Though several efforts have been made to stamp them down, the dark elves seem to be growing in number.\n有好几个 Dark Elf 部落在袭击沙漠附近 Elf 聚居点时，变得越来越猖狂。尽管人们多次努力镇压，Dark Elf 的数量似乎仍在增长。"

    old "Sounds like quite a handful."
    new "Sounds like quite a handful.\n听起来够棘手的。"

    old "This goes beyond simply being a 'handful.' These dark elf bandits often don't settle for simply stealing property. Lives are in danger."
    new "This goes beyond simply being a 'handful.' These dark elf bandits often don't settle for simply stealing property. Lives are in danger.\n这可不只是“棘手”而已。这些 Dark Elf 强盗往往不满足于劫掠财物。那是要出人命的。"

    old "Why is this relevant to us? We just got discussing the fact that some elder druids have their sights set on an invasion of the Empire."
    new "Why is this relevant to us? We just got discussing the fact that some elder druids have their sights set on an invasion of the Empire.\n这和我们有什么关系？我们刚刚还在讨论有些年长德鲁伊盯上了入侵帝国这件事。"

    old "The elder druids are only dangerous to the extent that they're able to convince their people to go to war with us. If we help the elves to defeat the dark elves bandits, then it would be hard for the elder druids to convince the elf population that attacking us when we are weak is a good thing."
    new "The elder druids are only dangerous to the extent that they're able to convince their people to go to war with us. If we help the elves to defeat the dark elves bandits, then it would be hard for the elder druids to convince the elf population that attacking us when we are weak is a good thing.\n年长德鲁伊的危险程度，仅仅取决于他们能否说服族人跟我们开战。如果我们帮助 Elf 击败 Dark Elf 强盗，那么年长德鲁伊就很难再向 Elf 民众鼓吹，趁我们虚弱时攻打我们是件好事。"

    old "Ah, a bit of a public relations campaign."
    new "Ah, a bit of a public relations campaign.\n啊，算是场公关活动。"

    old "Defeating the dark elves would benefit us in two ways: the more obvious way is that by doing favors for the elves, we decrease anti-Empire sentiment, especially among those who live on the borderlands."
    new "Defeating the dark elves would benefit us in two ways: the more obvious way is that by doing favors for the elves, we decrease anti-Empire sentiment, especially among those who live on the borderlands.\n击败 Dark Elf 会给我们带来两方面好处：比较显而易见的一点是，向 Elf 施以恩惠，能减少反帝国的情绪，尤其是在边境地区居民当中。"

    old "The other benefit is that putting down the dark elves would be a show of strength: the elves would not be so willing to go to war with us after that kind of demonstration of power."
    new "The other benefit is that putting down the dark elves would be a show of strength: the elves would not be so willing to go to war with us after that kind of demonstration of power.\n另一个好处是，镇压 Dark Elf 是一种实力的展示：在见识过这番武力之后，Elf 就不会那么轻易与我们开战了。"

    old "Interesting. One part compassion, one part intimidation."
    new "Interesting. One part compassion, one part intimidation.\n有意思。一半是同情，一半是威慑。"

    old "It does seem like a cynical way of looking at things, but yes, that is what it ultimately boils down to."
    new "It does seem like a cynical way of looking at things, but yes, that is what it ultimately boils down to.\n这样看待事情确实显得很功利，但没错，归根结底就是这么回事。"

    old "All right. I'll keep those two tasks in mind. Help the dwarves with the goblins, and make sure the elves don't plan on backstabbing us."
    new "All right. I'll keep those two tasks in mind. Help the dwarves with the goblins, and make sure the elves don't plan on backstabbing us.\n好，我会把这两项任务记在心里。帮 Dwarf 对付 Goblin，再确保 Elf 不打算在背后捅我们刀子。"

    old "Remember though, that training yourself and your team to defend Grimoire will be the priority. If you haven't finished doing those tasks by day 50, then don't worry too much about the dwarves and elves. The Council doesn't want you to be distracted from your main goal. So keep this in mind, [protag]."
    new "Remember though, that training yourself and your team to defend Grimoire will be the priority. If you haven't finished doing those tasks by day 50, then don't worry too much about the dwarves and elves. The Council doesn't want you to be distracted from your main goal. So keep this in mind, [protag].\n不过要记住，训练你自己和你的团队以保卫 Grimoire，才是重中之重。如果到第 50 天你还没完成那些任务，也不必太为 Dwarf 和 Elf 的事操心。议会不想让你偏离主要目标。所以要记住这一点，[protag]。"

    old "Finish those two tasks before day 50, but building up a good relationship with my team and training has the priority. Got it."
    new "Finish those two tasks before day 50, but building up a good relationship with my team and training has the priority. Got it.\n在第 50 天前完成那两项任务，但优先的还是和团队搞好关系并加强训练。明白了。"

    old "May Tayrion guide you, [protag]."
    new "May Tayrion guide you, [protag].\n愿 Tayrion 指引你，[protag]。"

    old "We reach the mine's entrance. The mine's interior is dark, and full of rocks and corners: a perfect place for an ambush."
    new "We reach the mine's entrance. The mine's interior is dark, and full of rocks and corners: a perfect place for an ambush.\n我们来到矿井入口。矿井内部一片漆黑，满是岩石和拐角，正是伏击的绝佳场所。"

    old "Let's proceed with caution. We don't know how many goblins are there inside, nor what kind of enemies they are."
    new "Let's proceed with caution. We don't know how many goblins are there inside, nor what kind of enemies they are.\n我们小心前进吧。我们不知道里面有多少 Goblin，也不知道他们是什么样的敌人。"

    old "I suppose most of them will be scouts and thieves. We're unlikely to encounter any wolf raiders; there wouldn't be enough space in there for them to take advantage of their abilities."
    new "I suppose most of them will be scouts and thieves. We're unlikely to encounter any wolf raiders; there wouldn't be enough space in there for them to take advantage of their abilities.\n我想他们大多是侦察兵和盗贼。我们不太可能遇到骑狼的劫掠者，里面没有足够的空间让他们发挥本领。"

    old "Spellscasters might still be able to position themselves on some higher rocks and still strike from distance. Remember that goblins are much shorter and agile than other races."
    new "Spellscasters might still be able to position themselves on some higher rocks and still strike from distance. Remember that goblins are much shorter and agile than other races.\n施法者或许仍能占据一些高处岩石，从远处发起攻击。记住，Goblin 比其他种族矮小得多，也灵活得多。"

    old "We enter the mines, and shortly after we're inside, we encounter the first group of goblins."
    new "We enter the mines, and shortly after we're inside, we encounter the first group of goblins.\n我们进入矿井，进去后没多久，就遇到了第一批 Goblin。"

    old "Damn. Those goblins are weak as individuals, but they make up for it with their numbers."
    new "Damn. Those goblins are weak as individuals, but they make up for it with their numbers.\n该死。这些 Goblin 单个很弱，但数量弥补了这一点。"

    old "Let's keep going."
    new "Let's keep going.\n我们继续前进。"

    old "We move forward, and we spot a big open space in the mine. Seems something artificial, it's unusually big for a mine."
    new "We move forward, and we spot a big open space in the mine. Seems something artificial, it's unusually big for a mine.\n我们向前走，在矿井里发现一片很大的空旷地带。看起来像是人工开凿的，对一座矿井来说，大得出奇。"

    old "I don't like this. Team, let's split up. Half with me, the other half stay here. It could be an ambush."
    new "I don't like this. Team, let's split up. Half with me, the other half stay here. It could be an ambush.\n我不喜欢这样。各位，我们分开行动。一半跟我走，另一半留在这里。这可能是埋伏。"

    old "I move forward with my group, and after a few meter, we see several goblins coming out from all around us."
    new "I move forward with my group, and after a few meter, we see several goblins coming out from all around us.\n我带着我这组人向前推进，走了几米后，就看到好几只 Goblin 从四面八方冒了出来。"

    old "Watch out! Goblins! We're surrounded!"
    new "Watch out! Goblins! We're surrounded!\n小心！Goblin！我们被包围了！"

    old "One of them, a wizard, shows up and starts to speak."
    new "One of them, a wizard, shows up and starts to speak.\n其中一个是巫师，他现身开口说话。"

    old "What we have here. Hihihi. Fresh meat to play with. I am Grob, pleased to meet you."
    new "What we have here. Hihihi. Fresh meat to play with. I am Grob, pleased to meet you.\n看看我们这儿来了什么。嘻嘻嘻。新鲜的肉，可以好好玩一玩了。我是 Grob，幸会幸会。"

    old "You're the leader of the goblins that are infesting the mine?"
    new "You're the leader of the goblins that are infesting the mine?\n你就是那群霸占这座矿井的 Goblin 的首领？"

    old "Infesting! Such a nice word. Thank you."
    new "Infesting! Such a nice word. Thank you.\n霸占！这个词用得真好。谢谢。"

    old "This goblin is different from the others. He's definitely the leader here. But he also sounds pretty clever and dangerous."
    new "This goblin is different from the others. He's definitely the leader here. But he also sounds pretty clever and dangerous.\n这只 Goblin 与众不同。他无疑就是这里的头目。不过，他听起来也相当狡猾而危险。"

    old "Any last words before I dispose of you, miserable [prace] [manwoman]?"
    new "Any last words before I dispose of you, miserable [prace] [manwoman]?\n在我收拾掉你之前，还有什么遗言吗，可悲的 [prace] [manwoman]？"

    old "Wait. Do you know who I am?"
    new "Wait. Do you know who I am?\n等等。你知道我是谁吗？"

    old "I've never seen your face before, so I don't see how I could know who you are."
    new "I've never seen your face before, so I don't see how I could know who you are.\n我从没见过你这张脸，所以实在看不出我怎么会认识你。"

    old "Perhaps you'll know me by my name, then. I'm [protag]."
    new "Perhaps you'll know me by my name, then. I'm [protag].\n那也许你会听过我的名字。我是 [protag]。"

    old "[protag], eh? I don't know of many people by that name, unless you're the Envoy of Grimoire. But what would the Envoy of Grimoire be doing in a place like this? This is dwarven territory. I can understand why dwarves would want to come at me with weapons, but not you. Shouldn't you be back in the Empire?"
    new "[protag], eh? I don't know of many people by that name, unless you're the Envoy of Grimoire. But what would the Envoy of Grimoire be doing in a place like this? This is dwarven territory. I can understand why dwarves would want to come at me with weapons, but not you. Shouldn't you be back in the Empire?\n[protag]，嗯？叫这个名字的人我可没听说过几个，除非你是 Grimoire 的特使。可 Grimoire 的特使到这种地方来做什么？这里可是 Dwarf 的地盘。Dwarf 想提着武器来找我，我还能理解，但你……你难道不该回帝国去吗？"

    old "Think about what the word Envoy means, Grob. I represent the Human Empire outside of its borders, and the dwarves happen to be our allies."
    new "Think about what the word Envoy means, Grob. I represent the Human Empire outside of its borders, and the dwarves happen to be our allies.\n想想“特使”这个词的意思吧，Grob。我代表的是人类帝国，在其疆界之外行事，而 Dwarf 恰好是我们的盟友。"

    old "Ohho. I suppose the dwarves told you all about how they've been hunting goblins since The Old Age, then? Well, now is our time to fight back. We goblins are going to take back what is rightfully ours, and this mine seems like a good place to start."
    new "Ohho. I suppose the dwarves told you all about how they've been hunting goblins since The Old Age, then? Well, now is our time to fight back. We goblins are going to take back what is rightfully ours, and this mine seems like a good place to start.\n哦嗬。那我猜，Dwarf 一定跟你说了，他们从远古时代起就一直在猎杀 Goblin 吧？哼，现在轮到我们反击了。我们 Goblin 要夺回本就属于我们的东西，而这座矿井，就是个不错的起点。"

    old "Interesting. When I heard that goblins had taken over the mine, I assumed they were driven purely by greed, but perhaps this Grog has other motivations beyond greed."
    new "Interesting. When I heard that goblins had taken over the mine, I assumed they were driven purely by greed, but perhaps this Grog has other motivations beyond greed.\n有意思。当我听说 Goblin 占领了矿井时，原以为他们纯粹是受贪婪驱使，但也许这个 Grob 还有贪婪之外的动机。"

    old "These goblins have to be dealt with, and violence may be all that they understand. But perhaps this Grob can be persuaded to let his guard down..."
    new "These goblins have to be dealt with, and violence may be all that they understand. But perhaps this Grob can be persuaded to let his guard down...\n这些 Goblin 必须被解决，而暴力也许就是他们唯一能听懂的语言。但或许，这个 Grob 能被说服，放松警惕……"

    old "Isn't a bit humid and dark inside here?"
    new "Isn't a bit humid and dark inside here?\n这里面是不是有点潮湿，又黑？"

    old "Doesn't matter! Dwarves hunted goblins for years. Now, we take their most precious mine! Now, dwarves are furious and us goblins are happy!"
    new "Doesn't matter! Dwarves hunted goblins for years. Now, we take their most precious mine! Now, dwarves are furious and us goblins are happy!\n那又怎样！Dwarf 猎杀 Goblin 这么多年。现在，我们夺下了他们最宝贵的矿井！如今 Dwarf 气急败坏，我们 Goblin 乐开了花！"

    old "Good, I'm sure you thought about everything. How to get food and water. How to make your followers happy while you occupy the dark, humid, cold mines."
    new "Good, I'm sure you thought about everything. How to get food and water. How to make your followers happy while you occupy the dark, humid, cold mines.\n很好，我确信你把一切都想好了。怎么弄到食物和水，怎么在你占据这些又黑又潮又冷的矿井时，让你的手下保持开心。"

    old "There's nothing worse for a leader to lose his consensus amongst his men. But that won't be a problem for you, right? After all, I'm sure you've already thought about all of this."
    new "There's nothing worse for a leader to lose his consensus amongst his men. But that won't be a problem for you, right? After all, I'm sure you've already thought about all of this.\n对一位首领来说，没有什么比失去手下的人心更糟糕的了。不过这对你来说不成问题，对吧？毕竟，我确信这些你都早已想过了。"

    old "Let me ask you only a question, Grob. What do you want?"
    new "Let me ask you only a question, Grob. What do you want?\n我只问你一个问题，Grob。你想要什么？"

    old "Right now? Feast on your dead bodies of course."
    new "Right now? Feast on your dead bodies of course.\n现在吗？当然是拿你们的尸体饱餐一顿。"

    old "Come on. If you kill us or not, it won't change your life. What is it that you really want?"
    new "Come on. If you kill us or not, it won't change your life. What is it that you really want?\n得了吧。杀不杀我们，都改变不了你的处境。你真正想要的是什么？"

    old "Power, of course. Who wouldn't want more power?"
    new "Power, of course. Who wouldn't want more power?\n当然是权力。谁不想要更大的权力？"

    old "And how you plan to obtain power by staying inside this mine? I can offer you what you want."
    new "And how you plan to obtain power by staying inside this mine? I can offer you what you want.\n那你打算怎么靠待在这座矿井里获得权力？你想要的东西，我可以给你。"

    old "Grob remains silent, looking at me and my companions and then back to his goblins, like if to assess his chances of victory."
    new "Grob remains silent, looking at me and my companions and then back to his goblins, like if to assess his chances of victory.\nGrob 沉默不语，看看我和我的同伴们，又回头看看他的 Goblin 们，仿佛在评估自己的胜算。"

    old "All right, [prace]. What do you propose?"
    new "All right, [prace]. What do you propose?\n好吧，[prace]。你有什么提议？"

    old "Leave the mines, now. If you do, I promise I'll talk to the Council in Grimoire about your situation. We'll find you and your goblin tribe a better place to live."
    new "Leave the mines, now. If you do, I promise I'll talk to the Council in Grimoire about your situation. We'll find you and your goblin tribe a better place to live.\n现在就离开矿井。如果你照做，我保证会向 Grimoire 的议会说明你们的处境。我们会为你们和你的 Goblin 部落找到一个更好的栖身之地。"

    old "The goblins behind Grob seems more convinced than him about my words. I can tell from Grob's expression that he doesn't like the idea of making a deal, but it doesn't matter: now that his followers have heard my offer, his only options are to accept it, or risk a mutiny."
    new "The goblins behind Grob seems more convinced than him about my words. I can tell from Grob's expression that he doesn't like the idea of making a deal, but it doesn't matter: now that his followers have heard my offer, his only options are to accept it, or risk a mutiny.\nGrob 身后的那些 Goblin 似乎比他更相信我的话。从 Grob 的表情看得出，他不喜欢做交易这个主意，但那已经无关紧要了：既然他的手下都听到了我的提议，他剩下的选择就只有接受，或者冒一场哗变的风险。"

    old "You better keep your word, [protag]."
    new "You better keep your word, [protag].\n你最好信守诺言，[protag]。"

    old "Of course, of course."
    new "Of course, of course.\n当然，当然。"

    old "If you don't hold up your end of the deal, there will be hell to pay. Your name is known farther and wider than you think, and now I know what your face looks like, too."
    new "If you don't hold up your end of the deal, there will be hell to pay. Your name is known farther and wider than you think, and now I know what your face looks like, too.\n要是你不兑现自己的承诺，会有你好看的。你的名声传得比你想象的更远更广，而且现在，我也记住你的长相了。"

    old "A big group of goblins move forward towards the exit. I make a quick signal, and the companions who remained behind ambush the goblins, killing them very quickly!"
    new "A big group of goblins move forward towards the exit. I make a quick signal, and the companions who remained behind ambush the goblins, killing them very quickly!\n一大群 Goblin 朝出口走去。我迅速打了个手势，留在后面的同伴们伏击了这些 Goblin，转眼间就把他们杀了个干净！"

    old "You...liar! I should have known!"
    new "You...liar! I should have known!\n你……骗子！我早该想到的！"

    old "Did you really think that I would make a deal with you?"
    new "Did you really think that I would make a deal with you?\n你真以为我会跟你做交易？"

    old "But...why? We never did anything to you!"
    new "But...why? We never did anything to you!\n可是……为什么？我们又没对你做过什么！"

    old "The dwarves are our allies. A slight against them is a slight against us. Now, it's time for you to pay for what you've done."
    new "The dwarves are our allies. A slight against them is a slight against us. Now, it's time for you to pay for what you've done.\nDwarf 是我们的盟友。冒犯他们，就是冒犯我们。现在，该轮到你们为所作所为付出代价了。"

    old "I'm sorry [protag], but I don't believe a single word of what you said!"
    new "I'm sorry [protag], but I don't believe a single word of what you said!\n抱歉，[protag]，但你说的话，我一个字都不信！"

    old "But—"
    new "But—\n可是——"

    old "Grob now is talking to me but also to his followers."
    new "Grob now is talking to me but also to his followers.\nGrob 现在既是在对我说话，也是在对他的手下说话。"

    old "Listen! The 'Envoy of Grimoire' is trying to fool us! Like all the others, [heshe] doesn't care about us goblins. We cannot trust [himher]!"
    new "Listen! The 'Envoy of Grimoire' is trying to fool us! Like all the others, [heshe] doesn't care about us goblins. We cannot trust [himher]!\n听好了！“Grimoire 特使”想糊弄我们！[heshe] 跟其他所有人一样，根本不在乎我们 Goblin。我们不能相信 [himher]！"

    old "The goblins cheer at Grob's words and start waving their weapons. They're about to attack. I quickly recall the other companions who join me in the coming fight."
    new "The goblins cheer at Grob's words and start waving their weapons. They're about to attack. I quickly recall the other companions who join me in the coming fight.\nGoblin 们听了 Grob 的话欢呼起来，挥舞起武器。他们就要动手了。我迅速召回其他同伴，一起投入即将到来的战斗。"

    old "Curses! You might have succeeded this time, but I'll have my revenge one day! Empire lapdog!"
    new "Curses! You might have succeeded this time, but I'll have my revenge one day! Empire lapdog!\n可恶！这次算你赢了，但总有一天我会报仇的！帝国的走狗！"

    old "Grob throws a potion on the ground and disappears inside a cloud of smoke."
    new "Grob throws a potion on the ground and disappears inside a cloud of smoke.\nGrob 把一瓶药水砸在地上，消失在一团烟雾之中。"

    old "Well, he might be back, but I doubt he'll manage to recruit enough goblins to occupy the mine again. Besides, I think the dwarves will do a better job of guarding this mine from now on."
    new "Well, he might be back, but I doubt he'll manage to recruit enough goblins to occupy the mine again. Besides, I think the dwarves will do a better job of guarding this mine from now on.\n唔，他也许还会回来，但我怀疑他能否再招募到足够的 Goblin 来占领这座矿井。再说，我想 Dwarf 从此以后会更好地守卫这座矿井。"

    old "Retreat! Fall back! Run to the exit!"
    new "Retreat! Fall back! Run to the exit!\n撤退！后退！往出口跑！"

    old "We manage to escape the goblins chasing us. As we reach the exit, they stop following us. Seems like they have no interest in killing us, only scaring us from the mine."
    new "We manage to escape the goblins chasing us. As we reach the exit, they stop following us. Seems like they have no interest in killing us, only scaring us from the mine.\n我们总算甩开了追赶的 Goblin。到了出口，他们就不再追了。看来他们没兴趣杀我们，只想把我们吓出矿井。"

    old "Let's heal up and—"
    new "Let's heal up and—\n我们先疗伤，然后——"

    old "A sudden noise catches us by surprise! Several goblin mages are casting an earthquake spell!"
    new "A sudden noise catches us by surprise! Several goblin mages are casting an earthquake spell!\n一阵突如其来的声响吓了我们一跳！几个 Goblin 法师正在施放地震法术！"

    old "They're sealing the entrance!"
    new "They're sealing the entrance!\n他们在封死入口！"

    old "We must stop them!"
    new "We must stop them!\n我们必须阻止他们！"

    old "Wait! If we go inside now, we'll need to fight without a way to escape, and we also risk to be buried alive in that mine."
    new "Wait! If we go inside now, we'll need to fight without a way to escape, and we also risk to be buried alive in that mine.\n等等！如果现在冲进去，我们就得在没有退路的情况下战斗，还有可能被活埋在那座矿井里。"

    old "In a few seconds, big rocks falls covering the entrance completely. There's no way to enter the mines now."
    new "In a few seconds, big rocks falls covering the entrance completely. There's no way to enter the mines now.\n几秒钟后，大块岩石落下，把入口完全封住了。现在再也无法进入矿井。"

    old "Those goblins. Are they stupid? They sealed themselves inside!"
    new "Those goblins. Are they stupid? They sealed themselves inside!\n那些 Goblin。他们是不是傻？他们把自己封在里面了！"

    old "Goblins are very small. Maybe they have one or more exits somewhere else. Who knows, they could have passageways leading to the other side of this mountain."
    new "Goblins are very small. Maybe they have one or more exits somewhere else. Who knows, they could have passageways leading to the other side of this mountain.\nGoblin 身材很小。也许他们在别处还有一两个出口。谁知道呢，说不定有通道通向这座山的另一面。"

    old "Or it could be that they are stupid enough to seal themselves in... We can't know. One thing is sure: we failed the task. The dwarves will likely come and open the entrance again, but it will take weeks to clear all those debris."
    new "Or it could be that they are stupid enough to seal themselves in... We can't know. One thing is sure: we failed the task. The dwarves will likely come and open the entrance again, but it will take weeks to clear all those debris.\n又或者，他们蠢到真的把自己封在了里面……我们无从得知。有一点可以肯定：我们的任务失败了。Dwarf 多半会来重新打通入口，但要清掉那些碎石得花上好几周。"

    old "I reach the border between the Great Forest and the Orcish Wastes. Reports from elf scouts spotted a group in the area only a few days ago."
    new "I reach the border between the Great Forest and the Orcish Wastes. Reports from elf scouts spotted a group in the area only a few days ago.\n我来到 Great Forest 与 Orcish Wastes 的边界。Elf 侦察兵的报告显示，就在几天前，这一带还发现过一伙人。"

    old "I must say, it is a privilege to be included in this little excursion of yours. I have never been hired to kill a dark elf before, and I have heard they're formidable fighters. This will be a good test of my skills."
    new "I must say, it is a privilege to be included in this little excursion of yours. I have never been hired to kill a dark elf before, and I have heard they're formidable fighters. This will be a good test of my skills.\n我得说，能被你带上参加这次小小的远行，是我的荣幸。我以前还从没被雇去杀过 Dark Elf，听说他们是了不起的战士。这会是检验我身手的好机会。"

    old "Sorry that we had to take the longer route around the Great Forest. I'm pretty sure they wouldn't have allowed me to walk freely there, even with your presence."
    new "Sorry that we had to take the longer route around the Great Forest. I'm pretty sure they wouldn't have allowed me to walk freely there, even with your presence.\n抱歉，我们不得不绕 Great Forest 走了远路。我很确定，就算有你在，他们也不会允许我在那里自由通行。"

    old "Be careful, [protag]. The dark elves may not be physically formidable, but like the elves they are very fast and excellent spellcasters."
    new "Be careful, [protag]. The dark elves may not be physically formidable, but like the elves they are very fast and excellent spellcasters.\n小心点，[protag]。Dark Elf 或许体格不算强悍，但和 Elf 一样，他们身手极快，又是出色的施法者。"

    old "The dark elves gave our tribe problems in the past. I have to admit, it's a bit satisfying to come with you and have the chance to teach them a lesson."
    new "The dark elves gave our tribe problems in the past. I have to admit, it's a bit satisfying to come with you and have the chance to teach them a lesson.\nDark Elf 过去给我们部落找过不少麻烦。我得承认，能随你前来，有机会给他们点教训，确实有点解气。"

    old "I hold up my hand, and everyone stops and remains silent. We spotted a big group of dark elves. Sounds like they're planning their next attack."
    new "I hold up my hand, and everyone stops and remains silent. We spotted a big group of dark elves. Sounds like they're planning their next attack.\n我举起手，众人停下脚步，保持安静。我们发现了一大群 Dark Elf。听上去他们正在筹划下一次袭击。"

    old "We could probably take them all, but if I can use my social skills to make some of them go away, it'll make this task easier. Negotiating with dark elves in good faith probably won't get me very far, but maybe I can tilt the tables in my favor with a bit of trickery."
    new "We could probably take them all, but if I can use my social skills to make some of them go away, it'll make this task easier. Negotiating with dark elves in good faith probably won't get me very far, but maybe I can tilt the tables in my favor with a bit of trickery.\n我们或许能把他们一网打尽，但如果我能靠社交手腕让一部分人离开，任务会轻松许多。真心实意地和 Dark Elf 谈判恐怕没什么用，不过也许我可以用点小伎俩，把局面扳向对我有利的方向。"

    old "Hey you, dark elves."
    new "Hey you, dark elves.\n嘿，那边的 Dark Elf。"

    old "I show myself, and my companions are surprised. They probably didn't expect me to reveal myself so quickly, but I hope they'll trust me on this."
    new "I show myself, and my companions are surprised. They probably didn't expect me to reveal myself so quickly, but I hope they'll trust me on this.\n我站了出来，同伴们都很惊讶。他们大概没料到我会这么快暴露自己，但我希望他们能相信我的判断。"

    old "Who are you?"
    new "Who are you?\n你是谁？"

    old "My name's [protag] and I'm the Envoy of Grimoire. You might have heard of me."
    new "My name's [protag] and I'm the Envoy of Grimoire. You might have heard of me.\n我叫 [protag]，是 Grimoire 的特使。你也许听说过我。"

    old "Now, I have more urgent matters to take care of, but the Council sent me to solve this problem. This is not my war, and I'm not one to follow orders too closely, so I'm here to make you a very generous offer."
    new "Now, I have more urgent matters to take care of, but the Council sent me to solve this problem. This is not my war, and I'm not one to follow orders too closely, so I'm here to make you a very generous offer.\n眼下，我还有更紧迫的事要处理，但议会派我来解决这个问题。这不是我的战争，我也不是那种唯命是从的人，所以我来这里，是想给你们开出一个非常慷慨的条件。"

    old "Here's some free advice."
    new "Here's some free advice.\n免费奉送一点忠告。"

    old "If you're pursuing riches, there are better uses of your time than stealing coin from passers by. I'm sure you all know the Unforgiving Swamps area, right?"
    new "If you're pursuing riches, there are better uses of your time than stealing coin from passers by. I'm sure you all know the Unforgiving Swamps area, right?\n如果你们图的是钱财，那比抢劫过路人更划算的来钱路子有的是。我想你们都熟悉 Unforgiving Swamps 一带吧？"

    old "What you probably don't know is that in those swamps there are still many unexplored ancient tombs and ruins with plenty of treasures, treasures beyond what you could hope to find here in the forest borderlands. A single bounty of that size would leave you quite well off for the rest of your days, and I say that knowing how long-lived many of you elves are."
    new "What you probably don't know is that in those swamps there are still many unexplored ancient tombs and ruins with plenty of treasures, treasures beyond what you could hope to find here in the forest borderlands. A single bounty of that size would leave you quite well off for the rest of your days, and I say that knowing how long-lived many of you elves are.\n你们大概不知道，那片沼泽里仍有许多尚未被探索的古代墓穴和遗迹，藏宝无数，远非你们在这片森林边境能指望找到的。单单一次这样的收获，就够你们下半辈子过得相当富足——我这么说，可是知道你们 Elf 有多长寿的。"

    old "If you flee now, not only will you save your lives, but you could end up rich. So why stay here and fight? Why risk your lives here?"
    new "If you flee now, not only will you save your lives, but you could end up rich. So why stay here and fight? Why risk your lives here?\n如果你们现在就走，不仅能保住性命，说不定还能发上一笔财。所以何必留在这里打仗？何必在这里拿性命冒险？"

    old "Of course, they likely don't know that that area is full of nagas and lizardmen, but I don't think I'll lose too much sleep if a few dark elves wander into danger on my advice. After all, free advice is often worth the price you pay."
    new "Of course, they likely don't know that that area is full of nagas and lizardmen, but I don't think I'll lose too much sleep if a few dark elves wander into danger on my advice. After all, free advice is often worth the price you pay.\n当然，他们多半不知道那片地区遍地是 Naga 和 Lizardman，但即便几个 Dark Elf 听了我的建议闯进险境，我也不会太愧疚。毕竟，免费的建议，往往也就值那个价。"

    old "Stop plundering the elves territories, and I'll spare your life."
    new "Stop plundering the elves territories, and I'll spare your life.\n停止劫掠 Elf 的领地，我就饶你一命。"

    old "I hear the sound of snickers and laughter coming from their ranks."
    new "I hear the sound of snickers and laughter coming from their ranks.\n我听到他们队伍里传来窃笑和哄笑声。"

    old "You can flee now if you'd like. The alternative is much less pleasant. And it doesn't involve dying. There are fates worse than death, you know?"
    new "You can flee now if you'd like. The alternative is much less pleasant. And it doesn't involve dying. There are fates worse than death, you know?\n想走的话，现在就可以走。另一条路可就没这么舒服了。而且那跟死无关。你们知道吗，这世上有比死亡更糟的下场。"

    old "We have ways of making prisoners regret the mistakes they've made. Believe me, when we're done with you, you'll long for the release of death. I haven't gotten a chance to torture a dark elf yet, so it will be an exciting new experience for me."
    new "We have ways of making prisoners regret the mistakes they've made. Believe me, when we're done with you, you'll long for the release of death. I haven't gotten a chance to torture a dark elf yet, so it will be an exciting new experience for me.\n我们有的是办法让囚犯为自己犯下的错追悔莫及。相信我，等我们收拾完你们，你们会渴望死亡的解脱。我还没机会拷问过一个 Dark Elf，所以这会是我一次令人兴奋的新体验。"

    old "The dark elves stop laughing."
    new "The dark elves stop laughing.\nDark Elf 们止住了笑声。"

    old "Some dark elves seems unsure whether to stay there and fight me or to head for the hills. After a standstill of a few moments, one of them starts running, and then several others follow him."
    new "Some dark elves seems unsure whether to stay there and fight me or to head for the hills. After a standstill of a few moments, one of them starts running, and then several others follow him.\n有些 Dark Elf 拿不定主意，不知该留下来跟我打，还是该转身往山里逃。僵持了片刻之后，其中一个拔腿就跑，接着又有几个跟了上去。"

    old "Traitors!"
    new "Traitors!\n叛徒！"

    old "Even as he yells it, several more turn tail and run."
    new "Even as he yells it, several more turn tail and run.\n就在他大喊的同时，又有几个掉头逃跑了。"

    old "Good, there are still many left, but definitely less than before."
    new "Good, there are still many left, but definitely less than before.\n好，虽然还剩不少，但肯定比刚才少了。"

    old "Unfortunately, my little show has no effect. I see two elves slink away, but the ones that remain seem angrier at me than before."
    new "Unfortunately, my little show has no effect. I see two elves slink away, but the ones that remain seem angrier at me than before.\n可惜，我的小把戏没起什么作用。我看到两个 Elf 悄悄溜走，但留下的那些似乎比先前更恨我了。"

    old "Very well. Let's see if you're a match for my blades!"
    new "Very well. Let's see if you're a match for my blades!\n很好。那就看看你配不配做我的刀下之敌！"

    old "This dark elf looks like their leader. It's going to be a tough fight."
    new "This dark elf looks like their leader. It's going to be a tough fight.\n这个 Dark Elf 看起来是他们的头目。会是一场硬仗。"

    old "Good, that's the last of them. Let's go back and inform the Elder Druids of our success."
    new "Good, that's the last of them. Let's go back and inform the Elder Druids of our success.\n好，这是最后一批了。我们回去向年长德鲁伊们禀报战果吧。"

    old "Retreat! They're too strong!"
    new "Retreat! They're too strong!\n撤退！他们太强了！"

    old "This is going to be a problem, [protag]."
    new "This is going to be a problem, [protag].\n这下麻烦了，[protag]。"

    old "Yes, they'll likely be more cautious from now on. We had the advantage of surprise, but we failed to win in spite of it. They'll change their routes and hide better. Or simply wait for weeks."
    new "Yes, they'll likely be more cautious from now on. We had the advantage of surprise, but we failed to win in spite of it. They'll change their routes and hide better. Or simply wait for weeks.\n是啊，他们从此多半会更谨慎。我们原本占了突袭之利，却没能借此取胜。他们会改换路线，藏得更好。或者干脆蛰伏上几个星期。"

    old "Waiting for weeks doesn't seem like an option, given the urgency of our mission."
    new "Waiting for weeks doesn't seem like an option, given the urgency of our mission.\n考虑到我们任务的紧迫性，等上几个星期似乎行不通。"

    old "I know. We probably won't be able to find them again in time before the next full moon."
    new "I know. We probably won't be able to find them again in time before the next full moon.\n我知道。在下个满月之前，我们恐怕来不及再找到他们了。"

    old "Apolimesho requested an audience with me. I reach him in his chambers."
    new "Apolimesho requested an audience with me. I reach him in his chambers.\nApolimesho 要求与我见面。我在他的房间里找到了他。"

    old "[protag], only ten days to the next full moon."
    new "[protag], only ten days to the next full moon.\n[protag]，离下个满月只有十天了。"

    old "I must say I was surprised to hear that you weren't able to successfully complete both the tasks I gave you. The Council wasn't impressed by this performance. However, they still have trust in your abilities to help Grimoire."
    new "I must say I was surprised to hear that you weren't able to successfully complete both the tasks I gave you. The Council wasn't impressed by this performance. However, they still have trust in your abilities to help Grimoire.\n我得说，听说你没能顺利完成我交给你的那两项任务，我很意外。议会对这样的表现并不满意。不过，他们仍相信你有能力帮助 Grimoire。"

    old "I'm sorry, Apolimesho."
    new "I'm sorry, Apolimesho.\n抱歉，Apolimesho。"

    old "I hope you do better in the coming battle. If not, the Council might change their mind about you. And as much as it pains me to say it, I might do the same."
    new "I hope you do better in the coming battle. If not, the Council might change their mind about you. And as much as it pains me to say it, I might do the same.\n希望你在接下来的战斗中表现更好。否则，议会可能会改变对你的看法。而且，尽管这话说出来让我难受，我可能也会如此。"

    old "Why I am no longer surprised that you managed to succeed in both tasks? The Council was extremely pleased with your performance, and I couldn't be happier myself."
    new "Why I am no longer surprised that you managed to succeed in both tasks? The Council was extremely pleased with your performance, and I couldn't be happier myself.\n为什么我对你成功完成那两项任务，已经不再感到惊讶了呢？议会对你的表现极为满意，我自己也高兴得不得了。"

    old "Both the dwarves and the elves sent us some gifts. A show of appreciation for your efforts."
    new "Both the dwarves and the elves sent us some gifts. A show of appreciation for your efforts.\nDwarf 和 Elf 都给我们送来了些礼物，以表对你努力的谢意。"

    old "Here are some items, directly from Hammerhands, freshly made by their forges, using the ore from that mine that you cleared from the goblins."
    new "Here are some items, directly from Hammerhands, freshly made by their forges, using the ore from that mine that you cleared from the goblins.\n这里有些物品，直接来自 Hammerhands，是他们用你从 Goblin 手中夺回的那座矿井里的矿石，在熔炉里现打造出来的。"

    old "And here are the elven gifts. I'm sure the Elder Druids weren't too happy about this, but they need to pretend to be our friends now, otherwise they might lose popular consensus."
    new "And here are the elven gifts. I'm sure the Elder Druids weren't too happy about this, but they need to pretend to be our friends now, otherwise they might lose popular consensus.\n这些是 Elf 的礼物。我敢肯定年长德鲁伊们对此并不太乐意，但他们如今不得不装成我们的朋友，否则就可能失去民心。"

    old "I'm incredibly grateful for this generosity, even if the elves' gifts came reluctantly. Not only will these be incredibly useful, but it will be a big morale boost to share these with the others."
    new "I'm incredibly grateful for this generosity, even if the elves' gifts came reluctantly. Not only will these be incredibly useful, but it will be a big morale boost to share these with the others.\n我由衷感激这份慷慨，即便 Elf 的礼物给得心不甘情不愿。这些东西不仅会非常有用，与大家分享还能大大提振士气。"

    old "The dwarves thank you for helping them with the mine problem. They have sent us some nice gifts too. Freshly made by their forges, using the ore from that mine that you cleared from the goblins."
    new "The dwarves thank you for helping them with the mine problem. They have sent us some nice gifts too. Freshly made by their forges, using the ore from that mine that you cleared from the goblins.\nDwarf 感谢你帮他们解决了矿井的麻烦。他们也给我们送来了一些不错的礼物，是用你从 Goblin 手中夺回的那座矿井里的矿石，在熔炉里现打造出来的。"

    old "Please, send them my thanks. I'll be sure to make good use of their gifts."
    new "Please, send them my thanks. I'll be sure to make good use of their gifts.\n请代我向他们道谢。我一定会好好利用他们的礼物。"

    old "The Elder Druids sent their thanks. I'm sure that deep down they're not so happy to not have a valid excuse anymore to attack us, but they need to pretend to be our friends now. They've sent some gifts to show their friendship."
    new "The Elder Druids sent their thanks. I'm sure that deep down they're not so happy to not have a valid excuse anymore to attack us, but they need to pretend to be our friends now. They've sent some gifts to show their friendship.\n年长德鲁伊们送来了谢意。我敢肯定，他们内心深处并不乐意——如今再也找不到正当借口来攻打我们了——但他们现在必须装成我们的朋友。他们送了些礼物以示友好。"

    old "Very nice. We'll put these gifts to good use."
    new "Very nice. We'll put these gifts to good use.\n很好。我们会好好利用这些礼物。"

    old "That's all, [protag]. We might see again a few days before the next full moon. Meanwhile, I recommend to keep training and talk to your party members. We need everyone to be fully motivated and loyal to you and our cause, and I recommend taking any opportunity you can to help your followers with their problems."
    new "That's all, [protag]. We might see again a few days before the next full moon. Meanwhile, I recommend to keep training and talk to your party members. We need everyone to be fully motivated and loyal to you and our cause, and I recommend taking any opportunity you can to help your followers with their problems.\n就这些了，[protag]。我们或许会在下个满月前几天再见。与此同时，我建议你继续训练，多和你的队员们聊聊。我们需要每个人都斗志昂扬，忠于你和我们的事业，我也建议你抓住一切机会，帮追随者们解决他们的难题。"

    old "I'll keep that in mind, Apolimesho. Thanks."
    new "I'll keep that in mind, Apolimesho. Thanks.\n我会记住的，Apolimesho。谢谢。"

    old "I set foot in the Unforgiving Swamp with a sense of trepidation."
    new "I set foot in the Unforgiving Swamp with a sense of trepidation.\n我怀着忐忑的心情踏入了 Unforgiving Swamp。"

    old "As I enter the foggy mist surrounding the swamp, I breathe in—and find my nose assaulted by a vile wetness. The air is literally thick with the stench of rotting plants and whatever else was unlucky enough to expire in this swamp, and my breathing becomes progressively more labored."
    new "As I enter the foggy mist surrounding the swamp, I breathe in—and find my nose assaulted by a vile wetness. The air is literally thick with the stench of rotting plants and whatever else was unlucky enough to expire in this swamp, and my breathing becomes progressively more labored.\n一走进环绕沼泽的浓雾，我深吸一口气——却感到一股恶浊的湿气直冲鼻腔。空气里弥漫着腐烂植物，以及一切不幸葬身此沼泽之物的恶臭，我的呼吸也变得越来越费力。"

    old "As I advance, my nose becomes more and more desensitized to the fetid odor of the swamp. I keep my feet on dry land, but beads of moisture coalesce on my exposed skin, mixing with my sweat and making me feel an unpleasant mix of damp and sticky."
    new "As I advance, my nose becomes more and more desensitized to the fetid odor of the swamp. I keep my feet on dry land, but beads of moisture coalesce on my exposed skin, mixing with my sweat and making me feel an unpleasant mix of damp and sticky.\n随着我前进，鼻子对沼泽的恶臭越来越麻木了。我尽量走在干燥的地面上，但暴露的皮肤上凝结起细小的水珠，和汗水混在一起，让我浑身又湿又黏，很不舒服。"

    old "I keep to the edges of the swamp, keeping a line of visibility to the nearest standing pool of water at all time. If there are any lizardmen lurking about, they won't be sneaking up on me—hopefully giving me enough time to make an effective retreat."
    new "I keep to the edges of the swamp, keeping a line of visibility to the nearest standing pool of water at all time. If there are any lizardmen lurking about, they won't be sneaking up on me—hopefully giving me enough time to make an effective retreat.\n我沿着沼泽边缘行走，始终保持着能看到最近一处静水潭的视线。如果有 Lizardman 潜伏在附近，他们就没法偷偷摸到我身边——但愿这能给我足够的时间有效撤退。"

    old "As my nose grows accustomed to the swamp's strong stench, I begin to find comfort in it. After all, carnivorous beasts tend to have a strong sense of smell, and anything that masks my own odor increases my chances of passing through the swamp undetected."
    new "As my nose grows accustomed to the swamp's strong stench, I begin to find comfort in it. After all, carnivorous beasts tend to have a strong sense of smell, and anything that masks my own odor increases my chances of passing through the swamp undetected.\n随着鼻子渐渐习惯沼泽的浓烈恶臭，我反倒从中找到了些许安心。毕竟，食肉野兽往往嗅觉灵敏，任何能掩盖我自身气味的东西，都能增加我无声穿过沼泽的几率。"

    old "The mist around the swamp also serves as a barrier to detection. I can scarcely see a stone's throw in front of me. If I do encounter any beasts, they'll likely be as startled as I am—and being that I'm on edge, I'll have the advantage."
    new "The mist around the swamp also serves as a barrier to detection. I can scarcely see a stone's throw in front of me. If I do encounter any beasts, they'll likely be as startled as I am—and being that I'm on edge, I'll have the advantage.\n环绕沼泽的迷雾也成了一道难以被察觉的屏障。我几乎看不清一箭之外的东西。要是真遇到什么野兽，它们多半和我一样吃惊——而我本就绷着神经，反倒占得先机。"

    old "Fortunately, my journey through the swamp passes uneventfully, and I soon find myself staring at the face of the Chzulu Ruins."
    new "Fortunately, my journey through the swamp passes uneventfully, and I soon find myself staring at the face of the Chzulu Ruins.\n幸运的是，我穿越沼泽的旅途平安无事，很快，我就发现自己正面对着 Chzulu Ruins 的正面。"

    old "I look around the perimeter of the ruins for the dropped satchels, and find one of them near the entrance of the ruins."
    new "I look around the perimeter of the ruins for the dropped satchels, and find one of them near the entrance of the ruins.\n我绕着遗迹四周寻找被丢弃的行囊，在遗迹入口附近找到了其中一个。"

    old "I open the satchel. It's filled to the brim with gold items."
    new "I open the satchel. It's filled to the brim with gold items.\n我打开行囊，里面塞满了金器。"

    old "Just what I was looking for."
    new "Just what I was looking for.\n正是我要找的东西。"

    old "I sling the satchel over my shoulder. Its weight is modest but noticeable. The items inside shift and rattle against each other as I move, so I cradle the satchel under one arm to avoid making any noise."
    new "I sling the satchel over my shoulder. Its weight is modest but noticeable. The items inside shift and rattle against each other as I move, so I cradle the satchel under one arm to avoid making any noise.\n我把行囊甩到肩上。它不算重，却颇有分量。里面的东西在我走动时会彼此碰撞、叮当作响，于是我把它夹在腋下，以免发出声响。"

    old "One down, two to go."
    new "One down, two to go.\n找到一袋，还剩两袋。"

    old "I continue walking around the exterior of the ruins, and find a second bag. I confirm the contents. The bag is filled with several jewels, most unrecognizable to me, but obviously stones of some value."
    new "I continue walking around the exterior of the ruins, and find a second bag. I confirm the contents. The bag is filled with several jewels, most unrecognizable to me, but obviously stones of some value.\n我继续绕着遗迹外围走，找到了第二个袋子。我确认了一下里面的东西。袋里装着好几颗宝石，大多数我认不出来，但显然是颇有价值的石头。"

    old "I sling the second satchel over my other shoulder and begin walking, cradling both satchels as I walk."
    new "I sling the second satchel over my other shoulder and begin walking, cradling both satchels as I walk.\n我把第二个行囊甩到另一边肩上，迈步前行，边走边用双臂护着两个行囊。"

    old "However, dedicating both arms to cradling the bags robs me of my balance. I keep my footing initially, but the uneven ground gets the better of me."
    new "However, dedicating both arms to cradling the bags robs me of my balance. I keep my footing initially, but the uneven ground gets the better of me.\n然而，两只手臂都用来护着袋子，让我失去了平衡。起初我还站得稳，但凹凸不平的地面还是让我栽了跟头。"

    old "The soft soil gives way as I put my foot down, and my foot slides forward into the mud. I drop the bags and land on my bottom."
    new "The soft soil gives way as I put my foot down, and my foot slides forward into the mud. I drop the bags and land on my bottom.\n我一落脚，松软的泥土就塌了下去，脚向前滑进了泥里。我丢下袋子，一屁股坐在地上。"

    old "I ease myself off the ground gingerly and rub the spot where I landed. Doesn't seem to be hurt."
    new "I ease myself off the ground gingerly and rub the spot where I landed. Doesn't seem to be hurt.\n我小心翼翼地爬起来，揉了揉着地的地方。似乎没摔伤。"

    old "What have we here?"
    new "What have we here?\n看看我们这儿是什么？"

    old "Looks like we've found ourselves a treasure hunter."
    new "Looks like we've found ourselves a treasure hunter.\n看来我们给自己找到了个寻宝人。"

    old "I turn around and see two serpent-like creatures behind me. Nagas."
    new "I turn around and see two serpent-like creatures behind me. Nagas.\n我转过身，看到身后有两个蛇形的生物。是 Naga。"

    old "Oh dear. Did we startle the poor thing?"
    new "Oh dear. Did we startle the poor thing?\n哦，天哪。我们吓到这个小可怜了？"

    old "Don't worry, darling. We aren't going to hurt you. In fact, I think we'd like to become your friend. What's your name, little one?"
    new "Don't worry, darling. We aren't going to hurt you. In fact, I think we'd like to become your friend. What's your name, little one?\n别担心，亲爱的。我们不会伤害你的。事实上，我想我们愿意做你的朋友。你叫什么名字，小家伙？"

    old "I'm Sylrissa, and the quiet one over there is my friend Enok."
    new "I'm Sylrissa, and the quiet one over there is my friend Enok.\n我是 Sylrissa，那边那位沉默寡言的是我的朋友 Enok。"

    old "We're treasure hunters like you. I believe that would make us rivals."
    new "We're treasure hunters like you. I believe that would make us rivals.\n我们和你一样，也是寻宝人。我想，这该让我们成为对手才是。"

    old "But making friends is so much more fun than making enemies. And it looks like you already know where we might find some easy treasure."
    new "But making friends is so much more fun than making enemies. And it looks like you already know where we might find some easy treasure.\n不过，交朋友可比树敌有趣多了。而且看起来，你已经知道在哪儿能轻松找到宝藏了。"

    old "Indeed I do."
    new "Indeed I do.\n我确实知道。"

    old "That's wrong, I'm afraid."
    new "That's wrong, I'm afraid.\n恐怕你猜错了。"

    old "Oh, come now. Don't lie to us. We want to be your friends, remember?"
    new "Oh, come now. Don't lie to us. We want to be your friends, remember?\n哦，得了吧。别对我们撒谎。我们想和你做朋友，记得吗？"

    old "You have two bags full of treasure, yet you're headed deeper into the swamp. Clearly, you're looking for something more than what you've found already."
    new "You have two bags full of treasure, yet you're headed deeper into the swamp. Clearly, you're looking for something more than what you've found already.\n你背着两袋满满的宝藏，却还在往沼泽深处走。显然，你要找的不止是已经到手的东西。"

    old "Now, don't lie again. Enok becomes cross when people are dishonest with him, you see?"
    new "Now, don't lie again. Enok becomes cross when people are dishonest with him, you see?\n来，别再撒谎了。别人对他不诚实的时候，Enok 可是会生气的，你瞧见了吧？"

    old "Some...acquaintances of mine were here earlier. Their expedition was cut short when they were attacked by a group of lizardmen. They escaped with their lives, but not the treasure. So I've come back to collect what they dropped. Three bags in total."
    new "Some...acquaintances of mine were here earlier. Their expedition was cut short when they were attacked by a group of lizardmen. They escaped with their lives, but not the treasure. So I've come back to collect what they dropped. Three bags in total.\n我的一些……熟人早些时候来过这里。他们遭到一群 Lizardman 袭击，探险被迫中断。他们捡回了一条命，却丢了宝藏。所以我回来回收他们落下的东西。一共三袋。"

    old "What a fortunate coincidence. Three bags, three of us here, do you think this might be the beginning of a beautiful friendship?"
    new "What a fortunate coincidence. Three bags, three of us here, do you think this might be the beginning of a beautiful friendship?\n多么幸运的巧合啊。三袋宝藏，我们这里正好三个人，你说，这会不会是一段美好友谊的开端？"

    old "I'd say I value our friendship at...one bag of treasure each. That ought to do it."
    new "I'd say I value our friendship at...one bag of treasure each. That ought to do it.\n要我说，我们这份友谊的价值嘛……每人一袋宝藏。这样应该就差不多了。"

    old "What do you say? Would you like to become our friend?"
    new "What do you say? Would you like to become our friend?\n你怎么说？愿意做我们的朋友吗？"

    old "I'll take any friends I can get in this swamp."
    new "I'll take any friends I can get in this swamp.\n在这片沼泽里，能交到朋友，我求之不得。"

    old "Excellent. In that case, we'll each be helping ourselves to one of these bags."
    new "Excellent. In that case, we'll each be helping ourselves to one of these bags.\n太好了。既然如此，我们就每人自取一袋了。"

    old "I think I'm fine on my own."
    new "I think I'm fine on my own.\n我想我一个人就行。"

    old "Oh dear. Little one, don't say something you won't regret."
    new "Oh dear. Little one, don't say something you won't regret.\n哦，天哪。小家伙，可别说些会让你后悔的话。"

    old "We're ruffians, you see. Ruffians with a sense of honor, but ruffians nonetheless. We offer loyalty and protection to those who we call friends. But to those who decline our offer of friendship...let's just say things may not go so well for you."
    new "We're ruffians, you see. Ruffians with a sense of honor, but ruffians nonetheless. We offer loyalty and protection to those who we call friends. But to those who decline our offer of friendship...let's just say things may not go so well for you.\n我们是恶棍，你瞧。有点荣誉感的恶棍，但终究是恶棍。对愿意与我们做朋友的人，我们给予忠诚和保护。但对那些拒绝我们友谊的人嘛……这么说吧，你的日子可能不会太好过。"

    old "It doesn't seem like you're giving me much of a choice."
    new "It doesn't seem like you're giving me much of a choice.\n你好像没给我留下多少选择。"

    old "Choice? But choice is so overrated! Some friendships are just fated to happen. Sometimes, friendship is something that just happens to you whether you like it or not. Isn't life so much more exciting when the unexpected happens and you don't have a choice in the matter?"
    new "Choice? But choice is so overrated! Some friendships are just fated to happen. Sometimes, friendship is something that just happens to you whether you like it or not. Isn't life so much more exciting when the unexpected happens and you don't have a choice in the matter?\n选择？可“选择”这东西被高估啦！有些友谊是注定要发生的。有时候，友谊就是这么找上你，不管你喜欢不喜欢。当意外降临，而你无从选择的时候，人生不才更精彩吗？"

    old "I know you didn't come here expecting to be a victim of extortion. But truth be told, these bags look heavy, and I think that you could use an escort out of here. An alliance would be in everyone's best interest."
    new "I know you didn't come here expecting to be a victim of extortion. But truth be told, these bags look heavy, and I think that you could use an escort out of here. An alliance would be in everyone's best interest.\n我知道你来这儿，没料到自己会被人敲诈。但说真的，这些袋子看着挺沉的，我觉得你需要个护送的人离开这里。结盟对大家都有好处。"

    old "Fine, I'll be your 'friend.'"
    new "Fine, I'll be your 'friend.'\n好吧，我当你们的“朋友”就是了。"

    old "Sylrissa claps her hands together."
    new "Sylrissa claps her hands together.\nSylrissa 拍了拍手。"

    old "Wonderful."
    new "Wonderful.\n太好了。"

    old "Now, if you don't mind, we'll be helping ourselves to our payment."
    new "Now, if you don't mind, we'll be helping ourselves to our payment.\n那么，如果你不介意，我们这就自取酬劳了。"

    old "Enok and Sylrissa pick up the bags I dropped and inspect their contents."
    new "Enok and Sylrissa pick up the bags I dropped and inspect their contents.\nEnok 和 Sylrissa 捡起我掉落的袋子，查看里面的东西。"

    old "Ooh, this one's got jewels in it. Are these emeralds? I've never seen one so big. Enok, what did you get?"
    new "Ooh, this one's got jewels in it. Are these emeralds? I've never seen one so big. Enok, what did you get?\n哦，这个里面是珠宝。这些是祖母绿吗？我从没见过这么大颗的。Enok，你拿到的是什么？"

    old "Enok reaches into the bag and pulls out a gold bangle."
    new "Enok reaches into the bag and pulls out a gold bangle.\nEnok 把手伸进袋子里，掏出一只金手镯。"

    old "A few nice pieces. Do you think this would look handsome on me?"
    new "A few nice pieces. Do you think this would look handsome on me?\n几件不错的东西。你觉得这个戴在我身上会好看吗？"

    old "I think it fits you splendidly. [protag], what do you think?"
    new "I think it fits you splendidly. [protag], what do you think?\n我觉得它配你极好。[protag]，你觉得呢？"

    old "It looks wonderful. I think it would suit you perfectly."
    new "It looks wonderful. I think it would suit you perfectly.\n看起来棒极了。我想它跟你再相配不过。"

    old "It does compliment the texture of my scales, doesn't it?"
    new "It does compliment the texture of my scales, doesn't it?\n它确实很衬我鳞片的质地，不是吗？"

    old "I think you could do better."
    new "I think you could do better.\n我觉得你值得更好的。"

    old "A man as handsome as you deserves better than a trinket like that."
    new "A man as handsome as you deserves better than a trinket like that.\n像你这么英俊的人，配得上比那件小玩意儿更好的东西。"

    old "If you're trying to flatter me, you should know that you're succeeding superbly."
    new "If you're trying to flatter me, you should know that you're succeeding superbly.\n如果你是想恭维我，那你得知道，你做得极为成功。"

    old "I think it looks ugly."
    new "I think it looks ugly.\n我觉得它看着很丑。"

    old "Really? I think it looks rather elegant."
    new "Really? I think it looks rather elegant.\n真的吗？我倒觉得它相当雅致。"

    old "It's unfashionable. It looks luxurious, but it doesn't match you at all."
    new "It's unfashionable. It looks luxurious, but it doesn't match you at all.\n它不时兴。看着是奢华，但跟你一点都不搭。"

    old "I suppose you're right. It would be rather tacky for me to wear gold simply for the sake of wearing gold, wouldn't it? It's not enough for an accessory to be valuable. It also has to be tasteful. If I were to adorn myself in every gold accessory I came across, it would look more gaudy than elegant."
    new "I suppose you're right. It would be rather tacky for me to wear gold simply for the sake of wearing gold, wouldn't it? It's not enough for an accessory to be valuable. It also has to be tasteful. If I were to adorn myself in every gold accessory I came across, it would look more gaudy than elegant.\n我想你说得对。要是我纯粹为了戴金子而戴金子，那确实挺俗气的，不是吗？一件饰物光是贵重还不够，还得有品味。如果我把自己碰到的每件金饰都往身上堆，那看起来不是优雅，而是浮夸了。"

    old "Well. We have our bags of treasure. You said there was a third bag. Let's find it."
    new "Well. We have our bags of treasure. You said there was a third bag. Let's find it.\n好了。我们的宝藏袋子都到手了。你说还有第三袋。我们去找找吧。"

    old "It should be somewhere near here."
    new "It should be somewhere near here.\n应该就在这附近某处。"

    old "Is this it?"
    new "Is this it?\n是这个吗？"

    old "Sylrissa holds up a satchel matching the ones I already found."
    new "Sylrissa holds up a satchel matching the ones I already found.\nSylrissa 举起一个行囊，和我之前找到的那两个一样。"

    old "I found it under a lily pad. Sorry about the wetness. But the bag looks like it's still intact."
    new "I found it under a lily pad. Sorry about the wetness. But the bag looks like it's still intact.\n我在一片睡莲叶子底下找到的。抱歉有点湿。不过袋子看起来还完好。"

    old "Sylrissa hands me the bag, and I open it."
    new "Sylrissa hands me the bag, and I open it.\nSylrissa 把袋子递给我，我打了开来。"

    old "What's inside?"
    new "What's inside?\n里面是什么？"

    old "I dig around in the bag."
    new "I dig around in the bag.\n我在袋子里翻找起来。"

    old "It's filled with...rocks."
    new "It's filled with...rocks.\n里面装满了……石头。"

    old "Oh, looks like poor [protag] got the worst of it."
    new "Oh, looks like poor [protag] got the worst of it.\n哦，看来可怜的 [protag] 拿到了最差的一份。"

    old "I wouldn't be too sure. You said your companions were here beforehand, right? They picked the contents of these backs from the depths of the ruins?"
    new "I wouldn't be too sure. You said your companions were here beforehand, right? They picked the contents of these backs from the depths of the ruins?\n我可没那么肯定。你说你的同伴们事先来过这里，对吧？他们是从遗迹深处把这些东西取出来的？"

    old "Well, they wouldn't have dragged those rocks out of there for nothing. Perhaps they have some magical properties, something not evident to the naked eye. You should take them to an appraiser."
    new "Well, they wouldn't have dragged those rocks out of there for nothing. Perhaps they have some magical properties, something not evident to the naked eye. You should take them to an appraiser.\n嗯，他们总不会无缘无故把这些石头拖出来。也许它们有某些魔力，肉眼看不出来。你应该把它们拿去给鉴定师看看。"

    old "I'll do that. I'd hate to think I came all the way out here just for a bag of rocks."
    new "I'll do that. I'd hate to think I came all the way out here just for a bag of rocks.\n我会的。我可不愿相信自己大老远跑到这里，只为了这一袋石头。"

    old "Of course...there's the possibility that someone looted the bag before you got here and filled it with ordinary rocks to weigh it down so that it would sink in the water."
    new "Of course...there's the possibility that someone looted the bag before you got here and filled it with ordinary rocks to weigh it down so that it would sink in the water.\n当然……也有可能是有人在你到达之前就洗劫了袋子，又塞进普通石头给它压重，好让它沉进水里。"

    old "Who would do something like that?"
    new "Who would do something like that?\n谁会做这种事？"

    old "Perish the thought. We have what you came here for. Let's get out of these ruins. It's not a safe place, especially for someone like you."
    new "Perish the thought. We have what you came here for. Let's get out of these ruins. It's not a safe place, especially for someone like you.\n别想这个了。你来这儿要找的东西已经到手。我们离开这些遗迹吧。这里不安全，尤其是对你这样的人来说。"

    old "Yes, let's get out of here. The presence of lizardmen makes my scales shudder."
    new "Yes, let's get out of here. The presence of lizardmen makes my scales shudder.\n是啊，我们离开这儿吧。Lizardman 的存在让我鳞片都发颤。"

    old "You came here from the south, yes? We can escort you to the edge of the swamp. I know the fastest way. Let's go."
    new "You came here from the south, yes? We can escort you to the edge of the swamp. I know the fastest way. Let's go.\n你是从南边过来的吧？我们可以护送你到沼泽边缘。我知道最快的路。走吧。"

    old "Enok leads the way southward through the swamp."
    new "Enok leads the way southward through the swamp.\nEnok 领路，朝南穿过沼泽。"

    old "Enok, are you sure that taking the fastest way is the best?"
    new "Enok, are you sure that taking the fastest way is the best?\nEnok，你确定走最快的路是最好的吗？"

    old "Of course. Faster means less time for us to get accosted by whatever might be lurking about."
    new "Of course. Faster means less time for us to get accosted by whatever might be lurking about.\n当然。走得快，就意味着我们被附近潜伏的什么东西缠上的时间更少。"

    old "Enok cuts through a wall of standing reeds."
    new "Enok cuts through a wall of standing reeds.\nEnok 穿过一堵密实的芦苇丛。"

    old "Speaking of things that are lurking about..."
    new "Speaking of things that are lurking about...\n说到潜伏在附近的东西……"

    old "Through the reeds, I see two, no, three lizardmen. And it seems that they've seen us."
    new "Through the reeds, I see two, no, three lizardmen. And it seems that they've seen us.\n透过芦苇，我看到两个，不，是三个 Lizardman。而且他们似乎也看到了我们。"

    old "Guess we'll have to fight our way out of this."
    new "Guess we'll have to fight our way out of this.\n看来我们得杀出一条路来了。"

    old "It's about time. You know, I was starting to get bored."
    new "It's about time. You know, I was starting to get bored.\n也该活动活动了。你知道吗，我都开始觉得无聊了。"

    old "[protag], can you handle yourself in a fight?"
    new "[protag], can you handle yourself in a fight?\n[protag]，你能在战斗中保护自己吗？"

    old "Just watch me. You might learn a thing or two."
    new "Just watch me. You might learn a thing or two.\n瞧好了。说不定你还能学到一两手。"

    old "That was unexpected. Sometimes you'll catch the odd lizardman sentry roaming around these parts, but that trio looked like a coordinated group, ready for combat. Almost as if they were on a mission."
    new "That was unexpected. Sometimes you'll catch the odd lizardman sentry roaming around these parts, but that trio looked like a coordinated group, ready for combat. Almost as if they were on a mission.\n真是出乎意料。有时你会碰到个把 Lizardman 哨兵在这一带游荡，但那三个看起来像是一支配合默契、随时准备战斗的小队。简直就像在执行任务。"

    old "There could be more of them. Who knows how many. It might be best to plan for escape rather than confrontation."
    new "There could be more of them. Who knows how many. It might be best to plan for escape rather than confrontation.\n可能还有更多。谁知道有多少。或许最好计划逃跑，而不是硬拼。"

    old "[protag], I'm worried about you. Enok and I can swim away in a hurry if things turn bad, but you don't have that luxury."
    new "[protag], I'm worried about you. Enok and I can swim away in a hurry if things turn bad, but you don't have that luxury.\n[protag]，我担心你。要是情况不妙，Enok 和我能迅速游走，可你没有这本事。"

    old "Sylrissa, I think you should stay here with [protag] while I scout ahead to figure out the safest route forward."
    new "Sylrissa, I think you should stay here with [protag] while I scout ahead to figure out the safest route forward.\nSylrissa，我想你留在这里陪 [protag]，我去前面侦察一下，找出最安全的行进路线。"

    old "I think I can handle that request."
    new "I think I can handle that request.\n我想这个请求我还能应付。"

    old "Enok begins heading south, and soon vanishes into the mist."
    new "Enok begins heading south, and soon vanishes into the mist.\nEnok 开始向南行进，很快消失在了雾中。"

    old "So, [protag]. We finally get some time alone to ourselves. I feel like there's so much we could discuss, and I'm not sure whether I want more to share about myself or learn about you, so I'll let you decide. What shall we talk about?"
    new "So, [protag]. We finally get some time alone to ourselves. I feel like there's so much we could discuss, and I'm not sure whether I want more to share about myself or learn about you, so I'll let you decide. What shall we talk about?\n那么，[protag]。我们终于能单独待一会儿了。我觉得我们有好多可聊的，我也不确定自己是更想说说自己，还是更想了解你，所以还是由你决定吧。我们聊点什么？"

    old "What do you want to know about me?"
    new "What do you want to know about me?\n你想了解我什么？"

    old "Well, I already know that you're the sort who risks life and limb to go hunting for treasure. What is it that compels you so?"
    new "Well, I already know that you're the sort who risks life and limb to go hunting for treasure. What is it that compels you so?\n哦，我已经知道你是那种肯拿性命去寻宝的人。是什么让你这么拼？"

    old "I wish I could say I'm just an ordinary treasure hunter hoping to strike it rich, but the truth is I came here at the behest of a friend. We're working toward a common goal, so I decided to go along with the plan, which involved me going exploring, and her staying behind at home to mourn my loss if my efforts proved unsuccessful."
    new "I wish I could say I'm just an ordinary treasure hunter hoping to strike it rich, but the truth is I came here at the behest of a friend. We're working toward a common goal, so I decided to go along with the plan, which involved me going exploring, and her staying behind at home to mourn my loss if my efforts proved unsuccessful.\n我倒希望自己能说，我只是个指望一夜暴富的普通寻宝人，但真相是，我是应一位朋友的请求来这里的。我们正朝一个共同的目标努力，于是我决定配合她的计划——由我出来探险，她留在后方，倘若我的努力没能成功，就为我哀悼。"

    old "How do you feel about that arrangement?"
    new "How do you feel about that arrangement?\n你对这个安排感觉如何？"

    old "Well, if you ask me, I got the short end of the stick. I'm the one going out and taking the risks. I'd rather sit home and have more peaceful missions."
    new "Well, if you ask me, I got the short end of the stick. I'm the one going out and taking the risks. I'd rather sit home and have more peaceful missions.\n哦，要我说，我分到的是吃亏的那头。出去冒险、承担风险的是我。我倒宁愿待在家里，做些更太平的差事。"

    old "Oh, but that's no fun at all."
    new "Oh, but that's no fun at all.\n哦，可那多没意思啊。"

    old "Shouldn't you feel lucky that you get to go out and have adventures? So many exciting and wonderful things can happen when you're gallivanting about."
    new "Shouldn't you feel lucky that you get to go out and have adventures? So many exciting and wonderful things can happen when you're gallivanting about.\n能出去闯荡冒险，你不该觉得幸运吗？四处游历的时候，会有那么多激动人心又美好的事情发生。"

    old "For example, if you'd stayed home, you would have missed out on the wonderful opportunity to meet me."
    new "For example, if you'd stayed home, you would have missed out on the wonderful opportunity to meet me.\n比如说，你要是待在家里，就会错过遇见我这么美妙的机会。"

    old "I could never lead a boring, stable life. Out here, it's catch as catch can, and that's exactly the way I like it. Life is best when it's unpredictable. And around this swamp, you never know what's coming next."
    new "I could never lead a boring, stable life. Out here, it's catch as catch can, and that's exactly the way I like it. Life is best when it's unpredictable. And around this swamp, you never know what's coming next.\n我永远过不了那种平淡安稳的日子。在外面，一切都是碰运气，而这正是我喜欢的方式。人生最妙之处就在于无法预料。而在这片沼泽附近，你永远不知道接下来会发生什么。"

    old "I'm pretty happy with my end of things, actually. She stays at home and does all of the boring tasks of leadership and whatnot. Meanwhile, I get to go run around and have adventures."
    new "I'm pretty happy with my end of things, actually. She stays at home and does all of the boring tasks of leadership and whatnot. Meanwhile, I get to go run around and have adventures.\n其实，我对自己这一头挺满意的。她待在家里，处理领导啦之类那些枯燥的事务。而我呢，却能四处奔跑，闯荡冒险。"

    old "After all, I met you. I wouldn't have had that chance if I were back home sitting safe and sound."
    new "After all, I met you. I wouldn't have had that chance if I were back home sitting safe and sound.\n毕竟，我遇见了你。要是我安安稳稳坐在家里，可就没这机会了。"

    old "Sylrissa grins and bites her lower lip."
    new "Sylrissa grins and bites her lower lip.\nSylrissa 咧嘴一笑，咬了咬下唇。"

    old "You. I like you."
    new "You. I like you.\n你呀。我喜欢你。"

    old "I feel exactly the same way. Living each day, not knowing if you'll see the next, it's the best way to live, isn't it?"
    new "I feel exactly the same way. Living each day, not knowing if you'll see the next, it's the best way to live, isn't it?\n我也正是这么想的。每一天都活在不知能否见到明天之中，这才是最好的活法，不是吗？"

    old "Enok and I, we don't live the most stable of lives. It's mostly catch as catch can, and around this swamp, you're never sure what's coming next. And that's exactly what's so thrilling about it."
    new "Enok and I, we don't live the most stable of lives. It's mostly catch as catch can, and around this swamp, you're never sure what's coming next. And that's exactly what's so thrilling about it.\nEnok 和我，我们的生活算不上安稳。大多时候都是碰运气，而在这片沼泽附近，你永远不知道接下来会发生什么。这正是它令人激动的地方。"

    old "Why don't you tell me about yourself?"
    new "Why don't you tell me about yourself?\n不如跟我说说你自己吧？"

    old "Me? Well, as you know, my name is Sylrissa. I live in this swamp, here with Enok."
    new "Me? Well, as you know, my name is Sylrissa. I live in this swamp, here with Enok.\n我？嗯，你也知道，我叫 Sylrissa。我和 Enok 一起住在这片沼泽里。"

    old "There are other nagas, most of them living to the east, but I much prefer to live life on the edge. Enok is my only real companion, and that's fine with me. I don't need anyone else slowing me down. Exploring, getting into trouble, and seeing the unexpected. Life is so much more fun when you don't know what's coming next, isn't it?"
    new "There are other nagas, most of them living to the east, but I much prefer to live life on the edge. Enok is my only real companion, and that's fine with me. I don't need anyone else slowing me down. Exploring, getting into trouble, and seeing the unexpected. Life is so much more fun when you don't know what's coming next, isn't it?\n这里还有别的 Naga，大多住在东边，但我更喜欢过这种活在刀尖上的日子。Enok 是我唯一的真正同伴，这样挺好。我不需要别人来拖我后腿。四处探索、惹点麻烦、见识意外之事——当生活充满未知时，才有意思得多，不是吗？"

    old "Yes, it is. And I should know a thing or two about that. After all, I came out here to this swamp without knowing what was awaiting me. And it turned out to be quite exciting."
    new "Yes, it is. And I should know a thing or two about that. After all, I came out here to this swamp without knowing what was awaiting me. And it turned out to be quite exciting.\n是啊，确实如此。对此我也略知一二。毕竟，我来这片沼泽时，也不知道等待我的是什么。结果还挺刺激的。"

    old "After all, I got to meet you."
    new "After all, I got to meet you.\n毕竟，我遇见了你。"

    old "Sylrissa is beaming."
    new "Sylrissa is beaming.\nSylrissa 笑容满面。"

    old "See, you understand. Life is one grand adventure, and it would be a shame to try and make it anything else."
    new "See, you understand. Life is one grand adventure, and it would be a shame to try and make it anything else.\n瞧，你懂的。人生就是一场盛大的冒险，硬要把它过成别的样子，那才可惜。"

    old "'Fun' isn't the word I'd use to describe it. Unexpected outcomes aren't always good."
    new "'Fun' isn't the word I'd use to describe it. Unexpected outcomes aren't always good.\n我可不会用“有趣”来形容它。意外的结果并不总是好事。"

    old "But that's what makes it so much fun! Something amazing could happen today, or something awful. And the fact that bad things can happen makes the good things so much better."
    new "But that's what makes it so much fun! Something amazing could happen today, or something awful. And the fact that bad things can happen makes the good things so much better.\n可这正是它有趣的地方啊！今天可能发生美妙的事，也可能发生糟糕的事。而正因为坏事可能发生，好事才显得格外珍贵。"

    old "You must know a thing or two about that. You're an adventurer, aren't you? You came out here to this swamp, anyway."
    new "You must know a thing or two about that. You're an adventurer, aren't you? You came out here to this swamp, anyway.\n对此你一定颇有体会。你是个冒险者，对吧？毕竟你都跑到这片沼泽来了。"

    old "Indeed I did. And this is far from my first escapade."
    new "Indeed I did. And this is far from my first escapade.\n我确实来了。而且这远不是我第一次冒险了。"

    old "So, what's the most thrilling thing you've gotten to do?"
    new "So, what's the most thrilling thing you've gotten to do?\n那么，你做过的最刺激的事是什么？"

    old "Well, I've come face to face with the undead. That was quite an experience."
    new "Well, I've come face to face with the undead. That was quite an experience.\n嗯，我和亡灵正面交过手。那可真是一段难忘的经历。"

    old "Sylrissa claps her hands."
    new "Sylrissa claps her hands.\nSylrissa 拍了拍手。"

    old "Undead. How exciting. You know, I've always wanted to meet a vampire. I hear their eyes glow. Just like mine."
    new "Undead. How exciting. You know, I've always wanted to meet a vampire. I hear their eyes glow. Just like mine.\n亡灵。多刺激啊。你知道吗，我一直想见见吸血鬼。听说他们的眼睛会发光。就像我的一样。"

    old "You'd like to befriend a vampire?"
    new "You'd like to befriend a vampire?\n你想和吸血鬼交朋友？"

    old "Befriend? Oh, heavens no. How can you trust someone who's undead? They're dead, but they're also not? How does that even work?"
    new "Befriend? Oh, heavens no. How can you trust someone who's undead? They're dead, but they're also not? How does that even work?\n交朋友？哦，天哪，才不。你怎么能信任一个不死之物？他们死了，可又没死？这到底是怎么回事？"

    old "If I ever met a vampire, I'd very much enjoy having the chance to dance with them, and then have a pleasant chat with them, and then slice them up a bit with my blade. No better way to get to know someone than from the inside out, don't you think?"
    new "If I ever met a vampire, I'd very much enjoy having the chance to dance with them, and then have a pleasant chat with them, and then slice them up a bit with my blade. No better way to get to know someone than from the inside out, don't you think?\n要是我真遇见吸血鬼，我会很乐意先和他们跳支舞，再愉快地聊上几句，然后拿我的刀把他们切开一点。想真正了解一个人，没有比从里到外看个明白更好的办法了，你不觉得吗？"

    old "Should I be worried that you'll try to disembowel me?"
    new "Should I be worried that you'll try to disembowel me?\n我是不是该担心你会想把我开膛破肚？"

    old "What? No, I'd never do something like that. After all, we're friends, remember?"
    new "What? No, I'd never do something like that. After all, we're friends, remember?\n什么？不，我绝不会做那种事。毕竟，我们是朋友，记得吗？"

    old "Well, that's-"
    new "Well, that's-\n呃，这——"

    old "A lone lizardman stumbles into the clearing and looks at us with an expression of shock."
    new "A lone lizardman stumbles into the clearing and looks at us with an expression of shock.\n一个落单的 Lizardman 跌跌撞撞闯进空地，一脸震惊地看着我们。"

    old "He must be a lone scout. It wouldn't do to let him report back to his friends, would it?"
    new "He must be a lone scout. It wouldn't do to let him report back to his friends, would it?\n他一定是个落单的侦察兵。可不能让他回去向同伴报信，对吧？"

    old "Let's make this quick."
    new "Let's make this quick.\n我们速战速决。"

    old "Looks like I missed all the fun."
    new "Looks like I missed all the fun.\n看来我错过了所有好戏。"

    old "He was alone, but we should get moving before more come along. Enok?"
    new "He was alone, but we should get moving before more come along. Enok?\n他是独自一个，但我们得趁更多同伴赶来之前动身。Enok？"

    old "The southern part of the swamp is thick with lizardmen. I know a detour to the east that we can take."
    new "The southern part of the swamp is thick with lizardmen. I know a detour to the east that we can take.\n沼泽南部遍布 Lizardman。我知道一条向东的绕行路线可以走。"

    old "Then let's go."
    new "Then let's go.\n那我们走。"

    old "As we march eastward, I notice Enok's eyes darting around, as if looking for something."
    new "As we march eastward, I notice Enok's eyes darting around, as if looking for something.\n我们向东行进时，我注意到 Enok 的眼神四处游移，仿佛在寻找什么。"

    old "Enok, are you alright? You seem tense."
    new "Enok, are you alright? You seem tense.\nEnok，你没事吧？你看起来紧绷绷的。"

    old "Hm? Ah, I'm just, a bit nervous. You never know what could be lurking about."
    new "Hm? Ah, I'm just, a bit nervous. You never know what could be lurking about.\n嗯？啊，我只是，有点紧张。谁知道附近潜伏着什么。"

    old "Enok, why don't you wait here with [protag] while I go scout ahead? I'll see if I can find a more direct route to exit the swamp."
    new "Enok, why don't you wait here with [protag] while I go scout ahead? I'll see if I can find a more direct route to exit the swamp.\nEnok，你先留在这里陪 [protag]，我去前面侦察一下怎么样？我去看看能不能找到一条更直接的出沼泽路线。"

    old "Enok relaxes and the tension in his shoulders lessens a bit."
    new "Enok relaxes and the tension in his shoulders lessens a bit.\nEnok 放松下来，肩头的紧绷也略略缓和了些。"

    old "That may be best."
    new "That may be best.\n那样或许最好。"

    old "Sylrissa heads, off, leaving me alone with Enok."
    new "Sylrissa heads, off, leaving me alone with Enok.\nSylrissa 离开了，留下我和 Enok 单独相处。"

    old "What was that all about?"
    new "What was that all about?\n刚才那是怎么回事？"

    old "I guess there's no point in hiding it. To put it simply, we're nearing naga territory, and I'm afraid of running into one of them."
    new "I guess there's no point in hiding it. To put it simply, we're nearing naga territory, and I'm afraid of running into one of them.\n我想再隐瞒也没什么意义了。简单来说，我们正靠近 Naga 的领地，我怕撞见他们中的某一个。"

    old "You're afraid of your own kind?"
    new "You're afraid of your own kind?\n你害怕自己的同类？"

    old "Yes. I'm...not exactly welcome among my fellow naga."
    new "Yes. I'm...not exactly welcome among my fellow naga.\n是的。我在 Naga 同胞当中……并不太受欢迎。"

    old "You are nice to ask. You could say that I don't get along well with most nagas."
    new "You are nice to ask. You could say that I don't get along well with most nagas.\n谢谢你这么问。可以说，我和大多数 Naga 都处不来。"

    old "Nagas kill many things. Anyone who steps into naga territory unwelcome is likely to made into a meal. Naga kill all the time, without provocation. There are very few rules and laws among naga restricting what we can and can't kill."
    new "Nagas kill many things. Anyone who steps into naga territory unwelcome is likely to made into a meal. Naga kill all the time, without provocation. There are very few rules and laws among naga restricting what we can and can't kill.\nNaga 杀戮成性。任何不受欢迎地踏入 Naga 领地的人，都可能被做成一顿美餐。Naga 无时无刻不在杀戮，哪怕毫无挑衅。Naga 之中，几乎没有约束我们什么能杀、什么不能杀的规矩和律法。"

    old "Sylrissa, she's not like me. She left the community of her own free will. Naga society is very traditional, and Sylrissa isn't much for tradition. Her views on killing are also similar to my own, although unlike me, Sylrissa is without sin."
    new "Sylrissa, she's not like me. She left the community of her own free will. Naga society is very traditional, and Sylrissa isn't much for tradition. Her views on killing are also similar to my own, although unlike me, Sylrissa is without sin.\n而 Sylrissa，她和我不一样。她是自愿离开族群的。Naga 社会非常守旧，而 Sylrissa 不太吃传统那一套。她对杀戮的看法也与我相似，不过与我不同，Sylrissa 没有罪孽。"

    old "I'm thankful to have her. In a way, we look after each other. I was alone and needed a companion. And in a way, she did, too."
    new "I'm thankful to have her. In a way, we look after each other. I was alone and needed a companion. And in a way, she did, too.\n我很感激有她在身边。从某种意义上说，我们彼此照应。我曾经孤身一人，需要个同伴。而她也一样。"

    old "What about Sylrissa? She doesn't seem to share your reservations."
    new "What about Sylrissa? She doesn't seem to share your reservations.\n那 Sylrissa 呢？她似乎没有你这样的顾虑。"

    old "Sylrissa is different. She left of her own volition."
    new "Sylrissa is different. She left of her own volition.\nSylrissa 不一样。她是自愿离开的。"

    old "Sylrissa left because she doesn't like naga society. I left because naga society doesn't like me."
    new "Sylrissa left because she doesn't like naga society. I left because naga society doesn't like me.\nSylrissa 离开，是因为她不喜欢 Naga 社会。我离开，是因为 Naga 社会不喜欢我。"

    old "What is it about naga society that Sylrissa finds distasteful?"
    new "What is it about naga society that Sylrissa finds distasteful?\nSylrissa 讨厌 Naga 社会的什么地方？"

    old "Nagas have very few rules when it comes to killing. Anyone who steps into naga territory unwelcome is likely to made into a meal. Naga kill all the time, without provocation."
    new "Nagas have very few rules when it comes to killing. Anyone who steps into naga territory unwelcome is likely to made into a meal. Naga kill all the time, without provocation.\nNaga 在杀戮方面几乎没有规矩。任何不受欢迎地踏入 Naga 领地的人，都可能被做成一顿美餐。Naga 无时无刻不在杀戮，哪怕毫无挑衅。"

    old "In a way, that's what led to me leaving naga society behind."
    new "In a way, that's what led to me leaving naga society behind.\n从某种意义上说，正是这一点导致我离开了 Naga 社会。"

    old "Do you want to talk about it?"
    new "Do you want to talk about it?\n你想谈谈吗？"

    old "Not particularly. But I had the feeling you were going to ask about it."
    new "Not particularly. But I had the feeling you were going to ask about it.\n不太想。但我有预感你会问起。"

    old "You seem bothered by the fact."
    new "You seem bothered by the fact.\n你似乎对此耿耿于怀。"

    old "I'm not bothered by the fact that you wanted to ask. But I dislike it when people try to conceal their intentions."
    new "I'm not bothered by the fact that you wanted to ask. But I dislike it when people try to conceal their intentions.\n你想问，我并不介意。但我讨厌别人掩饰自己的意图。"

    old "Hmm...given what I've seen of Sylrissa's outspoken personality, and Enok's preference for people who openly speak their intentions, it's no wonder the two seem to get along so well."
    new "Hmm...given what I've seen of Sylrissa's outspoken personality, and Enok's preference for people who openly speak their intentions, it's no wonder the two seem to get along so well.\n嗯……想想我见识过的 Sylrissa 那心直口快的个性，再加上 Enok 偏爱坦诚直说的人，难怪这两人看起来如此合拍。"

    old "I'm sorry. I just wasn't sure if you wanted to explain it."
    new "I'm sorry. I just wasn't sure if you wanted to explain it.\n抱歉。我只是不确定你想不想说。"

    old "Well, as I said before, I'm none too keen to encounter another naga. But as you might imagine, it wasn't always this way. There was...an incident."
    new "Well, as I said before, I'm none too keen to encounter another naga. But as you might imagine, it wasn't always this way. There was...an incident.\n嗯，正如我之前所说，我很不乐意再遇到别的 Naga。但你能想象得到，事情并非一直如此。曾经发生过……一件事。"

    old "Sylrissa and I, well, we get along fine with only each other for company."
    new "Sylrissa and I, well, we get along fine with only each other for company.\nSylrissa 和我，嗯，我们俩彼此作伴，处得挺好。"

    old "For obvious reasons, Sylrissa and I tend to stay away from this part of the swamp. And if I were to run across another naga, things might go very poorly. That's why I've been nervous."
    new "For obvious reasons, Sylrissa and I tend to stay away from this part of the swamp. And if I were to run across another naga, things might go very poorly. That's why I've been nervous.\n出于显而易见的原因，Sylrissa 和我通常会避开沼泽的这一带。而要是撞上另一个 Naga，事情可能会变得很糟。所以我一直很紧张。"

    old "I was with another naga named Simmons who was very liberal about killing. He and I were traveling the southern reaches of the swamp."
    new "I was with another naga named Simmons who was very liberal about killing. He and I were traveling the southern reaches of the swamp.\n我当时和另一个名叫 Simmons 的 Naga 在一起，他对杀戮看得很开。他和我结伴在沼泽南部游历。"

    old "We chanced upon a group of traveling dwarves. They were refugees, displaced from their home and on their way to the human empire, but they had become lost."
    new "We chanced upon a group of traveling dwarves. They were refugees, displaced from their home and on their way to the human empire, but they had become lost.\n我们偶然遇到了一群赶路的 Dwarf。他们是难民，背井离乡，正要去往人类帝国，却迷了路。"

    old "There was no reason for us to attack them. They had no intent of trespassing on our land, and they posed no threat to us. In fact, they were terrified of us. I can still remember them, quaking in their boots, with the painful look of fear etched on their faces."
    new "There was no reason for us to attack them. They had no intent of trespassing on our land, and they posed no threat to us. In fact, they were terrified of us. I can still remember them, quaking in their boots, with the painful look of fear etched on their faces.\n我们没有任何理由攻击他们。他们无意擅闯我们的领地，也不构成任何威胁。事实上，他们怕我们怕得要命。我至今仍记得他们抖得两腿发软、脸上刻满惊恐的样子。"

    old "I would have seen those dwarves on their way and been out of their lives as soon as possible, but Simmons just stood there, looking them up and down, licking his lips."
    new "I would have seen those dwarves on their way and been out of their lives as soon as possible, but Simmons just stood there, looking them up and down, licking his lips.\n我本会送那些 Dwarf 上路，尽快从他们的人生中消失，可 Simmons 只是站在原地，上下打量着他们，舔着嘴唇。"

    old "He watched as they quaked and flinched in fear, and laughed at them."
    new "He watched as they quaked and flinched in fear, and laughed at them.\n他看着他们瑟瑟发抖、畏惧退缩，还哈哈大笑。"

    old "He yelled at them. 'Scream for me,' he said. But they remained silently paralyzed in fear."
    new "He yelled at them. 'Scream for me,' he said. But they remained silently paralyzed in fear.\n他朝他们大吼：“给我叫啊。”他说道。可他们仍吓得僵在原地，默不作声。"

    old "So he walked up to one of them. A little girl. And in an instant, she was dead and bleeding upon the ground."
    new "So he walked up to one of them. A little girl. And in an instant, she was dead and bleeding upon the ground.\n于是他走到其中一个人面前。是个小女孩。眨眼之间，她就倒在地上，浑身是血，没了气息。"

    old "A woman began wailing, and as the other turned to flee, Simmons killed both of them with a ruthless swiftness."
    new "A woman began wailing, and as the other turned to flee, Simmons killed both of them with a ruthless swiftness.\n一个女人开始放声痛哭，另一个人转身想逃，Simmons 却以残忍的迅捷把两人都杀了。"

    old "All those lives, wiped out in the blink of an eye."
    new "All those lives, wiped out in the blink of an eye.\n那么多条性命，眨眼间就被抹去。"

    old "I stood silently as Simmons began laughing, looking at me and pointing at their remains. He killed those dwarves for nothing but his own amusement."
    new "I stood silently as Simmons began laughing, looking at me and pointing at their remains. He killed those dwarves for nothing but his own amusement.\n我默默站着，Simmons 开始大笑，看着我又指向他们的残骸。他杀那些 Dwarf，不为别的，只为取乐。"

    old "As I stood there, looking at Simmons's laughing face, I was filled with rage. I took my blade, and removed that laughing head right from his body."
    new "As I stood there, looking at Simmons's laughing face, I was filled with rage. I took my blade, and removed that laughing head right from his body.\n我站在那里，望着 Simmons 那张大笑的脸，胸中充满怒火。我拔出刀，把那颗笑着的头颅从他身上砍了下来。"

    old "As I said, there are few rules restricting when nagas may and may not kill."
    new "As I said, there are few rules restricting when nagas may and may not kill.\n正如我所说，几乎没有什么规矩限制 Naga 何时能杀、何时不能杀。"

    old "In fact, there is only one rule. Naga must never kill naga."
    new "In fact, there is only one rule. Naga must never kill naga.\n事实上，只有一条规矩。Naga 绝不可杀 Naga。"

    old "I broke that rule. And consequently, I live in exile."
    new "I broke that rule. And consequently, I live in exile.\n我打破了那条规矩。因此，我活在流亡之中。"

    old "Hey, you two. Hope you didn't get bored waiting for me."
    new "Hey, you two. Hope you didn't get bored waiting for me.\n嘿，你们两个。希望你们等我的时候没觉得无聊。"

    old "Not at all. Are you ready to lead us out of here?"
    new "Not at all. Are you ready to lead us out of here?\n一点也没有。你准备好带我们离开这里了吗？"

    old "Indeed I am."
    new "Indeed I am.\n准备好了。"

    old "Sylrissa leads us southward in a twisting path. Several minutes later, we find ourselves embedded deep within the southern region of the swamp. I begin to see formations that look familiar."
    new "Sylrissa leads us southward in a twisting path. Several minutes later, we find ourselves embedded deep within the southern region of the swamp. I begin to see formations that look familiar.\nSylrissa 领着我们在蜿蜒的小路上向南走。几分钟后，我们已深入沼泽南部腹地。我开始看到一些似曾相识的地形。"

    old "Sylrissa leads us through some thick reeds, and stops cold. She holds up a hand and puts a finger to her lips."
    new "Sylrissa leads us through some thick reeds, and stops cold. She holds up a hand and puts a finger to her lips.\nSylrissa 带着我们穿过一片茂密的芦苇丛，骤然停下。她举起一只手，把食指竖在唇边。"

    old "I creep forward silently and peer through the reeds. A pair of lizardmen are passing by."
    new "I creep forward silently and peer through the reeds. A pair of lizardmen are passing by.\n我悄悄向前挪动，透过芦苇窥探。两个 Lizardman 正从旁经过。"

    old "Sylrissa whispers."
    new "Sylrissa whispers.\nSylrissa 低声说。"

    old "What should we do?"
    new "What should we do?\n我们该怎么办？"

    old "Stay down."
    new "Stay down.\n趴下别动。"

    old "We all lower ourselves to the ground, and watch as the lizardmen pass."
    new "We all lower ourselves to the ground, and watch as the lizardmen pass.\n我们纷纷伏低身子，看着 Lizardman 走过。"

    old "Once the beasts are out of sight, Enok speaks up."
    new "Once the beasts are out of sight, Enok speaks up.\n等那两只野兽消失在视线之外，Enok 开口了。"

    old "Sneaking has gotten us this far. We're not going to start picking fights now, not when we have no idea how many lizardmen might be waiting to reinforce whoever we pounce on."
    new "Sneaking has gotten us this far. We're not going to start picking fights now, not when we have no idea how many lizardmen might be waiting to reinforce whoever we pounce on.\n悄悄摸进来已经让我们走到这一步了。现在不是主动挑事的时候，何况我们根本不知道有多少 Lizardman 会来增援被我们偷袭的同伴。"

    old "If we're going to sneak our way out of this swamp, we need to send someone to scout the way out of here. Three of us moving forward at once with no sense of what lies ahead is the fastest way for us to get caught."
    new "If we're going to sneak our way out of this swamp, we need to send someone to scout the way out of here. Three of us moving forward at once with no sense of what lies ahead is the fastest way for us to get caught.\n要悄悄摸出这片沼泽，就得派人去侦察出去的路。我们三个对前方一无所知却同时前进，是最快暴露的方法。"

    old "Right. I'll scout ahead."
    new "Right. I'll scout ahead.\n对。我去前面侦察。"

    old "No, I will."
    new "No, I will.\n不，我去。"

    old "Enok, don't you trust me?"
    new "Enok, don't you trust me?\nEnok，你不信任我吗？"

    old "It's not a matter of trust. If someone's going to take risks, it should be me."
    new "It's not a matter of trust. If someone's going to take risks, it should be me.\n这跟信不信任无关。要冒险，也该由我来。"

    old "[protag], settle this argument for us, will you?"
    new "[protag], settle this argument for us, will you?\n[protag]，替我们做个了断，好吗？"

    old "Neither of you needs to go. I will. I got myself into this swamp, and I can get myself out."
    new "Neither of you needs to go. I will. I got myself into this swamp, and I can get myself out.\n你们谁都不用去。我去。是我自己闯进这片沼泽的，我自己也能出去。"

    old "Enok shakes his head."
    new "Enok shakes his head.\nEnok 摇了摇头。"

    old "Out of the question. Tell me, did you encounter any lizardmen on your way into this swamp?"
    new "Out of the question. Tell me, did you encounter any lizardmen on your way into this swamp?\n绝对不行。告诉我，你进这片沼泽的路上有没有遇到 Lizardmen？"

    old "No, I didn't see any until after I met up with you."
    new "No, I didn't see any until after I met up with you.\n没有，我是在和你碰面之后才看到的。"

    old "Exactly. You know nothing about how the lizardmen move, how to avoid them, or how to fight them alone if worse comes to worst."
    new "Exactly. You know nothing about how the lizardmen move, how to avoid them, or how to fight them alone if worse comes to worst.\n正是如此。你根本不知道 Lizardmen 如何行动、如何躲避它们，更不知道万一情况糟到极点，该如何独自与它们作战。"

    old "We appreciate your intentions, but Enok and I know this swamp. Let us help you. We won't take no for an answer."
    new "We appreciate your intentions, but Enok and I know this swamp. Let us help you. We won't take no for an answer.\n我们很感激你的好意，但 Enok 和我熟悉这片沼泽。让我们帮你吧。这事我们可不会让你拒绝。"

    old "Sylrissa, let Enok go."
    new "Sylrissa, let Enok go.\nSylrissa，放 Enok 走吧。"

    old "You asked me to settle the argument, so I did. Let him go. We'll wait for you here, Enok."
    new "You asked me to settle the argument, so I did. Let him go. We'll wait for you here, Enok.\n是你让我来解决这场争执的，所以我照做了。放他走吧。我们在这里等你，Enok。"

    old "Enok nods. He turns to Sylrissa and whispers something in her ear, then leaves us behind in pursuit of an exit."
    new "Enok nods. He turns to Sylrissa and whispers something in her ear, then leaves us behind in pursuit of an exit.\nEnok 点点头。他转向 Sylrissa，在她耳边低语了几句，然后离开我们，去找出口了。"

    old "Sylrissa and I wait in silence for a new moments before Sylrissa begins squirming."
    new "Sylrissa and I wait in silence for a new moments before Sylrissa begins squirming.\nSylrissa 和我沉默地等了一小会儿，接着 Sylrissa 开始坐立不安起来。"

    old "Aren't you going to ask me what Enok said to me before he left?"
    new "Aren't you going to ask me what Enok said to me before he left?\n你不打算问我，Enok 离开前对我说了什么吗？"

    old "I figured it was for your ears only. Why else would he have whispered it only to you?"
    new "I figured it was for your ears only. Why else would he have whispered it only to you?\n我想那话是只说给你听的。不然他何必只对你一个人耳语？"

    old "Oh. I suppose that makes sense."
    new "Oh. I suppose that makes sense.\n哦，我想这么说也有道理。"

    old "I didn't see any of these lizardmen on my way in. How do you suppose it is that they've come this far south in such a short time?"
    new "I didn't see any of these lizardmen on my way in. How do you suppose it is that they've come this far south in such a short time?\n我进来的路上一个 Lizardmen 都没看见。你觉得他们是怎么在这么短的时间里跑到这么南边来的？"

    old "The lizardmen are very territorial beasts. It wouldn't surprise me if you left a few tracks on the way in."
    new "The lizardmen are very territorial beasts. It wouldn't surprise me if you left a few tracks on the way in.\nLizardmen 是领地意识很强的野兽。你要是进来时留下了些足迹，我也不觉得奇怪。"

    old "I look at the ground in shame."
    new "I look at the ground in shame.\n我羞愧地低头看着地面。"

    old "I hadn't considered that."
    new "I hadn't considered that.\n这我倒没想到。"

    old "Oh, don't look sad. It's an easy mistake to make."
    new "Oh, don't look sad. It's an easy mistake to make.\n哦，别难过。这种错误很容易犯。"

    old "Well, I guess I can say I've learned a lesson about learning to cover my own tracks."
    new "Well, I guess I can say I've learned a lesson about learning to cover my own tracks.\n嗯，我想我可以说是上了一课，学会了要掩盖自己的行踪。"

    old "And that's what counts, right? Getting better every day, learning to deal with the challenges the world throws at you. Life wouldn't be life if everything only went right all the time."
    new "And that's what counts, right? Getting better every day, learning to deal with the challenges the world throws at you. Life wouldn't be life if everything only went right all the time.\n这才是最重要的，对吧？每天进步一点，学会应对这个世界抛给你的挑战。如果事事都一帆风顺，生活也就不成其为生活了。"

    old "As we wait, the tension begins to grow thicker. Sylrissa begin picking at the scales on the back of her hand."
    new "As we wait, the tension begins to grow thicker. Sylrissa begin picking at the scales on the back of her hand.\n等待的时候，紧张的气氛越来越浓。Sylrissa 开始抠起她手背上的鳞片。"

    old "Sylrissa looks down at her hands and folds them."
    new "Sylrissa looks down at her hands and folds them.\nSylrissa 低头看着自己的双手，然后把它们交叠起来。"

    old "Sorry, bad habit. I sometimes do it when I feel nervous. When I was a little girl, sometimes I would pick at my scales so much that I'd start to bleed."
    new "Sorry, bad habit. I sometimes do it when I feel nervous. When I was a little girl, sometimes I would pick at my scales so much that I'd start to bleed.\n抱歉，这是个坏习惯。我紧张的时候有时会这样。小时候，我有时会把自己的鳞片抠到出血。"

    old "Sylrissa paces and looks around."
    new "Sylrissa paces and looks around.\nSylrissa 来回踱步，四处张望。"

    old "Enok shouldn't be taking this long."
    new "Enok shouldn't be taking this long.\nEnok 不该去这么久。"

    old "Do you think something happened to him? Maybe he got caught?"
    new "Do you think something happened to him? Maybe he got caught?\n你觉得他是不是出事了？也许他被抓了？"

    old "I'm afraid he may have."
    new "I'm afraid he may have.\n恐怕有可能。"

    old "I think the costs of continuing to wait may outweigh the benefits."
    new "I think the costs of continuing to wait may outweigh the benefits.\n我觉得继续等下去的代价，可能已经超过了收益。"

    old "I think so too. Let's go."
    new "I think so too. Let's go.\n我也这么想。我们走吧。"

    old "I allow Sylrissa to lead the way. As we walk, I become more attentive to the ground, noticing the footprints of what I can only presume must be the lizardmen."
    new "I allow Sylrissa to lead the way. As we walk, I become more attentive to the ground, noticing the footprints of what I can only presume must be the lizardmen.\n我让 Sylrissa 带路。行走时，我更加留意地面，注意到了那些我只敢断定是 Lizardmen 的脚印。"

    old "We're getting close to the edge of the swamp. Enok must be somewhere nearby."
    new "We're getting close to the edge of the swamp. Enok must be somewhere nearby.\n我们快到沼泽边缘了。Enok 一定就在附近。"

    old "We push forward through a wall of towering reeds, and Sylrissa stops cold."
    new "We push forward through a wall of towering reeds, and Sylrissa stops cold.\n我们穿过一堵高耸的芦苇墙，Sylrissa 猛地停住了。"

    old "Oh no."
    new "Oh no.\n哦，不。"

    old "I look over Sylrissa's shoulder, and see a line of lizardmen, all marching single file. I count nine, ten, eleven...there's twelve of them."
    new "I look over Sylrissa's shoulder, and see a line of lizardmen, all marching single file. I count nine, ten, eleven...there's twelve of them.\n我越过 Sylrissa 的肩头看去，只见一队 Lizardmen 排成单列行进。我数着：九、十、十一……一共十二个。"

    old "The three lizardmen at the end of the line are carrying something long and scaly."
    new "The three lizardmen at the end of the line are carrying something long and scaly.\n队伍末尾的三个 Lizardmen 抬着一件又长又带鳞的东西。"

    old "Is that..."
    new "Is that...\n那是……"

    old "It's his tail."
    new "It's his tail.\n是他的尾巴。"

    old "Sylrissa lets out an audible sob, and one of the lizardmen turns toward us."
    new "Sylrissa lets out an audible sob, and one of the lizardmen turns toward us.\nSylrissa 发出一声清晰的啜泣，一个 Lizardman 朝我们转过身来。"

    old "I hear the lizardman bellow, and eleven other heads turn to face us."
    new "I hear the lizardman bellow, and eleven other heads turn to face us.\n我听到那 Lizardman 一声咆哮，另外十一个脑袋齐齐转向我们。"

    old "Sylrissa, they see us."
    new "Sylrissa, they see us.\nSylrissa，他们看到我们了。"

    old "Enok-"
    new "Enok-\nEnok——"

    old "We have to go. {i}Now{/i}."
    new "We have to go. {i}Now{/i}.\n我们得走了。{i}现在{/i}。"

    old "Sylrissa nods with tears in her eyes, and we dash south with the lizardmen in hot pursuit, hoping against hope that there aren't any lizardmen waiting ahead of us."
    new "Sylrissa nods with tears in her eyes, and we dash south with the lizardmen in hot pursuit, hoping against hope that there aren't any lizardmen waiting ahead of us.\nSylrissa 眼含泪水地点点头，我们向南狂奔，Lizardmen 在身后紧追不舍，心中默默祈祷前方不要有 Lizardmen 埋伏。"

    old "After minutes of running, I arrive out of breath at the edge of the swamp. A river runs in front of us."
    new "After minutes of running, I arrive out of breath at the edge of the swamp. A river runs in front of us.\n跑了几分钟后，我气喘吁吁地来到沼泽边缘。一条河横在我们面前。"

    old "[protag], get behind me and wrap your arms around me."
    new "[protag], get behind me and wrap your arms around me.\n[protag]，到我身后来，抱住我。"

    old "I grab hold of Sylrissa, and she leaps into the river."
    new "I grab hold of Sylrissa, and she leaps into the river.\n我紧紧抓住 Sylrissa，她纵身跃入河中。"

    old "I find myself immersed in the cold embrace of the water, and I feel the current of the river assaulting my body, as if trying to tear me away from Sylrissa. I lock my arms around her, and hold on for dear life."
    new "I find myself immersed in the cold embrace of the water, and I feel the current of the river assaulting my body, as if trying to tear me away from Sylrissa. I lock my arms around her, and hold on for dear life.\n我整个人浸入冰冷的河水之中，河水的激流冲击着我的身体，仿佛要把我从 Sylrissa 身边撕开。我双臂紧紧锁住她，拼死也不松手。"

    old "I feel a force pressing down on my head, growing more and more intense and painful, until suddenly everything goes black."
    new "I feel a force pressing down on my head, growing more and more intense and painful, until suddenly everything goes black.\n我感到一股力量压在我的头上，越来越重、越来越疼，直到眼前突然一片漆黑。"

    old "[protag]? [protag]!"
    new "[protag]? [protag]!\n[protag]？[protag]！"

    old "I try to open my mouth, but what comes out is a fit of sputtering and coughing."
    new "I try to open my mouth, but what comes out is a fit of sputtering and coughing.\n我试着张开嘴，却只发出阵阵呛水和咳嗽。"

    old "Where are we?"
    new "Where are we?\n我们在哪儿？"

    old "We're down river. It was the only way I could think to get away."
    new "We're down river. It was the only way I could think to get away.\n我们在下游。这是我能想到的唯一的脱身办法。"

    old "They got him. If they got his tail, there's no way he escaped."
    new "They got him. If they got his tail, there's no way he escaped.\n他们抓到他了。既然他们拿到了他的尾巴，那他绝不可能逃脱。"

    old "I place my hands on the ground and force myself to sit up."
    new "I place my hands on the ground and force myself to sit up.\n我把双手撑在地上，强迫自己坐起身来。"

    old "If they got Enok, he's gone. There's no bringing him back."
    new "If they got Enok, he's gone. There's no bringing him back.\n如果他们抓到了 Enok，那他就完了。没有可能把他带回来了。"

    old "But where does that leave me?"
    new "But where does that leave me?\n可这样一来，我又该何去何从？"

    old "I don't know, Sylrissa."
    new "I don't know, Sylrissa.\n我不知道，Sylrissa。"

    old "What are you going? Where are you going?"
    new "What are you going? Where are you going?\n你要做什么？你要去哪里？"

    old "Me? I have responsibilities in Grimoire. That's where I have to head back to."
    new "Me? I have responsibilities in Grimoire. That's where I have to head back to.\n我吗？我在 Grimoire 还有职责在身。我必须回那里去。"

    old "That's right. You're hunting vampires, aren't you?"
    new "That's right. You're hunting vampires, aren't you?\n没错。你在猎杀 Vampires，对吧？"

    old "Do you think...do you think that I could join you? I'm not sure what else I have to do with myself at this point."
    new "Do you think...do you think that I could join you? I'm not sure what else I have to do with myself at this point.\n你觉得……你觉得我能加入你吗？事到如今，我也不知道自己还能做些什么。"

    old "You want to come with me?"
    new "You want to come with me?\n你想跟我一起走？"

    old "Well, I can't live in a human city. Or won't, is more accurate. I don't think I'd get along well with humans. This..."
    new "Well, I can't live in a human city. Or won't, is more accurate. I don't think I'd get along well with humans. This...\n嗯，我无法在人类的城市里生活。更准确地说，是不愿意。我想我和人类相处不来。这里……"

    old "Sylrissa gestures behind her, in the direction of the swamp."
    new "Sylrissa gestures behind her, in the direction of the swamp.\nSylrissa 朝她身后比了比，指向沼泽的方向。"

    old "This is still my home. But when you're ready to go and explore N'Mar, or if you need my 'skills' for something else, I'll join you."
    new "This is still my home. But when you're ready to go and explore N'Mar, or if you need my 'skills' for something else, I'll join you.\n这里仍是我的家。但等你准备好去探索 N'Mar，或者需要我的“本事”去做别的事，我就会加入你。"

    old "I'd be grateful if you would."
    new "I'd be grateful if you would.\n如果你愿意，我会很感激。"

    old "And I hope you'll come back to visit me in the swamp some time. I know you're busy, but...I'm here if you ever need me for something besides fighting."
    new "And I hope you'll come back to visit me in the swamp some time. I know you're busy, but...I'm here if you ever need me for something besides fighting.\n我也希望你以后能回沼泽来看看我。我知道你很忙，但……除了战斗之外，只要你需要我，我都在这里。"

    old "I won't forget about you, Sylrissa. I'll come back here again. I can't guarantee when, but you haven't seen the last of me."
    new "I won't forget about you, Sylrissa. I'll come back here again. I can't guarantee when, but you haven't seen the last of me.\n我不会忘记你的，Sylrissa。我会再回到这里来。我不能保证什么时候，但你不会再也见不到我。"

    old "Thanks."
    new "Thanks.\n谢谢。"

    old "Are you hurt anywhere?"
    new "Are you hurt anywhere?\n你哪里受伤了吗？"

    old "I stand up, and take a few steps."
    new "I stand up, and take a few steps.\n我站起身来，走了几步。"

    old "I'm good enough to travel."
    new "I'm good enough to travel.\n我身体还行，可以赶路。"

    old "Well then, enjoy your journey, wherever it takes you."
    new "Well then, enjoy your journey, wherever it takes you.\n那么，祝你旅途愉快，无论它把你带向何方。"

    old "And [protag], please keep the money."
    new "And [protag], please keep the money.\n还有，[protag]，请把那些钱留着。"

    old "Sylrissa hands me the satchel full of gold coins I found in the swamps."
    new "Sylrissa hands me the satchel full of gold coins I found in the swamps.\nSylrissa 把那个装满金币的袋子递给我——那是我在沼泽里找到的。"

    old "Thanks! But...are you sure?"
    new "Thanks! But...are you sure?\n谢谢！不过……你确定吗？"

    old "I like the gems more anyway."
    new "I like the gems more anyway.\n反正我更喜欢宝石。"

    old "Sylrissa turns around and dives back into the river."
    new "Sylrissa turns around and dives back into the river.\nSylrissa 转过身，再次跃入河中。"

    old "Enok, I think you should let Sylrissa go."
    new "Enok, I think you should let Sylrissa go.\nEnok，我想你应该放 Sylrissa 走。"

    old "Fine. I can't argue with the both of you."
    new "Fine. I can't argue with the both of you.\n好吧。我拗不过你们俩。"

    old "Don't you worry. I'll be back before you know it."
    new "Don't you worry. I'll be back before you know it.\n别担心。我很快就会回来，快到你还没察觉。"

    old "Sylrissa gives a wave over her shoulder as she leaves."
    new "Sylrissa gives a wave over her shoulder as she leaves.\nSylrissa 离开时，回头朝身后挥了挥手。"

    old "These lizardmen, how do you suppose there are so many of them roaming about? I didn't see any of them on the way in, yet the area is thick with them now."
    new "These lizardmen, how do you suppose there are so many of them roaming about? I didn't see any of them on the way in, yet the area is thick with them now.\n这些 Lizardmen，你觉得他们怎么会有这么多在这里游荡？我进来时一个都没看见，可现在这地方到处都是他们。"

    old "Did you leave behind any tracks on your way into the swamp?"
    new "Did you leave behind any tracks on your way into the swamp?\n你进沼泽的路上有没有留下什么足迹？"

    old "I hadn't considered that. You're right, that's probably it."
    new "I hadn't considered that. You're right, that's probably it.\n这我倒没想到。你说得对，多半就是这个原因。"

    old "Well, what's done is done. Looks like you've grown a little bit wiser. We can be better tomorrow than we were today."
    new "Well, what's done is done. Looks like you've grown a little bit wiser. We can be better tomorrow than we were today.\n算了，木已成舟。看来你变得稍微聪明了一点。明天我们可以比今天做得更好。"

    old "We wait in silence several minutes longer. Enok begins pacing about."
    new "We wait in silence several minutes longer. Enok begins pacing about.\n我们又沉默地等了好几分钟。Enok 开始来回踱步。"

    old "I'm just worried about Sylrissa, is all. She shouldn't be taking this long."
    new "I'm just worried about Sylrissa, is all. She shouldn't be taking this long.\n我只是担心 Sylrissa，仅此而已。她不该去这么久。"

    old "Do you think we should go after her, or keep waiting?"
    new "Do you think we should go after her, or keep waiting?\n你觉得我们该去找她，还是继续等下去？"

    old "I think that we stand to lose more by waiting."
    new "I think that we stand to lose more by waiting.\n我觉得再等下去，我们失去的只会更多。"

    old "In that case, let's go."
    new "In that case, let's go.\n既然如此，我们走。"

    old "I follow behind Enok. As we walk, I study the ground ahead of us, noticing the footprints of that I can only presume must be the lizardmen."
    new "I follow behind Enok. As we walk, I study the ground ahead of us, noticing the footprints of that I can only presume must be the lizardmen.\n我跟在 Enok 身后。行走时，我仔细察看前方的地面，注意到了那些我只敢断定是 Lizardmen 的脚印。"

    old "Sylrissa must be near. We'll be at the edge of the swamp before too long."
    new "Sylrissa must be near. We'll be at the edge of the swamp before too long.\nSylrissa 一定就在附近。用不了多久，我们就能到沼泽边缘。"

    old "Enok's pace quickens, and I find myself nearly out of breath as I struggle to keep up."
    new "Enok's pace quickens, and I find myself nearly out of breath as I struggle to keep up.\nEnok 加快了脚步，我拼命跟上，发现自己几乎喘不过气来。"

    old "We push forward through a wall of towering reeds, and are greeted by the sight of a group of lizardmen."
    new "We push forward through a wall of towering reeds, and are greeted by the sight of a group of lizardmen.\n我们穿过一堵高耸的芦苇墙，眼前出现了一群 Lizardmen。"

    old "Six of them are sitting on the ground, cutting and quartering something long and scaly."
    new "Six of them are sitting on the ground, cutting and quartering something long and scaly.\n其中六个坐在地上，正在切割、肢解一件又长又带鳞的东西。"

    old "Syl-"
    new "Syl-\nSyl——"

    old "One of the lizardmen looks up at us and opens its mouth. The others turn and look up at us."
    new "One of the lizardmen looks up at us and opens its mouth. The others turn and look up at us.\n一个 Lizardman 抬头看向我们，张开了嘴。其余的也转过身，抬头看向我们。"

    old "Run."
    new "Run.\n跑。"

    old "Enok dashes southward, and I follow in his wake, bounding over the soft damp ground. I can hear the lizardmen behind us, and I look over my shoulder-"
    new "Enok dashes southward, and I follow in his wake, bounding over the soft damp ground. I can hear the lizardmen behind us, and I look over my shoulder-\nEnok 向南冲去，我紧跟在他身后，在松软潮湿的地面上跳跃奔跑。我能听到身后的 Lizardmen，于是回头看了一眼——"

    old "My foot slips in the mud, and I fall to the ground. Enok lifts me off the ground and slings me over his shoulder as he continues moving forward."
    new "My foot slips in the mud, and I fall to the ground. Enok lifts me off the ground and slings me over his shoulder as he continues moving forward.\n我的脚在泥里一滑，摔倒在地。Enok 把我从地上拎起来，甩到他的肩上，继续向前跑。"

    old "The sound of the lizardmen chasing us grows closer and closer."
    new "The sound of the lizardmen chasing us grows closer and closer.\nLizardmen 追赶我们的声音越来越近。"

    old "Enok looks to the body of water next to us, and tightens his grip on me."
    new "Enok looks to the body of water next to us, and tightens his grip on me.\nEnok 看向我们身旁的那片水域，把我抓得更紧了。"

    old "Close your eyes, and hold your breath."
    new "Close your eyes, and hold your breath.\n闭上眼睛，屏住呼吸。"

    old "I snap my eyes shut and take a deep breath. Enok lurches forward and we plunge into the swamp water."
    new "I snap my eyes shut and take a deep breath. Enok lurches forward and we plunge into the swamp water.\n我猛地闭上眼，深吸一口气。Enok 向前一扑，我们一起扎进了沼泽水里。"

    old "The swamp water feels warm at first, and as we move through the water I can feel it stinging at me, as though I'm being pricked by tiny needles all over my skin."
    new "The swamp water feels warm at first, and as we move through the water I can feel it stinging at me, as though I'm being pricked by tiny needles all over my skin.\n沼泽水起初是温热的，我们在水中前行时，我能感到它刺痛着我，仿佛有无数细针扎遍了我的皮肤。"

    old "Suddenly, the touch of the water turns cold, and I feel a current tearing at my body, as if trying to rip me from Enok's grasp. I feel his arm tighten, squeezing my body into his."
    new "Suddenly, the touch of the water turns cold, and I feel a current tearing at my body, as if trying to rip me from Enok's grasp. I feel his arm tighten, squeezing my body into his.\n突然，水的触感变得冰冷，我感到一股水流撕扯着我的身体，仿佛要把我从 Enok 的怀里拽走。我感到他的手臂收紧，把我紧紧贴在他身上。"

    old "We break the surface, and I gasp for breath. Enok continues swimming, and I open my eyes. We're in the river outside the swamp."
    new "We break the surface, and I gasp for breath. Enok continues swimming, and I open my eyes. We're in the river outside the swamp.\n我们浮出水面，我大口喘着气。Enok 继续向前游，我睁开了眼睛。我们已经在沼泽外的河里了。"

    old "Enok keeps swimming until the current carries us far from where we exited the swamp, leaving the chasing lizardmen far behind us."
    new "Enok keeps swimming until the current carries us far from where we exited the swamp, leaving the chasing lizardmen far behind us.\nEnok 一直游着，直到水流把我们带离离开沼泽的地方很远，把追赶的 Lizardmen 远远甩在身后。"

    old "Enok hefts me onto the riverbank, and I flop on my back, taking long, deep breaths."
    new "Enok hefts me onto the riverbank, and I flop on my back, taking long, deep breaths.\nEnok 把我托上河岸，我仰面瘫倒在地，大口大口地深呼吸。"

    old "Did Sylrissa-"
    new "Did Sylrissa-\nSylrissa 她——"

    old "They got her. They were slicing up her tail when they saw us."
    new "They got her. They were slicing up her tail when they saw us.\n他们抓到了她。他们看见我们时，正在割她的尾巴。"

    old "I don't know what I'm going to do."
    new "I don't know what I'm going to do.\n我不知道自己该怎么办。"

    old "What about you? What's your next step?"
    new "What about you? What's your next step?\n那你呢？你接下来打算怎么做？"

    old "I'm going back to Grimoire. I have responsibilities to the people there."
    new "I'm going back to Grimoire. I have responsibilities to the people there.\n我要回 Grimoire 去。我对那里的人民负有责任。"

    old "Grimoire."
    new "Grimoire.\nGrimoire。"

    old "What responsibilities are you speaking of? What is your task?"
    new "What responsibilities are you speaking of? What is your task?\n你说的是什么责任？你的任务是什么？"

    old "I'm organizing a group of fighters. We're going to assault the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "I'm organizing a group of fighters. We're going to assault the Castle of N'Mar.\n我正在组织一支战斗队伍。我们打算攻打 N'Mar 的城堡。"

    old "N'Mar. Fighting ghouls, hmm?"
    new "N'Mar. Fighting ghouls, hmm?\nN'Mar。去和食尸鬼作战，嗯？"

    old "Yes, whatever foul beings await us within and around the castle, we will fight."
    new "Yes, whatever foul beings await us within and around the castle, we will fight.\n是的，无论城堡内外有什么邪恶的存在等着我们，我们都会战斗。"

    old "It seems that you have a mission. And I'm...well, I'd say right now that I'm in dire need of something to do with myself. Might I accompany you on your quest?"
    new "It seems that you have a mission. And I'm...well, I'd say right now that I'm in dire need of something to do with myself. Might I accompany you on your quest?\n看来你有使命在身。而我呢……嗯，我只能说，此刻我迫切需要找点事做。我能陪你一同去完成这个使命吗？"

    old "When it's time to fight, you'll be one of the people I call upon."
    new "When it's time to fight, you'll be one of the people I call upon.\n到战斗的时候，你将会是我召集的人之一。"

    old "I'll be waiting here in this area of the swamps, where you know you can find me again."
    new "I'll be waiting here in this area of the swamps, where you know you can find me again.\n我会在这片沼泽区域等你，你知道在哪里能找到我。"

    old "And [protag]. Keep the gems."
    new "And [protag]. Keep the gems.\n还有，[protag]，把那些宝石留着。"

    old "Enok hands me the satchel full of precious gems I found in the swamps."
    new "Enok hands me the satchel full of precious gems I found in the swamps.\nEnok 把那个装满珍贵宝石的袋子递给我——那是我在沼泽里找到的。"

    old "Looks like you need this more than me right now."
    new "Looks like you need this more than me right now.\n看来此刻你比我更需要这个。"

    old "Thanks, Enok."
    new "Thanks, Enok.\n谢谢，Enok。"

    old "I raise my hand to block out the sun as I gaze over the desert."
    new "I raise my hand to block out the sun as I gaze over the desert.\n我抬手挡住阳光，眺望着眼前的沙漠。"

    old "Karen did tell me that I'd know the tombs when I saw them, but before I can recognize them, I have to see them. And I seem to have gravely underestimated the size of this desert. Still, I'm well equipped for the journey. If I die out here, it won't be to the heat."
    new "Karen did tell me that I'd know the tombs when I saw them, but before I can recognize them, I have to see them. And I seem to have gravely underestimated the size of this desert. Still, I'm well equipped for the journey. If I die out here, it won't be to the heat.\nKaren 确实告诉过我，看到那些陵墓时我自会认得，但要想认出来，我总得先看到它们。而我似乎严重低估了这片沙漠的广袤。不过，我为这趟旅程做好了充分准备。就算我死在这里，也不会是死于酷热。"

    old "I take a swig from one of the flasks hanging from my belt, allowing the water to slide down my throat. The water seems nearly as hot as the ground I'm standing on, but it serves to quench my thirst, if not soothe my throat. Ah, the indignities an adventurer must suffer."
    new "I take a swig from one of the flasks hanging from my belt, allowing the water to slide down my throat. The water seems nearly as hot as the ground I'm standing on, but it serves to quench my thirst, if not soothe my throat. Ah, the indignities an adventurer must suffer.\n我从腰间挂着的一只水壶里灌了一口，让水流过喉咙。这水几乎和我脚下的地面一样烫，但好歹能解渴，即便不能润嗓。啊，冒险者就非得受这份罪。"

    old "I climb to the top of another hill and look down. Still nothing but the texture of yellow desert as far as the eye can see. Maybe the next summit will give me a better view of what I'm looking for."
    new "I climb to the top of another hill and look down. Still nothing but the texture of yellow desert as far as the eye can see. Maybe the next summit will give me a better view of what I'm looking for.\n我爬上又一座沙丘顶，向下望去。目之所及，仍只是黄色沙漠的纹理，别无他物。也许下一座山脊能让我把要找的东西看得更清楚。"

    old "I begin walking down the hill. I'm about halfway down when the ground begins to move underneath me, and before I know it I'm flat on my back, sliding down on a bed of sand. I close my eyes and brace for the impact, but to my surprise I find myself slow to a halt, giving me a soft landing."
    new "I begin walking down the hill. I'm about halfway down when the ground begins to move underneath me, and before I know it I'm flat on my back, sliding down on a bed of sand. I close my eyes and brace for the impact, but to my surprise I find myself slow to a halt, giving me a soft landing.\n我开始走下山丘。刚下到一半，脚下的地面开始移动，还没等我反应过来，我已经仰面朝天，顺着沙床滑了下去。我闭上眼睛，准备迎接撞击，却惊讶地发现自己缓缓停了下来，轻轻落了地。"

    old "I check my skin for lacerations or bruises. A tumble down any other hill would have left me quite battered, but the fine sand of the desert seems gentle in comparison. I guess today is my lucky day."
    new "I check my skin for lacerations or bruises. A tumble down any other hill would have left me quite battered, but the fine sand of the desert seems gentle in comparison. I guess today is my lucky day.\n我检查自己的皮肤，看有没有擦伤或瘀青。从别的山上这样滚下来，我多半会摔得鼻青脸肿，相比之下，沙漠的细沙倒显得温柔了。我想今天是我的幸运日。"

    old "I begin trekking up the next hill, but several steps up I find the ground giving way underneath me. I continue stepping forward, and I maintain my balance, but with each step I find myself sliding back down. I feel nothing but the soft give of sand beneath my feet, and it seems impossible to get a solid footing."
    new "I begin trekking up the next hill, but several steps up I find the ground giving way underneath me. I continue stepping forward, and I maintain my balance, but with each step I find myself sliding back down. I feel nothing but the soft give of sand beneath my feet, and it seems impossible to get a solid footing.\n我开始攀登下一座山丘，但往上走了几步，脚下的地面就往下陷。我继续迈步，保持着平衡，可每走一步都会往后滑。脚下除了松软的流沙，什么也感觉不到，似乎根本踩不实。"

    old "Ah well. I guess I'll have to find another way around these sand dunes."
    new "Ah well. I guess I'll have to find another way around these sand dunes.\n唉，算了。我想我得另找条路绕过这些沙丘了。"

    old "I turn around and begin climbing up the hill I just came from, but again find myself sliding back into the basin."
    new "I turn around and begin climbing up the hill I just came from, but again find myself sliding back into the basin.\n我转过身，开始攀爬我刚下来的那座山丘，却又发现自己滑回了凹地。"

    old "I guess climbing up a hill isn't always as easy as sliding down."
    new "I guess climbing up a hill isn't always as easy as sliding down.\n我想，爬上山丘可不像滑下来那么容易。"

    old "I begin digging in the sand, hoping to find some solid ground underneath. I get several feet deep before giving up. It seems that I'm surrounded by nothing but sand."
    new "I begin digging in the sand, hoping to find some solid ground underneath. I get several feet deep before giving up. It seems that I'm surrounded by nothing but sand.\n我开始在沙里挖掘，希望能找到下面坚实的土地。挖了好几英尺深，我还是放弃了。看来我四周除了沙子，什么都没有。"

    old "I try to get a running start to try and run up the dune, but my efforts prove fruitless, as my feet sink into the sand with each step."
    new "I try to get a running start to try and run up the dune, but my efforts prove fruitless, as my feet sink into the sand with each step.\n我试着助跑冲上沙丘，但我的努力毫无用处，每走一步，脚都陷进沙里。"

    old "I begin surveying the basin I've fallen into. Walls of sand on each side, what am I to do? Perhaps I need to take a step back and figure this out before I exhaust any more energy in a futile effort to climb the dunes. I sit down and take another sip from my flask."
    new "I begin surveying the basin I've fallen into. Walls of sand on each side, what am I to do? Perhaps I need to take a step back and figure this out before I exhaust any more energy in a futile effort to climb the dunes. I sit down and take another sip from my flask.\n我开始打量自己跌进来的这片凹地。两侧都是沙壁，我该怎么办？也许我该退一步，先想清楚，免得再白费力气去爬沙丘。我坐下来，又喝了一口水。"

    old "As I lower the water from my lips, I look up at the sun overhead, and suddenly find myself aware of just how much water I'm carrying. Four flasks left. That should be enough to last me until sunset. But suppose I do survive until sunset...what then?"
    new "As I lower the water from my lips, I look up at the sun overhead, and suddenly find myself aware of just how much water I'm carrying. Four flasks left. That should be enough to last me until sunset. But suppose I do survive until sunset...what then?\n我把水从唇边放下，抬头望向头顶的太阳，突然意识到自己还剩下多少水。还有四壶水。应该够我撑到日落。但就算我撑到了日落……然后呢？"

    old "I've got to get out of here at some point. It may as well be now."
    new "I've got to get out of here at some point. It may as well be now.\n我总得设法离开这里。不如就趁现在。"

    old "I stand up and feel my feet sink into the sand. Funny, I was sitting on that same patch of sand, yet the moment I try to stand, I find myself beginning to sink into it. Why do I sink more when I stand? I weigh the same sitting as standing, but then, I did have more of my body touching the ground when I was sitting. I wonder..."
    new "I stand up and feel my feet sink into the sand. Funny, I was sitting on that same patch of sand, yet the moment I try to stand, I find myself beginning to sink into it. Why do I sink more when I stand? I weigh the same sitting as standing, but then, I did have more of my body touching the ground when I was sitting. I wonder...\n我站起来，感到双脚陷进沙里。真奇怪，我刚才还坐在同一片沙子上，可一试着站起来，就开始往下陷。为什么我站着时陷得更深？坐着和站着体重一样，不过话说回来，我坐着时身体接触地面的面积确实更大。我想……"

    old "I flop down on my stomach and begin crawling up the sand dune. The sand is loose enough that I find myself sliding back whenever I stop to catch my breath, but still, I'm making upward progress. That's something to be grateful for."
    new "I flop down on my stomach and begin crawling up the sand dune. The sand is loose enough that I find myself sliding back whenever I stop to catch my breath, but still, I'm making upward progress. That's something to be grateful for.\n我趴下身子，开始向沙丘上爬。沙子松得每当我停下喘气，人就会往后滑，但我毕竟还是在向上推进。这一点值得庆幸。"

    old "I look up toward the top of the dune. My upward progress is slow, and after several minutes of crawling, I'm perhaps a third of the way up. The sand is beginning to get stuck in my boots and clothes, but there's nothing for me to do but keep climbing."
    new "I look up toward the top of the dune. My upward progress is slow, and after several minutes of crawling, I'm perhaps a third of the way up. The sand is beginning to get stuck in my boots and clothes, but there's nothing for me to do but keep climbing.\n我抬头望向沙丘顶部。向上爬得很慢，爬了好几分钟，我才大概到了三分之一处。沙子开始钻进我的靴子和衣服，但我别无他法，只能继续爬。"

    old "At last, I crest the top of the dune, and take a moment to sit and catch my breath. I'm about to take another swig of my flask when a shadow covers me."
    new "At last, I crest the top of the dune, and take a moment to sit and catch my breath. I'm about to take another swig of my flask when a shadow covers me.\n终于，我翻过了沙丘顶，坐下来歇口气。正要再灌一口水，一片阴影笼罩了我。"

    old "I look up and see the source of the shadow."
    new "I look up and see the source of the shadow.\n我抬头，看见了阴影的来源。"

    old "I hold up my hands."
    new "I hold up my hands.\n我举起双手。"

    old "I mean you no harm, stranger."
    new "I mean you no harm, stranger.\n我没有恶意，陌生人。"

    old "I'm [protag], from Grimoire."
    new "I'm [protag], from Grimoire.\n我是 [protag]，来自 Grimoire。"

    old "My name is Nuala. Tell me, [protag] from Grimoire, what brings you to this desert? You've been causing quite a disturbance."
    new "My name is Nuala. Tell me, [protag] from Grimoire, what brings you to this desert? You've been causing quite a disturbance.\n我叫 Nuala。告诉我，来自 Grimoire 的 [protag]，是什么风把你吹到这片沙漠来的？你可惹出了不小的动静。"

    old "I don't take kindly to strangers sneaking up on me. I reach for my weapon, just to make sure she knows I mean business."
    new "I don't take kindly to strangers sneaking up on me. I reach for my weapon, just to make sure she knows I mean business.\n我可不喜欢陌生人偷偷靠近。我伸手去拿武器，好让她知道我是认真的。"

    old "I mean you no harm, [prace], but do know that if you attack me, you'll eventually have my friends to contend with."
    new "I mean you no harm, [prace], but do know that if you attack me, you'll eventually have my friends to contend with.\n我对你没有恶意，[prace]，但你要知道，如果你攻击我，最终就得对付我的朋友们。"

    old "She's right, I'm out of my element here, and she appears to be a native of the desert. Even if I did win a fight with this girl, I might not leave the desert alive. Perhaps it's better that I avoid engendering any further hostility."
    new "She's right, I'm out of my element here, and she appears to be a native of the desert. Even if I did win a fight with this girl, I might not leave the desert alive. Perhaps it's better that I avoid engendering any further hostility.\n她说得对，我在这里人生地不熟，而她似乎是沙漠的原住民。就算我真打赢了这个女孩，也未必能活着走出沙漠。也许我最好还是别再挑起敌意了。"

    old "I lower my weapon, and the girl visibly relaxes."
    new "I lower my weapon, and the girl visibly relaxes.\n我放下武器，那女孩明显松了口气。"

    old "Pardon my rudeness. I'm [protag]. I'm from Grimoire."
    new "Pardon my rudeness. I'm [protag]. I'm from Grimoire.\n请原谅我的无礼。我是 [protag]，来自 Grimoire。"

    old "I am called Nuala."
    new "I am called Nuala.\n我叫 Nuala。"

    old "You've been causing quite a disturbance, [protag]."
    new "You've been causing quite a disturbance, [protag].\n你可惹出了不小的动静，[protag]。"

    old "Disturbance? What do you mean? I've been completely alone this whole time."
    new "Disturbance? What do you mean? I've been completely alone this whole time.\n动静？你什么意思？我一直都是独自一人。"

    old "You've been disturbing the sands."
    new "You've been disturbing the sands.\n你扰动了沙丘。"

    old "Nuala gestures to the slope behind me. The shape of the sand makes it obvious where I climbed up."
    new "Nuala gestures to the slope behind me. The shape of the sand makes it obvious where I climbed up.\nNuala 朝我身后的坡比了比。沙子的形状清楚地显露出我从哪里爬上来。"

    old "Sorry, is that a problem?"
    new "Sorry, is that a problem?\n抱歉，这有什么问题吗？"

    old "I could tell there was something in that basin by watching the top of the dune from afar. I came here thinking that you were prey, some animal trapped in the sand."
    new "I could tell there was something in that basin by watching the top of the dune from afar. I came here thinking that you were prey, some animal trapped in the sand.\n我远远望着沙丘顶，就知道那片凹地里有什么东西。我来这里时，还以为你是猎物，是困在沙里的什么动物。"

    old "And chances are, I'm not the only one."
    new "And chances are, I'm not the only one.\n而且，恐怕不止我一个这么想。"

    old "Nuala points to several black dots on a dune near us."
    new "Nuala points to several black dots on a dune near us.\nNuala 指了指我们附近一座沙丘上的几个黑点。"

    old "Jackals. Just like me, they saw the movement of the sand from when you climbed up. And just like me, they came here looking for a meal."
    new "Jackals. Just like me, they saw the movement of the sand from when you climbed up. And just like me, they came here looking for a meal.\n是胡狼。和我一样，它们也看到了你爬上来的动静。也和我一样，它们是来觅食的。"

    old "I think we should leave."
    new "I think we should leave.\n我想我们该离开这里。"

    old "Nuala shakes her head."
    new "Nuala shakes her head.\nNuala 摇了摇头。"

    old "No use running from jackals. Someone like you can't outrun them. Our only hope is that they perceive us as a threat and decide to leave us alone."
    new "No use running from jackals. Someone like you can't outrun them. Our only hope is that they perceive us as a threat and decide to leave us alone.\n从胡狼面前逃跑是没用的。像你这样的人跑不过它们。我们唯一的希望，就是让它们把我们当作威胁，从而知难而退。"

    old "What if they don't?"
    new "What if they don't?\n如果它们不退呢？"

    old "Then we have to fight."
    new "Then we have to fight.\n那我们就只能战斗。"

    old "Try to look formidable and intimidating."
    new "Try to look formidable and intimidating.\n尽量摆出凶悍骇人的样子。"

    old "I draw my weapon and hold it aloft, assuming the most intimidating stance I can. The jackals continue to approach, and their individual shapes come closer into focus."
    new "I draw my weapon and hold it aloft, assuming the most intimidating stance I can. The jackals continue to approach, and their individual shapes come closer into focus.\n我拔出武器高高举起，摆出我所能摆出的最吓人的架势。胡狼继续逼近，它们各自的身影越来越清晰。"

    old "Stay steadfast. Don't let them see any fear in you. If they see you shaking, they'll tag you as easy prey."
    new "Stay steadfast. Don't let them see any fear in you. If they see you shaking, they'll tag you as easy prey.\n站稳了。别让它们看出你有一丝恐惧。它们一旦看到你发抖，就会把你当成容易得手的猎物。"

    old "I maintain my pose, trying my best not to waver."
    new "I maintain my pose, trying my best not to waver.\n我保持着姿势，尽量不让自己动摇。"

    old "I let out a yell with a deep, bellowing voice, waving my arms in my best attempt to look intimidating."
    new "I let out a yell with a deep, bellowing voice, waving my arms in my best attempt to look intimidating.\n我发出一声低沉洪亮的吼叫，挥舞着双臂，尽力让自己显得可怕。"

    old "The jackals continue to approach, and their individual shapes come closer into focus. I continue waving and bellowing in my best attempt to scare them off."
    new "The jackals continue to approach, and their individual shapes come closer into focus. I continue waving and bellowing in my best attempt to scare them off.\n胡狼继续逼近，它们各自的身影越来越清晰。我继续挥臂吼叫，尽力吓退它们。"

    old "Nuala joins me, yelling and waving her staff."
    new "Nuala joins me, yelling and waving her staff.\nNuala 也加入进来，大喊着挥舞她的手杖。"

    old "The jackals continue to approach, and soon they are close enough that I can see the leader of the pack and look him in the eye."
    new "The jackals continue to approach, and soon they are close enough that I can see the leader of the pack and look him in the eye.\n胡狼继续逼近，很快它们就近到我已能看清狼群的首领，与它四目相对。"

    old "The lead jackal stops moving forward, and paces from left to right, eying me and Nuala before turning around. He begins walking away, and the other jackals fall into step behind him."
    new "The lead jackal stops moving forward, and paces from left to right, eying me and Nuala before turning around. He begins walking away, and the other jackals fall into step behind him.\n领头的胡狼停下脚步，从左到右地踱着，打量着我和 Nuala，然后转过身去。它开始走开，其余的胡狼纷纷跟上它的步伐。"

    old "Well done, [protag]. Today, you are the alpha predator."
    new "Well done, [protag]. Today, you are the alpha predator.\n干得好，[protag]。今天，你就是最顶级的掠食者。"

    old "The lead jackal stops in front of us, and two jackals come up beside him, flaking on the left and right side."
    new "The lead jackal stops in front of us, and two jackals come up beside him, flaking on the left and right side.\n领头的胡狼在我们面前停下，另外两只胡狼走到它两侧，一左一右。"

    old "Ready that weapon of yours, [protag]. I think we're in for a fight."
    new "Ready that weapon of yours, [protag]. I think we're in for a fight.\n准备好你的武器，[protag]。我看我们要打上一场了。"

    old "Be careful of the one in the middle. He's the leader of the pack."
    new "Be careful of the one in the middle. He's the leader of the pack.\n小心中间那只。它是狼群的首领。"

    old "Thanks for the help, Nuala. I don't know if I could have won that fight on my own."
    new "Thanks for the help, Nuala. I don't know if I could have won that fight on my own.\n谢谢你的帮助，Nuala。我不知道自己一个人能不能打赢那场仗。"

    old "[protag] of Grimoire. What is it that brings you to the dunes?"
    new "[protag] of Grimoire. What is it that brings you to the dunes?\nGrimoire 的 [protag]。是什么把你带到这些沙丘来的？"

    old "I came in search of the tomb of Urd."
    new "I came in search of the tomb of Urd.\n我来寻找 Urd 的陵墓。"

    old "The tomb you speak of is well known to my people. But you'll have no success finding it equipped as you are."
    new "The tomb you speak of is well known to my people. But you'll have no success finding it equipped as you are.\n你说的那座陵墓，我的人民都很熟悉。但以你这样的装备，是找不到它的。"

    old "Who are your people?"
    new "Who are your people?\n你的人民是谁？"

    old "We are Dunemarchers. The people of the empire might refer to us as 'nomads.'"
    new "We are Dunemarchers. The people of the empire might refer to us as 'nomads.'\n我们是 Dunemarchers。帝国的人或许会称我们为“游牧民”。"

    old "You're not nomads?"
    new "You're not nomads?\n你们不是游牧民吗？"

    old "We are nomads, but 'nomad' is a broad term. There are many nomadic groups that wander this desert. The Dunemarchers are but one of them."
    new "We are nomads, but 'nomad' is a broad term. There are many nomadic groups that wander this desert. The Dunemarchers are but one of them.\n我们是游牧民，但“游牧民”是个宽泛的说法。在这片沙漠里游荡的游牧部族有很多，Dunemarchers 只是其中之一。"

    old "You said that the tomb of Urd isn't accessible. How is it that your people know of it?"
    new "You said that the tomb of Urd isn't accessible. How is it that your people know of it?\n你说 Urd 的陵墓难以到达。那你的人民是怎么知道的？"

    old "I didn't say that the tomb is impossible to get to. I said that it's impossible for someone such as you. The way you march through the sand draws the attention of jackals. There are predators far more dangerous than that standing between you and the tomb of Urd."
    new "I didn't say that the tomb is impossible to get to. I said that it's impossible for someone such as you. The way you march through the sand draws the attention of jackals. There are predators far more dangerous than that standing between you and the tomb of Urd.\n我没说那陵墓无法到达。我是说，像你这样的人无法到达。你在沙中行走的方式会引来胡狼的注意。而横在你和 Urd 的陵墓之间的，还有远比胡狼更危险的掠食者。"

    old "And yet the predators don't seem to be a problem for you. Why is that?"
    new "And yet the predators don't seem to be a problem for you. Why is that?\n可那些掠食者对你似乎不构成问题。为什么？"

    old "As I said before, we are Dunemarchers."
    new "As I said before, we are Dunemarchers.\n正如我之前所说，我们是 Dunemarchers。"

    old "Nuala gestures to her legs, which are adorned with an odd sort of covering."
    new "Nuala gestures to her legs, which are adorned with an odd sort of covering.\nNuala 朝自己的双腿比了比，她的腿上套着一种奇怪的护具。"

    old "We insulate our legs and temper our footsteps so that we can move through the sands without disturbing them and attracting the attention of animals."
    new "We insulate our legs and temper our footsteps so that we can move through the sands without disturbing them and attracting the attention of animals.\n我们护住双腿、收敛脚步，这样就能穿行沙地而不扰动沙层，不引来动物的注意。"

    old "What do you know about the tomb of Urd?"
    new "What do you know about the tomb of Urd?\n你对 Urd 的陵墓了解多少？"

    old "I was taken there once as a young girl, on my second dune march."
    new "I was taken there once as a young girl, on my second dune march.\n我还是个小女孩时，曾被带去那里一次，那是我的第二次沙丘行军。"

    old "Dune march?"
    new "Dune march?\n沙丘行军？"

    old "It is a rite of passage among the Dunemarchers. On every child's thirteenth birthday, they are given greaves."
    new "It is a rite of passage among the Dunemarchers. On every child's thirteenth birthday, they are given greaves.\n那是 Dunemarchers 的一种成人礼。每个孩子十三岁生日那天，都会得到一副护胫。"

    old "Nuala gestures to her own legs."
    new "Nuala gestures to her own legs.\nNuala 朝自己的双腿比了比。"

    old "The greaves are designed to soften our footfalls, and with proper training, a child can walk the sands without disturbing them, concealing our movement through the dunes from predators."
    new "The greaves are designed to soften our footfalls, and with proper training, a child can walk the sands without disturbing them, concealing our movement through the dunes from predators.\n这种护胫能减轻我们的脚步声，经过适当的训练，孩子就能行走沙地而不扰动沙层，在穿过沙丘时把行踪瞒过掠食者。"

    old "So, if I had greaves like yours, I could make it to the tomb of Urd?"
    new "So, if I had greaves like yours, I could make it to the tomb of Urd?\n那么，如果我有像你那样的护胫，我就能到达 Urd 的陵墓了？"

    old "Having the greaves doesn't guarantee your safety, anymore than carrying a sword guarantees your victory in a fight. How you use the greaves matters just as much as the craftsmanship that composes them."
    new "Having the greaves doesn't guarantee your safety, anymore than carrying a sword guarantees your victory in a fight. How you use the greaves matters just as much as the craftsmanship that composes them.\n拥有护胫并不能保证你的安全，正如佩剑不能保证你在战斗中获胜。你如何使用护胫，与打造它的工艺同样重要。"

    old "Nuala points toward the horizon."
    new "Nuala points toward the horizon.\nNuala 指向地平线。"

    old "Do you see that?"
    new "Do you see that?\n你看到那个了吗？"

    old "More jackals. We should go."
    new "More jackals. We should go.\n更多胡狼。我们该走了。"

    old "We're not going to stay and fight?"
    new "We're not going to stay and fight?\n我们不留下战斗吗？"

    old "They're far enough away that we can get a lead on them. We can have you out of these sand dunes before they catch up to us."
    new "They're far enough away that we can get a lead on them. We can have you out of these sand dunes before they catch up to us.\n它们离得还远，我们能抢得先机。可以在它们追上之前，把你带出这些沙丘。"

    old "What if I don't want to leave?"
    new "What if I don't want to leave?\n如果我不想离开呢？"

    old "Would you rather face that pack of jackals? I count at least seven, and who knows how many more will follow them."
    new "Would you rather face that pack of jackals? I count at least seven, and who knows how many more will follow them.\n难道你宁愿去面对那群胡狼？我数了数至少有七只，谁知道后面还会跟来多少。"

    old "I follow Nuala's pointing finger and see several dots on the horizon."
    new "I follow Nuala's pointing finger and see several dots on the horizon.\n我顺着 Nuala 手指的方向望去，看到地平线上有几个小点。"

    old "I think I can see the jackals now."
    new "I think I can see the jackals now.\n我想我现在能看见那些胡狼了。"

    old "We should leave. Now."
    new "We should leave. Now.\n我们该走了。现在就走。"

    old "Nuala escorts me through the sand. Her pace is quick but deliberate, and as I struggle to keep up with her, I make note of the purposeful movement of her feet, how she lifts one foot off the ground just as the other touches it, and how she slows her footfalls just before touching the ground."
    new "Nuala escorts me through the sand. Her pace is quick but deliberate, and as I struggle to keep up with her, I make note of the purposeful movement of her feet, how she lifts one foot off the ground just as the other touches it, and how she slows her footfalls just before touching the ground.\nNuala 领着我穿过沙地。她的步子又快又稳，我吃力地跟上她，同时留意着她脚下富有章法的动作：她总是一只脚刚离地，另一只脚就落地，又在落地前放缓脚步。"

    old "The jackals gain on us, but we reach the edge of the dunes before they are close enough to attack. The jackals eventually give up the pursuit, and retreat back into the dunes."
    new "The jackals gain on us, but we reach the edge of the dunes before they are close enough to attack. The jackals eventually give up the pursuit, and retreat back into the dunes.\n胡狼追了上来，但我们在它们逼近到能攻击之前赶到了沙丘边缘。胡狼最终放弃了追赶，退回沙丘之中。"

    old "Before long, my feet are on solid ground, the familiar dry and hardened soil that makes up the desert flatlands."
    new "Before long, my feet are on solid ground, the familiar dry and hardened soil that makes up the desert flatlands.\n没过多久，我的脚就踏上了坚实的土地——那熟悉的、构成沙漠平地的干燥硬土。"

    old "You can make it out of this desert on your own from here, yes?"
    new "You can make it out of this desert on your own from here, yes?\n从这里起，你就能靠自己走出这片沙漠了，对吧？"

    old "These dunes are not a place for a [prace] such as yourself, [protag]. Leave the dunes to the Dunemarchers."
    new "These dunes are not a place for a [prace] such as yourself, [protag]. Leave the dunes to the Dunemarchers.\n这些沙丘不是你这样的 [prace] 该来的地方，[protag]。把沙丘留给 Dunemarchers 吧。"

    old "Are you going to be okay on your own? Those jackals might come back."
    new "Are you going to be okay on your own? Those jackals might come back.\n你一个人没事吧？那些胡狼可能会回来。"

    old "Don't worry about me, [prace]. I know these dunes better than the beasts themselves."
    new "Don't worry about me, [prace]. I know these dunes better than the beasts themselves.\n别担心我，[prace]。我对这些沙丘的了解，比那些野兽还要深。"

    old "Nuala turns and begins marching back into the sand dunes."
    new "Nuala turns and begins marching back into the sand dunes.\nNuala 转过身，开始朝沙丘深处走去。"

    old "Nuala told me that I shouldn't return to these dunes. Then again, Nuala also told me that the tomb of Urd is somewhere in this sand, so I suppose I don't have much choice if I'm to carry out Karen's wishes."
    new "Nuala told me that I shouldn't return to these dunes. Then again, Nuala also told me that the tomb of Urd is somewhere in this sand, so I suppose I don't have much choice if I'm to carry out Karen's wishes.\nNuala 告诉我，我不该再回这些沙丘。可话说回来，Nuala 也告诉过我 Urd 的陵墓就在这片沙地之中，所以若想完成 Karen 的嘱托，我想我别无选择。"

    old "Nuala found me and helped me once before. Perhaps she'll deign to do it once again."
    new "Nuala found me and helped me once before. Perhaps she'll deign to do it once again.\nNuala 曾找到我并帮过我一次。也许她愿意再帮一次。"

    old "I march through the dunes, keeping care that I don't wander too far. If I start to see wild beasts on the horizon, I should be able to make it to the desert flatlands from here before they catch up to me."
    new "I march through the dunes, keeping care that I don't wander too far. If I start to see wild beasts on the horizon, I should be able to make it to the desert flatlands from here before they catch up to me.\n我穿行在沙丘间，小心翼翼不让自己走得太远。一旦看到地平线上出现野兽，我应该能在它们追上之前从这里赶到沙漠平地。"

    old "Now, to get her attention."
    new "Now, to get her attention.\n现在，该引起她的注意了。"

    old "I pull out dagger with a small metal blade and begin tilting it to capture the sun's reflection. I aim the beam of light at the top of the nearest dune, and trace a line along the horizon with the light."
    new "I pull out dagger with a small metal blade and begin tilting it to capture the sun's reflection. I aim the beam of light at the top of the nearest dune, and trace a line along the horizon with the light.\n我抽出一把带着小金属刃的匕首，开始倾斜刀身去接住阳光的反光。我把光束对准最近一座沙丘的顶部，用光线沿着地平线划出一道线。"

    old "I see some vultures overhead. Apparently birds like shiny things. I can only hope that the response of the jackals will be intimidation and fear, rather than curiosity."
    new "I see some vultures overhead. Apparently birds like shiny things. I can only hope that the response of the jackals will be intimidation and fear, rather than curiosity.\n我看到头顶有几只秃鹫。看来鸟儿都喜欢亮闪闪的东西。我只能祈祷胡狼的反应是畏惧和恐惧，而不是好奇。"

    old "I see a figure approaching me, and I lower my mirror and begin waving. Within several minutes, I can make out the figure. Looks like Nuala has come to me once again."
    new "I see a figure approaching me, and I lower my mirror and begin waving. Within several minutes, I can make out the figure. Looks like Nuala has come to me once again.\n我看到一个人影向我走来，便放下镜子，挥手示意。几分钟后，我看清了那身影。看来 Nuala 又一次来到了我身边。"

    old "Nuala, my intentions haven't changed. I came to this desert seeking the tomb of Urd, and I've yet to find it. I'm hoping that you can assist me in finding it."
    new "Nuala, my intentions haven't changed. I came to this desert seeking the tomb of Urd, and I've yet to find it. I'm hoping that you can assist me in finding it.\nNuala，我的来意没有变。我来这片沙漠是为了寻找 Urd 的陵墓，至今还没找到。我希望你能帮我找到它。"

    old "This desert is vast. Why would you come alone?"
    new "This desert is vast. Why would you come alone?\n这片沙漠十分辽阔。你为什么要独自前来？"

    old "As unlikely as it seems, I was thinking that I might meet you again."
    new "As unlikely as it seems, I was thinking that I might meet you again.\n虽然听着不太可能，但我一直在想，也许我能再见到你。"

    old "Nuala smiles and shakes her head."
    new "Nuala smiles and shakes her head.\nNuala 笑着摇了摇头。"

    old "Funny, I was thinking the same thing. In fact, I had one of the Dunemarcher craftsmen begin working on another pair of greaves on the chance that you might appear again."
    new "Funny, I was thinking the same thing. In fact, I had one of the Dunemarcher craftsmen begin working on another pair of greaves on the chance that you might appear again.\n真巧，我也在想同样的事。事实上，我已经让一位 Dunemarcher 工匠开始打造另一副护胫，就赌你可能会再次出现。"

    old "You have an extra pair of dunemarching greaves?"
    new "You have an extra pair of dunemarching greaves?\n你还有一副多余的沙丘行军护胫？"

    old "Not with me. They're waiting back at camp."
    new "Not with me. They're waiting back at camp.\n不在我身上。它们放在营地里。"

    old "Can you take me there?"
    new "Can you take me there?\n你能带我去吗？"

    old "On one condition. You need to understand that the Dunemarchers aren't prone to random acts of charity."
    new "On one condition. You need to understand that the Dunemarchers aren't prone to random acts of charity.\n有个条件。你得明白，Dunemarchers 不是那种随意施舍的人。"

    old "You did save me the other day."
    new "You did save me the other day.\n那天你确实救了我。"

    old "And I found myself no poorer for it. If you want a pair of greaves to march these dunes, you'll need to work for them."
    new "And I found myself no poorer for it. If you want a pair of greaves to march these dunes, you'll need to work for them.\n而我也没因此损失什么。如果你想得到一副护胫去走这些沙丘，就得靠劳动来换。"

    old "What kind of task do you have in mind?"
    new "What kind of task do you have in mind?\n你心里想的是什么任务？"

    old "It's not up to me to decide. Come, I'll bring you to our tribe's leader."
    new "It's not up to me to decide. Come, I'll bring you to our tribe's leader.\n这由不得我决定。来吧，我带你去见我们部族的首领。"

    old "Nuala begins marching forward, back in the direction I came from."
    new "Nuala begins marching forward, back in the direction I came from.\nNuala 开始向前走，朝着我来的方向。"

    old "Your tribe is located in the flatlands?"
    new "Your tribe is located in the flatlands?\n你的部族住在平地上吗？"

    old "No, but with those boots of yours, taking a detour through the flatlands is our best chance at making it through the desert unharmed."
    new "No, but with those boots of yours, taking a detour through the flatlands is our best chance at making it through the desert unharmed.\n不，但以你那双靴子，绕道穿过平地是我们平安穿越沙漠的最好办法。"

    old "I fall into step behind Nuala, allowing her to lead the way to her tribe's settlement."
    new "I fall into step behind Nuala, allowing her to lead the way to her tribe's settlement.\n我迈步跟在 Nuala 身后，由她带路前往她部族的定居点。"

    old "Ho, Chief."
    new "Ho, Chief.\n您好，酋长。"

    old "Ho, Nuala. I see you've brought a visitor."
    new "Ho, Nuala. I see you've brought a visitor.\n你好，Nuala。我看你带来了位客人。"

    old "The same I told you about before."
    new "The same I told you about before.\n就是我之前跟你提过的那位。"

    old "Ah, yes. The one from Grimoire. You said [hisher] name was [protag], yes?"
    new "Ah, yes. The one from Grimoire. You said [hisher] name was [protag], yes?\n啊，对。Grimoire 来的那位。你说 [hisher] 名字叫 [protag]，对吧？"

    old "Yes, Chief."
    new "Yes, Chief.\n是的，酋长。"

    old "'Chief' is what the Dunemarchers call me. To you, I am Larik."
    new "'Chief' is what the Dunemarchers call me. To you, I am Larik.\n“酋长”是 Dunemarchers 对我的称呼。对你，我名叫 Larik。"

    old "Alright, Larik."
    new "Alright, Larik.\n好的，Larik。"

    old "If understand right, you came here in search of pressing for your legs. A Dunemarcher's greaves."
    new "If understand right, you came here in search of pressing for your legs. A Dunemarcher's greaves.\n如果我没理解错，你是来为你的双腿找护具的。一副 Dunemarcher 的护胫。"

    old "I came looking for the tomb of Urd. From what Nuala told me, it sounds like I'll be needing special footware from you if I want to reach there without disturbing the sands."
    new "I came looking for the tomb of Urd. From what Nuala told me, it sounds like I'll be needing special footware from you if I want to reach there without disturbing the sands.\n我是来寻找 Urd 的陵墓的。听 Nuala 所说，若想不扰动沙层地到达那里，我似乎需要你们的特制足具。"

    old "Indeed. And we have a pair for you to wear. But a Dunemarcher's greaves are something earned by tribulation."
    new "Indeed. And we have a pair for you to wear. But a Dunemarcher's greaves are something earned by tribulation.\n确实如此。我们有一副可以给你。但 Dunemarcher 的护胫，须经磨难方能赢得。"

    old "Does that mean that I could earn one, if I endured the tribulation?"
    new "Does that mean that I could earn one, if I endured the tribulation?\n也就是说，只要我经受住磨难，就能赢得一副？"

    old "Ha! You could indeed, though I didn't expect you to be so eager to march toward tribulation. Perhaps once you know what the tribulation is, you won't be so eager to weather it."
    new "Ha! You could indeed, though I didn't expect you to be so eager to march toward tribulation. Perhaps once you know what the tribulation is, you won't be so eager to weather it.\n哈！你确实可以，不过我倒没料到你会这么急着奔磨难而去。也许等你知道那磨难是什么，就没这么急着去熬了。"

    old "We have a scorpion problem. If you desire to walk like a Dunemarcher, help us eliminate it."
    new "We have a scorpion problem. If you desire to walk like a Dunemarcher, help us eliminate it.\n我们有个蝎子之患。如果你想像 Dunemarcher 一样行走，就帮我们除掉它。"

    old "'It?'"
    new "'It?'\n“它”？"

    old "There are numerous scorpions that have infiltrated the dunes by way of the flatlands, but there is one in particular that has been causing us problems."
    new "There are numerous scorpions that have infiltrated the dunes by way of the flatlands, but there is one in particular that has been causing us problems.\n经由平地潜入沙丘的蝎子数不胜数，但其中有一只，一直给我们带来麻烦。"

    old "I think I can take care of a scorpion by myself."
    new "I think I can take care of a scorpion by myself.\n我想一只蝎子我一个人就能对付。"

    old "This is no ordinary scorpion, [protag], and we wouldn't expect you to take care of it yourself. We'll send a shaman from our tribe to accompany you. Nuala is eager to wander these sands, so she may as well do something useful rather than prowl aimlessly."
    new "This is no ordinary scorpion, [protag], and we wouldn't expect you to take care of it yourself. We'll send a shaman from our tribe to accompany you. Nuala is eager to wander these sands, so she may as well do something useful rather than prowl aimlessly.\n这可不是普通的蝎子，[protag]，我们也不会让你独自去对付它。我们会派部族里的一位萨满陪你去。Nuala 正急着想在这些沙地间走动，与其让她漫无目的地游荡，不如让她做点有用的事。"

    old "You'll be needing these. Bind them tight."
    new "You'll be needing these. Bind them tight.\n你会需要这些。绑紧点。"

    old "Larik tosses a pair of greaves at my feet, and I strap them to my legs."
    new "Larik tosses a pair of greaves at my feet, and I strap them to my legs.\nLarik 把一副护胫扔到我脚边，我把它绑在了腿上。"

    old "Thank you for your generosity. I'm surprised to be welcomed so warmly by you and your people."
    new "Thank you for your generosity. I'm surprised to be welcomed so warmly by you and your people.\n谢谢你的慷慨。我没想到你和你的人民会这样热情地欢迎我。"

    old "It is my pleasure, though I am surprised to hear someone from an empire city to call it a 'warm welcome' when sent off to the den of an emperor scorpion."
    new "It is my pleasure, though I am surprised to hear someone from an empire city to call it a 'warm welcome' when sent off to the den of an emperor scorpion.\n这是我的荣幸，不过我倒很惊讶，一个帝国城市来的人，在被派去帝王蝎的巢穴时，竟把这称作“热情欢迎”。"

    old "I'm surprised that you're giving me the time of day at all. And you shared your tools with me, so that I could walk the desert. It's very generous of you, even if I am assisting you in return."
    new "I'm surprised that you're giving me the time of day at all. And you shared your tools with me, so that I could walk the desert. It's very generous of you, even if I am assisting you in return.\n我惊讶的是你们竟肯理会我。而且你们把工具借给我，好让我能在沙漠中行走。就算我是以相助作为回报，你们也太慷慨了。"

    old "How can we be anything but welcoming? The desert is already cruel enough without hostility between tribes. As long as there is reciprocity, we are happy to assist you. We are all working toward the same goal."
    new "How can we be anything but welcoming? The desert is already cruel enough without hostility between tribes. As long as there is reciprocity, we are happy to assist you. We are all working toward the same goal.\n我们怎能不热情相待？沙漠本就够残酷了，何必再让部族之间彼此为敌。只要有来有往，我们就乐于相助。我们都朝着同一个目标努力。"

    old "And that goal is?"
    new "And that goal is?\n那目标是什么？"

    old "Symbiosis with the desert. An understand of the world we inhabit. Mastery over nature. And most of all, survival."
    new "Symbiosis with the desert. An understand of the world we inhabit. Mastery over nature. And most of all, survival.\n与沙漠共生。理解我们所栖居的世界。驾驭自然。而最重要的是——生存。"

    old "Good luck, [protag]. Do well, and those greaves will be yours to keep."
    new "Good luck, [protag]. Do well, and those greaves will be yours to keep.\n祝你好运，[protag]。做得出色，那副护胫就归你了。"

    old "I follow Nuala through the desert. As we walk, I mimic her stepping pattern, slowing my footfalls as my feet touch the ground."
    new "I follow Nuala through the desert. As we walk, I mimic her stepping pattern, slowing my footfalls as my feet touch the ground.\n我跟着 Nuala 穿过沙漠。行走时，我模仿她的步伐，脚落地时放缓脚步。"

    old "It's not the first time I've followed Nuala in this fashion, but following her without disturbing the sand is much easier now. The greaves expand and contract with each motion of my legs, cushioning each step as my feet touch the sand. My footsteps leave only a small ripple in the sand as we march. Nuala's footprints are smaller still."
    new "It's not the first time I've followed Nuala in this fashion, but following her without disturbing the sand is much easier now. The greaves expand and contract with each motion of my legs, cushioning each step as my feet touch the sand. My footsteps leave only a small ripple in the sand as we march. Nuala's footprints are smaller still.\n这已不是我第一次这样跟着 Nuala，但现在要不扰动沙层地跟着她，容易多了。护胫随着我双腿的每个动作一张一缩，在脚触沙时缓冲每一步。行进时，我的脚印只在沙上留下小小的波纹，而 Nuala 的脚印更浅。"

    old "What is it like where you come from?"
    new "What is it like where you come from?\n你来的地方是什么样子的？"

    old "Are you asking about Grimoire?"
    new "Are you asking about Grimoire?\n你是在问 Grimoire 吗？"

    old "I mean the world outside this desert. You're well-traveled, yes? Tell me about the things you've seen."
    new "I mean the world outside this desert. You're well-traveled, yes? Tell me about the things you've seen.\n我指的是这片沙漠之外的世界。你见多识广，对吧？跟我说说你见过的事物。"

    old "Grimoire is the capital of the human empire, and the energy in that city is like nothing I have ever seen."
    new "Grimoire is the capital of the human empire, and the energy in that city is like nothing I have ever seen.\nGrimoire 是人类帝国的都城，那座城市里的活力，是我前所未见的。"

    old "Energy? Are you speaking of magic?"
    new "Energy? Are you speaking of magic?\n活力？你说的是魔法吗？"

    old "No, the energy that comes from having many people crowded into a single area."
    new "No, the energy that comes from having many people crowded into a single area.\n不，是许多人挤在一处所产生的活力。"

    old "Grimoire is loud. When you step out onto the street, you hear just how vibrant the city is. It's a mixture of people's voices, the sound of rolling wheels on streets, metal tools striking stone as stone masons continue to build the city, and a hundred other noises that all blend together in one grand cacophony."
    new "Grimoire is loud. When you step out onto the street, you hear just how vibrant the city is. It's a mixture of people's voices, the sound of rolling wheels on streets, metal tools striking stone as stone masons continue to build the city, and a hundred other noises that all blend together in one grand cacophony.\nGrimoire 很喧闹。当你走上街头，就能听到这座城市有多么生机勃勃。那是人声、街巷里车轮滚动声、石匠继续筑城时金属工具敲击石头的声音，以及上百种其他声响，全都交织成一片宏大的嘈杂。"

    old "In comparison, the desert is quiet. If you stop walking, you hear only the sound of the wind. It's something that I think the people of Grimoire envy."
    new "In comparison, the desert is quiet. If you stop walking, you hear only the sound of the wind. It's something that I think the people of Grimoire envy.\n相比之下，沙漠是安静的。你若停下脚步，就只能听见风声。我想，这是 Grimoire 的人们会羡慕的吧。"

    old "Is it always loud? Even when you sleep?"
    new "Is it always loud? Even when you sleep?\n那里一直这么吵吗？连睡觉的时候也是？"

    old "It depends on where you go in the city, but no matter where you go, there are going to be other people there. Even at night, you can hear the sound of people snoring through their walls, or rolling restlessly in their beds."
    new "It depends on where you go in the city, but no matter where you go, there are going to be other people there. Even at night, you can hear the sound of people snoring through their walls, or rolling restlessly in their beds.\n这取决于你在城里的哪个地方，但无论你去哪里，那里都会有其他人。即便到了夜里，你也能隔着墙壁听见人们的鼾声，或是他们躺在床上辗转反侧的声音。"

    old "How fascinating. The idea of hearing your neighbors, even when you can't see them. The idea of listening to conversations spoken by people you've never met before. I've never experienced anything like that."
    new "How fascinating. The idea of hearing your neighbors, even when you can't see them. The idea of listening to conversations spoken by people you've never met before. I've never experienced anything like that.\n真有意思。竟然能听见邻居的声音，哪怕看不见他们；竟然能听到素未谋面之人的谈话。我从没经历过这样的事。"

    old "There are other tribes in the desert, most of them residing in the flatlands and barrens. We have neighbors. But the idea that you might overhear another person who you've never seen face to face is unthinkable, especially in these sands."
    new "There are other tribes in the desert, most of them residing in the flatlands and barrens. We have neighbors. But the idea that you might overhear another person who you've never seen face to face is unthinkable, especially in these sands.\n沙漠里还有其他部族，大多住在平地和荒原上。我们也有邻居。但“无意中听到一个你从未谋面的人说话”这种念头，实在难以想象，尤其是在这片沙地之中。"

    old "Do you know of the Amazons?"
    new "Do you know of the Amazons?\n你知道 Amazons 吗？"

    old "I've heard of them, yes. Fierce warriors, from the sound of things."
    new "I've heard of them, yes. Fierce warriors, from the sound of things.\n是的，我听说过。听起来是些骁勇的战士。"

    old "The citadel where the Amazons is the embodiment of that warrior spirit. Just the sight of it is physically intimidating. And approaching it can be downright terrifying, especially for anyone who the Amazons consider an enemy."
    new "The citadel where the Amazons is the embodiment of that warrior spirit. Just the sight of it is physically intimidating. And approaching it can be downright terrifying, especially for anyone who the Amazons consider an enemy.\nAmazons 所在的要塞，正是那种战士精神的化身。光是看上一眼就令人胆寒。而靠近它则更是可怕，尤其对 Amazons 视为敌人的人而言。"

    old "Is the citadel heavily guarded?"
    new "Is the citadel heavily guarded?\n那要塞戒备森严吗？"

    old "The only path to the citadel is lined with tall, stone spires. Every one of them is physically imposing. And any one of them could be a perch for a warrior, ready to pounce and rain death upon you."
    new "The only path to the citadel is lined with tall, stone spires. Every one of them is physically imposing. And any one of them could be a perch for a warrior, ready to pounce and rain death upon you.\n通往要塞的唯一道路两侧，矗立着一排排高耸的石塔。每一座都气势逼人。而任何一座之上，都可能伏着一名战士，随时准备扑下，向你倾泻死亡。"

    old "We Dunemarchers use the landscape as a took for stalking prey, but the idea of using the landscape as a weapon seems amazing. To think that you could attack, or be attacked, from above..."
    new "We Dunemarchers use the landscape as a took for stalking prey, but the idea of using the landscape as a weapon seems amazing. To think that you could attack, or be attacked, from above...\n我们 Dunemarchers 把地形当作追踪猎物的工具，可把地形当作武器这种念头，实在令人惊叹。想想看，你竟能从上方发起攻击，或遭到来自上方的袭击……"

    old "Have you heard of the Great Forest?"
    new "Have you heard of the Great Forest?\n你听说过 Great Forest 吗？"

    old "The place the elves hail from? I've heard of it, yes. It sounds like a marvelous place of trees. I see little of the color green, and the thought of an entire landscape of green seems amazing."
    new "The place the elves hail from? I've heard of it, yes. It sounds like a marvelous place of trees. I see little of the color green, and the thought of an entire landscape of green seems amazing.\nElves 的故乡吗？是的，我听说过。听起来是个奇妙的树木之地。我很少见到绿色，一想到整片大地都是绿色，就觉得不可思议。"

    old "It's even more amazing than you imagine. The forest is green, yes, but it's more than that. It's a blend of bright and dark shades of green, of browns and yellows that make up the floor, of reds and blues that mark the creatures that dwell within it."
    new "It's even more amazing than you imagine. The forest is green, yes, but it's more than that. It's a blend of bright and dark shades of green, of browns and yellows that make up the floor, of reds and blues that mark the creatures that dwell within it.\n它比你想象的还要奇妙。那片森林确实是绿的，但不止于此。它是明暗交错的绿，是铺满地面的棕与黄，是点缀其间栖居生物的赤与蓝。"

    old "Here, in the desert, you have nothing but constant sunlight. The only way to hide from it is in a tent or in a cave, where you completely block it out. But in the forest, you may one moment be walking through overgrowth, with not a glimpse of sunshine, and then a moment later step into a clearing where you can bask in the sun's warm glow."
    new "Here, in the desert, you have nothing but constant sunlight. The only way to hide from it is in a tent or in a cave, where you completely block it out. But in the forest, you may one moment be walking through overgrowth, with not a glimpse of sunshine, and then a moment later step into a clearing where you can bask in the sun's warm glow.\n在这里的沙漠中，你只有永不停歇的阳光。想躲避它，只能躲进帐篷或洞穴，把阳光完全挡在外面。可在森林里，你也许前一秒还穿行在茂密的树丛间，不见一丝阳光，下一秒就踏进一片空地，沐浴在温暖的日光里。"

    old "Forests, and the Great Forest in particular, are always full of surprises. That's what I find most awe-inspiring about them. It's hard to say what the best part of the forest is, because every time you walk through the forest, you discover something new."
    new "Forests, and the Great Forest in particular, are always full of surprises. That's what I find most awe-inspiring about them. It's hard to say what the best part of the forest is, because every time you walk through the forest, you discover something new.\n森林，尤其是 Great Forest，总是充满惊喜。这正是它们最令我敬畏之处。很难说森林最美的地方是哪里，因为每次穿过森林，你都会有新的发现。"

    old "I'm getting jealous just hearing you describe it."
    new "I'm getting jealous just hearing you describe it.\n光是听你描述，我都开始嫉妒了。"

    old "Have you ever been outside the desert?"
    new "Have you ever been outside the desert?\n你出过沙漠吗？"

    old "Only to its edges, and only with my people. Even within the desert, it is seldom that I venture past the dunes. Occasionally I enter the desert flatlands, but these sands are what is comfortable and familiar to me."
    new "Only to its edges, and only with my people. Even within the desert, it is seldom that I venture past the dunes. Occasionally I enter the desert flatlands, but these sands are what is comfortable and familiar to me.\n只到过它的边缘，而且总是和我的族人一起。即使在沙漠之中，我也很少越过沙丘。偶尔我会进入沙漠平地，但这些沙地才是我感到舒适而熟悉的地方。"

    old "Why do you never wander beyond the dunes?"
    new "Why do you never wander beyond the dunes?\n你为什么从不走出沙丘？"

    old "The dunes are where I can move confidently. I have spent many years as a Dunemarcher. Whatever threat I face, I feel confident that I can outwit it or outpace it. If I leave my people to go hunting, I can feel confident in my ability to return with something to show for my efforts."
    new "The dunes are where I can move confidently. I have spent many years as a Dunemarcher. Whatever threat I face, I feel confident that I can outwit it or outpace it. If I leave my people to go hunting, I can feel confident in my ability to return with something to show for my efforts.\n沙丘是我能自信行动的地方。我当 Dunemarcher 已经许多年了。无论面对什么威胁，我都有信心智取它或跑赢它。若我离开族人去打猎，我也有信心带着成果归来。"

    old "You're a shaman, aren't you? I thought shamans were healers, not killers. How is it that you're also an accomplished hunter?"
    new "You're a shaman, aren't you? I thought shamans were healers, not killers. How is it that you're also an accomplished hunter?\n你是萨满，对吧？我还以为萨满是医者，不是杀手。你怎么又是一位出色的猎手？"

    old "I am good at waiting. Some people chase their prey and fight it. I am one for stalking prey and outlasting it. My shamanic powers ensure that I am always the last one standing."
    new "I am good at waiting. Some people chase their prey and fight it. I am one for stalking prey and outlasting it. My shamanic powers ensure that I am always the last one standing.\n我擅长等待。有的人追捕猎物、与之搏斗；我则喜欢潜行追踪、把猎物熬到力竭。我的萨满之力能保证我永远是站到最后的那一个。"

    old "So, when it comes to facing these scorpions..."
    new "So, when it comes to facing these scorpions...\n那么，等面对那些蝎子的时候……"

    old "The emperor scorpion is no ordinary prey. It draws its vim and vigor from the sand. We must draw it out and fight it."
    new "The emperor scorpion is no ordinary prey. It draws its vim and vigor from the sand. We must draw it out and fight it.\n帝王蝎可不是普通的猎物。它的精力与活力来自沙地。我们必须把它引出来，再与它战斗。"

    old "Where is the scorpion, anyway?"
    new "Where is the scorpion, anyway?\n话说回来，那蝎子到底在哪儿？"

    old "That is what is at issue. An emperor scorpion can be hard to find. We are in its general area, but the scorpion can travel below the sand. Hunting it down would be impossible. That is why we must draw us to it."
    new "That is what is at issue. An emperor scorpion can be hard to find. We are in its general area, but the scorpion can travel below the sand. Hunting it down would be impossible. That is why we must draw us to it.\n这正是问题所在。帝王蝎很难找到。我们就在它活动的大致区域，但它能在沙下穿行。要追捕它是不可能的，所以我们得把它引到我们这里来。"

    old "I suddenly become aware of the fact that we are at the bottom of a small basin between two large sand dunes."
    new "I suddenly become aware of the fact that we are at the bottom of a small basin between two large sand dunes.\n我突然意识到，我们正身处两座大沙丘之间的小凹地底部。"

    old "What exactly does that mean?"
    new "What exactly does that mean?\n这究竟意味着什么？"

    old "It means that we must become the prey."
    new "It means that we must become the prey.\n意味着我们必须把自己变成猎物。"

    old "How do we do that?"
    new "How do we do that?\n那该怎么做？"

    old "Dance, [prace]. Dance."
    new "Dance, [prace]. Dance.\n跳舞，[prace]。跳起来。"

    old "Nuala begins stamping her feet on the ground, jumping up and planting her feet in a way that sends tremors through the sand."
    new "Nuala begins stamping her feet on the ground, jumping up and planting her feet in a way that sends tremors through the sand.\nNuala 开始跺脚，跳起来再重重落足，让震颤传遍沙地。"

    old "I begin dancing with Nuala, leaping skyward and planting my heels into the ground as I land."
    new "I begin dancing with Nuala, leaping skyward and planting my heels into the ground as I land.\n我也开始和 Nuala 一起跳，纵身跃起，落地时把脚跟狠狠砸进地里。"

    old "Though our purpose is to disturb the sands, I find myself falling into rhythm with Nuala's movements, swinging my arms with the same cadence that her hips sway."
    new "Though our purpose is to disturb the sands, I find myself falling into rhythm with Nuala's movements, swinging my arms with the same cadence that her hips sway.\n尽管我们的目的是扰动沙层，我却发现自己渐渐融入了 Nuala 的节奏，手臂的摆动与她腰肢的摇曳合着同样的节拍。"

    old "It's obvious that the purpose of Nuala's dance is to disturb the sand and draw out the scorpion, but even her harsh movements, there is a certain sense of grace and balance."
    new "It's obvious that the purpose of Nuala's dance is to disturb the sand and draw out the scorpion, but even her harsh movements, there is a certain sense of grace and balance.\n显而易见，Nuala 跳舞是为了扰动沙层、引出蝎子，但即便她的动作猛烈，仍透着一种优雅与平衡。"

    old "As Nuala hits the ground, she sways her hips and moves her arms, as if trying to beckon the blessing of some deity through her impassioned frenzy."
    new "As Nuala hits the ground, she sways her hips and moves her arms, as if trying to beckon the blessing of some deity through her impassioned frenzy.\nNuala 落地时，她扭动腰肢、挥动双臂，仿佛想借这股狂热的劲头，求得某位神明的赐福。"

    old "The ground around us begins rumbling, and I see several black shapes emerge from the ground."
    new "The ground around us begins rumbling, and I see several black shapes emerge from the ground.\n我们周围的地面开始震颤，我看到几个黑色的身影从地下钻了出来。"

    old "Scorpions. Ready your weapon, [protag]."
    new "Scorpions. Ready your weapon, [protag].\n蝎子。准备好你的武器，[protag]。"

    old "Which one of those was the emperor?"
    new "Which one of those was the emperor?\n哪一只是帝王蝎？"

    old "The emperor scorpion is yet to come. Wait a moment."
    new "The emperor scorpion is yet to come. Wait a moment.\n帝王蝎还没现身。再等等。"

    old "Nuala plants her staff in the sand, and closes her eyes as her grip tightens around the staff."
    new "Nuala plants her staff in the sand, and closes her eyes as her grip tightens around the staff.\nNuala 把手杖插进沙里，闭上眼睛，握杖的手越攥越紧。"

    old "A massive creature erupts from the sand in front of us, and a black cloud forms around Nuala's head."
    new "A massive creature erupts from the sand in front of us, and a black cloud forms around Nuala's head.\n一个庞然大物从我们面前的沙中猛然钻出，一片黑云在 Nuala 头顶凝聚成形。"

    old "Ready yourself for battle, [protag]! He's fierce, but the powers of the desert are fiercer still."
    new "Ready yourself for battle, [protag]! He's fierce, but the powers of the desert are fiercer still.\n准备战斗，[protag]！它很凶猛，但沙漠的力量更加凶猛。"

    old "As the beast falls, it begins to fade into a black dust that is carried off with the wind. Within moments, the scorpion is completely disintegrated, leaving no trace of its existence behind."
    new "As the beast falls, it begins to fade into a black dust that is carried off with the wind. Within moments, the scorpion is completely disintegrated, leaving no trace of its existence behind.\n随着那野兽倒下，它开始化作黑色的尘埃，随风飘散。转眼之间，蝎子便彻底消散，不留一丝存在过的痕迹。"

    old "We're done here. Let's report back to Chief."
    new "We're done here. Let's report back to Chief.\n这里的事做完了。我们回去向酋长报告吧。"

    old "You're back. I trust the desert is one dead scorpion closer to being safe."
    new "You're back. I trust the desert is one dead scorpion closer to being safe.\n你们回来了。我相信沙漠离安全又近了一步，少了一只蝎子。"

    old "Excellent. Well, [protag]. You've got the greaves, and they're yours to keep. They look quite good on you."
    new "Excellent. Well, [protag]. You've got the greaves, and they're yours to keep. They look quite good on you.\n好极了。那么，[protag]，护胫你拿到了，它们归你了。穿在你身上相当不错。"

    old "Larik, I have a question. About the scorpion we fought."
    new "Larik, I have a question. About the scorpion we fought.\nLarik，我有个问题。关于我们打的那只蝎子。"

    old "When we defeated it, the scorpion simply...vanished. It didn't leave so much as an empty husk behind. What exactly did we fight?"
    new "When we defeated it, the scorpion simply...vanished. It didn't leave so much as an empty husk behind. What exactly did we fight?\n我们打败它时，那蝎子就……凭空消失了。连一具空壳都没留下。我们打的那到底是什么？"

    old "That is a good question, and one that I have been trying to answer myself. I have led the Dunemarchers through this desert for many years, but never have I seen creatures like the one you just described. That is, until..."
    new "That is a good question, and one that I have been trying to answer myself. I have led the Dunemarchers through this desert for many years, but never have I seen creatures like the one you just described. That is, until...\n问得好，这个问题我自己也一直在寻求答案。我率领 Dunemarchers 穿越这片沙漠已经许多年，却从未见过你刚才描述的那种生物。也就是说，直到……"

    old "Until what?"
    new "Until what?\n直到什么？"

    old "Several moons ago, we began encountering beasts infested with some kind of corruption, something which tainted them and made them prey upon the desert, spreading disease and the stench of death with them. Whenever we felled one, it would turn to dust, just as you described."
    new "Several moons ago, we began encountering beasts infested with some kind of corruption, something which tainted them and made them prey upon the desert, spreading disease and the stench of death with them. Whenever we felled one, it would turn to dust, just as you described.\n几个月前，我们开始遇到一些感染了某种腐化的野兽，这种腐化污染了它们，让它们开始祸害沙漠，随之散布疾病与死亡的恶臭。每当我们将一只放倒，它就会化为尘土，正如你所描述的那样。"

    old "It began slowly. First, it was the jackals that prowl the sands. Then, it was the vultures of the air. And now, it has spread to the subterranean beasts, like the scorpion you just encountered. With every full moon, some new kind of evil seems to awaken in this desert."
    new "It began slowly. First, it was the jackals that prowl the sands. Then, it was the vultures of the air. And now, it has spread to the subterranean beasts, like the scorpion you just encountered. With every full moon, some new kind of evil seems to awaken in this desert.\n起初很慢。先是沙地上游荡的胡狼，接着是空中的秃鹫。如今，它已经蔓延到了地下的野兽，比如你刚刚遇到的那只蝎子。每逢满月，沙漠里似乎就有某种新的邪恶苏醒。"

    old "Larik, I have a theory about what may be causing the corruption you describe."
    new "Larik, I have a theory about what may be causing the corruption you describe.\nLarik，关于你所说的这种腐化的成因，我有个推测。"

    old "Please, if you have answers, I am all ears."
    new "Please, if you have answers, I am all ears.\n请讲，如果你有答案，我洗耳恭听。"

    old "The thing that you describe—a kind of darkness corrupting the lands—it's something that the people of Grimoire have observed as well, from the plains around N'Mar. We think we know the source."
    new "The thing that you describe—a kind of darkness corrupting the lands—it's something that the people of Grimoire have observed as well, from the plains around N'Mar. We think we know the source.\n你所描述的那种东西——某种腐蚀大地的黑暗——Grimoire 的人们也观察到了，就在 N'Mar 周围的平原上。我们认为自己知道源头。"

    old "Actually, that's been my focus, ever since I found myself caught in those blighted plains. However this blight will end, we know that the answers we seek are inside the castle on N'Mar. I'm in charge of assembling a task force to infiltrate that castle."
    new "Actually, that's been my focus, ever since I found myself caught in those blighted plains. However this blight will end, we know that the answers we seek are inside the castle on N'Mar. I'm in charge of assembling a task force to infiltrate that castle.\n事实上，自从我发现自己被困在那片被污染的平原上以来，这一直是我关注的重点。无论这场污染如何终结，我们知道，我们寻求的答案就在 N'Mar 的城堡里。我正负责组建一支特遣队，渗透进那座城堡。"

    old "Interesting. It seems that the answers to the desert's blight may rest outside of the desert itself. In a way, I feel that the future of my people may rest in your hands, [protag]."
    new "Interesting. It seems that the answers to the desert's blight may rest outside of the desert itself. In a way, I feel that the future of my people may rest in your hands, [protag].\n有意思。看来沙漠之灾的答案，也许就藏在沙漠之外。从某种意义上说，我觉得我人民的未来，或许就握在你的手中，[protag]。"

    old "Of course, I would be a fool to run in blindly alongside you. There is the issue of trust, for even if I believe that you are telling me what you believe to be the truth, I remain skeptical of the idea that you know exactly what is transpiring behind the corruption that we see, both here and in N'Mar. By your own admission, you are still seeking answers."
    new "Of course, I would be a fool to run in blindly alongside you. There is the issue of trust, for even if I believe that you are telling me what you believe to be the truth, I remain skeptical of the idea that you know exactly what is transpiring behind the corruption that we see, both here and in N'Mar. By your own admission, you are still seeking answers.\n当然，我若是盲目地跟着你一头扎进去，那也太蠢了。这里有个信任的问题：即便我相信你对我说的都是你认定的真相，我仍然怀疑，你是否确切知道我们在这里和 N'Mar 所见的腐化背后究竟发生了什么。你自己也承认，你仍在寻找答案。"

    old "[protag], if you are telling the truth, I wish that I could help you, but before I can think about what the darkness will bring in one moon's time, I must thing about what the trials of the desert will bring in one day's time."
    new "[protag], if you are telling the truth, I wish that I could help you, but before I can think about what the darkness will bring in one moon's time, I must thing about what the trials of the desert will bring in one day's time.\n[protag]，如果你说的是实话，我真希望能帮上你。但在我考虑一个月后黑暗会带来什么之前，我必须先考虑沙漠的考验在一天之后会带来什么。"

    old "And yet, regardless of the purity of your intentions, I believe it would be to my benefit to remain attuned to what exactly is transpiring in N'Mar. I would go myself, but at this point, I think it may be best to send someone on my behalf."
    new "And yet, regardless of the purity of your intentions, I believe it would be to my benefit to remain attuned to what exactly is transpiring in N'Mar. I would go myself, but at this point, I think it may be best to send someone on my behalf.\n然而，无论你的初衷多么纯粹，我想，时刻掌握 N'Mar 那边究竟发生了什么，对我都有好处。我本可以亲自去，但就目前而言，我想最好还是派个人代表我前去。"

    old "Nuala's ears perk up, and she turns to face Larik, with a look of expectation on her face."
    new "Nuala's ears perk up, and she turns to face Larik, with a look of expectation on her face.\nNuala 的耳朵竖了起来，她转过身面对 Larik，脸上带着期待的神色。"

    old "I'm sure you've already sensed that Nuala has a great curiosity for what lies beyond the bounds of the desert. I think that having her accompany you might serve both our interests."
    new "I'm sure you've already sensed that Nuala has a great curiosity for what lies beyond the bounds of the desert. I think that having her accompany you might serve both our interests.\n我敢肯定你已经察觉到，Nuala 对沙漠之外的事物怀有极大的好奇。我想，让她陪着你，或许对我们双方都有利。"

    old "You must understand that whatever there is to see, I may encounter a great deal of peril in observing it. That would go for anyone who accompanied me as well."
    new "You must understand that whatever there is to see, I may encounter a great deal of peril in observing it. That would go for anyone who accompanied me as well.\n你必须明白，无论那里有什么可看的，我在观察时都可能遭遇巨大的危险。任何陪着我的人也同样如此。"

    old "And I'm sure Nuala here is well-equipped to face whatever perils await you. What she lacks in experience, she makes up for in instinct. Believe me, she won't be a burden. In fact, I think you'll find her to be quite the opposite."
    new "And I'm sure Nuala here is well-equipped to face whatever perils await you. What she lacks in experience, she makes up for in instinct. Believe me, she won't be a burden. In fact, I think you'll find her to be quite the opposite.\n而我确信，这里的 Nuala 完全有能力应对等待你的种种危险。她经验不足，但可以靠本能弥补。相信我，她不会成为负担。事实上，我想你会发现她恰恰相反。"

    old "Nuala, is this what you want?"
    new "Nuala, is this what you want?\nNuala，这是你想要的吗？"

    old "Nuala gives me an enthusiastic nod, and the look in her eyes tells me that she means it."
    new "Nuala gives me an enthusiastic nod, and the look in her eyes tells me that she means it.\nNuala 热切地朝我点点头，她眼中的神情告诉我，她是认真的。"

    old "Well then. I can't guarantee that Nuala will be party to everything that goes on in my operations around N'Mar. But if she's willing to lend a hand, I'm happy to accept it and have her report back to you whatever she experiences."
    new "Well then. I can't guarantee that Nuala will be party to everything that goes on in my operations around N'Mar. But if she's willing to lend a hand, I'm happy to accept it and have her report back to you whatever she experiences.\n那好吧。我无法保证 Nuala 能参与我在 N'Mar 周边行动中的每一件事。但如果她愿意出一份力，我很乐意接受，并让她把所见所闻向你汇报。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]. I know that I am not offering much, and my actions may seem motivated by self-interest, but I hope that this is the beginning of a lasting relationship between my people and yours."
    new "Thank you, [protag]. I know that I am not offering much, and my actions may seem motivated by self-interest, but I hope that this is the beginning of a lasting relationship between my people and yours.\n谢谢你，[protag]。我知道自己拿出的东西并不多，我的举动或许也显得出于私利，但我希望，这是我的人民与你的人民之间长久情谊的开始。"

    old "You're our friend now. You're welcome to visit us and trade with us whenever you have the chance to venture again in the desert."
    new "You're our friend now. You're welcome to visit us and trade with us whenever you have the chance to venture again in the desert.\n你现在是我们的朋友了。欢迎你随时来访、与我们互通有无，只要你有机会再次踏足沙漠。"

    old "I will remember your offer, Larik."
    new "I will remember your offer, Larik.\n我会记住你的提议的，Larik。"

    old "Where you will stay, Nuala?"
    new "Where you will stay, Nuala?\nNuala，你打算待在哪里？"

    old "I'm a Nomad. I am not used to stay for long in one place. However, I'll wander in the plains between Grimoire and the Orcish Wastes, scouting and exploring. I'll make sure you can always find me when you need me."
    new "I'm a Nomad. I am not used to stay for long in one place. However, I'll wander in the plains between Grimoire and the Orcish Wastes, scouting and exploring. I'll make sure you can always find me when you need me.\n我是个游牧民。我不习惯在一个地方久留。不过，我会在 Grimoire 与 Orcish Wastes 之间的平原上游荡，侦察和探索。我会确保你需要我时，总能找到我。"

    old "Nuala."
    new "Nuala.\nNuala。"

    old "I was headed for the grasslands. Do you wish to accompany me?"
    new "I was headed for the grasslands. Do you wish to accompany me?\n我正要去草原。你愿意陪我一起去吗？"

    old "I came to see you, so I guess that means the answer is yes."
    new "I came to see you, so I guess that means the answer is yes.\n我来找你，所以我想答案当然是愿意。"

    old "Excellent."
    new "Excellent.\n好极了。"

    old "Nuala bends down and begins removing her footwear."
    new "Nuala bends down and begins removing her footwear.\nNuala 弯下腰，开始脱掉她的鞋。"

    old "Ah, getting rid of your sand-walking shoes in favor of something more appropriate for the savannah?"
    new "Ah, getting rid of your sand-walking shoes in favor of something more appropriate for the savannah?\n啊，你要脱掉走沙地的鞋，换上更适合草原的鞋子吗？"

    old "What do you have? Some kind of moccasin?"
    new "What do you have? Some kind of moccasin?\n你带了什么？某种软皮鞋？"

    old "No, I don't have any special shoes for walking the grasslands."
    new "No, I don't have any special shoes for walking the grasslands.\n不，我没有专门走草原的鞋。"

    old "Then what are you wearing instead?"
    new "Then what are you wearing instead?\n那你换穿什么？"

    old "Nothing."
    new "Nothing.\n什么都不穿。"

    old "Nuala ties her sandals to her belt and begins walking barefoot."
    new "Nuala ties her sandals to her belt and begins walking barefoot.\nNuala 把她的凉鞋绑在腰带上，开始赤脚行走。"

    old "You're going barefoot?"
    new "You're going barefoot?\n你要赤脚走？"

    old "Is that safe? Aren't you worried about, I don't know, stepping on something?"
    new "Is that safe? Aren't you worried about, I don't know, stepping on something?\n那样安全吗？你就不担心，呃，踩到什么吗？"

    old "It's the grasslands."
    new "It's the grasslands.\n那可是草原。"

    old "What about things that aren't grass? Things like thistles, sticks, or rocks poking out of the ground?"
    new "What about things that aren't grass? Things like thistles, sticks, or rocks poking out of the ground?\n那那些不是草的东西呢？比如蓟草、树枝，或者从地里冒出来的石头？"

    old "My feet are used to stepping on such things. I've walked the grasslands barefoot long enough for the soles of my feet to harden up."
    new "My feet are used to stepping on such things. I've walked the grasslands barefoot long enough for the soles of my feet to harden up.\n我的脚早就习惯踩这些东西了。我赤脚在草原上走了这么久，脚底已经磨硬了。"

    old "What about things like ticks? Aren't you worried about them latching onto your bare feet and sucking your blood?"
    new "What about things like ticks? Aren't you worried about them latching onto your bare feet and sucking your blood?\n那虱子之类的东西呢？你就不担心它们爬到你赤裸的脚上，吸你的血？"

    old "I don't see how wearing sandals would prevent that from happening. And besides, ticks know how to jump. If I covered my feet, they'd attach to my legs."
    new "I don't see how wearing sandals would prevent that from happening. And besides, ticks know how to jump. If I covered my feet, they'd attach to my legs.\n我看不出穿凉鞋能阻止这种事。再说，虱子会跳。如果我包住脚，它们就会爬到我腿上。"

    old "You could cover your legs."
    new "You could cover your legs.\n你可以包住腿。"

    old "And then they would be drenched out here. [protag], understand this. Out here, the heat of the sun is the greatest threat to my well-being. Not sharp sticks littered on the ground, not ticks, not shrubbery."
    new "And then they would be drenched out here. [protag], understand this. Out here, the heat of the sun is the greatest threat to my well-being. Not sharp sticks littered on the ground, not ticks, not shrubbery.\n那样它们在这里就会湿透。[protag]，你要明白。在这里，太阳的酷热才是对我安危最大的威胁。不是散落在地的尖树枝，不是虱子，也不是灌木。"

    old "I appreciate your concern, but I've walked these grasslands far longer than you have."
    new "I appreciate your concern, but I've walked these grasslands far longer than you have.\n我很感激你的关心，但这些草原我走的时间比你长得多。"

    old "Is this part of your usual patrol?"
    new "Is this part of your usual patrol?\n这是你日常巡逻的一部分吗？"

    old "It's not part of my patrol. But I enjoy coming here."
    new "It's not part of my patrol. But I enjoy coming here.\n这不在我巡逻范围之内。但我喜欢来这里。"

    old "What is it about the savannah grassland that you find so appealing?"
    new "What is it about the savannah grassland that you find so appealing?\n这片稀树草原，你觉得哪里如此吸引人？"

    old "That."
    new "That.\n那个。"

    old "Nuala points to the shape of a large animal on the horizon."
    new "Nuala points to the shape of a large animal on the horizon.\nNuala 指向地平线上一个大型动物的身影。"

    old "That's Rue."
    new "That's Rue.\n那是 Rue。"

    old "It looks like a rhino to me."
    new "It looks like a rhino to me.\n在我看来像是一头犀牛。"

    old "Rue is no ordinary rhino."
    new "Rue is no ordinary rhino.\nRue 可不是普通的犀牛。"

    old "I study the rhino, and it's plain to see that Nuala is right. Its hide is scarred in several places, especially near its neck."
    new "I study the rhino, and it's plain to see that Nuala is right. Its hide is scarred in several places, especially near its neck.\n我打量着那头犀牛，很明显 Nuala 说得对。它的皮上有好几处疤痕，尤其是脖子附近。"

    old "I wonder how a rhino gets scars like that. You would think that the neck would be its most sensitive and protected area. Not a lot of chances for that part of its body to get scratched up."
    new "I wonder how a rhino gets scars like that. You would think that the neck would be its most sensitive and protected area. Not a lot of chances for that part of its body to get scratched up.\n我在想，一头犀牛怎么会留下那样的伤疤。你大概会觉得，脖子应该是它最敏感、最受保护的地方，身体那部分没多少机会被刮伤。"

    old "That scar, near her left hindquarter, is from last winter. I caught her sleeping, and thought that a pre-emptive strike would be enough for me win the day. Unfortunately, rhinos can lose a lot of blood and still have enough strength in them to be quite dangerous."
    new "That scar, near her left hindquarter, is from last winter. I caught her sleeping, and thought that a pre-emptive strike would be enough for me win the day. Unfortunately, rhinos can lose a lot of blood and still have enough strength in them to be quite dangerous.\n她左后腿附近的那道疤，是去年冬天留下的。我发现她在睡觉，以为先发制人一击就能让我赢得那一天。可惜，犀牛就算失血很多，体内仍留有足以构成威胁的力气。"

    old "The scar near the base of her neck, that came from a moment of peril. Rue had me on my back and was charging, hoping to flatten me. Mercifully, I managed to roll out from under her trampling feet and land a blow right as she passed by me. I was lucky to escape with my life."
    new "The scar near the base of her neck, that came from a moment of peril. Rue had me on my back and was charging, hoping to flatten me. Mercifully, I managed to roll out from under her trampling feet and land a blow right as she passed by me. I was lucky to escape with my life.\n她脖子根部附近的疤，则来自一个危险的时刻。Rue 把我掀翻在地，然后冲过来，想把我踩扁。幸运的是，我设法从她践踏的脚下滚开，在她经过我身边时给了她一击。我能捡回一条命，实属侥幸。"

    old "It seems like you and Rue have a history together."
    new "It seems like you and Rue have a history together.\n看来你和 Rue 之间有一段渊源。"

    old "You could say that. She has it out for me."
    new "You could say that. She has it out for me.\n可以这么说。她跟我有仇。"

    old "It seems to me more like you have it out for her."
    new "It seems to me more like you have it out for her.\n在我看来，更像是你跟她有仇。"

    old "So, what are you planning to do to Rue today? Another attempt on her life?"
    new "So, what are you planning to do to Rue today? Another attempt on her life?\n那么，你今天打算对 Rue 做什么？再一次取她性命？"

    old "No, not today. This part of the savannah is too flat. A charging rhino is most easily defeated by confronting it on uneven ground."
    new "No, not today. This part of the savannah is too flat. A charging rhino is most easily defeated by confronting it on uneven ground.\n不，今天不行。草原的这一带太平坦了。冲过来的犀牛，最好在不平的地形上对付。"

    old "What about those trees? Could you hide up there?"
    new "What about those trees? Could you hide up there?\n那些树呢？你能躲到树上吗？"

    old "Rue could destroy any of these trees by charging. No, this is not the place to confront her."
    new "Rue could destroy any of these trees by charging. No, this is not the place to confront her.\nRue 一冲撞就能摧毁这里的任何一棵树。不，这里不是对付她的地方。"

    old "So if you're not planning to confront Rue, why did we come here?"
    new "So if you're not planning to confront Rue, why did we come here?\n那如果你不打算对付 Rue，我们为什么要来这里？"

    old "I'm tracking her migration patterns. Rue has been known to change things up from season to season, so I need to keep an eye on her. Based on the direction she's moving, and considering I've seen of other rhinos, it seems like she's headed to the breeding grounds."
    new "I'm tracking her migration patterns. Rue has been known to change things up from season to season, so I need to keep an eye on her. Based on the direction she's moving, and considering I've seen of other rhinos, it seems like she's headed to the breeding grounds.\n我在追踪她的迁徙规律。Rue 以随季节改变习性而闻名，所以我得盯着她。根据她移动的方向，再结合我见过的其他犀牛来判断，她似乎正前往繁殖地。"

    old "Nuala smirks."
    new "Nuala smirks.\nNuala 露出一丝坏笑。"

    old "It means that she is in heat. And that means that she is vulnerable."
    new "It means that she is in heat. And that means that she is vulnerable.\n这意味着她正处在发情期。而这意味着她很脆弱。"

    old "The rhino stops for a moment, and turns to face Nuala."
    new "The rhino stops for a moment, and turns to face Nuala.\n那头犀牛停了一下，转身面对着 Nuala。"

    old "Nuala glares at the rhino, and the rhino seems to glare back. Nuala snarls, and the rhino turns away and resumes walking."
    new "Nuala glares at the rhino, and the rhino seems to glare back. Nuala snarls, and the rhino turns away and resumes walking.\nNuala 瞪着那头犀牛，那头犀牛似乎也瞪了回来。Nuala 低吼一声，犀牛便转过身，继续前行。"

    old "What was that?"
    new "What was that?\n刚才那是什么？"

    old "Disrespect. Rue doesn't see me as a threat. That will be her downfall."
    new "Disrespect. Rue doesn't see me as a threat. That will be her downfall.\n轻视。Rue 不把我放在眼里。这会是她的败因。"

    old "Nuala turns around and begins walking away from the beast."
    new "Nuala turns around and begins walking away from the beast.\nNuala 转过身，开始从那头野兽身边走开。"

    old "What are you going to do now?"
    new "What are you going to do now?\n你现在打算怎么办？"

    old "I told you. This is not the time or the place to confront Rue. So I will leave her, and come back on another day."
    new "I told you. This is not the time or the place to confront Rue. So I will leave her, and come back on another day.\n我说过了。现在不是对付 Rue 的时候，也不是地方。所以我会离开她，改天再来。"

    old "You're not going to stalk your prey?"
    new "You're not going to stalk your prey?\n你不去跟踪你的猎物？"

    old "Stalking can sometimes take days or weeks. It can even happen across seasons. As I told you, I've met Rue before, and I'll meet her again. And now, I have a good idea of where she's headed next."
    new "Stalking can sometimes take days or weeks. It can even happen across seasons. As I told you, I've met Rue before, and I'll meet her again. And now, I have a good idea of where she's headed next.\n追踪有时要花上好几天，甚至好几个星期，还可能横跨几个季节。我告诉过你，我以前见过 Rue，以后还会再见到她。而现在，我大致知道她接下来要去哪里了。"

    old "I told you. She's in heat. In several days, she'll be at the breeding grounds, at her most vulnerable. So then, I will strike."
    new "I told you. She's in heat. In several days, she'll be at the breeding grounds, at her most vulnerable. So then, I will strike.\n我告诉过你。她在发情期。几天后，她就会在繁殖地，处于最脆弱的状态。到那时，我就出手。"

    old "Something about that strikes me as a bit sinister."
    new "Something about that strikes me as a bit sinister.\n这让我觉得有点阴险。"

    old "What about it is sinister?"
    new "What about it is sinister?\n哪里阴险了？"

    old "Well, mating seems like a bit of a sacred thing, don't you think? Killing her when she's in that state doesn't strike me as very, well, sporting. It doesn't seem like a fair fight."
    new "Well, mating seems like a bit of a sacred thing, don't you think? Killing her when she's in that state doesn't strike me as very, well, sporting. It doesn't seem like a fair fight.\n嗯，交配似乎是一件挺神圣的事，你不觉得吗？趁她处于那种状态时杀她，在我看来，嗯，不太光彩。那不像是一场公平的较量。"

    old "A 'fair fight?' [protag], look at Rue, then look back at me. She is twenty times my size. What hope could I ever have of besting her in a 'fair fight?' I must exploit every advantage available to me if I am to best her."
    new "A 'fair fight?' [protag], look at Rue, then look back at me. She is twenty times my size. What hope could I ever have of besting her in a 'fair fight?' I must exploit every advantage available to me if I am to best her.\n“公平的较量”？[protag]，看看 Rue，再看看我。她是我的二十倍大。在一场“公平的较量”里，我怎么可能有半点胜算？要想胜过她，我就必须利用一切可用的优势。"

    old "That's a clever idea, waiting until she's unawares to strike."
    new "That's a clever idea, waiting until she's unawares to strike.\n这是个聪明的办法，等她毫无防备时再出手。"

    old "That is what a hunter does, [protag]. That's how a hunter can fell beasts that are twenty times her size. You can't do that with strength alone. It takes cunning and planning."
    new "That is what a hunter does, [protag]. That's how a hunter can fell beasts that are twenty times her size. You can't do that with strength alone. It takes cunning and planning.\n猎手就是这么做的，[protag]。这样，猎手才能放倒体型是她二十倍的野兽。光靠蛮力做不到，需要狡猾和谋划。"

    old "Nuala and I head back to where I first met her."
    new "Nuala and I head back to where I first met her.\nNuala 和我回到我第一次遇见她的地方。"

    old "I am done for today. Now, I must go home and rest to prepare for the days ahead. Perhaps you should go and do the same."
    new "I am done for today. Now, I must go home and rest to prepare for the days ahead. Perhaps you should go and do the same.\n我今天就到此为止。现在，我得回家休息，为往后的日子做准备。也许你也该回去做同样的事。"

    old "Very well, Nuala. Good luck."
    new "Very well, Nuala. Good luck.\n很好，Nuala。祝你好运。"

    old "Nuala. You seem excited?"
    new "Nuala. You seem excited?\nNuala。你看起来很兴奋？"

    old "Yes, I was looking for you."
    new "Yes, I was looking for you.\n是的，我在找你。"

    old "This is about Rue then?"
    new "This is about Rue then?\n那还是关于 Rue 的事？"

    old "No, this time it isn't something personal. It's about my tribe."
    new "No, this time it isn't something personal. It's about my tribe.\n不，这次不是私事。是关于我的部族。"

    old "Her tribe? If this is a problem they haven't been able to fix by themselves then it's probably pretty serious."
    new "Her tribe? If this is a problem they haven't been able to fix by themselves then it's probably pretty serious.\n她的部族？如果这问题连他们自己都解决不了，那大概相当严重。"

    old "I'm listening."
    new "I'm listening.\n我听着呢。"

    old "How much do you know about the northern part of this desert?"
    new "How much do you know about the northern part of this desert?\n你对这片沙漠的北部了解多少？"

    old "I can't say I'm familiar with it. The closest I've gotten to it was when I traveled to Hammerhands. Why?"
    new "I can't say I'm familiar with it. The closest I've gotten to it was when I traveled to Hammerhands. Why?\n我不敢说自己熟悉那里。我最接近它的时候，是我去 Hammerhands 那次。怎么了？"

    old "I see. Well, several orc tribes live in that zone. They live far enough away that they haven't previously been a problem for my tribe, but now..."
    new "I see. Well, several orc tribes live in that zone. They live far enough away that they haven't previously been a problem for my tribe, but now...\n我明白了。嗯，那一带有好几个 Orc 部族。他们住得足够远，以前不曾给我的部族带来麻烦，但现在……"

    old "Now they are? I take it that something has changed?"
    new "Now they are? I take it that something has changed?\n现在他们成了麻烦？我猜是什么发生了变化？"

    old "I look Nuala in the eyes and read a sense of dread in her expression. It's not fear, no. She's fearless. But she looks worried. I move closer to her and place a hand on her shoulder."
    new "I look Nuala in the eyes and read a sense of dread in her expression. It's not fear, no. She's fearless. But she looks worried. I move closer to her and place a hand on her shoulder.\n我直视 Nuala 的眼睛，从她的神情里读出一丝忧虑。不是恐惧，不，她无所畏惧。但她看起来忧心忡忡。我朝她靠近一步，把手搭在她的肩上。"

    old "Tell me. Maybe I can help."
    new "Tell me. Maybe I can help.\n告诉我。也许我能帮忙。"

    old "The village elders believe that this is a consequence of the mist from N'Mar. There are also rumors that demons have been sighted near the Everburn Mountains..."
    new "The village elders believe that this is a consequence of the mist from N'Mar. There are also rumors that demons have been sighted near the Everburn Mountains...\n村里的长老们认为，这是 N'Mar 那场迷雾造成的后果。还有传言说，Everburn Mountains 附近已经出现了恶魔……"

    old "As if we didn't have enough trouble. First undead and now demons?"
    new "As if we didn't have enough trouble. First undead and now demons?\n好像我们的麻烦还不够多。先是亡灵，现在又是恶魔？"

    old "I doubt it. Personally, I don't believe those rumors. The orcs might though. Regardless, the fact remains that they've started moving south for some reason."
    new "I doubt it. Personally, I don't believe those rumors. The orcs might though. Regardless, the fact remains that they've started moving south for some reason.\n我表示怀疑。就我个人而言，我不信那些传言。不过 Orcs 也许信。不管怎样，事实是，他们已经开始向南移动了，总有某种原因。"

    old "And near your area."
    new "And near your area.\n而且靠近你的地盘。"

    old "Exactly. And, as you know, orcs aren't exactly known to be a peaceful race."
    new "Exactly. And, as you know, orcs aren't exactly known to be a peaceful race.\n没错。而且，你也知道，Orcs 并不是以和平著称的种族。"

    old "That's an understatement."
    new "That's an understatement.\n那都是往轻里说了。"

    old "Nuala nods gravely."
    new "Nuala nods gravely.\nNuala 神色凝重地点了点头。"

    old "What happens when someone from my tribe is ambushed by an orc patrol? Or when resources become too scarce to support both nomads and orcs?"
    new "What happens when someone from my tribe is ambushed by an orc patrol? Or when resources become too scarce to support both nomads and orcs?\n我部族的人若是遭到 Orc 巡逻队的伏击，或者资源变得匮乏，难以同时供养 Nomads 和 Orcs，那会怎样？"

    old "I know this is a lot to ask, [protag]. But, please. Help me. Help my tribe."
    new "I know this is a lot to ask, [protag]. But, please. Help me. Help my tribe.\n我知道这个请求很重，[protag]。但是，求你了。帮帮我。帮帮我的部族。"

    old "Nuala takes a step closer to me. Her face is only a few inches away from mine now as her bold, brown eyes meet my own beseechingly. Her bronze skin smells of sand, of desert, and her hair is gently tossed to the side by the wind. It eclipses half of her face, and yet, does nothing to diminish the determination in her gaze."
    new "Nuala takes a step closer to me. Her face is only a few inches away from mine now as her bold, brown eyes meet my own beseechingly. Her bronze skin smells of sand, of desert, and her hair is gently tossed to the side by the wind. It eclipses half of her face, and yet, does nothing to diminish the determination in her gaze.\nNuala 又朝我靠近一步。她的脸离我只有几英寸，她那双大胆的棕色眼睛恳切地迎上我的目光。她古铜色的肌肤散发着沙子和沙漠的气息，头发被风轻轻吹向一侧。头发遮住了她半张脸，却丝毫未能削弱她目光中的坚定。"

    old "Just thinking out loud, but... can't you move south too? At least temporarily until the N'Mar problem is solved?"
    new "Just thinking out loud, but... can't you move south too? At least temporarily until the N'Mar problem is solved?\n只是随口想想，但……你们不能也往南迁吗？至少暂时迁一下，直到 N'Mar 的问题解决？"

    old "No, further south is where the dark elves live. To the east are the mountains. Neither is a viable option. Besides, my people would rather die in battle than abandon our territory completely."
    new "No, further south is where the dark elves live. To the east are the mountains. Neither is a viable option. Besides, my people would rather die in battle than abandon our territory completely.\n不行，再往南是 Dark Elves 的地盘，往东是群山。哪边都不是可行的选择。况且，我的人民宁愿战死，也不愿彻底放弃我们的领土。"

    old "I see. I thought so. Hmm. I guess there's only one thing to do then."
    new "I see. I thought so. Hmm. I guess there's only one thing to do then.\n我明白了。我也这么想。嗯。那我想，就只剩一件事可做了。"

    old "We should talk with the orcs."
    new "We should talk with the orcs.\n我们该和 Orcs 谈谈。"

    old "Talk? With orcs? Are you mad? It's impossible! They won't listen to us!"
    new "Talk? With orcs? Are you mad? It's impossible! They won't listen to us!\n谈谈？和 Orcs？你疯了吗？不可能！他们不会听我们的！"

    old "Why not?"
    new "Why not?\n为什么不呢？"

    old "You know why not! They're a fierce race in general and, now that they're fleeing from the north to the south, they'll be like a cornered beast, scared and aggressive."
    new "You know why not! They're a fierce race in general and, now that they're fleeing from the north to the south, they'll be like a cornered beast, scared and aggressive.\n你知道为什么！他们这个种族向来凶悍，如今他们正从北边逃往南边，会像被逼入绝境的野兽一样，又惊恐又好斗。"

    old "I agree, but maybe they'll listen to our offer precisely because of that."
    new "I agree, but maybe they'll listen to our offer precisely because of that.\n我同意，但也许正因如此，他们才会听我们的提议。"

    old "What offer?"
    new "What offer?\n什么提议？"

    old "I don't know yet. I need a bit of time to think."
    new "I don't know yet. I need a bit of time to think.\n我还不知道。我需要一点时间想一想。"

    old "Well, whatever you come up with, it better be good, [protag]. It'll have to be if this is going to work."
    new "Well, whatever you come up with, it better be good, [protag]. It'll have to be if this is going to work.\n嗯，不管你想出什么办法，最好都是个好办法，[protag]。要让它奏效，非如此不可。"

    old "She sighs."
    new "She sighs.\n她叹了口气。"

    old "I can tell she still has her doubts, but at least she's willing to put her trust in me for now."
    new "I can tell she still has her doubts, but at least she's willing to put her trust in me for now.\n我看得出她仍心存疑虑，但至少此刻她愿意信任我。"

    old "I'll get back to you as soon as I can. Meanwhile, arrange a meeting with the orc leaders."
    new "I'll get back to you as soon as I can. Meanwhile, arrange a meeting with the orc leaders.\n我会尽快给你答复。同时，去安排一场和 Orc 首领们的会面。"

    old "That's what my people want to do, but we can't afford to start another war right now."
    new "That's what my people want to do, but we can't afford to start another war right now.\n这也是我的人想做的事，可我们现在承受不起再打一场战争。"

    old "True. With all the fighting at N'Mar, a war between the nomads and the orcs is the last thing we need. But maybe... we don't need to kill them all."
    new "True. With all the fighting at N'Mar, a war between the nomads and the orcs is the last thing we need. But maybe... we don't need to kill them all.\n没错。N'Mar 那边战事正酣，Nomads 和 Orcs 之间的战争是我们最不想要的。但也许……我们不必把他们全杀光。"

    old "Only their leaders?"
    new "Only their leaders?\n只杀他们的首领？"

    old "Yes. An assassination mission."
    new "Yes. An assassination mission.\n对。一场暗杀行动。"

    old "Hm. It won't be easy. They set up temporary camps at the end of each day since they're always on the move."
    new "Hm. It won't be easy. They set up temporary camps at the end of each day since they're always on the move.\n嗯。这不容易。他们总是在移动，每天结束时都会搭起临时营地。"

    old "Perfect. We'll strike at night. They'll be tired after walking all day."
    new "Perfect. We'll strike at night. They'll be tired after walking all day.\n完美。我们夜里出击。他们走了一整天，会疲惫不堪。"

    old "You said 'we'. Who exactly are you referring to?"
    new "You said 'we'. Who exactly are you referring to?\n你说“我们”。你指的到底是谁？"

    old "You, me, and whoever else wants to join."
    new "You, me, and whoever else wants to join.\n你，我，还有任何想加入的人。"

    old "You think the others would be willing to help?"
    new "You think the others would be willing to help?\n你觉得其他人会愿意帮忙吗？"

    old "Why not? They like you. And, in any case, helping you means helping our cause."
    new "Why not? They like you. And, in any case, helping you means helping our cause.\n为什么不呢？他们喜欢你。而且，无论如何，帮你就等于帮我们的事业。"

    old "I'll be here waiting for you then. Please hurry. Larik doesn't know about this encounter. If he moves before we do..."
    new "I'll be here waiting for you then. Please hurry. Larik doesn't know about this encounter. If he moves before we do...\n那我就在这里等你。请快点。Larik 不知道这次碰面。如果他在我们之前行动……"

    old "What does he plan to do about the orcs?"
    new "What does he plan to do about the orcs?\n他打算怎么对付 Orcs？"

    old "He wants to attack them. He believes that the only solution is a full scale war. He's planning to form an alliance with other tribes in the area and march towards the orcs."
    new "He wants to attack them. He believes that the only solution is a full scale war. He's planning to form an alliance with other tribes in the area and march towards the orcs.\n他想攻击他们。他相信唯一的办法就是全面开战。他正计划和这一带的其他部族结盟，向 Orcs 进军。"

    old "That's a terrible plan. Even if he ultimately wins, something like that will end in a lot of bloodshed. My plan is faster and there's less risk of casualties for your people."
    new "That's a terrible plan. Even if he ultimately wins, something like that will end in a lot of bloodshed. My plan is faster and there's less risk of casualties for your people.\n那是个糟糕透顶的计划。就算他最终获胜，这样的事也会以大量的流血收场。我的计划更快，你的人民伤亡的风险也更小。"

    old "I trust you, and I'm sure Larik would too. But there is a lot of pressure from the village elders and the other chiefs."
    new "I trust you, and I'm sure Larik would too. But there is a lot of pressure from the village elders and the other chiefs.\n我相信你，也相信 Larik 会信你。但村里的长老和其他酋长带来了很大的压力。"

    old "I think they plan to attack shortly after the next full moon, day [nuala_deadline]. If we want to stop this, we have to do it before that date."
    new "I think they plan to attack shortly after the next full moon, day [nuala_deadline]. If we want to stop this, we have to do it before that date.\n我想他们计划在下一个满月后不久发动攻击，就是 [nuala_deadline] 那天。要想阻止这件事，我们必须在那个日期之前动手。"

    old "N'Mar comes first, Nuala. But after the next full moon, I promise I'll try to help."
    new "N'Mar comes first, Nuala. But after the next full moon, I promise I'll try to help.\nN'Mar 优先，Nuala。但下一个满月之后，我保证我会尽力帮忙。"

    old "I think they plan to do it on day [nuala_deadline]. If we want to stop this, we have to do it before that date."
    new "I think they plan to do it on day [nuala_deadline]. If we want to stop this, we have to do it before that date.\n我想他们计划在 [nuala_deadline] 那天动手。要想阻止这件事，我们必须在那个日期之前动手。"

    old "I'll do my best."
    new "I'll do my best.\n我会尽力的。"

    old "Nuala?"
    new "Nuala?\nNuala？"

    old "Why is she so sad? Wait. What day is it?"
    new "Why is she so sad? Wait. What day is it?\n她为什么这么伤心？等等。今天是什么日子？"

    old "My eyes widen as I recall the answer to my question."
    new "My eyes widen as I recall the answer to my question.\n我想起自己那个问题的答案，眼睛顿时睁大了。"

    old "Shit! There were so many things going on... I... I'm sorry, Nuala. I completely forgot!"
    new "Shit! There were so many things going on... I... I'm sorry, Nuala. I completely forgot!\n该死！事情太多了……我……我很抱歉，Nuala。我完全忘了！"

    old "Did your tribe end up going to war with the orcs?"
    new "Did your tribe end up going to war with the orcs?\n你的部族最后和 Orcs 开战了吗？"

    old "Yes. We won a few battles and the orcs ended up moving east, near the Everburn mountains. They seem to have settled there for now, but..."
    new "Yes. We won a few battles and the orcs ended up moving east, near the Everburn mountains. They seem to have settled there for now, but...\n是的。我们赢了几场战斗，Orcs 最终向东迁移，到了 Everburn Mountains 附近。他们似乎暂时在那里定居了，但是……"

    old "We lost many men. Many elders, many young. It was a massacre."
    new "We lost many men. Many elders, many young. It was a massacre.\n我们失去了很多人。许多长者，许多年轻人。那是一场屠杀。"

    old "I try to get closer to Nuala to comfort her, but she instinctively moves away from me."
    new "I try to get closer to Nuala to comfort her, but she instinctively moves away from me.\n我试着靠近 Nuala 去安慰她，但她本能地从我身边挪开了。"

    old "I know what happened is not your fault, [protag]. But... somehow I hoped you could find the time to help me. To help us."
    new "I know what happened is not your fault, [protag]. But... somehow I hoped you could find the time to help me. To help us.\n我知道发生的事不是你的错，[protag]。但……我不知怎的还是希望你能抽出时间来帮我。帮我们。"

    old "Nuala, come. There are more injured to attend to."
    new "Nuala, come. There are more injured to attend to.\nNuala，过来吧。还有更多伤者要照料。"

    old "I am coming, Larik."
    new "I am coming, Larik.\n我来了，Larik。"

    old "I open the mouth to say something, but then stop. There's nothing I can say to make this situation better. Words aren't going to fix what happened here."
    new "I open the mouth to say something, but then stop. There's nothing I can say to make this situation better. Words aren't going to fix what happened here.\n我张嘴想说点什么，却又停住了。我说什么都无法让这局面好起来。言语弥补不了这里发生的一切。"

    old "Nuala's eyes meet mine. No matter what expression she shows me, there's usually an underlying determination to it. But that's not there today. Today, I only read sadness and defeat in her gaze."
    new "Nuala's eyes meet mine. No matter what expression she shows me, there's usually an underlying determination to it. But that's not there today. Today, I only read sadness and defeat in her gaze.\nNuala 的目光与我的相遇。无论她对我露出什么表情，通常背后总透着一股决心。但今天没有了。今天，我从她的目光里只读到了悲伤和挫败。"

    old "I need to go now. I hope to see you again."
    new "I need to go now. I hope to see you again.\n我现在得走了。希望还能再见到你。"

    old "I hope so too."
    new "I hope so too.\n我也希望如此。"

    old "And Nuala?"
    new "And Nuala?\n还有，Nuala？"

    old " Yes?"
    new " Yes?\n嗯？"

    old "I'm sorry. I wish I could have done more for you and your people."
    new "I'm sorry. I wish I could have done more for you and your people.\n对不起。我多希望自己当初能为你和你的人民做得更多。"

    old "I know, [protag]. I know."
    new "I know, [protag]. I know.\n我知道，[protag]。我知道。"

    old "I arrive at the desert expecting to meet up with Nuala alone. However, to my surprise, I find that Larik is there as well."
    new "I arrive at the desert expecting to meet up with Nuala alone. However, to my surprise, I find that Larik is there as well.\n我抵达沙漠时，本想着单独和 Nuala 碰面。然而，令我惊讶的是，Larik 也在那里。"

    old "[protag], Larik would like to join us on this mission."
    new "[protag], Larik would like to join us on this mission.\n[protag]，Larik 想加入我们这次行动。"

    old "I see. I thought you wanted to keep him out of this?"
    new "I see. I thought you wanted to keep him out of this?\n我明白了。我还以为你想让他置身事外？"

    old "No, I only said that he was unaware of our previous meeting. When you told me that you were coming, I decided to inform him."
    new "No, I only said that he was unaware of our previous meeting. When you told me that you were coming, I decided to inform him.\n不，我只是说他不知道我们之前的会面。当你告诉我你要来时，我决定通知他。"

    old "While I fear it may be inevitable, I do not crave a full scale war with the orcs. Not right now. So, if you have a better plan, I'm willing to try it."
    new "While I fear it may be inevitable, I do not crave a full scale war with the orcs. Not right now. So, if you have a better plan, I'm willing to try it.\n虽然我担心这也许在所难免，但我并不渴望与 Orcs 全面开战。至少现在不想。所以，如果你有更好的计划，我愿意一试。"

    old "That's good."
    new "That's good.\n那很好。"

    old "Nuala turns her attention to the other party members behind me."
    new "Nuala turns her attention to the other party members behind me.\nNuala 把注意力转向我身后的其他同伴。"

    old "Thank you all for coming."
    new "Thank you all for coming.\n谢谢大家能来。"

    old "I only came because Karen told me to verify the rumors behind those demon sightings."
    new "I only came because Karen told me to verify the rumors behind those demon sightings.\n我只是因为 Karen 让我来核实那些恶魔目击事件背后的传言才来的。"

    old "Oh. Well, thanks for being honest, I guess."
    new "Oh. Well, thanks for being honest, I guess.\n哦。嗯，谢谢你的坦诚，我想。"

    old "Anything to help you, Nuala!"
    new "Anything to help you, Nuala!\n只要能帮到你，Nuala，我什么都愿意做！"

    old "Oh, you too Larik. Sorry."
    new "Oh, you too Larik. Sorry.\n哦，你也是，Larik。抱歉。"

    old "It's been awhile since I've fought orcs. They're talented warriors and I figured I could use the training."
    new "It's been awhile since I've fought orcs. They're talented warriors and I figured I could use the training.\n我很久没跟 Orcs 交过手了。他们都是出色的战士，我想我可以借机锻炼一下。"

    old "Ah, but I'm mainly here to help you, of course."
    new "Ah, but I'm mainly here to help you, of course.\n啊，不过我当然主要是来帮你的。"

    old "I'm not fond of the desert and the heat. However, you're a good person Nuala. I wanted to help you."
    new "I'm not fond of the desert and the heat. However, you're a good person Nuala. I wanted to help you.\n我不太喜欢沙漠和酷热。不过，你是个好人，Nuala。我想帮你。"

    old "Thanks, Jasper."
    new "Thanks, Jasper.\n谢谢，Jasper。"

    old "I'm still hoping that we can find a peaceful solution to this problem."
    new "I'm still hoping that we can find a peaceful solution to this problem.\n我仍然希望我们能找到一个和平的解决办法。"

    old "Be careful of the orc shamans. They tend to be tough opponents."
    new "Be careful of the orc shamans. They tend to be tough opponents.\n小心那些 Orc 萨满。他们往往是难缠的对手。"

    old "I take you've fought them before?"
    new "I take you've fought them before?\n我猜你以前和他们交过手？"

    old "A couple of times, yes."
    new "A couple of times, yes.\n交过几次，是的。"

    old "Orcs are powerful, but they aren't very quick. They will be no match for my blades."
    new "Orcs are powerful, but they aren't very quick. They will be no match for my blades.\nOrcs 很强大，但速度不太快。他们不会是我的双刃的对手。"

    old "You seem pretty sure of yourself, Sylrissa."
    new "You seem pretty sure of yourself, Sylrissa.\n你看起来相当自信，Sylrissa。"

    old "As always."
    new "As always.\n一向如此。"

    old "I gather everyone around me and start explaining the plan."
    new "I gather everyone around me and start explaining the plan.\n我把大家召集到身边，开始讲解计划。"

    old "All right people, listen."
    new "All right people, listen.\n好了，大家听我说。"

    old "I know that many of you think that this is foolish, but we're going to parley with the orc leaders. You're here to back us up if things go bad, but we are trying to resolve this peacefully."
    new "I know that many of you think that this is foolish, but we're going to parley with the orc leaders. You're here to back us up if things go bad, but we are trying to resolve this peacefully.\n我知道你们很多人觉得这很蠢，但我们要去和 Orc 首领们谈判。如果情况恶化，你们在这里为我们撑腰，但我们是想要和平解决这件事。"

    old "And what makes you think that they'll listen in the first place?"
    new "And what makes you think that they'll listen in the first place?\n你又凭什么认为他们一开始会听呢？"

    old "Remember, I represent the interests of the Council of Grimoire right now. That position should carry enough weight to get them to at least hear us out."
    new "Remember, I represent the interests of the Council of Grimoire right now. That position should carry enough weight to get them to at least hear us out.\n记住，我现在代表的是 Grimoire 议会的利益。这个身份应该足够有分量，能让他们至少听我们把话说完。"

    old "What are you planning to say?"
    new "What are you planning to say?\n你打算说些什么？"

    old "Watch out, they're coming."
    new "Watch out, they're coming.\n小心，他们来了。"

    old "A small group of orcs approaches us. The leaders then step forward, with their escort guards."
    new "A small group of orcs approaches us. The leaders then step forward, with their escort guards.\n一小群 Orcs 向我们走来。接着，首领们带着他们的护卫走上前来。"

    old "One of them in particular is large and imposing. He's the one that gets the closest. I suppose that means he's the one I'll be dealing with."
    new "One of them in particular is large and imposing. He's the one that gets the closest. I suppose that means he's the one I'll be dealing with.\n其中有一个格外高大威猛。他走得最靠前。我想这意味着他就是我要打交道的人。"

    old "I'm Hozor, ruler of the Skullsplitter Clan. Biggest and most feared orc clan of the Orcish Wastes. Why is the Envoy of Grimoire here?"
    new "I'm Hozor, ruler of the Skullsplitter Clan. Biggest and most feared orc clan of the Orcish Wastes. Why is the Envoy of Grimoire here?\n我是 Hozor，Skullsplitter 氏族的统治者，Orcish Wastes 最大、最令人畏惧的 Orc 氏族。Grimoire 的特使来这里做什么？"

    old "I see my reputation precedes me. My name is [protag]. It's a pleasure to meet you, Hozor, and the rest of you estimate leaders of the orc tribes of the north. "
    new "I see my reputation precedes me. My name is [protag]. It's a pleasure to meet you, Hozor, and the rest of you estimate leaders of the orc tribes of the north. \n看来我的名声传到了我前面。我叫 [protag]。很高兴见到你，Hozor，以及诸位，北方的 Orc 部族首领们。"

    old "Not 'north' for much longer."
    new "Not 'north' for much longer.\n很快就不是“北方”了。"

    old "You'd better think twice before moving any further south!"
    new "You'd better think twice before moving any further south!\n你再往南走之前，最好三思！"

    old "Oh, it's already happening. And you and your pathetic tribes won't stop us."
    new "Oh, it's already happening. And you and your pathetic tribes won't stop us.\n哦，这已经发生了。你和你那些可悲的部落阻止不了我们。"

    old "Well now, this meeting is already off to a good start. I need to do something before they start killing each other."
    new "Well now, this meeting is already off to a good start. I need to do something before they start killing each other.\n这下好了，这场会面一开始就不妙。我得在他们自相残杀之前做点什么。"

    old "Ha! This [prace] has guts. I like it."
    new "Ha! This [prace] has guts. I like it.\n哈！这个 [prace] 有胆量。我喜欢。"

    old "Now that I have your attention, let's talk about a solution."
    new "Now that I have your attention, let's talk about a solution.\n既然我引起了你的注意，我们来谈谈解决办法吧。"

    old "I step between the two just in time to intercept a push that Hozor meant for Larik. Unfortunately, that push sends me backwards and into the ground."
    new "I step between the two just in time to intercept a push that Hozor meant for Larik. Unfortunately, that push sends me backwards and into the ground.\n我及时插到两人中间，拦下了 Hozor 原本冲着 Larik 的那一推。可惜，那一推把我推得向后倒去，摔在地上。"

    old "I get up and dust the sand off of myself, flashing Hozor an annoyed glare in the process. He remains unfazed."
    new "I get up and dust the sand off of myself, flashing Hozor an annoyed glare in the process. He remains unfazed.\n我站起身，拍掉身上的沙，同时恼怒地瞪了 Hozor 一眼。他依旧泰然自若。"

    old "Ha. You need to work on your muscles, [protag]. Still, I apologize. I may have let my temper get the better of me."
    new "Ha. You need to work on your muscles, [protag]. Still, I apologize. I may have let my temper get the better of me.\n哈。你得练练你的肌肉了，[protag]。不过，我还是道歉。我刚才可能有些被脾气冲昏了头。"

    old "This orc is a beast. I've fought mighty adversaries before, but never anyone this physically strong."
    new "This orc is a beast. I've fought mighty adversaries before, but never anyone this physically strong.\n这个 Orc 真是头野兽。我以前和强大的对手交过手，但从未遇到过体格这么强壮的人。"

    old "Apology accepted. Now, please listen to what I have to say."
    new "Apology accepted. Now, please listen to what I have to say.\n我接受你的道歉。现在，请听我说。"

    old "Larik and Hozor keep arguing, completely ignoring me."
    new "Larik and Hozor keep arguing, completely ignoring me.\nLarik 和 Hozor 继续争吵，完全无视我。"

    old "<Coughs> Ahem, are you two done? I'm sure we can come up with a compromise if we just cooperate with each other."
    new "<Coughs> Ahem, are you two done? I'm sure we can come up with a compromise if we just cooperate with each other.\n（咳嗽）咳咳，你们两个说完了吗？我相信只要我们彼此合作，一定能达成妥协。"

    old "All right, amuse me. What do you propose?"
    new "All right, amuse me. What do you propose?\n好吧，逗我开心一下。你有什么提议？"

    old "First of all, why are you moving south in the first place? I've heard some stories but I'd like to know the truth from the orc leaders themselves."
    new "First of all, why are you moving south in the first place? I've heard some stories but I'd like to know the truth from the orc leaders themselves.\n首先，你们当初为什么南下？我听过一些说法，但我想听 Orc 首领们亲口说出真相。"

    old "And why is this your concern? Why should we tell our secrets to you? So you can exploit our weaknesses?"
    new "And why is this your concern? Why should we tell our secrets to you? So you can exploit our weaknesses?\n这又与你何干？我们为什么要把秘密告诉你？好让你利用我们的弱点吗？"

    old "Hozor remains silent for a few seconds, his eyes on mine as he carefully assesses me. Then, he turns to the other orcs and gives me my answer."
    new "Hozor remains silent for a few seconds, his eyes on mine as he carefully assesses me. Then, he turns to the other orcs and gives me my answer.\nHozor 沉默了几秒，他目光紧盯着我，仔细地打量着我。然后，他转向其他 Orcs，给了我答复。"

    old "I suppose what you say makes sense."
    new "I suppose what you say makes sense.\n我想你说的有道理。"

    old "Yes, we'd prefer not to explain."
    new "Yes, we'd prefer not to explain.\n是的，我们宁愿不作解释。"

    old "I see..."
    new "I see...\n我明白了……"

    old "The demons are supposed to be gone."
    new "The demons are supposed to be gone.\n恶魔本该已经消失了。"

    old "I was skeptical too. I still am."
    new "I was skeptical too. I still am.\n我本来也怀疑。现在依然怀疑。"

    old "I haven't seen any demons myself, but some of my orcs claim that they've seen one."
    new "I haven't seen any demons myself, but some of my orcs claim that they've seen one.\n我自己没见过任何恶魔，但我的一些 Orc 族人声称他们见过。"

    old "Do you believe them?"
    new "Do you believe them?\n你相信他们吗？"

    old "I'll believe them when I see a demon for myself."
    new "I'll believe them when I see a demon for myself.\n等我亲眼见到恶魔，我就会相信他们。"

    old "You asked why we're moving south. The answer is simple enough. We used to be happy up north. From there, we could ambush caravans from Horus and Hammerhands."
    new "You asked why we're moving south. The answer is simple enough. We used to be happy up north. From there, we could ambush caravans from Horus and Hammerhands.\n你问我们为什么南下。答案很简单。我们以前在北方过得很自在。从那里，我们可以伏击来往 Horus 和 Hammerhands 的车队。"

    old "I don't even want to know what the faces of my companions look like upon hearing that. I just hope they'll keep quiet."
    new "I don't even want to know what the faces of my companions look like upon hearing that. I just hope they'll keep quiet.\n我根本不想知道同伴们听到这话时脸上的表情。我只希望他们保持安静。"

    old "We had food, water. We could plunder undisturbed. We didn't lack anything."
    new "We had food, water. We could plunder undisturbed. We didn't lack anything.\n我们有食物，有水。我们可以不受打扰地劫掠。我们什么都不缺。"

    old "But that started to change about a month ago. Strange things began happening."
    new "But that started to change about a month ago. Strange things began happening.\n但大约一个月前，情况开始改变。怪事接连发生。"

    old "Orc scouts disappearing out of nowhere, rotting animal carcasses, polluted water."
    new "Orc scouts disappearing out of nowhere, rotting animal carcasses, polluted water.\nOrc 侦察兵凭空消失，动物尸体腐烂，水源被污染。"

    old "The whole area seems to be under the influence of some powerful blight. We don't know the origin of this corruption, but we do know that if we stay there, we're dead."
    new "The whole area seems to be under the influence of some powerful blight. We don't know the origin of this corruption, but we do know that if we stay there, we're dead.\n整个地区似乎都笼罩在某种强大的灾疫之下。我们不知道这种腐化的源头，但我们确实知道，如果留在那里，我们就死定了。"

    old "I know the source of the blight."
    new "I know the source of the blight.\n我知道那灾疫的源头。"

    old "Uh?"
    new "Uh?\n呃？"

    old "It's the Castle of N'Mar."
    new "It's the Castle of N'Mar.\n是 N'Mar 的城堡。"

    old "Lies. The Castle is too far away from here."
    new "Lies. The Castle is too far away from here.\n谎言。那座城堡离这里太远了。"

    old "Ask Nuala and Larik. The mist is only around N'Mar, but signs of its corruption are everywhere. The Tomb of Urd, for example. The Great Forest."
    new "Ask Nuala and Larik. The mist is only around N'Mar, but signs of its corruption are everywhere. The Tomb of Urd, for example. The Great Forest.\n问问 Nuala 和 Larik。迷雾只在 N'Mar 周围，但它的腐化迹象却随处可见。比如 Urd 的陵墓。还有 Great Forest。"

    old "Our mission is to put an end to that corruption but, in order to do that, we need to focus on N'Mar. Right now, you're waylaying our efforts."
    new "Our mission is to put an end to that corruption but, in order to do that, we need to focus on N'Mar. Right now, you're waylaying our efforts.\n我们的使命就是终结那种腐化，但要做到这一点，我们必须专注于 N'Mar。而现在，你们在拖我们的后腿。"

    old "Even if I wanted to believe you, what can you do to help my people?"
    new "Even if I wanted to believe you, what can you do to help my people?\n就算我愿意相信你，你又能做些什么来帮助我的人民？"

    old "Well, as you know, I represent the interests of the Council of Grimoire."
    new "Well, as you know, I represent the interests of the Council of Grimoire.\n嗯，如你所知，我代表的是 Grimoire 议会的利益。"

    old "Pah, the 'powerful' Human Empire."
    new "Pah, the 'powerful' Human Empire.\n呸，那个“强大”的人类帝国。"

    old "As far as I know, they've beaten you several times in the past already."
    new "As far as I know, they've beaten you several times in the past already.\n据我所知，他们过去已经打败过你们好几次了。"

    old "Get to the point."
    new "Get to the point.\n说重点。"

    old "Was that a threat?!"
    new "Was that a threat?!\n那是威胁吗？！"

    old "No. It was a warning. I have no personal grudge against you, however..."
    new "No. It was a warning. I have no personal grudge against you, however...\n不，是警告。我对你没有私人恩怨，不过……"

    old "Let's say that you do keep pushing south and end up clashing with the nomad tribes. The Empire might decide to come and aid them. And maybe they'd do that under the pretense of gaining the favor of those tribes, but I imagine that the real draw would be putting an end to their annoying orc problem once and for all."
    new "Let's say that you do keep pushing south and end up clashing with the nomad tribes. The Empire might decide to come and aid them. And maybe they'd do that under the pretense of gaining the favor of those tribes, but I imagine that the real draw would be putting an end to their annoying orc problem once and for all.\n假设你们真的继续南进，最终与游牧部族发生冲突。帝国也许会决定前来援助他们。也许他们会打着博取那些部落好感的旗号这么做，但我想，真正的好处会是——一劳永逸地解决掉他们烦人的 Orc 问题。"

    old "Yes, that seems like something that the Council would instantly approve."
    new "Yes, that seems like something that the Council would instantly approve.\n是的，这听上去像是议会会立即批准的事。"

    old "Hopefully, they don't know that the Council is so broke that they can't afford a war with the orcs right now."
    new "Hopefully, they don't know that the Council is so broke that they can't afford a war with the orcs right now.\n只希望他们不知道议会如今穷得连一场与 Orcs 的战争都打不起。"

    old "Ha! They'd rather see us die than help us!"
    new "Ha! They'd rather see us die than help us!\n哈！他们宁愿看着我们死，也不愿帮我们！"

    old "True enough. If you were the ones asking they wouldn't lift a finger to help."
    new "True enough. If you were the ones asking they wouldn't lift a finger to help.\n一点没错。如果是你们去求他们，他们一根手指都不会抬。"

    old "But you aren't the ones asking. I am. I'll make it clear that helping you is essential to the success of my mission. And they'll believe me."
    new "But you aren't the ones asking. I am. I'll make it clear that helping you is essential to the success of my mission. And they'll believe me.\n但去求他们的不是你们，而是我。我会说清楚，帮助你们对我使命的成功至关重要。而他们会相信我的。"

    old "And what could they possibly do to help?"
    new "And what could they possibly do to help?\n他们又能做些什么来帮忙？"

    old "Well, you're going to need food and water, right? If you move south, you won't be able to ambush the caravans travelling to Horus or Hammerhands anymore. You would be too far away."
    new "Well, you're going to need food and water, right? If you move south, you won't be able to ambush the caravans travelling to Horus or Hammerhands anymore. You would be too far away.\n嗯，你们会需要食物和水，对吧？如果你们南下，就再也无法伏击前往 Horus 或 Hammerhands 的车队了。你们会离得太远。"

    old "But if the Council willingly sent you food and water that wouldn't be an issue."
    new "But if the Council willingly sent you food and water that wouldn't be an issue.\n但如果议会主动给你们送来食物和水，那就不成问题了。"

    old "They would do that?!"
    new "They would do that?!\n他们会那么做？！"

    old "If I ask, probably. I imagine that you don't want to let your orcs starve or die of thirst, right?"
    new "If I ask, probably. I imagine that you don't want to let your orcs starve or die of thirst, right?\n如果我去请求，大概会。我想你也不愿意让你的 Orcs 挨饿或渴死，对吧？"

    old "Shelter? Where?"
    new "Shelter? Where?\n避难所？在哪里？"

    old "Well, Horus and Lothark are the closest towns, and-"
    new "Well, Horus and Lothark are the closest towns, and-\n嗯，Horus 和 Lothark 是最近的城镇，而——"

    old "Please, [protag]. Do you take me for a fool? You can't honestly believe that they would open their gates to us orcs. Orcs who assassinated their soldiers, who robbed their merchants, who-"
    new "Please, [protag]. Do you take me for a fool? You can't honestly believe that they would open their gates to us orcs. Orcs who assassinated their soldiers, who robbed their merchants, who-\n拜托，[protag]。你把我当傻瓜吗？你不会真以为他们会为我们 Orcs 敞开大门吧。这些 Orcs 刺杀过他们的士兵，抢劫过他们的商旅，还——"

    old "I get it, I get it. Maybe..."
    new "I get it, I get it. Maybe...\n我懂，我懂。也许……"

    old "Hozor, you need to understand one thing."
    new "Hozor, you need to understand one thing.\nHozor，你需要明白一件事。"

    old "We've fought the Empire before. We might lose, but we won't go down without a fight."
    new "We've fought the Empire before. We might lose, but we won't go down without a fight.\n我们以前和帝国打过仗。我们也许会输，但我们不会不战而降。"

    old "This time though, it isn't just the Empire. Queen Karen is supporting our war efforts on N'Mar. The amazons are fighting with us too."
    new "This time though, it isn't just the Empire. Queen Karen is supporting our war efforts on N'Mar. The amazons are fighting with us too.\n不过这一次，对手不只有帝国。Karen 女王在支持我们对 N'Mar 的战争。Amazons 也在和我们并肩作战。"

    old "Not the whole truth, but he doesn't need to know that, right?"
    new "Not the whole truth, but he doesn't need to know that, right?\n不全是实话，但他不必知道，对吧？"

    old "What? The amazons?"
    new "What? The amazons?\n什么？Amazons？"

    old "Good. That had the intended effect on him. The amazons are feared thoroughout Aravorn for their skill in combat."
    new "Good. That had the intended effect on him. The amazons are feared thoroughout Aravorn for their skill in combat.\n好。这对他起到了预期的效果。Amazons 的武艺在整个 Aravorn 都令人闻风丧胆。"

    old "Do not misunderstand me, [protag]. I do not want a war. Not this time. But if we are going to die anyway, we will die fighting!"
    new "Do not misunderstand me, [protag]. I do not want a war. Not this time. But if we are going to die anyway, we will die fighting!\n别误解我，[protag]。我不想要战争。至少这次不想。但如果我们横竖都是死，我们就战斗到底！"

    old "Let's hope that we can find an alternative then. All I'm asking for is more time."
    new "Let's hope that we can find an alternative then. All I'm asking for is more time.\n那我们希望还能找到别的办法。我要求的只是更多时间。"

    old "Hmm... I suppose if we halved the rations and are more careful with our resources... maybe..."
    new "Hmm... I suppose if we halved the rations and are more careful with our resources... maybe...\n嗯……我想，如果我们把口粮减半，对资源更省着点用……也许……"

    old "You probably won't believe me, but I assure you that it's the truth."
    new "You probably won't believe me, but I assure you that it's the truth.\n你大概不会相信我，但我向你保证，那是事实。"

    old "You saw it yourself. The corruption is everywhere. You're running from it and I can understand that. You can't face it alone. But together? Together we can do something about it."
    new "You saw it yourself. The corruption is everywhere. You're running from it and I can understand that. You can't face it alone. But together? Together we can do something about it.\n你自己也看到了。腐化无处不在。你在逃离它，这我能理解。你无法独自面对它。但如果我们一起呢？一起的话，我们就能做点什么。"

    old "Fight the undead north of your area. Help us. Help the Human Empire, the Amazons, the Elves."
    new "Fight the undead north of your area. Help us. Help the Human Empire, the Amazons, the Elves.\n去与你北边的亡灵作战。帮帮我们。帮帮人类帝国、Amazons 和 Elves。"

    old "Help them? Why we should?"
    new "Help them? Why we should?\n帮他们？我们为什么要帮他们？"

    old "Because if we don't band together now, the undead win. We will either succeed together or we will fall."
    new "Because if we don't band together now, the undead win. We will either succeed together or we will fall.\n因为如果我们现在不团结起来，亡灵就会获胜。我们要么一起成功，要么一起倒下。"

    old "You didn't want to tell me why you were moving south, but let me guess: corruption, undead, death everywhere."
    new "You didn't want to tell me why you were moving south, but let me guess: corruption, undead, death everywhere.\n你本不想告诉我你们南下的原因，但让我猜猜：腐化、亡灵、遍地死亡。"

    old "How did you know?! Have you been spying on us?"
    new "How did you know?! Have you been spying on us?\n你怎么知道的？！你一直在监视我们？"

    old "There was no need for that. We've been investigating this phenomenon for several weeks now. It originates from N'Mar, but it's spreading everywhere."
    new "There was no need for that. We've been investigating this phenomenon for several weeks now. It originates from N'Mar, but it's spreading everywhere.\n没那个必要。这个现象我们已经调查好几个星期了。它源自 N'Mar，但正在四处扩散。"

    old "You can keep moving south for now, but eventually there won't be anywhere to run to if we don't stop this together."
    new "You can keep moving south for now, but eventually there won't be anywhere to run to if we don't stop this together.\n你们眼下可以继续南迁，但如果我们不一起阻止它，最终你将无处可逃。"

    old "What! Orcs don't run from anyone!"
    new "What! Orcs don't run from anyone!\n什么！Orcs 不会逃避任何人！"

    old "Really? Because that's what it looks like you're doing to me right now."
    new "Really? Because that's what it looks like you're doing to me right now.\n是吗？因为在我看来，你现在就在这么做。"

    old "W-we're only moving south because we have no more food or water..."
    new "W-we're only moving south because we have no more food or water...\n我、我们南下只是因为我们没有食物和水了……"

    old "The undead will continue corrupting the land as they dog your steps. How long you will be able to run? Your clan is going to have to eventually fight to survive one way or the other. Wouldn't it be better to fight back against the undead?"
    new "The undead will continue corrupting the land as they dog your steps. How long you will be able to run? Your clan is going to have to eventually fight to survive one way or the other. Wouldn't it be better to fight back against the undead?\n亡灵会步步紧逼，继续腐化大地。你还能跑多久？你的氏族终究得为了生存而战，无论以哪种方式。反击亡灵难道不是更好吗？"

    old "Don't you want to fight back like a real Orc Warchief?"
    new "Don't you want to fight back like a real Orc Warchief?\n你难道不想像一个真正的 Orc 战争首领那样反击吗？"

    old "You're right, [protag]. This is not how a warchief should behave."
    new "You're right, [protag]. This is not how a warchief should behave.\n你说得对，[protag]。一个战争首领不该这样行事。"

    old "Still, this isn't a decision that can be made lightly."
    new "Still, this isn't a decision that can be made lightly.\n不过，这不是一个能轻易做出的决定。"

    old "I've heard enough. I'll consult with the other leaders and then come back with our answer."
    new "I've heard enough. I'll consult with the other leaders and then come back with our answer.\n我听够了。我会先和其他首领商议，然后带着我们的答复回来。"

    old "Hozor leaves us behind and rejoins his fellow orcs. I watch nervously from afar as they debate."
    new "Hozor leaves us behind and rejoins his fellow orcs. I watch nervously from afar as they debate.\nHozor 丢下我们，回到他的 Orc 同胞们中间。我紧张地从远处看着他们争论。"

    old "I feel a hand on my arm and soft hair brushing my shoulders. I turn to see Nuala's face very close to mine. She leans in closer and whispers in my ear."
    new "I feel a hand on my arm and soft hair brushing my shoulders. I turn to see Nuala's face very close to mine. She leans in closer and whispers in my ear.\n我感到一只手搭在我的手臂上，柔软的发丝拂过我的肩膀。我转过身，看见 Nuala 的脸离我极近。她俯身靠得更近，在我耳边低语。"

    old "Do you think you were... convincing?"
    new "Do you think you were... convincing?\n你觉得你刚才……有说服力吗？"

    old "I guess we'll know shortly. Look, Hozor is coming back now."
    new "I guess we'll know shortly. Look, Hozor is coming back now.\n我想我们很快就会知道了。看，Hozor 回来了。"

    old "We won't move further south. For now. We have enough food and water for about 50, maybe 60 days."
    new "We won't move further south. For now. We have enough food and water for about 50, maybe 60 days.\n我们暂时不会再往南移了。我们现有的食物和水，大概够五十天，也许六十天。"

    old "Do what you need to do. You have my word that we won't move from here for the next 50 days."
    new "Do what you need to do. You have my word that we won't move from here for the next 50 days.\n去做你该做的事吧。我向你保证，接下来的五十天，我们不会离开这里。"

    old "However, after that... We might not have another choice."
    new "However, after that... We might not have another choice.\n不过，在那之后……我们可能就别无选择了。"

    old "Don't worry Hozor. In 60 days, this won't be a problem anymore."
    new "Don't worry Hozor. In 60 days, this won't be a problem anymore.\n别担心，Hozor。六十天后，这就不再是问题了。"

    old "He extends his hand. I admit I'm caught by surprise, but I quickly collect myself enough to shake his hand."
    new "He extends his hand. I admit I'm caught by surprise, but I quickly collect myself enough to shake his hand.\n他伸出手。我承认自己有些意外，但我很快镇定下来，握住了他的手。"

    old "Meeting you was... interesting, [protag]. Perhaps we'll meet again in future."
    new "Meeting you was... interesting, [protag]. Perhaps we'll meet again in future.\n见到你……很有意思，[protag]。也许将来我们会再见。"

    old "Perhaps."
    new "Perhaps.\n也许吧。"

    old "I must say that I was surprised by you, [protag]. The Council made a good choice when they appointed you as their envoy."
    new "I must say that I was surprised by you, [protag]. The Council made a good choice when they appointed you as their envoy.\n我必须说，你让我感到意外，[protag]。议会任命你为特使，是个明智的选择。"

    old "However, my people come first. I cannot promise you anything at the moment."
    new "However, my people come first. I cannot promise you anything at the moment.\n然而，我的人民优先。此刻我无法向你承诺任何事。"

    old "So you intend to continue moving further south?"
    new "So you intend to continue moving further south?\n所以你打算继续南进？"

    old "We'll see, but I'm afraid that it's likely. Farewell."
    new "We'll see, but I'm afraid that it's likely. Farewell.\n走着瞧吧，但恐怕很有可能。再会。"

    old "Without another word, he and the other orcs begin leaving. Soon, they dissappear into the dunes, leaving nothing behind but a sense of dread. This meeting may not have ended in bloodshed, but I still failed."
    new "Without another word, he and the other orcs begin leaving. Soon, they dissappear into the dunes, leaving nothing behind but a sense of dread. This meeting may not have ended in bloodshed, but I still failed.\n没有再说什么，他和其他 Orcs 便开始离开。很快，他们消失在沙丘之中，只留下一种不祥的预感。这场会面也许没有以流血收场，但我终究还是失败了。"

    old "[protag], I don't know what you intended to accomplish with this meeting but it was a waste of time."
    new "[protag], I don't know what you intended to accomplish with this meeting but it was a waste of time.\n[protag]，我不知道你想通过这场会面达成什么，但这纯属浪费时间。"

    old "What? But-"
    new "What? But-\n什么？可是——"

    old "Shut up, [prace]. I don't know what the Council sees in you, but you did not impress me at all."
    new "Shut up, [prace]. I don't know what the Council sees in you, but you did not impress me at all.\n闭嘴，[prace]。我不知道议会看中了你什么，但你一点都没给我留下好印象。"

    old "Take your threats, your big words, and your false promises elsewhere. We're done here."
    new "Take your threats, your big words, and your false promises elsewhere. We're done here.\n把你的威胁、你的大话、你的虚假承诺都带到别处去吧。我们之间到此为止。"

    old "You, nomads. Be careful. We may attack at any moment."
    new "You, nomads. Be careful. We may attack at any moment.\n你们这些游牧民。当心点。我们随时可能进攻。"

    old "You!!!"
    new "You!!!\n你！！！"

    old "I grab Larik and, with a considerable effort, manage to hold him back until all of the orcs have left the meeting place."
    new "I grab Larik and, with a considerable effort, manage to hold him back until all of the orcs have left the meeting place.\n我抓住 Larik，费了相当大的力气，才把他拦住，直到所有 Orcs 都离开了会面地点。"

    old "It's only then that I realize how mentally and physically exhausted I am. All that effort... and it still ended in failure."
    new "It's only then that I realize how mentally and physically exhausted I am. All that effort... and it still ended in failure.\n直到这时，我才意识到自己身心俱疲。付出了那么多努力……却仍以失败告终。"

    old "Nuala runs towards me and throws her arms around my neck, wrapping me in a tight hug."
    new "Nuala runs towards me and throws her arms around my neck, wrapping me in a tight hug.\nNuala 朝我跑来，张开双臂搂住我的脖子，紧紧拥抱住我。"

    old "Hey, um... Nuala..."
    new "Hey, um... Nuala...\n嘿，呃……Nuala……"

    old "I c-can't breathe-"
    new "I c-can't breathe-\n我、我没法呼吸了——"

    old "Oh, sorry! I'm just so happy with how this all turned out!"
    new "Oh, sorry! I'm just so happy with how this all turned out!\n哦，抱歉！我只是太高兴事情能有这样的结局！"

    old "Nuala releases me and Larik takes the opportunity to approach me next."
    new "Nuala releases me and Larik takes the opportunity to approach me next.\nNuala 松开我，Larik 趁机接着走上前来。"

    old "I hope you're not planning to hug me as well."
    new "I hope you're not planning to hug me as well.\n我希望你不会也打算拥抱我。"

    old "Ha! No. You might not come out of it alive if I were to hug you."
    new "Ha! No. You might not come out of it alive if I were to hug you.\n哈！不会。我要是抱你，你恐怕没法活着出来。"

    old "Everyone laughs. I look around me and see nothing but happy faces. I can't help but smile myself. For once we've managed to achieve our goal without spilling blood and it feels good."
    new "Everyone laughs. I look around me and see nothing but happy faces. I can't help but smile myself. For once we've managed to achieve our goal without spilling blood and it feels good.\n大家都笑了。我环顾四周，看到的只有一张张笑脸。我自己也忍不住微笑起来。这一回，我们终于在不流血的情况下达成了目标，感觉真好。"

    old "We'd better head back to Grimoire now."
    new "We'd better head back to Grimoire now.\n我们现在最好动身回 Grimoire 了。"

    old "And we'll go back to our tribe. I need to inform the other chiefs of what happened here today-- how the Envoy of Grimoire helped us avoid another war with the orcs."
    new "And we'll go back to our tribe. I need to inform the other chiefs of what happened here today-- how the Envoy of Grimoire helped us avoid another war with the orcs.\n而我们要回部族去。我得把今天发生的事告诉其他酋长——Grimoire 的特使如何帮我们避免了一场与 Orcs 的战争。"

    old "I'm sorry Nuala. I thought I could make this work."
    new "I'm sorry Nuala. I thought I could make this work.\n对不起，Nuala。我以为我能办成这件事。"

    old "You tried your best, [protag]. And, honestly, making those orcs see reason was probably a lost cause in the first place.."
    new "You tried your best, [protag]. And, honestly, making those orcs see reason was probably a lost cause in the first place..\n你尽力了，[protag]。而且，说实话，让那些 Orcs 讲道理，多半从一开始就是徒劳。"

    old "What is going to happen now?"
    new "What is going to happen now?\n现在会发生什么？"

    old "I'll go back to my village and meet with the other warchiefs. We need to plan a strategy in case the orcs attack sooner rather than later."
    new "I'll go back to my village and meet with the other warchiefs. We need to plan a strategy in case the orcs attack sooner rather than later.\n我会回我的村子，和其他战争首领碰头。我们需要制定策略，以防 Orcs 早于预期发动进攻。"

    old "I don't like leaving it like this. There has to be something else I can-"
    new "I don't like leaving it like this. There has to be something else I can-\n我不喜欢就这样搁下。一定还有别的什么我能——"

    old "No. Your mission is much more important than this. That's where your focus needs to be."
    new "No. Your mission is much more important than this. That's where your focus needs to be.\n不。你的使命比这重要得多。那才是你该专注的地方。"

    old "Besides, I think you were more successful than you realize."
    new "Besides, I think you were more successful than you realize.\n而且，我觉得你比你意识到的还要成功。"

    old "You made some good points when you spoke with them. They may have seemed confident, but I'm sure that they're going to think twice before attacking us now. We might have more time than we originally thought."
    new "You made some good points when you spoke with them. They may have seemed confident, but I'm sure that they're going to think twice before attacking us now. We might have more time than we originally thought.\n你和他们谈话时提出了几个好观点。他们也许看着自信，但我敢肯定，他们现在进攻我们之前会三思。我们可能比原先预想的拥有更多时间。"

    old "I see. Do you think you two will be all right?"
    new "I see. Do you think you two will be all right?\n我明白了。你觉得你们俩会没事吗？"

    old "We spoke about this before you arrived. Larik and I will always be at your disposal."
    new "We spoke about this before you arrived. Larik and I will always be at your disposal.\n你到之前我们就谈过了。Larik 和我随时听候你的差遣。"

    old "What? But your people need you!"
    new "What? But your people need you!\n什么？但你的人民需要你们！"

    old "There's this young fighter, Musamba, who is eager to prove his valor. I'll let him lead my tribe in this war if the orcs attack before we're done with our N'Mar business."
    new "There's this young fighter, Musamba, who is eager to prove his valor. I'll let him lead my tribe in this war if the orcs attack before we're done with our N'Mar business.\n有位年轻战士 Musamba，急于证明自己的勇武。如果在我们办完 N'Mar 的事之前 Orcs 就发动进攻，我会让他带领我的部族打这场仗。"

    old "Are you sure that's wise?"
    new "Are you sure that's wise?\n你确定那样明智吗？"

    old "We're just two people. All the other tribes, the other nomads... I don't know the exact number, but believe me, we are many. The orcs are many too, but the two of us won't make much of a difference."
    new "We're just two people. All the other tribes, the other nomads... I don't know the exact number, but believe me, we are many. The orcs are many too, but the two of us won't make much of a difference.\n我们只是两个人。所有其他部族，其他游牧民……我不知道确切的数字，但相信我，我们人很多。Orcs 也很多，但少我们两个，不会有多大差别。"

    old "I hope you're right. You two sure make a difference on my team."
    new "I hope you're right. You two sure make a difference on my team.\n希望你是对的。你们俩在我的队伍里，可绝对是一股力量。"

    old "Who knows? Maybe we'll finish our mission at N'Mar before they attack and then you'll be able to join us in the war against the orcs."
    new "Who knows? Maybe we'll finish our mission at N'Mar before they attack and then you'll be able to join us in the war against the orcs.\n谁知道呢？也许我们会在他们进攻之前完成 N'Mar 的使命，然后你就能加入我们对 Orcs 的战争了。"

    old "Or, maybe once evil at N'Mar is stopped, the corruption in the north will be gone and the orcs won't have a reason to invade our territory anymore."
    new "Or, maybe once evil at N'Mar is stopped, the corruption in the north will be gone and the orcs won't have a reason to invade our territory anymore.\n或者，也许一旦 N'Mar 的邪恶被阻止，北方的腐化就会消失，Orcs 就再也没有理由入侵我们的领土了。"

    old "I would like that."
    new "I would like that.\n我希望如此。"

    old "We're going to wait until nightfall. The orcs have spent all day travelling in the desert. With any luck, they'll be tired and we can use that to our advantage."
    new "We're going to wait until nightfall. The orcs have spent all day travelling in the desert. With any luck, they'll be tired and we can use that to our advantage.\n我们要等到夜幕降临。Orcs 在沙漠里走了一整天。运气好的话，他们会疲惫不堪，我们可以利用这一点。"

    old "This is going to be a stealth mission so be cautious and try to make as little noise as possible, understood?"
    new "This is going to be a stealth mission so be cautious and try to make as little noise as possible, understood?\n这将是一次潜入行动，所以要谨慎，尽量少发出声响，明白吗？"

    old "Stealth? That's my specialty."
    new "Stealth? That's my specialty.\n潜入？那可是我的专长。"

    old "I'm glad to have you with us, Sylrissa."
    new "I'm glad to have you with us, Sylrissa.\n很高兴有你和我们在一起，Sylrissa。"

    old "Stealth? Hmpf, I suppose I can try to be quiet."
    new "Stealth? Hmpf, I suppose I can try to be quiet.\n潜入？哼，我想我可以试试保持安静。"

    old "That means no battlecries or yells, Galan."
    new "That means no battlecries or yells, Galan.\n意思是不许喊战吼，也不许大喊大叫，Galan。"

    old "All right, all right."
    new "All right, all right.\n好了，好了。"

    old "We wait until nightfall and then start moving towards the orc camp."
    new "We wait until nightfall and then start moving towards the orc camp.\n我们等到夜幕降临，然后开始向 Orc 营地移动。"

    old "Here we are."
    new "Here we are.\n我们到了。"

    old "Any idea where the leaders might be?"
    new "Any idea where the leaders might be?\n知道首领们可能在哪里吗？"

    old "Our scouts said that they meet in a big, red tent. According to them, we won't be able to miss the smell of wine and roasted meat. They also mentioned that one of the orc leaders also likes to smoke."
    new "Our scouts said that they meet in a big, red tent. According to them, we won't be able to miss the smell of wine and roasted meat. They also mentioned that one of the orc leaders also likes to smoke.\n我们的侦察兵说，他们在一顶红色的大帐篷里碰头。据他们说，我们绝不会错过酒和烤肉的气味。他们还提到，其中一个 Orc 首领还喜欢抽烟。"

    old "That's quite a bit of information that they managed to gather. You have some good scouts, Larik."
    new "That's quite a bit of information that they managed to gather. You have some good scouts, Larik.\n他们收集到的信息可真不少。你有一些出色的侦察兵，Larik。"

    old "Ha! Not to brag, but I trained some of them myself."
    new "Ha! Not to brag, but I trained some of them myself.\n哈！不是自夸，但其中有几个是我亲手训练的。"

    old "There's the big red tent. And the smell. It's definitely that one."
    new "There's the big red tent. And the smell. It's definitely that one.\n那顶红色大帐篷在那儿。还有那气味。肯定就是它了。"

    old "There are also two guards outside. As expected."
    new "There are also two guards outside. As expected.\n外面还有两个守卫。果然如我们所料。"

    old "I can make an opening in the back of the tent with my axe if we want to try catching them by surprise."
    new "I can make an opening in the back of the tent with my axe if we want to try catching them by surprise.\n如果你们想出其不意地抓住他们，我可以用我的斧子在帐篷后面开个口子。"

    old "Got it. I think we can do this one of two ways."
    new "Got it. I think we can do this one of two ways.\n明白了。我想我们有两种做法。"

    old "One, we attack the guards and kill them quickly before they can sound the alarm. The orcs inside will probably hear us anyway though and rush outside to join the battle."
    new "One, we attack the guards and kill them quickly before they can sound the alarm. The orcs inside will probably hear us anyway though and rush outside to join the battle.\n第一种，我们攻击守卫，在他们拉响警报之前迅速解决他们。不过里面的 Orcs 多半还是会听到我们的动静，冲出来加入战斗。"

    old "Still, that should give us just enough time to kill the guards before we have to face off against the leaders."
    new "Still, that should give us just enough time to kill the guards before we have to face off against the leaders.\n但那仍应给我们留出足够的时间，赶在不得不面对首领们之前解决掉守卫。"

    old "Our second option is to cut the back of the tent open as Larik suggested: we'll have the element of surprise in our favor, but the two guards outside will probably join the battle before we can kill the orc leaders so we'll end up fighting them all at the same time."
    new "Our second option is to cut the back of the tent open as Larik suggested: we'll have the element of surprise in our favor, but the two guards outside will probably join the battle before we can kill the orc leaders so we'll end up fighting them all at the same time.\n第二个选择是像 Larik 建议的那样，把帐篷后面割开：这样我们就有了出其不意的优势，但外面的两个守卫很可能会在我们杀死 Orc 首领之前加入战斗，最终我们会同时和所有敌人作战。"

    old "In both cases, after we're done killing the leaders, we'll need to escape quickly before the rest of the camp is on to us."
    new "In both cases, after we're done killing the leaders, we'll need to escape quickly before the rest of the camp is on to us.\n无论哪种方案，我们杀完首领后，都得在营地其余的人察觉之前迅速撤离。"

    old "Which plan do you want to go with, [protag]?"
    new "Which plan do you want to go with, [protag]?\n[protag]，你想用哪个计划？"

    old "Let's take out the guards first."
    new "Let's take out the guards first.\n我们先解决守卫。"

    old "Nuala and Larik nod, agreeing to the suggested plan. We take a minute to get into position before charging in."
    new "Nuala and Larik nod, agreeing to the suggested plan. We take a minute to get into position before charging in.\nNuala 和 Larik 点点头，同意了这个计划。我们花了一分钟各就各位，然后冲了进去。"

    old "Halt! Who goes there?"
    new "Halt! Who goes there?\n站住！谁在那里？"

    old "Surprise!"
    new "Surprise!\n惊喜！"

    old "There's not much point in telling you that seeing as you're all going to be dead in a moment."
    new "There's not much point in telling you that seeing as you're all going to be dead in a moment.\n反正你们马上就要死了，跟你说这些也没什么意义。"

    old "You'll regret this!"
    new "You'll regret this!\n你会后悔的！"

    old "Die!"
    new "Die!\n去死吧！"

    old "I like Larik's idea. Let's go to the back of the tent."
    new "I like Larik's idea. Let's go to the back of the tent.\n我喜欢 Larik 的主意。我们去帐篷后面。"

    old "We silently move behind the tent. Once we're ready, I give Larik the signal. He rips the tent open with his axe and we catch the 3 orc leaders by surprise!"
    new "We silently move behind the tent. Once we're ready, I give Larik the signal. He rips the tent open with his axe and we catch the 3 orc leaders by surprise!\n我们悄悄绕到帐篷后面。准备就绪后，我向 Larik 发出信号。他用斧子撕开帐篷，我们出其不意地逮住了那三个 Orc 首领！"

    old "Guards! Guards!"
    new "Guards! Guards!\n守卫！守卫！"

    old "We did it!"
    new "We did it!\n我们成功了！"

    old "Now's not the time to celebrate. We have to get out of here before more orcs come."
    new "Now's not the time to celebrate. We have to get out of here before more orcs come.\n现在不是庆祝的时候。我们得赶在更多 Orcs 赶来之前离开这里。"

    old "We hastily run away from the camp. Without torches or other light sources, the orcs quickly lose our tracks and we're able to reach the grasslands safely."
    new "We hastily run away from the camp. Without torches or other light sources, the orcs quickly lose our tracks and we're able to reach the grasslands safely.\n我们仓促逃离营地。没有火把或其他光源，Orcs 很快失去了我们的踪迹，我们得以安全到达草原。"

    old "We're far away enough now. We should be safe here."
    new "We're far away enough now. We should be safe here.\n我们现在离得够远了。在这里应该安全。"

    old "Yes, I think so too. The mission was a success!"
    new "Yes, I think so too. The mission was a success!\n是的，我也这么想。任务成功了！"

    old "Without their leader, the orc clans will be in total chaos. Each one will need to pick a new leader and then they'll all have to agree on a plan again which should take a considerable amount of time."
    new "Without their leader, the orc clans will be in total chaos. Each one will need to pick a new leader and then they'll all have to agree on a plan again which should take a considerable amount of time.\n没了首领，那些 Orc 氏族将陷入一片混乱。每个氏族都得选出新首领，然后他们又得重新商定一个计划，这需要相当长的时间。"

    old "Will it be enough though?"
    new "Will it be enough though?\n但时间足够吗？"

    old "Ha! You have no idea how orcs choose a new leader, do you?"
    new "Ha! You have no idea how orcs choose a new leader, do you?\n哈！你完全不知道 Orcs 是怎么选新首领的，对吧？"

    old "I admit that my knowledge is a bit lacking when it comes to orc politics."
    new "I admit that my knowledge is a bit lacking when it comes to orc politics.\n我承认，谈到 Orc 政治，我的知识确实有些欠缺。"

    old "All the candidates fight each other in duels until only one remains alive. Those fights can take days."
    new "All the candidates fight each other in duels until only one remains alive. Those fights can take days.\n所有候选人互相决斗，直到只剩一个人活着。那些决斗可能要好几天。"

    old "At the very least, this should cut down on the number of tough orcs we'll need to fight if it does come down to a war."
    new "At the very least, this should cut down on the number of tough orcs we'll need to fight if it does come down to a war.\n至少，如果真的演变成战争，这应该能减少我们需要面对的强悍 Orcs 的数量。"

    old "Well, it sounds like it'll all work out then."
    new "Well, it sounds like it'll all work out then.\n嗯，听起来一切都会好起来的。"

    old "I rest up while I watch Larik and Nuala go around thanking everyone else who helped with the mission. They eventually leave one by one until only Nuala remains."
    new "I rest up while I watch Larik and Nuala go around thanking everyone else who helped with the mission. They eventually leave one by one until only Nuala remains.\n我休息时，看着 Larik 和 Nuala 四处走动，感谢所有为任务出力的人。他们最终一个接一个地离开，直到只剩下 Nuala。"

    old "She then makes her way over to me."
    new "She then makes her way over to me.\n然后她朝我走了过来。"

    old "Nuala, you seem more relaxed now."
    new "Nuala, you seem more relaxed now.\nNuala，你现在看起来放松多了。"

    old "Yes, my tribe and the other nomad tribes in the area are safe and it's all thanks to us. I am really happy."
    new "Yes, my tribe and the other nomad tribes in the area are safe and it's all thanks to us. I am really happy.\n是的，我的部族和这一带的其他游牧部族都安全了，这全都归功于我们。我真的很开心。"

    old "She beams, showing me a big smile."
    new "She beams, showing me a big smile.\n她笑逐颜开，朝我露出一个大大的笑容。"

    old "You're even more beautiful when you smile, Nuala. You should do it more often."
    new "You're even more beautiful when you smile, Nuala. You should do it more often.\n你笑起来更美了，Nuala。你应该多笑笑。"

    old "What? The fierce Nuala is blushing?"
    new "What? The fierce Nuala is blushing?\n什么？凶猛的 Nuala 脸红了？"

    old "Nuala playfully punches my arm, laughing. Still, despite her casual response, I can still tell that she's embarrassed by my words."
    new "Nuala playfully punches my arm, laughing. Still, despite her casual response, I can still tell that she's embarrassed by my words.\nNuala 笑着轻轻捶了一下我的手臂。不过，尽管她回应得漫不经心，我仍能看出她被我的话弄得有些不好意思。"

    old "Shut up, you!"
    new "Shut up, you!\n闭嘴，你！"

    old "I need to go back to my people now. I'm sure you have other things to get to as well."
    new "I need to go back to my people now. I'm sure you have other things to get to as well.\n我现在得回到我的人民身边了。我相信你也有别的事要忙。"

    old "I hope to see you again soon."
    new "I hope to see you again soon.\n希望很快能再见到你。"

    old "You will, Nuala."
    new "You will, Nuala.\n你会的，Nuala。"

    old "The battle lost, we break away and start running from the orc camp as fast as we can. We have to rely on several of our party member's skills to make it out, but eventually they give up and we're able to reach the grasslands."
    new "The battle lost, we break away and start running from the orc camp as fast as we can. We have to rely on several of our party member's skills to make it out, but eventually they give up and we're able to reach the grasslands.\n战斗失利，我们脱离战局，尽可能快地逃离 Orc 营地。我们只能依靠几位同伴的本领才得以脱身，但最终他们放弃了追赶，我们得以到达草原。"

    old "Is everyone okay?"
    new "Is everyone okay?\n大家都还好吗？"

    old "Yes? I think so. That was too close."
    new "Yes? I think so. That was too close.\n是的？我想是的。刚才太险了。"

    old "I'm sorry. This was a terrible idea."
    new "I'm sorry. This was a terrible idea.\n对不起。这是个糟糕的主意。"

    old "Don't say that. At least you tried."
    new "Don't say that. At least you tried.\n别这么说。至少你试过了。"

    old "Nuala, come. We need to get back to our camp. The orcs will be even angrier now. A war is probably imminent."
    new "Nuala, come. We need to get back to our camp. The orcs will be even angrier now. A war is probably imminent.\nNuala，过来。我们得回营地了。Orcs 现在会更愤怒。战争恐怕一触即发。"

    old "What happens now?"
    new "What happens now?\n现在会发生什么？"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. Your mission comes first."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. Your mission comes first.\n别担心，[protag]。你的使命优先。"

    old "But... your people!"
    new "But... your people!\n但是……你们的人民！"

    old "We've made an alliance with all of the other desert tribes, remember? The orcs are many, but so we are. I will train new recruits and Nuala will tend to the injured. We don't need to be physically involved in the war."
    new "We've made an alliance with all of the other desert tribes, remember? The orcs are many, but so we are. I will train new recruits and Nuala will tend to the injured. We don't need to be physically involved in the war.\n我们已经和所有其他沙漠部族结盟了，记得吗？Orcs 人多，但我们人也不少。我会训练新兵，Nuala 会照顾伤员。我们不必亲自上阵。"

    old "We'll still take care of our people, [protag], just in a different way."
    new "We'll still take care of our people, [protag], just in a different way.\n我们仍会照顾我们的人民，[protag]，只是换一种方式。"

    old "Good, that makes me feel a little better."
    new "Good, that makes me feel a little better.\n好，这让我感觉好多了。"

    old "Larik and Nuala leave. Then, the rest of the group and I make our way safely back to Grimoire."
    new "Larik and Nuala leave. Then, the rest of the group and I make our way safely back to Grimoire.\nLarik 和 Nuala 离开了。然后，我和队伍里其余的人安全地返回了 Grimoire。"

    old "You're walking with a sense of purpose. Stalking that rhino again?"
    new "You're walking with a sense of purpose. Stalking that rhino again?\n你走起路来目标明确。又去跟踪那头犀牛？"

    old "Yes. You're welcome to come along. Once more rhinos begin arriving, it will be more difficult to pick out Rue—and more dangerous when I confront her."
    new "Yes. You're welcome to come along. Once more rhinos begin arriving, it will be more difficult to pick out Rue—and more dangerous when I confront her.\n是的。欢迎你一起来。一旦更多犀牛开始到来，想挑出 Rue 就更难了——而当我面对她时，也会更危险。"

    old "Can I ask what's so special about Rue?"
    new "Can I ask what's so special about Rue?\n我能问问 Rue 有什么特别之处吗？"

    old "We have a history together. The first time I met her, I was a young girl. I was traveling with several warriors from my tribe."
    new "We have a history together. The first time I met her, I was a young girl. I was traveling with several warriors from my tribe.\n我们之间有一段渊源。我第一次见到她时，还是个小女孩。当时我正和部族里的几名战士一起赶路。"

    old "Is it common for the Dunemarchers to venture into the savannah? I thought you were, well, Dunemarchers."
    new "Is it common for the Dunemarchers to venture into the savannah? I thought you were, well, Dunemarchers.\nDunemarchers 深入草原很常见吗？我还以为你们，嗯，是 Dunemarchers。"

    old "We are sometimes forced to hunt outside the sands due to scarcity of food."
    new "We are sometimes forced to hunt outside the sands due to scarcity of food.\n由于食物匮乏，我们有时被迫到沙地之外打猎。"

    old "Is that still a problem?"
    new "Is that still a problem?\n现在这还是个问题吗？"

    old "No. In the past thirty years, we have only had one season so bad that we had to hunt outside of the sands. And that season was the season that I met Rue."
    new "No. In the past thirty years, we have only had one season so bad that we had to hunt outside of the sands. And that season was the season that I met Rue.\n不是了。在过去三十年里，我们只有一个季节糟到不得不到沙地之外打猎。而那个季节，正是我遇见 Rue 的季节。"

    old "I imagine that you two didn't exactly get off on the right foot."
    new "I imagine that you two didn't exactly get off on the right foot.\n我想你们俩当初的相遇恐怕并不愉快。"

    old "She nearly killed the two warriors I was traveling with. They were left with broken bones, and I was so young that my healing magic was not enough to repair them. So I did the best I could."
    new "She nearly killed the two warriors I was traveling with. They were left with broken bones, and I was so young that my healing magic was not enough to repair them. So I did the best I could.\n她差点杀死了与我同行的两名战士。他们被撞断了骨头，而我那时还太年轻，我的治愈魔法不足以修复他们。所以我尽了全力。"

    old "For three days and three nights, I stood vigil over my tribesmen. I didn't sleep. By night, I hunted for small animals to find as a source of food to keep them fed and to keep up my own energy for healing."
    new "For three days and three nights, I stood vigil over my tribesmen. I didn't sleep. By night, I hunted for small animals to find as a source of food to keep them fed and to keep up my own energy for healing.\n三天三夜，我一直守在我的族人身边。我没有合眼。夜里，我猎捕小动物，作为食物来源，让他们不至于挨饿，也维持我自己的治愈能量。"

    old "By day, I practiced what little healing magic I knew to keep them their blood flowing and keep them breathing. My strength had nearly given out by the time another group of Dunemarchers arrived to rescue us."
    new "By day, I practiced what little healing magic I knew to keep them their blood flowing and keep them breathing. My strength had nearly given out by the time another group of Dunemarchers arrived to rescue us.\n白天，我练习我所会的那点治愈魔法，让他们的血液继续流动，呼吸得以维持。等到另一群 Dunemarchers 赶来营救我们时，我的力气几乎已经耗尽了。"

    old "It's amazing that you were able to do that as a young girl. It must have taken immense courage on your part."
    new "It's amazing that you were able to do that as a young girl. It must have taken immense courage on your part.\n你那么小就能做到这些，真了不起。那一定需要极大的勇气。"

    old "Courage? Maybe. At the time, I wasn't fixated on such things. I was more concerned with simple survival, and keeping my clansmen alive."
    new "Courage? Maybe. At the time, I wasn't fixated on such things. I was more concerned with simple survival, and keeping my clansmen alive.\n勇气？也许吧。当时，我并没有执着于这些东西。我更关心的是单纯的生存，以及保住我族人的性命。"

    old "That experience was also the start of a new personal journey for me."
    new "That experience was also the start of a new personal journey for me.\n那段经历也是我个人一段新旅程的开始。"

    old "It's awful that you had to go through that as a young girl."
    new "It's awful that you had to go through that as a young girl.\n你那么小就得经历那些，真让人难受。"

    old "It was a harrowing experience. But I wouldn't be the woman I am today if it weren't for those trials."
    new "It was a harrowing experience. But I wouldn't be the woman I am today if it weren't for those trials.\n那是段折磨人的经历。但如果没有那些磨难，我也不会成为今天的我。"

    old "If my healing had been stronger, I could have healed them enough so that they could walk. But because my powers were weak, I was forced to fight a battle of survival for three days."
    new "If my healing had been stronger, I could have healed them enough so that they could walk. But because my powers were weak, I was forced to fight a battle of survival for three days.\n如果我的治愈力再强一些，我就能把他们治好，让他们能行走。但正因为我的力量太弱，我才被迫打了一场为期三天的生存之战。"

    old "After I got back to the desert, I resolved to become a stronger, more capable healer. That I would do a better job of keeping my people safe."
    new "After I got back to the desert, I resolved to become a stronger, more capable healer. That I would do a better job of keeping my people safe.\n回到沙漠后，我决心成为一个更强大、更有能力的医者。我要更好地保护我的人民。"

    old "Since meeting you, I've never doubted your resolve. I didn't realize that your resolve was born out of such trying circumstances."
    new "Since meeting you, I've never doubted your resolve. I didn't realize that your resolve was born out of such trying circumstances.\n自从认识你以来，我从未怀疑过你的决心。我不知道的是，你的决心竟诞生于如此艰难的环境。"

    old "That experience also awakened something else in me."
    new "That experience also awakened something else in me.\n那段经历也唤醒了我内心的另一些东西。"

    old "What did it awaken i you?"
    new "What did it awaken i you?\n它唤醒了你什么？"

    old "Nuala gazes across the grassland wistfully."
    new "Nuala gazes across the grassland wistfully.\nNuala 若有所思地凝望着草原。"

    old "This rhino hunt is a bit like the end of a journey that began when I was a young child. Every story must have its beginning, and every story must also have its end."
    new "This rhino hunt is a bit like the end of a journey that began when I was a young child. Every story must have its beginning, and every story must also have its end.\n这场犀牛狩猎，有点像一段始于我幼年时的旅程的终结。每个故事都得有开端，每个故事也必然要有结尾。"

    old "When I was young, I allowed the rhino to best me. Now, if I have become the Dunemarcher that I was meant to be, I should be able to best the rhino. That is why I am here."
    new "When I was young, I allowed the rhino to best me. Now, if I have become the Dunemarcher that I was meant to be, I should be able to best the rhino. That is why I am here.\n我年幼时，任由那头犀牛胜过了我。如今，若我已成长为我本该成为的那个 Dunemarcher，我就应该能胜过那头犀牛。这就是我来这里的原因。"

    old "But it is a bittersweet end to the story. Because, although Rue was the cause of a terrifying experience in my youth, I would not be the Dunemarcher I am on this day without that incident. So, although she acted against me in malice, Rue gave me a gift on that day. And yet I must return that gift with malice."
    new "But it is a bittersweet end to the story. Because, although Rue was the cause of a terrifying experience in my youth, I would not be the Dunemarcher I am on this day without that incident. So, although she acted against me in malice, Rue gave me a gift on that day. And yet I must return that gift with malice.\n但这是故事的一个苦乐参半的结局。因为，尽管 Rue 是我年少时那段可怕经历的原因，但若没有那次事件，我也不会成为今日的我。所以，尽管她当年出于恶意伤害我，Rue 在那一天却给了我一份礼物。而我却必须以恶意来回报这份礼物。"

    old "You're certain of that?"
    new "You're certain of that?\n你确定要这样？"

    old "How else could things be?"
    new "How else could things be?\n事情还能怎么样呢？"

    old "Nuala seems troubled. I wonder, did she take me out here hoping that I would talk her out of something? Or is she hoping for me to strengthen her resolve to carry out with a difficult decision?"
    new "Nuala seems troubled. I wonder, did she take me out here hoping that I would talk her out of something? Or is she hoping for me to strengthen her resolve to carry out with a difficult decision?\nNuala 显得心神不宁。我在想，她带我来这里，是希望我劝她放弃某件事吗？还是希望我坚定她的决心，去做一个艰难的决定？"

    old "Nuala, you came out here for a reason. You've told me why you've stalked Rue all of these years. But why are you here today? Tell me, right here and in this moment, what are you here to do?"
    new "Nuala, you came out here for a reason. You've told me why you've stalked Rue all of these years. But why are you here today? Tell me, right here and in this moment, what are you here to do?\nNuala，你来到这里是有原因的。你告诉过我，为什么这么多年你一直追踪 Rue。但你今天为什么在这里？告诉我，就在此刻此地，你来这里是要做什么？"

    old "I am here to fulfill my destiny. I'm here to serve my purpose as part of nature."
    new "I am here to fulfill my destiny. I'm here to serve my purpose as part of nature.\n我来这里完成我的命运。我来这里履行我作为自然一部分的使命。"

    old "In a way, I am not so different from these animals. Does a mother jackal truly have any choice in whether she cares for her offspring? Or is it an instinct, something inescapable that she's destined for? Does the lion have any choice in whether it attacks a gazelle? Do I have any choice in whether I pursue Rue and slay her?"
    new "In a way, I am not so different from these animals. Does a mother jackal truly have any choice in whether she cares for her offspring? Or is it an instinct, something inescapable that she's destined for? Does the lion have any choice in whether it attacks a gazelle? Do I have any choice in whether I pursue Rue and slay her?\n从某种意义上说，我和这些动物并没有那么不同。母胡狼是否照顾幼崽，她真的有的选吗？还是说，那是一种本能，是她注定要背负的、无法逃避的东西？狮子是否攻击瞪羚，它有的选吗？我是否追捕 Rue 并杀死她，我有的选吗？"

    old "Nuala smiles and shakes her head, as if it's a question she's contemplated many times before."
    new "Nuala smiles and shakes her head, as if it's a question she's contemplated many times before.\nNuala 微笑着摇了摇头，仿佛这是个她已反复思量过多次的问题。"

    old "It's an old question. Do we really have the power of choice, or are we simply carrying out the actions that are in our nature?"
    new "It's an old question. Do we really have the power of choice, or are we simply carrying out the actions that are in our nature?\n这是个老问题。我们真的拥有选择的能力，还是我们只是在执行天性使然的行动？"

    old "You look like you have the answer to it."
    new "You look like you have the answer to it.\n你看起来已经有了答案。"

    old "Are you asking me to give you the answer to the biggest question in your life?"
    new "Are you asking me to give you the answer to the biggest question in your life?\n你是要我回答你生命中最大的那个问题吗？"

    old "You are right, that is a big question. I think I will ask you a smaller question instead."
    new "You are right, that is a big question. I think I will ask you a smaller question instead.\n你说得对，那是个大问题。我想我还是问你一个小一点的问题吧。"

    old "When you came to the desert and we met the first time, what brought you here? Did you come to visit me of your own volition?"
    new "When you came to the desert and we met the first time, what brought you here? Did you come to visit me of your own volition?\n你当初来到沙漠，我们第一次相遇时，是什么把你带到这里？你是出于自己的意愿来看我的吗？"

    old "I think destiny brought me here."
    new "I think destiny brought me here.\n我想是命运把我带到了这里。"

    old "Destiny, hmm? That must be a humbling way to look at it."
    new "Destiny, hmm? That must be a humbling way to look at it.\n命运，嗯？这样看问题，一定让人谦卑。"

    old "Humbling in what sense?"
    new "Humbling in what sense?\n何以谦卑？"

    old "You can't claim credit for any of your achievements. You only carried those things out because you were destined to do so."
    new "You can't claim credit for any of your achievements. You only carried those things out because you were destined to do so.\n你的任何成就都无法归功于自己。你之所以做成那些事，仅仅是因为你注定要那么做。"

    old "You don't like that?"
    new "You don't like that?\n你不喜欢这样？"

    old "It is difficult to say. It makes me feel small. And most people do not like being made to feel small. But in a way, there is something comforting about it. It makes me feel as though I am merely carrying out a role in a larger world."
    new "It is difficult to say. It makes me feel small. And most people do not like being made to feel small. But in a way, there is something comforting about it. It makes me feel as though I am merely carrying out a role in a larger world.\n很难说。这让我觉得自己很渺小。而大多数人都不喜欢被弄得渺小。但从某方面说，这又有些令人宽慰。它让我觉得，自己不过是在一个更大的世界里扮演一个角色。"

    old "As though I'm but a part of nature, no different from the animals I hunt, or even the wind that sculpts the sand dunes."
    new "As though I'm but a part of nature, no different from the animals I hunt, or even the wind that sculpts the sand dunes.\n仿佛我不过是自然的一部分，与我所猎取的动物，甚至与雕琢沙丘的风，并无不同。"

    old "It is an interesting idea to think about. But the more I think about it, the more it seems like whatever I'm destined to face with Rue, that is a destiny that belongs solely to me. A confrontation with Rue is not part of your destiny."
    new "It is an interesting idea to think about. But the more I think about it, the more it seems like whatever I'm destined to face with Rue, that is a destiny that belongs solely to me. A confrontation with Rue is not part of your destiny.\n这是个有趣的想法。但我越想，越觉得无论我注定要和 Rue 面对什么，那都只是属于我一个人的命运。与 Rue 的对峙，并不是你命运的一部分。"

    old "Are you telling me to leave?"
    new "Are you telling me to leave?\n你是在叫我离开吗？"

    old "I think it would be best for me to confront this alone."
    new "I think it would be best for me to confront this alone.\n我想，最好还是让我独自面对这件事。"

    old "Very well, Nuala. I'll respect your wishes. I hope you live to tell me about it."
    new "Very well, Nuala. I'll respect your wishes. I hope you live to tell me about it.\n很好，Nuala。我尊重你的意愿。希望你能活着回来讲给我听。"

    old "I chose to do it. I made that decision."
    new "I chose to do it. I made that decision.\n我选择这么做。那个决定是我自己做的。"

    old "When we first met, you told me you were here in the service of a larger mission. Some authority concerned with N'Mar sent you here."
    new "When we first met, you told me you were here in the service of a larger mission. Some authority concerned with N'Mar sent you here.\n我们初次见面时，你告诉我，你是为一个更大的使命而来。某个与 N'Mar 有关的权威派你来的。"

    old "It's true, I did come here in the service of that mission. But just because I am told what to do does not mean that I am obligated to do it."
    new "It's true, I did come here in the service of that mission. But just because I am told what to do does not mean that I am obligated to do it.\n确实，我是为那个使命而来。但别人告诉我该做什么，并不意味着我就有义务去做。"

    old "But what is it in you that drives you to behave in that way, even when you are not told by other people to do it? Is there some will inside of you that drives those decisions? Or is it simply in your nature?"
    new "But what is it in you that drives you to behave in that way, even when you are not told by other people to do it? Is there some will inside of you that drives those decisions? Or is it simply in your nature?\n但你内心是什么在驱使你那样行事，即便没有别人命令你？你体内是否有什么意志在驱动那些决定？还是那仅仅出于你的本性？"

    old "Everything in life is about making choices. It's the reason that sitting inside of a prison cell is considered a worse fate than sitting on a street corner. When you have four solid walls around you, your choices are much more limited."
    new "Everything in life is about making choices. It's the reason that sitting inside of a prison cell is considered a worse fate than sitting on a street corner. When you have four solid walls around you, your choices are much more limited.\n生活中的一切都在于做出选择。正因如此，坐在牢房里才被认为是比坐在街角更糟的命运。当四堵坚实的墙围着你时，你的选择就受限得多。"

    old "Many people would prefer to live outside the walls of a prison and risk starvation or being attacked by wild beasts rather than be well-fed and kept in captivity."
    new "Many people would prefer to live outside the walls of a prison and risk starvation or being attacked by wild beasts rather than be well-fed and kept in captivity.\n许多人宁愿住在监狱的高墙之外，冒着挨饿或被野兽袭击的危险，也不愿被养得饱饱的、关在笼子里。"

    old "So you make choices that lead you to more choices."
    new "So you make choices that lead you to more choices.\n所以你做出选择，而这些选择又带你走向更多选择。"

    old "Yes. That is the way of things, Nuala. I'm sorry I don't have a more eloquent way to put it."
    new "Yes. That is the way of things, Nuala. I'm sorry I don't have a more eloquent way to put it.\n是的。事情就是这样，Nuala。抱歉，我没有更雄辩的说法了。"

    old "That is an interesting thought. And it's something that I think I should take more time to think about, at least before I rush in to face Rue."
    new "That is an interesting thought. And it's something that I think I should take more time to think about, at least before I rush in to face Rue.\n这是个有趣的想法。我想我应该多花些时间去思考，至少在我冲去面对 Rue 之前。"

    old "Nuala turns back and begins walking toward the dunes again."
    new "Nuala turns back and begins walking toward the dunes again.\nNuala 转过身，又开始朝沙丘走去。"

    old "This is a decision to be made on another day. But I'll make a decision by the next time we talk."
    new "This is a decision to be made on another day. But I'll make a decision by the next time we talk.\n这个决定改天再做吧。不过，等我们下次谈话时，我会做出决定的。"

    old "Alright. I look forward to hearing about it."
    new "Alright. I look forward to hearing about it.\n好的。我期待听到结果。"

    old "[protag]. One more thing."
    new "[protag]. One more thing.\n[protag]。还有一件事。"

    old "I've spent a lot of time showing you the desert where I live. You've met the Dunemarchers. You've met my people. The next time we meet, I'd like to explore the cities of the empire. I want to see the land you're fighting to protect."
    new "I've spent a lot of time showing you the desert where I live. You've met the Dunemarchers. You've met my people. The next time we meet, I'd like to explore the cities of the empire. I want to see the land you're fighting to protect.\n我花了很多时间，带你看了我生活的沙漠。你见过 Dunemarchers，也见过我的人民。下次见面时，我想去探索帝国的城市。我想看看你为之战斗的这片土地。"

    old "I was beginning to think you'd never ask. I'd be glad to show you around, Nuala."
    new "I was beginning to think you'd never ask. I'd be glad to show you around, Nuala.\n我正开始想，你大概永远不会开口了。我很乐意带你四处看看，Nuala。"

    old "On the way to Grimoire, I notice a familiar-looking woman on her way to the city gate."
    new "On the way to Grimoire, I notice a familiar-looking woman on her way to the city gate.\n在去 Grimoire 的路上，我注意到一个长相眼熟的女人正朝城门走去。"

    old "Nuala. It's good to see you."
    new "Nuala. It's good to see you.\nNuala。很高兴见到你。"

    old "It's good to see you too. Though, I must admit I'm a bit more preoccupied with the surroundings. The world outside the desert is quite...large."
    new "It's good to see you too. Though, I must admit I'm a bit more preoccupied with the surroundings. The world outside the desert is quite...large.\n我也很高兴见到你。不过，我得承认，我的心思更多放在了周围的环境上。沙漠之外的世界相当……大。"

    old "You've only seen a tiny portion of what this world has to offer, Nuala. There's even more to see outside the reaches of the human empire."
    new "You've only seen a tiny portion of what this world has to offer, Nuala. There's even more to see outside the reaches of the human empire.\n你只看到了这个世界能呈现的一小部分，Nuala。人类帝国疆域之外，还有更多可看的。"

    old "You have the entirety of this immense city at your fingertips, and yet you still thirst for greater sights. I like that about you, [protag]. You and I come from such different places, yet we seem to have the same desire to wander. My wanderlust led me to the edges of the desert, and yours led you to the edges of the earth."
    new "You have the entirety of this immense city at your fingertips, and yet you still thirst for greater sights. I like that about you, [protag]. You and I come from such different places, yet we seem to have the same desire to wander. My wanderlust led me to the edges of the desert, and yours led you to the edges of the earth.\n这整座宏伟的城市都尽在你的指掌之间，而你却仍渴望着更壮阔的景致。我喜欢你这一点，[protag]。你和我来自如此不同的地方，我们却似乎有着同样的流浪之欲。我的漫游之心把我带到了沙漠边缘，而你的把你带到了大地的尽头。"

    old "We enter through the city gates, and Nuala watches the movement on the city streets with fascination and amusement."
    new "We enter through the city gates, and Nuala watches the movement on the city streets with fascination and amusement.\n我们穿过城门，Nuala 满怀好奇与愉悦地看着街道上的车水马龙。"

    old "The people here walk so quickly. There are no beasts chasing them, and yet they move with such fervor. It is something I do not see often."
    new "The people here walk so quickly. There are no beasts chasing them, and yet they move with such fervor. It is something I do not see often.\n这里的人走得真快。没有野兽在追他们，他们却如此行色匆匆。这是我不常看到的情景。"

    old "Dunemarchers don't move with a sense of urgency?"
    new "Dunemarchers don't move with a sense of urgency?\nDunemarchers 做事不匆忙吗？"

    old "Dunemarchers are methodical in all things. In the sand dunes, the impulse to run will often cause you to move in a way that causes your feet to sink into the sand. So even when Dunemarchers are in a hurry, they place their footfalls carefully."
    new "Dunemarchers are methodical in all things. In the sand dunes, the impulse to run will often cause you to move in a way that causes your feet to sink into the sand. So even when Dunemarchers are in a hurry, they place their footfalls carefully.\nDunemarchers 凡事都有条不紊。在沙丘里，奔跑的冲动往往会让你走起来脚陷沙中。所以即便 Dunemarchers 赶时间，他们也会谨慎地落步。"

    old "And in the moments when we are not moving about the sands, we are similarly methodical. When it comes to activities like skinning and animal, or cooking meat, or enjoying the company of our fellow Dunemarchers, we try to experience every moment fully. We do not draw it out longer than necessary, but neither do we rush for it to be over."
    new "And in the moments when we are not moving about the sands, we are similarly methodical. When it comes to activities like skinning and animal, or cooking meat, or enjoying the company of our fellow Dunemarchers, we try to experience every moment fully. We do not draw it out longer than necessary, but neither do we rush for it to be over.\n而不在沙地上行走的时候，我们也同样有条不紊。无论是给动物剥皮、烹饪肉食，还是与 Dunemarchers 同伴相聚，我们都尽量充分体验每一刻。我们不会拖得太久，但也不会急着让它结束。"

    old "A man carrying a bucket rushes down the street, and bits of milk slosh from the bucket into the street as he moves."
    new "A man carrying a bucket rushes down the street, and bits of milk slosh from the bucket into the street as he moves.\n一个拎着桶的男人冲过街道，他走动时，桶里的牛奶溅到了街上。"

    old "Such haste! That man wants nothing more than for his journey to be over. Why is it that he cannot enjoy walking? Especially when the streets are so full of activity. I think I could stand here and watch people all day and not become bored."
    new "Such haste! That man wants nothing more than for his journey to be over. Why is it that he cannot enjoy walking? Especially when the streets are so full of activity. I think I could stand here and watch people all day and not become bored.\n真匆忙啊！那个人只想让他的路程快点结束。他为什么不能享受走路呢？尤其是街上还这么热闹。我想我可以站在这里看人看上一整天也不会腻。"

    old "I'm not sure I was expecting you to react to the city like this, Nuala."
    new "I'm not sure I was expecting you to react to the city like this, Nuala.\n我不确定我是否料到你会对这座城市有这种反应，Nuala。"

    old "I've learned to sit still and watch. That's what creatures of the desert do, [protag]. Oftentimes, jackals are most terrifying when they are simply watching you, waiting for a moment when they think they can attack."
    new "I've learned to sit still and watch. That's what creatures of the desert do, [protag]. Oftentimes, jackals are most terrifying when they are simply watching you, waiting for a moment when they think they can attack.\n我学会了静静地坐着观察。这就是沙漠生物的做法，[protag]。很多时候，胡狼只是在注视着你、等待它们认为可以发动攻击的那一刻时，才最令人胆寒。"

    old "Of course, I'm not about to attack anyone. But when I stand here, I feel a stirring. Perhaps the urgency of these people, all hurrying and scurrying, is contagious. I do think that this is a place that I could enjoy."
    new "Of course, I'm not about to attack anyone. But when I stand here, I feel a stirring. Perhaps the urgency of these people, all hurrying and scurrying, is contagious. I do think that this is a place that I could enjoy.\n当然，我不打算攻击任何人。但当我站在这里时，我感到一种悸动。也许这些人行色匆匆、奔忙不息的紧迫感是会传染的。我确实觉得，这会是个我能喜欢上的地方。"

    old "I begin walking through the streets with Nuala."
    new "I begin walking through the streets with Nuala.\n我开始和 Nuala 一起穿过街道。"

    old "Nuala, the last time we met, you said you were about to make a decision. What ever became of Rue?"
    new "Nuala, the last time we met, you said you were about to make a decision. What ever became of Rue?\nNuala，我们上次见面时，你说你就要做出一个决定。Rue 后来怎么样了？"

    old "Rue and I had a meeting with destiny."
    new "Rue and I had a meeting with destiny.\nRue 和我与命运有约。"

    old "Rue's destiny has been fulfilled. She carried out all that she had to do in this world, and met her end."
    new "Rue's destiny has been fulfilled. She carried out all that she had to do in this world, and met her end.\nRue 的命运已经完成。她履行了她在这个世界上必须做的一切，然后走到了生命的尽头。"

    old "You killed her? I think I would have liked to see that."
    new "You killed her? I think I would have liked to see that.\n你杀了她？我想我会很想看到那一幕。"

    old "I don't think you would have. It was a very slow process."
    new "I don't think you would have. It was a very slow process.\n我想你不会喜欢的。那是个非常缓慢的过程。"

    old "How long did it take?"
    new "How long did it take?\n花了多长时间？"

    old "Rue has been dying for years. She was an old beast, [protag]. Beasts of that age often succumb to disease. In the end, I did not slay Rue with knife or club. I merely outlasted her."
    new "Rue has been dying for years. She was an old beast, [protag]. Beasts of that age often succumb to disease. In the end, I did not slay Rue with knife or club. I merely outlasted her.\nRue 已经濒死多年了。她是头年迈的野兽，[protag]。那个年纪的野兽常常死于疾病。到最后，我并没有用刀或棍棒杀死 Rue。我只是熬过了她。"

    old "You watched her until she died of old age?"
    new "You watched her until she died of old age?\n你看着她，直到她老死？"

    old "Well, I did hasten the process. My magic has the power to worsen disease as well as cure it. I decided to increase the diseases that already ailed her, and a death that might have lasted for several years ended in only several days."
    new "Well, I did hasten the process. My magic has the power to worsen disease as well as cure it. I decided to increase the diseases that already ailed her, and a death that might have lasted for several years ended in only several days.\n嗯，我确实加快了这一过程。我的魔法既能治愈疾病，也能让疾病恶化。我决定加重已经困扰她的那些疾病，于是本可能拖上数年的死亡，只在短短几天内就结束了。"

    old "So, you killed her, but indirectly."
    new "So, you killed her, but indirectly.\n所以，你杀了她，但是间接的。"

    old "It was Rue's destiny to live out her days and live a fruitful before succumbing to the diseases of old age. She fulfilled that destiny. And my destiny was to inflict death on Rue. I also fulfilled mine. In a way, we both got to live the best versions of our lives."
    new "It was Rue's destiny to live out her days and live a fruitful before succumbing to the diseases of old age. She fulfilled that destiny. And my destiny was to inflict death on Rue. I also fulfilled mine. In a way, we both got to live the best versions of our lives.\nRue 的命运是过完她的日子，在向老年的疾病屈服之前活得丰足。她完成了那个命运。而我的命运是给 Rue 带去死亡。我也完成了我的。从某种意义上说，我们俩都活出了自己最好的人生。"

    old "I didn't expect you to solve the problem this way, Nuala. That's impressive."
    new "I didn't expect you to solve the problem this way, Nuala. That's impressive.\n我没想到你会用这种方式解决问题，Nuala。真让人印象深刻。"

    old "I decided to leave Rue behind."
    new "I decided to leave Rue behind.\n我决定放过 Rue。"

    old "You've had a change of heart?"
    new "You've had a change of heart?\n你回心转意了？"

    old "No, my heart is still in the same place. I think my desire was always to leave Rue be. But a sense of obligation always haunted me. Rather than listen to that voice, I decided to follow my heart."
    new "No, my heart is still in the same place. I think my desire was always to leave Rue be. But a sense of obligation always haunted me. Rather than listen to that voice, I decided to follow my heart.\n不，我的心仍在原处。我想，我一直以来的愿望都是放过 Rue。但一种义务感始终缠绕着我。这一次，我没有听从那个声音，而是决定跟随我的心。"

    old "Rue is an old animal, [protag]. An animal of that age is not long for this world. She will be dead in several years, whether I'm there or not. And I think I can leave well enough alone until then. I've already waited this long."
    new "Rue is an old animal, [protag]. An animal of that age is not long for this world. She will be dead in several years, whether I'm there or not. And I think I can leave well enough alone until then. I've already waited this long.\nRue 是头年迈的动物，[protag]。那个年纪的动物在这世上活不长了。无论我在不在场，她几年之内都会死去。我想，在那之前我可以就此放手。我已经等了这么久。"

    old "You're simply going to let this go? What about the grudge?"
    new "You're simply going to let this go? What about the grudge?\n你就这样放下了？那仇怨怎么办？"

    old "A grudge is a choice to hold onto anger and resentment. Perhaps Rue still harbors a grudge. But there's no reason for me to do the same. It may seem sudden to do this, but the truth is that letting it go is an easier, more passive thing to do."
    new "A grudge is a choice to hold onto anger and resentment. Perhaps Rue still harbors a grudge. But there's no reason for me to do the same. It may seem sudden to do this, but the truth is that letting it go is an easier, more passive thing to do.\n仇恨是一种选择，是抓住愤怒与怨恨不放。也许 Rue 仍心怀怨恨。但我没有理由也那样做。这样做也许显得突然，但事实是，放下它是一件更容易、更被动的事。"

    old "I won't forget what happened, but looking back, Rue was only doing what any wild beast would do. She was looking out for herself and her own. And now it's time for me to do the same, instead of lusting for vengeance."
    new "I won't forget what happened, but looking back, Rue was only doing what any wild beast would do. She was looking out for herself and her own. And now it's time for me to do the same, instead of lusting for vengeance.\n我不会忘记发生的事，但回首往事，Rue 只是在做任何野兽都会做的事。她在为自己和她的同类着想。现在，该轮到我做同样的事了，而不是渴求复仇。"

    old "I spend the rest of the afternoon with Nuala, touring Grimoire as she observes the city with curiosity and fascination."
    new "I spend the rest of the afternoon with Nuala, touring Grimoire as she observes the city with curiosity and fascination.\n下午剩下的时间，我都和 Nuala 在一起，带她游览 Grimoire，她则满怀好奇与迷恋地观察着这座城市。"

    old "I stop and purchase a loaf of sweet bread from a local vendor, and Nuala grins as she bites into it."
    new "I stop and purchase a loaf of sweet bread from a local vendor, and Nuala grins as she bites into it.\n我停下来，从当地小贩那里买了一条甜面包，Nuala 咬了一口，咧嘴笑了。"

    old "This is what I came here for."
    new "This is what I came here for.\n这就是我来这里的目的。"

    old "You came to this city just to taste bread?"
    new "You came to this city just to taste bread?\n你来这座城市，只是为了尝尝面包？"

    old "The taste is enjoyable. But more than the taste, I think I understand the people of this city better. This city is hectic, and yet at the same time, there is a certain comfort to it."
    new "The taste is enjoyable. But more than the taste, I think I understand the people of this city better. This city is hectic, and yet at the same time, there is a certain comfort to it.\n味道很好。但比起味道，我想我更理解这座城市的人了。这座城市忙乱喧嚣，但同时又有着某种令人安心的东西。"

    old "Just wait until you see an actual bed."
    new "Just wait until you see an actual bed.\n等你见到真正的床，再说吧。"

    old "A young child bumps into Nuala. He looks up at her with a shocked expression, and she smiles at him for a moment before growling at the boy. The growl is enough to scare the boy off, and Nuala laughs as the boy scampers away."
    new "A young child bumps into Nuala. He looks up at her with a shocked expression, and she smiles at him for a moment before growling at the boy. The growl is enough to scare the boy off, and Nuala laughs as the boy scampers away.\n一个年幼的孩子撞到了 Nuala。他抬头看着她，一脸惊愕，而她对他微笑了一瞬，随后冲男孩低吼了一声。那声低吼足以把男孩吓跑，Nuala 看着他连滚带爬地逃开，笑了起来。"

    old "People here live differently."
    new "People here live differently.\n这里的人生活的方式不一样。"

    old "You mean the way everyone is always hurrying to whatever their next engagement is?"
    new "You mean the way everyone is always hurrying to whatever their next engagement is?\n你是说每个人总在急匆匆赶赴下一场约定？"

    old "That's just part of it. Even though they're hurrying as though they're being chased by something, there is something oddly docile about them. So many of them walk with their heads down, as if they're not ready to be challenged by anything unexpected."
    new "That's just part of it. Even though they're hurrying as though they're being chased by something, there is something oddly docile about them. So many of them walk with their heads down, as if they're not ready to be challenged by anything unexpected.\n那只是其中一部分。尽管他们像被什么东西追赶似地匆忙，他们身上却有一种奇异的温顺。许多人低着头走路，仿佛还没准备好应对任何出乎意料的事物。"

    old "It is, I suppose, a bit surprising. I was expecting that I'd find more people who were like you."
    new "It is, I suppose, a bit surprising. I was expecting that I'd find more people who were like you.\n我想，这多少有点令人惊讶。我原以为会找到更多像你这样的人。"

    old "You're saying I'm not like most people."
    new "You're saying I'm not like most people.\n你是说我和大多数人不一样。"

    old "You're different from the people of this city, that is for certain. You've got a certain quality about you."
    new "You're different from the people of this city, that is for certain. You've got a certain quality about you.\n你和这座城市的人不一样，这是肯定的。你身上有一种特质。"

    old "What is that quality?"
    new "What is that quality?\n什么特质？"

    old "You are...you are like an animal. You are unpredictable in a way that is exciting and terrifying."
    new "You are...you are like an animal. You are unpredictable in a way that is exciting and terrifying.\n你……你就像一只动物。你以一种令人兴奋又畏惧的方式，难以预测。"

    old "I didn't realize you saw me that way."
    new "I didn't realize you saw me that way.\n我没想到你是那样看我的。"

    old "I like that about you. I think it's because you wander into danger so often."
    new "I like that about you. I think it's because you wander into danger so often.\n我喜欢你这一点。我想，那是因为你总是主动踏入险境。"

    old "Nuala gestures to a crowd beside us."
    new "Nuala gestures to a crowd beside us.\nNuala 朝我们身旁的人群比了比。"

    old "These people don't know what living is, because they never confront death. You and I are different. You and I know what it's like to stand, staring down a beast, with weapon in hand. We know what it means to live because we know what it means to die."
    new "These people don't know what living is, because they never confront death. You and I are different. You and I know what it's like to stand, staring down a beast, with weapon in hand. We know what it means to live because we know what it means to die.\n这些人不知道生活是什么，因为他们从不直面死亡。你和我不同。你我都知道，手握武器、直面一头野兽是什么感觉。我们知道活着意味着什么，因为我们也知道死亡意味着什么。"

    old "But now, I think I understand why it is that you fight to protect these people. Their obliviousness allows them to experience something that we can't. They don't live in fear of immediate death, but that has allowed them to construct buildings, create artwork, and bake this delicious bread."
    new "But now, I think I understand why it is that you fight to protect these people. Their obliviousness allows them to experience something that we can't. They don't live in fear of immediate death, but that has allowed them to construct buildings, create artwork, and bake this delicious bread.\n但现在，我想我明白了你为什么战斗去保护这些人。他们的浑然不觉，让他们得以体验一些我们无法体验的东西。他们不活在对即刻死亡的恐惧中，正因如此，他们才能建造楼宇、创作艺术品、烤出这美味的面包。"

    old "Nuala tosses the last of the loaf into her mouth."
    new "Nuala tosses the last of the loaf into her mouth.\nNuala 把最后一口面包丢进嘴里。"

    old "The docile people need animals like us to protect their way of life."
    new "The docile people need animals like us to protect their way of life.\n温顺的人需要我们这样的动物来守护他们的生活方式。"

    old "They've learned to ignore their instincts. The instincts that tell them to fight. And...other things, too."
    new "They've learned to ignore their instincts. The instincts that tell them to fight. And...other things, too.\n他们学会了忽视自己的本能。那些叫他们去战斗的本能。还有……其他一些东西。"

    old "Nuala looks at me with big eyes and leans in, close enough for me to feel her breath on my neck."
    new "Nuala looks at me with big eyes and leans in, close enough for me to feel her breath on my neck.\nNuala 睁大眼睛看着我，倾身靠过来，近得我能感到她呼在我脖颈上的气息。"

    old "Can you feel it, too? The sensation that's begging you to give into your impulses and do what animals do?"
    new "Can you feel it, too? The sensation that's begging you to give into your impulses and do what animals do?\n你也能感觉到吗？那种乞求你屈从冲动、去做动物所做的事的渴望？"

    old "Nuala leans in and nuzzles my neck, then gives my earlobe a less-than-gentle bite, seemingly oblivious to the crowd around us."
    new "Nuala leans in and nuzzles my neck, then gives my earlobe a less-than-gentle bite, seemingly oblivious to the crowd around us.\nNuala 靠过来，用鼻尖蹭了蹭我的脖子，然后不那么轻柔地咬了一下我的耳垂，似乎全然不顾周围的人群。"

    old "This doesn't seem to be the place."
    new "This doesn't seem to be the place.\n这里似乎不是做这种事的地方。"

    old "Then let's find a place."
    new "Then let's find a place.\n那我们就找个地方。"

    old "Let's find a place, then."
    new "Let's find a place, then.\n那我们就找个地方吧。"

    old "I grab Nuala by the hand and pull her down the street toward the nearest inn."
    new "I grab Nuala by the hand and pull her down the street toward the nearest inn.\n我抓住 Nuala 的手，拉着她沿街朝最近的客栈走去。"

    old "Nuala drags me into the room and slams the door shut before pinning me to the wall. She leans in and bites my lower lip. She flicks my lip with her tongue before releasing it."
    new "Nuala drags me into the room and slams the door shut before pinning me to the wall. She leans in and bites my lower lip. She flicks my lip with her tongue before releasing it.\nNuala 把我拽进房间，猛地关上门，然后把我按在墙上。她倾身咬住我的下唇，用舌尖拨弄了一下，才松开。"

    old "Is that all?"
    new "Is that all?\n就这样？"

    old "Nuala grabs my head, forcing my mouth onto hers, and she pulls me in for another kiss. The kiss starts deep—my lips explore hers for a few moments—but soon I feel her teeth again, biting down on my lower lip. The sharp pain stirs something in me, and I grab Nuala by the belt, pulling her hips into mine as she continues the biting kiss."
    new "Nuala grabs my head, forcing my mouth onto hers, and she pulls me in for another kiss. The kiss starts deep—my lips explore hers for a few moments—but soon I feel her teeth again, biting down on my lower lip. The sharp pain stirs something in me, and I grab Nuala by the belt, pulling her hips into mine as she continues the biting kiss.\nNuala 抓住我的头，把我的嘴按到她的唇上，拉我进入又一场深吻。这一吻始于深入——我的唇在她唇上探寻了片刻——但很快，我又感到了她的牙齿，咬住了我的下唇。那阵尖锐的痛楚激起了我体内的某种东西，我抓住 Nuala 的腰带，把她的胯拉向我的，她则继续着这咬噬的吻。"

    old "I place a hand on her waist, and feel the touch of her smooth skin against mine. She reaches up, placing her hand over mine, and she lifts my hand to her cheek. She licks my fingers."
    new "I place a hand on her waist, and feel the touch of her smooth skin against mine. She reaches up, placing her hand over mine, and she lifts my hand to her cheek. She licks my fingers.\n我把一只手放在她的腰上，感受到她光滑的皮肤贴着我的触感。她抬起手，覆在我的手上，然后把我的手引向她的脸颊。她舔了舔我的手指。"

    old "I don't want to be comfortable. I want to feel alive."
    new "I don't want to be comfortable. I want to feel alive.\n我不想舒服。我想感受活着。"

    old "Do you know what I love about combat? The best part of fighting is the pain. That sensation that reminds you take that remind you that you're still alive."
    new "Do you know what I love about combat? The best part of fighting is the pain. That sensation that reminds you take that remind you that you're still alive.\n你知道我喜欢战斗的什么吗？战斗最美妙的部分就是疼痛。那种感觉提醒着你——你仍然活着。"

    old "Nuala leans in, biting my lip again, this time hard enough that it doesn't feel like she's going to let go—she only pulls away when I feel a warm wetness and the familiar taste of blood in my mouth."
    new "Nuala leans in, biting my lip again, this time hard enough that it doesn't feel like she's going to let go—she only pulls away when I feel a warm wetness and the familiar taste of blood in my mouth.\nNuala 又靠过来，咬住我的嘴唇，这次咬得极重，仿佛不打算松口——直到我感到一股温热的湿润，以及口中熟悉的血腥味，她才松开。"

    old "This is what we were born to do. To bleed. To experience pain. That's the purest form of passion, isn't it?"
    new "This is what we were born to do. To bleed. To experience pain. That's the purest form of passion, isn't it?\n这就是我们生来要做的事。流血。感受疼痛。那是最纯粹的激情，不是吗？"

    old "I grab Nuala by the shoulders and tackle her to the floor. She lets out a yelp, and I feel her hands on my chest, grabbing my shirt. I hear the sound of tearing fabric and the touch of her hands on the bare skin of my chest. She caresses me for a moment, then pinches me."
    new "I grab Nuala by the shoulders and tackle her to the floor. She lets out a yelp, and I feel her hands on my chest, grabbing my shirt. I hear the sound of tearing fabric and the touch of her hands on the bare skin of my chest. She caresses me for a moment, then pinches me.\n我抓住 Nuala 的肩膀，把她扑倒在地。她发出一声轻叫，我感到她的双手按在我的胸口，抓住我的衬衫。我听到布料撕裂的声音，以及她的手触上我胸前裸露肌肤的感觉。她抚摸了我一会儿，然后捏了我一下。"

    old "Nuala gives me a cheeky grin, as if inviting me to return the favor. I run a hand through her hair, and grab a fistfull of it and pull it. She squeals as I yank on her hair, and pull her in for a kiss."
    new "Nuala gives me a cheeky grin, as if inviting me to return the favor. I run a hand through her hair, and grab a fistfull of it and pull it. She squeals as I yank on her hair, and pull her in for a kiss.\nNuala 朝我露出一个俏皮的笑，仿佛在邀请我还以颜色。我用手穿过她的头发，抓起一绺，猛地一拽。我扯她的头发时，她尖声叫了出来，我则把她拉进一个吻。"

    old "This time, I'm the one who starts off biting her lip, but the kiss quickly becomes a dance of our tongues each assaulting each other's mouths. I pull back from the kiss for a moment, and whisper into her ear."
    new "This time, I'm the one who starts off biting her lip, but the kiss quickly becomes a dance of our tongues each assaulting each other's mouths. I pull back from the kiss for a moment, and whisper into her ear.\n这一次，先咬住她嘴唇的人是我，但那个吻很快变成了我们舌头的舞蹈，彼此侵犯着对方的口舌。我从吻中抽身片刻，在她耳边低语。"

    old "You're mine."
    new "You're mine.\n你是我的。"

    old "Nuala pulls back. She backs up, but she shakes her hips, as if beckoning me forward."
    new "Nuala pulls back. She backs up, but she shakes her hips, as if beckoning me forward.\nNuala 向后退开。她后退着，却扭动着腰肢，仿佛在召唤我上前。"

    old "Then come and get me."
    new "Then come and get me.\n那就来抓我啊。"

    old "I crawl toward Nuala and say it again."
    new "I crawl toward Nuala and say it again.\n我朝 Nuala 爬过去，又说了一遍。"

    old "You're mine, Nuala."
    new "You're mine, Nuala.\n你是我的，Nuala。"

    old "I reach out to touch her hair again, but she grabs me by the wrist and pins me down as she rolls on top of me."
    new "I reach out to touch her hair again, but she grabs me by the wrist and pins me down as she rolls on top of me.\n我伸手再去碰她的头发，她却抓住我的手腕，把我按倒，翻身骑到我身上。"

    old "No, you're mine, [protag]."
    new "No, you're mine, [protag].\n不，你是我的，[protag]。"

    old "Nuala crawls on top of me, and she grins as she straddles me and starts to undo my belt."
    new "Nuala crawls on top of me, and she grins as she straddles me and starts to undo my belt.\nNuala 爬到我身上，她跨坐上来，咧嘴笑着，开始解我的腰带。"

    old "I have a better idea. I think there's a spirit deep within you that wants a different kind of action after walking among the docile for a day."
    new "I have a better idea. I think there's a spirit deep within you that wants a different kind of action after walking among the docile for a day.\n我有个更好的主意。我想你内心深处有某种精神，在温顺的人群中走了一天后，正渴望一种不同的活动。"

    old "I begin leading Nuala through the streets."
    new "I begin leading Nuala through the streets.\n我开始领着 Nuala 穿过街道。"

    old "Where are we going?"
    new "Where are we going?\n我们要去哪里？"

    old "To the sparring grounds, where the city guard trains new recruits. Come on, let's spar."
    new "To the sparring grounds, where the city guard trains new recruits. Come on, let's spar.\n去训练场，城卫训练新兵的地方。来吧，我们切磋切磋。"

    old "Minutes later, Nuala is standing with a weapon in her hand, and looking more at ease. In her combat stance, with that fierceness in her eyes, Nuala really does look like an animal, poised to strike."
    new "Minutes later, Nuala is standing with a weapon in her hand, and looking more at ease. In her combat stance, with that fierceness in her eyes, Nuala really does look like an animal, poised to strike.\n几分钟后，Nuala 手持武器站着，看起来自在多了。在她战斗的姿势里，眼里透着那股狠劲，Nuala 真的像一只蓄势待发的野兽。"

    old "What brings you in the desert again?"
    new "What brings you in the desert again?\n又是什么风把你吹到沙漠里来了？"

    old "I came to see you."
    new "I came to see you.\n我来看你。"

    old "Oh. I'm flattered."
    new "Oh. I'm flattered.\n哦。我受宠若惊。"

    old "I wanted to know more about the nomads tribes."
    new "I wanted to know more about the nomads tribes.\n我想多了解一些游牧部族的情况。"

    old "What you wish to know?"
    new "What you wish to know?\n你想知道什么？"

    old "I understand that there are many nomad tribes. The Dunemarchers are one of them, but I presume there are others."
    new "I understand that there are many nomad tribes. The Dunemarchers are one of them, but I presume there are others.\n我知道游牧部族有很多。Dunemarchers 是其中之一，但我想应该还有别的。"

    old "Yes, you're correct."
    new "Yes, you're correct.\n是的，你说得对。"

    old "There are many others? Do you know them? Have you meet them?"
    new "There are many others? Do you know them? Have you meet them?\n还有很多吗？你认识他们吗？你见过他们吗？"

    old "Why all this curiosity, [protag]?"
    new "Why all this curiosity, [protag]?\n为什么这么好奇，[protag]？"

    old "My people are the Dunemarchers."
    new "My people are the Dunemarchers.\n我的人民是 Dunemarchers。"

    old "So you don't identify with other tribes, or nomads as broad term?"
    new "So you don't identify with other tribes, or nomads as broad term?\n所以你不认同其他部族，或者说，不认同广义上的游牧民？"

    old "Of course I do. But I don't know them as well as the Dunemarchers, who I consider to be my own people."
    new "Of course I do. But I don't know them as well as the Dunemarchers, who I consider to be my own people.\n我当然认同。但我不像了解 Dunemarchers 那样了解他们，我把 Dunemarchers 视为我自己的人民。"

    old "Also, sometimes nomad tribe goes at war with each other."
    new "Also, sometimes nomad tribe goes at war with each other.\n而且，有时游牧部族之间也会互相开战。"

    old "Nuala chuckles."
    new "Nuala chuckles.\nNuala 轻笑了一声。"

    old "Haha, you're always joking, eh [protag]?"
    new "Haha, you're always joking, eh [protag]?\n哈哈，你总爱开玩笑，嗯，[protag]？"

    old "I'm not the only young shaman of my people, though probably I am one of the youngest, if this is what you're wondering."
    new "I'm not the only young shaman of my people, though probably I am one of the youngest, if this is what you're wondering.\n我不是我人民中唯一的年轻萨满，不过如果你想知道的话，我大概是其中最年轻的之一。"

    old "Anyways, you've become rather...famous in Grimoire, Nuala. People on the street talk about the 'beauty from the desert' that sometimes comes in town. You're popular."
    new "Anyways, you've become rather...famous in Grimoire, Nuala. People on the street talk about the 'beauty from the desert' that sometimes comes in town. You're popular.\n话说回来，你在 Grimoire 已经变得相当……出名了，Nuala。街上的人们都在谈论那个偶尔进城来的“沙漠美人”。你很受欢迎。"

    old "Thanks, [protag], but I'm hardly the only popular nomad. I'm sure you heard of Amukiki, for example."
    new "Thanks, [protag], but I'm hardly the only popular nomad. I'm sure you heard of Amukiki, for example.\n谢谢，[protag]，但我绝不是唯一受欢迎的游牧民。比如说，我敢肯定你听说过 Amukiki。"

    old "The arena gladiator?"
    new "The arena gladiator?\n那个竞技场角斗士？"

    old "Yes. He is not in Grimoire at the moment, but his fame is spreading fast. He is a formidable gladiator."
    new "Yes. He is not in Grimoire at the moment, but his fame is spreading fast. He is a formidable gladiator.\n是的。他此刻不在 Grimoire，但他的名声正迅速传开。他是个了得的角斗士。"

    old "Is he from your tribe?"
    new "Is he from your tribe?\n他是你部族的人吗？"

    old "No, though I've met his tribe, the Bears, some years ago."
    new "No, though I've met his tribe, the Bears, some years ago.\n不是，不过我几年前见过他的部族——Bears。"

    old "A peaceful meeting, I hope?"
    new "A peaceful meeting, I hope?\n但愿那是次和平的会面？"

    old "Not exactly. Our warchief, Larik, was challenged to duel with Amukiki."
    new "Not exactly. Our warchief, Larik, was challenged to duel with Amukiki.\n不完全是。我们的战争首领 Larik，曾被 Amukiki 挑战决斗。"

    old "And...?"
    new "And...?\n然后……？"

    old "It was a good fight, but in the end Larik lost, and Amukiki spared his life. It turned out that he only wanted to test his strength against one of the most famous warchiefs."
    new "It was a good fight, but in the end Larik lost, and Amukiki spared his life. It turned out that he only wanted to test his strength against one of the most famous warchiefs.\n那是场精彩的战斗，但最终 Larik 输了，而 Amukiki 饶了他一命。原来，他只是想和最著名的战争首领之一较量较量自己的实力。"

    old "Shortly after, Amukiki left the nomads and started being a gladiator."
    new "Shortly after, Amukiki left the nomads and started being a gladiator.\n不久之后，Amukiki 离开了游牧民，开始当角斗士。"

    old "I'm not sure, I don't know him well, but he must have had his reasons."
    new "I'm not sure, I don't know him well, but he must have had his reasons.\n我不确定，我不太了解他，但他必定有他的理由。"

    old "It has been nice to talk with you [protag], but now I must go. And I'm sure you have business to attend to as well."
    new "It has been nice to talk with you [protag], but now I must go. And I'm sure you have business to attend to as well.\n很高兴能和你聊天，[protag]，但现在我必须走了。我相信你也还有事要忙。"

    old "Sure I do. Talk to you later, Nuala."
    new "Sure I do. Talk to you later, Nuala.\n当然有。回头再聊，Nuala。"

    old "I wake to the loud sound of breaking glass."
    new "I wake to the loud sound of breaking glass.\n我被一声响亮的玻璃碎裂声惊醒。"

    old "Was that my window? But that would mean that someone is breaking into my home. Who would be bold enough to do that?"
    new "Was that my window? But that would mean that someone is breaking into my home. Who would be bold enough to do that?\n那是我的窗户吗？但那意味着有人闯进了我家。谁会这么大胆？"

    old "Nuala? What the hell?"
    new "Nuala? What the hell?\nNuala？搞什么鬼？"

    old "I'm sorry. I'll repay you for the broken window."
    new "I'm sorry. I'll repay you for the broken window.\n对不起。打破的窗户我会赔给你的。"

    old "Couldn't you just knock on the door? Or better yet, couldn't you have just waited until tomorrow morning?"
    new "Couldn't you just knock on the door? Or better yet, couldn't you have just waited until tomorrow morning?\n你就不能敲门吗？或者更好，你就不能等到明天早上吗？"

    old "What's so urgent that you felt that you needed to break into my house in the middle of the night?"
    new "What's so urgent that you felt that you needed to break into my house in the middle of the night?\n到底有什么急事，让你觉得非得半夜闯进我家？"

    old "You slept with other people."
    new "You slept with other people.\n你和别人上床了。"

    old "Ah. I'm in trouble."
    new "Ah. I'm in trouble.\n啊。我有麻烦了。"

    old "What does this mean, [protag]?"
    new "What does this mean, [protag]?\n这是什么意思，[protag]？"

    old "I know that maybe it wasn't fair to you, but..."
    new "I know that maybe it wasn't fair to you, but...\n我知道也许这对你不公平，但是……"

    old "So that was it? We just had a night of 'fun'?"
    new "So that was it? We just had a night of 'fun'?\n所以就只是这样？我们只是共度了一夜“欢愉”？"

    old "She lunges forward, grabbing my shoulders in the process. I have to admit that for a second I thought that she was going to attack me. Also... I might have been just a little scared."
    new "She lunges forward, grabbing my shoulders in the process. I have to admit that for a second I thought that she was going to attack me. Also... I might have been just a little scared.\n她猛扑过来，一把抓住我的肩膀。我不得不承认，有那么一瞬，我以为她要攻击我。而且……我也许确实有点害怕。"

    old "You played with me, [protag]! You said that I was yours."
    new "You played with me, [protag]! You said that I was yours.\n你玩弄了我，[protag]！你说过我是你的。"

    old "I am sorry if you misunderstood, Nuala. I never meant that... you know..."
    new "I am sorry if you misunderstood, Nuala. I never meant that... you know...\n如果你误会了，我很抱歉，Nuala。我从来没那个意思……你知道的……"

    old "That you loved me?"
    new "That you loved me?\n没那个意思说你爱我？"

    old "Yes. Sorry."
    new "Yes. Sorry.\n是的。抱歉。"

    old "You're lucky that we need you for the upcoming mission at N'Mar or I would pluck your eyes out with my bare hands, [protag]."
    new "You're lucky that we need you for the upcoming mission at N'Mar or I would pluck your eyes out with my bare hands, [protag].\n算你走运，我们即将到来的 N'Mar 任务还需要你，否则我会用这双空手把你的眼珠子抠出来，[protag]。"

    old "Nuala, please. Calm down."
    new "Nuala, please. Calm down.\nNuala，求你了。冷静点。"

    old "She let's go of me and then sits on the bed, burying her face in her hands. Wait. Is she crying?"
    new "She let's go of me and then sits on the bed, burying her face in her hands. Wait. Is she crying?\n她松开我，然后坐到床上，把脸埋进双手里。等等。她在哭吗？"

    old "I approach her cautiously and try to place a hand gently on her shoulder but she quickly slaps it away."
    new "I approach her cautiously and try to place a hand gently on her shoulder but she quickly slaps it away.\n我小心翼翼地靠近她，试着轻轻地把手放在她的肩上，但她很快把手拍开了。"

    old "I know, [protag]. I hoped that you loved only me, the way I love you, but apparently I was wrong."
    new "I know, [protag]. I hoped that you loved only me, the way I love you, but apparently I was wrong.\n我知道，[protag]。我曾希望，你只爱我一个人，就像我爱你一样，但显然我错了。"

    old "I still want to remain your friend, Nuala."
    new "I still want to remain your friend, Nuala.\n我仍然想做你的朋友，Nuala。"

    old "Nuala forces herself to smile. She can't quite hide that hint of sadness lurking just under the surface."
    new "Nuala forces herself to smile. She can't quite hide that hint of sadness lurking just under the surface.\nNuala 强挤出一个微笑。她没能完全藏住潜藏在表面之下的那一丝悲伤。"

    old "For now, we'll keep working together to defeat the evil lurking in N'Mar."
    new "For now, we'll keep working together to defeat the evil lurking in N'Mar.\n眼下，我们会继续合作，去击败潜伏在 N'Mar 的邪恶。"

    old "Then... we'll see. Maybe I will have the strength to forgive you by then."
    new "Then... we'll see. Maybe I will have the strength to forgive you by then.\n然后……我们再看吧。也许到那时，我就有力气原谅你了。"

    old "I hope so, Nuala."
    new "I hope so, Nuala.\n我希望如此，Nuala。"

    old "She leaves me on my own shortly after. I'm not sure I'll be able to get back to sleep tonight..."
    new "She leaves me on my own shortly after. I'm not sure I'll be able to get back to sleep tonight...\n不久后，她留下我独自一人。我不确定今晚还能不能再睡着……"

    old "I know and it was a mistake."
    new "I know and it was a mistake.\n我知道，那是个错误。"

    old "A big mistake."
    new "A big mistake.\n一个很大的错误。"

    old "Try to understand though... It's not like we were engaged. We didn't set any rules and I wasn't sure what your feelings were--"
    new "Try to understand though... It's not like we were engaged. We didn't set any rules and I wasn't sure what your feelings were--\n不过试着理解一下……我们又不是订了婚。我们没有定下任何规则，我也不确定你的感受——"

    old "I love you."
    new "I love you.\n我爱你。"

    old "Those three words spill from her mouth so naturally as her eyes steadily fix on mine. The ferocious beast that was terrifying me mere moments ago has suddenly stirred up a very different emotion."
    new "Those three words spill from her mouth so naturally as her eyes steadily fix on mine. The ferocious beast that was terrifying me mere moments ago has suddenly stirred up a very different emotion.\n那三个字从她嘴里如此自然地流出，她的目光稳稳地锁住我的。片刻之前还让我心惊胆战的凶猛野兽，此刻却突然激起了一种截然不同的情感。"

    old "I love you too, Nuala."
    new "I love you too, Nuala.\n我也爱你，Nuala。"

    old "Please, let's leave the past behind us. I won't betray you ever again. I swear it."
    new "Please, let's leave the past behind us. I won't betray you ever again. I swear it.\n求你了，让我们把过去抛在脑后。我再也不会背叛你。我发誓。"

    old "You better keep your promise, [protag], or..."
    new "You better keep your promise, [protag], or...\n你最好信守诺言，[protag]，否则……"

    old "Or what?"
    new "Or what?\n否则什么？"

    old "Or I won't be letting you do this anymore."
    new "Or I won't be letting you do this anymore.\n否则我就不会再让你这么做了。"

    old "Nuala smiles, and walks toward the bed... I'm starting to understand her intentions now."
    new "Nuala smiles, and walks toward the bed... I'm starting to understand her intentions now.\nNuala 微笑着，朝床边走去……我现在开始明白她的意图了。"

    old "Looks like I won't be getting back to sleep any time soon. Not that I mind."
    new "Looks like I won't be getting back to sleep any time soon. Not that I mind.\n看来我一时半会儿是睡不成了。不过我倒不介意。"

    old "It's almost dusk when I meet with Nuala near the Orcish Wastes."
    new "It's almost dusk when I meet with Nuala near the Orcish Wastes.\n我在 Orcish Wastes 附近与 Nuala 会面时，天色已近黄昏。"

    old "[protag]! You came. I wasn't sure you'd be able to find the time."
    new "[protag]! You came. I wasn't sure you'd be able to find the time.\n[protag]！你来了。我不确定你能不能抽出时间。"

    old "For you, Nuala, I managed. So, what's the plan?"
    new "For you, Nuala, I managed. So, what's the plan?\n为了你，Nuala，我办到了。那么，计划是什么？"

    old "I wanted to show you something."
    new "I wanted to show you something.\n我想给你看样东西。"

    old "You're being mysterious. I like that."
    new "You're being mysterious. I like that.\n你在卖关子。我喜欢。"

    old "I think it's something that you town-people don't see very often."
    new "I think it's something that you town-people don't see very often.\n我想，这是你们城里人不常看到的东西。"

    old "Let me guess: it involves the desert and... something wild. Some rare animal?"
    new "Let me guess: it involves the desert and... something wild. Some rare animal?\n让我猜猜：它和沙漠有关，还有……某种野性的东西。某种珍稀动物？"

    old "Yes, in a way. But follow me please."
    new "Yes, in a way. But follow me please.\n是的，从某种意义上说。不过请跟我来。"

    old "I follow Nuala further into the desert until we reach an area I've never been before. At least, I think it's an area I've never seen before. It's kind of hard for me to tell when it comes to deserts."
    new "I follow Nuala further into the desert until we reach an area I've never been before. At least, I think it's an area I've never seen before. It's kind of hard for me to tell when it comes to deserts.\n我跟着 Nuala 深入沙漠，直到来到一片我从没去过的地方。至少，我认为那是我从没见过的地方。对我来说，沙漠里这种地方真的很难分辨。"

    old "If wasn't for Nuala's magic light, I wouldn't be able to see anything. It's pretty dark here in the desert, in middle of nowhere."
    new "If wasn't for Nuala's magic light, I wouldn't be able to see anything. It's pretty dark here in the desert, in middle of nowhere.\n要不是 Nuala 的魔法光，我什么都看不见。在这沙漠的荒郊野岭，天已经相当黑了。"

    old "Sorry, we're almost there. This should be the area."
    new "Sorry, we're almost there. This should be the area.\n抱歉，我们快到了。应该就是这片区域。"

    old "Ehm, Nuala... I think someone or something is following us."
    new "Ehm, Nuala... I think someone or something is following us.\n呃，Nuala……我觉得有什么人或什么东西在跟踪我们。"

    old "Oh yes, I know. I was hoping to meet her here."
    new "Oh yes, I know. I was hoping to meet her here.\n哦，是的，我知道。我正希望在这里见到她。"

    old "'Her'? Who is 'her'?"
    new "'Her'? Who is 'her'?\n“她”？“她”是谁？"

    old "It's Sheeba."
    new "It's Sheeba.\n是 Sheeba。"

    old "Nuala moves in close and gestures to keep quiet. From behind a rock, I see a... well, a big feline. I'm not sure what kind of cat she is."
    new "Nuala moves in close and gestures to keep quiet. From behind a rock, I see a... well, a big feline. I'm not sure what kind of cat she is.\nNuala 靠近过来，做了个手势让我保持安静。从一块岩石后面，我看到一只……嗯，一只大型猫科动物。我不确定她是什么品种的猫。"

    old "Nuala, is it safe?"
    new "Nuala, is it safe?\nNuala，这安全吗？"

    old "Yes, don't worry. We've known each other for a long time."
    new "Yes, don't worry. We've known each other for a long time.\n安全，别担心。我们认识很久了。"

    old "I hope you're right about that. I mean, we've fought coyotes before but this is slightly bigger than them!"
    new "I hope you're right about that. I mean, we've fought coyotes before but this is slightly bigger than them!\n希望你没弄错。我是说，我们以前跟郊狼交过手，但这位可比它们大多了！"

    old "Amusing. [protag], the envoy of Grimoire, is scared of a kitty cat."
    new "Amusing. [protag], the envoy of Grimoire, is scared of a kitty cat.\n有意思。Grimoire 的特使 [protag]，居然怕一只小猫咪。"

    old "I'm only being prudent, you know."
    new "I'm only being prudent, you know.\n我只是谨慎一点，你知道的。"

    old "So, do you like her? Isn't she magnificent?"
    new "So, do you like her? Isn't she magnificent?\n那么，你喜欢她吗？她是不是很壮观？"

    old "Well, I must admit that I've never seen a wild animal up close quite like this."
    new "Well, I must admit that I've never seen a wild animal up close quite like this.\n嗯，我必须承认，我从来没有这样近距离地见过野生动物。"

    old "She looks so peaceful. Almost as if she'd let me pet her."
    new "She looks so peaceful. Almost as if she'd let me pet her.\n她看起来那么平静。几乎像是会让我摸摸她似的。"

    old "You probably shouldn't do that."
    new "You probably shouldn't do that.\n你最好还是别那么做。"

    old "She might tolerate that from me, but I doubt she'd let you get away with something like that."
    new "She might tolerate that from me, but I doubt she'd let you get away with something like that.\n她或许能容忍我那样做，但我怀疑她会让你得逞。"

    old "Heh. Thanks for the warning. Still... This is pretty incredible."
    new "Heh. Thanks for the warning. Still... This is pretty incredible.\n嘿。谢谢你的提醒。不过……这确实太不可思议了。"

    old "How did you manage to earn her trust?"
    new "How did you manage to earn her trust?\n你是怎么赢得她的信任的？"

    old "It's actually a very cute story. I was chasing some prey when I stumbled upon her. She was injured, scared."
    new "It's actually a very cute story. I was chasing some prey when I stumbled upon her. She was injured, scared.\n其实是个很可爱的故事。我当时正在追捕猎物，偶然撞见了她。她受了伤，受了惊吓。"

    old "I used my magic to heal her and then I followed her at distance to see where she was going."
    new "I used my magic to heal her and then I followed her at distance to see where she was going.\n我用我的魔法治好了她，然后远远地跟着她，看她要去哪里。"

    old "In her lair, she had three kittens were waiting for her. They were hungry, but she hadn't been able to bring them food. She was too weak. I was able to heal her wounds, but I couldn't give her back her strength. She needed food for that."
    new "In her lair, she had three kittens were waiting for her. They were hungry, but she hadn't been able to bring them food. She was too weak. I was able to heal her wounds, but I couldn't give her back her strength. She needed food for that.\n在她的巢穴里，有三只幼崽在等她。它们很饿，可她已经没法给它们带回食物。她太虚弱了。我治好了她的伤口，却无法把力气还给她。那需要食物。"

    old "Amazing. So I guess you fed them?"
    new "Amazing. So I guess you fed them?\n太神奇了。那我猜你喂了它们？"

    old "Yes, for several days I went hunting in their mother's stead. I brought them food and they slowly learned to trust me."
    new "Yes, for several days I went hunting in their mother's stead. I brought them food and they slowly learned to trust me.\n是的，有好几天，我代替它们的母亲去打猎。我给它们带回食物，它们慢慢学会了信任我。"

    old "I am not entirely sure if this one is her-- Sheeba, I mean-- or one of her kittens that grew up though. They look rather similar to me."
    new "I am not entirely sure if this one is her-- Sheeba, I mean-- or one of her kittens that grew up though. They look rather similar to me.\n不过，我不太确定这只是不是她——我是说 Sheeba——还是她某只长大了的幼崽。它们在我看来相当像。"

    old "You were right. That was really a sweet story."
    new "You were right. That was really a sweet story.\n你没说错。这真是个温暖的故事。"

    old "You know, sometimes I come here alone to relax with her. When I do, I kind of feel like I'm a beast too."
    new "You know, sometimes I come here alone to relax with her. When I do, I kind of feel like I'm a beast too.\n你知道吗，有时我会一个人来这里，和她一起放松。那时候，我有点觉得自己也是一头野兽。"

    old "Hm. You do look like one. Just a much cuter one."
    new "Hm. You do look like one. Just a much cuter one.\n嗯。你看起来确实像。只是可爱得多。"

    old "Heheh. Thanks, [protag]. Sometimes I also do something else that you might find interesting."
    new "Heheh. Thanks, [protag]. Sometimes I also do something else that you might find interesting.\n嘿嘿。谢谢，[protag]。有时我还会做点别的事，你也许会觉得有趣。"

    old "Let me show you."
    new "Let me show you.\n让我展示给你看。"

    old "My attention is drawn to Nuala's hips. They sway back and forth almost as if Nuala is dancing while she starts to slowly undress. Soon enough, she discards the last article of clothing as the big feline continues watching us from a safe distance."
    new "My attention is drawn to Nuala's hips. They sway back and forth almost as if Nuala is dancing while she starts to slowly undress. Soon enough, she discards the last article of clothing as the big feline continues watching us from a safe distance.\n我的注意力被 Nuala 的腰肢吸引住了。它们前后摇摆，几乎就像 Nuala 在跳舞，同时她开始慢慢褪去衣衫。很快，她脱掉了最后一件衣物，而那只大型猫科动物仍在安全的距离外注视着我们。"

    old "I...I..."
    new "I...I...\n我……我……"

    old "I've managed to leave you speechless, have I?"
    new "I've managed to leave you speechless, have I?\n我设法让你说不出话来了，是吗？"

    old "Something like that. You don't see something as beautiful as this every day."
    new "Something like that. You don't see something as beautiful as this every day.\n差不多吧。这么美的东西，可不是天天能见到的。"

    old "Heheh. Thanks [protag]. Isn't being so close to such a ferocious beast exciting? It makes you feel alive."
    new "Heheh. Thanks [protag]. Isn't being so close to such a ferocious beast exciting? It makes you feel alive.\n嘿嘿。谢谢，[protag]。离这么凶猛的野兽这么近，是不是很刺激？它让你感觉自己还活着。"

    old "In a way, yes. Though, I must admit that if you weren't here, I probably would have run away by now."
    new "In a way, yes. Though, I must admit that if you weren't here, I probably would have run away by now.\n从某种意义上说，是的。不过，我必须承认，要不是你在这里，我大概早就跑了。"

    old "Sheeba is not a threat, believe me. Still, all this excitement has me thinking..."
    new "Sheeba is not a threat, believe me. Still, all this excitement has me thinking...\nSheeba 不是威胁，相信我。不过，这所有的兴奋让我在想……"

